 must (1) specify its\nfederated-query merge strategy with stable ordering guarantees, (2) define\ncursor payload/format and pagination semantics for cross-tier queries, and (3)\ndescribe migration coordination for cursors that span operational-to-historical\ntransitions so implementers of cpt-cf-uc-fr-pluggable-storage provide consistent\nbehavior and documentation across backends.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nNitpick comments:\nIn `@modules/system/usage_collector/docs/DESIGN.md`:\n- Around line 154-167: The DESIGN note defers federated-query merge and cursor\nsemantics to the pluggable storage adapter framework\n(cpt-cf-uc-fr-pluggable-storage) but does not require adapters to document or\nimplement those specifics; update the DESIGN to require that any storage adapter\nimplementing federated queries must (1) specify its federated-query merge\nstrategy with stable ordering guarantees, (2) define cursor payload/format and\npagination semantics for cross-tier queries, and (3) describe migration\ncoordination for cursors that span operational-to-historical transitions so\nimplementers of cpt-cf-uc-fr-pluggable-storage provide consistent behavior and\ndocumentation across backends.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/619#pullrequestreview-3819091288","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/619","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/619#pullrequestreview-3819091288"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/619"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-18T10:36:37Z","commit_id":"