tem **MUST** monitor storage adapter health, buffer records during failures, retry with backoff, and alert on persistent issues. A record is acknowledged only after it is durably persisted **or** durably buffered; in-memory buffering alone MUST NOT be acknowledged as successful ingestion.\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@modules/system/usage_collector/docs/PRD.md` around lines 292 - 299, Update\nthe Storage Health Monitoring requirement (ID: cpt-cf-uc-fr-storage-health) to\nexplicitly state buffering and acknowledgement semantics: specify whether the\nbuffer is durable (e.g., persisted to local disk or replicated) or ephemeral,\nand state that client acknowledgements are withheld until the record is durably\npersisted either to the storage backend or to the durable buffer; if non-durable\nbuffering is allowed, document the associated risk and that retries/backoff plus\noperator alerts are the only guarantees. Also add a short failure flow (buffer\n-> retry with backoff -> alert -> operator intervention) and note any\nexactly-once/persistence boundary implications so readers know which component\n(storage adapter vs platform) provides durability and when ACKs are emitted.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nInline comments:\nIn `@modules/system/usage_collector/docs/PRD.md`:\n- Around line 352-362: Clarify the atomicity semantics for backfill in the\n`cpt-cf-uc-fr-backfill-api` requirement: explicitly state that \"atomic\nreplacement\" applies only to the Blocking mode (where real-time ingestion for\nthe range is suspended and the replacement is performed atomically), and for\nNon-blocking mode define the weaker guarantee (e.g., eventual convergence under\na deterministic conflict resolution policy or specify the exact\nconflict-resolution rules and visibility semantics). Update the PRD text around\n`p2`/`cpt-cf-uc-fr-backfill-api` to either restrict the phrase \"ensuring atomic\nreplacement\" to the Blocking mode or add a sentence describing the non-blocking\natomicity alternative (deterministic conflict resolution and eventual\nconsistency).\n\n---\n\nNitpick comments:\nIn `@modules/system/usage_collector/docs/PRD.md`:\n- Around line 292-299: Update the Storage Health Monitoring requirement (ID:\ncpt-cf-uc-fr-storage-health) to explicitly state buffering and acknowledgement\nsemantics: specify whether the buffer is durable (e.g., persisted to local disk\nor replicated) or ephemeral, and state that client acknowledgements are withheld\nuntil the record is durably persisted either to the storage backend or to the\ndurable buffer; if non-durable buffering is allowed, document the associated\nrisk and that retries/backoff plus operator alerts are the only guarantees. Also\nadd a short failure flow (buffer -> retry with backoff -> alert -> operator\nintervention) and note any exactly-once/persistence boundary implications so\nreaders know which component (storage adapter vs platform) provides durability\nand when ACKs are emitted.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/619#pullrequestreview-3819225224","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/619","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/619#pullrequestreview-3819225224"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/619"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-18T11:04:10Z","commit_id":"62a54830c54763b331ec0538e16d147414a233eb"},{"id":3852243003,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7lnJA7","user