"diff_hunk":"@@ -245,7 +245,8 @@ impl LockManager {\n                     )\n                     .as_bytes(),\n                 )\n-                .await;\n+                .await,\n+            );","path":"libs/modkit-db/src/advisory_locks.rs","commit_id":"9ce5e8dfb0aef62efa8c1d0065f788e19ee54161","original_commit_id":"9ce5e8dfb0aef62efa8c1d0065f788e19ee54161","user":{"login":"graphite-app[bot]","id":96075541,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOBbn_FQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/158384?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/graphite-app","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Critical write failure is silently ignored. If `write_all()` fails (disk full, I/O error, permissions), the lock file will be incomplete or empty, but the lock is still acquired and returned as successful. This could cause:\n\n1. Other processes reading the lock file to fail or get corrupted data\n2. Debugging issues when investigating lock problems\n3. Silent data loss of lock metadata (PID, key, timestamp)\n\nThe error should be propagated:\n\n```rust\nf.write_all(\n    format!(\n        \"PID: {}\\nKey: {}\\nTimestamp: {}\\n\",\n        std::process::id(),\n        key,\n        std::time::SystemTime::now().duration_since(std::time::UNIX_EPOCH).unwrap().as_secs()\n    )\n    .as_bytes(),\n).await?;\n```\n\nOr at minimum, log the error before dropping it.\n```suggestion\n            f.write_all(\n                format!(\n                    \"PID: {}\\nKey: {}\\nTimestamp: {}\\n\",\n                    std::process::id(),\n                    key,\n                    std::time::SystemTime::now()\n                        .duration_since(std::time::UNIX_EPOCH)\n                        .unwrap()\n                        .as_secs()\n                )\n                .as_bytes(),\n            )\n            .await?;\n```\n  \n\n*Spotted by [Graphite Agent](https://app.graphite.com/diamond/?org=cyberfabric&ref=ai-review-comment)*<i class='graphite__hidden'><br /><br /><a href=\"https://app.graphite.com/github/pr/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/616?chatWithGeneratedComment=8cd9d4b7-defd-41eb-9a5e-0008c8c372cb\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Fix in Graphite\" src=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-dark.svg\"></picture></a></i><i class='graphite__hidden'><br /><br />Is this helpful? React 👍 or 👎 to let us know.</i>","created_at":"2026-02-13T17:34:52Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T17:34:54Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/616#discussion_r2805330498","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/616","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2805330498"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/616#discussion_r2805330498"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/616"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2805330498/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":238,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":249,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":26,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2805348171","pull_request_review_id":3798595888,"id":2805348171,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6nNjdL","diff_hunk":"@@ -276,12 +276,14 @@ impl Lifecycle {\n             let status_on_ready = self.status.clone();\n             tokio::spawn(async move {\n                 if ready_rx.await.is_ok() {\n-                    let _ = status_on_ready.compare_exchange(\n-                        Status::Starting.as_u8(),\n-                        Status::Running.as_u8(),\n-                        Ordering::AcqRel,\n-                        Ordering::Acquire,\n-                    );\n+                    let _ = status_on_ready\n+                        .compare_exchange(\n+                            Status::Starting.as_u8(),\n+                            Status::Running.as_u8(),\n+                            Ordering::AcqRel,\n+                            Ordering::Acquire,\n+                        )\n+                        .ok();","path":"libs/modkit/src/lifecycle.rs","commit_id":"9ce5e8dfb0aef62efa8c1d0065f788e19ee54161","original_commit_id":"9ce5e8dfb0aef62efa8c1d0065f788e19ee54161","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# First, let's check the file and the specific lines mentioned\ncat -n libs/modkit/src/lifecycle.rs | sed -n '270,295p'\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 1430\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Let's check if there's a deny lint configuration for #[must_use]\nfind . -name \"lib.rs\" -o -name \"main.rs\" | head -20 | xargs grep -l \"must_use\" 2>/dev/null | head -5\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 54\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for deny lint rules in the codebase\nrg \"deny|warn.*must\" --max-count=20 -A 2 -B 2\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 50388\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if there are any existing #[must_use] related lint rules\nrg \"must_use\" --type rust -C 3\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 50387\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Look for Clippy or lint configuration\nfind . -name \"clippy.toml\" -o -name \".clippy.toml\" -o -name \"rustfmt.toml\" -o -name \"Cargo.toml\" | head -20 | xargs grep -l \"let_underscore\" 2>/dev/null\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 84\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check for deny configuration\nfind . -name \"deny.toml\" -o -name \"clippy.toml\" 2>/dev/null | xargs cat 2>/dev/null\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 6437\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Look for lint levels in Cargo.toml or lib.rs\nfind . -name \"Cargo.toml\" -o -name \"lib.rs\" | xargs grep -A 5 \"^\\[lints\\]\" 2>/dev/null | head -40\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 1967\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check the main lib.rs or root for lint configuration\ncat -n libs/modkit/src/lib.rs | head -30\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 1419\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check the root Cargo.toml for workspace lint configuration\ncat -n Cargo.toml | grep -A 50 \"\\[workspace.lints\"\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 2239\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Look specifically for clippy lint rules in workspace\ncat -n Cargo.toml | grep -A 100 \"\\[workspace.lints.clippy\"\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 3714\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Replace `let _ = ... .ok()` with `drop(...)` to satisfy the `let_underscore_must_use` deny lint.**\n\nThe workspace enforces `let_underscore_must_use = \"deny\"` at the Clippy level. Assigning a `#[must_use]` value (returned by `.ok()`) to `_` will fail compilation. Use `drop()` to explicitly discard the value.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-                    let _ = status_on_ready\n-                        .compare_exchange(\n-                            Status::Starting.as_u8(),\n-                            Status::Running.as_u8(),\n-                            Ordering::AcqRel,\n-                            Ordering::Acquire,\n-                        )\n-                        .ok();\n+                    drop(status_on_ready.compare_exchange(\n+                        Status::Starting.as_u8(),\n+                        Status::Running.as_u8(),\n+                        Ordering::AcqRel,\n+                        Ordering::Acquire,\n+                    ));\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@libs/modkit/src/lifecycle.rs` around lines 278 - 286, The current code\nassigns the must-use result of status_on_ready.compare_exchange(...).ok() to '_'\nwhich violates the let_underscore_must_use deny lint; replace the assignment\nwith an explicit drop call so the return value is intentionally discarded (i.e.\ncall drop(...) on the result of status_on_ready.compare_exchange(...).ok()) in\nthe block that follows ready_rx.await, referencing the ready_rx.await and\nstatus_on_ready.compare_exchange(Status::Starting.as_u8(),\nStatus::Running.as_u8(), Ordering::AcqRel, Ordering::Acquire) invocation.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-13T17:39:26Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T17:39:26Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/616#discussion_r2805348171","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/616","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2805348171"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/616#discussion_r2805348171"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/616"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2805348171/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":278,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":286,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":26,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"}],"source_reviews":[{"id":3798595888,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7iafkw","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 1**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@libs/modkit/src/lifecycle.rs`:\n- Around line 278-286: The current code assigns the must-use result of\nstatus_on_ready.compare_exchange(...).ok() to '_' which violates the\nlet_underscore_must_use deny lint; replace the assignment with an explicit drop\ncall so the return value is intentionally discarded (i.e. call drop(...) on the\nresult of status_on_ready.compare_exchange(...).ok()) in the block that follows\nready_rx.await, referencing the ready_rx.await and\nstatus_on_ready.compare_exchange(Status::Starting.as_u8(),\nStatus::Running.as_u8(), Ordering::AcqRel, Ordering::Acquire) invocation.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (4)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-node-info/src/syscap_collector.rs (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`228-228`: **Simplify by removing redundant `let _ =`.**\n\nThe `.ok()` method already converts the `Result` to `Option`, which is not `#[must_use]`. The `let _ =` binding is unnecessary after `.ok()`.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>✨ Suggested simplification</summary>\n\n```diff\n-                let _ = write!(details, \", VRAM: {vram:.0} MB\").ok();\n+                write!(details, \", VRAM: {vram:.0} MB\").ok();\n```\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`232-232`: **Same simplification applies here.**\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>✨ Suggested simplification</summary>\n\n```diff\n-                let _ = write!(details, \", Cores: {cores}\").ok();\n+                write!(details, \", Cores: {cores}\").ok();\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/file-parser/src/domain/markdown.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`70-77`: **Simplify by removing redundant `let _ =` bindings.**\n\nSimilar to the syscap_collector changes, the `let _ =` is unnecessary after `.ok()` since `Option<()>` is not `#[must_use]`.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>✨ Suggested simplification</summary>\n\n```diff\n             if let Some(ref lang) = doc.language {\n-                let _ = writeln!(header, \"language: {lang}\").ok();\n+                writeln!(header, \"language: {lang}\").ok();\n             }\n             if let Some(ref filename) = doc.meta.original_filename {\n-                let _ = writeln!(header, \"filename: {filename}\").ok();\n+                writeln!(header, \"filename: {filename}\").ok();\n             }\n             if let Some(ref content_type) = doc.meta.content_type {\n-                let _ = writeln!(header, \"content-type: {content_type}\").ok();\n+                writeln!(header, \"content-type: {content_type}\").ok();\n             }\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-db/src/options.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`805-805`: **Consider simplifying the result discard.**\n\nThe current pattern `let _ = parsed.set_password(Some(\"***\")).ok();` has redundancy—`.ok()` already converts `Result` to `Option` (discarding the error), and `let _ =` then discards the `Option`.\n\nEither of these would be cleaner:\n- `drop(parsed.set_password(Some(\"***\")));` — discards the `Result` directly\n- `parsed.set_password(Some(\"***\")).ok();` — the `.ok()` expression discards the error implicitly\n\nThat said, the current form is functionally correct and satisfies the lint.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/616#pullrequestreview-3798595888","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/616","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/616#pullrequestreview-3798595888"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/616"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-13T17:39:26Z","commit_id":"9ce5e8dfb0aef62efa8c1d0065f788e19ee54161"}]},{"source_pr_number":615,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615","source_state":"closed","source_author":"alexpitsikoulis","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #615] [Docs] Add ADR for universal lazy layer approcah to solving fragile OoP module wiring","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"docs/oop-lazy-layer-adr","pr_head_sha":"edd86e3e6cf91af1a08e3970d60dc26bc6acb6e6","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"alexpitsikoulis","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615","id":3281670154,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPaLyBs7DmlAK","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/615","number":615,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"[Docs] Add ADR for universal lazy layer approcah to solving fragile OoP module wiring","user":{"login":"alexpitsikoulis","id":50185728,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMTg1NzI4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50185728?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis","html_url":"https://github.com/alexpitsikoulis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Added ADR document detailing decision process and implementation details of a universal lazy layer in modkit.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Descriptor-driven lazy OOP clients with connection caching, backoff/retry and per-call resolution; REST default, gRPC opt-in.\n  * ClientDescriptor/ClientConfig, provider APIs, lazy client examples (e.g., LazyCalculatorClient) and macro-driven auto-registration into modules and ClientHub.\n  * Registry support for hard vs soft out-of-process dependencies and REST discovery endpoints; ServiceError → HTTP 424 mapping.\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Expanded design docs, examples, migration and phased rollout guidance.\n\n* **Tests**\n  * Added unit, integration, and E2E tests for providers, backoff, discovery, and unavailable dependencies.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-02-13T16:49:30Z","updated_at":"2026-02-24T12:16:35Z","closed_at":"2026-02-24T12:16:35Z","merged_at":"2026-02-24T12:16:35Z","merge_commit_sha":"4b4dd3f0499b1726500100d1be7e01ce31eb9cd9","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/615/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/statuses/edd86e3e6cf91af1a08e3970d60dc26bc6acb6e6","head":{"label":"alexpitsikoulis:docs/oop-lazy-layer-adr","ref":"docs/oop-lazy-layer-adr","sha":"edd86e3e6cf91af1a08e3970d60dc26bc6acb6e6","user":{"login":"alexpitsikoulis","id":50185728,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMTg1NzI4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50185728?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis","html_url":"https://github.com/alexpitsikoulis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.githu