oyment","deployment_status","discussion","discussion_comment","fork","gollum","issues","issue_comment","label","merge_group","milestone","page_build","public","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","push","registry_package","release","repository","repository_dispatch","status","watch","workflow_dispatch","workflow_run"]}}],"source_review_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2805170387","pull_request_review_id":3798360415,"id":2805170387,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6nM4DT","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,943 @@\n+# Proposal: Universal Lazy Typed Clients for OoP gRPC Modules\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+This proposal details the implementation of **universal lazy typed clients** for out-of-process (OoP) gRPC modules in ModKit. The solution eliminates fragile eager wiring during module startup, enabling graceful degradation when OoP dependencies are unavailable.\n+\n+**Chosen approach**: Universal lazy layer in ModKit + code generation macro + `clients` declarations in `#[modkit::module]`.\n+\n+## Problem Statement\n+\n+The current OoP client wiring pattern has several issues:\n+\n+1. **Eager wiring is fragile**: Consumer modules call `wire_client()` in `init()`, which fails if the OoP dependency is not yet available.\n+2. **Startup coupling**: The entire module fails to start if any OoP dependency is temporarily unavailable.\n+3. **Boilerplate duplication**: Each SDK repeats the same resolve/connect/cache logic.\n+4. **No graceful degradation**: Missing dependencies cause module-level failures instead of per-operation failures (HTTP 424).\n+\n+### Current Pattern (calculator_gateway example)\n+\n+```rust\n+// Current: Consumer must wire client manually, and it happens eagerly\n+pub async fn wire_client(hub: &ClientHub, resolver: &dyn DirectoryClient) -> Result<()> {\n+    let endpoint = resolver.resolve_grpc_service(SERVICE_NAME).await?;  // Fails if OoP not ready\n+    let client = CalculatorGrpcClient::connect(&endpoint.uri).await?;   // Fails if network issue\n+    hub.register::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>(Arc::new(client));\n+    Ok(())\n+}\n+```\n+\n+## Proposed Solution\n+\n+### Architecture Overview\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           SDK Crate (calculator-sdk)                    │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  CalculatorClientDescriptor                                             │\n+│    - MODULE_NAME: \"calculator\"                                          │\n+│    - SERVICE_NAME: \"calculator.v1.CalculatorService\"                    │\n+│    - Api: dyn CalculatorClientV1                                        │\n+│    - Availability: Optional (default)                                   │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  CalculatorGrpcClient (existing)                                        │\n+│    - Implements CalculatorClientV1                                      │\n+│    - Direct gRPC calls                                                  │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           ModKit (libs/modkit)                          │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  GrpcClientProvider<TClient>                                            │\n+│    - Lazy resolution via DirectoryClient                                │\n+│    - Connection caching with eviction on error                          │\n+│    - Backoff/rate-limiting for reconnects                               │\n+│    - Transport middleware (timeouts, keepalive, tracing)                │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  LazyGrpcClient<D: GrpcClientDescriptor>                                │\n+│    - Generated wrapper implementing D::Api                              │\n+│    - Request-scoped middleware (SecurityContext propagation)            │\n+│    - Error mapping to SDK error types                                   │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  #[modkit::module] macro extension                                      │\n+│    - clients = [CalculatorClientDescriptor]                             │\n+│    - Auto-registers LazyGrpcClient into ClientHub                       │\n+│    - Auto-augments deps with module_name                                │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                      Consumer Module (calculator_gateway)               │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  #[modkit::module(                                                      │\n+│      name = \"calculator_gateway\",                                       │\n+│      deps = [\"calculator\"],        // Soft OoP dep                      │\n+│      capabilities = [rest],                                             │\n+│      clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],            │\n+│  )]                                                                     │\n+│                                                                         │\n+│  // No wire_client() call needed!                                       │\n+│  // Client is always available from ClientHub                           │\n+│  let calc = hub.get::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>()?;                       │\n+│  calc.add(ctx, a, b).await?;  // Lazy connect on first call             │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```","path":"docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md","commit_id":"f948350f607d352064e3588bf0d83968c9100d42","original_commit_id":"f948350f607d352064e3588bf0d83968c9100d42","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Add language specifier to fenced code block.**\n\nThe ASCII diagram should have a language specifier for proper rendering. Consider using `text` or `plaintext` as the identifier.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-```\n+```text\n ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n │                           SDK Crate (calculator-sdk)                    │\n```\n</details>\n\nAs per coding guidelines, fenced code blocks should have a language specified.\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Tools</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 markdownlint-cli2 (0.20.0)</summary>\n\n[warning] 34-34: Fenced code blocks should have a language specified\n\n(MD040, fenced-code-language)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n````\nIn `@docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md` around lines 34 - 86,\nThe fenced ASCII diagram block lacks a language specifier; update the opening\nfence to include a language (e.g., change ``` to ```text) for the diagram that\nbegins with the \"SDK Crate (calculator-sdk)\" header so the diagram renders\ncorrectly; ensure the closing fence remains ``` and apply this to the fenced\nblock containing the GrpcClientProvider, LazyGrpcClient, #[modkit::module]\nsection and the Consumer Module example.\n````\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit b42514f","created_at":"2026-02-13T16:55:16Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T17:02:00Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2805170387","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2805170387"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2805170387"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2805170387/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":34,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":86,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":86,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2805170403","pull_request_review_id":3798360415,"id":2805170403,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6nM4Dj","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,943 @@\n+# Proposal: Universal Lazy Typed Clients for OoP gRPC Modules\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+This proposal details the implementation of **universal lazy typed clients** for out-of-process (OoP) gRPC modules in ModKit. The solution eliminates fragile eager wiring during module startup, enabling graceful degradation when OoP dependencies are unavailable.\n+\n+**Chosen approach**: Universal lazy layer in ModKit + code generation macro + `clients` declarations in `#[modkit::module]`.\n+\n+## Problem Statement\n+\n+The current OoP client wiring pattern has several issues:\n+\n+1. **Eager wiring is fragile**: Consumer modules call `wire_client()` in `init()`, which fails if the OoP dependency is not yet available.\n+2. **Startup coupling**: The entire module fails to start if any OoP dependency is temporarily unavailable.\n+3. **Boilerplate duplication**: Each SDK repeats the same resolve/connect/cache logic.\n+4. **No graceful degradation**: Missing dependencies cause module-level failures instead of per-operation failures (HTTP 424).\n+\n+### Current Pattern (calculator_gateway example)\n+\n+```rust\n+// Current: Consumer must wire client manually, and it happens eagerly\n+pub async fn wire_client(hub: &ClientHub, resolver: &dyn DirectoryClient) -> Result<()> {\n+    let endpoint = resolver.resolve_grpc_service(SERVICE_NAME).await?;  // Fails if OoP not ready\n+    let client = CalculatorGrpcClient::connect(&endpoint.uri).await?;   // Fails if network issue\n+    hub.register::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>(Arc::new(client));\n+    Ok(())\n+}\n+```\n+\n+## Proposed Solution\n+\n+### Architecture Overview\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           SDK Crate (calculator-sdk)                    │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  CalculatorClientDescriptor                                             │\n+│    - MODULE_NAME: \"calculator\"                                          │\n+│    - SERVICE_NAME: \"calculator.v1.CalculatorService\"                    │\n+│    - Api: dyn CalculatorClientV1                                        │\n+│    - Availability: Optional (default)                                   │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  CalculatorGrpcClient (existing)                                        │\n+│    - Implements CalculatorClientV1                                      │\n+│    - Direct gRPC calls                                                  │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           ModKit (libs/modkit)                          │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  GrpcClientProvider<TClient>                                            │\n+│    - Lazy resolution via DirectoryClient                                │\n+│    - Connection caching with eviction on error                          │\n+│    - Backoff/rate-limiting for reconnects                               │\n+│    - Transport middleware (timeouts, keepalive, tracing)                │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  LazyGrpcClient<D: GrpcClientDescriptor>                                │\n+│    - Generated wrapper implementing D::Api                              │\n+│    - Request-scoped middleware (SecurityContext propagation)            │\n+│    - Error mapping to SDK error types                                   │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  #[modkit::module] macro extension                                      │\n+│    - clients = [CalculatorClientDescriptor]                             │\n+│    - Auto-registers LazyGrpcClient into ClientHub                       │\n+│    - Auto-augments deps with module_name                                │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                      Consumer Module (calculator_gateway)               │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  #[modkit::module(                                                      │\n+│      name = \"calculator_gateway\",                                       │\n+│      deps = [\"calculator\"],        // Soft OoP dep                      │\n+│      capabilities = [rest],                                             │\n+│      clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],            │\n+│  )]                                                                     │\n+│                                                                         │\n+│  // No wire_client() call needed!                                       │\n+│  // Client is always available from ClientHub                           │\n+│  let calc = hub.get::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>()?;                       │\n+│  calc.add(ctx, a, b).await?;  // Lazy connect on first call             │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Detailed Implementation\n+\n+### Phase 1: GrpcClientDescriptor Trait (SDK-side)\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/descriptor.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Client descriptor traits for typed OoP client metadata.\n+\n+use std::time::Duration;\n+\n+/// Availability policy for OoP clients.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum ClientAvailability {\n+    /// Client is optional; operations fail gracefully with SDK error (maps to HTTP 424).\n+    #[default]\n+    Optional,\n+    /// Client is required; module readiness may depend on availability.\n+    Required,\n+}\n+\n+/// Configuration for gRPC client behavior.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct GrpcClientConfig {\n+    /// Connection timeout for initial connect.\n+    pub connect_timeout: Duration,\n+    /// Request timeout for individual RPC calls.\n+    pub request_timeout: Duration,\n+    /// Keepalive interval.\n+    pub keepalive_interval: Option<Duration>,\n+    /// Maximum backoff duration between reconnect attempts.\n+    pub max_backoff: Duration,\n+    /// Availability policy.\n+    pub availability: ClientAvailability,\n+}\n+\n+impl Default for GrpcClientConfig {\n+    fn default() -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            connect_timeout: Duration::from_secs(5),\n+            request_timeout: Duration::from_secs(30),\n+            keepalive_interval: Some(Duration::from_secs(30)),\n+            max_backoff: Duration::from_secs(60),\n+            availability: ClientAvailability::Optional,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Descriptor for a gRPC client, defined in SDK crates.\n+///\n+/// This trait binds compile-time type information to runtime metadata\n+/// needed for lazy client resolution and registration.\n+///\n+/// # Example\n+///\n+/// ```rust,ignore\n+/// pub struct CalculatorClientDescriptor;\n+///\n+/// impl GrpcClientDescriptor for CalculatorClientDescriptor {\n+///     type Api = dyn CalculatorClientV1;\n+///     type GrpcClient = CalculatorGrpcClient;\n+///\n+///     const MODULE_NAME: &'static str = \"calculator\";\n+///     const SERVICE_NAME: &'static str = \"calculator.v1.CalculatorService\";\n+///\n+///     fn config() -> GrpcClientConfig {\n+///         GrpcClientConfig::default()\n+///     }\n+/// }\n+/// ```\n+pub trait GrpcClientDescriptor: Send + Sync + 'static {\n+    /// The SDK API trait type (e.g., `dyn CalculatorClientV1`).\n+    type Api: ?Sized + Send + Sync + 'static;\n+\n+    /// The concrete gRPC client type that implements `Api`.\n+    /// Must implement `From<tonic::transport::Channel>` or have a `new(Channel)` constructor.\n+    type GrpcClient: Send + Sync + 'static;\n+\n+    /// Module name for dependency graph (used in `deps`).\n+    const MODULE_NAME: &'static str;\n+\n+    /// gRPC service name for Directory resolution.\n+    const SERVICE_NAME: &'static str;\n+\n+    /// Client configuration (timeouts, backoff, availability).\n+    fn config() -> GrpcClientConfig {\n+        GrpcClientConfig::default()\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Phase 2: GrpcClientProvider (ModKit Core)\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/grpc_provider.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Universal lazy gRPC client provider.\n+//!\n+//! Encapsulates endpoint resolution, connection management, caching,\n+//! and reconnection logic for any gRPC client.\n+\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+use std::time::{Duration, Instant};\n+\n+use parking_lot::RwLock;\n+use tokio::sync::Semaphore;\n+use tonic::transport::Channel;\n+\n+use crate::client_hub::ClientHub;\n+use crate::directory::DirectoryClient;\n+use crate::clients::descriptor::GrpcClientConfig;\n+\n+/// Error type for provider operations.\n+#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\n+pub enum GrpcProviderError {\n+    #[error(\"service not found in directory: {service_name}\")]\n+    ServiceNotFound { service_name: &'static str },\n+\n+    #[error(\"connection failed: {0}\")]\n+    ConnectionFailed(#[source] tonic::transport::Error),\n+\n+    #[error(\"directory resolution failed: {0}\")]\n+    DirectoryError(#[source] anyhow::Error),\n+\n+    #[error(\"service temporarily unavailable (backoff active)\")]\n+    Backoff { retry_after: Duration },\n+}\n+\n+/// Cached connection state.\n+struct CachedConnection {\n+    channel: Channel,\n+    connected_at: Instant,\n+}\n+\n+/// Internal state for the provider.\n+struct ProviderState {\n+    cached: Option<CachedConnection>,\n+    last_failure: Option<Instant>,\n+    failure_count: u32,\n+}\n+\n+/// Universal lazy gRPC client provider.\n+///\n+/// This provider handles:\n+/// - Lazy endpoint resolution via DirectoryClient\n+/// - Connection caching with automatic eviction on errors\n+/// - Exponential backoff for reconnection attempts\n+/// - Rate limiting to prevent thundering herds\n+pub struct GrpcClientProvider {\n+    service_name: &'static str,\n+    config: GrpcClientConfig,\n+    hub: Arc<ClientHub>,\n+    state: RwLock<ProviderState>,\n+    connect_semaphore: Semaphore,\n+}\n+\n+impl GrpcClientProvider {\n+    /// Create a new provider for the given service.\n+    pub fn new(\n+        service_name: &'static str,\n+        config: GrpcClientConfig,\n+        hub: Arc<ClientHub>,\n+    ) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            service_name,\n+            config,\n+            hub,\n+            state: RwLock::new(ProviderState {\n+                cached: None,\n+                last_failure: None,\n+                failure_count: 0,\n+            }),\n+            connect_semaphore: Semaphore::new(1),\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Get a connected channel, resolving and connecting lazily.\n+    ///\n+    /// Returns a cached channel if available, otherwise resolves the endpoint\n+    /// and establishes a new connection.\n+    pub async fn get_channel(&self) -> Result<Channel, GrpcProviderError> {\n+        // Fast path: return cached connection\n+        {\n+            let state = self.state.read();\n+            if let Some(ref cached) = state.cached {\n+                return Ok(cached.channel.clone());\n+            }\n+\n+            // Check backoff\n+            if let Some(last_failure) = state.last_failure {\n+                let backoff = self.calculate_backoff(state.failure_count);\n+                let elapsed = last_failure.elapsed();\n+                if elapsed < backoff {\n+                    return Err(GrpcProviderError::Backoff {\n+                        retry_after: backoff - elapsed,\n+                    });\n+                }\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        // Slow path: acquire semaphore and connect\n+        let _permit = self.connect_semaphore.acquire().await.unwrap();\n+\n+        // Double-check after acquiring semaphore\n+        {\n+            let state = self.state.read();\n+            if let Some(ref cached) = state.cached {\n+                return Ok(cached.channel.clone());\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        // Resolve and connect\n+        self.connect_internal().await\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Evict the cached connection (call on transport errors).\n+    pub fn evict(&self) {\n+        let mut state = self.state.write();\n+        state.cached = None;\n+        state.last_failure = Some(Instant::now());\n+        state.failure_count = state.failure_count.saturating_add(1);\n+        tracing::warn!(\n+            service = self.service_name,\n+            failure_count = state.failure_count,\n+            \"Evicted cached gRPC connection\"\n+        );\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Reset failure state (call on successful RPC).\n+    pub fn reset_failures(&self) {\n+        let mut state = self.state.write();\n+        if state.failure_count > 0 {\n+            state.failure_count = 0;\n+            state.last_failure = None;\n+            tracing::debug!(service = self.service_name, \"Reset failure state after success\");\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    async fn connect_internal(&self) -> Result<Channel, GrpcProviderError> {\n+        // Resolve endpoint from DirectoryClient\n+        let directory = self\n+            .hub\n+            .get::<dyn DirectoryClient>()\n+            .map_err(|e| GrpcProviderError::DirectoryError(e.into()))?;\n+\n+        let endpoint = directory\n+            .resolve_grpc_service(self.service_name)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(|e| GrpcProviderError::DirectoryError(e))?;\n+\n+        tracing::debug!(\n+            service = self.service_name,\n+            uri = %endpoint.uri,\n+            \"Resolved service endpoint\"\n+        );\n+\n+        // Connect with configured timeouts\n+        let channel = Channel::from_shared(endpoint.uri.clone())\n+            .map_err(|e| GrpcProviderError::ConnectionFailed(e.into()))?\n+            .connect_timeout(self.config.connect_timeout)\n+            .timeout(self.config.request_timeout);\n+\n+        let channel = if let Some(keepalive) = self.config.keepalive_interval {\n+            channel\n+                .http2_keep_alive_interval(keepalive)\n+                .keep_alive_timeout(Duration::from_secs(20))\n+        } else {\n+            channel\n+        };\n+\n+        let channel = channel\n+            .connect()\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(GrpcProviderError::ConnectionFailed)?;\n+\n+        // Cache the connection\n+        {\n+            let mut state = self.state.write();\n+            state.cached = Some(CachedConnection {\n+                channel: channel.clone(),\n+                connected_at: Instant::now(),\n+            });\n+            state.failure_count = 0;\n+            state.last_failure = None;\n+        }\n+\n+        tracing::info!(\n+            service = self.service_name,\n+            uri = %endpoint.uri,\n+            \"Established gRPC connection\"\n+        );\n+\n+        Ok(channel)\n+    }\n+\n+    fn calculate_backoff(&self, failure_count: u32) -> Duration {\n+        let base = Duration::from_millis(100);\n+        let max = self.config.max_backoff;\n+        let backoff = base.saturating_mul(2u32.saturating_pow(failure_count.min(10)));\n+        backoff.min(max)\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Phase 3: LazyGrpcClient Wrapper (Generated or Manual)\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/lazy_client.rs`\n+\n+For the initial implementation, we provide a manual wrapper pattern. The macro generation can be added later.\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Lazy gRPC client wrapper that implements SDK traits.\n+//!\n+//! This wrapper delegates to GrpcClientProvider for connection management\n+//! and handles SecurityContext propagation.\n+\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+\n+use crate::clients::grpc_provider::{GrpcClientProvider, GrpcProviderError};\n+use crate::clients::descriptor::GrpcClientDescriptor;\n+\n+/// Error returned by lazy clients when the OoP dependency is unavailable.\n+#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\n+pub enum LazyClientError {\n+    #[error(\"service unavailable: {service_name}\")]\n+    Unavailable {\n+        service_name: &'static str,\n+        #[source]\n+        source: GrpcProviderError,\n+    },\n+\n+    #[error(\"RPC failed: {0}\")]\n+    RpcFailed(#[source] tonic::Status),\n+}\n+\n+impl LazyClientError {\n+    /// Returns true if this error indicates the service is temporarily unavailable.\n+    /// REST handlers should map this to HTTP 424 Failed Dependency.\n+    pub fn is_dependency_unavailable(&self) -> bool {\n+        matches!(self, LazyClientError::Unavailable { .. })\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Macro to generate a lazy client wrapper for a GrpcClientDescriptor.\n+///\n+/// This generates a struct that:\n+/// - Implements the SDK API trait\n+/// - Uses GrpcClientProvider for lazy connection management\n+/// - Propagates SecurityContext via gRPC metadata\n+/// - Maps transport errors to SDK error types\n+///\n+/// # Example\n+///\n+/// ```rust,ignore\n+/// modkit::lazy_grpc_client! {\n+///     /// Lazy client for Calculator service.\n+///     pub struct LazyCalculatorClient for calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor {\n+///         // Method implementations are generated based on the trait\n+///     }\n+/// }\n+/// ```\n+#[macro_export]\n+macro_rules! lazy_grpc_client {\n+    (\n+        $(#[$meta:meta])*\n+        $vis:vis struct $name:ident for $descriptor:ty {\n+            $(\n+                async fn $method:ident(\n+                    &self,\n+                    ctx: &SecurityContext\n+                    $(, $arg:ident : $arg_ty:ty)*\n+                ) -> Result<$ret:ty, $err:ty> $body:block\n+            )*\n+        }\n+    ) => {\n+        $(#[$meta])*\n+        $vis struct $name {\n+            provider: std::sync::Arc<$crate::clients::grpc_provider::GrpcClientProvider>,\n+        }\n+\n+        impl $name {\n+            pub fn new(provider: std::sync::Arc<$crate::clients::grpc_provider::GrpcClientProvider>) -> Self {\n+                Self { provider }\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        // Trait implementation would be generated here\n+        // For now, this is a placeholder showing the pattern\n+    };\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Phase 4: SDK Crate Updates (calculator-sdk example)\n+\n+**Location**: `examples/oop-modules/calculator/calculator-sdk/src/descriptor.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Client descriptor for Calculator SDK.\n+\n+use modkit::clients::descriptor::{GrpcClientDescriptor, GrpcClientConfig, ClientAvailability};\n+use crate::api::CalculatorClientV1;\n+use crate::client::CalculatorGrpcClient;\n+\n+/// Descriptor for the Calculator gRPC client.\n+///\n+/// Used by consumer modules to declare their dependency on the Calculator service\n+/// via `#[modkit::module(clients = [CalculatorClientDescriptor])]`.\n+pub struct CalculatorClientDescriptor;\n+\n+impl GrpcClientDescriptor for CalculatorClientDescriptor {\n+    type Api = dyn CalculatorClientV1;\n+    type GrpcClient = CalculatorGrpcClient;\n+\n+    const MODULE_NAME: &'static str = \"calculator\";\n+    const SERVICE_NAME: &'static str = crate::SERVICE_NAME;\n+\n+    fn config() -> GrpcClientConfig {\n+        GrpcClientConfig {\n+            availability: ClientAvailability::Optional,\n+            ..Default::default()\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Updated SDK lib.rs**:\n+\n+```rust\n+// ... existing exports ...\n+\n+// Client descriptor for lazy wiring\n+mod descriptor;\n+pub use descriptor::CalculatorClientDescriptor;\n+```\n+\n+### Phase 5: Lazy Client Implementation for Calculator\n+\n+**Location**: `examples/oop-modules/calculator/calculator-sdk/src/lazy_client.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Lazy gRPC client for Calculator service.\n+//!\n+//! This client wraps GrpcClientProvider and implements CalculatorClientV1,\n+//! providing lazy connection management and graceful degradation.\n+\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use modkit::clients::grpc_provider::GrpcClientProvider;\n+use modkit_security::SecurityContext;\n+use tonic::metadata::MetadataMap;\n+\n+use crate::api::{CalculatorClientV1, CalculatorError};\n+use crate::client::CalculatorGrpcClient;\n+use crate::proto;\n+\n+/// Lazy client for Calculator service.\n+///\n+/// This client:\n+/// - Resolves the Calculator endpoint lazily on first call\n+/// - Caches the connection for subsequent calls\n+/// - Handles reconnection with backoff on failures\n+/// - Propagates SecurityContext via gRPC metadata\n+pub struct LazyCalculatorClient {\n+    provider: Arc<GrpcClientProvider>,\n+}\n+\n+impl LazyCalculatorClient {\n+    /// Create a new lazy client with the given provider.\n+    pub fn new(provider: Arc<GrpcClientProvider>) -> Self {\n+        Self { provider }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl CalculatorClientV1 for LazyCalculatorClient {\n+    async fn add(&self, ctx: &SecurityContext, a: i64, b: i64) -> Result<i64, CalculatorError> {\n+        // Get channel (lazy connect)\n+        let channel = self.provider.get_channel().await.map_err(|e| {\n+            tracing::warn!(error = %e, \"Calculator service unavailable\");\n+            CalculatorError::Unavailable {\n+                message: format!(\"Calculator service unavailable: {}\", e),\n+            }\n+        })?;\n+\n+        // Create client and attach security context\n+        let mut client = proto::calculator_service_client::CalculatorServiceClient::new(channel);\n+\n+        // Propagate security context via metadata\n+        let mut request = tonic::Request::new(proto::AddRequest { a, b });\n+        inject_security_context(ctx, request.metadata_mut());\n+\n+        // Make the call\n+        let response = client.add(request).await.map_err(|status| {\n+            // Evict connection on transport errors\n+            if is_transport_error(&status) {\n+                self.provider.evict();\n+            }\n+            map_status_to_error(status)\n+        })?;\n+\n+        // Reset failure state on success\n+        self.provider.reset_failures();\n+\n+        Ok(response.into_inner().result)\n+    }\n+\n+    async fn subtract(&self, ctx: &SecurityContext, a: i64, b: i64) -> Result<i64, CalculatorError> {\n+        let channel = self.provider.get_channel().await.map_err(|e| {\n+            CalculatorError::Unavailable {\n+                message: format!(\"Calculator service unavailable: {}\", e),\n+            }\n+        })?;\n+\n+        let mut client = proto::calculator_service_client::CalculatorServiceClient::new(channel);\n+        let mut request = tonic::Request::new(proto::SubtractRequest { a, b });\n+        inject_security_context(ctx, request.metadata_mut());\n+\n+        let response = client.subtract(request).await.map_err(|status| {\n+            if is_transport_error(&status) {\n+                self.provider.evict();\n+            }\n+            map_status_to_error(status)\n+        })?;\n+\n+        self.provider.reset_failures();\n+        Ok(response.into_inner().result)\n+    }\n+\n+    // ... other methods follow the same pattern ...\n+}\n+\n+/// Inject SecurityContext into gRPC metadata.\n+fn inject_security_context(ctx: &SecurityContext, metadata: &mut MetadataMap) {\n+    if let Some(tenant_id) = ctx.tenant_id() {\n+        if let Ok(value) = tenant_id.to_string().parse() {\n+            metadata.insert(\"x-tenant-id\", value);\n+        }\n+    }\n+    if let Some(user_id) = ctx.user_id() {\n+        if let Ok(value) = user_id.to_string().parse() {\n+            metadata.insert(\"x-user-id\", value);\n+        }\n+    }\n+    // Add other context fields as needed\n+}\n+\n+/// Check if the error is a transport-level error (connection lost, etc.)\n+fn is_transport_error(status: &tonic::Status) -> bool {\n+    matches!(\n+        status.code(),\n+        tonic::Code::Unavailable | tonic::Code::Unknown | tonic::Code::Internal\n+    )\n+}\n+\n+/// Map tonic Status to SDK error type.\n+fn map_status_to_error(status: tonic::Status) -> CalculatorError {\n+    match status.code() {\n+        tonic::Code::InvalidArgument => CalculatorError::InvalidArgument {\n+            message: status.message().to_string(),\n+        },\n+        tonic::Code::NotFound => CalculatorError::NotFound {\n+            message: status.message().to_string(),\n+        },\n+        tonic::Code::Unavailable => CalculatorError::Unavailable {\n+            message: status.message().to_string(),\n+        },\n+        _ => CalculatorError::Internal {\n+            message: status.message().to_string(),\n+        },\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Phase 6: Module Macro Extension\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit-macros/src/module.rs` (extension)\n+\n+The `#[modkit::module]` macro will be extended to support `clients = [...]`:\n+\n+```rust\n+// Conceptual macro expansion for:\n+// #[modkit::module(\n+//     name = \"calculator_gateway\",\n+//     deps = [\"calculator\"],\n+//     capabilities = [rest],\n+//     clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],\n+// )]\n+\n+// Generated code (simplified):\n+impl CalculatorGateway {\n+    fn __register_lazy_clients(ctx: &ModuleCtx) -> anyhow::Result<()> {\n+        use modkit::clients::descriptor::GrpcClientDescriptor;\n+\n+        // For each descriptor in `clients`:\n+        {\n+            type D = calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor;\n+            let config = D::config();\n+            let provider = std::sync::Arc::new(\n+                modkit::clients::grpc_provider::GrpcClientProvider::new(\n+                    D::SERVICE_NAME,\n+                    config,\n+                    ctx.client_hub(),\n+                )\n+            );\n+            let lazy_client: std::sync::Arc<<D as GrpcClientDescriptor>::Api> =\n+                std::sync::Arc::new(calculator_sdk::LazyCalculatorClient::new(provider));\n+            ctx.client_hub().register::<<D as GrpcClientDescriptor>::Api>(lazy_client);\n+        }\n+\n+        Ok(())\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+// The macro also ensures deps includes the module_name from each descriptor\n+// (validated at compile time or augmented automatically)\n+```\n+\n+### Phase 7: Registry Extension for Soft OoP Deps\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/registry.rs` (extension)\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Extended dependency resolution for OoP modules.\n+impl ModuleRegistry {\n+    /// Resolve dependencies, treating unknown deps as potential OoP soft deps.\n+    ///\n+    /// - If dep is a registered core module → hard dep (topo-sort)\n+    /// - If dep is configured as `runtime.type = oop` → soft dep (no topo-sort)\n+    /// - Otherwise → error (unknown dependency)\n+    pub fn resolve_dependencies_with_oop(\n+        &self,\n+        module_name: &str,\n+        deps: &[&str],\n+        config: &AppConfig,\n+    ) -> Result<ResolvedDeps, RegistryError> {\n+        let mut hard_deps = Vec::new();\n+        let mut soft_deps = Vec::new();\n+\n+        for dep in deps {\n+            if self.has_module(dep) {\n+                // Known in-process module\n+                hard_deps.push(*dep);\n+            } else if config.is_oop_module(dep) {\n+                // OoP module declared in config\n+                soft_deps.push(*dep);\n+            } else {\n+                return Err(RegistryError::UnknownDependency {\n+                    module: module_name.to_string(),\n+                    dependency: dep.to_string(),\n+                });\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        Ok(ResolvedDeps { hard_deps, soft_deps })\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Result of dependency resolution.\n+pub struct ResolvedDeps {\n+    /// Hard dependencies (in-process, participate in topo-sort).\n+    pub hard_deps: Vec<&'static str>,\n+    /// Soft dependencies (OoP, do not block startup).\n+    pub soft_deps: Vec<&'static str>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Consumer Module Changes (calculator_gateway)\n+\n+### Before (current pattern)\n+\n+```rust\n+#[modkit::module(\n+    name = \"calculator_gateway\",\n+    capabilities = [rest],\n+    deps = [\"calculator\"]\n+)]\n+pub struct CalculatorGateway;\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl modkit::Module for CalculatorGateway {\n+    async fn init(&self, ctx: &ModuleCtx) -> Result<()> {\n+        // Must wire client manually - FAILS if calculator not ready\n+        let directory = ctx.client_hub().get::<dyn DirectoryClient>()?;\n+        calculator_sdk::wire_client(ctx.client_hub(), &*directory).await?;\n+        // ...\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### After (proposed pattern)\n+\n+```rust\n+#[modkit::module(\n+    name = \"calculator_gateway\",\n+    capabilities = [rest],\n+    deps = [\"calculator\"],  // Soft OoP dep (validated via config)\n+    clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],  // NEW\n+)]\n+pub struct CalculatorGateway;\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl modkit::Module for CalculatorGateway {\n+    async fn init(&self, ctx: &ModuleCtx) -> Result<()> {\n+        // No wire_client() needed!\n+        // LazyCalculatorClient is auto-registered by the macro.\n+        let service = Arc::new(Service::new(ctx.client_hub()));\n+        ctx.client_hub().register::<Service>(service);\n+        Ok(())\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+// In domain service - unchanged!\n+impl Service {\n+    pub async fn add(&self, ctx: &SecurityContext, a: i64, b: i64) -> Result<i64, ServiceError> {\n+        let calculator = self.client_hub.get::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>()?;\n+        // Lazy connect happens here on first call\n+        calculator.add(ctx, a, b).await.map_err(|e| {\n+            // CalculatorError::Unavailable maps to HTTP 424\n+            ServiceError::RemoteError(e.to_string())\n+        })\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Error Handling and HTTP 424\n+\n+The lazy client returns `CalculatorError::Unavailable` when the OoP service cannot be reached. REST handlers should map this to HTTP 424 Failed Dependency:\n+\n+```rust\n+// In REST handler error mapping\n+impl From<ServiceError> for Problem {\n+    fn from(err: ServiceError) -> Self {\n+        match err {\n+            ServiceError::RemoteError(msg) if msg.contains(\"unavailable\") => {\n+                Problem::failed_dependency()\n+                    .with_detail(msg)\n+            }\n+            ServiceError::RemoteError(msg) => {\n+                Problem::bad_gateway()\n+                    .with_detail(msg)\n+            }\n+            ServiceError::Internal(msg) => {\n+                Problem::internal_server_error()\n+                    .with_detail(msg)\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+```","path":"docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md","commit_id":"edd86e3e6cf91af1a08e3970d60dc26bc6acb6e6","original_commit_id":"f948350f607d352064e3588bf0d83968c9100d42","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Use typed error matching instead of string comparison.**\n\nThe error mapping uses `msg.contains(\"unavailable\")` to detect dependency failures, but the `LazyClientError` type provides an `is_dependency_unavailable()` method (defined at line 428). Relying on string matching is fragile and error-prone.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Proposed fix using typed errors</summary>\n\n```diff\n+// Assume ServiceError variants are updated to preserve error type information\n+// or CalculatorError variants are checked directly\n+\n impl From<ServiceError> for Problem {\n     fn from(err: ServiceError) -> Self {\n         match err {\n-            ServiceError::RemoteError(msg) if msg.contains(\"unavailable\") => {\n+            ServiceError::DependencyUnavailable(msg) => {\n                 Problem::failed_dependency()\n                     .with_detail(msg)\n             }\n             ServiceError::RemoteError(msg) => {\n                 Problem::bad_gateway()\n                     .with_detail(msg)\n             }\n             ServiceError::Internal(msg) => {\n                 Problem::internal_server_error()\n                     .with_detail(msg)\n             }\n         }\n     }\n }\n```\n\nAlternatively, if `CalculatorError` is available at the REST layer:\n\n```rust\n// When converting CalculatorError -> ServiceError -> Problem\nmatch calculator_error {\n    CalculatorError::Unavailable { .. } => ServiceError::DependencyUnavailable,\n    // ... other variants\n}\n```\n\nThis ensures type-safe error classification without string parsing.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md` around lines 823 - 843,\nThe ServiceError -> Problem conversion currently detects dependency failures by\nstring matching inside the RemoteError message; instead use the typed error\nclassifier (e.g., call the LazyClientError::is_dependency_unavailable() helper\nor map CalculatorError::Unavailable earlier) so the From<ServiceError> for\nProblem match inspects the underlying error type/variant rather than\nmsg.contains(\"unavailable\"); update the ServiceError::RemoteError arm to check\nthe wrapped error's is_dependency_unavailable() (or add a new\nServiceError::DependencyUnavailable variant upstream and match that) and then\nreturn Problem::failed_dependency().with_detail(...) for that case, keeping\nother RemoteError/Internal branches unchanged.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit b42514f","created_at":"2026-02-13T16:55:16Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T17:01:58Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2805170403","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2805170403"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2805170403"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2805170403/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":1676,"original_start_line":823,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":1707,"original_line":843,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":843,"position":1707,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2805170411","pull_request_review_id":3798360415,"id":2805170411,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6nM4Dr","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,943 @@\n+# Proposal: Universal Lazy Typed Clients for OoP gRPC Modules\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+This proposal details the implementation of **universal lazy typed clients** for out-of-process (OoP) gRPC modules in ModKit. The solution eliminates fragile eager wiring during module startup, enabling graceful degradation when OoP dependencies are unavailable.\n+\n+**Chosen approach**: Universal lazy layer in ModKit + code generation macro + `clients` declarations in `#[modkit::module]`.\n+\n+## Problem Statement\n+\n+The current OoP client wiring pattern has several issues:\n+\n+1. **Eager wiring is fragile**: Consumer modules call `wire_client()` in `init()`, which fails if the OoP dependency is not yet available.\n+2. **Startup coupling**: The entire module fails to start if any OoP dependency is temporarily unavailable.\n+3. **Boilerplate duplication**: Each SDK repeats the same resolve/connect/cache logic.\n+4. **No graceful degradation**: Missing dependencies cause module-level failures instead of per-operation failures (HTTP 424).\n+\n+### Current Pattern (calculator_gateway example)\n+\n+```rust\n+// Current: Consumer must wire client manually, and it happens eagerly\n+pub async fn wire_client(hub: &ClientHub, resolver: &dyn DirectoryClient) -> Result<()> {\n+    let endpoint = resolver.resolve_grpc_service(SERVICE_NAME).await?;  // Fails if OoP not ready\n+    let client = CalculatorGrpcClient::connect(&endpoint.uri).await?;   // Fails if network issue\n+    hub.register::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>(Arc::new(client));\n+    Ok(())\n+}\n+```\n+\n+## Proposed Solution\n+\n+### Architecture Overview\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           SDK Crate (calculator-sdk)                    │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  CalculatorClientDescriptor                                             │\n+│    - MODULE_NAME: \"calculator\"                                          │\n+│    - SERVICE_NAME: \"calculator.v1.CalculatorService\"                    │\n+│    - Api: dyn CalculatorClientV1                                        │\n+│    - Availability: Optional (default)                                   │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  CalculatorGrpcClient (existing)                                        │\n+│    - Implements CalculatorClientV1                                      │\n+│    - Direct gRPC calls                                                  │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           ModKit (libs/modkit)                          │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  GrpcClientProvider<TClient>                                            │\n+│    - Lazy resolution via DirectoryClient                                │\n+│    - Connection caching with eviction on error                          │\n+│    - Backoff/rate-limiting for reconnects                               │\n+│    - Transport middleware (timeouts, keepalive, tracing)                │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  LazyGrpcClient<D: GrpcClientDescriptor>                                │\n+│    - Generated wrapper implementing D::Api                              │\n+│    - Request-scoped middleware (SecurityContext propagation)            │\n+│    - Error mapping to SDK error types                                   │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  #[modkit::module] macro extension                                      │\n+│    - clients = [CalculatorClientDescriptor]                             │\n+│    - Auto-registers LazyGrpcClient into ClientHub                       │\n+│    - Auto-augments deps with module_name                                │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                      Consumer Module (calculator_gateway)               │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  #[modkit::module(                                                      │\n+│      name = \"calculator_gateway\",                                       │\n+│      deps = [\"calculator\"],        // Soft OoP dep                      │\n+│      capabilities = [rest],                                             │\n+│      clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],            │\n+│  )]                                                                     │\n+│                                                                         │\n+│  // No wire_client() call needed!                                       │\n+│  // Client is always available from ClientHub                           │\n+│  let calc = hub.get::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>()?;                       │\n+│  calc.add(ctx, a, b).await?;  // Lazy connect on first call             │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Detailed Implementation\n+\n+### Phase 1: GrpcClientDescriptor Trait (SDK-side)\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/descriptor.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Client descriptor traits for typed OoP client metadata.\n+\n+use std::time::Duration;\n+\n+/// Availability policy for OoP clients.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum ClientAvailability {\n+    /// Client is optional; operations fail gracefully with SDK error (maps to HTTP 424).\n+    #[default]\n+    Optional,\n+    /// Client is required; module readiness may depend on availability.\n+    Required,\n+}\n+\n+/// Configuration for gRPC client behavior.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct GrpcClientConfig {\n+    /// Connection timeout for initial connect.\n+    pub connect_timeout: Duration,\n+    /// Request timeout for individual RPC calls.\n+    pub request_timeout: Duration,\n+    /// Keepalive interval.\n+    pub keepalive_interval: Option<Duration>,\n+    /// Maximum backoff duration between reconnect attempts.\n+    pub max_backoff: Duration,\n+    /// Availability policy.\n+    pub availability: ClientAvailability,\n+}\n+\n+impl Default for GrpcClientConfig {\n+    fn default() -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            connect_timeout: Duration::from_secs(5),\n+            request_timeout: Duration::from_secs(30),\n+            keepalive_interval: Some(Duration::from_secs(30)),\n+            max_backoff: Duration::from_secs(60),\n+            availability: ClientAvailability::Optional,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Descriptor for a gRPC client, defined in SDK crates.\n+///\n+/// This trait binds compile-time type information to runtime metadata\n+/// needed for lazy client resolution and registration.\n+///\n+/// # Example\n+///\n+/// ```rust,ignore\n+/// pub struct CalculatorClientDescriptor;\n+///\n+/// impl GrpcClientDescriptor for CalculatorClientDescriptor {\n+///     type Api = dyn CalculatorClientV1;\n+///     type GrpcClient = CalculatorGrpcClient;\n+///\n+///     const MODULE_NAME: &'static str = \"calculator\";\n+///     const SERVICE_NAME: &'static str = \"calculator.v1.CalculatorService\";\n+///\n+///     fn config() -> GrpcClientConfig {\n+///         GrpcClientConfig::default()\n+///     }\n+/// }\n+/// ```\n+pub trait GrpcClientDescriptor: Send + Sync + 'static {\n+    /// The SDK API trait type (e.g., `dyn CalculatorClientV1`).\n+    type Api: ?Sized + Send + Sync + 'static;\n+\n+    /// The concrete gRPC client type that implements `Api`.\n+    /// Must implement `From<tonic::transport::Channel>` or have a `new(Channel)` constructor.\n+    type GrpcClient: Send + Sync + 'static;\n+\n+    /// Module name for dependency graph (used in `deps`).\n+    const MODULE_NAME: &'static str;\n+\n+    /// gRPC service name for Directory resolution.\n+    const SERVICE_NAME: &'static str;\n+\n+    /// Client configuration (timeouts, backoff, availability).\n+    fn config() -> GrpcClientConfig {\n+        GrpcClientConfig::default()\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Phase 2: GrpcClientProvider (ModKit Core)\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/grpc_provider.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Universal lazy gRPC client provider.\n+//!\n+//! Encapsulates endpoint resolution, connection management, caching,\n+//! and reconnection logic for any gRPC client.\n+\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+use std::time::{Duration, Instant};\n+\n+use parking_lot::RwLock;\n+use tokio::sync::Semaphore;\n+use tonic::transport::Channel;\n+\n+use crate::client_hub::ClientHub;\n+use crate::directory::DirectoryClient;\n+use crate::clients::descriptor::GrpcClientConfig;\n+\n+/// Error type for provider operations.\n+#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\n+pub enum GrpcProviderError {\n+    #[error(\"service not found in directory: {service_name}\")]\n+    ServiceNotFound { service_name: &'static str },\n+\n+    #[error(\"connection failed: {0}\")]\n+    ConnectionFailed(#[source] tonic::transport::Error),\n+\n+    #[error(\"directory resolution failed: {0}\")]\n+    DirectoryError(#[source] anyhow::Error),\n+\n+    #[error(\"service temporarily unavailable (backoff active)\")]\n+    Backoff { retry_after: Duration },\n+}\n+\n+/// Cached connection state.\n+struct CachedConnection {\n+    channel: Channel,\n+    connected_at: Instant,\n+}\n+\n+/// Internal state for the provider.\n+struct ProviderState {\n+    cached: Option<CachedConnection>,\n+    last_failure: Option<Instant>,\n+    failure_count: u32,\n+}\n+\n+/// Universal lazy gRPC client provider.\n+///\n+/// This provider handles:\n+/// - Lazy endpoint resolution via DirectoryClient\n+/// - Connection caching with automatic eviction on errors\n+/// - Exponential backoff for reconnection attempts\n+/// - Rate limiting to prevent thundering herds\n+pub struct GrpcClientProvider {\n+    service_name: &'static str,\n+    config: GrpcClientConfig,\n+    hub: Arc<ClientHub>,\n+    state: RwLock<ProviderState>,\n+    connect_semaphore: Semaphore,\n+}\n+\n+impl GrpcClientProvider {\n+    /// Create a new provider for the given service.\n+    pub fn new(\n+        service_name: &'static str,\n+        config: GrpcClientConfig,\n+        hub: Arc<ClientHub>,\n+    ) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            service_name,\n+            config,\n+            hub,\n+            state: RwLock::new(ProviderState {\n+                cached: None,\n+                last_failure: None,\n+                failure_count: 0,\n+            }),\n+            connect_semaphore: Semaphore::new(1),\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Get a connected channel, resolving and connecting lazily.\n+    ///\n+    /// Returns a cached channel if available, otherwise resolves the endpoint\n+    /// and establishes a new connection.\n+    pub async fn get_channel(&self) -> Result<Channel, GrpcProviderError> {\n+        // Fast path: return cached connection\n+        {\n+            let state = self.state.read();\n+            if let Some(ref cached) = state.cached {\n+                return Ok(cached.channel.clone());\n+            }\n+\n+            // Check backoff\n+            if let Some(last_failure) = state.last_failure {\n+                let backoff = self.calculate_backoff(state.failure_count);\n+                let elapsed = last_failure.elapsed();\n+                if elapsed < backoff {\n+                    return Err(GrpcProviderError::Backoff {\n+                        retry_after: backoff - elapsed,\n+                    });\n+                }\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        // Slow path: acquire semaphore and connect\n+        let _permit = self.connect_semaphore.acquire().await.unwrap();\n+\n+        // Double-check after acquiring semaphore\n+        {\n+            let state = self.state.read();\n+            if let Some(ref cached) = state.cached {\n+                return Ok(cached.channel.clone());\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        // Resolve and connect\n+        self.connect_internal().await\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Evict the cached connection (call on transport errors).\n+    pub fn evict(&self) {\n+        let mut state = self.state.write();\n+        state.cached = None;\n+        state.last_failure = Some(Instant::now());\n+        state.failure_count = state.failure_count.saturating_add(1);\n+        tracing::warn!(\n+            service = self.service_name,\n+            failure_count = state.failure_count,\n+            \"Evicted cached gRPC connection\"\n+        );\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Reset failure state (call on successful RPC).\n+    pub fn reset_failures(&self) {\n+        let mut state = self.state.write();\n+        if state.failure_count > 0 {\n+            state.failure_count = 0;\n+            state.last_failure = None;\n+            tracing::debug!(service = self.service_name, \"Reset failure state after success\");\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    async fn connect_internal(&self) -> Result<Channel, GrpcProviderError> {\n+        // Resolve endpoint from DirectoryClient\n+        let directory = self\n+            .hub\n+            .get::<dyn DirectoryClient>()\n+            .map_err(|e| GrpcProviderError::DirectoryError(e.into()))?;\n+\n+        let endpoint = directory\n+            .resolve_grpc_service(self.service_name)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(|e| GrpcProviderError::DirectoryError(e))?;\n+\n+        tracing::debug!(\n+            service = self.service_name,\n+            uri = %endpoint.uri,\n+            \"Resolved service endpoint\"\n+        );\n+\n+        // Connect with configured timeouts\n+        let channel = Channel::from_shared(endpoint.uri.clone())\n+            .map_err(|e| GrpcProviderError::ConnectionFailed(e.into()))?\n+            .connect_timeout(self.config.connect_timeout)\n+            .timeout(self.config.request_timeout);\n+\n+        let channel = if let Some(keepalive) = self.config.keepalive_interval {\n+            channel\n+                .http2_keep_alive_interval(keepalive)\n+                .keep_alive_timeout(Duration::from_secs(20))\n+        } else {\n+            channel\n+        };\n+\n+        let channel = channel\n+            .connect()\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(GrpcProviderError::ConnectionFailed)?;\n+\n+        // Cache the connection\n+        {\n+            let mut state = self.state.write();\n+            state.cached = Some(CachedConnection {\n+                channel: channel.clone(),\n+                connected_at: Instant::now(),\n+            });\n+            state.failure_count = 0;\n+            state.last_failure = None;\n+        }\n+\n+        tracing::info!(\n+            service = self.service_name,\n+            uri = %endpoint.uri,\n+            \"Established gRPC connection\"\n+        );\n+\n+        Ok(channel)\n+    }\n+\n+    fn calculate_backoff(&self, failure_count: u32) -> Duration {\n+        let base = Duration::from_millis(100);\n+        let max = self.config.max_backoff;\n+        let backoff = base.saturating_mul(2u32.saturating_pow(failure_count.min(10)));\n+        backoff.min(max)\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Phase 3: LazyGrpcClient Wrapper (Generated or Manual)\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/lazy_client.rs`\n+\n+For the initial implementation, we provide a manual wrapper pattern. The macro generation can be added later.\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Lazy gRPC client wrapper that implements SDK traits.\n+//!\n+//! This wrapper delegates to GrpcClientProvider for connection management\n+//! and handles SecurityContext propagation.\n+\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+\n+use crate::clients::grpc_provider::{GrpcClientProvider, GrpcProviderError};\n+use crate::clients::descriptor::GrpcClientDescriptor;\n+\n+/// Error returned by lazy clients when the OoP dependency is unavailable.\n+#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\n+pub enum LazyClientError {\n+    #[error(\"service unavailable: {service_name}\")]\n+    Unavailable {\n+        service_name: &'static str,\n+        #[source]\n+        source: GrpcProviderError,\n+    },\n+\n+    #[error(\"RPC failed: {0}\")]\n+    RpcFailed(#[source] tonic::Status),\n+}\n+\n+impl LazyClientError {\n+    /// Returns true if this error indicates the service is temporarily unavailable.\n+    /// REST handlers should map this to HTTP 424 Failed Dependency.\n+    pub fn is_dependency_unavailable(&self) -> bool {\n+        matches!(self, LazyClientError::Unavailable { .. })\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Macro to generate a lazy client wrapper for a GrpcClientDescriptor.\n+///\n+/// This generates a struct that:\n+/// - Implements the SDK API trait\n+/// - Uses GrpcClientProvider for lazy connection management\n+/// - Propagates SecurityContext via gRPC metadata\n+/// - Maps transport errors to SDK error types\n+///\n+/// # Example\n+///\n+/// ```rust,ignore\n+/// modkit::lazy_grpc_client! {\n+///     /// Lazy client for Calculator service.\n+///     pub struct LazyCalculatorClient for calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor {\n+///         // Method implementations are generated based on the trait\n+///     }\n+/// }\n+/// ```\n+#[macro_export]\n+macro_rules! lazy_grpc_client {\n+    (\n+        $(#[$meta:meta])*\n+        $vis:vis struct $name:ident for $descriptor:ty {\n+            $(\n+                async fn $method:ident(\n+                    &self,\n+                    ctx: &SecurityContext\n+                    $(, $arg:ident : $arg_ty:ty)*\n+                ) -> Result<$ret:ty, $err:ty> $body:block\n+            )*\n+        }\n+    ) => {\n+        $(#[$meta])*\n+        $vis struct $name {\n+            provider: std::sync::Arc<$crate::clients::grpc_provider::GrpcClientProvider>,\n+        }\n+\n+        impl $name {\n+            pub fn new(provider: std::sync::Arc<$crate::clients::grpc_provider::GrpcClientProvider>) -> Self {\n+                Self { provider }\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        // Trait implementation would be generated here\n+        // For now, this is a placeholder showing the pattern\n+    };\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Phase 4: SDK Crate Updates (calculator-sdk example)\n+\n+**Location**: `examples/oop-modules/calculator/calculator-sdk/src/descriptor.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Client descriptor for Calculator SDK.\n+\n+use modkit::clients::descriptor::{GrpcClientDescriptor, GrpcClientConfig, ClientAvailability};\n+use crate::api::CalculatorClientV1;\n+use crate::client::CalculatorGrpcClient;\n+\n+/// Descriptor for the Calculator gRPC client.\n+///\n+/// Used by consumer modules to declare their dependency on the Calculator service\n+/// via `#[modkit::module(clients = [CalculatorClientDescriptor])]`.\n+pub struct CalculatorClientDescriptor;\n+\n+impl GrpcClientDescriptor for CalculatorClientDescriptor {\n+    type Api = dyn CalculatorClientV1;\n+    type GrpcClient = CalculatorGrpcClient;\n+\n+    const MODULE_NAME: &'static str = \"calculator\";\n+    const SERVICE_NAME: &'static str = crate::SERVICE_NAME;\n+\n+    fn config() -> GrpcClientConfig {\n+        GrpcClientConfig {\n+            availability: ClientAvailability::Optional,\n+            ..Default::default()\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Updated SDK lib.rs**:\n+\n+```rust\n+// ... existing exports ...\n+\n+// Client descriptor for lazy wiring\n+mod descriptor;\n+pub use descriptor::CalculatorClientDescriptor;\n+```\n+\n+### Phase 5: Lazy Client Implementation for Calculator\n+\n+**Location**: `examples/oop-modules/calculator/calculator-sdk/src/lazy_client.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Lazy gRPC client for Calculator service.\n+//!\n+//! This client wraps GrpcClientProvider and implements CalculatorClientV1,\n+//! providing lazy connection management and graceful degradation.\n+\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use modkit::clients::grpc_provider::GrpcClientProvider;\n+use modkit_security::SecurityContext;\n+use tonic::metadata::MetadataMap;\n+\n+use crate::api::{CalculatorClientV1, CalculatorError};\n+use crate::client::CalculatorGrpcClient;\n+use crate::proto;\n+\n+/// Lazy client for Calculator service.\n+///\n+/// This client:\n+/// - Resolves the Calculator endpoint lazily on first call\n+/// - Caches the connection for subsequent calls\n+/// - Handles reconnection with backoff on failures\n+/// - Propagates SecurityContext via gRPC metadata\n+pub struct LazyCalculatorClient {\n+    provider: Arc<GrpcClientProvider>,\n+}\n+\n+impl LazyCalculatorClient {\n+    /// Create a new lazy client with the given provider.\n+    pub fn new(provider: Arc<GrpcClientProvider>) -> Self {\n+        Self { provider }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl CalculatorClientV1 for LazyCalculatorClient {\n+    async fn add(&self, ctx: &SecurityContext, a: i64, b: i64) -> Result<i64, CalculatorError> {\n+        // Get channel (lazy connect)\n+        let channel = self.provider.get_channel().await.map_err(|e| {\n+            tracing::warn!(error = %e, \"Calculator service unavailable\");\n+            CalculatorError::Unavailable {\n+                message: format!(\"Calculator service unavailable: {}\", e),\n+            }\n+        })?;\n+\n+        // Create client and attach security context\n+        let mut client = proto::calculator_service_client::CalculatorServiceClient::new(channel);\n+\n+        // Propagate security context via metadata\n+        let mut request = tonic::Request::new(proto::AddRequest { a, b });\n+        inject_security_context(ctx, request.metadata_mut());\n+\n+        // Make the call\n+        let response = client.add(request).await.map_err(|status| {\n+            // Evict connection on transport errors\n+            if is_transport_error(&status) {\n+                self.provider.evict();\n+            }\n+            map_status_to_error(status)\n+        })?;\n+\n+        // Reset failure state on success\n+        self.provider.reset_failures();\n+\n+        Ok(response.into_inner().result)\n+    }\n+\n+    async fn subtract(&self, ctx: &SecurityContext, a: i64, b: i64) -> Result<i64, CalculatorError> {\n+        let channel = self.provider.get_channel().await.map_err(|e| {\n+            CalculatorError::Unavailable {\n+                message: format!(\"Calculator service unavailable: {}\", e),\n+            }\n+        })?;\n+\n+        let mut client = proto::calculator_service_client::CalculatorServiceClient::new(channel);\n+        let mut request = tonic::Request::new(proto::SubtractRequest { a, b });\n+        inject_security_context(ctx, request.metadata_mut());\n+\n+        let response = client.subtract(request).await.map_err(|status| {\n+            if is_transport_error(&status) {\n+                self.provider.evict();\n+            }\n+            map_status_to_error(status)\n+        })?;\n+\n+        self.provider.reset_failures();\n+        Ok(response.into_inner().result)\n+    }\n+\n+    // ... other methods follow the same pattern ...\n+}\n+\n+/// Inject SecurityContext into gRPC metadata.\n+fn inject_security_context(ctx: &SecurityContext, metadata: &mut MetadataMap) {\n+    if let Some(tenant_id) = ctx.tenant_id() {\n+        if let Ok(value) = tenant_id.to_string().parse() {\n+            metadata.insert(\"x-tenant-id\", value);\n+        }\n+    }\n+    if let Some(user_id) = ctx.user_id() {\n+        if let Ok(value) = user_id.to_string().parse() {\n+            metadata.insert(\"x-user-id\", value);\n+        }\n+    }\n+    // Add other context fields as needed\n+}\n+\n+/// Check if the error is a transport-level error (connection lost, etc.)\n+fn is_transport_error(status: &tonic::Status) -> bool {\n+    matches!(\n+        status.code(),\n+        tonic::Code::Unavailable | tonic::Code::Unknown | tonic::Code::Internal\n+    )\n+}\n+\n+/// Map tonic Status to SDK error type.\n+fn map_status_to_error(status: tonic::Status) -> CalculatorError {\n+    match status.code() {\n+        tonic::Code::InvalidArgument => CalculatorError::InvalidArgument {\n+            message: status.message().to_string(),\n+        },\n+        tonic::Code::NotFound => CalculatorError::NotFound {\n+            message: status.message().to_string(),\n+        },\n+        tonic::Code::Unavailable => CalculatorError::Unavailable {\n+            message: status.message().to_string(),\n+        },\n+        _ => CalculatorError::Internal {\n+            message: status.message().to_string(),\n+        },\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Phase 6: Module Macro Extension\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit-macros/src/module.rs` (extension)\n+\n+The `#[modkit::module]` macro will be extended to support `clients = [...]`:\n+\n+```rust\n+// Conceptual macro expansion for:\n+// #[modkit::module(\n+//     name = \"calculator_gateway\",\n+//     deps = [\"calculator\"],\n+//     capabilities = [rest],\n+//     clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],\n+// )]\n+\n+// Generated code (simplified):\n+impl CalculatorGateway {\n+    fn __register_lazy_clients(ctx: &ModuleCtx) -> anyhow::Result<()> {\n+        use modkit::clients::descriptor::GrpcClientDescriptor;\n+\n+        // For each descriptor in `clients`:\n+        {\n+            type D = calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor;\n+            let config = D::config();\n+            let provider = std::sync::Arc::new(\n+                modkit::clients::grpc_provider::GrpcClientProvider::new(\n+                    D::SERVICE_NAME,\n+                    config,\n+                    ctx.client_hub(),\n+                )\n+            );\n+            let lazy_client: std::sync::Arc<<D as GrpcClientDescriptor>::Api> =\n+                std::sync::Arc::new(calculator_sdk::LazyCalculatorClient::new(provider));\n+            ctx.client_hub().register::<<D as GrpcClientDescriptor>::Api>(lazy_client);\n+        }\n+\n+        Ok(())\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+// The macro also ensures deps includes the module_name from each descriptor\n+// (validated at compile time or augmented automatically)\n+```\n+\n+### Phase 7: Registry Extension for Soft OoP Deps\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/registry.rs` (extension)\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Extended dependency resolution for OoP modules.\n+impl ModuleRegistry {\n+    /// Resolve dependencies, treating unknown deps as potential OoP soft deps.\n+    ///\n+    /// - If dep is a registered core module → hard dep (topo-sort)\n+    /// - If dep is configured as `runtime.type = oop` → soft dep (no topo-sort)\n+    /// - Otherwise → error (unknown dependency)\n+    pub fn resolve_dependencies_with_oop(\n+        &self,\n+        module_name: &str,\n+        deps: &[&str],\n+        config: &AppConfig,\n+    ) -> Result<ResolvedDeps, RegistryError> {\n+        let mut hard_deps = Vec::new();\n+        let mut soft_deps = Vec::new();\n+\n+        for dep in deps {\n+            if self.has_module(dep) {\n+                // Known in-process module\n+                hard_deps.push(*dep);\n+            } else if config.is_oop_module(dep) {\n+                // OoP module declared in config\n+                soft_deps.push(*dep);\n+            } else {\n+                return Err(RegistryError::UnknownDependency {\n+                    module: module_name.to_string(),\n+                    dependency: dep.to_string(),\n+                });\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        Ok(ResolvedDeps { hard_deps, soft_deps })\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Result of dependency resolution.\n+pub struct ResolvedDeps {\n+    /// Hard dependencies (in-process, participate in topo-sort).\n+    pub hard_deps: Vec<&'static str>,\n+    /// Soft dependencies (OoP, do not block startup).\n+    pub soft_deps: Vec<&'static str>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Consumer Module Changes (calculator_gateway)\n+\n+### Before (current pattern)\n+\n+```rust\n+#[modkit::module(\n+    name = \"calculator_gateway\",\n+    capabilities = [rest],\n+    deps = [\"calculator\"]\n+)]\n+pub struct CalculatorGateway;\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl modkit::Module for CalculatorGateway {\n+    async fn init(&self, ctx: &ModuleCtx) -> Result<()> {\n+        // Must wire client manually - FAILS if calculator not ready\n+        let directory = ctx.client_hub().get::<dyn DirectoryClient>()?;\n+        calculator_sdk::wire_client(ctx.client_hub(), &*directory).await?;\n+        // ...\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### After (proposed pattern)\n+\n+```rust\n+#[modkit::module(\n+    name = \"calculator_gateway\",\n+    capabilities = [rest],\n+    deps = [\"calculator\"],  // Soft OoP dep (validated via config)\n+    clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],  // NEW\n+)]\n+pub struct CalculatorGateway;\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl modkit::Module for CalculatorGateway {\n+    async fn init(&self, ctx: &ModuleCtx) -> Result<()> {\n+        // No wire_client() needed!\n+        // LazyCalculatorClient is auto-registered by the macro.\n+        let service = Arc::new(Service::new(ctx.client_hub()));\n+        ctx.client_hub().register::<Service>(service);\n+        Ok(())\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+// In domain service - unchanged!\n+impl Service {\n+    pub async fn add(&self, ctx: &SecurityContext, a: i64, b: i64) -> Result<i64, ServiceError> {\n+        let calculator = self.client_hub.get::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>()?;\n+        // Lazy connect happens here on first call\n+        calculator.add(ctx, a, b).await.map_err(|e| {\n+            // CalculatorError::Unavailable maps to HTTP 424\n+            ServiceError::RemoteError(e.to_string())\n+        })\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Error Handling and HTTP 424\n+\n+The lazy client returns `CalculatorError::Unavailable` when the OoP service cannot be reached. REST handlers should map this to HTTP 424 Failed Dependency:\n+\n+```rust\n+// In REST handler error mapping\n+impl From<ServiceError> for Problem {\n+    fn from(err: ServiceError) -> Self {\n+        match err {\n+            ServiceError::RemoteError(msg) if msg.contains(\"unavailable\") => {\n+                Problem::failed_dependency()\n+                    .with_detail(msg)\n+            }\n+            ServiceError::RemoteError(msg) => {\n+                Problem::bad_gateway()\n+                    .with_detail(msg)\n+            }\n+            ServiceError::Internal(msg) => {\n+                Problem::internal_server_error()\n+                    .with_detail(msg)\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Implementation Phases\n+\n+### Phase 1: Core Infrastructure (Week 1-2)\n+1. Add `GrpcClientDescriptor` trait to `libs/modkit/src/clients/descriptor.rs`\n+2. Implement `GrpcClientProvider` in `libs/modkit/src/clients/grpc_provider.rs`\n+3. Add `LazyClientError` type and helper utilities\n+4. Unit tests for provider (mock DirectoryClient)\n+\n+### Phase 2: SDK Updates (Week 2-3)\n+1. Add `CalculatorClientDescriptor` to calculator-sdk\n+2. Implement `LazyCalculatorClient` manually\n+3. Update calculator-sdk exports\n+4. Integration tests with mock gRPC server\n+\n+### Phase 3: Macro Extension (Week 3-4)\n+1. Extend `#[modkit::module]` to parse `clients = [...]`\n+2. Generate lazy client registration code\n+3. Auto-augment `deps` with module names from descriptors\n+4. Compile-time validation of descriptor types\n+\n+### Phase 4: Registry Extension (Week 4)\n+1. Implement soft OoP dep resolution in registry\n+2. Update topo-sort to exclude soft deps\n+3. Add config validation for OoP modules\n+4. Integration tests for startup ordering\n+\n+### Phase 5: Migration & Documentation (Week 5)\n+1. Update calculator_gateway example\n+2. Update OoP documentation (`09_oop_grpc_sdk_pattern.md`)\n+3. Add migration guide for existing SDKs\n+4. Update checklists\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Testing Strategy\n+\n+### Unit Tests\n+- `GrpcClientProvider`: connection caching, backoff, eviction\n+- `LazyCalculatorClient`: error mapping, context propagation\n+- Registry: soft dep resolution\n+\n+### Integration Tests\n+- Startup with unavailable OoP → module starts successfully\n+- First call triggers lazy connect\n+- Connection failure → backoff → retry\n+- Successful call → failure state reset\n+\n+### E2E Tests\n+- calculator_gateway starts without calculator OoP\n+- REST call returns 424 when calculator unavailable\n+- REST call succeeds after calculator becomes available\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Risks and Mitigations\n+\n+| Risk | Mitigation |\n+|------|------------|\n+| Macro complexity | Start with manual lazy client impl; add codegen later |\n+| Breaking existing SDKs | Backward-compatible: `wire_client()` still works |\n+| Performance overhead | Provider uses fast-path caching; no overhead on hot path |\n+| Debugging difficulty | Detailed tracing in provider and lazy client |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Success Criteria\n+\n+1. **No eager wiring**: Consumer modules do not call `wire_client()` in `init()`\n+2. **Graceful startup**: Modules start even if OoP dependencies are unavailable\n+3. **Per-operation degradation**: Missing OoP → HTTP 424 for affected endpoints only\n+4. **Single source of truth**: `clients = [...]` declares all OoP dependencies\n+5. **Consistent behavior**: All gRPC clients use the same provider infrastructure\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Appendix: File Structure\n+\n+```\n+libs/modkit/src/\n+├── clients/\n+│   ├── mod.rs              # Module exports\n+│   ├── descriptor.rs       # GrpcClientDescriptor trait\n+│   ├── grpc_provider.rs    # GrpcClientProvider implementation\n+│   └── lazy_client.rs      # LazyClientError and utilities\n+├── lib.rs                  # Add `pub mod clients;`\n+└── ...\n+\n+libs/modkit-macros/src/\n+├── module.rs               # Extended to parse `clients = [...]`\n+└── ...\n+\n+examples/oop-modules/calculator/calculator-sdk/src/\n+├── descriptor.rs           # CalculatorClientDescriptor\n+├── lazy_client.rs          # LazyCalculatorClient\n+├── lib.rs                  # Updated exports\n+└── ...\n+```","path":"docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md","commit_id":"f948350f607d352064e3588bf0d83968c9100d42","original_commit_id":"f948350f607d352064e3588bf0d83968c9100d42","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Add language specifier to fenced code block.**\n\nThe file structure tree should have a language specifier for proper rendering. Consider using `text` or `plaintext`.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-```\n+```text\n libs/modkit/src/\n ├── clients/\n```\n</details>\n\nAs per coding guidelines, fenced code blocks should have a language specified.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Tools</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 markdownlint-cli2 (0.20.0)</summary>\n\n[warning] 924-924: Fenced code blocks should have a language specified\n\n(MD040, fenced-code-language)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n````\nIn `@docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md` around lines 924 - 943,\nThe fenced code block that shows the project tree (the block beginning with\n\"libs/modkit/src/\") is missing a language specifier; update that block to use a\nplain/text specifier (e.g., change ``` to ```text) so the file tree renders\ncorrectly in the ADR (the block containing the clients/, modkit-macros entries\nand example paths).\n````\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit b42514f","created_at":"2026-02-13T16:55:17Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T17:02:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2805170411","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2805170411"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2805170411"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2805170411/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":924,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":943,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":943,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2805216376","pull_request_review_id":3798412652,"id":2805216376,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6nNDR4","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,975 @@\n+# Proposal: Universal Lazy Typed Clients for OoP gRPC Modules\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+This proposal details the implementation of **universal lazy typed clients** for out-of-process (OoP) gRPC modules in ModKit. The solution eliminates fragile eager wiring during module startup, enabling graceful degradation when OoP dependencies are unavailable.\n+\n+**Chosen approach**: Universal lazy layer in ModKit + code generation macro + `clients` declarations in `#[modkit::module]`.","path":"docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md","commit_id":"f27d777a7f704e5245de0afa449987e708c41cc7","original_commit_id":"3c9e4819f47928ba3df27b37fd0199b2296eb259","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Fetch ModKit unified system README\ncat docs/modkit_unified_system/README.md\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 4477\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Fetch the ADR file in question\ncat docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 33474\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Fix diagram label and clarify dependency auto-augmentation in example.**\n\nThe architecture diagram labels `GrpcClientProvider<TClient>`, but the implementation shows this struct is non-generic. Update the diagram to match: `GrpcClientProvider` (without type parameter).\n\nIn the \"After (proposed pattern)\" example, the text states \"Auto-augments deps with module_name\", but the code shows `deps = [\"calculator\"]` declared manually. Clarify whether developers must include OoP deps in the macro attribute or whether the `clients = [...]` parameter automatically injects them. If auto-injected, remove the manual `deps` entry from the example; if manual, update the surrounding text to match.\n\nAdditionally, per the ModKit routing table in `@/docs/modkit_unified_system/README.md`, this ADR proposes changes to the OoP gRPC pattern. Ensure the implementation guide section references `09_oop_grpc_sdk_pattern.md` as the primary doc to update during the migration phase.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md` around lines 1 - 7,\nUpdate the architecture diagram label to use GrpcClientProvider (remove the\ngeneric parameter TClient) to match the actual implementation, and clarify the\nexample's deps behavior: specify whether the macro auto-injects OoP dependencies\nwhen using the clients = [...] parameter or requires explicit deps =\n[\"module_name\"] entries; then either remove the manual deps from the \"After\"\nexample (if auto-injected) or change the surrounding text to state that\ndevelopers must declare deps manually. Finally, update the implementation guide\nreferences so the migration section points to 09_oop_grpc_sdk_pattern.md as the\nprimary doc to change during migration.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit f27d777","created_at":"2026-02-13T17:06:36Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T17:10:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2805216376","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2805216376"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2805216376"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2805216376/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":1,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":7,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":7,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2805216388","pull_request_review_id":3798412652,"id":2805216388,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6nNDSE","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,975 @@\n+# Proposal: Universal Lazy Typed Clients for OoP gRPC Modules\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+This proposal details the implementation of **universal lazy typed clients** for out-of-process (OoP) gRPC modules in ModKit. The solution eliminates fragile eager wiring during module startup, enabling graceful degradation when OoP dependencies are unavailable.\n+\n+**Chosen approach**: Universal lazy layer in ModKit + code generation macro + `clients` declarations in `#[modkit::module]`.\n+\n+## Problem Statement\n+\n+The current OoP client wiring pattern has several issues:\n+\n+1. **Eager wiring is fragile**: Consumer modules call `wire_client()` in `init()`, which fails if the OoP dependency is not yet available.\n+2. **Startup coupling**: The entire module fails to start if any OoP dependency is temporarily unavailable.\n+3. **Boilerplate duplication**: Each SDK repeats the same resolve/connect/cache logic.\n+4. **No graceful degradation**: Missing dependencies cause module-level failures instead of per-operation failures (HTTP 424).\n+\n+### Current Pattern (calculator_gateway example)\n+\n+```rust\n+// Current: Consumer must wire client manually, and it happens eagerly\n+pub async fn wire_client(hub: &ClientHub, resolver: &dyn DirectoryClient) -> Result<()> {\n+    let endpoint = resolver.resolve_grpc_service(SERVICE_NAME).await?;  // Fails if OoP not ready\n+    let client = CalculatorGrpcClient::connect(&endpoint.uri).await?;   // Fails if network issue\n+    hub.register::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>(Arc::new(client));\n+    Ok(())\n+}\n+```\n+\n+## Proposed Solution\n+\n+### Architecture Overview\n+\n+```text\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           SDK Crate (calculator-sdk)                    │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  CalculatorClientDescriptor                                             │\n+│    - MODULE_NAME: \"calculator\"                                          │\n+│    - SERVICE_NAME: \"calculator.v1.CalculatorService\"                    │\n+│    - Api: dyn CalculatorClientV1                                        │\n+│    - Availability: Optional (default)                                   │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  CalculatorGrpcClient (existing)                                        │\n+│    - Implements CalculatorClientV1                                      │\n+│    - Direct gRPC calls                                                  │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           ModKit (libs/modkit)                          │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  GrpcClientProvider<TClient>                                            │\n+│    - Lazy resolution via DirectoryClient                                │\n+│    - Connection caching with eviction on error                          │\n+│    - Backoff/rate-limiting for reconnects                               │","path":"docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md","commit_id":"3c9e4819f47928ba3df27b37fd0199b2296eb259","original_commit_id":"3c9e4819f47928ba3df27b37fd0199b2296eb259","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Update provider label to match non-generic struct.**\n\nThe diagram shows `GrpcClientProvider<TClient>`, but the later definition is `GrpcClientProvider` without generics. This can mislead readers about the API shape.  \n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-│  GrpcClientProvider<TClient>                                            │\n+│  GrpcClientProvider                                                     │\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n│  GrpcClientProvider                                                     │\n│    - Lazy resolution via DirectoryClient                                │\n│    - Connection caching with eviction on error                          │\n│    - Backoff/rate-limiting for reconnects                               │\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md` around lines 53 - 56,\nThe diagram label currently shows GrpcClientProvider<TClient> but the\nimplementation is defined as the non-generic GrpcClientProvider; update the\ndiagram and any nearby mentions to use GrpcClientProvider (remove the generic\nparameter) so the API shape matches the later definition, and scan the file for\nany other occurrences of GrpcClientProvider<TClient> to replace for consistency.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-13T17:06:36Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T17:06:37Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2805216388","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2805216388"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2805216388"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2805216388/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":53,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":56,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":56,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2805216400","pull_request_review_id":3798412652,"id":2805216400,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6nNDSQ","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,975 @@\n+# Proposal: Universal Lazy Typed Clients for OoP gRPC Modules\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+This proposal details the implementation of **universal lazy typed clients** for out-of-process (OoP) gRPC modules in ModKit. The solution eliminates fragile eager wiring during module startup, enabling graceful degradation when OoP dependencies are unavailable.\n+\n+**Chosen approach**: Universal lazy layer in ModKit + code generation macro + `clients` declarations in `#[modkit::module]`.\n+\n+## Problem Statement\n+\n+The current OoP client wiring pattern has several issues:\n+\n+1. **Eager wiring is fragile**: Consumer modules call `wire_client()` in `init()`, which fails if the OoP dependency is not yet available.\n+2. **Startup coupling**: The entire module fails to start if any OoP dependency is temporarily unavailable.\n+3. **Boilerplate duplication**: Each SDK repeats the same resolve/connect/cache logic.\n+4. **No graceful degradation**: Missing dependencies cause module-level failures instead of per-operation failures (HTTP 424).\n+\n+### Current Pattern (calculator_gateway example)\n+\n+```rust\n+// Current: Consumer must wire client manually, and it happens eagerly\n+pub async fn wire_client(hub: &ClientHub, resolver: &dyn DirectoryClient) -> Result<()> {\n+    let endpoint = resolver.resolve_grpc_service(SERVICE_NAME).await?;  // Fails if OoP not ready\n+    let client = CalculatorGrpcClient::connect(&endpoint.uri).await?;   // Fails if network issue\n+    hub.register::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>(Arc::new(client));\n+    Ok(())\n+}\n+```\n+\n+## Proposed Solution\n+\n+### Architecture Overview\n+\n+```text\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           SDK Crate (calculator-sdk)                    │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  CalculatorClientDescriptor                                             │\n+│    - MODULE_NAME: \"calculator\"                                          │\n+│    - SERVICE_NAME: \"calculator.v1.CalculatorService\"                    │\n+│    - Api: dyn CalculatorClientV1                                        │\n+│    - Availability: Optional (default)                                   │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  CalculatorGrpcClient (existing)                                        │\n+│    - Implements CalculatorClientV1                                      │\n+│    - Direct gRPC calls                                                  │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           ModKit (libs/modkit)                          │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  GrpcClientProvider<TClient>                                            │\n+│    - Lazy resolution via DirectoryClient                                │\n+│    - Connection caching with eviction on error                          │\n+│    - Backoff/rate-limiting for reconnects                               │\n+│    - Transport middleware (timeouts, keepalive, tracing)                │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  LazyGrpcClient<D: GrpcClientDescriptor>                                │\n+│    - Generated wrapper implementing D::Api                              │\n+│    - Request-scoped middleware (SecurityContext propagation)            │\n+│    - Error mapping to SDK error types                                   │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  #[modkit::module] macro extension                                      │\n+│    - clients = [CalculatorClientDescriptor]                             │\n+│    - Auto-registers LazyGrpcClient into ClientHub                       │\n+│    - Auto-augments deps with module_name                                │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                      Consumer Module (calculator_gateway)               │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  #[modkit::module(                                                      │\n+│      name = \"calculator_gateway\",                                       │\n+│      deps = [\"calculator\"],        // Soft OoP dep                      │\n+│      capabilities = [rest],                                             │\n+│      clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],            │\n+│  )]                                                                     │\n+│                                                                         │\n+│  // No wire_client() call needed!                                       │\n+│  // Client is always available from ClientHub                           │\n+│  let calc = hub.get::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>()?;                       │\n+│  calc.add(ctx, a, b).await?;  // Lazy connect on first call             │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Detailed Implementation\n+\n+### Phase 1: GrpcClientDescriptor Trait (SDK-side)\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/descriptor.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Client descriptor traits for typed OoP client metadata.\n+\n+use std::time::Duration;\n+\n+/// Availability policy for OoP clients.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum ClientAvailability {\n+    /// Client is optional; operations fail gracefully with SDK error (maps to HTTP 424).\n+    #[default]\n+    Optional,\n+    /// Client is required; module readiness may depend on availability.\n+    Required,\n+}\n+\n+/// Configuration for gRPC client behavior.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct GrpcClientConfig {\n+    /// Connection timeout for initial connect.\n+    pub connect_timeout: Duration,\n+    /// Request timeout for individual RPC calls.\n+    pub request_timeout: Duration,\n+    /// Keepalive interval.\n+    pub keepalive_interval: Option<Duration>,\n+    /// Maximum backoff duration between reconnect attempts.\n+    pub max_backoff: Duration,\n+    /// Availability policy.\n+    pub availability: ClientAvailability,\n+}\n+\n+impl Default for GrpcClientConfig {\n+    fn default() -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            connect_timeout: Duration::from_secs(5),\n+            request_timeout: Duration::from_secs(30),\n+            keepalive_interval: Some(Duration::from_secs(30)),\n+            max_backoff: Duration::from_secs(60),\n+            availability: ClientAvailability::Optional,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Descriptor for a gRPC client, defined in SDK crates.\n+///\n+/// This trait binds compile-time type information to runtime metadata\n+/// needed for lazy client resolution and registration.\n+///\n+/// # Example\n+///\n+/// ```rust,ignore\n+/// pub struct CalculatorClientDescriptor;\n+///\n+/// impl GrpcClientDescriptor for CalculatorClientDescriptor {\n+///     type Api = dyn CalculatorClientV1;\n+///     type GrpcClient = CalculatorGrpcClient;\n+///\n+///     const MODULE_NAME: &'static str = \"calculator\";\n+///     const SERVICE_NAME: &'static str = \"calculator.v1.CalculatorService\";\n+///\n+///     fn config() -> GrpcClientConfig {\n+///         GrpcClientConfig::default()\n+///     }\n+/// }\n+/// ```\n+pub trait GrpcClientDescriptor: Send + Sync + 'static {\n+    /// The SDK API trait type (e.g., `dyn CalculatorClientV1`).\n+    type Api: ?Sized + Send + Sync + 'static;\n+\n+    /// The concrete gRPC client type that implements `Api`.\n+    /// Must be constructible from a Channel.\n+    type GrpcClient: From<tonic::transport::Channel> + Send + Sync + 'static;\n+\n+    /// Module name for dependency graph (used in `deps`).\n+    const MODULE_NAME: &'static str;\n+\n+    /// gRPC service name for Directory resolution.\n+    const SERVICE_NAME: &'static str;\n+\n+    /// Client configuration (timeouts, backoff, availability).\n+    fn config() -> GrpcClientConfig {\n+        GrpcClientConfig::default()\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Phase 2: GrpcClientProvider (ModKit Core)\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/grpc_provider.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Universal lazy gRPC client provider.\n+//!\n+//! Encapsulates endpoint resolution, connection management, caching,\n+//! and reconnection logic for any gRPC client.\n+\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+use std::time::{Duration, Instant};\n+\n+use parking_lot::RwLock;\n+use tokio::sync::Semaphore;\n+use tonic::transport::Channel;\n+\n+use crate::client_hub::ClientHub;\n+use crate::directory::DirectoryClient;\n+use crate::clients::descriptor::GrpcClientConfig;\n+\n+/// Error type for provider operations.\n+#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\n+pub enum GrpcProviderError {\n+    #[error(\"service not found in directory: {service_name}\")]\n+    ServiceNotFound { service_name: &'static str },\n+\n+    #[error(\"connection failed: {0}\")]\n+    ConnectionFailed(#[source] tonic::transport::Error),\n+\n+    #[error(\"directory resolution failed: {0}\")]\n+    DirectoryError(#[source] anyhow::Error),\n+\n+    #[error(\"service temporarily unavailable (backoff active)\")]\n+    Backoff { retry_after: Duration },\n+}\n+\n+/// Cached connection state.\n+struct CachedConnection {\n+    channel: Channel,\n+    connected_at: Instant,\n+}\n+\n+/// Internal state for the provider.\n+struct ProviderState {\n+    cached: Option<CachedConnection>,\n+    last_failure: Option<Instant>,\n+    failure_count: u32,\n+}\n+\n+/// Universal lazy gRPC client provider.\n+///\n+/// This provider handles:\n+/// - Lazy endpoint resolution via DirectoryClient\n+/// - Connection caching with automatic eviction on errors\n+/// - Exponential backoff for reconnection attempts\n+/// - Rate limiting to prevent thundering herds\n+pub struct GrpcClientProvider {\n+    service_name: &'static str,\n+    config: GrpcClientConfig,\n+    hub: Arc<ClientHub>,\n+    state: RwLock<ProviderState>,\n+    connect_semaphore: Semaphore,\n+}\n+\n+impl GrpcClientProvider {\n+    /// Create a new provider for the given service.\n+    pub fn new(\n+        service_name: &'static str,\n+        config: GrpcClientConfig,\n+        hub: Arc<ClientHub>,\n+    ) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            service_name,\n+            config,\n+            hub,\n+            state: RwLock::new(ProviderState {\n+                cached: None,\n+                last_failure: None,\n+                failure_count: 0,\n+            }),\n+            connect_semaphore: Semaphore::new(1),\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Get a connected channel, resolving and connecting lazily.\n+    ///\n+    /// Returns a cached channel if available, otherwise resolves the endpoint\n+    /// and establishes a new connection.\n+    pub async fn get_channel(&self) -> Result<Channel, GrpcProviderError> {\n+        // Fast path: return cached connection\n+        {\n+            let state = self.state.read();\n+            if let Some(ref cached) = state.cached {\n+                return Ok(cached.channel.clone());\n+            }\n+\n+            // Check backoff\n+            if let Some(last_failure) = state.last_failure {\n+                let backoff = self.calculate_backoff(state.failure_count);\n+                let elapsed = last_failure.elapsed();\n+                if elapsed < backoff {\n+                    return Err(GrpcProviderError::Backoff {\n+                        retry_after: backoff - elapsed,\n+                    });\n+                }\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        // Slow path: acquire semaphore and connect\n+        let _permit = self.connect_semaphore.acquire().await\n+            .expect(\"semaphore is never closed\");\n+\n+        // Double-check after acquiring semaphore\n+        {\n+            let state = self.state.read();\n+            if let Some(ref cached) = state.cached {\n+                return Ok(cached.channel.clone());\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        // Resolve and connect\n+        self.connect_internal().await\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Evict the cached connection (call on transport errors).\n+    pub fn evict(&self) {\n+        let mut state = self.state.write();\n+        state.cached = None;\n+        state.last_failure = Some(Instant::now());\n+        state.failure_count = state.failure_count.saturating_add(1);\n+        tracing::warn!(\n+            service = self.service_name,\n+            failure_count = state.failure_count,\n+            \"Evicted cached gRPC connection\"\n+        );\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Reset failure state (call on successful RPC).\n+    pub fn reset_failures(&self) {\n+        let mut state = self.state.write();\n+        if state.failure_count > 0 {\n+            state.failure_count = 0;\n+            state.last_failure = None;\n+            tracing::debug!(service = self.service_name, \"Reset failure state after success\");\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    async fn connect_internal(&self) -> Result<Channel, GrpcProviderError> {\n+        // Resolve endpoint from DirectoryClient\n+        let directory = self\n+            .hub\n+            .get::<dyn DirectoryClient>()\n+            .map_err(|e| GrpcProviderError::DirectoryError(e.into()))?;\n+\n+        let endpoint = directory\n+            .resolve_grpc_service(self.service_name)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(|e| GrpcProviderError::DirectoryError(e))?;\n+\n+        tracing::debug!(\n+            service = self.service_name,\n+            uri = %endpoint.uri,\n+            \"Resolved service endpoint\"\n+        );\n+\n+        // Connect with configured timeouts\n+        let channel = Channel::from_shared(endpoint.uri.clone())\n+            .map_err(GrpcProviderError::ConnectionFailed)?\n+            .connect_timeout(self.config.connect_timeout)\n+            .timeout(self.config.request_timeout);\n+\n+        let channel = if let Some(keepalive) = self.config.keepalive_interval {\n+            channel\n+                .http2_keep_alive_interval(keepalive)\n+                .keep_alive_timeout(Duration::from_secs(20))\n+        } else {\n+            channel\n+        };\n+\n+        let channel = channel\n+            .connect()\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(GrpcProviderError::ConnectionFailed)?;\n+\n+        // Cache the connection\n+        {\n+            let mut state = self.state.write();\n+            state.cached = Some(CachedConnection {\n+                channel: channel.clone(),\n+                connected_at: Instant::now(),\n+            });\n+            state.failure_count = 0;\n+            state.last_failure = None;\n+        }\n+\n+        tracing::info!(\n+            service = self.service_name,\n+            uri = %endpoint.uri,\n+            \"Established gRPC connection\"\n+        );\n+\n+        Ok(channel)\n+    }\n+\n+    fn calculate_backoff(&self, failure_count: u32) -> Duration {\n+        let base = Duration::from_millis(100);\n+        let max = self.config.max_backoff;\n+        let backoff = base.saturating_mul(2u32.saturating_pow(failure_count.min(10)));\n+        backoff.min(max)\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Phase 3: LazyGrpcClient Wrapper (Generated or Manual)\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/lazy_client.rs`\n+\n+For the initial implementation, we provide a manual wrapper pattern. The macro generation can be added later.\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Lazy gRPC client wrapper that implements SDK traits.\n+//!\n+//! This wrapper delegates to GrpcClientProvider for connection management\n+//! and handles SecurityContext propagation.\n+\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+\n+use crate::clients::grpc_provider::{GrpcClientProvider, GrpcProviderError};\n+use crate::clients::descriptor::GrpcClientDescriptor;\n+\n+/// Error returned by lazy clients when the OoP dependency is unavailable.\n+#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\n+pub enum LazyClientError {\n+    #[error(\"service unavailable: {service_name}\")]\n+    Unavailable {\n+        service_name: &'static str,\n+        #[source]\n+        source: GrpcProviderError,\n+    },\n+\n+    #[error(\"RPC failed: {0}\")]\n+    RpcFailed(#[source] tonic::Status),\n+}\n+\n+impl LazyClientError {\n+    /// Returns true if this error indicates the service is temporarily unavailable.\n+    /// REST handlers should map this to HTTP 424 Failed Dependency.\n+    pub fn is_dependency_unavailable(&self) -> bool {\n+        matches!(self, LazyClientError::Unavailable { .. })\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Macro to generate a lazy client wrapper for a GrpcClientDescriptor.\n+///\n+/// This generates a struct that:\n+/// - Implements the SDK API trait\n+/// - Uses GrpcClientProvider for lazy connection management\n+/// - Propagates SecurityContext via gRPC metadata\n+/// - Maps transport errors to SDK error types\n+///\n+/// # Example\n+///\n+/// ```rust,ignore\n+/// modkit::lazy_grpc_client! {\n+///     /// Lazy client for Calculator service.\n+///     pub struct LazyCalculatorClient for calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor {\n+///         // Method implementations are generated based on the trait\n+///     }\n+/// }\n+/// ```\n+#[macro_export]\n+macro_rules! lazy_grpc_client {\n+    (\n+        $(#[$meta:meta])*\n+        $vis:vis struct $name:ident for $descriptor:ty {\n+            $(\n+                async fn $method:ident(\n+                    &self,\n+                    ctx: &SecurityContext\n+                    $(, $arg:ident : $arg_ty:ty)*\n+                ) -> Result<$ret:ty, $err:ty> $body:block\n+            )*\n+        }\n+    ) => {\n+        $(#[$meta])*\n+        $vis struct $name {\n+            provider: std::sync::Arc<$crate::clients::grpc_provider::GrpcClientProvider>,\n+        }\n+\n+        impl $name {\n+            pub fn new(provider: std::sync::Arc<$crate::clients::grpc_provider::GrpcClientProvider>) -> Self {\n+                Self { provider }\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        // Trait implementation would be generated here\n+        // For now, this is a placeholder showing the pattern\n+    };\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Phase 4: SDK Crate Updates (calculator-sdk example)\n+\n+**Location**: `examples/oop-modules/calculator/calculator-sdk/src/descriptor.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Client descriptor for Calculator SDK.\n+\n+use modkit::clients::descriptor::{GrpcClientDescriptor, GrpcClientConfig, ClientAvailability};\n+use crate::api::CalculatorClientV1;\n+use crate::client::CalculatorGrpcClient;\n+\n+/// Descriptor for the Calculator gRPC client.\n+///\n+/// Used by consumer modules to declare their dependency on the Calculator service\n+/// via `#[modkit::module(clients = [CalculatorClientDescriptor])]`.\n+pub struct CalculatorClientDescriptor;\n+\n+impl GrpcClientDescriptor for CalculatorClientDescriptor {\n+    type Api = dyn CalculatorClientV1;\n+    type GrpcClient = CalculatorGrpcClient;\n+\n+    const MODULE_NAME: &'static str = \"calculator\";\n+    const SERVICE_NAME: &'static str = crate::SERVICE_NAME;\n+\n+    fn config() -> GrpcClientConfig {\n+        GrpcClientConfig {\n+            availability: ClientAvailability::Optional,\n+            ..Default::default()\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Updated SDK lib.rs**:\n+\n+```rust\n+// ... existing exports ...\n+\n+// Client descriptor for lazy wiring\n+mod descriptor;\n+pub use descriptor::CalculatorClientDescriptor;\n+```\n+\n+### Phase 5: Lazy Client Implementation for Calculator\n+\n+**Location**: `examples/oop-modules/calculator/calculator-sdk/src/lazy_client.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Lazy gRPC client for Calculator service.\n+//!\n+//! This client wraps GrpcClientProvider and implements CalculatorClientV1,\n+//! providing lazy connection management and graceful degradation.\n+\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use modkit::clients::grpc_provider::GrpcClientProvider;\n+use modkit_security::SecurityContext;\n+use tonic::metadata::MetadataMap;\n+\n+use crate::api::{CalculatorClientV1, CalculatorError};\n+use crate::client::CalculatorGrpcClient;\n+use crate::proto;\n+\n+/// Lazy client for Calculator service.\n+///\n+/// This client:\n+/// - Resolves the Calculator endpoint lazily on first call\n+/// - Caches the connection for subsequent calls\n+/// - Handles reconnection with backoff on failures\n+/// - Propagates SecurityContext via gRPC metadata\n+pub struct LazyCalculatorClient {\n+    provider: Arc<GrpcClientProvider>,\n+}\n+\n+impl LazyCalculatorClient {\n+    /// Create a new lazy client with the given provider.\n+    pub fn new(provider: Arc<GrpcClientProvider>) -> Self {\n+        Self { provider }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl CalculatorClientV1 for LazyCalculatorClient {\n+    async fn add(&self, ctx: &SecurityContext, a: i64, b: i64) -> Result<i64, CalculatorError> {\n+        // Get channel (lazy connect)\n+        let channel = self.provider.get_channel().await.map_err(|e| {\n+            tracing::warn!(error = %e, \"Calculator service unavailable\");\n+            CalculatorError::Unavailable {\n+                message: format!(\"Calculator service unavailable: {}\", e),\n+            }\n+        })?;\n+\n+        // Create the gRPC client using the descriptor's GrpcClient type.\n+        // CalculatorGrpcClient wraps the proto client and implements From<Channel>.\n+        let client = CalculatorGrpcClient::from(channel);\n+\n+        // Propagate security context via metadata\n+        let mut request = tonic::Request::new(proto::AddRequest { a, b });\n+        inject_security_context(ctx, request.metadata_mut());\n+\n+        // Make the call\n+        let response = client.add(request).await.map_err(|status| {\n+            // Evict connection on transport errors\n+            if is_transport_error(&status) {\n+                self.provider.evict();\n+            }\n+            map_status_to_error(status)\n+        })?;\n+\n+        // Reset failure state on success\n+        self.provider.reset_failures();\n+\n+        Ok(response.into_inner().result)\n+    }\n+\n+    async fn subtract(&self, ctx: &SecurityContext, a: i64, b: i64) -> Result<i64, CalculatorError> {\n+        let channel = self.provider.get_channel().await.map_err(|e| {\n+            CalculatorError::Unavailable {\n+                message: format!(\"Calculator service unavailable: {}\", e),\n+            }\n+        })?;\n+\n+        let client = CalculatorGrpcClient::from(channel);\n+        let mut request = tonic::Request::new(proto::SubtractRequest { a, b });\n+        inject_security_context(ctx, request.metadata_mut());\n+\n+        let response = client.subtract(request).await.map_err(|status| {\n+            if is_transport_error(&status) {\n+                self.provider.evict();\n+            }\n+            map_status_to_error(status)\n+        })?;\n+\n+        self.provider.reset_failures();\n+        Ok(response.into_inner().result)\n+    }\n+\n+    // ... other methods follow the same pattern ...\n+}\n+\n+/// Inject SecurityContext into gRPC metadata.\n+fn inject_security_context(ctx: &SecurityContext, metadata: &mut MetadataMap) {\n+    if let Some(tenant_id) = ctx.tenant_id() {\n+        if let Ok(value) = tenant_id.to_string().parse() {\n+            metadata.insert(\"x-tenant-id\", value);\n+        }\n+    }\n+    if let Some(user_id) = ctx.user_id() {\n+        if let Ok(value) = user_id.to_string().parse() {\n+            metadata.insert(\"x-user-id\", value);\n+        }\n+    }\n+    // Add other context fields as needed\n+}\n+\n+/// Check if the error is a transport-level error (connection lost, etc.)\n+fn is_transport_error(status: &tonic::Status) -> bool {\n+    matches!(\n+        status.code(),\n+        tonic::Code::Unavailable | tonic::Code::Unknown | tonic::Code::Internal\n+    )\n+}\n+\n+/// Map tonic Status to SDK error type.\n+fn map_status_to_error(status: tonic::Status) -> CalculatorError {\n+    match status.code() {\n+        tonic::Code::InvalidArgument => CalculatorError::InvalidArgument {\n+            message: status.message().to_string(),\n+        },\n+        tonic::Code::NotFound => CalculatorError::NotFound {\n+            message: status.message().to_string(),\n+        },\n+        tonic::Code::Unavailable => CalculatorError::Unavailable {\n+            message: status.message().to_string(),\n+        },\n+        _ => CalculatorError::Internal {\n+            message: status.message().to_string(),\n+        },\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Phase 6: Module Macro Extension\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit-macros/src/module.rs` (extension)\n+\n+The `#[modkit::module]` macro will be extended to support `clients = [...]`:\n+\n+```rust\n+// Conceptual macro expansion for:\n+// #[modkit::module(\n+//     name = \"calculator_gateway\",\n+//     deps = [\"calculator\"],\n+//     capabilities = [rest],\n+//     clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],\n+// )]\n+\n+// Generated code (simplified):\n+impl CalculatorGateway {\n+    fn __register_lazy_clients(ctx: &ModuleCtx) -> anyhow::Result<()> {\n+        use modkit::clients::descriptor::GrpcClientDescriptor;\n+\n+        // For each descriptor in `clients`:\n+        {\n+            type D = calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor;\n+            let config = D::config();\n+            let provider = std::sync::Arc::new(\n+                modkit::clients::grpc_provider::GrpcClientProvider::new(\n+                    D::SERVICE_NAME,\n+                    config,\n+                    ctx.client_hub(),\n+                )\n+            );\n+            let lazy_client: std::sync::Arc<<D as GrpcClientDescriptor>::Api> =\n+                std::sync::Arc::new(calculator_sdk::LazyCalculatorClient::new(provider));\n+            ctx.client_hub().register::<<D as GrpcClientDescriptor>::Api>(lazy_client);\n+        }\n+\n+        Ok(())\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+// The macro also ensures deps includes the module_name from each descriptor\n+// (validated at compile time or augmented automatically)\n+```\n+\n+### Phase 7: Registry Extension for Soft OoP Deps\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/registry.rs` (extension)\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Extended dependency resolution for OoP modules.\n+impl ModuleRegistry {\n+    /// Resolve dependencies, treating unknown deps as potential OoP soft deps.\n+    ///\n+    /// - If dep is a registered core module → hard dep (topo-sort)\n+    /// - If dep is configured as `runtime.type = oop` → soft dep (no topo-sort)\n+    /// - Otherwise → error (unknown dependency)\n+    pub fn resolve_dependencies_with_oop(\n+        &self,\n+        module_name: &str,\n+        deps: &[&str],\n+        config: &AppConfig,\n+    ) -> Result<ResolvedDeps, RegistryError> {\n+        let mut hard_deps = Vec::new();\n+        let mut soft_deps = Vec::new();\n+\n+        for dep in deps {\n+            if self.has_module(dep) {\n+                // Known in-process module\n+                hard_deps.push(*dep);\n+            } else if config.is_oop_module(dep) {\n+                // OoP module declared in config\n+                soft_deps.push(*dep);\n+            } else {\n+                return Err(RegistryError::UnknownDependency {\n+                    module: module_name.to_string(),\n+                    dependency: dep.to_string(),\n+                });\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        Ok(ResolvedDeps { hard_deps, soft_deps })\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Result of dependency resolution.\n+pub struct ResolvedDeps {\n+    /// Hard dependencies (in-process, participate in topo-sort).\n+    pub hard_deps: Vec<&'static str>,\n+    /// Soft dependencies (OoP, do not block startup).\n+    pub soft_deps: Vec<&'static str>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Consumer Module Changes (calculator_gateway)\n+\n+### Before (current pattern)\n+\n+```rust\n+#[modkit::module(\n+    name = \"calculator_gateway\",\n+    capabilities = [rest],\n+    deps = [\"calculator\"]\n+)]\n+pub struct CalculatorGateway;\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl modkit::Module for CalculatorGateway {\n+    async fn init(&self, ctx: &ModuleCtx) -> Result<()> {\n+        // Must wire client manually - FAILS if calculator not ready\n+        let directory = ctx.client_hub().get::<dyn DirectoryClient>()?;\n+        calculator_sdk::wire_client(ctx.client_hub(), &*directory).await?;\n+        // ...\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### After (proposed pattern)\n+\n+```rust\n+#[modkit::module(\n+    name = \"calculator_gateway\",\n+    capabilities = [rest],\n+    deps = [\"calculator\"],  // Soft OoP dep (validated via config)\n+    clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],  // NEW\n+)]","path":"docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md","commit_id":"edd86e3e6cf91af1a08e3970d60dc26bc6acb6e6","original_commit_id":"3c9e4819f47928ba3df27b37fd0199b2296eb259","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Clarify deps vs clients auto-augmentation.**\n\nThe example keeps `deps = [\"calculator\"]` while earlier text says the macro auto-augments deps from `clients`. Consider removing `deps` here or adding a brief note that it’s optional when `clients` is present.  \n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Possible clarification</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    deps = [\"calculator\"],  // Soft OoP dep (validated via config)\n+    // deps is optional when clients are declared; macro auto-augments deps\n+    // deps = [\"calculator\"],\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md` around lines 787 - 792,\nThe example for modkit::module (name = \"calculator_gateway\") is inconsistent: it\nlists deps = [\"calculator\"] even though the macro auto-augments deps from\nclients; either remove the explicit deps entry from the attribute to avoid\nredundancy, or add a one-line note above the snippet clarifying that deps is\noptional when clients (e.g., clients =\n[calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor]) are present and will be\nauto-augmented by the macro; update the example to show the preferred approach\n(recommended: remove deps) and keep the modkit::module attribute and its\nname/client symbols unchanged.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit f27d777","created_at":"2026-02-13T17:06:36Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T17:09:59Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2805216400","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2805216400"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2805216400"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2805216400/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":1653,"original_start_line":787,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":1657,"original_line":792,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":792,"position":1657,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2805242391","pull_request_review_id":3798441951,"id":2805242391,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6nNJoX","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,976 @@\n+# Proposal: Universal Lazy Typed Clients for OoP gRPC Modules\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+This proposal details the implementation of **universal lazy typed clients** for out-of-process (OoP) gRPC modules in ModKit. The solution eliminates fragile eager wiring during module startup, enabling graceful degradation when OoP dependencies are unavailable.\n+\n+**Chosen approach**: Universal lazy layer in ModKit + code generation macro + `clients` declarations in `#[modkit::module]`.\n+\n+## Problem Statement\n+\n+The current OoP client wiring pattern has several issues:\n+\n+1. **Eager wiring is fragile**: Consumer modules call `wire_client()` in `init()`, which fails if the OoP dependency is not yet available.\n+2. **Startup coupling**: The entire module fails to start if any OoP dependency is temporarily unavailable.\n+3. **Boilerplate duplication**: Each SDK repeats the same resolve/connect/cache logic.\n+4. **No graceful degradation**: Missing dependencies cause module-level failures instead of per-operation failures (HTTP 424).\n+\n+### Current Pattern (calculator_gateway example)\n+\n+```rust\n+// Current: Consumer must wire client manually, and it happens eagerly\n+pub async fn wire_client(hub: &ClientHub, resolver: &dyn DirectoryClient) -> Result<()> {\n+    let endpoint = resolver.resolve_grpc_service(SERVICE_NAME).await?;  // Fails if OoP not ready\n+    let client = CalculatorGrpcClient::connect(&endpoint.uri).await?;   // Fails if network issue\n+    hub.register::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>(Arc::new(client));\n+    Ok(())\n+}\n+```\n+\n+## Proposed Solution\n+\n+### Architecture Overview\n+\n+```text\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           SDK Crate (calculator-sdk)                    │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  CalculatorClientDescriptor                                             │\n+│    - MODULE_NAME: \"calculator\"                                          │\n+│    - SERVICE_NAME: \"calculator.v1.CalculatorService\"                    │\n+│    - Api: dyn CalculatorClientV1                                        │\n+│    - Availability: Optional (default)                                   │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  CalculatorGrpcClient (existing)                                        │\n+│    - Implements CalculatorClientV1                                      │\n+│    - Direct gRPC calls                                                  │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           ModKit (libs/modkit)                          │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  GrpcClientProvider                                                     │\n+│    - Lazy resolution via DirectoryClient                                │\n+│    - Connection caching with eviction on error                          │\n+│    - Backoff/rate-limiting for reconnects                               │\n+│    - Transport middleware (timeouts, keepalive, tracing)                │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  LazyGrpcClient<D: GrpcClientDescriptor>                                │\n+│    - Generated wrapper implementing D::Api                              │\n+│    - Request-scoped middleware (SecurityContext propagation)            │\n+│    - Error mapping to SDK error types                                   │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  #[modkit::module] macro extension                                      │\n+│    - clients = [CalculatorClientDescriptor]                             │\n+│    - Auto-registers LazyGrpcClient into ClientHub                       │\n+│    - Auto-injects MODULE_NAME from each descriptor into deps            │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                      Consumer Module (calculator_gateway)               │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  #[modkit::module(                                                      │\n+│      name = \"calculator_gateway\",                                       │\n+│      capabilities = [rest],                                             │\n+│      clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],            │\n+│      // deps auto-injected: [\"calculator\"] from descriptor              │\n+│  )]                                                                     │\n+│                                                                         │\n+│  // No wire_client() call needed!                                       │\n+│  // Client is always available from ClientHub                           │\n+│  let calc = hub.get::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>()?;                       │\n+│  calc.add(ctx, a, b).await?;  // Lazy connect on first call             │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Detailed Implementation\n+\n+### Phase 1: GrpcClientDescriptor Trait (SDK-side)\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/descriptor.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Client descriptor traits for typed OoP client metadata.\n+\n+use std::time::Duration;\n+\n+/// Availability policy for OoP clients.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum ClientAvailability {\n+    /// Client is optional; operations fail gracefully with SDK error (maps to HTTP 424).\n+    #[default]\n+    Optional,\n+    /// Client is required; module readiness may depend on availability.\n+    Required,\n+}\n+\n+/// Configuration for gRPC client behavior.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct GrpcClientConfig {\n+    /// Connection timeout for initial connect.\n+    pub connect_timeout: Duration,\n+    /// Request timeout for individual RPC calls.\n+    pub request_timeout: Duration,\n+    /// Keepalive interval.\n+    pub keepalive_interval: Option<Duration>,\n+    /// Maximum backoff duration between reconnect attempts.\n+    pub max_backoff: Duration,\n+    /// Availability policy.\n+    pub availability: ClientAvailability,\n+}\n+\n+impl Default for GrpcClientConfig {\n+    fn default() -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            connect_timeout: Duration::from_secs(5),\n+            request_timeout: Duration::from_secs(30),\n+            keepalive_interval: Some(Duration::from_secs(30)),\n+            max_backoff: Duration::from_secs(60),\n+            availability: ClientAvailability::Optional,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Descriptor for a gRPC client, defined in SDK crates.\n+///\n+/// This trait binds compile-time type information to runtime metadata\n+/// needed for lazy client resolution and registration.\n+///\n+/// # Example\n+///\n+/// ```rust,ignore\n+/// pub struct CalculatorClientDescriptor;\n+///\n+/// impl GrpcClientDescriptor for CalculatorClientDescriptor {\n+///     type Api = dyn CalculatorClientV1;\n+///     type GrpcClient = CalculatorGrpcClient;\n+///\n+///     const MODULE_NAME: &'static str = \"calculator\";\n+///     const SERVICE_NAME: &'static str = \"calculator.v1.CalculatorService\";\n+///\n+///     fn config() -> GrpcClientConfig {\n+///         GrpcClientConfig::default()\n+///     }\n+/// }\n+/// ```\n+pub trait GrpcClientDescriptor: Send + Sync + 'static {\n+    /// The SDK API trait type (e.g., `dyn CalculatorClientV1`).\n+    type Api: ?Sized + Send + Sync + 'static;\n+\n+    /// The concrete gRPC client type that implements `Api`.\n+    /// Must be constructible from a Channel.\n+    type GrpcClient: From<tonic::transport::Channel> + Send + Sync + 'static;\n+\n+    /// Module name for dependency graph (used in `deps`).\n+    const MODULE_NAME: &'static str;\n+\n+    /// gRPC service name for Directory resolution.\n+    const SERVICE_NAME: &'static str;\n+\n+    /// Client configuration (timeouts, backoff, availability).\n+    fn config() -> GrpcClientConfig {\n+        GrpcClientConfig::default()\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Phase 2: GrpcClientProvider (ModKit Core)\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/grpc_provider.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Universal lazy gRPC client provider.\n+//!\n+//! Encapsulates endpoint resolution, connection management, caching,\n+//! and reconnection logic for any gRPC client.\n+\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+use std::time::{Duration, Instant};\n+\n+use parking_lot::RwLock;\n+use tokio::sync::Semaphore;\n+use tonic::transport::Channel;\n+\n+use crate::client_hub::ClientHub;\n+use crate::directory::DirectoryClient;\n+use crate::clients::descriptor::GrpcClientConfig;\n+\n+/// Error type for provider operations.\n+#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\n+pub enum GrpcProviderError {\n+    #[error(\"service not found in directory: {service_name}\")]\n+    ServiceNotFound { service_name: &'static str },\n+\n+    #[error(\"connection failed: {0}\")]\n+    ConnectionFailed(#[source] tonic::transport::Error),\n+\n+    #[error(\"directory resolution failed: {0}\")]\n+    DirectoryError(#[source] anyhow::Error),\n+\n+    #[error(\"service temporarily unavailable (backoff active)\")]\n+    Backoff { retry_after: Duration },\n+}\n+\n+/// Cached connection state.\n+struct CachedConnection {\n+    channel: Channel,\n+    connected_at: Instant,\n+}\n+\n+/// Internal state for the provider.\n+struct ProviderState {\n+    cached: Option<CachedConnection>,\n+    last_failure: Option<Instant>,\n+    failure_count: u32,\n+}\n+\n+/// Universal lazy gRPC client provider.\n+///\n+/// This provider handles:\n+/// - Lazy endpoint resolution via DirectoryClient\n+/// - Connection caching with automatic eviction on errors\n+/// - Exponential backoff for reconnection attempts\n+/// - Rate limiting to prevent thundering herds\n+pub struct GrpcClientProvider {\n+    service_name: &'static str,\n+    config: GrpcClientConfig,\n+    hub: Arc<ClientHub>,\n+    state: RwLock<ProviderState>,\n+    connect_semaphore: Semaphore,\n+}\n+\n+impl GrpcClientProvider {\n+    /// Create a new provider for the given service.\n+    pub fn new(\n+        service_name: &'static str,\n+        config: GrpcClientConfig,\n+        hub: Arc<ClientHub>,\n+    ) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            service_name,\n+            config,\n+            hub,\n+            state: RwLock::new(ProviderState {\n+                cached: None,\n+                last_failure: None,\n+                failure_count: 0,\n+            }),\n+            connect_semaphore: Semaphore::new(1),\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Get a connected channel, resolving and connecting lazily.\n+    ///\n+    /// Returns a cached channel if available, otherwise resolves the endpoint\n+    /// and establishes a new connection.\n+    pub async fn get_channel(&self) -> Result<Channel, GrpcProviderError> {\n+        // Fast path: return cached connection\n+        {\n+            let state = self.state.read();\n+            if let Some(ref cached) = state.cached {\n+                return Ok(cached.channel.clone());\n+            }\n+\n+            // Check backoff\n+            if let Some(last_failure) = state.last_failure {\n+                let backoff = self.calculate_backoff(state.failure_count);\n+                let elapsed = last_failure.elapsed();\n+                if elapsed < backoff {\n+                    return Err(GrpcProviderError::Backoff {\n+                        retry_after: backoff - elapsed,\n+                    });\n+                }\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        // Slow path: acquire semaphore and connect\n+        let _permit = self.connect_semaphore.acquire().await\n+            .expect(\"semaphore is never closed\");\n+\n+        // Double-check after acquiring semaphore\n+        {\n+            let state = self.state.read();\n+            if let Some(ref cached) = state.cached {\n+                return Ok(cached.channel.clone());\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        // Resolve and connect\n+        self.connect_internal().await\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Evict the cached connection (call on transport errors).\n+    pub fn evict(&self) {\n+        let mut state = self.state.write();\n+        state.cached = None;\n+        state.last_failure = Some(Instant::now());\n+        state.failure_count = state.failure_count.saturating_add(1);\n+        tracing::warn!(\n+            service = self.service_name,\n+            failure_count = state.failure_count,\n+            \"Evicted cached gRPC connection\"\n+        );\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Reset failure state (call on successful RPC).\n+    pub fn reset_failures(&self) {\n+        let mut state = self.state.write();\n+        if state.failure_count > 0 {\n+            state.failure_count = 0;\n+            state.last_failure = None;\n+            tracing::debug!(service = self.service_name, \"Reset failure state after success\");\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    async fn connect_internal(&self) -> Result<Channel, GrpcProviderError> {\n+        // Resolve endpoint from DirectoryClient\n+        let directory = self\n+            .hub\n+            .get::<dyn DirectoryClient>()\n+            .map_err(|e| GrpcProviderError::DirectoryError(e.into()))?;\n+\n+        let endpoint = directory\n+            .resolve_grpc_service(self.service_name)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(|e| GrpcProviderError::DirectoryError(e))?;\n+\n+        tracing::debug!(\n+            service = self.service_name,\n+            uri = %endpoint.uri,\n+            \"Resolved service endpoint\"\n+        );\n+\n+        // Connect with configured timeouts\n+        let channel = Channel::from_shared(endpoint.uri.clone())\n+            .map_err(GrpcProviderError::ConnectionFailed)?\n+            .connect_timeout(self.config.connect_timeout)\n+            .timeout(self.config.request_timeout);\n+\n+        let channel = if let Some(keepalive) = self.config.keepalive_interval {\n+            channel\n+                .http2_keep_alive_interval(keepalive)\n+                .keep_alive_timeout(Duration::from_secs(20))\n+        } else {\n+            channel\n+        };\n+\n+        let channel = channel\n+            .connect()\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(GrpcProviderError::ConnectionFailed)?;\n+\n+        // Cache the connection\n+        {\n+            let mut state = self.state.write();\n+            state.cached = Some(CachedConnection {\n+                channel: channel.clone(),\n+                connected_at: Instant::now(),\n+            });\n+            state.failure_count = 0;\n+            state.last_failure = None;\n+        }\n+\n+        tracing::info!(\n+            service = self.service_name,\n+            uri = %endpoint.uri,\n+            \"Established gRPC connection\"\n+        );\n+\n+        Ok(channel)\n+    }\n+\n+    fn calculate_backoff(&self, failure_count: u32) -> Duration {\n+        let base = Duration::from_millis(100);\n+        let max = self.config.max_backoff;\n+        let backoff = base.saturating_mul(2u32.saturating_pow(failure_count.min(10)));\n+        backoff.min(max)\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Phase 3: LazyGrpcClient Wrapper (Generated or Manual)\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/lazy_client.rs`\n+\n+For the initial implementation, we provide a manual wrapper pattern. The macro generation can be added later.\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Lazy gRPC client wrapper that implements SDK traits.\n+//!\n+//! This wrapper delegates to GrpcClientProvider for connection management\n+//! and handles SecurityContext propagation.\n+\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+\n+use crate::clients::grpc_provider::{GrpcClientProvider, GrpcProviderError};\n+use crate::clients::descriptor::GrpcClientDescriptor;\n+\n+/// Error returned by lazy clients when the OoP dependency is unavailable.\n+#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\n+pub enum LazyClientError {\n+    #[error(\"service unavailable: {service_name}\")]\n+    Unavailable {\n+        service_name: &'static str,\n+        #[source]\n+        source: GrpcProviderError,\n+    },\n+\n+    #[error(\"RPC failed: {0}\")]\n+    RpcFailed(#[source] tonic::Status),\n+}\n+\n+impl LazyClientError {\n+    /// Returns true if this error indicates the service is temporarily unavailable.\n+    /// REST handlers should map this to HTTP 424 Failed Dependency.\n+    pub fn is_dependency_unavailable(&self) -> bool {\n+        matches!(self, LazyClientError::Unavailable { .. })\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Macro to generate a lazy client wrapper for a GrpcClientDescriptor.\n+///\n+/// This generates a struct that:\n+/// - Implements the SDK API trait\n+/// - Uses GrpcClientProvider for lazy connection management\n+/// - Propagates SecurityContext via gRPC metadata\n+/// - Maps transport errors to SDK error types\n+///\n+/// # Example\n+///\n+/// ```rust,ignore\n+/// modkit::lazy_grpc_client! {\n+///     /// Lazy client for Calculator service.\n+///     pub struct LazyCalculatorClient for calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor {\n+///         // Method implementations are generated based on the trait\n+///     }\n+/// }\n+/// ```\n+#[macro_export]\n+macro_rules! lazy_grpc_client {\n+    (\n+        $(#[$meta:meta])*\n+        $vis:vis struct $name:ident for $descriptor:ty {\n+            $(\n+                async fn $method:ident(\n+                    &self,\n+                    ctx: &SecurityContext\n+                    $(, $arg:ident : $arg_ty:ty)*\n+                ) -> Result<$ret:ty, $err:ty> $body:block\n+            )*\n+        }\n+    ) => {\n+        $(#[$meta])*\n+        $vis struct $name {\n+            provider: std::sync::Arc<$crate::clients::grpc_provider::GrpcClientProvider>,\n+        }\n+\n+        impl $name {\n+            pub fn new(provider: std::sync::Arc<$crate::clients::grpc_provider::GrpcClientProvider>) -> Self {\n+                Self { provider }\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        // Trait implementation would be generated here\n+        // For now, this is a placeholder showing the pattern\n+    };\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Phase 4: SDK Crate Updates (calculator-sdk example)\n+\n+**Location**: `examples/oop-modules/calculator/calculator-sdk/src/descriptor.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Client descriptor for Calculator SDK.\n+\n+use modkit::clients::descriptor::{GrpcClientDescriptor, GrpcClientConfig, ClientAvailability};\n+use crate::api::CalculatorClientV1;\n+use crate::client::CalculatorGrpcClient;\n+\n+/// Descriptor for the Calculator gRPC client.\n+///\n+/// Used by consumer modules to declare their dependency on the Calculator service\n+/// via `#[modkit::module(clients = [CalculatorClientDescriptor])]`.\n+pub struct CalculatorClientDescriptor;\n+\n+impl GrpcClientDescriptor for CalculatorClientDescriptor {\n+    type Api = dyn CalculatorClientV1;\n+    type GrpcClient = CalculatorGrpcClient;\n+\n+    const MODULE_NAME: &'static str = \"calculator\";\n+    const SERVICE_NAME: &'static str = crate::SERVICE_NAME;\n+\n+    fn config() -> GrpcClientConfig {\n+        GrpcClientConfig {\n+            availability: ClientAvailability::Optional,\n+            ..Default::default()\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Updated SDK lib.rs**:\n+\n+```rust\n+// ... existing exports ...\n+\n+// Client descriptor for lazy wiring\n+mod descriptor;\n+pub use descriptor::CalculatorClientDescriptor;\n+```\n+\n+### Phase 5: Lazy Client Implementation for Calculator\n+\n+**Location**: `examples/oop-modules/calculator/calculator-sdk/src/lazy_client.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Lazy gRPC client for Calculator service.\n+//!\n+//! This client wraps GrpcClientProvider and implements CalculatorClientV1,\n+//! providing lazy connection management and graceful degradation.\n+\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use modkit::clients::grpc_provider::GrpcClientProvider;\n+use modkit_security::SecurityContext;\n+use tonic::metadata::MetadataMap;\n+\n+use crate::api::{CalculatorClientV1, CalculatorError};\n+use crate::client::CalculatorGrpcClient;\n+use crate::proto;\n+\n+/// Lazy client for Calculator service.\n+///\n+/// This client:\n+/// - Resolves the Calculator endpoint lazily on first call\n+/// - Caches the connection for subsequent calls\n+/// - Handles reconnection with backoff on failures\n+/// - Propagates SecurityContext via gRPC metadata\n+pub struct LazyCalculatorClient {\n+    provider: Arc<GrpcClientProvider>,\n+}\n+\n+impl LazyCalculatorClient {\n+    /// Create a new lazy client with the given provider.\n+    pub fn new(provider: Arc<GrpcClientProvider>) -> Self {\n+        Self { provider }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl CalculatorClientV1 for LazyCalculatorClient {\n+    async fn add(&self, ctx: &SecurityContext, a: i64, b: i64) -> Result<i64, CalculatorError> {\n+        // Get channel (lazy connect)\n+        let channel = self.provider.get_channel().await.map_err(|e| {\n+            tracing::warn!(error = %e, \"Calculator service unavailable\");\n+            CalculatorError::Unavailable {\n+                message: format!(\"Calculator service unavailable: {}\", e),\n+            }\n+        })?;\n+\n+        // Create the gRPC client using the descriptor's GrpcClient type.\n+        // CalculatorGrpcClient wraps the proto client and implements From<Channel>.\n+        let client = CalculatorGrpcClient::from(channel);\n+\n+        // Propagate security context via metadata\n+        let mut request = tonic::Request::new(proto::AddRequest { a, b });\n+        inject_security_context(ctx, request.metadata_mut());\n+\n+        // Make the call\n+        let response = client.add(request).await.map_err(|status| {\n+            // Evict connection on transport errors\n+            if is_transport_error(&status) {\n+                self.provider.evict();\n+            }\n+            map_status_to_error(status)\n+        })?;\n+\n+        // Reset failure state on success\n+        self.provider.reset_failures();\n+\n+        Ok(response.into_inner().result)\n+    }\n+\n+    async fn subtract(&self, ctx: &SecurityContext, a: i64, b: i64) -> Result<i64, CalculatorError> {\n+        let channel = self.provider.get_channel().await.map_err(|e| {\n+            CalculatorError::Unavailable {\n+                message: format!(\"Calculator service unavailable: {}\", e),\n+            }\n+        })?;\n+\n+        let client = CalculatorGrpcClient::from(channel);\n+        let mut request = tonic::Request::new(proto::SubtractRequest { a, b });\n+        inject_security_context(ctx, request.metadata_mut());\n+\n+        let response = client.subtract(request).await.map_err(|status| {\n+            if is_transport_error(&status) {\n+                self.provider.evict();\n+            }\n+            map_status_to_error(status)\n+        })?;\n+\n+        self.provider.reset_failures();\n+        Ok(response.into_inner().result)\n+    }\n+\n+    // ... other methods follow the same pattern ...\n+}\n+\n+/// Inject SecurityContext into gRPC metadata.\n+fn inject_security_context(ctx: &SecurityContext, metadata: &mut MetadataMap) {\n+    if let Some(tenant_id) = ctx.tenant_id() {\n+        if let Ok(value) = tenant_id.to_string().parse() {\n+            metadata.insert(\"x-tenant-id\", value);\n+        }\n+    }\n+    if let Some(user_id) = ctx.user_id() {\n+        if let Ok(value) = user_id.to_string().parse() {\n+            metadata.insert(\"x-user-id\", value);\n+        }\n+    }\n+    // Add other context fields as needed\n+}\n+\n+/// Check if the error is a transport-level error (connection lost, etc.)\n+fn is_transport_error(status: &tonic::Status) -> bool {\n+    matches!(\n+        status.code(),\n+        tonic::Code::Unavailable | tonic::Code::Unknown | tonic::Code::Internal\n+    )\n+}\n+\n+/// Map tonic Status to SDK error type.\n+fn map_status_to_error(status: tonic::Status) -> CalculatorError {\n+    match status.code() {\n+        tonic::Code::InvalidArgument => CalculatorError::InvalidArgument {\n+            message: status.message().to_string(),\n+        },\n+        tonic::Code::NotFound => CalculatorError::NotFound {\n+            message: status.message().to_string(),\n+        },\n+        tonic::Code::Unavailable => CalculatorError::Unavailable {\n+            message: status.message().to_string(),\n+        },\n+        _ => CalculatorError::Internal {\n+            message: status.message().to_string(),\n+        },\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Phase 6: Module Macro Extension\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit-macros/src/module.rs` (extension)\n+\n+The `#[modkit::module]` macro will be extended to support `clients = [...]`:\n+\n+```rust\n+// Conceptual macro expansion for:\n+// #[modkit::module(\n+//     name = \"calculator_gateway\",\n+//     capabilities = [rest],\n+//     clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],\n+//     // Note: deps is auto-injected from clients; no need to specify manually.\n+// )]\n+\n+// Generated code (simplified):\n+impl CalculatorGateway {\n+    fn __register_lazy_clients(ctx: &ModuleCtx) -> anyhow::Result<()> {\n+        use modkit::clients::descriptor::GrpcClientDescriptor;\n+\n+        // For each descriptor in `clients`:\n+        {\n+            type D = calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor;\n+            let config = D::config();\n+            let provider = std::sync::Arc::new(\n+                modkit::clients::grpc_provider::GrpcClientProvider::new(\n+                    D::SERVICE_NAME,\n+                    config,\n+                    ctx.client_hub(),\n+                )\n+            );\n+            let lazy_client: std::sync::Arc<<D as GrpcClientDescriptor>::Api> =\n+                std::sync::Arc::new(calculator_sdk::LazyCalculatorClient::new(provider));\n+            ctx.client_hub().register::<<D as GrpcClientDescriptor>::Api>(lazy_client);\n+        }\n+\n+        Ok(())\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+// The macro also ensures deps includes the module_name from each descriptor\n+// (validated at compile time or augmented automatically)\n+```\n+\n+### Phase 7: Registry Extension for Soft OoP Deps\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/registry.rs` (extension)\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Extended dependency resolution for OoP modules.\n+impl ModuleRegistry {\n+    /// Resolve dependencies, treating unknown deps as potential OoP soft deps.\n+    ///\n+    /// - If dep is a registered core module → hard dep (topo-sort)\n+    /// - If dep is configured as `runtime.type = oop` → soft dep (no topo-sort)\n+    /// - Otherwise → error (unknown dependency)\n+    pub fn resolve_dependencies_with_oop(\n+        &self,\n+        module_name: &str,\n+        deps: &[&str],\n+        config: &AppConfig,\n+    ) -> Result<ResolvedDeps, RegistryError> {\n+        let mut hard_deps = Vec::new();\n+        let mut soft_deps = Vec::new();\n+\n+        for dep in deps {\n+            if self.has_module(dep) {\n+                // Known in-process module\n+                hard_deps.push(*dep);\n+            } else if config.is_oop_module(dep) {\n+                // OoP module declared in config\n+                soft_deps.push(*dep);\n+            } else {\n+                return Err(RegistryError::UnknownDependency {\n+                    module: module_name.to_string(),\n+                    dependency: dep.to_string(),\n+                });\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        Ok(ResolvedDeps { hard_deps, soft_deps })\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Result of dependency resolution.\n+pub struct ResolvedDeps {\n+    /// Hard dependencies (in-process, participate in topo-sort).\n+    pub hard_deps: Vec<&'static str>,\n+    /// Soft dependencies (OoP, do not block startup).\n+    pub soft_deps: Vec<&'static str>,\n+}\n+```","path":"docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md","commit_id":"edd86e3e6cf91af1a08e3970d60dc26bc6acb6e6","original_commit_id":"f27d777a7f704e5245de0afa449987e708c41cc7","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`Rust function taking &[&str] returning &'static str lifetime mismatch`\n\n💡 Result:\n\nIn Rust, `&'static str` means “a string slice that is guaranteed to live for the entire program” (typically a string literal embedded in the binary) [1]. So a function that *takes* `&[&str]` (borrowed data) generally **cannot** promise to *return* `&'static str`, because the inputs usually don’t live for `'static`—returning them as `'static` would be lying.\n\n### What to do instead\n\n#### 1) If you’re returning one of the input strings, tie the output lifetime to the input\nUse an explicit lifetime so the return value can’t outlive the input slice/strings:\n\n```rust\nfn pick_first<'a>(xs: &'a [&'a str]) -> &'a str {\n    xs[0]\n}\n```\n\nThis expresses: “I return a `&str` that’s borrowed from the provided inputs,” which is the normal pattern; you can’t create a fresh `&str` “out of thin air” inside the function [2].\n\n#### 2) If you truly need to return `'static`, only return string literals (or other truly-static storage)\n```rust\nfn classify(xs: &[&str]) -> &'static str {\n    if xs.is_empty() { \"empty\" } else { \"non-empty\" }\n}\n```\n\nThis works because `\"empty\"` / `\"non-empty\"` are string literals, which are `'static` [1].\n\n#### 3) If you’re building/formatting a string inside the function, return an owned value (or `Cow`)\nYou can’t return a `&str` pointing into a local `String` that will be dropped at function end [3]. Return `String` (or `Cow` if you want “borrow when possible, allocate otherwise”):\n\n```rust\nfn build_message(xs: &[&str]) -> String {\n    format!(\"count={}\", xs.len())\n}\n```\n\nThis is the same core issue as trying to return `Vec<&'static str>` from data created inside the function: it can’t be `'static` because it doesn’t live long enough [4].\n\n---\n\nIf you paste your exact function signature + body and the compiler error, I can rewrite it in the most idiomatic form (often `-> &'a str` or `-> Cow<'a, str>`).  \n\n**Sources:** [1] Rust Book on `'static` and why it’s often the wrong “fix”; [2] Rust forum explanation that `&str` must refer to already-long-lived data (and why returning `&str` is hard without tying lifetimes); [3] Stack Overflow example: can’t return `&str` that points into a local `String`; [4] Stack Overflow example: can’t return `'static` references to data created in the function.\n\n---\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`Rust idiomatic pattern returning borrowed strings from function`\n\n💡 Result:\n\nIn Rust, returning a borrowed string (`&str`) is idiomatic **only when the returned slice is borrowed from an input** (or is a string literal with `'static` lifetime). You **cannot** return `&str` that points into a `String` created inside the function, because that `String` is dropped when the function returns. [4][6][7]\n\n### 1) Return a slice borrowed from an argument (most common)\n```rust\nfn first_char<'a>(s: &'a str) -> &'a str {\n    &s[..1]\n}\n\n// lifetime elision also works for the 1-input-1-output case:\nfn first_char_elided(s: &str) -> &str { &s[..1] }\n```\nThis works because the output reference is tied to the input reference’s lifetime (via explicit lifetime or elision rules). [8]\n\n### 2) Return a string literal (`&'static str`) when appropriate\n```rust\nfn status(ok: bool) -> &'static str {\n    if ok { \"ok\" } else { \"error\" }\n}\n```\nString literals are effectively `'static`, so returning them by reference is fine. [9]\n\n### 3) If you might return either borrowed *or* newly-created text: use `Cow<'a, str>` (idiomatic)\n```rust\nuse std::borrow::Cow;\n\nfn normalize<'a>(s: &'a str) -> Cow<'a, str> {\n    if s.contains('_') { Cow::Owned(s.replace('_', \"-\")) }\n    else { Cow::Borrowed(s) }\n}\n```\n`Cow` can be either `Borrowed(&'a B)` or `Owned(...)`, avoiding unnecessary allocation when you can borrow. [1]\n\n### 4) If you’re producing new text, just return an owned type\n```rust\nfn make_message(name: &str) -> String {\n    format!(\"hello, {name}\")\n}\n```\nThis is the standard fix when the data is created inside the function. [6][7]\n\n### 5) Advanced: accept a caller-owned buffer and return slices into it\nIf you truly need `Vec<&str>` from processed text, the backing storage must outlive the returned slices—so the buffer must be owned by the caller (passed in). [4]\n\n---\n\n**Rule of thumb:** return `&str` only when you can clearly point to “what it’s borrowed from” (an input reference or `'static`), otherwise return `String` (or `Cow<'_, str>` when borrowing is sometimes possible). [6][7][8]\n\n**Sources:** `Cow` docs [1], Rustonomicon lifetime elision [8], Stack Overflow explanations/examples [4][6][7], `'static` literal example discussion [9].\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nfd \"0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md\" --type f\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 124\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nif [ -f \"docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md\" ]; then\n  # Check if the code snippet exists in the file\n  sed -n '714,757p' \"docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md\" | head -80\nfi\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 1541\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Fix `ResolvedDeps` lifetimes to avoid a compile-time mismatch.**\n\n`resolve_dependencies_with_oop` takes `&[&str]` but returns `ResolvedDeps` with `Vec<&'static str>`, which cannot be derived from non-`'static` inputs. This will not compile. Either make `ResolvedDeps` generic over a lifetime, or return owned `String`s.\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Example fix using lifetimes</summary>\n\n```diff\n-pub struct ResolvedDeps {\n+pub struct ResolvedDeps<'a> {\n     /// Hard dependencies (in-process, participate in topo-sort).\n-    pub hard_deps: Vec<&'static str>,\n+    pub hard_deps: Vec<&'a str>,\n     /// Soft dependencies (OoP, do not block startup).\n-    pub soft_deps: Vec<&'static str>,\n+    pub soft_deps: Vec<&'a str>,\n }\n```\n\n```diff\n-pub fn resolve_dependencies_with_oop(\n+pub fn resolve_dependencies_with_oop<'a>(\n     &self,\n     module_name: &str,\n-    deps: &[&str],\n+    deps: &'a [&'a str],\n     config: &AppConfig,\n-) -> Result<ResolvedDeps, RegistryError> {\n+) -> Result<ResolvedDeps<'a>, RegistryError> {\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md` around lines 714 - 757,\nThe ResolvedDeps struct currently uses Vec<&'static str> but\nresolve_dependencies_with_oop accepts &[&str] (non-'static), causing a lifetime\nmismatch; update the API by either making ResolvedDeps generic over a lifetime\n(e.g., struct ResolvedDeps<'a> { hard_deps: Vec<&'a str>, soft_deps: Vec<&'a\nstr> } and change resolve_dependencies_with_oop signature to return\nResult<ResolvedDeps<'_>, RegistryError>) or convert to owned strings (change\nfields to Vec<String>, push dep.to_string() when building hard_deps/soft_deps);\nadjust all callers of ResolvedDeps and the resolve_dependencies_with_oop\nsignature accordingly to match the chosen approach (modify function return type\nand any usages of ResolvedDeps::hard_deps / soft_deps).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-13T17:13:30Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T17:13:31Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2805242391","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2805242391"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2805242391"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2805242391/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":1595,"original_start_line":714,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":1628,"original_line":757,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":757,"position":1628,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2818571201","pull_request_review_id":3815733575,"id":2818571201,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6n__vB","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1045 @@\n+# ADR-0003: Universal Lazy Typed REST Clients for OoP Modules\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+This proposal outlines a migration from gRPC to REST as the default transport for out-of-process (OoP) modules and introduces a **universal lazy typed client layer** for OoP module communication in ModKit. The implementation is structured in phases:\n+\n+1. **Phase 1 - REST as default transport**: Establish REST as the default OoP transport; gRPC becomes opt-in\n+2. **Phase 2 - ClientDescriptor trait**: SDK-defined metadata binding compile-time types to runtime resolution\n+3. **Phase 3 - ClientProvider**: Lazy resolution, caching, backoff, and reconnection infrastructure\n+4. **Phase 4 - Macro extension**: `clients = [...]` auto-registers lazy clients into `ClientHub`\n+5. **Phase 5 - Soft OoP deps**: Dependencies on OoP modules don't block startup\n+6. **Phase 6 - Registry extension**: Soft OoP dep resolution:  \n+\n+**Current pattern** (problematic):\n+```rust\n+// Consumer must wire client manually in init() - FAILS if OoP module is not ready\n+calculator_sdk::wire_client(hub, &*directory).await?;\n+```\n+\n+**Proposed pattern**:\n+```rust\n+#[modkit::module(\n+    name = \"calculator_gateway\",\n+    clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],  // REST by default\n+)]\n+// No wire_client() needed - lazy client auto-registered\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Problem Statement\n+\n+The current OoP client wiring pattern has several issues:\n+\n+1. **Eager wiring is fragile**: Consumer modules call `wire_client()` in `init()`, which fails if the OoP dependency is not yet available.\n+2. **Startup coupling**: The entire module fails to start if any OoP dependency is temporarily unavailable.\n+3. **Boilerplate duplication**: Each SDK repeats the same resolve/connect/cache logic.\n+4. **No graceful degradation**: Missing dependencies cause module-level failures instead of per-operation failures (HTTP 424).\n+5. **gRPC complexity**: Binary protobuf payloads are hard to debug; requires specialized tooling.\n+\n+### Current Pattern (calculator_gateway example)\n+\n+```rust\n+// Current: Consumer must wire client manually, and it happens eagerly\n+pub async fn wire_client(hub: &ClientHub, resolver: &dyn DirectoryClient) -> Result<()> {\n+    let endpoint = resolver.resolve_grpc_service(SERVICE_NAME).await?;  // Fails if OoP not ready\n+    let client = CalculatorGrpcClient::connect(&endpoint.uri).await?;   // Fails if network issue\n+    hub.register::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>(Arc::new(client));\n+    Ok(())\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Proposed Solution\n+\n+### Architecture Overview\n+\n+```text\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           SDK Crate (calculator-sdk)                    │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  CalculatorClientDescriptor                                             │\n+│    - MODULE_NAME: \"calculator\"                                          │\n+│    - Api: dyn CalculatorClientV1                                        │\n+│    - Transport: Rest (default) | Grpc (opt-in)                          │\n+│    - Availability Policy: Optional (default)                            │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  LazyCalculatorClient                                                   │\n+│    - Implements CalculatorClientV1                                      │\n+│    - Delegates to ClientProvider for lazy connection                    │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           ModKit (libs/modkit)                          │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  ClientProvider (transport-agnostic interface)                          │\n+│    - Lazy resolution via DirectoryClient                                │\n+│    - Endpoint/connection caching with eviction on error                 │\n+│    - Backoff/rate-limiting for reconnects                               │\n+│    - Transport middleware (timeouts, retries, tracing)                  │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  RestClientProvider (default) | GrpcClientProvider (feature = \"grpc\")   │\n+│    - Transport-specific implementations                                 │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  #[modkit::module] macro extension                                      │\n+│    - clients = [CalculatorClientDescriptor]                             │\n+│    - Auto-registers LazyClient into ClientHub                           │\n+│    - Auto-injects MODULE_NAME from each descriptor into deps            │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                      Consumer Module (calculator_gateway)               │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  #[modkit::module(                                                      │\n+│      name = \"calculator_gateway\",                                       │\n+│      capabilities = [rest],                                             │\n+│      clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],            │\n+│      // deps auto-injected: [\"calculator\"] from descriptor              │\n+│  )]                                                                     │\n+│                                                                         │\n+│  // No wire_client() call needed!                                       │\n+│  // Client is always available from ClientHub                           │\n+│  let calc = hub.get::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>()?;                       │\n+│  calc.add(ctx, a, b).await?;  // Lazy connect on first call             │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Detailed Implementation\n+\n+### Phase 1: REST as Default Transport\n+\n+**Rationale**: REST is simpler to debug, requires no code generation, and is sufficient for most OoP calls. gRPC remains available for streaming or high-throughput use cases.\n+\n+| Factor          | REST                            | gRPC                         |\n+|-----------------|---------------------------------|------------------------------|\n+| Debuggability   | ✅ curl, browser, any HTTP tool | ❌ Requires specialized tools |\n+| Simplicity      | ✅ JSON, standard HTTP          | ❌ Protobuf, code generation  |\n+| Browser support | ✅ Native                       | ❌ Requires gRPC-Web proxy    |\n+| API reuse       | ✅ Same as public REST API      | ❌ Separate interface         |\n+| Streaming       | ❌ Requires SSE/WebSocket       | ✅ Native support             |\n+| Performance     | ⚠️ JSON overhead                | ✅ Binary, efficient          |\n+\n+#### 1.1 Transport Enum\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/transport.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Transport protocol for OoP communication.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum Transport {\n+    /// REST with JSON serialization (default).\n+    #[default]\n+    Rest,\n+    /// gRPC with protobuf serialization (opt-in, requires feature = \"grpc\").\n+    #[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+    Grpc,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### 1.2 REST Service Discovery Infrastructure\n+\n+REST service discovery requires extending the existing `ModuleInstance`, `ModuleManager`, and `DirectoryClient` to track and resolve REST endpoints.\n+\n+##### 1.2.1 Extend `ModuleInstance` to track REST endpoints\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/runtime/module_manager.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Represents a single instance of a module\n+#[derive(Debug)]\n+pub struct ModuleInstance {\n+    pub module: String,\n+    pub instance_id: Uuid,\n+    pub control: Option<Endpoint>,\n+    pub grpc_services: HashMap<String, Endpoint>,\n+    pub rest_endpoint: Option<Endpoint>,  // NEW: REST base URL for this instance\n+    pub version: Option<String>,\n+    inner: Arc<parking_lot::RwLock<InstanceRuntimeState>>,\n+}\n+\n+impl ModuleInstance {\n+    // ... existing methods ...\n+\n+    /// Set the REST endpoint for this instance\n+    pub fn with_rest_endpoint(mut self, ep: Endpoint) -> Self {\n+        self.rest_endpoint = Some(ep);\n+        self\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.2 Extend `ModuleManager` with REST discovery\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/runtime/module_manager.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+impl ModuleManager {\n+    /// Pick a REST endpoint for a module using round-robin selection.\n+    /// Returns (module_name, instance, endpoint) if found.\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn pick_rest_endpoint_round_robin(\n+        &self,\n+        module_name: &str,\n+    ) -> Option<(String, Arc<ModuleInstance>, Endpoint)> {\n+        let instances_entry = self.inner.get(module_name)?;\n+        let instances = instances_entry.value();\n+\n+        // Filter to instances with REST endpoints and healthy/ready state\n+        let candidates: Vec<_> = instances\n+            .iter()\n+            .filter(|inst| {\n+                inst.rest_endpoint.is_some()\n+                    && matches!(inst.state(), InstanceState::Healthy | InstanceState::Ready)\n+            })\n+            .cloned()\n+            .collect();\n+\n+        if candidates.is_empty() {\n+            return None;\n+        }\n+\n+        let len = candidates.len();\n+        let rr_key = format!(\"rest:{}\", module_name);\n+        let mut counter = self.rr_counters.entry(rr_key).or_insert(0);\n+        let idx = *counter % len;\n+        *counter = (*counter + 1) % len;\n+\n+        candidates.get(idx).map(|inst| {\n+            (\n+                module_name.to_owned(),\n+                inst.clone(),\n+                inst.rest_endpoint.clone().expect(\"filtered above\"),\n+            )\n+        })\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.3 Extend `DirectoryClient` trait\n+\n+**Location**: `cf_system_sdks/src/directory.rs` (upstream crate — requires update)\n+\n+```rust\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait DirectoryClient: Send + Sync {\n+    /// Resolve REST endpoint for a module (default for OoP).\n+    async fn resolve_rest_service(&self, module_name: &str) -> Result<RestEndpoint>;\n+\n+    /// Resolve gRPC endpoint for a module (opt-in).\n+    async fn resolve_grpc_service(&self, service_name: &str) -> Result<ServiceEndpoint>;\n+\n+    // ... existing methods (list_instances, register_instance, etc.) ...\n+}\n+\n+/// REST endpoint for a module\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct RestEndpoint {\n+    /// Base URL for the module's REST API (e.g., \"http://calculator:8080\")\n+    pub base_url: String,\n+}\n+\n+impl RestEndpoint {\n+    pub fn new(base_url: impl Into<String>) -> Self {\n+        Self { base_url: base_url.into() }\n+    }\n+\n+    pub fn http(host: &str, port: u16) -> Self {\n+        Self { base_url: format!(\"http://{}:{}\", host, port) }\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.4 Implement `resolve_rest_service` in `LocalDirectoryClient`\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/directory.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl DirectoryClient for LocalDirectoryClient {\n+    async fn resolve_rest_service(&self, module_name: &str) -> Result<RestEndpoint> {\n+        if let Some((_, _, ep)) = self.mgr.pick_rest_endpoint_round_robin(module_name) {\n+            return Ok(RestEndpoint::new(ep.uri));\n+        }\n+\n+        anyhow::bail!(\"REST service not found or no healthy instances: {module_name}\")\n+    }\n+\n+    // ... existing methods unchanged ...\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.5 Extend `RegisterInstanceInfo` for REST registration\n+\n+**Location**: `cf_system_sdks/src/directory.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Information needed to register a module instance\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct RegisterInstanceInfo {\n+    pub module: String,\n+    pub instance_id: String,\n+    pub grpc_services: Vec<(String, ServiceEndpoint)>,\n+    pub rest_endpoint: Option<RestEndpoint>,  // NEW\n+    pub version: Option<String>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.6 OoP Module REST Registration\n+\n+When an OoP module starts, it registers its REST endpoint with the DirectoryService:\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/oop.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+async fn register_with_directory(\n+    directory: &dyn DirectoryClient,\n+    module_name: &str,\n+    instance_id: Uuid,\n+    rest_port: u16,\n+    grpc_services: Vec<(String, ServiceEndpoint)>,\n+) -> Result<()> {\n+    let info = RegisterInstanceInfo {\n+        module: module_name.to_owned(),\n+        instance_id: instance_id.to_string(),\n+        grpc_services,\n+        rest_endpoint: Some(RestEndpoint::http(\"0.0.0.0\", rest_port)),\n+        version: Some(env!(\"CARGO_PKG_VERSION\").to_owned()),\n+    };\n+\n+    directory.register_instance(info).await\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.7 Design Decisions\n+\n+| Decision | Rationale |\n+|----------|-----------|\n+| **One REST endpoint per instance** | Unlike gRPC (multiple services per instance), REST modules expose a single base URL with path-based routing |\n+| **Module-name based resolution** | REST discovery uses `module_name` (e.g., \"calculator\"), not service name |\n+| **Reuse existing health tracking** | REST endpoints use the same `InstanceState` and heartbeat mechanism as gRPC |\n+| **Symmetric API** | `resolve_rest_service()` mirrors `resolve_grpc_service()` for consistency |\n+\n+##### 1.2.8 Migration Notes\n+\n+1. **`cf_system_sdks` must be updated first** — Add `RestEndpoint`, extend `RegisterInstanceInfo`, and add `resolve_rest_service()` to `DirectoryClient`\n+2. **`ModuleInstance` is extended** — Existing code continues to work; `rest_endpoint` defaults to `None`\n+3. **OoP modules must register REST endpoints** — Update bootstrap to include REST port in registration\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Phase 2: ClientDescriptor Trait\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/descriptor.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Client descriptor traits for typed OoP client metadata.\n+\n+use std::time::Duration;\n+\n+/// Availability policy for OoP clients.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum ClientAvailabilityPolicy {\n+    /// Client is optional; operations fail gracefully with SDK error (maps to HTTP 424).\n+    #[default]\n+    Optional,\n+    /// Client is required; module readiness may depend on availability.\n+    Required,\n+}\n+\n+/// Configuration for client behavior.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct ClientConfig {\n+    /// Transport protocol (REST default, gRPC opt-in).\n+    pub transport: Transport,\n+    /// Connection timeout for initial connect.\n+    pub connect_timeout: Duration,\n+    /// Request timeout for individual calls.\n+    pub request_timeout: Duration,\n+    /// Maximum backoff duration between reconnect attempts.\n+    pub max_backoff: Duration,\n+    /// Availability policy.\n+    pub availability_policy: ClientAvailabilityPolicy,\n+}\n+\n+impl Default for ClientConfig {\n+    fn default() -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            transport: Transport::Rest,\n+            connect_timeout: Duration::from_secs(5),\n+            request_timeout: Duration::from_secs(30),\n+            max_backoff: Duration::from_secs(60),\n+            availability_policy: ClientAvailabilityPolicy::Optional,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl ClientConfig {\n+    /// Create a REST client config (default).\n+    pub fn rest() -> Self {\n+        Self::default()\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Create a gRPC client config (opt-in).\n+    #[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+    pub fn grpc() -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            transport: Transport::Grpc,\n+            ..Self::default()\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Descriptor for an OoP client, defined in SDK crates.\n+///\n+/// This trait binds compile-time type information to runtime metadata\n+/// needed for lazy client resolution and registration.\n+pub trait ClientDescriptor: Send + Sync + 'static {\n+    /// The SDK API trait type (e.g., `dyn CalculatorClientV1`).\n+    type Api: ?Sized + Send + Sync + 'static;\n+\n+    /// Module name for dependency graph and Directory resolution.\n+    const MODULE_NAME: &'static str;\n+\n+    /// Client configuration (transport, timeouts, backoff, availability).\n+    fn config() -> ClientConfig {\n+        ClientConfig::default()\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Phase 3: ClientProvider Infrastructure\n+\n+#### 3.1 RestClientProvider (Default)\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/rest_provider.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Universal lazy REST client provider (default transport).\n+\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+use std::time::{Duration, Instant};\n+\n+use parking_lot::RwLock;\n+use tokio::sync::Semaphore;\n+\n+use crate::client_hub::ClientHub;\n+use crate::directory::DirectoryClient;\n+use crate::clients::descriptor::ClientConfig;\n+use modkit_http::HttpClient;\n+\n+/// Error type for REST provider operations.\n+#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\n+pub enum RestProviderError {\n+    #[error(\"service not found in directory: {module_name}\")]\n+    ServiceNotFound { module_name: &'static str },\n+\n+    #[error(\"HTTP request failed: {0}\")]\n+    HttpError(#[source] modkit_http::HttpError),\n+\n+    #[error(\"directory resolution failed: {0}\")]\n+    DirectoryError(#[source] anyhow::Error),\n+\n+    #[error(\"service temporarily unavailable (backoff active)\")]\n+    Backoff { retry_after: Duration },\n+}\n+\n+struct CachedEndpoint {\n+    base_url: String,\n+    resolved_at: Instant,\n+}\n+\n+struct ProviderState {\n+    cached: Option<CachedEndpoint>,\n+    last_failure: Option<Instant>,\n+    failure_count: u32,\n+}\n+\n+/// Universal lazy REST client provider.\n+///\n+/// Handles:\n+/// - Lazy endpoint resolution via DirectoryClient\n+/// - Base URL caching with automatic eviction on errors\n+/// - Exponential backoff for reconnection attempts\n+/// - Rate limiting to prevent thundering herds\n+pub struct RestClientProvider {\n+    module_name: &'static str,\n+    config: ClientConfig,\n+    hub: Arc<ClientHub>,\n+    http_client: HttpClient,\n+    state: RwLock<ProviderState>,\n+    resolve_semaphore: Semaphore,\n+}\n+\n+impl RestClientProvider {\n+    pub fn new(\n+        module_name: &'static str,\n+        config: ClientConfig,\n+        hub: Arc<ClientHub>,\n+    ) -> Self {\n+        let http_client = HttpClient::builder()\n+            .timeout(config.request_timeout)\n+            .connect_timeout(config.connect_timeout)\n+            .build();\n+\n+        Self {\n+            module_name,\n+            config,\n+            hub,\n+            http_client,\n+            state: RwLock::new(ProviderState {\n+                cached: None,\n+                last_failure: None,\n+                failure_count: 0,\n+            }),\n+            resolve_semaphore: Semaphore::new(1),\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Get the base URL for the service, resolving lazily.\n+    pub async fn get_base_url(&self) -> Result<String, RestProviderError> {\n+        // Fast path: return cached endpoint\n+        {\n+            let state = self.state.read();\n+            if let Some(ref cached) = state.cached {\n+                return Ok(cached.base_url.clone());\n+            }\n+\n+            // Check backoff\n+            if let Some(last_failure) = state.last_failure {\n+                let backoff = self.calculate_backoff(state.failure_count);\n+                let elapsed = last_failure.elapsed();\n+                if elapsed < backoff {\n+                    return Err(RestProviderError::Backoff {\n+                        retry_after: backoff - elapsed,\n+                    });\n+                }\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        // Slow path: acquire semaphore and resolve\n+        let _permit = self.resolve_semaphore.acquire().await\n+            .expect(\"semaphore is never closed\");\n+\n+        // Double-check after acquiring semaphore\n+        {\n+            let state = self.state.read();\n+            if let Some(ref cached) = state.cached {\n+                return Ok(cached.base_url.clone());\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        self.resolve_internal().await\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Get the HTTP client for making requests.\n+    pub fn http_client(&self) -> &HttpClient {\n+        &self.http_client\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Evict the cached endpoint (call on transport errors).\n+    pub fn evict(&self) {\n+        let mut state = self.state.write();\n+        state.cached = None;\n+        state.last_failure = Some(Instant::now());\n+        state.failure_count = state.failure_count.saturating_add(1);\n+        tracing::warn!(\n+            module = self.module_name,\n+            failure_count = state.failure_count,\n+            \"Evicted cached REST endpoint\"\n+        );\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Reset failure state (call on successful request).\n+    pub fn reset_failures(&self) {\n+        let mut state = self.state.write();\n+        if state.failure_count > 0 {\n+            state.failure_count = 0;\n+            state.last_failure = None;\n+            tracing::debug!(module = self.module_name, \"Reset failure state after success\");\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    async fn resolve_internal(&self) -> Result<String, RestProviderError> {\n+        let directory = self\n+            .hub\n+            .get::<dyn DirectoryClient>()\n+            .map_err(|e| RestProviderError::DirectoryError(e.into()))?;\n+\n+        let endpoint = directory\n+            .resolve_rest_service(self.module_name)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(RestProviderError::DirectoryError)?;\n+\n+        tracing::debug!(\n+            module = self.module_name,\n+            base_url = %endpoint.base_url,\n+            \"Resolved REST endpoint\"\n+        );\n+\n+        {\n+            let mut state = self.state.write();\n+            state.cached = Some(CachedEndpoint {\n+                base_url: endpoint.base_url.clone(),\n+                resolved_at: Instant::now(),\n+            });\n+            state.failure_count = 0;\n+            state.last_failure = None;\n+        }\n+\n+        Ok(endpoint.base_url)\n+    }\n+\n+    fn calculate_backoff(&self, failure_count: u32) -> Duration {\n+        let base = Duration::from_millis(100);\n+        let max = self.config.max_backoff;\n+        let backoff = base.saturating_mul(2u32.saturating_pow(failure_count.min(10)));\n+        backoff.min(max)\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### 3.2 GrpcClientProvider (Optional)\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/grpc_provider.rs`\n+\n+> Feature-gated behind `feature = \"grpc\"` for streaming/high-throughput use cases.\n+\n+```rust\n+#[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+//! Lazy gRPC client provider (optional transport).\n+\n+// Implementation follows same pattern as RestClientProvider\n+// but manages tonic::transport::Channel instead of base URL\n+```\n+\n+#### 3.3 LazyClientError\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/error.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Error returned by lazy clients when the OoP dependency is unavailable.\n+#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\n+pub enum LazyClientError {\n+    #[error(\"service unavailable: {module_name}\")]\n+    Unavailable {\n+        module_name: &'static str,\n+        #[source]\n+        source: Box<dyn std::error::Error + Send + Sync>,\n+    },\n+\n+    #[error(\"request failed: {0}\")]\n+    RequestFailed(String),\n+\n+    #[error(\"response parsing failed: {0}\")]\n+    ParseError(#[source] serde_json::Error),\n+}\n+\n+impl LazyClientError {\n+    /// Returns true if this error indicates the service is temporarily unavailable.\n+    /// REST handlers should map this to HTTP 424 Failed Dependency.\n+    pub fn is_dependency_unavailable(&self) -> bool {\n+        matches!(self, LazyClientError::Unavailable { .. })\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Phase 4: SDK Crate Updates (calculator-sdk example)\n+\n+#### 4.1 Descriptor\n+\n+**Location**: `calculator-sdk/src/descriptor.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit::clients::descriptor::{ClientDescriptor, ClientConfig};\n+use crate::api::CalculatorClientV1;\n+\n+/// Descriptor for the Calculator client (REST by default).\n+pub struct CalculatorClientDescriptor;\n+\n+impl ClientDescriptor for CalculatorClientDescriptor {\n+    type Api = dyn CalculatorClientV1;\n+    const MODULE_NAME: &'static str = \"calculator\";\n+\n+    fn config() -> ClientConfig {\n+        ClientConfig::rest()  // Default: REST transport\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+// Optional: gRPC descriptor for high-throughput use cases\n+#[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+pub struct CalculatorGrpcClientDescriptor;\n+\n+#[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+impl ClientDescriptor for CalculatorGrpcClientDescriptor {\n+    type Api = dyn CalculatorClientV1;\n+    const MODULE_NAME: &'static str = \"calculator\";\n+\n+    fn config() -> ClientConfig {\n+        ClientConfig::grpc()  // Opt-in: gRPC transport\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### 4.2 Lazy Client Implementation\n+\n+**Location**: `calculator-sdk/src/lazy_client.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use modkit::clients::rest_provider::RestClientProvider;\n+use modkit_security::SecurityContext;\n+\n+use crate::api::{CalculatorClientV1, CalculatorError};\n+\n+/// Lazy client for Calculator service (REST transport).\n+pub struct LazyCalculatorClient {\n+    provider: Arc<RestClientProvider>,\n+}\n+\n+impl LazyCalculatorClient {\n+    pub fn new(provider: Arc<RestClientProvider>) -> Self {\n+        Self { provider }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl CalculatorClientV1 for LazyCalculatorClient {\n+    async fn add(&self, ctx: &SecurityContext, a: i64, b: i64) -> Result<i64, CalculatorError> {\n+        let base_url = self.provider.get_base_url().await.map_err(|e| {\n+            tracing::warn!(error = %e, \"Calculator service unavailable\");\n+            CalculatorError::Unavailable {\n+                message: format!(\"Calculator service unavailable: {}\", e),\n+            }\n+        })?;\n+\n+        let url = format!(\"{}/api/v1/calculator/add\", base_url);\n+        let response = self.provider.http_client()\n+            .post(&url)\n+            .header(\"x-tenant-id\", ctx.tenant_id().map(|t| t.to_string()).unwrap_or_default())\n+            .json(&serde_json::json!({ \"a\": a, \"b\": b }))\n+            .send()\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(|e| {\n+                if e.is_connect() || e.is_timeout() {\n+                    self.provider.evict();\n+                }\n+                CalculatorError::Unavailable {\n+                    message: format!(\"HTTP request failed: {}\", e),\n+                }\n+            })?;\n+\n+        if !response.status().is_success() {\n+            return Err(map_http_error(response.status(), &response.text().await.unwrap_or_default()));\n+        }\n+\n+        let result: AddResponse = response.json().await.map_err(|e| {\n+            CalculatorError::Internal { message: format!(\"Failed to parse response: {}\", e) }\n+        })?;\n+\n+        self.provider.reset_failures();\n+        Ok(result.result)\n+    }\n+\n+    // ... other methods follow the same pattern ...\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(serde::Deserialize)]\n+struct AddResponse { result: i64 }\n+\n+fn map_http_error(status: reqwest::StatusCode, body: &str) -> CalculatorError {\n+    match status.as_u16() {\n+        400 => CalculatorError::InvalidArgument { message: body.to_string() },\n+        404 => CalculatorError::NotFound { message: body.to_string() },\n+        503 => CalculatorError::Unavailable { message: body.to_string() },\n+        _ => CalculatorError::Internal { message: format!(\"HTTP {}: {}\", status, body) },\n+    }\n+}","path":"docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md","commit_id":"edd86e3e6cf91af1a08e3970d60dc26bc6acb6e6","original_commit_id":"45c842d72a1b66b9fd91d166c47739812b96116d","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Find modkit-related files and understand the structure\nfind . -type f -name \"*.rs\" | grep -i \"modkit\\|http\" | head -20\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 1450\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for modkit_http or modkit crate definition\nrg -n \"mod modkit_http|pub mod modkit|crate::modkit\" --type rust -i | head -20\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 54\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for HttpClient definition\nrg -n \"struct HttpClient|pub struct HttpClient\" --type rust -A 3 | head -30\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 948\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for Response and StatusCode usage with reqwest\nrg -n \"use reqwest|from reqwest|StatusCode|Response\" --type rust | grep -E \"(StatusCode|Response)\" | head -20\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 2696\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Read the HttpClient implementation to see method signatures and response types\ncat -n libs/modkit-http/src/client.rs | head -150\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 5928\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Look for response type definitions and method implementations\nrg -n \"pub fn (get|post|request|send)\" libs/modkit-http/src/ -A 5\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 1731\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check what types are exported from modkit_http\ncat -n libs/modkit-http/src/lib.rs | head -100\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 2700\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for Response or StatusCode type definitions in modkit_http\nrg -n \"type Response|struct Response|pub Response|pub use.*Response|pub use.*StatusCode\" libs/modkit-http/src/ -B 2 -A 2\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 8890\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Find the HttpResponse type definition\ncat -n libs/modkit-http/src/response.rs | head -200\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 7979\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Look for the status() method and what it returns\nrg -n \"fn status|pub fn status\" libs/modkit-http/src/ -A 3\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 295\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if http crate has StatusCode and what methods are available\nrg -n \"impl HttpResponse|status\\(\\)|text\\(\\)|json\\(\\)\" libs/modkit-http/src/response.rs -B 2 -A 5\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 3434\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Find RequestBuilder.send() method to see what it returns\nrg -n \"impl RequestBuilder|pub async fn send|pub fn send\" libs/modkit-http/src/request.rs -A 10\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 889\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check the return type of send() method\ncat -n libs/modkit-http/src/request.rs | grep -A 20 \"pub async fn send\"\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 1034\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Fix type mismatch: `http::StatusCode` vs `reqwest::StatusCode`.**\n\nThe `map_http_error` function signature uses `reqwest::StatusCode`, but `modkit_http::HttpClient` returns responses with `http::StatusCode` (from the `http` crate). The example will not compile as shown. Update the function signature to use `http::StatusCode`:\n\n```rust\nfn map_http_error(status: http::StatusCode, body: &str) -> CalculatorError {\n    match status.as_u16() {\n        400 => CalculatorError::InvalidArgument { message: body.to_string() },\n        404 => CalculatorError::NotFound { message: body.to_string() },\n        503 => CalculatorError::Unavailable { message: body.to_string() },\n        _ => CalculatorError::Internal { message: format!(\"HTTP {}: {}\", status, body) },\n    }\n}\n```\n\nAlternatively, add a note clarifying that the example assumes a client wrapper with reqwest types.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md` around lines 698 - 767,\nThe map_http_error signature currently expects reqwest::StatusCode but the\nLazyCalculatorClient implementation (response.status() from the HTTP client)\nyields http::StatusCode; change the map_http_error function signature to accept\nhttp::StatusCode (fn map_http_error(status: http::StatusCode, body: &str) ->\nCalculatorError) and update any imports/docs accordingly so map_http_error is\ncalled with the correct type from response.status(); alternatively, document\nthat the example assumes a reqwest-based client wrapper if you prefer to keep\nreqwest types.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-17T18:53:48Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T18:53:49Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2818571201","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2818571201"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2818571201"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2818571201/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":1462,"original_start_line":698,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":1532,"original_line":767,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":767,"position":1532,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2818625069","pull_request_review_id":3815792182,"id":2818625069,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6oAM4t","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1047 @@\n+# ADR-0003: Universal Lazy Typed REST Clients for OoP Modules\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+This proposal outlines a migration from gRPC to REST as the default transport for out-of-process (OoP) modules and introduces a **universal lazy typed client layer** for OoP module communication in ModKit. The implementation is structured in phases:\n+\n+1. **Phase 1 - REST as default transport**: Establish REST as the default OoP transport; gRPC becomes opt-in\n+2. **Phase 2 - ClientDescriptor trait**: SDK-defined metadata binding compile-time types to runtime resolution\n+3. **Phase 3 - ClientProvider**: Lazy resolution, caching, backoff, and reconnection infrastructure\n+4. **Phase 4 - Macro extension**: `clients = [...]` auto-registers lazy clients into `ClientHub`\n+5. **Phase 5 - Soft OoP deps**: Dependencies on OoP modules don't block startup\n+6. **Phase 6 - Registry extension**: Soft OoP dep resolution:  \n+\n+**Current pattern** (problematic):\n+```rust\n+// Consumer must wire client manually in init() - FAILS if OoP module is not ready\n+calculator_sdk::wire_client(hub, &*directory).await?;\n+```\n+\n+**Proposed pattern**:\n+```rust\n+#[modkit::module(\n+    name = \"calculator_gateway\",\n+    clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],  // REST by default\n+)]\n+// No wire_client() needed - lazy client auto-registered\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Problem Statement\n+\n+The current OoP client wiring pattern has several issues:\n+\n+1. **Eager wiring is fragile**: Consumer modules call `wire_client()` in `init()`, which fails if the OoP dependency is not yet available.\n+2. **Startup coupling**: The entire module fails to start if any OoP dependency is temporarily unavailable.\n+3. **Boilerplate duplication**: Each SDK repeats the same resolve/connect/cache logic.\n+4. **No graceful degradation**: Missing dependencies cause module-level failures instead of per-operation failures (HTTP 424).\n+5. **gRPC complexity**: Binary protobuf payloads are hard to debug; requires specialized tooling.\n+\n+### Current Pattern (calculator_gateway example)\n+\n+```rust\n+// Current: Consumer must wire client manually, and it happens eagerly\n+pub async fn wire_client(hub: &ClientHub, resolver: &dyn DirectoryClient) -> Result<()> {\n+    let endpoint = resolver.resolve_grpc_service(SERVICE_NAME).await?;  // Fails if OoP not ready\n+    let client = CalculatorGrpcClient::connect(&endpoint.uri).await?;   // Fails if network issue\n+    hub.register::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>(Arc::new(client));\n+    Ok(())\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Proposed Solution\n+\n+### Architecture Overview\n+\n+```text\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           SDK Crate (calculator-sdk)                    │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  CalculatorClientDescriptor                                             │\n+│    - MODULE_NAME: \"calculator\"                                          │\n+│    - Api: dyn CalculatorClientV1                                        │\n+│    - Transport: Rest (default) | Grpc (opt-in)                          │\n+│    - Availability Policy: Optional (default)                            │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  LazyCalculatorClient                                                   │\n+│    - Implements CalculatorClientV1                                      │\n+│    - Delegates to ClientProvider for lazy connection                    │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           ModKit (libs/modkit)                          │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  ClientProvider (transport-agnostic interface)                          │\n+│    - Lazy resolution via DirectoryClient                                │\n+│    - Endpoint/connection caching with eviction on error                 │\n+│    - Backoff/rate-limiting for reconnects                               │\n+│    - Transport middleware (timeouts, retries, tracing)                  │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  RestClientProvider (default) | GrpcClientProvider (feature = \"grpc\")   │\n+│    - Transport-specific implementations                                 │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  #[modkit::module] macro extension                                      │\n+│    - clients = [CalculatorClientDescriptor]                             │\n+│    - Auto-registers LazyClient into ClientHub                           │\n+│    - Auto-injects MODULE_NAME from each descriptor into deps            │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                      Consumer Module (calculator_gateway)               │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  #[modkit::module(                                                      │\n+│      name = \"calculator_gateway\",                                       │\n+│      capabilities = [rest],                                             │\n+│      clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],            │\n+│      // deps auto-injected: [\"calculator\"] from descriptor              │\n+│  )]                                                                     │\n+│                                                                         │\n+│  // No wire_client() call needed!                                       │\n+│  // Client is always available from ClientHub                           │\n+│  let calc = hub.get::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>()?;                       │\n+│  calc.add(ctx, a, b).await?;  // Lazy connect on first call             │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Detailed Implementation\n+\n+### Phase 1: REST as Default Transport\n+\n+**Rationale**: REST is simpler to debug, requires no code generation, and is sufficient for most OoP calls. gRPC remains available for streaming or high-throughput use cases.\n+\n+| Factor          | REST                            | gRPC                         |\n+|-----------------|---------------------------------|------------------------------|\n+| Debuggability   | ✅ curl, browser, any HTTP tool | ❌ Requires specialized tools |\n+| Simplicity      | ✅ JSON, standard HTTP          | ❌ Protobuf, code generation  |\n+| Browser support | ✅ Native                       | ❌ Requires gRPC-Web proxy    |\n+| API reuse       | ✅ Same as public REST API      | ❌ Separate interface         |\n+| Streaming       | ❌ Requires SSE/WebSocket       | ✅ Native support             |\n+| Performance     | ⚠️ JSON overhead                | ✅ Binary, efficient          |\n+\n+#### 1.1 Transport Enum\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/transport.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Transport protocol for OoP communication.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum Transport {\n+    /// REST with JSON serialization (default).\n+    #[default]\n+    Rest,\n+    /// gRPC with protobuf serialization (opt-in, requires feature = \"grpc\").\n+    #[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+    Grpc,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### 1.2 REST Service Discovery Infrastructure\n+\n+REST service discovery requires extending the existing `ModuleInstance`, `ModuleManager`, and `DirectoryClient` to track and resolve REST endpoints.\n+\n+##### 1.2.1 Extend `ModuleInstance` to track REST endpoints\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/runtime/module_manager.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Represents a single instance of a module\n+#[derive(Debug)]\n+pub struct ModuleInstance {\n+    pub module: String,\n+    pub instance_id: Uuid,\n+    pub control: Option<Endpoint>,\n+    pub grpc_services: HashMap<String, Endpoint>,\n+    pub rest_endpoint: Option<Endpoint>,  // NEW: REST base URL for this instance\n+    pub version: Option<String>,\n+    inner: Arc<parking_lot::RwLock<InstanceRuntimeState>>,\n+}\n+\n+impl ModuleInstance {\n+    // ... existing methods ...\n+\n+    /// Set the REST endpoint for this instance\n+    pub fn with_rest_endpoint(mut self, ep: Endpoint) -> Self {\n+        self.rest_endpoint = Some(ep);\n+        self\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.2 Extend `ModuleManager` with REST discovery\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/runtime/module_manager.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+impl ModuleManager {\n+    /// Pick a REST endpoint for a module using round-robin selection.\n+    /// Returns (module_name, instance, endpoint) if found.\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn pick_rest_endpoint_round_robin(\n+        &self,\n+        module_name: &str,\n+    ) -> Option<(String, Arc<ModuleInstance>, Endpoint)> {\n+        let instances_entry = self.inner.get(module_name)?;\n+        let instances = instances_entry.value();\n+\n+        // Filter to instances with REST endpoints and healthy/ready state\n+        let candidates: Vec<_> = instances\n+            .iter()\n+            .filter(|inst| {\n+                inst.rest_endpoint.is_some()\n+                    && matches!(inst.state(), InstanceState::Healthy | InstanceState::Ready)\n+            })\n+            .cloned()\n+            .collect();\n+\n+        if candidates.is_empty() {\n+            return None;\n+        }\n+\n+        let len = candidates.len();\n+        let rr_key = format!(\"rest:{}\", module_name);\n+        let mut counter = self.rr_counters.entry(rr_key).or_insert(0);\n+        let idx = *counter % len;\n+        *counter = (*counter + 1) % len;\n+\n+        candidates.get(idx).map(|inst| {\n+            (\n+                module_name.to_owned(),\n+                inst.clone(),\n+                inst.rest_endpoint.clone().expect(\"filtered above\"),\n+            )\n+        })\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.3 Extend `DirectoryClient` trait\n+\n+**Location**: `cf_system_sdks/src/directory.rs` (upstream crate — requires update)\n+\n+```rust\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait DirectoryClient: Send + Sync {\n+    /// Resolve REST endpoint for a module (default for OoP).\n+    async fn resolve_rest_service(&self, module_name: &str) -> Result<RestEndpoint>;\n+\n+    /// Resolve gRPC endpoint for a module (opt-in).\n+    async fn resolve_grpc_service(&self, service_name: &str) -> Result<ServiceEndpoint>;\n+\n+    // ... existing methods (list_instances, register_instance, etc.) ...\n+}\n+\n+/// REST endpoint for a module\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct RestEndpoint {\n+    /// Base URL for the module's REST API (e.g., \"http://calculator:8080\")\n+    pub base_url: String,\n+}\n+\n+impl RestEndpoint {\n+    pub fn new(base_url: impl Into<String>) -> Self {\n+        Self { base_url: base_url.into() }\n+    }\n+\n+    pub fn http(host: &str, port: u16) -> Self {\n+        Self { base_url: format!(\"http://{}:{}\", host, port) }\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.4 Implement `resolve_rest_service` in `LocalDirectoryClient`\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/directory.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl DirectoryClient for LocalDirectoryClient {\n+    async fn resolve_rest_service(&self, module_name: &str) -> Result<RestEndpoint> {\n+        if let Some((_, _, ep)) = self.mgr.pick_rest_endpoint_round_robin(module_name) {\n+            return Ok(RestEndpoint::new(ep.uri));\n+        }\n+\n+        anyhow::bail!(\"REST service not found or no healthy instances: {module_name}\")\n+    }\n+\n+    // ... existing methods unchanged ...\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.5 Extend `RegisterInstanceInfo` for REST registration\n+\n+**Location**: `cf_system_sdks/src/directory.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Information needed to register a module instance\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct RegisterInstanceInfo {\n+    pub module: String,\n+    pub instance_id: String,\n+    pub grpc_services: Vec<(String, ServiceEndpoint)>,\n+    pub rest_endpoint: Option<RestEndpoint>,  // NEW\n+    pub version: Option<String>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.6 OoP Module REST Registration\n+\n+When an OoP module starts, it registers its REST endpoint with the DirectoryService:\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/oop.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+async fn register_with_directory(\n+    directory: &dyn DirectoryClient,\n+    module_name: &str,\n+    instance_id: Uuid,\n+    rest_port: u16,\n+    grpc_services: Vec<(String, ServiceEndpoint)>,\n+) -> Result<()> {\n+    let info = RegisterInstanceInfo {\n+        module: module_name.to_owned(),\n+        instance_id: instance_id.to_string(),\n+        grpc_services,\n+        rest_endpoint: Some(RestEndpoint::http(\"0.0.0.0\", rest_port)),\n+        version: Some(env!(\"CARGO_PKG_VERSION\").to_owned()),\n+    };\n+\n+    directory.register_instance(info).await\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.7 Design Decisions\n+\n+| Decision | Rationale |\n+|----------|-----------|\n+| **One REST endpoint per instance** | Unlike gRPC (multiple services per instance), REST modules expose a single base URL with path-based routing |\n+| **Module-name based resolution** | REST discovery uses `module_name` (e.g., \"calculator\"), not service name |\n+| **Reuse existing health tracking** | REST endpoints use the same `InstanceState` and heartbeat mechanism as gRPC |\n+| **Symmetric API** | `resolve_rest_service()` mirrors `resolve_grpc_service()` for consistency |\n+\n+##### 1.2.8 Migration Notes\n+\n+1. **`cf_system_sdks` must be updated first** — Add `RestEndpoint`, extend `RegisterInstanceInfo`, and add `resolve_rest_service()` to `DirectoryClient`\n+2. **`ModuleInstance` is extended** — Existing code continues to work; `rest_endpoint` defaults to `None`\n+3. **OoP modules must register REST endpoints** — Update bootstrap to include REST port in registration\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Phase 2: ClientDescriptor Trait\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/descriptor.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Client descriptor traits for typed OoP client metadata.\n+\n+use std::time::Duration;\n+\n+/// Availability policy for OoP clients.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum ClientAvailabilityPolicy {\n+    /// Client is optional; operations fail gracefully with SDK error (maps to HTTP 424).\n+    #[default]\n+    Optional,\n+    /// Client is required; module readiness may depend on availability.\n+    Required,\n+}\n+\n+/// Configuration for client behavior.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct ClientConfig {\n+    /// Transport protocol (REST default, gRPC opt-in).\n+    pub transport: Transport,\n+    /// Connection timeout for initial connect.\n+    pub connect_timeout: Duration,\n+    /// Request timeout for individual calls.\n+    pub request_timeout: Duration,\n+    /// Maximum backoff duration between reconnect attempts.\n+    pub max_backoff: Duration,\n+    /// Availability policy.\n+    pub availability_policy: ClientAvailabilityPolicy,\n+}\n+\n+impl Default for ClientConfig {\n+    fn default() -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            transport: Transport::Rest,\n+            connect_timeout: Duration::from_secs(5),\n+            request_timeout: Duration::from_secs(30),\n+            max_backoff: Duration::from_secs(60),\n+            availability_policy: ClientAvailabilityPolicy::Optional,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl ClientConfig {\n+    /// Create a REST client config (default).\n+    pub fn rest() -> Self {\n+        Self::default()\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Create a gRPC client config (opt-in).\n+    #[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+    pub fn grpc() -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            transport: Transport::Grpc,\n+            ..Self::default()\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Descriptor for an OoP client, defined in SDK crates.\n+///\n+/// This trait binds compile-time type information to runtime metadata\n+/// needed for lazy client resolution and registration.\n+pub trait ClientDescriptor: Send + Sync + 'static {\n+    /// The SDK API trait type (e.g., `dyn CalculatorClientV1`).\n+    type Api: ?Sized + Send + Sync + 'static;\n+\n+    /// Module name for dependency graph and Directory resolution.\n+    const MODULE_NAME: &'static str;\n+\n+    /// Client configuration (transport, timeouts, backoff, availability).\n+    fn config() -> ClientConfig {\n+        ClientConfig::default()\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Phase 3: ClientProvider Infrastructure\n+\n+#### 3.1 RestClientProvider (Default)\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/rest_provider.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Universal lazy REST client provider (default transport).\n+\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+use std::time::{Duration, Instant};\n+\n+use parking_lot::RwLock;\n+use tokio::sync::Semaphore;\n+\n+use crate::client_hub::ClientHub;\n+use crate::directory::DirectoryClient;\n+use crate::clients::descriptor::ClientConfig;\n+use modkit_http::HttpClient;\n+\n+/// Error type for REST provider operations.\n+#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\n+pub enum RestProviderError {\n+    #[error(\"service not found in directory: {module_name}\")]\n+    ServiceNotFound { module_name: &'static str },\n+\n+    #[error(\"HTTP request failed: {0}\")]\n+    HttpError(#[source] modkit_http::HttpError),\n+\n+    #[error(\"directory resolution failed: {0}\")]\n+    DirectoryError(#[source] anyhow::Error),\n+\n+    #[error(\"service temporarily unavailable (backoff active)\")]\n+    Backoff { retry_after: Duration },\n+}\n+\n+struct CachedEndpoint {\n+    base_url: String,\n+    resolved_at: Instant,\n+}\n+\n+struct ProviderState {\n+    cached: Option<CachedEndpoint>,\n+    last_failure: Option<Instant>,\n+    failure_count: u32,\n+}\n+\n+/// Universal lazy REST client provider.\n+///\n+/// Handles:\n+/// - Lazy endpoint resolution via DirectoryClient\n+/// - Base URL caching with automatic eviction on errors\n+/// - Exponential backoff for reconnection attempts\n+/// - Rate limiting to prevent thundering herds\n+pub struct RestClientProvider {\n+    module_name: &'static str,\n+    config: ClientConfig,\n+    hub: Arc<ClientHub>,\n+    http_client: HttpClient,\n+    state: RwLock<ProviderState>,\n+    resolve_semaphore: Semaphore,\n+}\n+\n+impl RestClientProvider {\n+    pub fn new(\n+        module_name: &'static str,\n+        config: ClientConfig,\n+        hub: Arc<ClientHub>,\n+    ) -> Self {\n+        let http_client = HttpClient::builder()\n+            .timeout(config.request_timeout)\n+            .connect_timeout(config.connect_timeout)\n+            .build();\n+\n+        Self {\n+            module_name,\n+            config,\n+            hub,\n+            http_client,\n+            state: RwLock::new(ProviderState {\n+                cached: None,\n+                last_failure: None,\n+                failure_count: 0,\n+            }),\n+            resolve_semaphore: Semaphore::new(1),\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Get the base URL for the service, resolving lazily.\n+    pub async fn get_base_url(&self) -> Result<String, RestProviderError> {\n+        // Fast path: return cached endpoint\n+        {\n+            let state = self.state.read();\n+            if let Some(ref cached) = state.cached {\n+                return Ok(cached.base_url.clone());\n+            }\n+\n+            // Check backoff\n+            if let Some(last_failure) = state.last_failure {\n+                let backoff = self.calculate_backoff(state.failure_count);\n+                let elapsed = last_failure.elapsed();\n+                if elapsed < backoff {\n+                    return Err(RestProviderError::Backoff {\n+                        retry_after: backoff - elapsed,\n+                    });\n+                }\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        // Slow path: acquire semaphore and resolve\n+        let _permit = self.resolve_semaphore.acquire().await\n+            .expect(\"semaphore is never closed\");\n+\n+        // Double-check after acquiring semaphore\n+        {\n+            let state = self.state.read();\n+            if let Some(ref cached) = state.cached {\n+                return Ok(cached.base_url.clone());\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        self.resolve_internal().await\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Get the HTTP client for making requests.\n+    pub fn http_client(&self) -> &HttpClient {\n+        &self.http_client\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Evict the cached endpoint (call on transport errors).\n+    pub fn evict(&self) {\n+        let mut state = self.state.write();\n+        state.cached = None;\n+        state.last_failure = Some(Instant::now());\n+        state.failure_count = state.failure_count.saturating_add(1);\n+        tracing::warn!(\n+            module = self.module_name,\n+            failure_count = state.failure_count,\n+            \"Evicted cached REST endpoint\"\n+        );\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Reset failure state (call on successful request).\n+    pub fn reset_failures(&self) {\n+        let mut state = self.state.write();\n+        if state.failure_count > 0 {\n+            state.failure_count = 0;\n+            state.last_failure = None;\n+            tracing::debug!(module = self.module_name, \"Reset failure state after success\");\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    async fn resolve_internal(&self) -> Result<String, RestProviderError> {\n+        let directory = self\n+            .hub\n+            .get::<dyn DirectoryClient>()\n+            .map_err(|e| RestProviderError::DirectoryError(e.into()))?;\n+\n+        let endpoint = directory\n+            .resolve_rest_service(self.module_name)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(RestProviderError::DirectoryError)?;\n+\n+        tracing::debug!(\n+            module = self.module_name,\n+            base_url = %endpoint.base_url,\n+            \"Resolved REST endpoint\"\n+        );\n+\n+        {\n+            let mut state = self.state.write();\n+            state.cached = Some(CachedEndpoint {\n+                base_url: endpoint.base_url.clone(),\n+                resolved_at: Instant::now(),\n+            });\n+            state.failure_count = 0;\n+            state.last_failure = None;\n+        }\n+\n+        Ok(endpoint.base_url)\n+    }\n+\n+    fn calculate_backoff(&self, failure_count: u32) -> Duration {\n+        let base = Duration::from_millis(100);\n+        let max = self.config.max_backoff;\n+        let backoff = base.saturating_mul(2u32.saturating_pow(failure_count.min(10)));\n+        backoff.min(max)\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### 3.2 GrpcClientProvider (Optional)\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/grpc_provider.rs`\n+\n+> Feature-gated behind `feature = \"grpc\"` for streaming/high-throughput use cases.\n+\n+```rust\n+#[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+//! Lazy gRPC client provider (optional transport).\n+\n+// Implementation follows same pattern as RestClientProvider\n+// but manages tonic::transport::Channel instead of base URL\n+```\n+\n+#### 3.3 LazyClientError\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/error.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Error returned by lazy clients when the OoP dependency is unavailable.\n+#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\n+pub enum LazyClientError {\n+    #[error(\"service unavailable: {module_name}\")]\n+    Unavailable {\n+        module_name: &'static str,\n+        #[source]\n+        source: Box<dyn std::error::Error + Send + Sync>,\n+    },\n+\n+    #[error(\"request failed: {0}\")]\n+    RequestFailed(String),\n+\n+    #[error(\"response parsing failed: {0}\")]\n+    ParseError(#[source] serde_json::Error),\n+}\n+\n+impl LazyClientError {\n+    /// Returns true if this error indicates the service is temporarily unavailable.\n+    /// REST handlers should map this to HTTP 424 Failed Dependency.\n+    pub fn is_dependency_unavailable(&self) -> bool {\n+        matches!(self, LazyClientError::Unavailable { .. })\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Phase 4: SDK Crate Updates (calculator-sdk example)\n+\n+#### 4.1 Descriptor\n+\n+**Location**: `calculator-sdk/src/descriptor.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit::clients::descriptor::{ClientDescriptor, ClientConfig};\n+use crate::api::CalculatorClientV1;\n+\n+/// Descriptor for the Calculator client (REST by default).\n+pub struct CalculatorClientDescriptor;\n+\n+impl ClientDescriptor for CalculatorClientDescriptor {\n+    type Api = dyn CalculatorClientV1;\n+    const MODULE_NAME: &'static str = \"calculator\";\n+\n+    fn config() -> ClientConfig {\n+        ClientConfig::rest()  // Default: REST transport\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+// Optional: gRPC descriptor for high-throughput use cases\n+#[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+pub struct CalculatorGrpcClientDescriptor;\n+\n+#[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+impl ClientDescriptor for CalculatorGrpcClientDescriptor {\n+    type Api = dyn CalculatorClientV1;\n+    const MODULE_NAME: &'static str = \"calculator\";\n+\n+    fn config() -> ClientConfig {\n+        ClientConfig::grpc()  // Opt-in: gRPC transport\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### 4.2 Lazy Client Implementation\n+\n+**Location**: `calculator-sdk/src/lazy_client.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use modkit::clients::rest_provider::RestClientProvider;\n+use modkit_security::SecurityContext;\n+\n+use crate::api::{CalculatorClientV1, CalculatorError};\n+\n+/// Lazy client for Calculator service (REST transport).\n+pub struct LazyCalculatorClient {\n+    provider: Arc<RestClientProvider>,\n+}\n+\n+impl LazyCalculatorClient {\n+    pub fn new(provider: Arc<RestClientProvider>) -> Self {\n+        Self { provider }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl CalculatorClientV1 for LazyCalculatorClient {\n+    async fn add(&self, ctx: &SecurityContext, a: i64, b: i64) -> Result<i64, CalculatorError> {\n+        let base_url = self.provider.get_base_url().await.map_err(|e| {\n+            tracing::warn!(error = %e, \"Calculator service unavailable\");\n+            CalculatorError::Unavailable {\n+                message: format!(\"Calculator service unavailable: {}\", e),\n+            }\n+        })?;\n+\n+        let url = format!(\"{}/api/v1/calculator/add\", base_url);\n+        let response = self.provider.http_client()\n+            .post(&url)\n+            .header(\"x-tenant-id\", ctx.tenant_id().map(|t| t.to_string()).unwrap_or_default())\n+            .json(&serde_json::json!({ \"a\": a, \"b\": b }))\n+            .send()\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(|e| {\n+                if e.is_connect() || e.is_timeout() {\n+                    self.provider.evict();\n+                }\n+                CalculatorError::Unavailable {\n+                    message: format!(\"HTTP request failed: {}\", e),\n+                }\n+            })?;\n+\n+        if !response.status().is_success() {\n+            return Err(map_http_error(response.status(), &response.text().await.unwrap_or_default()));\n+        }\n+\n+        let result: AddResponse = response.json().await.map_err(|e| {\n+            CalculatorError::Internal { message: format!(\"Failed to parse response: {}\", e) }\n+        })?;\n+\n+        self.provider.reset_failures();\n+        Ok(result.result)\n+    }\n+\n+    // ... other methods follow the same pattern ...\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(serde::Deserialize)]\n+struct AddResponse { result: i64 }\n+\n+/// Maps HTTP status codes to SDK errors.\n+/// Note: This example assumes a reqwest-based HTTP client wrapper.\n+fn map_http_error(status: reqwest::StatusCode, body: &str) -> CalculatorError {\n+    match status.as_u16() {\n+        400 => CalculatorError::InvalidArgument { message: body.to_string() },\n+        404 => CalculatorError::NotFound { message: body.to_string() },\n+        503 => CalculatorError::Unavailable { message: body.to_string() },\n+        _ => CalculatorError::Internal { message: format!(\"HTTP {}: {}\", status, body) },\n+    }\n+}","path":"docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md","commit_id":"0894889d189d3891110c1c1b1cb0855ecc970855","original_commit_id":"0894889d189d3891110c1c1b1cb0855ecc970855","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Documentation inconsistency: HTTP client type vs implementation.**\n\nThe comment on line 761 states this example assumes a reqwest-based HTTP client wrapper, but the code above (lines 727-744) directly uses `self.provider.http_client()` from `modkit_http::HttpClient`, which returns `http::StatusCode` (from the `http` crate), not `reqwest::StatusCode`. Either:\n\n1. Update the comment to clarify that `map_http_error` is a conceptual example and implementers should use `http::StatusCode` in practice, or\n2. Change the function signature to match the actual implementation shown above\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested clarification</summary>\n\n```diff\n #[derive(serde::Deserialize)]\n struct AddResponse { result: i64 }\n\n-/// Maps HTTP status codes to SDK errors.\n-/// Note: This example assumes a reqwest-based HTTP client wrapper.\n-fn map_http_error(status: reqwest::StatusCode, body: &str) -> CalculatorError {\n+/// Maps HTTP status codes to SDK errors.\n+/// Note: Signature should use http::StatusCode to match modkit_http::HttpClient shown above.\n+fn map_http_error(status: http::StatusCode, body: &str) -> CalculatorError {\n     match status.as_u16() {\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n#[derive(serde::Deserialize)]\nstruct AddResponse { result: i64 }\n\n/// Maps HTTP status codes to SDK errors.\n/// Note: Signature should use http::StatusCode to match modkit_http::HttpClient shown above.\nfn map_http_error(status: http::StatusCode, body: &str) -> CalculatorError {\n    match status.as_u16() {\n        400 => CalculatorError::InvalidArgument { message: body.to_string() },\n        404 => CalculatorError::NotFound { message: body.to_string() },\n        503 => CalculatorError::Unavailable { message: body.to_string() },\n        _ => CalculatorError::Internal { message: format!(\"HTTP {}: {}\", status, body) },\n    }\n}\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md` around lines 761 - 769,\nThe doc example's map_http_error signature is inconsistent with the actual usage\nof self.provider.http_client() (modkit_http::HttpClient) which returns\nhttp::StatusCode, not reqwest::StatusCode; update map_http_error to accept\nhttp::StatusCode (from the http crate) instead of reqwest::StatusCode and keep\nthe same body: &str handling and match on status.as_u16() so it matches the\nsurrounding implementation, or alternatively change the surrounding usage to\nprovide a reqwest::StatusCode if you prefer that client—adjust all references to\nmap_http_error and calls from self.provider.http_client() accordingly.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-17T19:07:22Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T19:07:22Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2818625069","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2818625069"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2818625069"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2818625069/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":761,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":769,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":769,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2828719155","pull_request_review_id":3826843149,"id":2828719155,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6omtQz","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1050 @@\n+# ADR-0003: Universal Lazy Typed REST Clients for OoP Modules\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+This proposal outlines a migration from gRPC to REST as the default transport for out-of-process (OoP) modules and introduces a **universal lazy typed client layer** for OoP module communication in ModKit. The implementation is structured in phases:\n+\n+1. **Phase 1 - REST as default transport**: Establish REST as the default OoP transport; gRPC becomes opt-in\n+2. **Phase 2 - ClientDescriptor trait**: SDK-defined metadata binding compile-time types to runtime resolution\n+3. **Phase 3 - ClientProvider**: Lazy resolution, caching, backoff, and reconnection infrastructure\n+4. **Phase 4 - Macro extension**: `clients = [...]` auto-registers lazy clients into `ClientHub`\n+5. **Phase 5 - Soft OoP deps**: Dependencies on OoP modules don't block startup\n+6. **Phase 6 - Registry extension**: Soft OoP dep resolution:  \n+\n+**Current pattern** (problematic):\n+```rust\n+// Consumer must wire client manually in init() - FAILS if OoP module is not ready\n+calculator_sdk::wire_client(hub, &*directory).await?;\n+```\n+\n+**Proposed pattern**:\n+```rust\n+#[modkit::module(\n+    name = \"calculator_gateway\",\n+    clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],  // REST by default\n+)]\n+// No wire_client() needed - lazy client auto-registered\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Problem Statement\n+\n+The current OoP client wiring pattern has several issues:\n+\n+1. **Eager wiring is fragile**: Consumer modules call `wire_client()` in `init()`, which fails if the OoP dependency is not yet available.\n+2. **Startup coupling**: The entire module fails to start if any OoP dependency is temporarily unavailable.\n+3. **Boilerplate duplication**: Each SDK repeats the same resolve/connect/cache logic.\n+4. **No graceful degradation**: Missing dependencies cause module-level failures instead of per-operation failures (HTTP 424).\n+5. **gRPC complexity**: Binary protobuf payloads are hard to debug; requires specialized tooling.\n+\n+### Current Pattern (calculator_gateway example)\n+\n+```rust\n+// Current: Consumer must wire client manually, and it happens eagerly\n+pub async fn wire_client(hub: &ClientHub, resolver: &dyn DirectoryClient) -> Result<()> {\n+    let endpoint = resolver.resolve_grpc_service(SERVICE_NAME).await?;  // Fails if OoP not ready\n+    let client = CalculatorGrpcClient::connect(&endpoint.uri).await?;   // Fails if network issue\n+    hub.register::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>(Arc::new(client));\n+    Ok(())\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Proposed Solution\n+\n+### Architecture Overview\n+\n+```text\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           SDK Crate (calculator-sdk)                    │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  CalculatorClientDescriptor                                             │\n+│    - MODULE_NAME: \"calculator\"                                          │\n+│    - Api: dyn CalculatorClientV1                                        │\n+│    - Transport: Rest (default) | Grpc (opt-in)                          │\n+│    - Availability Policy: Optional (default)                            │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  LazyCalculatorClient                                                   │\n+│    - Implements CalculatorClientV1                                      │\n+│    - Delegates to ClientProvider for lazy connection                    │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           ModKit (libs/modkit)                          │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  ClientProvider (transport-agnostic interface)                          │\n+│    - Lazy resolution via DirectoryClient                                │\n+│    - Endpoint/connection caching with eviction on error                 │\n+│    - Backoff/rate-limiting for reconnects                               │\n+│    - Transport middleware (timeouts, retries, tracing)                  │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  RestClientProvider (default) | GrpcClientProvider (feature = \"grpc\")   │\n+│    - Transport-specific implementations                                 │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  #[modkit::module] macro extension                                      │\n+│    - clients = [CalculatorClientDescriptor]                             │\n+│    - Auto-registers LazyClient into ClientHub                           │\n+│    - Auto-injects MODULE_NAME from each descriptor into deps            │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                      Consumer Module (calculator_gateway)               │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  #[modkit::module(                                                      │\n+│      name = \"calculator_gateway\",                                       │\n+│      capabilities = [rest],                                             │\n+│      clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],            │\n+│      // deps auto-injected: [\"calculator\"] from descriptor              │\n+│  )]                                                                     │\n+│                                                                         │\n+│  // No wire_client() call needed!                                       │\n+│  // Client is always available from ClientHub                           │\n+│  let calc = hub.get::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>()?;                       │\n+│  calc.add(ctx, a, b).await?;  // Lazy connect on first call             │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Detailed Implementation\n+\n+### Phase 1: REST as Default Transport\n+\n+**Rationale**: REST is simpler to debug, requires no code generation, and is sufficient for most OoP calls. gRPC remains available for streaming or high-throughput use cases.\n+\n+| Factor          | REST                            | gRPC                         |\n+|-----------------|---------------------------------|------------------------------|\n+| Debuggability   | ✅ curl, browser, any HTTP tool | ❌ Requires specialized tools |\n+| Simplicity      | ✅ JSON, standard HTTP          | ❌ Protobuf, code generation  |\n+| Browser support | ✅ Native                       | ❌ Requires gRPC-Web proxy    |\n+| API reuse       | ✅ Same as public REST API      | ❌ Separate interface         |\n+| Streaming       | ❌ Requires SSE/WebSocket       | ✅ Native support             |\n+| Performance     | ⚠️ JSON overhead                | ✅ Binary, efficient          |\n+\n+#### 1.1 Transport Enum\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/transport.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Transport protocol for OoP communication.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum Transport {\n+    /// REST with JSON serialization (default).\n+    #[default]\n+    Rest,\n+    /// gRPC with protobuf serialization (opt-in, requires feature = \"grpc\").\n+    #[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+    Grpc,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### 1.2 REST Service Discovery Infrastructure\n+\n+REST service discovery requires extending the existing `ModuleInstance`, `ModuleManager`, and `DirectoryClient` to track and resolve REST endpoints.\n+\n+##### 1.2.1 Extend `ModuleInstance` to track REST endpoints\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/runtime/module_manager.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Represents a single instance of a module\n+#[derive(Debug)]\n+pub struct ModuleInstance {\n+    pub module: String,\n+    pub instance_id: Uuid,\n+    pub control: Option<Endpoint>,\n+    pub grpc_services: HashMap<String, Endpoint>,\n+    pub rest_endpoint: Option<Endpoint>,  // NEW: REST base URL for this instance\n+    pub version: Option<String>,\n+    inner: Arc<parking_lot::RwLock<InstanceRuntimeState>>,\n+}\n+\n+impl ModuleInstance {\n+    // ... existing methods ...\n+\n+    /// Set the REST endpoint for this instance\n+    pub fn with_rest_endpoint(mut self, ep: Endpoint) -> Self {\n+        self.rest_endpoint = Some(ep);\n+        self\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.2 Extend `ModuleManager` with REST discovery\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/runtime/module_manager.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+impl ModuleManager {\n+    /// Pick a REST endpoint for a module using round-robin selection.\n+    /// Returns (module_name, instance, endpoint) if found.\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn pick_rest_endpoint_round_robin(\n+        &self,\n+        module_name: &str,\n+    ) -> Option<(String, Arc<ModuleInstance>, Endpoint)> {\n+        let instances_entry = self.inner.get(module_name)?;\n+        let instances = instances_entry.value();\n+\n+        // Filter to instances with REST endpoints and healthy/ready state\n+        let candidates: Vec<_> = instances\n+            .iter()\n+            .filter(|inst| {\n+                inst.rest_endpoint.is_some()\n+                    && matches!(inst.state(), InstanceState::Healthy | InstanceState::Ready)\n+            })\n+            .cloned()\n+            .collect();\n+\n+        if candidates.is_empty() {\n+            return None;\n+        }\n+\n+        let len = candidates.len();\n+        let rr_key = format!(\"rest:{}\", module_name);\n+        let mut counter = self.rr_counters.entry(rr_key).or_insert(0);\n+        let idx = *counter % len;\n+        *counter = (*counter + 1) % len;\n+\n+        candidates.get(idx).map(|inst| {\n+            (\n+                module_name.to_owned(),\n+                inst.clone(),\n+                inst.rest_endpoint.clone().expect(\"filtered above\"),\n+            )\n+        })\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.3 Extend `DirectoryClient` trait\n+\n+**Location**: `cf_system_sdks/src/directory.rs` (upstream crate — requires update)\n+\n+```rust\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait DirectoryClient: Send + Sync {\n+    /// Resolve REST endpoint for a module (default for OoP).\n+    async fn resolve_rest_service(&self, module_name: &str) -> Result<RestEndpoint>;\n+\n+    /// Resolve gRPC endpoint for a module (opt-in).\n+    async fn resolve_grpc_service(&self, service_name: &str) -> Result<ServiceEndpoint>;\n+\n+    // ... existing methods (list_instances, register_instance, etc.) ...\n+}\n+\n+/// REST endpoint for a module\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct RestEndpoint {\n+    /// Base URL for the module's REST API (e.g., \"http://calculator:8080\")\n+    pub base_url: String,\n+}\n+\n+impl RestEndpoint {\n+    pub fn new(base_url: impl Into<String>) -> Self {\n+        Self { base_url: base_url.into() }\n+    }\n+\n+    pub fn http(host: &str, port: u16) -> Self {\n+        Self { base_url: format!(\"http://{}:{}\", host, port) }\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.4 Implement `resolve_rest_service` in `LocalDirectoryClient`\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/directory.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl DirectoryClient for LocalDirectoryClient {\n+    async fn resolve_rest_service(&self, module_name: &str) -> Result<RestEndpoint> {\n+        if let Some((_, _, ep)) = self.mgr.pick_rest_endpoint_round_robin(module_name) {\n+            return Ok(RestEndpoint::new(ep.uri));\n+        }\n+\n+        anyhow::bail!(\"REST service not found or no healthy instances: {module_name}\")\n+    }\n+\n+    // ... existing methods unchanged ...\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.5 Extend `RegisterInstanceInfo` for REST registration\n+\n+**Location**: `cf_system_sdks/src/directory.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Information needed to register a module instance\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct RegisterInstanceInfo {\n+    pub module: String,\n+    pub instance_id: String,\n+    pub grpc_services: Vec<(String, ServiceEndpoint)>,\n+    pub rest_endpoint: Option<RestEndpoint>,  // NEW\n+    pub version: Option<String>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.6 OoP Module REST Registration\n+\n+When an OoP module starts, it registers its REST endpoint with the DirectoryService:\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/oop.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+async fn register_with_directory(\n+    directory: &dyn DirectoryClient,\n+    module_name: &str,\n+    instance_id: Uuid,\n+    rest_port: u16,\n+    grpc_services: Vec<(String, ServiceEndpoint)>,\n+) -> Result<()> {\n+    let info = RegisterInstanceInfo {\n+        module: module_name.to_owned(),\n+        instance_id: instance_id.to_string(),\n+        grpc_services,\n+        rest_endpoint: Some(RestEndpoint::http(\"0.0.0.0\", rest_port)),\n+        version: Some(env!(\"CARGO_PKG_VERSION\").to_owned()),\n+    };\n+\n+    directory.register_instance(info).await\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.7 Design Decisions\n+\n+| Decision | Rationale |\n+|----------|-----------|\n+| **One REST endpoint per instance** | Unlike gRPC (multiple services per instance), REST modules expose a single base URL with path-based routing |\n+| **Module-name based resolution** | REST discovery uses `module_name` (e.g., \"calculator\"), not service name |\n+| **Reuse existing health tracking** | REST endpoints use the same `InstanceState` and heartbeat mechanism as gRPC |\n+| **Symmetric API** | `resolve_rest_service()` mirrors `resolve_grpc_service()` for consistency |\n+\n+##### 1.2.8 Migration Notes\n+\n+1. **`cf_system_sdks` must be updated first** — Add `RestEndpoint`, extend `RegisterInstanceInfo`, and add `resolve_rest_service()` to `DirectoryClient`\n+2. **`ModuleInstance` is extended** — Existing code continues to work; `rest_endpoint` defaults to `None`\n+3. **OoP modules must register REST endpoints** — Update bootstrap to include REST port in registration\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Phase 2: ClientDescriptor Trait\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/descriptor.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Client descriptor traits for typed OoP client metadata.\n+\n+use std::time::Duration;\n+\n+/// Availability policy for OoP clients.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum ClientAvailabilityPolicy {\n+    /// Client is optional; operations fail gracefully with SDK error (maps to HTTP 424).\n+    #[default]\n+    Optional,\n+    /// Client is required; module readiness may depend on availability.\n+    Required,\n+}\n+\n+/// Configuration for client behavior.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct ClientConfig {\n+    /// Transport protocol (REST default, gRPC opt-in).\n+    pub transport: Transport,\n+    /// Connection timeout for initial connect.\n+    pub connect_timeout: Duration,\n+    /// Request timeout for individual calls.\n+    pub request_timeout: Duration,\n+    /// Maximum backoff duration between reconnect attempts.\n+    pub max_backoff: Duration,\n+    /// Availability policy.\n+    pub availability_policy: ClientAvailabilityPolicy,\n+}\n+\n+impl Default for ClientConfig {\n+    fn default() -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            transport: Transport::Rest,\n+            connect_timeout: Duration::from_secs(5),\n+            request_timeout: Duration::from_secs(30),\n+            max_backoff: Duration::from_secs(60),\n+            availability_policy: ClientAvailabilityPolicy::Optional,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl ClientConfig {\n+    /// Create a REST client config (default).\n+    pub fn rest() -> Self {\n+        Self::default()\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Create a gRPC client config (opt-in).\n+    #[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+    pub fn grpc() -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            transport: Transport::Grpc,\n+            ..Self::default()\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Descriptor for an OoP client, defined in SDK crates.\n+///\n+/// This trait binds compile-time type information to runtime metadata\n+/// needed for lazy client resolution and registration.\n+pub trait ClientDescriptor: Send + Sync + 'static {\n+    /// The SDK API trait type (e.g., `dyn CalculatorClientV1`).\n+    type Api: ?Sized + Send + Sync + 'static;\n+\n+    /// Module name for dependency graph and Directory resolution.\n+    const MODULE_NAME: &'static str;","path":"docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md","commit_id":"edd86e3e6cf91af1a08e3970d60dc26bc6acb6e6","original_commit_id":"030bc79ea9322b429e351c332cbffd4f44791b3c","user":{"login":"striped-zebra-dev","id":225538363,"node_id":"U_kgDODXFxOw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225538363?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/striped-zebra-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"As I understand it, the module name is introduced by the client implementation that is brought onto the platform.\n\nWhy do we require each service to specify this value explicitly? Can it be derived automatically instead?\n\nAlso, is there any practical benefit to changing the module name between releases?","created_at":"2026-02-19T16:03:44Z","updated_at":"2026-02-19T16:03:44Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2828719155","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2828719155"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2828719155"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2828719155/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":411,"original_line":407,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":407,"position":411,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2828771682","pull_request_review_id":3826905697,"id":2828771682,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6om6Fi","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1050 @@\n+# ADR-0003: Universal Lazy Typed REST Clients for OoP Modules\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+This proposal outlines a migration from gRPC to REST as the default transport for out-of-process (OoP) modules and introduces a **universal lazy typed client layer** for OoP module communication in ModKit. The implementation is structured in phases:\n+\n+1. **Phase 1 - REST as default transport**: Establish REST as the default OoP transport; gRPC becomes opt-in\n+2. **Phase 2 - ClientDescriptor trait**: SDK-defined metadata binding compile-time types to runtime resolution\n+3. **Phase 3 - ClientProvider**: Lazy resolution, caching, backoff, and reconnection infrastructure\n+4. **Phase 4 - Macro extension**: `clients = [...]` auto-registers lazy clients into `ClientHub`\n+5. **Phase 5 - Soft OoP deps**: Dependencies on OoP modules don't block startup\n+6. **Phase 6 - Registry extension**: Soft OoP dep resolution:  \n+\n+**Current pattern** (problematic):\n+```rust\n+// Consumer must wire client manually in init() - FAILS if OoP module is not ready\n+calculator_sdk::wire_client(hub, &*directory).await?;\n+```\n+\n+**Proposed pattern**:\n+```rust\n+#[modkit::module(\n+    name = \"calculator_gateway\",\n+    clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],  // REST by default\n+)]\n+// No wire_client() needed - lazy client auto-registered\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Problem Statement\n+\n+The current OoP client wiring pattern has several issues:\n+\n+1. **Eager wiring is fragile**: Consumer modules call `wire_client()` in `init()`, which fails if the OoP dependency is not yet available.\n+2. **Startup coupling**: The entire module fails to start if any OoP dependency is temporarily unavailable.\n+3. **Boilerplate duplication**: Each SDK repeats the same resolve/connect/cache logic.\n+4. **No graceful degradation**: Missing dependencies cause module-level failures instead of per-operation failures (HTTP 424).\n+5. **gRPC complexity**: Binary protobuf payloads are hard to debug; requires specialized tooling.\n+\n+### Current Pattern (calculator_gateway example)\n+\n+```rust\n+// Current: Consumer must wire client manually, and it happens eagerly\n+pub async fn wire_client(hub: &ClientHub, resolver: &dyn DirectoryClient) -> Result<()> {\n+    let endpoint = resolver.resolve_grpc_service(SERVICE_NAME).await?;  // Fails if OoP not ready\n+    let client = CalculatorGrpcClient::connect(&endpoint.uri).await?;   // Fails if network issue\n+    hub.register::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>(Arc::new(client));\n+    Ok(())\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Proposed Solution\n+\n+### Architecture Overview\n+\n+```text\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           SDK Crate (calculator-sdk)                    │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  CalculatorClientDescriptor                                             │\n+│    - MODULE_NAME: \"calculator\"                                          │\n+│    - Api: dyn CalculatorClientV1                                        │\n+│    - Transport: Rest (default) | Grpc (opt-in)                          │\n+│    - Availability Policy: Optional (default)                            │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  LazyCalculatorClient                                                   │\n+│    - Implements CalculatorClientV1                                      │\n+│    - Delegates to ClientProvider for lazy connection                    │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           ModKit (libs/modkit)                          │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  ClientProvider (transport-agnostic interface)                          │\n+│    - Lazy resolution via DirectoryClient                                │\n+│    - Endpoint/connection caching with eviction on error                 │\n+│    - Backoff/rate-limiting for reconnects                               │\n+│    - Transport middleware (timeouts, retries, tracing)                  │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  RestClientProvider (default) | GrpcClientProvider (feature = \"grpc\")   │\n+│    - Transport-specific implementations                                 │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  #[modkit::module] macro extension                                      │\n+│    - clients = [CalculatorClientDescriptor]                             │\n+│    - Auto-registers LazyClient into ClientHub                           │\n+│    - Auto-injects MODULE_NAME from each descriptor into deps            │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                      Consumer Module (calculator_gateway)               │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  #[modkit::module(                                                      │\n+│      name = \"calculator_gateway\",                                       │\n+│      capabilities = [rest],                                             │\n+│      clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],            │\n+│      // deps auto-injected: [\"calculator\"] from descriptor              │\n+│  )]                                                                     │\n+│                                                                         │\n+│  // No wire_client() call needed!                                       │\n+│  // Client is always available from ClientHub                           │\n+│  let calc = hub.get::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>()?;                       │\n+│  calc.add(ctx, a, b).await?;  // Lazy connect on first call             │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Detailed Implementation\n+\n+### Phase 1: REST as Default Transport\n+\n+**Rationale**: REST is simpler to debug, requires no code generation, and is sufficient for most OoP calls. gRPC remains available for streaming or high-throughput use cases.\n+\n+| Factor          | REST                            | gRPC                         |\n+|-----------------|---------------------------------|------------------------------|\n+| Debuggability   | ✅ curl, browser, any HTTP tool | ❌ Requires specialized tools |\n+| Simplicity      | ✅ JSON, standard HTTP          | ❌ Protobuf, code generation  |\n+| Browser support | ✅ Native                       | ❌ Requires gRPC-Web proxy    |\n+| API reuse       | ✅ Same as public REST API      | ❌ Separate interface         |\n+| Streaming       | ❌ Requires SSE/WebSocket       | ✅ Native support             |\n+| Performance     | ⚠️ JSON overhead                | ✅ Binary, efficient          |\n+\n+#### 1.1 Transport Enum\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/transport.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Transport protocol for OoP communication.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum Transport {\n+    /// REST with JSON serialization (default).\n+    #[default]\n+    Rest,\n+    /// gRPC with protobuf serialization (opt-in, requires feature = \"grpc\").\n+    #[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+    Grpc,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### 1.2 REST Service Discovery Infrastructure\n+\n+REST service discovery requires extending the existing `ModuleInstance`, `ModuleManager`, and `DirectoryClient` to track and resolve REST endpoints.\n+\n+##### 1.2.1 Extend `ModuleInstance` to track REST endpoints\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/runtime/module_manager.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Represents a single instance of a module\n+#[derive(Debug)]\n+pub struct ModuleInstance {\n+    pub module: String,\n+    pub instance_id: Uuid,\n+    pub control: Option<Endpoint>,\n+    pub grpc_services: HashMap<String, Endpoint>,\n+    pub rest_endpoint: Option<Endpoint>,  // NEW: REST base URL for this instance\n+    pub version: Option<String>,\n+    inner: Arc<parking_lot::RwLock<InstanceRuntimeState>>,\n+}\n+\n+impl ModuleInstance {\n+    // ... existing methods ...\n+\n+    /// Set the REST endpoint for this instance\n+    pub fn with_rest_endpoint(mut self, ep: Endpoint) -> Self {\n+        self.rest_endpoint = Some(ep);\n+        self\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.2 Extend `ModuleManager` with REST discovery\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/runtime/module_manager.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+impl ModuleManager {\n+    /// Pick a REST endpoint for a module using round-robin selection.\n+    /// Returns (module_name, instance, endpoint) if found.\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn pick_rest_endpoint_round_robin(\n+        &self,\n+        module_name: &str,\n+    ) -> Option<(String, Arc<ModuleInstance>, Endpoint)> {\n+        let instances_entry = self.inner.get(module_name)?;\n+        let instances = instances_entry.value();\n+\n+        // Filter to instances with REST endpoints and healthy/ready state\n+        let candidates: Vec<_> = instances\n+            .iter()\n+            .filter(|inst| {\n+                inst.rest_endpoint.is_some()\n+                    && matches!(inst.state(), InstanceState::Healthy | InstanceState::Ready)\n+            })\n+            .cloned()\n+            .collect();\n+\n+        if candidates.is_empty() {\n+            return None;\n+        }\n+\n+        let len = candidates.len();\n+        let rr_key = format!(\"rest:{}\", module_name);\n+        let mut counter = self.rr_counters.entry(rr_key).or_insert(0);\n+        let idx = *counter % len;\n+        *counter = (*counter + 1) % len;\n+\n+        candidates.get(idx).map(|inst| {\n+            (\n+                module_name.to_owned(),\n+                inst.clone(),\n+                inst.rest_endpoint.clone().expect(\"filtered above\"),\n+            )\n+        })\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.3 Extend `DirectoryClient` trait\n+\n+**Location**: `cf_system_sdks/src/directory.rs` (upstream crate — requires update)\n+\n+```rust\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait DirectoryClient: Send + Sync {\n+    /// Resolve REST endpoint for a module (default for OoP).\n+    async fn resolve_rest_service(&self, module_name: &str) -> Result<RestEndpoint>;\n+\n+    /// Resolve gRPC endpoint for a module (opt-in).\n+    async fn resolve_grpc_service(&self, service_name: &str) -> Result<ServiceEndpoint>;\n+\n+    // ... existing methods (list_instances, register_instance, etc.) ...\n+}\n+\n+/// REST endpoint for a module\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct RestEndpoint {\n+    /// Base URL for the module's REST API (e.g., \"http://calculator:8080\")\n+    pub base_url: String,\n+}\n+\n+impl RestEndpoint {\n+    pub fn new(base_url: impl Into<String>) -> Self {\n+        Self { base_url: base_url.into() }\n+    }\n+\n+    pub fn http(host: &str, port: u16) -> Self {\n+        Self { base_url: format!(\"http://{}:{}\", host, port) }\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.4 Implement `resolve_rest_service` in `LocalDirectoryClient`\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/directory.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl DirectoryClient for LocalDirectoryClient {\n+    async fn resolve_rest_service(&self, module_name: &str) -> Result<RestEndpoint> {\n+        if let Some((_, _, ep)) = self.mgr.pick_rest_endpoint_round_robin(module_name) {\n+            return Ok(RestEndpoint::new(ep.uri));\n+        }\n+\n+        anyhow::bail!(\"REST service not found or no healthy instances: {module_name}\")\n+    }\n+\n+    // ... existing methods unchanged ...\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.5 Extend `RegisterInstanceInfo` for REST registration\n+\n+**Location**: `cf_system_sdks/src/directory.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Information needed to register a module instance\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct RegisterInstanceInfo {\n+    pub module: String,\n+    pub instance_id: String,\n+    pub grpc_services: Vec<(String, ServiceEndpoint)>,\n+    pub rest_endpoint: Option<RestEndpoint>,  // NEW\n+    pub version: Option<String>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.6 OoP Module REST Registration\n+\n+When an OoP module starts, it registers its REST endpoint with the DirectoryService:\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/oop.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+async fn register_with_directory(\n+    directory: &dyn DirectoryClient,\n+    module_name: &str,\n+    instance_id: Uuid,\n+    rest_port: u16,\n+    grpc_services: Vec<(String, ServiceEndpoint)>,\n+) -> Result<()> {\n+    let info = RegisterInstanceInfo {\n+        module: module_name.to_owned(),\n+        instance_id: instance_id.to_string(),\n+        grpc_services,\n+        rest_endpoint: Some(RestEndpoint::http(\"0.0.0.0\", rest_port)),\n+        version: Some(env!(\"CARGO_PKG_VERSION\").to_owned()),\n+    };\n+\n+    directory.register_instance(info).await\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.7 Design Decisions\n+\n+| Decision | Rationale |\n+|----------|-----------|\n+| **One REST endpoint per instance** | Unlike gRPC (multiple services per instance), REST modules expose a single base URL with path-based routing |\n+| **Module-name based resolution** | REST discovery uses `module_name` (e.g., \"calculator\"), not service name |\n+| **Reuse existing health tracking** | REST endpoints use the same `InstanceState` and heartbeat mechanism as gRPC |\n+| **Symmetric API** | `resolve_rest_service()` mirrors `resolve_grpc_service()` for consistency |\n+\n+##### 1.2.8 Migration Notes\n+\n+1. **`cf_system_sdks` must be updated first** — Add `RestEndpoint`, extend `RegisterInstanceInfo`, and add `resolve_rest_service()` to `DirectoryClient`\n+2. **`ModuleInstance` is extended** — Existing code continues to work; `rest_endpoint` defaults to `None`\n+3. **OoP modules must register REST endpoints** — Update bootstrap to include REST port in registration\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Phase 2: ClientDescriptor Trait\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/descriptor.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Client descriptor traits for typed OoP client metadata.\n+\n+use std::time::Duration;\n+\n+/// Availability policy for OoP clients.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum ClientAvailabilityPolicy {\n+    /// Client is optional; operations fail gracefully with SDK error (maps to HTTP 424).\n+    #[default]\n+    Optional,\n+    /// Client is required; module readiness may depend on availability.\n+    Required,\n+}\n+\n+/// Configuration for client behavior.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct ClientConfig {\n+    /// Transport protocol (REST default, gRPC opt-in).\n+    pub transport: Transport,\n+    /// Connection timeout for initial connect.\n+    pub connect_timeout: Duration,\n+    /// Request timeout for individual calls.\n+    pub request_timeout: Duration,\n+    /// Maximum backoff duration between reconnect attempts.\n+    pub max_backoff: Duration,\n+    /// Availability policy.\n+    pub availability_policy: ClientAvailabilityPolicy,\n+}\n+\n+impl Default for ClientConfig {\n+    fn default() -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            transport: Transport::Rest,\n+            connect_timeout: Duration::from_secs(5),\n+            request_timeout: Duration::from_secs(30),\n+            max_backoff: Duration::from_secs(60),\n+            availability_policy: ClientAvailabilityPolicy::Optional,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl ClientConfig {\n+    /// Create a REST client config (default).\n+    pub fn rest() -> Self {\n+        Self::default()\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Create a gRPC client config (opt-in).\n+    #[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+    pub fn grpc() -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            transport: Transport::Grpc,\n+            ..Self::default()\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Descriptor for an OoP client, defined in SDK crates.\n+///\n+/// This trait binds compile-time type information to runtime metadata\n+/// needed for lazy client resolution and registration.\n+pub trait ClientDescriptor: Send + Sync + 'static {\n+    /// The SDK API trait type (e.g., `dyn CalculatorClientV1`).\n+    type Api: ?Sized + Send + Sync + 'static;\n+\n+    /// Module name for dependency graph and Directory resolution.\n+    const MODULE_NAME: &'static str;\n+\n+    /// Client configuration (transport, timeouts, backoff, availability).\n+    fn config() -> ClientConfig {\n+        ClientConfig::default()\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Phase 3: ClientProvider Infrastructure\n+\n+#### 3.1 RestClientProvider (Default)\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/rest_provider.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Universal lazy REST client provider (default transport).\n+\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+use std::time::{Duration, Instant};\n+\n+use parking_lot::RwLock;\n+use tokio::sync::Semaphore;\n+\n+use crate::client_hub::ClientHub;\n+use crate::directory::DirectoryClient;\n+use crate::clients::descriptor::ClientConfig;\n+use modkit_http::HttpClient;\n+\n+/// Error type for REST provider operations.\n+#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\n+pub enum RestProviderError {\n+    #[error(\"service not found in directory: {module_name}\")]\n+    ServiceNotFound { module_name: &'static str },\n+\n+    #[error(\"HTTP request failed: {0}\")]\n+    HttpError(#[source] modkit_http::HttpError),\n+\n+    #[error(\"directory resolution failed: {0}\")]\n+    DirectoryError(#[source] anyhow::Error),\n+\n+    #[error(\"service temporarily unavailable (backoff active)\")]\n+    Backoff { retry_after: Duration },\n+}\n+\n+struct CachedEndpoint {\n+    base_url: String,\n+    resolved_at: Instant,\n+}\n+\n+struct ProviderState {\n+    cached: Option<CachedEndpoint>,\n+    last_failure: Option<Instant>,\n+    failure_count: u32,\n+}\n+\n+/// Universal lazy REST client provider.\n+///\n+/// Handles:\n+/// - Lazy endpoint resolution via DirectoryClient\n+/// - Base URL caching with automatic eviction on errors\n+/// - Exponential backoff for reconnection attempts\n+/// - Rate limiting to prevent thundering herds\n+pub struct RestClientProvider {\n+    module_name: &'static str,\n+    config: ClientConfig,\n+    hub: Arc<ClientHub>,\n+    http_client: HttpClient,\n+    state: RwLock<ProviderState>,\n+    resolve_semaphore: Semaphore,\n+}\n+\n+impl RestClientProvider {\n+    pub fn new(\n+        module_name: &'static str,\n+        config: ClientConfig,\n+        hub: Arc<ClientHub>,\n+    ) -> Self {\n+        let http_client = HttpClient::builder()\n+            .timeout(config.request_timeout)\n+            .connect_timeout(config.connect_timeout)\n+            .build();\n+\n+        Self {\n+            module_name,\n+            config,\n+            hub,\n+            http_client,\n+            state: RwLock::new(ProviderState {\n+                cached: None,\n+                last_failure: None,\n+                failure_count: 0,\n+            }),\n+            resolve_semaphore: Semaphore::new(1),\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Get the base URL for the service, resolving lazily.\n+    pub async fn get_base_url(&self) -> Result<String, RestProviderError> {\n+        // Fast path: return cached endpoint\n+        {\n+            let state = self.state.read();\n+            if let Some(ref cached) = state.cached {\n+                return Ok(cached.base_url.clone());\n+            }\n+\n+            // Check backoff\n+            if let Some(last_failure) = state.last_failure {\n+                let backoff = self.calculate_backoff(state.failure_count);\n+                let elapsed = last_failure.elapsed();\n+                if elapsed < backoff {\n+                    return Err(RestProviderError::Backoff {\n+                        retry_after: backoff - elapsed,\n+                    });\n+                }\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        // Slow path: acquire semaphore and resolve\n+        let _permit = self.resolve_semaphore.acquire().await\n+            .expect(\"semaphore is never closed\");\n+\n+        // Double-check after acquiring semaphore\n+        {\n+            let state = self.state.read();\n+            if let Some(ref cached) = state.cached {\n+                return Ok(cached.base_url.clone());\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        self.resolve_internal().await\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Get the HTTP client for making requests.\n+    pub fn http_client(&self) -> &HttpClient {\n+        &self.http_client\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Evict the cached endpoint (call on transport errors).\n+    pub fn evict(&self) {\n+        let mut state = self.state.write();\n+        state.cached = None;\n+        state.last_failure = Some(Instant::now());\n+        state.failure_count = state.failure_count.saturating_add(1);\n+        tracing::warn!(\n+            module = self.module_name,\n+            failure_count = state.failure_count,\n+            \"Evicted cached REST endpoint\"\n+        );\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Reset failure state (call on successful request).\n+    pub fn reset_failures(&self) {\n+        let mut state = self.state.write();\n+        if state.failure_count > 0 {\n+            state.failure_count = 0;\n+            state.last_failure = None;\n+            tracing::debug!(module = self.module_name, \"Reset failure state after success\");\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    async fn resolve_internal(&self) -> Result<String, RestProviderError> {\n+        let directory = self\n+            .hub\n+            .get::<dyn DirectoryClient>()\n+            .map_err(|e| RestProviderError::DirectoryError(e.into()))?;\n+\n+        let endpoint = directory\n+            .resolve_rest_service(self.module_name)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(RestProviderError::DirectoryError)?;\n+\n+        tracing::debug!(\n+            module = self.module_name,\n+            base_url = %endpoint.base_url,\n+            \"Resolved REST endpoint\"\n+        );\n+\n+        {\n+            let mut state = self.state.write();\n+            state.cached = Some(CachedEndpoint {\n+                base_url: endpoint.base_url.clone(),\n+                resolved_at: Instant::now(),\n+            });\n+            state.failure_count = 0;\n+            state.last_failure = None;\n+        }\n+\n+        Ok(endpoint.base_url)\n+    }\n+\n+    fn calculate_backoff(&self, failure_count: u32) -> Duration {\n+        let base = Duration::from_millis(100);\n+        let max = self.config.max_backoff;\n+        let backoff = base.saturating_mul(2u32.saturating_pow(failure_count.min(10)));\n+        backoff.min(max)\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### 3.2 GrpcClientProvider (Optional)\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/grpc_provider.rs`\n+\n+> Feature-gated behind `feature = \"grpc\"` for streaming/high-throughput use cases.\n+\n+```rust\n+#[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+//! Lazy gRPC client provider (optional transport).\n+\n+// Implementation follows same pattern as RestClientProvider\n+// but manages tonic::transport::Channel instead of base URL\n+```\n+\n+#### 3.3 LazyClientError\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/error.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Error returned by lazy clients when the OoP dependency is unavailable.\n+#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\n+pub enum LazyClientError {\n+    #[error(\"service unavailable: {module_name}\")]\n+    Unavailable {\n+        module_name: &'static str,\n+        #[source]\n+        source: Box<dyn std::error::Error + Send + Sync>,\n+    },\n+\n+    #[error(\"request failed: {0}\")]\n+    RequestFailed(String),\n+\n+    #[error(\"response parsing failed: {0}\")]\n+    ParseError(#[source] serde_json::Error),\n+}\n+\n+impl LazyClientError {\n+    /// Returns true if this error indicates the service is temporarily unavailable.\n+    /// REST handlers should map this to HTTP 424 Failed Dependency.\n+    pub fn is_dependency_unavailable(&self) -> bool {\n+        matches!(self, LazyClientError::Unavailable { .. })\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Phase 4: SDK Crate Updates (calculator-sdk example)\n+\n+#### 4.1 Descriptor\n+\n+**Location**: `calculator-sdk/src/descriptor.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit::clients::descriptor::{ClientDescriptor, ClientConfig};\n+use crate::api::CalculatorClientV1;\n+\n+/// Descriptor for the Calculator client (REST by default).\n+pub struct CalculatorClientDescriptor;\n+\n+impl ClientDescriptor for CalculatorClientDescriptor {\n+    type Api = dyn CalculatorClientV1;\n+    const MODULE_NAME: &'static str = \"calculator\";\n+\n+    fn config() -> ClientConfig {\n+        ClientConfig::rest()  // Default: REST transport\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+// Optional: gRPC descriptor for high-throughput use cases\n+#[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+pub struct CalculatorGrpcClientDescriptor;\n+\n+#[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+impl ClientDescriptor for CalculatorGrpcClientDescriptor {\n+    type Api = dyn CalculatorClientV1;\n+    const MODULE_NAME: &'static str = \"calculator\";\n+\n+    fn config() -> ClientConfig {\n+        ClientConfig::grpc()  // Opt-in: gRPC transport\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### 4.2 Lazy Client Implementation\n+\n+**Location**: `calculator-sdk/src/lazy_client.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use modkit::clients::rest_provider::RestClientProvider;\n+use modkit_security::SecurityContext;\n+\n+use crate::api::{CalculatorClientV1, CalculatorError};\n+\n+/// Lazy client for Calculator service (REST transport).\n+pub struct LazyCalculatorClient {\n+    provider: Arc<RestClientProvider>,\n+}\n+\n+impl LazyCalculatorClient {\n+    pub fn new(provider: Arc<RestClientProvider>) -> Self {\n+        Self { provider }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl CalculatorClientV1 for LazyCalculatorClient {\n+    async fn add(&self, ctx: &SecurityContext, a: i64, b: i64) -> Result<i64, CalculatorError> {\n+        let base_url = self.provider.get_base_url().await.map_err(|e| {\n+            tracing::warn!(error = %e, \"Calculator service unavailable\");\n+            CalculatorError::Unavailable {\n+                message: format!(\"Calculator service unavailable: {}\", e),\n+            }\n+        })?;\n+\n+        let url = format!(\"{}/api/v1/calculator/add\", base_url);\n+        let response = self.provider.http_client()\n+            .post(&url)\n+            .header(\"x-tenant-id\", ctx.tenant_id().map(|t| t.to_string()).unwrap_or_default())\n+            .json(&serde_json::json!({ \"a\": a, \"b\": b }))\n+            .send()\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(|e| {\n+                if e.is_connect() || e.is_timeout() {\n+                    self.provider.evict();\n+                }\n+                CalculatorError::Unavailable {\n+                    message: format!(\"HTTP request failed: {}\", e),\n+                }\n+            })?;\n+\n+        if !response.status().is_success() {\n+            return Err(map_http_error(response.status(), &response.text().await.unwrap_or_default()));\n+        }\n+\n+        let result: AddResponse = response.json().await.map_err(|e| {\n+            CalculatorError::Internal { message: format!(\"Failed to parse response: {}\", e) }\n+        })?;\n+\n+        self.provider.reset_failures();\n+        Ok(result.result)\n+    }\n+\n+    // ... other methods follow the same pattern ...\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(serde::Deserialize)]","path":"docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md","commit_id":"edd86e3e6cf91af1a08e3970d60dc26bc6acb6e6","original_commit_id":"030bc79ea9322b429e351c332cbffd4f44791b3c","user":{"login":"striped-zebra-dev","id":225538363,"node_id":"U_kgDODXFxOw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225538363?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/striped-zebra-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Double time definition of the \n```\n#[derive(serde::Deserialize)]\nstruct AddResponse { result: i64 }\n```","created_at":"2026-02-19T16:13:19Z","updated_at":"2026-02-19T16:13:19Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2828771682","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2828771682"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2828771682"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2828771682/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":1520,"original_line":757,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":757,"position":1520,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2828789279","pull_request_review_id":3826923920,"id":2828789279,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6om-Yf","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1050 @@\n+# ADR-0003: Universal Lazy Typed REST Clients for OoP Modules\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+This proposal outlines a migration from gRPC to REST as the default transport for out-of-process (OoP) modules and introduces a **universal lazy typed client layer** for OoP module communication in ModKit. The implementation is structured in phases:\n+\n+1. **Phase 1 - REST as default transport**: Establish REST as the default OoP transport; gRPC becomes opt-in\n+2. **Phase 2 - ClientDescriptor trait**: SDK-defined metadata binding compile-time types to runtime resolution\n+3. **Phase 3 - ClientProvider**: Lazy resolution, caching, backoff, and reconnection infrastructure\n+4. **Phase 4 - Macro extension**: `clients = [...]` auto-registers lazy clients into `ClientHub`\n+5. **Phase 5 - Soft OoP deps**: Dependencies on OoP modules don't block startup\n+6. **Phase 6 - Registry extension**: Soft OoP dep resolution:  \n+\n+**Current pattern** (problematic):\n+```rust\n+// Consumer must wire client manually in init() - FAILS if OoP module is not ready\n+calculator_sdk::wire_client(hub, &*directory).await?;\n+```\n+\n+**Proposed pattern**:\n+```rust\n+#[modkit::module(\n+    name = \"calculator_gateway\",\n+    clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],  // REST by default\n+)]\n+// No wire_client() needed - lazy client auto-registered\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Problem Statement\n+\n+The current OoP client wiring pattern has several issues:\n+\n+1. **Eager wiring is fragile**: Consumer modules call `wire_client()` in `init()`, which fails if the OoP dependency is not yet available.\n+2. **Startup coupling**: The entire module fails to start if any OoP dependency is temporarily unavailable.\n+3. **Boilerplate duplication**: Each SDK repeats the same resolve/connect/cache logic.\n+4. **No graceful degradation**: Missing dependencies cause module-level failures instead of per-operation failures (HTTP 424).\n+5. **gRPC complexity**: Binary protobuf payloads are hard to debug; requires specialized tooling.\n+\n+### Current Pattern (calculator_gateway example)\n+\n+```rust\n+// Current: Consumer must wire client manually, and it happens eagerly\n+pub async fn wire_client(hub: &ClientHub, resolver: &dyn DirectoryClient) -> Result<()> {\n+    let endpoint = resolver.resolve_grpc_service(SERVICE_NAME).await?;  // Fails if OoP not ready\n+    let client = CalculatorGrpcClient::connect(&endpoint.uri).await?;   // Fails if network issue\n+    hub.register::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>(Arc::new(client));\n+    Ok(())\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Proposed Solution\n+\n+### Architecture Overview\n+\n+```text\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           SDK Crate (calculator-sdk)                    │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  CalculatorClientDescriptor                                             │\n+│    - MODULE_NAME: \"calculator\"                                          │\n+│    - Api: dyn CalculatorClientV1                                        │\n+│    - Transport: Rest (default) | Grpc (opt-in)                          │\n+│    - Availability Policy: Optional (default)                            │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  LazyCalculatorClient                                                   │\n+│    - Implements CalculatorClientV1                                      │\n+│    - Delegates to ClientProvider for lazy connection                    │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           ModKit (libs/modkit)                          │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  ClientProvider (transport-agnostic interface)                          │\n+│    - Lazy resolution via DirectoryClient                                │\n+│    - Endpoint/connection caching with eviction on error                 │\n+│    - Backoff/rate-limiting for reconnects                               │\n+│    - Transport middleware (timeouts, retries, tracing)                  │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  RestClientProvider (default) | GrpcClientProvider (feature = \"grpc\")   │","path":"docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md","commit_id":"edd86e3e6cf91af1a08e3970d60dc26bc6acb6e6","original_commit_id":"030bc79ea9322b429e351c332cbffd4f44791b3c","user":{"login":"striped-zebra-dev","id":225538363,"node_id":"U_kgDODXFxOw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225538363?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/striped-zebra-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I'd love to see the proposal of Circular dependency resolution.\n\nWhat's the initialization order guarantee? If the DirectoryClient isn't registered before the lazy client tries to resolve, it fails (multi exec run case).","created_at":"2026-02-19T16:16:55Z","updated_at":"2026-02-19T16:16:55Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2828789279","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2828789279"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2828789279"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2828789279/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":84,"original_line":84,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":84,"position":84,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2828793871","pull_request_review_id":3826928695,"id":2828793871,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6om_gP","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1050 @@\n+# ADR-0003: Universal Lazy Typed REST Clients for OoP Modules\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+This proposal outlines a migration from gRPC to REST as the default transport for out-of-process (OoP) modules and introduces a **universal lazy typed client layer** for OoP module communication in ModKit. The implementation is structured in phases:\n+\n+1. **Phase 1 - REST as default transport**: Establish REST as the default OoP transport; gRPC becomes opt-in\n+2. **Phase 2 - ClientDescriptor trait**: SDK-defined metadata binding compile-time types to runtime resolution\n+3. **Phase 3 - ClientProvider**: Lazy resolution, caching, backoff, and reconnection infrastructure\n+4. **Phase 4 - Macro extension**: `clients = [...]` auto-registers lazy clients into `ClientHub`\n+5. **Phase 5 - Soft OoP deps**: Dependencies on OoP modules don't block startup\n+6. **Phase 6 - Registry extension**: Soft OoP dep resolution:  \n+\n+**Current pattern** (problematic):\n+```rust\n+// Consumer must wire client manually in init() - FAILS if OoP module is not ready\n+calculator_sdk::wire_client(hub, &*directory).await?;\n+```\n+\n+**Proposed pattern**:\n+```rust\n+#[modkit::module(\n+    name = \"calculator_gateway\",\n+    clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],  // REST by default\n+)]\n+// No wire_client() needed - lazy client auto-registered\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Problem Statement\n+\n+The current OoP client wiring pattern has several issues:\n+\n+1. **Eager wiring is fragile**: Consumer modules call `wire_client()` in `init()`, which fails if the OoP dependency is not yet available.\n+2. **Startup coupling**: The entire module fails to start if any OoP dependency is temporarily unavailable.\n+3. **Boilerplate duplication**: Each SDK repeats the same resolve/connect/cache logic.\n+4. **No graceful degradation**: Missing dependencies cause module-level failures instead of per-operation failures (HTTP 424).\n+5. **gRPC complexity**: Binary protobuf payloads are hard to debug; requires specialized tooling.\n+\n+### Current Pattern (calculator_gateway example)\n+\n+```rust\n+// Current: Consumer must wire client manually, and it happens eagerly\n+pub async fn wire_client(hub: &ClientHub, resolver: &dyn DirectoryClient) -> Result<()> {\n+    let endpoint = resolver.resolve_grpc_service(SERVICE_NAME).await?;  // Fails if OoP not ready\n+    let client = CalculatorGrpcClient::connect(&endpoint.uri).await?;   // Fails if network issue\n+    hub.register::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>(Arc::new(client));\n+    Ok(())\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Proposed Solution\n+\n+### Architecture Overview\n+\n+```text\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           SDK Crate (calculator-sdk)                    │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  CalculatorClientDescriptor                                             │\n+│    - MODULE_NAME: \"calculator\"                                          │\n+│    - Api: dyn CalculatorClientV1                                        │\n+│    - Transport: Rest (default) | Grpc (opt-in)                          │\n+│    - Availability Policy: Optional (default)                            │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  LazyCalculatorClient                                                   │\n+│    - Implements CalculatorClientV1                                      │\n+│    - Delegates to ClientProvider for lazy connection                    │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           ModKit (libs/modkit)                          │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  ClientProvider (transport-agnostic interface)                          │\n+│    - Lazy resolution via DirectoryClient                                │\n+│    - Endpoint/connection caching with eviction on error                 │\n+│    - Backoff/rate-limiting for reconnects                               │\n+│    - Transport middleware (timeouts, retries, tracing)                  │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  RestClientProvider (default) | GrpcClientProvider (feature = \"grpc\")   │\n+│    - Transport-specific implementations                                 │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  #[modkit::module] macro extension                                      │\n+│    - clients = [CalculatorClientDescriptor]                             │\n+│    - Auto-registers LazyClient into ClientHub                           │\n+│    - Auto-injects MODULE_NAME from each descriptor into deps            │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                      Consumer Module (calculator_gateway)               │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  #[modkit::module(                                                      │\n+│      name = \"calculator_gateway\",                                       │\n+│      capabilities = [rest],                                             │\n+│      clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],            │\n+│      // deps auto-injected: [\"calculator\"] from descriptor              │\n+│  )]                                                                     │\n+│                                                                         │\n+│  // No wire_client() call needed!                                       │\n+│  // Client is always available from ClientHub                           │\n+│  let calc = hub.get::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>()?;                       │\n+│  calc.add(ctx, a, b).await?;  // Lazy connect on first call             │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Detailed Implementation\n+\n+### Phase 1: REST as Default Transport\n+\n+**Rationale**: REST is simpler to debug, requires no code generation, and is sufficient for most OoP calls. gRPC remains available for streaming or high-throughput use cases.\n+\n+| Factor          | REST                            | gRPC                         |\n+|-----------------|---------------------------------|------------------------------|\n+| Debuggability   | ✅ curl, browser, any HTTP tool | ❌ Requires specialized tools |\n+| Simplicity      | ✅ JSON, standard HTTP          | ❌ Protobuf, code generation  |\n+| Browser support | ✅ Native                       | ❌ Requires gRPC-Web proxy    |\n+| API reuse       | ✅ Same as public REST API      | ❌ Separate interface         |\n+| Streaming       | ❌ Requires SSE/WebSocket       | ✅ Native support             |\n+| Performance     | ⚠️ JSON overhead                | ✅ Binary, efficient          |\n+\n+#### 1.1 Transport Enum\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/transport.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Transport protocol for OoP communication.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum Transport {\n+    /// REST with JSON serialization (default).\n+    #[default]\n+    Rest,\n+    /// gRPC with protobuf serialization (opt-in, requires feature = \"grpc\").\n+    #[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+    Grpc,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### 1.2 REST Service Discovery Infrastructure\n+\n+REST service discovery requires extending the existing `ModuleInstance`, `ModuleManager`, and `DirectoryClient` to track and resolve REST endpoints.\n+\n+##### 1.2.1 Extend `ModuleInstance` to track REST endpoints\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/runtime/module_manager.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Represents a single instance of a module\n+#[derive(Debug)]\n+pub struct ModuleInstance {\n+    pub module: String,\n+    pub instance_id: Uuid,\n+    pub control: Option<Endpoint>,\n+    pub grpc_services: HashMap<String, Endpoint>,\n+    pub rest_endpoint: Option<Endpoint>,  // NEW: REST base URL for this instance\n+    pub version: Option<String>,\n+    inner: Arc<parking_lot::RwLock<InstanceRuntimeState>>,\n+}\n+\n+impl ModuleInstance {\n+    // ... existing methods ...\n+\n+    /// Set the REST endpoint for this instance\n+    pub fn with_rest_endpoint(mut self, ep: Endpoint) -> Self {\n+        self.rest_endpoint = Some(ep);\n+        self\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.2 Extend `ModuleManager` with REST discovery\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/runtime/module_manager.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+impl ModuleManager {\n+    /// Pick a REST endpoint for a module using round-robin selection.\n+    /// Returns (module_name, instance, endpoint) if found.\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn pick_rest_endpoint_round_robin(\n+        &self,\n+        module_name: &str,\n+    ) -> Option<(String, Arc<ModuleInstance>, Endpoint)> {\n+        let instances_entry = self.inner.get(module_name)?;\n+        let instances = instances_entry.value();\n+\n+        // Filter to instances with REST endpoints and healthy/ready state\n+        let candidates: Vec<_> = instances\n+            .iter()\n+            .filter(|inst| {\n+                inst.rest_endpoint.is_some()\n+                    && matches!(inst.state(), InstanceState::Healthy | InstanceState::Ready)\n+            })\n+            .cloned()\n+            .collect();\n+\n+        if candidates.is_empty() {\n+            return None;\n+        }\n+\n+        let len = candidates.len();\n+        let rr_key = format!(\"rest:{}\", module_name);\n+        let mut counter = self.rr_counters.entry(rr_key).or_insert(0);\n+        let idx = *counter % len;\n+        *counter = (*counter + 1) % len;\n+\n+        candidates.get(idx).map(|inst| {\n+            (\n+                module_name.to_owned(),\n+                inst.clone(),\n+                inst.rest_endpoint.clone().expect(\"filtered above\"),\n+            )\n+        })\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.3 Extend `DirectoryClient` trait\n+\n+**Location**: `cf_system_sdks/src/directory.rs` (upstream crate — requires update)\n+\n+```rust\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait DirectoryClient: Send + Sync {\n+    /// Resolve REST endpoint for a module (default for OoP).\n+    async fn resolve_rest_service(&self, module_name: &str) -> Result<RestEndpoint>;\n+\n+    /// Resolve gRPC endpoint for a module (opt-in).\n+    async fn resolve_grpc_service(&self, service_name: &str) -> Result<ServiceEndpoint>;\n+\n+    // ... existing methods (list_instances, register_instance, etc.) ...\n+}\n+\n+/// REST endpoint for a module\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct RestEndpoint {\n+    /// Base URL for the module's REST API (e.g., \"http://calculator:8080\")\n+    pub base_url: String,\n+}\n+\n+impl RestEndpoint {\n+    pub fn new(base_url: impl Into<String>) -> Self {\n+        Self { base_url: base_url.into() }\n+    }\n+\n+    pub fn http(host: &str, port: u16) -> Self {\n+        Self { base_url: format!(\"http://{}:{}\", host, port) }\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.4 Implement `resolve_rest_service` in `LocalDirectoryClient`\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/directory.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl DirectoryClient for LocalDirectoryClient {\n+    async fn resolve_rest_service(&self, module_name: &str) -> Result<RestEndpoint> {\n+        if let Some((_, _, ep)) = self.mgr.pick_rest_endpoint_round_robin(module_name) {\n+            return Ok(RestEndpoint::new(ep.uri));\n+        }\n+\n+        anyhow::bail!(\"REST service not found or no healthy instances: {module_name}\")\n+    }\n+\n+    // ... existing methods unchanged ...\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.5 Extend `RegisterInstanceInfo` for REST registration\n+\n+**Location**: `cf_system_sdks/src/directory.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Information needed to register a module instance\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct RegisterInstanceInfo {\n+    pub module: String,\n+    pub instance_id: String,\n+    pub grpc_services: Vec<(String, ServiceEndpoint)>,\n+    pub rest_endpoint: Option<RestEndpoint>,  // NEW\n+    pub version: Option<String>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.6 OoP Module REST Registration\n+\n+When an OoP module starts, it registers its REST endpoint with the DirectoryService:\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/oop.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+async fn register_with_directory(\n+    directory: &dyn DirectoryClient,\n+    module_name: &str,\n+    instance_id: Uuid,\n+    rest_port: u16,\n+    grpc_services: Vec<(String, ServiceEndpoint)>,\n+) -> Result<()> {\n+    let info = RegisterInstanceInfo {\n+        module: module_name.to_owned(),\n+        instance_id: instance_id.to_string(),\n+        grpc_services,\n+        rest_endpoint: Some(RestEndpoint::http(\"0.0.0.0\", rest_port)),\n+        version: Some(env!(\"CARGO_PKG_VERSION\").to_owned()),\n+    };\n+\n+    directory.register_instance(info).await\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.7 Design Decisions\n+\n+| Decision | Rationale |\n+|----------|-----------|\n+| **One REST endpoint per instance** | Unlike gRPC (multiple services per instance), REST modules expose a single base URL with path-based routing |\n+| **Module-name based resolution** | REST discovery uses `module_name` (e.g., \"calculator\"), not service name |\n+| **Reuse existing health tracking** | REST endpoints use the same `InstanceState` and heartbeat mechanism as gRPC |\n+| **Symmetric API** | `resolve_rest_service()` mirrors `resolve_grpc_service()` for consistency |\n+\n+##### 1.2.8 Migration Notes\n+\n+1. **`cf_system_sdks` must be updated first** — Add `RestEndpoint`, extend `RegisterInstanceInfo`, and add `resolve_rest_service()` to `DirectoryClient`\n+2. **`ModuleInstance` is extended** — Existing code continues to work; `rest_endpoint` defaults to `None`\n+3. **OoP modules must register REST endpoints** — Update bootstrap to include REST port in registration\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Phase 2: ClientDescriptor Trait\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/descriptor.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Client descriptor traits for typed OoP client metadata.\n+\n+use std::time::Duration;\n+\n+/// Availability policy for OoP clients.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum ClientAvailabilityPolicy {\n+    /// Client is optional; operations fail gracefully with SDK error (maps to HTTP 424).\n+    #[default]\n+    Optional,\n+    /// Client is required; module readiness may depend on availability.\n+    Required,\n+}\n+\n+/// Configuration for client behavior.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct ClientConfig {\n+    /// Transport protocol (REST default, gRPC opt-in).\n+    pub transport: Transport,\n+    /// Connection timeout for initial connect.\n+    pub connect_timeout: Duration,\n+    /// Request timeout for individual calls.\n+    pub request_timeout: Duration,\n+    /// Maximum backoff duration between reconnect attempts.\n+    pub max_backoff: Duration,\n+    /// Availability policy.\n+    pub availability_policy: ClientAvailabilityPolicy,\n+}\n+\n+impl Default for ClientConfig {\n+    fn default() -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            transport: Transport::Rest,\n+            connect_timeout: Duration::from_secs(5),\n+            request_timeout: Duration::from_secs(30),\n+            max_backoff: Duration::from_secs(60),\n+            availability_policy: ClientAvailabilityPolicy::Optional,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl ClientConfig {\n+    /// Create a REST client config (default).\n+    pub fn rest() -> Self {\n+        Self::default()\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Create a gRPC client config (opt-in).\n+    #[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+    pub fn grpc() -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            transport: Transport::Grpc,\n+            ..Self::default()\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Descriptor for an OoP client, defined in SDK crates.\n+///\n+/// This trait binds compile-time type information to runtime metadata\n+/// needed for lazy client resolution and registration.\n+pub trait ClientDescriptor: Send + Sync + 'static {\n+    /// The SDK API trait type (e.g., `dyn CalculatorClientV1`).\n+    type Api: ?Sized + Send + Sync + 'static;\n+\n+    /// Module name for dependency graph and Directory resolution.\n+    const MODULE_NAME: &'static str;\n+\n+    /// Client configuration (transport, timeouts, backoff, availability).\n+    fn config() -> ClientConfig {\n+        ClientConfig::default()\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Phase 3: ClientProvider Infrastructure\n+\n+#### 3.1 RestClientProvider (Default)\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/rest_provider.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Universal lazy REST client provider (default transport).\n+\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+use std::time::{Duration, Instant};\n+\n+use parking_lot::RwLock;\n+use tokio::sync::Semaphore;\n+\n+use crate::client_hub::ClientHub;\n+use crate::directory::DirectoryClient;\n+use crate::clients::descriptor::ClientConfig;\n+use modkit_http::HttpClient;\n+\n+/// Error type for REST provider operations.\n+#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\n+pub enum RestProviderError {\n+    #[error(\"service not found in directory: {module_name}\")]\n+    ServiceNotFound { module_name: &'static str },\n+\n+    #[error(\"HTTP request failed: {0}\")]\n+    HttpError(#[source] modkit_http::HttpError),\n+\n+    #[error(\"directory resolution failed: {0}\")]\n+    DirectoryError(#[source] anyhow::Error),\n+\n+    #[error(\"service temporarily unavailable (backoff active)\")]\n+    Backoff { retry_after: Duration },\n+}\n+\n+struct CachedEndpoint {\n+    base_url: String,\n+    resolved_at: Instant,\n+}\n+\n+struct ProviderState {\n+    cached: Option<CachedEndpoint>,\n+    last_failure: Option<Instant>,\n+    failure_count: u32,\n+}\n+\n+/// Universal lazy REST client provider.\n+///\n+/// Handles:\n+/// - Lazy endpoint resolution via DirectoryClient\n+/// - Base URL caching with automatic eviction on errors\n+/// - Exponential backoff for reconnection attempts\n+/// - Rate limiting to prevent thundering herds\n+pub struct RestClientProvider {\n+    module_name: &'static str,\n+    config: ClientConfig,\n+    hub: Arc<ClientHub>,\n+    http_client: HttpClient,\n+    state: RwLock<ProviderState>,\n+    resolve_semaphore: Semaphore,\n+}\n+\n+impl RestClientProvider {\n+    pub fn new(\n+        module_name: &'static str,\n+        config: ClientConfig,\n+        hub: Arc<ClientHub>,\n+    ) -> Self {\n+        let http_client = HttpClient::builder()\n+            .timeout(config.request_timeout)\n+            .connect_timeout(config.connect_timeout)\n+            .build();\n+\n+        Self {\n+            module_name,\n+            config,\n+            hub,\n+            http_client,\n+            state: RwLock::new(ProviderState {\n+                cached: None,\n+                last_failure: None,\n+                failure_count: 0,\n+            }),\n+            resolve_semaphore: Semaphore::new(1),\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Get the base URL for the service, resolving lazily.\n+    pub async fn get_base_url(&self) -> Result<String, RestProviderError> {\n+        // Fast path: return cached endpoint\n+        {\n+            let state = self.state.read();\n+            if let Some(ref cached) = state.cached {\n+                return Ok(cached.base_url.clone());\n+            }\n+\n+            // Check backoff\n+            if let Some(last_failure) = state.last_failure {\n+                let backoff = self.calculate_backoff(state.failure_count);\n+                let elapsed = last_failure.elapsed();\n+                if elapsed < backoff {\n+                    return Err(RestProviderError::Backoff {\n+                        retry_after: backoff - elapsed,\n+                    });\n+                }\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        // Slow path: acquire semaphore and resolve\n+        let _permit = self.resolve_semaphore.acquire().await\n+            .expect(\"semaphore is never closed\");\n+\n+        // Double-check after acquiring semaphore\n+        {\n+            let state = self.state.read();\n+            if let Some(ref cached) = state.cached {\n+                return Ok(cached.base_url.clone());\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        self.resolve_internal().await\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Get the HTTP client for making requests.\n+    pub fn http_client(&self) -> &HttpClient {\n+        &self.http_client\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Evict the cached endpoint (call on transport errors).\n+    pub fn evict(&self) {\n+        let mut state = self.state.write();\n+        state.cached = None;\n+        state.last_failure = Some(Instant::now());\n+        state.failure_count = state.failure_count.saturating_add(1);\n+        tracing::warn!(\n+            module = self.module_name,\n+            failure_count = state.failure_count,\n+            \"Evicted cached REST endpoint\"\n+        );\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Reset failure state (call on successful request).\n+    pub fn reset_failures(&self) {\n+        let mut state = self.state.write();\n+        if state.failure_count > 0 {\n+            state.failure_count = 0;\n+            state.last_failure = None;\n+            tracing::debug!(module = self.module_name, \"Reset failure state after success\");\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    async fn resolve_internal(&self) -> Result<String, RestProviderError> {\n+        let directory = self\n+            .hub\n+            .get::<dyn DirectoryClient>()\n+            .map_err(|e| RestProviderError::DirectoryError(e.into()))?;\n+\n+        let endpoint = directory\n+            .resolve_rest_service(self.module_name)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(RestProviderError::DirectoryError)?;\n+\n+        tracing::debug!(\n+            module = self.module_name,\n+            base_url = %endpoint.base_url,\n+            \"Resolved REST endpoint\"\n+        );\n+\n+        {\n+            let mut state = self.state.write();\n+            state.cached = Some(CachedEndpoint {\n+                base_url: endpoint.base_url.clone(),\n+                resolved_at: Instant::now(),\n+            });\n+            state.failure_count = 0;\n+            state.last_failure = None;\n+        }\n+\n+        Ok(endpoint.base_url)\n+    }\n+\n+    fn calculate_backoff(&self, failure_count: u32) -> Duration {\n+        let base = Duration::from_millis(100);\n+        let max = self.config.max_backoff;\n+        let backoff = base.saturating_mul(2u32.saturating_pow(failure_count.min(10)));\n+        backoff.min(max)\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### 3.2 GrpcClientProvider (Optional)\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/grpc_provider.rs`\n+\n+> Feature-gated behind `feature = \"grpc\"` for streaming/high-throughput use cases.\n+\n+```rust\n+#[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+//! Lazy gRPC client provider (optional transport).\n+\n+// Implementation follows same pattern as RestClientProvider\n+// but manages tonic::transport::Channel instead of base URL\n+```\n+\n+#### 3.3 LazyClientError\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/error.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Error returned by lazy clients when the OoP dependency is unavailable.\n+#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\n+pub enum LazyClientError {\n+    #[error(\"service unavailable: {module_name}\")]\n+    Unavailable {\n+        module_name: &'static str,\n+        #[source]\n+        source: Box<dyn std::error::Error + Send + Sync>,\n+    },\n+\n+    #[error(\"request failed: {0}\")]\n+    RequestFailed(String),\n+\n+    #[error(\"response parsing failed: {0}\")]\n+    ParseError(#[source] serde_json::Error),\n+}\n+\n+impl LazyClientError {\n+    /// Returns true if this error indicates the service is temporarily unavailable.\n+    /// REST handlers should map this to HTTP 424 Failed Dependency.\n+    pub fn is_dependency_unavailable(&self) -> bool {\n+        matches!(self, LazyClientError::Unavailable { .. })\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Phase 4: SDK Crate Updates (calculator-sdk example)\n+\n+#### 4.1 Descriptor\n+\n+**Location**: `calculator-sdk/src/descriptor.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit::clients::descriptor::{ClientDescriptor, ClientConfig};\n+use crate::api::CalculatorClientV1;\n+\n+/// Descriptor for the Calculator client (REST by default).\n+pub struct CalculatorClientDescriptor;\n+\n+impl ClientDescriptor for CalculatorClientDescriptor {\n+    type Api = dyn CalculatorClientV1;\n+    const MODULE_NAME: &'static str = \"calculator\";\n+\n+    fn config() -> ClientConfig {\n+        ClientConfig::rest()  // Default: REST transport\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+// Optional: gRPC descriptor for high-throughput use cases\n+#[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+pub struct CalculatorGrpcClientDescriptor;\n+\n+#[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+impl ClientDescriptor for CalculatorGrpcClientDescriptor {\n+    type Api = dyn CalculatorClientV1;\n+    const MODULE_NAME: &'static str = \"calculator\";\n+\n+    fn config() -> ClientConfig {\n+        ClientConfig::grpc()  // Opt-in: gRPC transport\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### 4.2 Lazy Client Implementation\n+\n+**Location**: `calculator-sdk/src/lazy_client.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use modkit::clients::rest_provider::RestClientProvider;\n+use modkit_security::SecurityContext;\n+\n+use crate::api::{CalculatorClientV1, CalculatorError};\n+\n+/// Lazy client for Calculator service (REST transport).\n+pub struct LazyCalculatorClient {\n+    provider: Arc<RestClientProvider>,\n+}\n+\n+impl LazyCalculatorClient {\n+    pub fn new(provider: Arc<RestClientProvider>) -> Self {\n+        Self { provider }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl CalculatorClientV1 for LazyCalculatorClient {\n+    async fn add(&self, ctx: &SecurityContext, a: i64, b: i64) -> Result<i64, CalculatorError> {\n+        let base_url = self.provider.get_base_url().await.map_err(|e| {\n+            tracing::warn!(error = %e, \"Calculator service unavailable\");\n+            CalculatorError::Unavailable {\n+                message: format!(\"Calculator service unavailable: {}\", e),\n+            }\n+        })?;\n+\n+        let url = format!(\"{}/api/v1/calculator/add\", base_url);\n+        let response = self.provider.http_client()\n+            .post(&url)\n+            .header(\"x-tenant-id\", ctx.tenant_id().map(|t| t.to_string()).unwrap_or_default())","path":"docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md","commit_id":"030bc79ea9322b429e351c332cbffd4f44791b3c","original_commit_id":"030bc79ea9322b429e351c332cbffd4f44791b3c","user":{"login":"striped-zebra-dev","id":225538363,"node_id":"U_kgDODXFxOw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225538363?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/striped-zebra-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I guess this `x-tenant-id` just leaked from somewhere, please drop it we don't have such concept.","created_at":"2026-02-19T16:17:54Z","updated_at":"2026-02-19T16:17:54Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2828793871","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2828793871"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2828793871"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2828793871/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":729,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":729,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2828805752","pull_request_review_id":3826940754,"id":2828805752,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6onCZ4","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1050 @@\n+# ADR-0003: Universal Lazy Typed REST Clients for OoP Modules\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+This proposal outlines a migration from gRPC to REST as the default transport for out-of-process (OoP) modules and introduces a **universal lazy typed client layer** for OoP module communication in ModKit. The implementation is structured in phases:\n+\n+1. **Phase 1 - REST as default transport**: Establish REST as the default OoP transport; gRPC becomes opt-in\n+2. **Phase 2 - ClientDescriptor trait**: SDK-defined metadata binding compile-time types to runtime resolution\n+3. **Phase 3 - ClientProvider**: Lazy resolution, caching, backoff, and reconnection infrastructure\n+4. **Phase 4 - Macro extension**: `clients = [...]` auto-registers lazy clients into `ClientHub`\n+5. **Phase 5 - Soft OoP deps**: Dependencies on OoP modules don't block startup\n+6. **Phase 6 - Registry extension**: Soft OoP dep resolution:  \n+\n+**Current pattern** (problematic):\n+```rust\n+// Consumer must wire client manually in init() - FAILS if OoP module is not ready\n+calculator_sdk::wire_client(hub, &*directory).await?;\n+```\n+\n+**Proposed pattern**:\n+```rust\n+#[modkit::module(\n+    name = \"calculator_gateway\",\n+    clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],  // REST by default\n+)]\n+// No wire_client() needed - lazy client auto-registered\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Problem Statement\n+\n+The current OoP client wiring pattern has several issues:\n+\n+1. **Eager wiring is fragile**: Consumer modules call `wire_client()` in `init()`, which fails if the OoP dependency is not yet available.\n+2. **Startup coupling**: The entire module fails to start if any OoP dependency is temporarily unavailable.\n+3. **Boilerplate duplication**: Each SDK repeats the same resolve/connect/cache logic.\n+4. **No graceful degradation**: Missing dependencies cause module-level failures instead of per-operation failures (HTTP 424).\n+5. **gRPC complexity**: Binary protobuf payloads are hard to debug; requires specialized tooling.\n+\n+### Current Pattern (calculator_gateway example)\n+\n+```rust\n+// Current: Consumer must wire client manually, and it happens eagerly\n+pub async fn wire_client(hub: &ClientHub, resolver: &dyn DirectoryClient) -> Result<()> {\n+    let endpoint = resolver.resolve_grpc_service(SERVICE_NAME).await?;  // Fails if OoP not ready\n+    let client = CalculatorGrpcClient::connect(&endpoint.uri).await?;   // Fails if network issue\n+    hub.register::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>(Arc::new(client));\n+    Ok(())\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Proposed Solution\n+\n+### Architecture Overview\n+\n+```text\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           SDK Crate (calculator-sdk)                    │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  CalculatorClientDescriptor                                             │\n+│    - MODULE_NAME: \"calculator\"                                          │\n+│    - Api: dyn CalculatorClientV1                                        │\n+│    - Transport: Rest (default) | Grpc (opt-in)                          │\n+│    - Availability Policy: Optional (default)                            │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  LazyCalculatorClient                                                   │\n+│    - Implements CalculatorClientV1                                      │\n+│    - Delegates to ClientProvider for lazy connection                    │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           ModKit (libs/modkit)                          │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  ClientProvider (transport-agnostic interface)                          │\n+│    - Lazy resolution via DirectoryClient                                │\n+│    - Endpoint/connection caching with eviction on error                 │\n+│    - Backoff/rate-limiting for reconnects                               │\n+│    - Transport middleware (timeouts, retries, tracing)                  │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  RestClientProvider (default) | GrpcClientProvider (feature = \"grpc\")   │\n+│    - Transport-specific implementations                                 │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  #[modkit::module] macro extension                                      │\n+│    - clients = [CalculatorClientDescriptor]                             │\n+│    - Auto-registers LazyClient into ClientHub                           │\n+│    - Auto-injects MODULE_NAME from each descriptor into deps            │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                      Consumer Module (calculator_gateway)               │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  #[modkit::module(                                                      │\n+│      name = \"calculator_gateway\",                                       │\n+│      capabilities = [rest],                                             │\n+│      clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],            │\n+│      // deps auto-injected: [\"calculator\"] from descriptor              │\n+│  )]                                                                     │\n+│                                                                         │\n+│  // No wire_client() call needed!                                       │\n+│  // Client is always available from ClientHub                           │\n+│  let calc = hub.get::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>()?;                       │\n+│  calc.add(ctx, a, b).await?;  // Lazy connect on first call             │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Detailed Implementation\n+\n+### Phase 1: REST as Default Transport\n+\n+**Rationale**: REST is simpler to debug, requires no code generation, and is sufficient for most OoP calls. gRPC remains available for streaming or high-throughput use cases.\n+\n+| Factor          | REST                            | gRPC                         |\n+|-----------------|---------------------------------|------------------------------|\n+| Debuggability   | ✅ curl, browser, any HTTP tool | ❌ Requires specialized tools |\n+| Simplicity      | ✅ JSON, standard HTTP          | ❌ Protobuf, code generation  |\n+| Browser support | ✅ Native                       | ❌ Requires gRPC-Web proxy    |\n+| API reuse       | ✅ Same as public REST API      | ❌ Separate interface         |\n+| Streaming       | ❌ Requires SSE/WebSocket       | ✅ Native support             |\n+| Performance     | ⚠️ JSON overhead                | ✅ Binary, efficient          |\n+\n+#### 1.1 Transport Enum\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/transport.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Transport protocol for OoP communication.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum Transport {\n+    /// REST with JSON serialization (default).\n+    #[default]\n+    Rest,\n+    /// gRPC with protobuf serialization (opt-in, requires feature = \"grpc\").\n+    #[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+    Grpc,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### 1.2 REST Service Discovery Infrastructure\n+\n+REST service discovery requires extending the existing `ModuleInstance`, `ModuleManager`, and `DirectoryClient` to track and resolve REST endpoints.\n+\n+##### 1.2.1 Extend `ModuleInstance` to track REST endpoints\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/runtime/module_manager.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Represents a single instance of a module\n+#[derive(Debug)]\n+pub struct ModuleInstance {\n+    pub module: String,\n+    pub instance_id: Uuid,\n+    pub control: Option<Endpoint>,\n+    pub grpc_services: HashMap<String, Endpoint>,\n+    pub rest_endpoint: Option<Endpoint>,  // NEW: REST base URL for this instance\n+    pub version: Option<String>,\n+    inner: Arc<parking_lot::RwLock<InstanceRuntimeState>>,\n+}\n+\n+impl ModuleInstance {\n+    // ... existing methods ...\n+\n+    /// Set the REST endpoint for this instance\n+    pub fn with_rest_endpoint(mut self, ep: Endpoint) -> Self {\n+        self.rest_endpoint = Some(ep);\n+        self\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.2 Extend `ModuleManager` with REST discovery\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/runtime/module_manager.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+impl ModuleManager {\n+    /// Pick a REST endpoint for a module using round-robin selection.\n+    /// Returns (module_name, instance, endpoint) if found.\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn pick_rest_endpoint_round_robin(\n+        &self,\n+        module_name: &str,\n+    ) -> Option<(String, Arc<ModuleInstance>, Endpoint)> {\n+        let instances_entry = self.inner.get(module_name)?;\n+        let instances = instances_entry.value();\n+\n+        // Filter to instances with REST endpoints and healthy/ready state\n+        let candidates: Vec<_> = instances\n+            .iter()\n+            .filter(|inst| {\n+                inst.rest_endpoint.is_some()\n+                    && matches!(inst.state(), InstanceState::Healthy | InstanceState::Ready)\n+            })\n+            .cloned()\n+            .collect();\n+\n+        if candidates.is_empty() {\n+            return None;\n+        }\n+\n+        let len = candidates.len();\n+        let rr_key = format!(\"rest:{}\", module_name);\n+        let mut counter = self.rr_counters.entry(rr_key).or_insert(0);\n+        let idx = *counter % len;\n+        *counter = (*counter + 1) % len;\n+\n+        candidates.get(idx).map(|inst| {\n+            (\n+                module_name.to_owned(),\n+                inst.clone(),\n+                inst.rest_endpoint.clone().expect(\"filtered above\"),\n+            )\n+        })\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.3 Extend `DirectoryClient` trait\n+\n+**Location**: `cf_system_sdks/src/directory.rs` (upstream crate — requires update)\n+\n+```rust\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait DirectoryClient: Send + Sync {\n+    /// Resolve REST endpoint for a module (default for OoP).\n+    async fn resolve_rest_service(&self, module_name: &str) -> Result<RestEndpoint>;\n+\n+    /// Resolve gRPC endpoint for a module (opt-in).\n+    async fn resolve_grpc_service(&self, service_name: &str) -> Result<ServiceEndpoint>;\n+\n+    // ... existing methods (list_instances, register_instance, etc.) ...\n+}\n+\n+/// REST endpoint for a module\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct RestEndpoint {\n+    /// Base URL for the module's REST API (e.g., \"http://calculator:8080\")\n+    pub base_url: String,\n+}\n+\n+impl RestEndpoint {\n+    pub fn new(base_url: impl Into<String>) -> Self {\n+        Self { base_url: base_url.into() }\n+    }\n+\n+    pub fn http(host: &str, port: u16) -> Self {\n+        Self { base_url: format!(\"http://{}:{}\", host, port) }\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.4 Implement `resolve_rest_service` in `LocalDirectoryClient`\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/directory.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl DirectoryClient for LocalDirectoryClient {\n+    async fn resolve_rest_service(&self, module_name: &str) -> Result<RestEndpoint> {\n+        if let Some((_, _, ep)) = self.mgr.pick_rest_endpoint_round_robin(module_name) {\n+            return Ok(RestEndpoint::new(ep.uri));\n+        }\n+\n+        anyhow::bail!(\"REST service not found or no healthy instances: {module_name}\")\n+    }\n+\n+    // ... existing methods unchanged ...\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.5 Extend `RegisterInstanceInfo` for REST registration\n+\n+**Location**: `cf_system_sdks/src/directory.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Information needed to register a module instance\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct RegisterInstanceInfo {\n+    pub module: String,\n+    pub instance_id: String,\n+    pub grpc_services: Vec<(String, ServiceEndpoint)>,\n+    pub rest_endpoint: Option<RestEndpoint>,  // NEW\n+    pub version: Option<String>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.6 OoP Module REST Registration\n+\n+When an OoP module starts, it registers its REST endpoint with the DirectoryService:\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/oop.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+async fn register_with_directory(\n+    directory: &dyn DirectoryClient,\n+    module_name: &str,\n+    instance_id: Uuid,\n+    rest_port: u16,\n+    grpc_services: Vec<(String, ServiceEndpoint)>,\n+) -> Result<()> {\n+    let info = RegisterInstanceInfo {\n+        module: module_name.to_owned(),\n+        instance_id: instance_id.to_string(),\n+        grpc_services,\n+        rest_endpoint: Some(RestEndpoint::http(\"0.0.0.0\", rest_port)),\n+        version: Some(env!(\"CARGO_PKG_VERSION\").to_owned()),\n+    };\n+\n+    directory.register_instance(info).await\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.7 Design Decisions\n+\n+| Decision | Rationale |\n+|----------|-----------|\n+| **One REST endpoint per instance** | Unlike gRPC (multiple services per instance), REST modules expose a single base URL with path-based routing |\n+| **Module-name based resolution** | REST discovery uses `module_name` (e.g., \"calculator\"), not service name |\n+| **Reuse existing health tracking** | REST endpoints use the same `InstanceState` and heartbeat mechanism as gRPC |\n+| **Symmetric API** | `resolve_rest_service()` mirrors `resolve_grpc_service()` for consistency |\n+\n+##### 1.2.8 Migration Notes\n+\n+1. **`cf_system_sdks` must be updated first** — Add `RestEndpoint`, extend `RegisterInstanceInfo`, and add `resolve_rest_service()` to `DirectoryClient`\n+2. **`ModuleInstance` is extended** — Existing code continues to work; `rest_endpoint` defaults to `None`\n+3. **OoP modules must register REST endpoints** — Update bootstrap to include REST port in registration\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Phase 2: ClientDescriptor Trait\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/descriptor.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Client descriptor traits for typed OoP client metadata.\n+\n+use std::time::Duration;\n+\n+/// Availability policy for OoP clients.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum ClientAvailabilityPolicy {\n+    /// Client is optional; operations fail gracefully with SDK error (maps to HTTP 424).\n+    #[default]\n+    Optional,\n+    /// Client is required; module readiness may depend on availability.\n+    Required,\n+}\n+\n+/// Configuration for client behavior.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct ClientConfig {\n+    /// Transport protocol (REST default, gRPC opt-in).\n+    pub transport: Transport,\n+    /// Connection timeout for initial connect.\n+    pub connect_timeout: Duration,\n+    /// Request timeout for individual calls.\n+    pub request_timeout: Duration,\n+    /// Maximum backoff duration between reconnect attempts.\n+    pub max_backoff: Duration,\n+    /// Availability policy.\n+    pub availability_policy: ClientAvailabilityPolicy,\n+}\n+\n+impl Default for ClientConfig {\n+    fn default() -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            transport: Transport::Rest,\n+            connect_timeout: Duration::from_secs(5),\n+            request_timeout: Duration::from_secs(30),\n+            max_backoff: Duration::from_secs(60),\n+            availability_policy: ClientAvailabilityPolicy::Optional,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl ClientConfig {\n+    /// Create a REST client config (default).\n+    pub fn rest() -> Self {\n+        Self::default()\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Create a gRPC client config (opt-in).\n+    #[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+    pub fn grpc() -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            transport: Transport::Grpc,\n+            ..Self::default()\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Descriptor for an OoP client, defined in SDK crates.\n+///\n+/// This trait binds compile-time type information to runtime metadata\n+/// needed for lazy client resolution and registration.\n+pub trait ClientDescriptor: Send + Sync + 'static {\n+    /// The SDK API trait type (e.g., `dyn CalculatorClientV1`).\n+    type Api: ?Sized + Send + Sync + 'static;\n+\n+    /// Module name for dependency graph and Directory resolution.\n+    const MODULE_NAME: &'static str;\n+\n+    /// Client configuration (transport, timeouts, backoff, availability).\n+    fn config() -> ClientConfig {\n+        ClientConfig::default()\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Phase 3: ClientProvider Infrastructure\n+\n+#### 3.1 RestClientProvider (Default)\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/rest_provider.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Universal lazy REST client provider (default transport).\n+\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+use std::time::{Duration, Instant};\n+\n+use parking_lot::RwLock;\n+use tokio::sync::Semaphore;\n+\n+use crate::client_hub::ClientHub;\n+use crate::directory::DirectoryClient;\n+use crate::clients::descriptor::ClientConfig;\n+use modkit_http::HttpClient;\n+\n+/// Error type for REST provider operations.\n+#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\n+pub enum RestProviderError {\n+    #[error(\"service not found in directory: {module_name}\")]\n+    ServiceNotFound { module_name: &'static str },\n+\n+    #[error(\"HTTP request failed: {0}\")]\n+    HttpError(#[source] modkit_http::HttpError),\n+\n+    #[error(\"directory resolution failed: {0}\")]\n+    DirectoryError(#[source] anyhow::Error),\n+\n+    #[error(\"service temporarily unavailable (backoff active)\")]\n+    Backoff { retry_after: Duration },\n+}\n+\n+struct CachedEndpoint {\n+    base_url: String,\n+    resolved_at: Instant,\n+}\n+\n+struct ProviderState {\n+    cached: Option<CachedEndpoint>,\n+    last_failure: Option<Instant>,\n+    failure_count: u32,\n+}\n+\n+/// Universal lazy REST client provider.\n+///\n+/// Handles:\n+/// - Lazy endpoint resolution via DirectoryClient\n+/// - Base URL caching with automatic eviction on errors\n+/// - Exponential backoff for reconnection attempts\n+/// - Rate limiting to prevent thundering herds\n+pub struct RestClientProvider {\n+    module_name: &'static str,\n+    config: ClientConfig,\n+    hub: Arc<ClientHub>,\n+    http_client: HttpClient,\n+    state: RwLock<ProviderState>,\n+    resolve_semaphore: Semaphore,\n+}\n+\n+impl RestClientProvider {\n+    pub fn new(\n+        module_name: &'static str,\n+        config: ClientConfig,\n+        hub: Arc<ClientHub>,\n+    ) -> Self {\n+        let http_client = HttpClient::builder()\n+            .timeout(config.request_timeout)\n+            .connect_timeout(config.connect_timeout)\n+            .build();\n+\n+        Self {\n+            module_name,\n+            config,\n+            hub,\n+            http_client,\n+            state: RwLock::new(ProviderState {\n+                cached: None,\n+                last_failure: None,\n+                failure_count: 0,\n+            }),\n+            resolve_semaphore: Semaphore::new(1),\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Get the base URL for the service, resolving lazily.\n+    pub async fn get_base_url(&self) -> Result<String, RestProviderError> {\n+        // Fast path: return cached endpoint\n+        {\n+            let state = self.state.read();\n+            if let Some(ref cached) = state.cached {\n+                return Ok(cached.base_url.clone());\n+            }\n+\n+            // Check backoff\n+            if let Some(last_failure) = state.last_failure {\n+                let backoff = self.calculate_backoff(state.failure_count);\n+                let elapsed = last_failure.elapsed();\n+                if elapsed < backoff {\n+                    return Err(RestProviderError::Backoff {\n+                        retry_after: backoff - elapsed,\n+                    });\n+                }\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        // Slow path: acquire semaphore and resolve\n+        let _permit = self.resolve_semaphore.acquire().await\n+            .expect(\"semaphore is never closed\");\n+\n+        // Double-check after acquiring semaphore\n+        {\n+            let state = self.state.read();\n+            if let Some(ref cached) = state.cached {\n+                return Ok(cached.base_url.clone());\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        self.resolve_internal().await\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Get the HTTP client for making requests.\n+    pub fn http_client(&self) -> &HttpClient {\n+        &self.http_client\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Evict the cached endpoint (call on transport errors).\n+    pub fn evict(&self) {\n+        let mut state = self.state.write();\n+        state.cached = None;\n+        state.last_failure = Some(Instant::now());\n+        state.failure_count = state.failure_count.saturating_add(1);\n+        tracing::warn!(\n+            module = self.module_name,\n+            failure_count = state.failure_count,\n+            \"Evicted cached REST endpoint\"\n+        );\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Reset failure state (call on successful request).\n+    pub fn reset_failures(&self) {\n+        let mut state = self.state.write();\n+        if state.failure_count > 0 {\n+            state.failure_count = 0;\n+            state.last_failure = None;\n+            tracing::debug!(module = self.module_name, \"Reset failure state after success\");\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    async fn resolve_internal(&self) -> Result<String, RestProviderError> {\n+        let directory = self\n+            .hub\n+            .get::<dyn DirectoryClient>()\n+            .map_err(|e| RestProviderError::DirectoryError(e.into()))?;\n+\n+        let endpoint = directory\n+            .resolve_rest_service(self.module_name)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(RestProviderError::DirectoryError)?;\n+\n+        tracing::debug!(\n+            module = self.module_name,\n+            base_url = %endpoint.base_url,\n+            \"Resolved REST endpoint\"\n+        );\n+\n+        {\n+            let mut state = self.state.write();\n+            state.cached = Some(CachedEndpoint {\n+                base_url: endpoint.base_url.clone(),\n+                resolved_at: Instant::now(),\n+            });\n+            state.failure_count = 0;\n+            state.last_failure = None;\n+        }\n+\n+        Ok(endpoint.base_url)\n+    }\n+\n+    fn calculate_backoff(&self, failure_count: u32) -> Duration {\n+        let base = Duration::from_millis(100);\n+        let max = self.config.max_backoff;\n+        let backoff = base.saturating_mul(2u32.saturating_pow(failure_count.min(10)));\n+        backoff.min(max)\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### 3.2 GrpcClientProvider (Optional)\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/grpc_provider.rs`\n+\n+> Feature-gated behind `feature = \"grpc\"` for streaming/high-throughput use cases.\n+\n+```rust\n+#[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+//! Lazy gRPC client provider (optional transport).\n+\n+// Implementation follows same pattern as RestClientProvider\n+// but manages tonic::transport::Channel instead of base URL\n+```\n+\n+#### 3.3 LazyClientError\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/error.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Error returned by lazy clients when the OoP dependency is unavailable.\n+#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\n+pub enum LazyClientError {\n+    #[error(\"service unavailable: {module_name}\")]\n+    Unavailable {\n+        module_name: &'static str,\n+        #[source]\n+        source: Box<dyn std::error::Error + Send + Sync>,\n+    },\n+\n+    #[error(\"request failed: {0}\")]\n+    RequestFailed(String),\n+\n+    #[error(\"response parsing failed: {0}\")]\n+    ParseError(#[source] serde_json::Error),\n+}\n+\n+impl LazyClientError {\n+    /// Returns true if this error indicates the service is temporarily unavailable.\n+    /// REST handlers should map this to HTTP 424 Failed Dependency.\n+    pub fn is_dependency_unavailable(&self) -> bool {\n+        matches!(self, LazyClientError::Unavailable { .. })\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Phase 4: SDK Crate Updates (calculator-sdk example)\n+\n+#### 4.1 Descriptor\n+\n+**Location**: `calculator-sdk/src/descriptor.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit::clients::descriptor::{ClientDescriptor, ClientConfig};\n+use crate::api::CalculatorClientV1;\n+\n+/// Descriptor for the Calculator client (REST by default).\n+pub struct CalculatorClientDescriptor;\n+\n+impl ClientDescriptor for CalculatorClientDescriptor {\n+    type Api = dyn CalculatorClientV1;\n+    const MODULE_NAME: &'static str = \"calculator\";\n+\n+    fn config() -> ClientConfig {\n+        ClientConfig::rest()  // Default: REST transport","path":"docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md","commit_id":"edd86e3e6cf91af1a08e3970d60dc26bc6acb6e6","original_commit_id":"030bc79ea9322b429e351c332cbffd4f44791b3c","user":{"login":"striped-zebra-dev","id":225538363,"node_id":"U_kgDODXFxOw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225538363?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/striped-zebra-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I'd love to see the possible content of the client config, is this the place we have all the retry/not-retry, and other strategies?","created_at":"2026-02-19T16:20:18Z","updated_at":"2026-02-19T16:20:18Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2828805752","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2828805752"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2828805752"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2828805752/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":1438,"original_line":674,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":674,"position":1438,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2830022076","pull_request_review_id":3828366785,"id":2830022076,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6orrW8","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1050 @@\n+# ADR-0003: Universal Lazy Typed REST Clients for OoP Modules\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+This proposal outlines a migration from gRPC to REST as the default transport for out-of-process (OoP) modules and introduces a **universal lazy typed client layer** for OoP module communication in ModKit. The implementation is structured in phases:\n+\n+1. **Phase 1 - REST as default transport**: Establish REST as the default OoP transport; gRPC becomes opt-in\n+2. **Phase 2 - ClientDescriptor trait**: SDK-defined metadata binding compile-time types to runtime resolution\n+3. **Phase 3 - ClientProvider**: Lazy resolution, caching, backoff, and reconnection infrastructure\n+4. **Phase 4 - Macro extension**: `clients = [...]` auto-registers lazy clients into `ClientHub`\n+5. **Phase 5 - Soft OoP deps**: Dependencies on OoP modules don't block startup\n+6. **Phase 6 - Registry extension**: Soft OoP dep resolution:  \n+\n+**Current pattern** (problematic):\n+```rust\n+// Consumer must wire client manually in init() - FAILS if OoP module is not ready\n+calculator_sdk::wire_client(hub, &*directory).await?;\n+```\n+\n+**Proposed pattern**:\n+```rust\n+#[modkit::module(\n+    name = \"calculator_gateway\",\n+    clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],  // REST by default\n+)]\n+// No wire_client() needed - lazy client auto-registered\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Problem Statement\n+\n+The current OoP client wiring pattern has several issues:\n+\n+1. **Eager wiring is fragile**: Consumer modules call `wire_client()` in `init()`, which fails if the OoP dependency is not yet available.\n+2. **Startup coupling**: The entire module fails to start if any OoP dependency is temporarily unavailable.\n+3. **Boilerplate duplication**: Each SDK repeats the same resolve/connect/cache logic.\n+4. **No graceful degradation**: Missing dependencies cause module-level failures instead of per-operation failures (HTTP 424).\n+5. **gRPC complexity**: Binary protobuf payloads are hard to debug; requires specialized tooling.\n+\n+### Current Pattern (calculator_gateway example)\n+\n+```rust\n+// Current: Consumer must wire client manually, and it happens eagerly\n+pub async fn wire_client(hub: &ClientHub, resolver: &dyn DirectoryClient) -> Result<()> {\n+    let endpoint = resolver.resolve_grpc_service(SERVICE_NAME).await?;  // Fails if OoP not ready\n+    let client = CalculatorGrpcClient::connect(&endpoint.uri).await?;   // Fails if network issue\n+    hub.register::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>(Arc::new(client));\n+    Ok(())\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Proposed Solution\n+\n+### Architecture Overview\n+\n+```text\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           SDK Crate (calculator-sdk)                    │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  CalculatorClientDescriptor                                             │\n+│    - MODULE_NAME: \"calculator\"                                          │\n+│    - Api: dyn CalculatorClientV1                                        │\n+│    - Transport: Rest (default) | Grpc (opt-in)                          │\n+│    - Availability Policy: Optional (default)                            │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  LazyCalculatorClient                                                   │\n+│    - Implements CalculatorClientV1                                      │\n+│    - Delegates to ClientProvider for lazy connection                    │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           ModKit (libs/modkit)                          │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  ClientProvider (transport-agnostic interface)                          │\n+│    - Lazy resolution via DirectoryClient                                │\n+│    - Endpoint/connection caching with eviction on error                 │\n+│    - Backoff/rate-limiting for reconnects                               │\n+│    - Transport middleware (timeouts, retries, tracing)                  │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  RestClientProvider (default) | GrpcClientProvider (feature = \"grpc\")   │\n+│    - Transport-specific implementations                                 │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  #[modkit::module] macro extension                                      │\n+│    - clients = [CalculatorClientDescriptor]                             │\n+│    - Auto-registers LazyClient into ClientHub                           │\n+│    - Auto-injects MODULE_NAME from each descriptor into deps            │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                      Consumer Module (calculator_gateway)               │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  #[modkit::module(                                                      │\n+│      name = \"calculator_gateway\",                                       │\n+│      capabilities = [rest],                                             │\n+│      clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],            │\n+│      // deps auto-injected: [\"calculator\"] from descriptor              │\n+│  )]                                                                     │\n+│                                                                         │\n+│  // No wire_client() call needed!                                       │\n+│  // Client is always available from ClientHub                           │\n+│  let calc = hub.get::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>()?;                       │\n+│  calc.add(ctx, a, b).await?;  // Lazy connect on first call             │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Detailed Implementation\n+\n+### Phase 1: REST as Default Transport\n+\n+**Rationale**: REST is simpler to debug, requires no code generation, and is sufficient for most OoP calls. gRPC remains available for streaming or high-throughput use cases.\n+\n+| Factor          | REST                            | gRPC                         |\n+|-----------------|---------------------------------|------------------------------|\n+| Debuggability   | ✅ curl, browser, any HTTP tool | ❌ Requires specialized tools |\n+| Simplicity      | ✅ JSON, standard HTTP          | ❌ Protobuf, code generation  |\n+| Browser support | ✅ Native                       | ❌ Requires gRPC-Web proxy    |\n+| API reuse       | ✅ Same as public REST API      | ❌ Separate interface         |\n+| Streaming       | ❌ Requires SSE/WebSocket       | ✅ Native support             |\n+| Performance     | ⚠️ JSON overhead                | ✅ Binary, efficient          |\n+\n+#### 1.1 Transport Enum\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/transport.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Transport protocol for OoP communication.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum Transport {\n+    /// REST with JSON serialization (default).\n+    #[default]\n+    Rest,\n+    /// gRPC with protobuf serialization (opt-in, requires feature = \"grpc\").\n+    #[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+    Grpc,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### 1.2 REST Service Discovery Infrastructure\n+\n+REST service discovery requires extending the existing `ModuleInstance`, `ModuleManager`, and `DirectoryClient` to track and resolve REST endpoints.\n+\n+##### 1.2.1 Extend `ModuleInstance` to track REST endpoints\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/runtime/module_manager.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Represents a single instance of a module\n+#[derive(Debug)]\n+pub struct ModuleInstance {\n+    pub module: String,\n+    pub instance_id: Uuid,\n+    pub control: Option<Endpoint>,\n+    pub grpc_services: HashMap<String, Endpoint>,\n+    pub rest_endpoint: Option<Endpoint>,  // NEW: REST base URL for this instance\n+    pub version: Option<String>,\n+    inner: Arc<parking_lot::RwLock<InstanceRuntimeState>>,\n+}\n+\n+impl ModuleInstance {\n+    // ... existing methods ...\n+\n+    /// Set the REST endpoint for this instance\n+    pub fn with_rest_endpoint(mut self, ep: Endpoint) -> Self {\n+        self.rest_endpoint = Some(ep);\n+        self\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.2 Extend `ModuleManager` with REST discovery\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/runtime/module_manager.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+impl ModuleManager {\n+    /// Pick a REST endpoint for a module using round-robin selection.\n+    /// Returns (module_name, instance, endpoint) if found.\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn pick_rest_endpoint_round_robin(\n+        &self,\n+        module_name: &str,\n+    ) -> Option<(String, Arc<ModuleInstance>, Endpoint)> {\n+        let instances_entry = self.inner.get(module_name)?;\n+        let instances = instances_entry.value();\n+\n+        // Filter to instances with REST endpoints and healthy/ready state\n+        let candidates: Vec<_> = instances\n+            .iter()\n+            .filter(|inst| {\n+                inst.rest_endpoint.is_some()\n+                    && matches!(inst.state(), InstanceState::Healthy | InstanceState::Ready)\n+            })\n+            .cloned()\n+            .collect();\n+\n+        if candidates.is_empty() {\n+            return None;\n+        }\n+\n+        let len = candidates.len();\n+        let rr_key = format!(\"rest:{}\", module_name);\n+        let mut counter = self.rr_counters.entry(rr_key).or_insert(0);\n+        let idx = *counter % len;\n+        *counter = (*counter + 1) % len;\n+\n+        candidates.get(idx).map(|inst| {\n+            (\n+                module_name.to_owned(),\n+                inst.clone(),\n+                inst.rest_endpoint.clone().expect(\"filtered above\"),\n+            )\n+        })\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.3 Extend `DirectoryClient` trait\n+\n+**Location**: `cf_system_sdks/src/directory.rs` (upstream crate — requires update)\n+\n+```rust\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait DirectoryClient: Send + Sync {\n+    /// Resolve REST endpoint for a module (default for OoP).\n+    async fn resolve_rest_service(&self, module_name: &str) -> Result<RestEndpoint>;\n+\n+    /// Resolve gRPC endpoint for a module (opt-in).\n+    async fn resolve_grpc_service(&self, service_name: &str) -> Result<ServiceEndpoint>;\n+\n+    // ... existing methods (list_instances, register_instance, etc.) ...\n+}\n+\n+/// REST endpoint for a module\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct RestEndpoint {\n+    /// Base URL for the module's REST API (e.g., \"http://calculator:8080\")\n+    pub base_url: String,\n+}\n+\n+impl RestEndpoint {\n+    pub fn new(base_url: impl Into<String>) -> Self {\n+        Self { base_url: base_url.into() }\n+    }\n+\n+    pub fn http(host: &str, port: u16) -> Self {\n+        Self { base_url: format!(\"http://{}:{}\", host, port) }\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.4 Implement `resolve_rest_service` in `LocalDirectoryClient`\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/directory.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl DirectoryClient for LocalDirectoryClient {\n+    async fn resolve_rest_service(&self, module_name: &str) -> Result<RestEndpoint> {\n+        if let Some((_, _, ep)) = self.mgr.pick_rest_endpoint_round_robin(module_name) {\n+            return Ok(RestEndpoint::new(ep.uri));\n+        }\n+\n+        anyhow::bail!(\"REST service not found or no healthy instances: {module_name}\")\n+    }\n+\n+    // ... existing methods unchanged ...\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.5 Extend `RegisterInstanceInfo` for REST registration\n+\n+**Location**: `cf_system_sdks/src/directory.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Information needed to register a module instance\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct RegisterInstanceInfo {\n+    pub module: String,\n+    pub instance_id: String,\n+    pub grpc_services: Vec<(String, ServiceEndpoint)>,\n+    pub rest_endpoint: Option<RestEndpoint>,  // NEW\n+    pub version: Option<String>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.6 OoP Module REST Registration\n+\n+When an OoP module starts, it registers its REST endpoint with the DirectoryService:\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/oop.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+async fn register_with_directory(\n+    directory: &dyn DirectoryClient,\n+    module_name: &str,\n+    instance_id: Uuid,\n+    rest_port: u16,\n+    grpc_services: Vec<(String, ServiceEndpoint)>,\n+) -> Result<()> {\n+    let info = RegisterInstanceInfo {\n+        module: module_name.to_owned(),\n+        instance_id: instance_id.to_string(),\n+        grpc_services,\n+        rest_endpoint: Some(RestEndpoint::http(\"0.0.0.0\", rest_port)),\n+        version: Some(env!(\"CARGO_PKG_VERSION\").to_owned()),\n+    };\n+\n+    directory.register_instance(info).await\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.7 Design Decisions\n+\n+| Decision | Rationale |\n+|----------|-----------|\n+| **One REST endpoint per instance** | Unlike gRPC (multiple services per instance), REST modules expose a single base URL with path-based routing |\n+| **Module-name based resolution** | REST discovery uses `module_name` (e.g., \"calculator\"), not service name |\n+| **Reuse existing health tracking** | REST endpoints use the same `InstanceState` and heartbeat mechanism as gRPC |\n+| **Symmetric API** | `resolve_rest_service()` mirrors `resolve_grpc_service()` for consistency |\n+\n+##### 1.2.8 Migration Notes\n+\n+1. **`cf_system_sdks` must be updated first** — Add `RestEndpoint`, extend `RegisterInstanceInfo`, and add `resolve_rest_service()` to `DirectoryClient`\n+2. **`ModuleInstance` is extended** — Existing code continues to work; `rest_endpoint` defaults to `None`\n+3. **OoP modules must register REST endpoints** — Update bootstrap to include REST port in registration\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Phase 2: ClientDescriptor Trait\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/descriptor.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Client descriptor traits for typed OoP client metadata.\n+\n+use std::time::Duration;\n+\n+/// Availability policy for OoP clients.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum ClientAvailabilityPolicy {\n+    /// Client is optional; operations fail gracefully with SDK error (maps to HTTP 424).\n+    #[default]\n+    Optional,\n+    /// Client is required; module readiness may depend on availability.\n+    Required,\n+}\n+\n+/// Configuration for client behavior.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct ClientConfig {\n+    /// Transport protocol (REST default, gRPC opt-in).\n+    pub transport: Transport,\n+    /// Connection timeout for initial connect.\n+    pub connect_timeout: Duration,\n+    /// Request timeout for individual calls.\n+    pub request_timeout: Duration,\n+    /// Maximum backoff duration between reconnect attempts.\n+    pub max_backoff: Duration,\n+    /// Availability policy.\n+    pub availability_policy: ClientAvailabilityPolicy,\n+}\n+\n+impl Default for ClientConfig {\n+    fn default() -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            transport: Transport::Rest,\n+            connect_timeout: Duration::from_secs(5),\n+            request_timeout: Duration::from_secs(30),\n+            max_backoff: Duration::from_secs(60),\n+            availability_policy: ClientAvailabilityPolicy::Optional,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl ClientConfig {\n+    /// Create a REST client config (default).\n+    pub fn rest() -> Self {\n+        Self::default()\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Create a gRPC client config (opt-in).\n+    #[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+    pub fn grpc() -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            transport: Transport::Grpc,\n+            ..Self::default()\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Descriptor for an OoP client, defined in SDK crates.\n+///\n+/// This trait binds compile-time type information to runtime metadata\n+/// needed for lazy client resolution and registration.\n+pub trait ClientDescriptor: Send + Sync + 'static {\n+    /// The SDK API trait type (e.g., `dyn CalculatorClientV1`).\n+    type Api: ?Sized + Send + Sync + 'static;\n+\n+    /// Module name for dependency graph and Directory resolution.\n+    const MODULE_NAME: &'static str;","path":"docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md","commit_id":"edd86e3e6cf91af1a08e3970d60dc26bc6acb6e6","original_commit_id":"030bc79ea9322b429e351c332cbffd4f44791b3c","user":{"login":"alexpitsikoulis","id":50185728,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMTg1NzI4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50185728?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis","html_url":"https://github.com/alexpitsikoulis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I have it set explicitly because it crosses module boundary. It could be derived but that would rely on some magic naming convention and will break if it isn't followed. It works if we wish to enforce that convention but that just seemed a little opinionated to me. No benefit to changing the module name, its just its directory identifier.","created_at":"2026-02-19T20:31:59Z","updated_at":"2026-02-19T20:31:59Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2830022076","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2830022076"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2830022076"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2830022076/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":411,"original_line":407,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2828719155,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":407,"position":411,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2830061281","pull_request_review_id":3828409721,"id":2830061281,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6or07h","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1050 @@\n+# ADR-0003: Universal Lazy Typed REST Clients for OoP Modules\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+This proposal outlines a migration from gRPC to REST as the default transport for out-of-process (OoP) modules and introduces a **universal lazy typed client layer** for OoP module communication in ModKit. The implementation is structured in phases:\n+\n+1. **Phase 1 - REST as default transport**: Establish REST as the default OoP transport; gRPC becomes opt-in\n+2. **Phase 2 - ClientDescriptor trait**: SDK-defined metadata binding compile-time types to runtime resolution\n+3. **Phase 3 - ClientProvider**: Lazy resolution, caching, backoff, and reconnection infrastructure\n+4. **Phase 4 - Macro extension**: `clients = [...]` auto-registers lazy clients into `ClientHub`\n+5. **Phase 5 - Soft OoP deps**: Dependencies on OoP modules don't block startup\n+6. **Phase 6 - Registry extension**: Soft OoP dep resolution:  \n+\n+**Current pattern** (problematic):\n+```rust\n+// Consumer must wire client manually in init() - FAILS if OoP module is not ready\n+calculator_sdk::wire_client(hub, &*directory).await?;\n+```\n+\n+**Proposed pattern**:\n+```rust\n+#[modkit::module(\n+    name = \"calculator_gateway\",\n+    clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],  // REST by default\n+)]\n+// No wire_client() needed - lazy client auto-registered\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Problem Statement\n+\n+The current OoP client wiring pattern has several issues:\n+\n+1. **Eager wiring is fragile**: Consumer modules call `wire_client()` in `init()`, which fails if the OoP dependency is not yet available.\n+2. **Startup coupling**: The entire module fails to start if any OoP dependency is temporarily unavailable.\n+3. **Boilerplate duplication**: Each SDK repeats the same resolve/connect/cache logic.\n+4. **No graceful degradation**: Missing dependencies cause module-level failures instead of per-operation failures (HTTP 424).\n+5. **gRPC complexity**: Binary protobuf payloads are hard to debug; requires specialized tooling.\n+\n+### Current Pattern (calculator_gateway example)\n+\n+```rust\n+// Current: Consumer must wire client manually, and it happens eagerly\n+pub async fn wire_client(hub: &ClientHub, resolver: &dyn DirectoryClient) -> Result<()> {\n+    let endpoint = resolver.resolve_grpc_service(SERVICE_NAME).await?;  // Fails if OoP not ready\n+    let client = CalculatorGrpcClient::connect(&endpoint.uri).await?;   // Fails if network issue\n+    hub.register::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>(Arc::new(client));\n+    Ok(())\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Proposed Solution\n+\n+### Architecture Overview\n+\n+```text\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           SDK Crate (calculator-sdk)                    │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  CalculatorClientDescriptor                                             │\n+│    - MODULE_NAME: \"calculator\"                                          │\n+│    - Api: dyn CalculatorClientV1                                        │\n+│    - Transport: Rest (default) | Grpc (opt-in)                          │\n+│    - Availability Policy: Optional (default)                            │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  LazyCalculatorClient                                                   │\n+│    - Implements CalculatorClientV1                                      │\n+│    - Delegates to ClientProvider for lazy connection                    │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           ModKit (libs/modkit)                          │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  ClientProvider (transport-agnostic interface)                          │\n+│    - Lazy resolution via DirectoryClient                                │\n+│    - Endpoint/connection caching with eviction on error                 │\n+│    - Backoff/rate-limiting for reconnects                               │\n+│    - Transport middleware (timeouts, retries, tracing)                  │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  RestClientProvider (default) | GrpcClientProvider (feature = \"grpc\")   │\n+│    - Transport-specific implementations                                 │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  #[modkit::module] macro extension                                      │\n+│    - clients = [CalculatorClientDescriptor]                             │\n+│    - Auto-registers LazyClient into ClientHub                           │\n+│    - Auto-injects MODULE_NAME from each descriptor into deps            │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                      Consumer Module (calculator_gateway)               │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  #[modkit::module(                                                      │\n+│      name = \"calculator_gateway\",                                       │\n+│      capabilities = [rest],                                             │\n+│      clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],            │\n+│      // deps auto-injected: [\"calculator\"] from descriptor              │\n+│  )]                                                                     │\n+│                                                                         │\n+│  // No wire_client() call needed!                                       │\n+│  // Client is always available from ClientHub                           │\n+│  let calc = hub.get::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>()?;                       │\n+│  calc.add(ctx, a, b).await?;  // Lazy connect on first call             │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Detailed Implementation\n+\n+### Phase 1: REST as Default Transport\n+\n+**Rationale**: REST is simpler to debug, requires no code generation, and is sufficient for most OoP calls. gRPC remains available for streaming or high-throughput use cases.\n+\n+| Factor          | REST                            | gRPC                         |\n+|-----------------|---------------------------------|------------------------------|\n+| Debuggability   | ✅ curl, browser, any HTTP tool | ❌ Requires specialized tools |\n+| Simplicity      | ✅ JSON, standard HTTP          | ❌ Protobuf, code generation  |\n+| Browser support | ✅ Native                       | ❌ Requires gRPC-Web proxy    |\n+| API reuse       | ✅ Same as public REST API      | ❌ Separate interface         |\n+| Streaming       | ❌ Requires SSE/WebSocket       | ✅ Native support             |\n+| Performance     | ⚠️ JSON overhead                | ✅ Binary, efficient          |\n+\n+#### 1.1 Transport Enum\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/transport.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Transport protocol for OoP communication.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum Transport {\n+    /// REST with JSON serialization (default).\n+    #[default]\n+    Rest,\n+    /// gRPC with protobuf serialization (opt-in, requires feature = \"grpc\").\n+    #[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+    Grpc,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### 1.2 REST Service Discovery Infrastructure\n+\n+REST service discovery requires extending the existing `ModuleInstance`, `ModuleManager`, and `DirectoryClient` to track and resolve REST endpoints.\n+\n+##### 1.2.1 Extend `ModuleInstance` to track REST endpoints\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/runtime/module_manager.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Represents a single instance of a module\n+#[derive(Debug)]\n+pub struct ModuleInstance {\n+    pub module: String,\n+    pub instance_id: Uuid,\n+    pub control: Option<Endpoint>,\n+    pub grpc_services: HashMap<String, Endpoint>,\n+    pub rest_endpoint: Option<Endpoint>,  // NEW: REST base URL for this instance\n+    pub version: Option<String>,\n+    inner: Arc<parking_lot::RwLock<InstanceRuntimeState>>,\n+}\n+\n+impl ModuleInstance {\n+    // ... existing methods ...\n+\n+    /// Set the REST endpoint for this instance\n+    pub fn with_rest_endpoint(mut self, ep: Endpoint) -> Self {\n+        self.rest_endpoint = Some(ep);\n+        self\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.2 Extend `ModuleManager` with REST discovery\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/runtime/module_manager.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+impl ModuleManager {\n+    /// Pick a REST endpoint for a module using round-robin selection.\n+    /// Returns (module_name, instance, endpoint) if found.\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn pick_rest_endpoint_round_robin(\n+        &self,\n+        module_name: &str,\n+    ) -> Option<(String, Arc<ModuleInstance>, Endpoint)> {\n+        let instances_entry = self.inner.get(module_name)?;\n+        let instances = instances_entry.value();\n+\n+        // Filter to instances with REST endpoints and healthy/ready state\n+        let candidates: Vec<_> = instances\n+            .iter()\n+            .filter(|inst| {\n+                inst.rest_endpoint.is_some()\n+                    && matches!(inst.state(), InstanceState::Healthy | InstanceState::Ready)\n+            })\n+            .cloned()\n+            .collect();\n+\n+        if candidates.is_empty() {\n+            return None;\n+        }\n+\n+        let len = candidates.len();\n+        let rr_key = format!(\"rest:{}\", module_name);\n+        let mut counter = self.rr_counters.entry(rr_key).or_insert(0);\n+        let idx = *counter % len;\n+        *counter = (*counter + 1) % len;\n+\n+        candidates.get(idx).map(|inst| {\n+            (\n+                module_name.to_owned(),\n+                inst.clone(),\n+                inst.rest_endpoint.clone().expect(\"filtered above\"),\n+            )\n+        })\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.3 Extend `DirectoryClient` trait\n+\n+**Location**: `cf_system_sdks/src/directory.rs` (upstream crate — requires update)\n+\n+```rust\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait DirectoryClient: Send + Sync {\n+    /// Resolve REST endpoint for a module (default for OoP).\n+    async fn resolve_rest_service(&self, module_name: &str) -> Result<RestEndpoint>;\n+\n+    /// Resolve gRPC endpoint for a module (opt-in).\n+    async fn resolve_grpc_service(&self, service_name: &str) -> Result<ServiceEndpoint>;\n+\n+    // ... existing methods (list_instances, register_instance, etc.) ...\n+}\n+\n+/// REST endpoint for a module\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct RestEndpoint {\n+    /// Base URL for the module's REST API (e.g., \"http://calculator:8080\")\n+    pub base_url: String,\n+}\n+\n+impl RestEndpoint {\n+    pub fn new(base_url: impl Into<String>) -> Self {\n+        Self { base_url: base_url.into() }\n+    }\n+\n+    pub fn http(host: &str, port: u16) -> Self {\n+        Self { base_url: format!(\"http://{}:{}\", host, port) }\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.4 Implement `resolve_rest_service` in `LocalDirectoryClient`\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/directory.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl DirectoryClient for LocalDirectoryClient {\n+    async fn resolve_rest_service(&self, module_name: &str) -> Result<RestEndpoint> {\n+        if let Some((_, _, ep)) = self.mgr.pick_rest_endpoint_round_robin(module_name) {\n+            return Ok(RestEndpoint::new(ep.uri));\n+        }\n+\n+        anyhow::bail!(\"REST service not found or no healthy instances: {module_name}\")\n+    }\n+\n+    // ... existing methods unchanged ...\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.5 Extend `RegisterInstanceInfo` for REST registration\n+\n+**Location**: `cf_system_sdks/src/directory.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Information needed to register a module instance\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct RegisterInstanceInfo {\n+    pub module: String,\n+    pub instance_id: String,\n+    pub grpc_services: Vec<(String, ServiceEndpoint)>,\n+    pub rest_endpoint: Option<RestEndpoint>,  // NEW\n+    pub version: Option<String>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.6 OoP Module REST Registration\n+\n+When an OoP module starts, it registers its REST endpoint with the DirectoryService:\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/oop.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+async fn register_with_directory(\n+    directory: &dyn DirectoryClient,\n+    module_name: &str,\n+    instance_id: Uuid,\n+    rest_port: u16,\n+    grpc_services: Vec<(String, ServiceEndpoint)>,\n+) -> Result<()> {\n+    let info = RegisterInstanceInfo {\n+        module: module_name.to_owned(),\n+        instance_id: instance_id.to_string(),\n+        grpc_services,\n+        rest_endpoint: Some(RestEndpoint::http(\"0.0.0.0\", rest_port)),\n+        version: Some(env!(\"CARGO_PKG_VERSION\").to_owned()),\n+    };\n+\n+    directory.register_instance(info).await\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.7 Design Decisions\n+\n+| Decision | Rationale |\n+|----------|-----------|\n+| **One REST endpoint per instance** | Unlike gRPC (multiple services per instance), REST modules expose a single base URL with path-based routing |\n+| **Module-name based resolution** | REST discovery uses `module_name` (e.g., \"calculator\"), not service name |\n+| **Reuse existing health tracking** | REST endpoints use the same `InstanceState` and heartbeat mechanism as gRPC |\n+| **Symmetric API** | `resolve_rest_service()` mirrors `resolve_grpc_service()` for consistency |\n+\n+##### 1.2.8 Migration Notes\n+\n+1. **`cf_system_sdks` must be updated first** — Add `RestEndpoint`, extend `RegisterInstanceInfo`, and add `resolve_rest_service()` to `DirectoryClient`\n+2. **`ModuleInstance` is extended** — Existing code continues to work; `rest_endpoint` defaults to `None`\n+3. **OoP modules must register REST endpoints** — Update bootstrap to include REST port in registration\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Phase 2: ClientDescriptor Trait\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/descriptor.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Client descriptor traits for typed OoP client metadata.\n+\n+use std::time::Duration;\n+\n+/// Availability policy for OoP clients.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum ClientAvailabilityPolicy {\n+    /// Client is optional; operations fail gracefully with SDK error (maps to HTTP 424).\n+    #[default]\n+    Optional,\n+    /// Client is required; module readiness may depend on availability.\n+    Required,\n+}\n+\n+/// Configuration for client behavior.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct ClientConfig {\n+    /// Transport protocol (REST default, gRPC opt-in).\n+    pub transport: Transport,\n+    /// Connection timeout for initial connect.\n+    pub connect_timeout: Duration,\n+    /// Request timeout for individual calls.\n+    pub request_timeout: Duration,\n+    /// Maximum backoff duration between reconnect attempts.\n+    pub max_backoff: Duration,\n+    /// Availability policy.\n+    pub availability_policy: ClientAvailabilityPolicy,\n+}\n+\n+impl Default for ClientConfig {\n+    fn default() -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            transport: Transport::Rest,\n+            connect_timeout: Duration::from_secs(5),\n+            request_timeout: Duration::from_secs(30),\n+            max_backoff: Duration::from_secs(60),\n+            availability_policy: ClientAvailabilityPolicy::Optional,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl ClientConfig {\n+    /// Create a REST client config (default).\n+    pub fn rest() -> Self {\n+        Self::default()\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Create a gRPC client config (opt-in).\n+    #[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+    pub fn grpc() -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            transport: Transport::Grpc,\n+            ..Self::default()\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Descriptor for an OoP client, defined in SDK crates.\n+///\n+/// This trait binds compile-time type information to runtime metadata\n+/// needed for lazy client resolution and registration.\n+pub trait ClientDescriptor: Send + Sync + 'static {\n+    /// The SDK API trait type (e.g., `dyn CalculatorClientV1`).\n+    type Api: ?Sized + Send + Sync + 'static;\n+\n+    /// Module name for dependency graph and Directory resolution.\n+    const MODULE_NAME: &'static str;\n+\n+    /// Client configuration (transport, timeouts, backoff, availability).\n+    fn config() -> ClientConfig {\n+        ClientConfig::default()\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Phase 3: ClientProvider Infrastructure\n+\n+#### 3.1 RestClientProvider (Default)\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/rest_provider.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Universal lazy REST client provider (default transport).\n+\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+use std::time::{Duration, Instant};\n+\n+use parking_lot::RwLock;\n+use tokio::sync::Semaphore;\n+\n+use crate::client_hub::ClientHub;\n+use crate::directory::DirectoryClient;\n+use crate::clients::descriptor::ClientConfig;\n+use modkit_http::HttpClient;\n+\n+/// Error type for REST provider operations.\n+#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\n+pub enum RestProviderError {\n+    #[error(\"service not found in directory: {module_name}\")]\n+    ServiceNotFound { module_name: &'static str },\n+\n+    #[error(\"HTTP request failed: {0}\")]\n+    HttpError(#[source] modkit_http::HttpError),\n+\n+    #[error(\"directory resolution failed: {0}\")]\n+    DirectoryError(#[source] anyhow::Error),\n+\n+    #[error(\"service temporarily unavailable (backoff active)\")]\n+    Backoff { retry_after: Duration },\n+}\n+\n+struct CachedEndpoint {\n+    base_url: String,\n+    resolved_at: Instant,\n+}\n+\n+struct ProviderState {\n+    cached: Option<CachedEndpoint>,\n+    last_failure: Option<Instant>,\n+    failure_count: u32,\n+}\n+\n+/// Universal lazy REST client provider.\n+///\n+/// Handles:\n+/// - Lazy endpoint resolution via DirectoryClient\n+/// - Base URL caching with automatic eviction on errors\n+/// - Exponential backoff for reconnection attempts\n+/// - Rate limiting to prevent thundering herds\n+pub struct RestClientProvider {\n+    module_name: &'static str,\n+    config: ClientConfig,\n+    hub: Arc<ClientHub>,\n+    http_client: HttpClient,\n+    state: RwLock<ProviderState>,\n+    resolve_semaphore: Semaphore,\n+}\n+\n+impl RestClientProvider {\n+    pub fn new(\n+        module_name: &'static str,\n+        config: ClientConfig,\n+        hub: Arc<ClientHub>,\n+    ) -> Self {\n+        let http_client = HttpClient::builder()\n+            .timeout(config.request_timeout)\n+            .connect_timeout(config.connect_timeout)\n+            .build();\n+\n+        Self {\n+            module_name,\n+            config,\n+            hub,\n+            http_client,\n+            state: RwLock::new(ProviderState {\n+                cached: None,\n+                last_failure: None,\n+                failure_count: 0,\n+            }),\n+            resolve_semaphore: Semaphore::new(1),\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Get the base URL for the service, resolving lazily.\n+    pub async fn get_base_url(&self) -> Result<String, RestProviderError> {\n+        // Fast path: return cached endpoint\n+        {\n+            let state = self.state.read();\n+            if let Some(ref cached) = state.cached {\n+                return Ok(cached.base_url.clone());\n+            }\n+\n+            // Check backoff\n+            if let Some(last_failure) = state.last_failure {\n+                let backoff = self.calculate_backoff(state.failure_count);\n+                let elapsed = last_failure.elapsed();\n+                if elapsed < backoff {\n+                    return Err(RestProviderError::Backoff {\n+                        retry_after: backoff - elapsed,\n+                    });\n+                }\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        // Slow path: acquire semaphore and resolve\n+        let _permit = self.resolve_semaphore.acquire().await\n+            .expect(\"semaphore is never closed\");\n+\n+        // Double-check after acquiring semaphore\n+        {\n+            let state = self.state.read();\n+            if let Some(ref cached) = state.cached {\n+                return Ok(cached.base_url.clone());\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        self.resolve_internal().await\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Get the HTTP client for making requests.\n+    pub fn http_client(&self) -> &HttpClient {\n+        &self.http_client\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Evict the cached endpoint (call on transport errors).\n+    pub fn evict(&self) {\n+        let mut state = self.state.write();\n+        state.cached = None;\n+        state.last_failure = Some(Instant::now());\n+        state.failure_count = state.failure_count.saturating_add(1);\n+        tracing::warn!(\n+            module = self.module_name,\n+            failure_count = state.failure_count,\n+            \"Evicted cached REST endpoint\"\n+        );\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Reset failure state (call on successful request).\n+    pub fn reset_failures(&self) {\n+        let mut state = self.state.write();\n+        if state.failure_count > 0 {\n+            state.failure_count = 0;\n+            state.last_failure = None;\n+            tracing::debug!(module = self.module_name, \"Reset failure state after success\");\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    async fn resolve_internal(&self) -> Result<String, RestProviderError> {\n+        let directory = self\n+            .hub\n+            .get::<dyn DirectoryClient>()\n+            .map_err(|e| RestProviderError::DirectoryError(e.into()))?;\n+\n+        let endpoint = directory\n+            .resolve_rest_service(self.module_name)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(RestProviderError::DirectoryError)?;\n+\n+        tracing::debug!(\n+            module = self.module_name,\n+            base_url = %endpoint.base_url,\n+            \"Resolved REST endpoint\"\n+        );\n+\n+        {\n+            let mut state = self.state.write();\n+            state.cached = Some(CachedEndpoint {\n+                base_url: endpoint.base_url.clone(),\n+                resolved_at: Instant::now(),\n+            });\n+            state.failure_count = 0;\n+            state.last_failure = None;\n+        }\n+\n+        Ok(endpoint.base_url)\n+    }\n+\n+    fn calculate_backoff(&self, failure_count: u32) -> Duration {\n+        let base = Duration::from_millis(100);\n+        let max = self.config.max_backoff;\n+        let backoff = base.saturating_mul(2u32.saturating_pow(failure_count.min(10)));\n+        backoff.min(max)\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### 3.2 GrpcClientProvider (Optional)\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/grpc_provider.rs`\n+\n+> Feature-gated behind `feature = \"grpc\"` for streaming/high-throughput use cases.\n+\n+```rust\n+#[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+//! Lazy gRPC client provider (optional transport).\n+\n+// Implementation follows same pattern as RestClientProvider\n+// but manages tonic::transport::Channel instead of base URL\n+```\n+\n+#### 3.3 LazyClientError\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/error.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Error returned by lazy clients when the OoP dependency is unavailable.\n+#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\n+pub enum LazyClientError {\n+    #[error(\"service unavailable: {module_name}\")]\n+    Unavailable {\n+        module_name: &'static str,\n+        #[source]\n+        source: Box<dyn std::error::Error + Send + Sync>,\n+    },\n+\n+    #[error(\"request failed: {0}\")]\n+    RequestFailed(String),\n+\n+    #[error(\"response parsing failed: {0}\")]\n+    ParseError(#[source] serde_json::Error),\n+}\n+\n+impl LazyClientError {\n+    /// Returns true if this error indicates the service is temporarily unavailable.\n+    /// REST handlers should map this to HTTP 424 Failed Dependency.\n+    pub fn is_dependency_unavailable(&self) -> bool {\n+        matches!(self, LazyClientError::Unavailable { .. })\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Phase 4: SDK Crate Updates (calculator-sdk example)\n+\n+#### 4.1 Descriptor\n+\n+**Location**: `calculator-sdk/src/descriptor.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit::clients::descriptor::{ClientDescriptor, ClientConfig};\n+use crate::api::CalculatorClientV1;\n+\n+/// Descriptor for the Calculator client (REST by default).\n+pub struct CalculatorClientDescriptor;\n+\n+impl ClientDescriptor for CalculatorClientDescriptor {\n+    type Api = dyn CalculatorClientV1;\n+    const MODULE_NAME: &'static str = \"calculator\";\n+\n+    fn config() -> ClientConfig {\n+        ClientConfig::rest()  // Default: REST transport\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+// Optional: gRPC descriptor for high-throughput use cases\n+#[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+pub struct CalculatorGrpcClientDescriptor;\n+\n+#[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+impl ClientDescriptor for CalculatorGrpcClientDescriptor {\n+    type Api = dyn CalculatorClientV1;\n+    const MODULE_NAME: &'static str = \"calculator\";\n+\n+    fn config() -> ClientConfig {\n+        ClientConfig::grpc()  // Opt-in: gRPC transport\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### 4.2 Lazy Client Implementation\n+\n+**Location**: `calculator-sdk/src/lazy_client.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use modkit::clients::rest_provider::RestClientProvider;\n+use modkit_security::SecurityContext;\n+\n+use crate::api::{CalculatorClientV1, CalculatorError};\n+\n+/// Lazy client for Calculator service (REST transport).\n+pub struct LazyCalculatorClient {\n+    provider: Arc<RestClientProvider>,\n+}\n+\n+impl LazyCalculatorClient {\n+    pub fn new(provider: Arc<RestClientProvider>) -> Self {\n+        Self { provider }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl CalculatorClientV1 for LazyCalculatorClient {\n+    async fn add(&self, ctx: &SecurityContext, a: i64, b: i64) -> Result<i64, CalculatorError> {\n+        let base_url = self.provider.get_base_url().await.map_err(|e| {\n+            tracing::warn!(error = %e, \"Calculator service unavailable\");\n+            CalculatorError::Unavailable {\n+                message: format!(\"Calculator service unavailable: {}\", e),\n+            }\n+        })?;\n+\n+        let url = format!(\"{}/api/v1/calculator/add\", base_url);\n+        let response = self.provider.http_client()\n+            .post(&url)\n+            .header(\"x-tenant-id\", ctx.tenant_id().map(|t| t.to_string()).unwrap_or_default())\n+            .json(&serde_json::json!({ \"a\": a, \"b\": b }))\n+            .send()\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(|e| {\n+                if e.is_connect() || e.is_timeout() {\n+                    self.provider.evict();\n+                }\n+                CalculatorError::Unavailable {\n+                    message: format!(\"HTTP request failed: {}\", e),\n+                }\n+            })?;\n+\n+        if !response.status().is_success() {\n+            return Err(map_http_error(response.status(), &response.text().await.unwrap_or_default()));\n+        }\n+\n+        let result: AddResponse = response.json().await.map_err(|e| {\n+            CalculatorError::Internal { message: format!(\"Failed to parse response: {}\", e) }\n+        })?;\n+\n+        self.provider.reset_failures();\n+        Ok(result.result)\n+    }\n+\n+    // ... other methods follow the same pattern ...\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(serde::Deserialize)]","path":"docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md","commit_id":"edd86e3e6cf91af1a08e3970d60dc26bc6acb6e6","original_commit_id":"030bc79ea9322b429e351c332cbffd4f44791b3c","user":{"login":"alexpitsikoulis","id":50185728,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMTg1NzI4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50185728?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis","html_url":"https://github.com/alexpitsikoulis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"removed","created_at":"2026-02-19T20:42:10Z","updated_at":"2026-02-19T20:42:10Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2830061281","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2830061281"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2830061281"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2830061281/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":1520,"original_line":757,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2828771682,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":757,"position":1520,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2830061874","pull_request_review_id":3828410327,"id":2830061874,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6or1Ey","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1050 @@\n+# ADR-0003: Universal Lazy Typed REST Clients for OoP Modules\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+This proposal outlines a migration from gRPC to REST as the default transport for out-of-process (OoP) modules and introduces a **universal lazy typed client layer** for OoP module communication in ModKit. The implementation is structured in phases:\n+\n+1. **Phase 1 - REST as default transport**: Establish REST as the default OoP transport; gRPC becomes opt-in\n+2. **Phase 2 - ClientDescriptor trait**: SDK-defined metadata binding compile-time types to runtime resolution\n+3. **Phase 3 - ClientProvider**: Lazy resolution, caching, backoff, and reconnection infrastructure\n+4. **Phase 4 - Macro extension**: `clients = [...]` auto-registers lazy clients into `ClientHub`\n+5. **Phase 5 - Soft OoP deps**: Dependencies on OoP modules don't block startup\n+6. **Phase 6 - Registry extension**: Soft OoP dep resolution:  \n+\n+**Current pattern** (problematic):\n+```rust\n+// Consumer must wire client manually in init() - FAILS if OoP module is not ready\n+calculator_sdk::wire_client(hub, &*directory).await?;\n+```\n+\n+**Proposed pattern**:\n+```rust\n+#[modkit::module(\n+    name = \"calculator_gateway\",\n+    clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],  // REST by default\n+)]\n+// No wire_client() needed - lazy client auto-registered\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Problem Statement\n+\n+The current OoP client wiring pattern has several issues:\n+\n+1. **Eager wiring is fragile**: Consumer modules call `wire_client()` in `init()`, which fails if the OoP dependency is not yet available.\n+2. **Startup coupling**: The entire module fails to start if any OoP dependency is temporarily unavailable.\n+3. **Boilerplate duplication**: Each SDK repeats the same resolve/connect/cache logic.\n+4. **No graceful degradation**: Missing dependencies cause module-level failures instead of per-operation failures (HTTP 424).\n+5. **gRPC complexity**: Binary protobuf payloads are hard to debug; requires specialized tooling.\n+\n+### Current Pattern (calculator_gateway example)\n+\n+```rust\n+// Current: Consumer must wire client manually, and it happens eagerly\n+pub async fn wire_client(hub: &ClientHub, resolver: &dyn DirectoryClient) -> Result<()> {\n+    let endpoint = resolver.resolve_grpc_service(SERVICE_NAME).await?;  // Fails if OoP not ready\n+    let client = CalculatorGrpcClient::connect(&endpoint.uri).await?;   // Fails if network issue\n+    hub.register::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>(Arc::new(client));\n+    Ok(())\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Proposed Solution\n+\n+### Architecture Overview\n+\n+```text\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           SDK Crate (calculator-sdk)                    │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  CalculatorClientDescriptor                                             │\n+│    - MODULE_NAME: \"calculator\"                                          │\n+│    - Api: dyn CalculatorClientV1                                        │\n+│    - Transport: Rest (default) | Grpc (opt-in)                          │\n+│    - Availability Policy: Optional (default)                            │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  LazyCalculatorClient                                                   │\n+│    - Implements CalculatorClientV1                                      │\n+│    - Delegates to ClientProvider for lazy connection                    │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           ModKit (libs/modkit)                          │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  ClientProvider (transport-agnostic interface)                          │\n+│    - Lazy resolution via DirectoryClient                                │\n+│    - Endpoint/connection caching with eviction on error                 │\n+│    - Backoff/rate-limiting for reconnects                               │\n+│    - Transport middleware (timeouts, retries, tracing)                  │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  RestClientProvider (default) | GrpcClientProvider (feature = \"grpc\")   │\n+│    - Transport-specific implementations                                 │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  #[modkit::module] macro extension                                      │\n+│    - clients = [CalculatorClientDescriptor]                             │\n+│    - Auto-registers LazyClient into ClientHub                           │\n+│    - Auto-injects MODULE_NAME from each descriptor into deps            │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                      Consumer Module (calculator_gateway)               │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  #[modkit::module(                                                      │\n+│      name = \"calculator_gateway\",                                       │\n+│      capabilities = [rest],                                             │\n+│      clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],            │\n+│      // deps auto-injected: [\"calculator\"] from descriptor              │\n+│  )]                                                                     │\n+│                                                                         │\n+│  // No wire_client() call needed!                                       │\n+│  // Client is always available from ClientHub                           │\n+│  let calc = hub.get::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>()?;                       │\n+│  calc.add(ctx, a, b).await?;  // Lazy connect on first call             │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Detailed Implementation\n+\n+### Phase 1: REST as Default Transport\n+\n+**Rationale**: REST is simpler to debug, requires no code generation, and is sufficient for most OoP calls. gRPC remains available for streaming or high-throughput use cases.\n+\n+| Factor          | REST                            | gRPC                         |\n+|-----------------|---------------------------------|------------------------------|\n+| Debuggability   | ✅ curl, browser, any HTTP tool | ❌ Requires specialized tools |\n+| Simplicity      | ✅ JSON, standard HTTP          | ❌ Protobuf, code generation  |\n+| Browser support | ✅ Native                       | ❌ Requires gRPC-Web proxy    |\n+| API reuse       | ✅ Same as public REST API      | ❌ Separate interface         |\n+| Streaming       | ❌ Requires SSE/WebSocket       | ✅ Native support             |\n+| Performance     | ⚠️ JSON overhead                | ✅ Binary, efficient          |\n+\n+#### 1.1 Transport Enum\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/transport.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Transport protocol for OoP communication.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum Transport {\n+    /// REST with JSON serialization (default).\n+    #[default]\n+    Rest,\n+    /// gRPC with protobuf serialization (opt-in, requires feature = \"grpc\").\n+    #[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+    Grpc,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### 1.2 REST Service Discovery Infrastructure\n+\n+REST service discovery requires extending the existing `ModuleInstance`, `ModuleManager`, and `DirectoryClient` to track and resolve REST endpoints.\n+\n+##### 1.2.1 Extend `ModuleInstance` to track REST endpoints\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/runtime/module_manager.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Represents a single instance of a module\n+#[derive(Debug)]\n+pub struct ModuleInstance {\n+    pub module: String,\n+    pub instance_id: Uuid,\n+    pub control: Option<Endpoint>,\n+    pub grpc_services: HashMap<String, Endpoint>,\n+    pub rest_endpoint: Option<Endpoint>,  // NEW: REST base URL for this instance\n+    pub version: Option<String>,\n+    inner: Arc<parking_lot::RwLock<InstanceRuntimeState>>,\n+}\n+\n+impl ModuleInstance {\n+    // ... existing methods ...\n+\n+    /// Set the REST endpoint for this instance\n+    pub fn with_rest_endpoint(mut self, ep: Endpoint) -> Self {\n+        self.rest_endpoint = Some(ep);\n+        self\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.2 Extend `ModuleManager` with REST discovery\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/runtime/module_manager.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+impl ModuleManager {\n+    /// Pick a REST endpoint for a module using round-robin selection.\n+    /// Returns (module_name, instance, endpoint) if found.\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn pick_rest_endpoint_round_robin(\n+        &self,\n+        module_name: &str,\n+    ) -> Option<(String, Arc<ModuleInstance>, Endpoint)> {\n+        let instances_entry = self.inner.get(module_name)?;\n+        let instances = instances_entry.value();\n+\n+        // Filter to instances with REST endpoints and healthy/ready state\n+        let candidates: Vec<_> = instances\n+            .iter()\n+            .filter(|inst| {\n+                inst.rest_endpoint.is_some()\n+                    && matches!(inst.state(), InstanceState::Healthy | InstanceState::Ready)\n+            })\n+            .cloned()\n+            .collect();\n+\n+        if candidates.is_empty() {\n+            return None;\n+        }\n+\n+        let len = candidates.len();\n+        let rr_key = format!(\"rest:{}\", module_name);\n+        let mut counter = self.rr_counters.entry(rr_key).or_insert(0);\n+        let idx = *counter % len;\n+        *counter = (*counter + 1) % len;\n+\n+        candidates.get(idx).map(|inst| {\n+            (\n+                module_name.to_owned(),\n+                inst.clone(),\n+                inst.rest_endpoint.clone().expect(\"filtered above\"),\n+            )\n+        })\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.3 Extend `DirectoryClient` trait\n+\n+**Location**: `cf_system_sdks/src/directory.rs` (upstream crate — requires update)\n+\n+```rust\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait DirectoryClient: Send + Sync {\n+    /// Resolve REST endpoint for a module (default for OoP).\n+    async fn resolve_rest_service(&self, module_name: &str) -> Result<RestEndpoint>;\n+\n+    /// Resolve gRPC endpoint for a module (opt-in).\n+    async fn resolve_grpc_service(&self, service_name: &str) -> Result<ServiceEndpoint>;\n+\n+    // ... existing methods (list_instances, register_instance, etc.) ...\n+}\n+\n+/// REST endpoint for a module\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct RestEndpoint {\n+    /// Base URL for the module's REST API (e.g., \"http://calculator:8080\")\n+    pub base_url: String,\n+}\n+\n+impl RestEndpoint {\n+    pub fn new(base_url: impl Into<String>) -> Self {\n+        Self { base_url: base_url.into() }\n+    }\n+\n+    pub fn http(host: &str, port: u16) -> Self {\n+        Self { base_url: format!(\"http://{}:{}\", host, port) }\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.4 Implement `resolve_rest_service` in `LocalDirectoryClient`\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/directory.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl DirectoryClient for LocalDirectoryClient {\n+    async fn resolve_rest_service(&self, module_name: &str) -> Result<RestEndpoint> {\n+        if let Some((_, _, ep)) = self.mgr.pick_rest_endpoint_round_robin(module_name) {\n+            return Ok(RestEndpoint::new(ep.uri));\n+        }\n+\n+        anyhow::bail!(\"REST service not found or no healthy instances: {module_name}\")\n+    }\n+\n+    // ... existing methods unchanged ...\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.5 Extend `RegisterInstanceInfo` for REST registration\n+\n+**Location**: `cf_system_sdks/src/directory.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Information needed to register a module instance\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct RegisterInstanceInfo {\n+    pub module: String,\n+    pub instance_id: String,\n+    pub grpc_services: Vec<(String, ServiceEndpoint)>,\n+    pub rest_endpoint: Option<RestEndpoint>,  // NEW\n+    pub version: Option<String>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.6 OoP Module REST Registration\n+\n+When an OoP module starts, it registers its REST endpoint with the DirectoryService:\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/oop.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+async fn register_with_directory(\n+    directory: &dyn DirectoryClient,\n+    module_name: &str,\n+    instance_id: Uuid,\n+    rest_port: u16,\n+    grpc_services: Vec<(String, ServiceEndpoint)>,\n+) -> Result<()> {\n+    let info = RegisterInstanceInfo {\n+        module: module_name.to_owned(),\n+        instance_id: instance_id.to_string(),\n+        grpc_services,\n+        rest_endpoint: Some(RestEndpoint::http(\"0.0.0.0\", rest_port)),\n+        version: Some(env!(\"CARGO_PKG_VERSION\").to_owned()),\n+    };\n+\n+    directory.register_instance(info).await\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.7 Design Decisions\n+\n+| Decision | Rationale |\n+|----------|-----------|\n+| **One REST endpoint per instance** | Unlike gRPC (multiple services per instance), REST modules expose a single base URL with path-based routing |\n+| **Module-name based resolution** | REST discovery uses `module_name` (e.g., \"calculator\"), not service name |\n+| **Reuse existing health tracking** | REST endpoints use the same `InstanceState` and heartbeat mechanism as gRPC |\n+| **Symmetric API** | `resolve_rest_service()` mirrors `resolve_grpc_service()` for consistency |\n+\n+##### 1.2.8 Migration Notes\n+\n+1. **`cf_system_sdks` must be updated first** — Add `RestEndpoint`, extend `RegisterInstanceInfo`, and add `resolve_rest_service()` to `DirectoryClient`\n+2. **`ModuleInstance` is extended** — Existing code continues to work; `rest_endpoint` defaults to `None`\n+3. **OoP modules must register REST endpoints** — Update bootstrap to include REST port in registration\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Phase 2: ClientDescriptor Trait\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/descriptor.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Client descriptor traits for typed OoP client metadata.\n+\n+use std::time::Duration;\n+\n+/// Availability policy for OoP clients.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum ClientAvailabilityPolicy {\n+    /// Client is optional; operations fail gracefully with SDK error (maps to HTTP 424).\n+    #[default]\n+    Optional,\n+    /// Client is required; module readiness may depend on availability.\n+    Required,\n+}\n+\n+/// Configuration for client behavior.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct ClientConfig {\n+    /// Transport protocol (REST default, gRPC opt-in).\n+    pub transport: Transport,\n+    /// Connection timeout for initial connect.\n+    pub connect_timeout: Duration,\n+    /// Request timeout for individual calls.\n+    pub request_timeout: Duration,\n+    /// Maximum backoff duration between reconnect attempts.\n+    pub max_backoff: Duration,\n+    /// Availability policy.\n+    pub availability_policy: ClientAvailabilityPolicy,\n+}\n+\n+impl Default for ClientConfig {\n+    fn default() -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            transport: Transport::Rest,\n+            connect_timeout: Duration::from_secs(5),\n+            request_timeout: Duration::from_secs(30),\n+            max_backoff: Duration::from_secs(60),\n+            availability_policy: ClientAvailabilityPolicy::Optional,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl ClientConfig {\n+    /// Create a REST client config (default).\n+    pub fn rest() -> Self {\n+        Self::default()\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Create a gRPC client config (opt-in).\n+    #[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+    pub fn grpc() -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            transport: Transport::Grpc,\n+            ..Self::default()\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Descriptor for an OoP client, defined in SDK crates.\n+///\n+/// This trait binds compile-time type information to runtime metadata\n+/// needed for lazy client resolution and registration.\n+pub trait ClientDescriptor: Send + Sync + 'static {\n+    /// The SDK API trait type (e.g., `dyn CalculatorClientV1`).\n+    type Api: ?Sized + Send + Sync + 'static;\n+\n+    /// Module name for dependency graph and Directory resolution.\n+    const MODULE_NAME: &'static str;\n+\n+    /// Client configuration (transport, timeouts, backoff, availability).\n+    fn config() -> ClientConfig {\n+        ClientConfig::default()\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Phase 3: ClientProvider Infrastructure\n+\n+#### 3.1 RestClientProvider (Default)\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/rest_provider.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Universal lazy REST client provider (default transport).\n+\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+use std::time::{Duration, Instant};\n+\n+use parking_lot::RwLock;\n+use tokio::sync::Semaphore;\n+\n+use crate::client_hub::ClientHub;\n+use crate::directory::DirectoryClient;\n+use crate::clients::descriptor::ClientConfig;\n+use modkit_http::HttpClient;\n+\n+/// Error type for REST provider operations.\n+#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\n+pub enum RestProviderError {\n+    #[error(\"service not found in directory: {module_name}\")]\n+    ServiceNotFound { module_name: &'static str },\n+\n+    #[error(\"HTTP request failed: {0}\")]\n+    HttpError(#[source] modkit_http::HttpError),\n+\n+    #[error(\"directory resolution failed: {0}\")]\n+    DirectoryError(#[source] anyhow::Error),\n+\n+    #[error(\"service temporarily unavailable (backoff active)\")]\n+    Backoff { retry_after: Duration },\n+}\n+\n+struct CachedEndpoint {\n+    base_url: String,\n+    resolved_at: Instant,\n+}\n+\n+struct ProviderState {\n+    cached: Option<CachedEndpoint>,\n+    last_failure: Option<Instant>,\n+    failure_count: u32,\n+}\n+\n+/// Universal lazy REST client provider.\n+///\n+/// Handles:\n+/// - Lazy endpoint resolution via DirectoryClient\n+/// - Base URL caching with automatic eviction on errors\n+/// - Exponential backoff for reconnection attempts\n+/// - Rate limiting to prevent thundering herds\n+pub struct RestClientProvider {\n+    module_name: &'static str,\n+    config: ClientConfig,\n+    hub: Arc<ClientHub>,\n+    http_client: HttpClient,\n+    state: RwLock<ProviderState>,\n+    resolve_semaphore: Semaphore,\n+}\n+\n+impl RestClientProvider {\n+    pub fn new(\n+        module_name: &'static str,\n+        config: ClientConfig,\n+        hub: Arc<ClientHub>,\n+    ) -> Self {\n+        let http_client = HttpClient::builder()\n+            .timeout(config.request_timeout)\n+            .connect_timeout(config.connect_timeout)\n+            .build();\n+\n+        Self {\n+            module_name,\n+            config,\n+            hub,\n+            http_client,\n+            state: RwLock::new(ProviderState {\n+                cached: None,\n+                last_failure: None,\n+                failure_count: 0,\n+            }),\n+            resolve_semaphore: Semaphore::new(1),\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Get the base URL for the service, resolving lazily.\n+    pub async fn get_base_url(&self) -> Result<String, RestProviderError> {\n+        // Fast path: return cached endpoint\n+        {\n+            let state = self.state.read();\n+            if let Some(ref cached) = state.cached {\n+                return Ok(cached.base_url.clone());\n+            }\n+\n+            // Check backoff\n+            if let Some(last_failure) = state.last_failure {\n+                let backoff = self.calculate_backoff(state.failure_count);\n+                let elapsed = last_failure.elapsed();\n+                if elapsed < backoff {\n+                    return Err(RestProviderError::Backoff {\n+                        retry_after: backoff - elapsed,\n+                    });\n+                }\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        // Slow path: acquire semaphore and resolve\n+        let _permit = self.resolve_semaphore.acquire().await\n+            .expect(\"semaphore is never closed\");\n+\n+        // Double-check after acquiring semaphore\n+        {\n+            let state = self.state.read();\n+            if let Some(ref cached) = state.cached {\n+                return Ok(cached.base_url.clone());\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        self.resolve_internal().await\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Get the HTTP client for making requests.\n+    pub fn http_client(&self) -> &HttpClient {\n+        &self.http_client\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Evict the cached endpoint (call on transport errors).\n+    pub fn evict(&self) {\n+        let mut state = self.state.write();\n+        state.cached = None;\n+        state.last_failure = Some(Instant::now());\n+        state.failure_count = state.failure_count.saturating_add(1);\n+        tracing::warn!(\n+            module = self.module_name,\n+            failure_count = state.failure_count,\n+            \"Evicted cached REST endpoint\"\n+        );\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Reset failure state (call on successful request).\n+    pub fn reset_failures(&self) {\n+        let mut state = self.state.write();\n+        if state.failure_count > 0 {\n+            state.failure_count = 0;\n+            state.last_failure = None;\n+            tracing::debug!(module = self.module_name, \"Reset failure state after success\");\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    async fn resolve_internal(&self) -> Result<String, RestProviderError> {\n+        let directory = self\n+            .hub\n+            .get::<dyn DirectoryClient>()\n+            .map_err(|e| RestProviderError::DirectoryError(e.into()))?;\n+\n+        let endpoint = directory\n+            .resolve_rest_service(self.module_name)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(RestProviderError::DirectoryError)?;\n+\n+        tracing::debug!(\n+            module = self.module_name,\n+            base_url = %endpoint.base_url,\n+            \"Resolved REST endpoint\"\n+        );\n+\n+        {\n+            let mut state = self.state.write();\n+            state.cached = Some(CachedEndpoint {\n+                base_url: endpoint.base_url.clone(),\n+                resolved_at: Instant::now(),\n+            });\n+            state.failure_count = 0;\n+            state.last_failure = None;\n+        }\n+\n+        Ok(endpoint.base_url)\n+    }\n+\n+    fn calculate_backoff(&self, failure_count: u32) -> Duration {\n+        let base = Duration::from_millis(100);\n+        let max = self.config.max_backoff;\n+        let backoff = base.saturating_mul(2u32.saturating_pow(failure_count.min(10)));\n+        backoff.min(max)\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### 3.2 GrpcClientProvider (Optional)\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/grpc_provider.rs`\n+\n+> Feature-gated behind `feature = \"grpc\"` for streaming/high-throughput use cases.\n+\n+```rust\n+#[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+//! Lazy gRPC client provider (optional transport).\n+\n+// Implementation follows same pattern as RestClientProvider\n+// but manages tonic::transport::Channel instead of base URL\n+```\n+\n+#### 3.3 LazyClientError\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/error.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Error returned by lazy clients when the OoP dependency is unavailable.\n+#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\n+pub enum LazyClientError {\n+    #[error(\"service unavailable: {module_name}\")]\n+    Unavailable {\n+        module_name: &'static str,\n+        #[source]\n+        source: Box<dyn std::error::Error + Send + Sync>,\n+    },\n+\n+    #[error(\"request failed: {0}\")]\n+    RequestFailed(String),\n+\n+    #[error(\"response parsing failed: {0}\")]\n+    ParseError(#[source] serde_json::Error),\n+}\n+\n+impl LazyClientError {\n+    /// Returns true if this error indicates the service is temporarily unavailable.\n+    /// REST handlers should map this to HTTP 424 Failed Dependency.\n+    pub fn is_dependency_unavailable(&self) -> bool {\n+        matches!(self, LazyClientError::Unavailable { .. })\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Phase 4: SDK Crate Updates (calculator-sdk example)\n+\n+#### 4.1 Descriptor\n+\n+**Location**: `calculator-sdk/src/descriptor.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit::clients::descriptor::{ClientDescriptor, ClientConfig};\n+use crate::api::CalculatorClientV1;\n+\n+/// Descriptor for the Calculator client (REST by default).\n+pub struct CalculatorClientDescriptor;\n+\n+impl ClientDescriptor for CalculatorClientDescriptor {\n+    type Api = dyn CalculatorClientV1;\n+    const MODULE_NAME: &'static str = \"calculator\";\n+\n+    fn config() -> ClientConfig {\n+        ClientConfig::rest()  // Default: REST transport\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+// Optional: gRPC descriptor for high-throughput use cases\n+#[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+pub struct CalculatorGrpcClientDescriptor;\n+\n+#[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+impl ClientDescriptor for CalculatorGrpcClientDescriptor {\n+    type Api = dyn CalculatorClientV1;\n+    const MODULE_NAME: &'static str = \"calculator\";\n+\n+    fn config() -> ClientConfig {\n+        ClientConfig::grpc()  // Opt-in: gRPC transport\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### 4.2 Lazy Client Implementation\n+\n+**Location**: `calculator-sdk/src/lazy_client.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use modkit::clients::rest_provider::RestClientProvider;\n+use modkit_security::SecurityContext;\n+\n+use crate::api::{CalculatorClientV1, CalculatorError};\n+\n+/// Lazy client for Calculator service (REST transport).\n+pub struct LazyCalculatorClient {\n+    provider: Arc<RestClientProvider>,\n+}\n+\n+impl LazyCalculatorClient {\n+    pub fn new(provider: Arc<RestClientProvider>) -> Self {\n+        Self { provider }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl CalculatorClientV1 for LazyCalculatorClient {\n+    async fn add(&self, ctx: &SecurityContext, a: i64, b: i64) -> Result<i64, CalculatorError> {\n+        let base_url = self.provider.get_base_url().await.map_err(|e| {\n+            tracing::warn!(error = %e, \"Calculator service unavailable\");\n+            CalculatorError::Unavailable {\n+                message: format!(\"Calculator service unavailable: {}\", e),\n+            }\n+        })?;\n+\n+        let url = format!(\"{}/api/v1/calculator/add\", base_url);\n+        let response = self.provider.http_client()\n+            .post(&url)\n+            .header(\"x-tenant-id\", ctx.tenant_id().map(|t| t.to_string()).unwrap_or_default())","path":"docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md","commit_id":"030bc79ea9322b429e351c332cbffd4f44791b3c","original_commit_id":"030bc79ea9322b429e351c332cbffd4f44791b3c","user":{"login":"alexpitsikoulis","id":50185728,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMTg1NzI4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50185728?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis","html_url":"https://github.com/alexpitsikoulis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"removed","created_at":"2026-02-19T20:42:18Z","updated_at":"2026-02-19T20:42:18Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2830061874","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2830061874"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2830061874"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2830061874/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":729,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2828793871,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":729,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2830064804","pull_request_review_id":3828413366,"id":2830064804,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6or1yk","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1050 @@\n+# ADR-0003: Universal Lazy Typed REST Clients for OoP Modules\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+This proposal outlines a migration from gRPC to REST as the default transport for out-of-process (OoP) modules and introduces a **universal lazy typed client layer** for OoP module communication in ModKit. The implementation is structured in phases:\n+\n+1. **Phase 1 - REST as default transport**: Establish REST as the default OoP transport; gRPC becomes opt-in\n+2. **Phase 2 - ClientDescriptor trait**: SDK-defined metadata binding compile-time types to runtime resolution\n+3. **Phase 3 - ClientProvider**: Lazy resolution, caching, backoff, and reconnection infrastructure\n+4. **Phase 4 - Macro extension**: `clients = [...]` auto-registers lazy clients into `ClientHub`\n+5. **Phase 5 - Soft OoP deps**: Dependencies on OoP modules don't block startup\n+6. **Phase 6 - Registry extension**: Soft OoP dep resolution:  \n+\n+**Current pattern** (problematic):\n+```rust\n+// Consumer must wire client manually in init() - FAILS if OoP module is not ready\n+calculator_sdk::wire_client(hub, &*directory).await?;\n+```\n+\n+**Proposed pattern**:\n+```rust\n+#[modkit::module(\n+    name = \"calculator_gateway\",\n+    clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],  // REST by default\n+)]\n+// No wire_client() needed - lazy client auto-registered\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Problem Statement\n+\n+The current OoP client wiring pattern has several issues:\n+\n+1. **Eager wiring is fragile**: Consumer modules call `wire_client()` in `init()`, which fails if the OoP dependency is not yet available.\n+2. **Startup coupling**: The entire module fails to start if any OoP dependency is temporarily unavailable.\n+3. **Boilerplate duplication**: Each SDK repeats the same resolve/connect/cache logic.\n+4. **No graceful degradation**: Missing dependencies cause module-level failures instead of per-operation failures (HTTP 424).\n+5. **gRPC complexity**: Binary protobuf payloads are hard to debug; requires specialized tooling.\n+\n+### Current Pattern (calculator_gateway example)\n+\n+```rust\n+// Current: Consumer must wire client manually, and it happens eagerly\n+pub async fn wire_client(hub: &ClientHub, resolver: &dyn DirectoryClient) -> Result<()> {\n+    let endpoint = resolver.resolve_grpc_service(SERVICE_NAME).await?;  // Fails if OoP not ready\n+    let client = CalculatorGrpcClient::connect(&endpoint.uri).await?;   // Fails if network issue\n+    hub.register::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>(Arc::new(client));\n+    Ok(())\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Proposed Solution\n+\n+### Architecture Overview\n+\n+```text\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           SDK Crate (calculator-sdk)                    │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  CalculatorClientDescriptor                                             │\n+│    - MODULE_NAME: \"calculator\"                                          │\n+│    - Api: dyn CalculatorClientV1                                        │\n+│    - Transport: Rest (default) | Grpc (opt-in)                          │\n+│    - Availability Policy: Optional (default)                            │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  LazyCalculatorClient                                                   │\n+│    - Implements CalculatorClientV1                                      │\n+│    - Delegates to ClientProvider for lazy connection                    │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           ModKit (libs/modkit)                          │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  ClientProvider (transport-agnostic interface)                          │\n+│    - Lazy resolution via DirectoryClient                                │\n+│    - Endpoint/connection caching with eviction on error                 │\n+│    - Backoff/rate-limiting for reconnects                               │\n+│    - Transport middleware (timeouts, retries, tracing)                  │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  RestClientProvider (default) | GrpcClientProvider (feature = \"grpc\")   │","path":"docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md","commit_id":"edd86e3e6cf91af1a08e3970d60dc26bc6acb6e6","original_commit_id":"030bc79ea9322b429e351c332cbffd4f44791b3c","user":{"login":"alexpitsikoulis","id":50185728,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMTg1NzI4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50185728?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis","html_url":"https://github.com/alexpitsikoulis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Detailed [here](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/615/changes#diff-6266ed6376409008cc7a7f4e42200283adf62977f78ed120f405aa13c07eb257R1280-R1414)","created_at":"2026-02-19T20:42:55Z","updated_at":"2026-02-19T20:42:55Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2830064804","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2830064804"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2830064804"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2830064804/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":84,"original_line":84,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2828789279,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":84,"position":84,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2830082687","pull_request_review_id":3828432566,"id":2830082687,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6or6J_","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1050 @@\n+# ADR-0003: Universal Lazy Typed REST Clients for OoP Modules\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+This proposal outlines a migration from gRPC to REST as the default transport for out-of-process (OoP) modules and introduces a **universal lazy typed client layer** for OoP module communication in ModKit. The implementation is structured in phases:\n+\n+1. **Phase 1 - REST as default transport**: Establish REST as the default OoP transport; gRPC becomes opt-in\n+2. **Phase 2 - ClientDescriptor trait**: SDK-defined metadata binding compile-time types to runtime resolution\n+3. **Phase 3 - ClientProvider**: Lazy resolution, caching, backoff, and reconnection infrastructure\n+4. **Phase 4 - Macro extension**: `clients = [...]` auto-registers lazy clients into `ClientHub`\n+5. **Phase 5 - Soft OoP deps**: Dependencies on OoP modules don't block startup\n+6. **Phase 6 - Registry extension**: Soft OoP dep resolution:  \n+\n+**Current pattern** (problematic):\n+```rust\n+// Consumer must wire client manually in init() - FAILS if OoP module is not ready\n+calculator_sdk::wire_client(hub, &*directory).await?;\n+```\n+\n+**Proposed pattern**:\n+```rust\n+#[modkit::module(\n+    name = \"calculator_gateway\",\n+    clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],  // REST by default\n+)]\n+// No wire_client() needed - lazy client auto-registered\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Problem Statement\n+\n+The current OoP client wiring pattern has several issues:\n+\n+1. **Eager wiring is fragile**: Consumer modules call `wire_client()` in `init()`, which fails if the OoP dependency is not yet available.\n+2. **Startup coupling**: The entire module fails to start if any OoP dependency is temporarily unavailable.\n+3. **Boilerplate duplication**: Each SDK repeats the same resolve/connect/cache logic.\n+4. **No graceful degradation**: Missing dependencies cause module-level failures instead of per-operation failures (HTTP 424).\n+5. **gRPC complexity**: Binary protobuf payloads are hard to debug; requires specialized tooling.\n+\n+### Current Pattern (calculator_gateway example)\n+\n+```rust\n+// Current: Consumer must wire client manually, and it happens eagerly\n+pub async fn wire_client(hub: &ClientHub, resolver: &dyn DirectoryClient) -> Result<()> {\n+    let endpoint = resolver.resolve_grpc_service(SERVICE_NAME).await?;  // Fails if OoP not ready\n+    let client = CalculatorGrpcClient::connect(&endpoint.uri).await?;   // Fails if network issue\n+    hub.register::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>(Arc::new(client));\n+    Ok(())\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Proposed Solution\n+\n+### Architecture Overview\n+\n+```text\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           SDK Crate (calculator-sdk)                    │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  CalculatorClientDescriptor                                             │\n+│    - MODULE_NAME: \"calculator\"                                          │\n+│    - Api: dyn CalculatorClientV1                                        │\n+│    - Transport: Rest (default) | Grpc (opt-in)                          │\n+│    - Availability Policy: Optional (default)                            │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  LazyCalculatorClient                                                   │\n+│    - Implements CalculatorClientV1                                      │\n+│    - Delegates to ClientProvider for lazy connection                    │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           ModKit (libs/modkit)                          │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  ClientProvider (transport-agnostic interface)                          │\n+│    - Lazy resolution via DirectoryClient                                │\n+│    - Endpoint/connection caching with eviction on error                 │\n+│    - Backoff/rate-limiting for reconnects                               │\n+│    - Transport middleware (timeouts, retries, tracing)                  │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  RestClientProvider (default) | GrpcClientProvider (feature = \"grpc\")   │\n+│    - Transport-specific implementations                                 │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  #[modkit::module] macro extension                                      │\n+│    - clients = [CalculatorClientDescriptor]                             │\n+│    - Auto-registers LazyClient into ClientHub                           │\n+│    - Auto-injects MODULE_NAME from each descriptor into deps            │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                      Consumer Module (calculator_gateway)               │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  #[modkit::module(                                                      │\n+│      name = \"calculator_gateway\",                                       │\n+│      capabilities = [rest],                                             │\n+│      clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],            │\n+│      // deps auto-injected: [\"calculator\"] from descriptor              │\n+│  )]                                                                     │\n+│                                                                         │\n+│  // No wire_client() call needed!                                       │\n+│  // Client is always available from ClientHub                           │\n+│  let calc = hub.get::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>()?;                       │\n+│  calc.add(ctx, a, b).await?;  // Lazy connect on first call             │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Detailed Implementation\n+\n+### Phase 1: REST as Default Transport\n+\n+**Rationale**: REST is simpler to debug, requires no code generation, and is sufficient for most OoP calls. gRPC remains available for streaming or high-throughput use cases.\n+\n+| Factor          | REST                            | gRPC                         |\n+|-----------------|---------------------------------|------------------------------|\n+| Debuggability   | ✅ curl, browser, any HTTP tool | ❌ Requires specialized tools |\n+| Simplicity      | ✅ JSON, standard HTTP          | ❌ Protobuf, code generation  |\n+| Browser support | ✅ Native                       | ❌ Requires gRPC-Web proxy    |\n+| API reuse       | ✅ Same as public REST API      | ❌ Separate interface         |\n+| Streaming       | ❌ Requires SSE/WebSocket       | ✅ Native support             |\n+| Performance     | ⚠️ JSON overhead                | ✅ Binary, efficient          |\n+\n+#### 1.1 Transport Enum\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/transport.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Transport protocol for OoP communication.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum Transport {\n+    /// REST with JSON serialization (default).\n+    #[default]\n+    Rest,\n+    /// gRPC with protobuf serialization (opt-in, requires feature = \"grpc\").\n+    #[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+    Grpc,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### 1.2 REST Service Discovery Infrastructure\n+\n+REST service discovery requires extending the existing `ModuleInstance`, `ModuleManager`, and `DirectoryClient` to track and resolve REST endpoints.\n+\n+##### 1.2.1 Extend `ModuleInstance` to track REST endpoints\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/runtime/module_manager.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Represents a single instance of a module\n+#[derive(Debug)]\n+pub struct ModuleInstance {\n+    pub module: String,\n+    pub instance_id: Uuid,\n+    pub control: Option<Endpoint>,\n+    pub grpc_services: HashMap<String, Endpoint>,\n+    pub rest_endpoint: Option<Endpoint>,  // NEW: REST base URL for this instance\n+    pub version: Option<String>,\n+    inner: Arc<parking_lot::RwLock<InstanceRuntimeState>>,\n+}\n+\n+impl ModuleInstance {\n+    // ... existing methods ...\n+\n+    /// Set the REST endpoint for this instance\n+    pub fn with_rest_endpoint(mut self, ep: Endpoint) -> Self {\n+        self.rest_endpoint = Some(ep);\n+        self\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.2 Extend `ModuleManager` with REST discovery\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/runtime/module_manager.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+impl ModuleManager {\n+    /// Pick a REST endpoint for a module using round-robin selection.\n+    /// Returns (module_name, instance, endpoint) if found.\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn pick_rest_endpoint_round_robin(\n+        &self,\n+        module_name: &str,\n+    ) -> Option<(String, Arc<ModuleInstance>, Endpoint)> {\n+        let instances_entry = self.inner.get(module_name)?;\n+        let instances = instances_entry.value();\n+\n+        // Filter to instances with REST endpoints and healthy/ready state\n+        let candidates: Vec<_> = instances\n+            .iter()\n+            .filter(|inst| {\n+                inst.rest_endpoint.is_some()\n+                    && matches!(inst.state(), InstanceState::Healthy | InstanceState::Ready)\n+            })\n+            .cloned()\n+            .collect();\n+\n+        if candidates.is_empty() {\n+            return None;\n+        }\n+\n+        let len = candidates.len();\n+        let rr_key = format!(\"rest:{}\", module_name);\n+        let mut counter = self.rr_counters.entry(rr_key).or_insert(0);\n+        let idx = *counter % len;\n+        *counter = (*counter + 1) % len;\n+\n+        candidates.get(idx).map(|inst| {\n+            (\n+                module_name.to_owned(),\n+                inst.clone(),\n+                inst.rest_endpoint.clone().expect(\"filtered above\"),\n+            )\n+        })\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.3 Extend `DirectoryClient` trait\n+\n+**Location**: `cf_system_sdks/src/directory.rs` (upstream crate — requires update)\n+\n+```rust\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait DirectoryClient: Send + Sync {\n+    /// Resolve REST endpoint for a module (default for OoP).\n+    async fn resolve_rest_service(&self, module_name: &str) -> Result<RestEndpoint>;\n+\n+    /// Resolve gRPC endpoint for a module (opt-in).\n+    async fn resolve_grpc_service(&self, service_name: &str) -> Result<ServiceEndpoint>;\n+\n+    // ... existing methods (list_instances, register_instance, etc.) ...\n+}\n+\n+/// REST endpoint for a module\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct RestEndpoint {\n+    /// Base URL for the module's REST API (e.g., \"http://calculator:8080\")\n+    pub base_url: String,\n+}\n+\n+impl RestEndpoint {\n+    pub fn new(base_url: impl Into<String>) -> Self {\n+        Self { base_url: base_url.into() }\n+    }\n+\n+    pub fn http(host: &str, port: u16) -> Self {\n+        Self { base_url: format!(\"http://{}:{}\", host, port) }\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.4 Implement `resolve_rest_service` in `LocalDirectoryClient`\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/directory.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl DirectoryClient for LocalDirectoryClient {\n+    async fn resolve_rest_service(&self, module_name: &str) -> Result<RestEndpoint> {\n+        if let Some((_, _, ep)) = self.mgr.pick_rest_endpoint_round_robin(module_name) {\n+            return Ok(RestEndpoint::new(ep.uri));\n+        }\n+\n+        anyhow::bail!(\"REST service not found or no healthy instances: {module_name}\")\n+    }\n+\n+    // ... existing methods unchanged ...\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.5 Extend `RegisterInstanceInfo` for REST registration\n+\n+**Location**: `cf_system_sdks/src/directory.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Information needed to register a module instance\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct RegisterInstanceInfo {\n+    pub module: String,\n+    pub instance_id: String,\n+    pub grpc_services: Vec<(String, ServiceEndpoint)>,\n+    pub rest_endpoint: Option<RestEndpoint>,  // NEW\n+    pub version: Option<String>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.6 OoP Module REST Registration\n+\n+When an OoP module starts, it registers its REST endpoint with the DirectoryService:\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/oop.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+async fn register_with_directory(\n+    directory: &dyn DirectoryClient,\n+    module_name: &str,\n+    instance_id: Uuid,\n+    rest_port: u16,\n+    grpc_services: Vec<(String, ServiceEndpoint)>,\n+) -> Result<()> {\n+    let info = RegisterInstanceInfo {\n+        module: module_name.to_owned(),\n+        instance_id: instance_id.to_string(),\n+        grpc_services,\n+        rest_endpoint: Some(RestEndpoint::http(\"0.0.0.0\", rest_port)),\n+        version: Some(env!(\"CARGO_PKG_VERSION\").to_owned()),\n+    };\n+\n+    directory.register_instance(info).await\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.7 Design Decisions\n+\n+| Decision | Rationale |\n+|----------|-----------|\n+| **One REST endpoint per instance** | Unlike gRPC (multiple services per instance), REST modules expose a single base URL with path-based routing |\n+| **Module-name based resolution** | REST discovery uses `module_name` (e.g., \"calculator\"), not service name |\n+| **Reuse existing health tracking** | REST endpoints use the same `InstanceState` and heartbeat mechanism as gRPC |\n+| **Symmetric API** | `resolve_rest_service()` mirrors `resolve_grpc_service()` for consistency |\n+\n+##### 1.2.8 Migration Notes\n+\n+1. **`cf_system_sdks` must be updated first** — Add `RestEndpoint`, extend `RegisterInstanceInfo`, and add `resolve_rest_service()` to `DirectoryClient`\n+2. **`ModuleInstance` is extended** — Existing code continues to work; `rest_endpoint` defaults to `None`\n+3. **OoP modules must register REST endpoints** — Update bootstrap to include REST port in registration\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Phase 2: ClientDescriptor Trait\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/descriptor.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Client descriptor traits for typed OoP client metadata.\n+\n+use std::time::Duration;\n+\n+/// Availability policy for OoP clients.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum ClientAvailabilityPolicy {\n+    /// Client is optional; operations fail gracefully with SDK error (maps to HTTP 424).\n+    #[default]\n+    Optional,\n+    /// Client is required; module readiness may depend on availability.\n+    Required,\n+}\n+\n+/// Configuration for client behavior.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct ClientConfig {\n+    /// Transport protocol (REST default, gRPC opt-in).\n+    pub transport: Transport,\n+    /// Connection timeout for initial connect.\n+    pub connect_timeout: Duration,\n+    /// Request timeout for individual calls.\n+    pub request_timeout: Duration,\n+    /// Maximum backoff duration between reconnect attempts.\n+    pub max_backoff: Duration,\n+    /// Availability policy.\n+    pub availability_policy: ClientAvailabilityPolicy,\n+}\n+\n+impl Default for ClientConfig {\n+    fn default() -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            transport: Transport::Rest,\n+            connect_timeout: Duration::from_secs(5),\n+            request_timeout: Duration::from_secs(30),\n+            max_backoff: Duration::from_secs(60),\n+            availability_policy: ClientAvailabilityPolicy::Optional,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl ClientConfig {\n+    /// Create a REST client config (default).\n+    pub fn rest() -> Self {\n+        Self::default()\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Create a gRPC client config (opt-in).\n+    #[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+    pub fn grpc() -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            transport: Transport::Grpc,\n+            ..Self::default()\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Descriptor for an OoP client, defined in SDK crates.\n+///\n+/// This trait binds compile-time type information to runtime metadata\n+/// needed for lazy client resolution and registration.\n+pub trait ClientDescriptor: Send + Sync + 'static {\n+    /// The SDK API trait type (e.g., `dyn CalculatorClientV1`).\n+    type Api: ?Sized + Send + Sync + 'static;\n+\n+    /// Module name for dependency graph and Directory resolution.\n+    const MODULE_NAME: &'static str;\n+\n+    /// Client configuration (transport, timeouts, backoff, availability).\n+    fn config() -> ClientConfig {\n+        ClientConfig::default()\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Phase 3: ClientProvider Infrastructure\n+\n+#### 3.1 RestClientProvider (Default)\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/rest_provider.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Universal lazy REST client provider (default transport).\n+\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+use std::time::{Duration, Instant};\n+\n+use parking_lot::RwLock;\n+use tokio::sync::Semaphore;\n+\n+use crate::client_hub::ClientHub;\n+use crate::directory::DirectoryClient;\n+use crate::clients::descriptor::ClientConfig;\n+use modkit_http::HttpClient;\n+\n+/// Error type for REST provider operations.\n+#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\n+pub enum RestProviderError {\n+    #[error(\"service not found in directory: {module_name}\")]\n+    ServiceNotFound { module_name: &'static str },\n+\n+    #[error(\"HTTP request failed: {0}\")]\n+    HttpError(#[source] modkit_http::HttpError),\n+\n+    #[error(\"directory resolution failed: {0}\")]\n+    DirectoryError(#[source] anyhow::Error),\n+\n+    #[error(\"service temporarily unavailable (backoff active)\")]\n+    Backoff { retry_after: Duration },\n+}\n+\n+struct CachedEndpoint {\n+    base_url: String,\n+    resolved_at: Instant,\n+}\n+\n+struct ProviderState {\n+    cached: Option<CachedEndpoint>,\n+    last_failure: Option<Instant>,\n+    failure_count: u32,\n+}\n+\n+/// Universal lazy REST client provider.\n+///\n+/// Handles:\n+/// - Lazy endpoint resolution via DirectoryClient\n+/// - Base URL caching with automatic eviction on errors\n+/// - Exponential backoff for reconnection attempts\n+/// - Rate limiting to prevent thundering herds\n+pub struct RestClientProvider {\n+    module_name: &'static str,\n+    config: ClientConfig,\n+    hub: Arc<ClientHub>,\n+    http_client: HttpClient,\n+    state: RwLock<ProviderState>,\n+    resolve_semaphore: Semaphore,\n+}\n+\n+impl RestClientProvider {\n+    pub fn new(\n+        module_name: &'static str,\n+        config: ClientConfig,\n+        hub: Arc<ClientHub>,\n+    ) -> Self {\n+        let http_client = HttpClient::builder()\n+            .timeout(config.request_timeout)\n+            .connect_timeout(config.connect_timeout)\n+            .build();\n+\n+        Self {\n+            module_name,\n+            config,\n+            hub,\n+            http_client,\n+            state: RwLock::new(ProviderState {\n+                cached: None,\n+                last_failure: None,\n+                failure_count: 0,\n+            }),\n+            resolve_semaphore: Semaphore::new(1),\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Get the base URL for the service, resolving lazily.\n+    pub async fn get_base_url(&self) -> Result<String, RestProviderError> {\n+        // Fast path: return cached endpoint\n+        {\n+            let state = self.state.read();\n+            if let Some(ref cached) = state.cached {\n+                return Ok(cached.base_url.clone());\n+            }\n+\n+            // Check backoff\n+            if let Some(last_failure) = state.last_failure {\n+                let backoff = self.calculate_backoff(state.failure_count);\n+                let elapsed = last_failure.elapsed();\n+                if elapsed < backoff {\n+                    return Err(RestProviderError::Backoff {\n+                        retry_after: backoff - elapsed,\n+                    });\n+                }\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        // Slow path: acquire semaphore and resolve\n+        let _permit = self.resolve_semaphore.acquire().await\n+            .expect(\"semaphore is never closed\");\n+\n+        // Double-check after acquiring semaphore\n+        {\n+            let state = self.state.read();\n+            if let Some(ref cached) = state.cached {\n+                return Ok(cached.base_url.clone());\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        self.resolve_internal().await\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Get the HTTP client for making requests.\n+    pub fn http_client(&self) -> &HttpClient {\n+        &self.http_client\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Evict the cached endpoint (call on transport errors).\n+    pub fn evict(&self) {\n+        let mut state = self.state.write();\n+        state.cached = None;\n+        state.last_failure = Some(Instant::now());\n+        state.failure_count = state.failure_count.saturating_add(1);\n+        tracing::warn!(\n+            module = self.module_name,\n+            failure_count = state.failure_count,\n+            \"Evicted cached REST endpoint\"\n+        );\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Reset failure state (call on successful request).\n+    pub fn reset_failures(&self) {\n+        let mut state = self.state.write();\n+        if state.failure_count > 0 {\n+            state.failure_count = 0;\n+            state.last_failure = None;\n+            tracing::debug!(module = self.module_name, \"Reset failure state after success\");\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    async fn resolve_internal(&self) -> Result<String, RestProviderError> {\n+        let directory = self\n+            .hub\n+            .get::<dyn DirectoryClient>()\n+            .map_err(|e| RestProviderError::DirectoryError(e.into()))?;\n+\n+        let endpoint = directory\n+            .resolve_rest_service(self.module_name)\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(RestProviderError::DirectoryError)?;\n+\n+        tracing::debug!(\n+            module = self.module_name,\n+            base_url = %endpoint.base_url,\n+            \"Resolved REST endpoint\"\n+        );\n+\n+        {\n+            let mut state = self.state.write();\n+            state.cached = Some(CachedEndpoint {\n+                base_url: endpoint.base_url.clone(),\n+                resolved_at: Instant::now(),\n+            });\n+            state.failure_count = 0;\n+            state.last_failure = None;\n+        }\n+\n+        Ok(endpoint.base_url)\n+    }\n+\n+    fn calculate_backoff(&self, failure_count: u32) -> Duration {\n+        let base = Duration::from_millis(100);\n+        let max = self.config.max_backoff;\n+        let backoff = base.saturating_mul(2u32.saturating_pow(failure_count.min(10)));\n+        backoff.min(max)\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### 3.2 GrpcClientProvider (Optional)\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/grpc_provider.rs`\n+\n+> Feature-gated behind `feature = \"grpc\"` for streaming/high-throughput use cases.\n+\n+```rust\n+#[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+//! Lazy gRPC client provider (optional transport).\n+\n+// Implementation follows same pattern as RestClientProvider\n+// but manages tonic::transport::Channel instead of base URL\n+```\n+\n+#### 3.3 LazyClientError\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/error.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Error returned by lazy clients when the OoP dependency is unavailable.\n+#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\n+pub enum LazyClientError {\n+    #[error(\"service unavailable: {module_name}\")]\n+    Unavailable {\n+        module_name: &'static str,\n+        #[source]\n+        source: Box<dyn std::error::Error + Send + Sync>,\n+    },\n+\n+    #[error(\"request failed: {0}\")]\n+    RequestFailed(String),\n+\n+    #[error(\"response parsing failed: {0}\")]\n+    ParseError(#[source] serde_json::Error),\n+}\n+\n+impl LazyClientError {\n+    /// Returns true if this error indicates the service is temporarily unavailable.\n+    /// REST handlers should map this to HTTP 424 Failed Dependency.\n+    pub fn is_dependency_unavailable(&self) -> bool {\n+        matches!(self, LazyClientError::Unavailable { .. })\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Phase 4: SDK Crate Updates (calculator-sdk example)\n+\n+#### 4.1 Descriptor\n+\n+**Location**: `calculator-sdk/src/descriptor.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit::clients::descriptor::{ClientDescriptor, ClientConfig};\n+use crate::api::CalculatorClientV1;\n+\n+/// Descriptor for the Calculator client (REST by default).\n+pub struct CalculatorClientDescriptor;\n+\n+impl ClientDescriptor for CalculatorClientDescriptor {\n+    type Api = dyn CalculatorClientV1;\n+    const MODULE_NAME: &'static str = \"calculator\";\n+\n+    fn config() -> ClientConfig {\n+        ClientConfig::rest()  // Default: REST transport","path":"docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md","commit_id":"edd86e3e6cf91af1a08e3970d60dc26bc6acb6e6","original_commit_id":"030bc79ea9322b429e351c332cbffd4f44791b3c","user":{"login":"alexpitsikoulis","id":50185728,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMTg1NzI4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50185728?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis","html_url":"https://github.com/alexpitsikoulis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexpitsikoulis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Yes ClientConifg has availability policy, circuit breaker, fallback strategy, and other config options defined.","created_at":"2026-02-19T20:46:32Z","updated_at":"2026-02-19T20:46:33Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2830082687","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2830082687"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2830082687"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2830082687/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":1438,"original_line":674,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2828805752,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":674,"position":1438,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2833412613","pull_request_review_id":3832257863,"id":2833412613,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6o4nIF","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1050 @@\n+# ADR-0003: Universal Lazy Typed REST Clients for OoP Modules\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+This proposal outlines a migration from gRPC to REST as the default transport for out-of-process (OoP) modules and introduces a **universal lazy typed client layer** for OoP module communication in ModKit. The implementation is structured in phases:\n+\n+1. **Phase 1 - REST as default transport**: Establish REST as the default OoP transport; gRPC becomes opt-in\n+2. **Phase 2 - ClientDescriptor trait**: SDK-defined metadata binding compile-time types to runtime resolution\n+3. **Phase 3 - ClientProvider**: Lazy resolution, caching, backoff, and reconnection infrastructure\n+4. **Phase 4 - Macro extension**: `clients = [...]` auto-registers lazy clients into `ClientHub`\n+5. **Phase 5 - Soft OoP deps**: Dependencies on OoP modules don't block startup\n+6. **Phase 6 - Registry extension**: Soft OoP dep resolution:  \n+\n+**Current pattern** (problematic):\n+```rust\n+// Consumer must wire client manually in init() - FAILS if OoP module is not ready\n+calculator_sdk::wire_client(hub, &*directory).await?;\n+```\n+\n+**Proposed pattern**:\n+```rust\n+#[modkit::module(\n+    name = \"calculator_gateway\",\n+    clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],  // REST by default\n+)]\n+// No wire_client() needed - lazy client auto-registered\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Problem Statement\n+\n+The current OoP client wiring pattern has several issues:\n+\n+1. **Eager wiring is fragile**: Consumer modules call `wire_client()` in `init()`, which fails if the OoP dependency is not yet available.\n+2. **Startup coupling**: The entire module fails to start if any OoP dependency is temporarily unavailable.\n+3. **Boilerplate duplication**: Each SDK repeats the same resolve/connect/cache logic.\n+4. **No graceful degradation**: Missing dependencies cause module-level failures instead of per-operation failures (HTTP 424).\n+5. **gRPC complexity**: Binary protobuf payloads are hard to debug; requires specialized tooling.\n+\n+### Current Pattern (calculator_gateway example)\n+\n+```rust\n+// Current: Consumer must wire client manually, and it happens eagerly\n+pub async fn wire_client(hub: &ClientHub, resolver: &dyn DirectoryClient) -> Result<()> {\n+    let endpoint = resolver.resolve_grpc_service(SERVICE_NAME).await?;  // Fails if OoP not ready\n+    let client = CalculatorGrpcClient::connect(&endpoint.uri).await?;   // Fails if network issue\n+    hub.register::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>(Arc::new(client));\n+    Ok(())\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Proposed Solution\n+\n+### Architecture Overview\n+\n+```text\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           SDK Crate (calculator-sdk)                    │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  CalculatorClientDescriptor                                             │\n+│    - MODULE_NAME: \"calculator\"                                          │\n+│    - Api: dyn CalculatorClientV1                                        │\n+│    - Transport: Rest (default) | Grpc (opt-in)                          │\n+│    - Availability Policy: Optional (default)                            │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  LazyCalculatorClient                                                   │\n+│    - Implements CalculatorClientV1                                      │\n+│    - Delegates to ClientProvider for lazy connection                    │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           ModKit (libs/modkit)                          │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  ClientProvider (transport-agnostic interface)                          │\n+│    - Lazy resolution via DirectoryClient                                │\n+│    - Endpoint/connection caching with eviction on error                 │\n+│    - Backoff/rate-limiting for reconnects                               │\n+│    - Transport middleware (timeouts, retries, tracing)                  │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  RestClientProvider (default) | GrpcClientProvider (feature = \"grpc\")   │","path":"docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md","commit_id":"edd86e3e6cf91af1a08e3970d60dc26bc6acb6e6","original_commit_id":"030bc79ea9322b429e351c332cbffd4f44791b3c","user":{"login":"striped-zebra-dev","id":225538363,"node_id":"U_kgDODXFxOw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225538363?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/striped-zebra-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Thx, noted.","created_at":"2026-02-20T14:17:04Z","updated_at":"2026-02-20T14:17:05Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2833412613","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2833412613"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2833412613"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2833412613/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":84,"original_line":84,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2828789279,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":84,"position":84,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2833430835","pull_request_review_id":3832277723,"id":2833430835,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6o4rkz","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1050 @@\n+# ADR-0003: Universal Lazy Typed REST Clients for OoP Modules\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+This proposal outlines a migration from gRPC to REST as the default transport for out-of-process (OoP) modules and introduces a **universal lazy typed client layer** for OoP module communication in ModKit. The implementation is structured in phases:\n+\n+1. **Phase 1 - REST as default transport**: Establish REST as the default OoP transport; gRPC becomes opt-in\n+2. **Phase 2 - ClientDescriptor trait**: SDK-defined metadata binding compile-time types to runtime resolution\n+3. **Phase 3 - ClientProvider**: Lazy resolution, caching, backoff, and reconnection infrastructure\n+4. **Phase 4 - Macro extension**: `clients = [...]` auto-registers lazy clients into `ClientHub`\n+5. **Phase 5 - Soft OoP deps**: Dependencies on OoP modules don't block startup\n+6. **Phase 6 - Registry extension**: Soft OoP dep resolution:  \n+\n+**Current pattern** (problematic):\n+```rust\n+// Consumer must wire client manually in init() - FAILS if OoP module is not ready\n+calculator_sdk::wire_client(hub, &*directory).await?;\n+```\n+\n+**Proposed pattern**:\n+```rust\n+#[modkit::module(\n+    name = \"calculator_gateway\",\n+    clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],  // REST by default\n+)]\n+// No wire_client() needed - lazy client auto-registered\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Problem Statement\n+\n+The current OoP client wiring pattern has several issues:\n+\n+1. **Eager wiring is fragile**: Consumer modules call `wire_client()` in `init()`, which fails if the OoP dependency is not yet available.\n+2. **Startup coupling**: The entire module fails to start if any OoP dependency is temporarily unavailable.\n+3. **Boilerplate duplication**: Each SDK repeats the same resolve/connect/cache logic.\n+4. **No graceful degradation**: Missing dependencies cause module-level failures instead of per-operation failures (HTTP 424).\n+5. **gRPC complexity**: Binary protobuf payloads are hard to debug; requires specialized tooling.\n+\n+### Current Pattern (calculator_gateway example)\n+\n+```rust\n+// Current: Consumer must wire client manually, and it happens eagerly\n+pub async fn wire_client(hub: &ClientHub, resolver: &dyn DirectoryClient) -> Result<()> {\n+    let endpoint = resolver.resolve_grpc_service(SERVICE_NAME).await?;  // Fails if OoP not ready\n+    let client = CalculatorGrpcClient::connect(&endpoint.uri).await?;   // Fails if network issue\n+    hub.register::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>(Arc::new(client));\n+    Ok(())\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Proposed Solution\n+\n+### Architecture Overview\n+\n+```text\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           SDK Crate (calculator-sdk)                    │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  CalculatorClientDescriptor                                             │\n+│    - MODULE_NAME: \"calculator\"                                          │\n+│    - Api: dyn CalculatorClientV1                                        │\n+│    - Transport: Rest (default) | Grpc (opt-in)                          │\n+│    - Availability Policy: Optional (default)                            │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  LazyCalculatorClient                                                   │\n+│    - Implements CalculatorClientV1                                      │\n+│    - Delegates to ClientProvider for lazy connection                    │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           ModKit (libs/modkit)                          │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  ClientProvider (transport-agnostic interface)                          │\n+│    - Lazy resolution via DirectoryClient                                │\n+│    - Endpoint/connection caching with eviction on error                 │\n+│    - Backoff/rate-limiting for reconnects                               │\n+│    - Transport middleware (timeouts, retries, tracing)                  │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  RestClientProvider (default) | GrpcClientProvider (feature = \"grpc\")   │\n+│    - Transport-specific implementations                                 │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  #[modkit::module] macro extension                                      │\n+│    - clients = [CalculatorClientDescriptor]                             │\n+│    - Auto-registers LazyClient into ClientHub                           │\n+│    - Auto-injects MODULE_NAME from each descriptor into deps            │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    │\n+                                    ▼\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                      Consumer Module (calculator_gateway)               │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  #[modkit::module(                                                      │\n+│      name = \"calculator_gateway\",                                       │\n+│      capabilities = [rest],                                             │\n+│      clients = [calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor],            │\n+│      // deps auto-injected: [\"calculator\"] from descriptor              │\n+│  )]                                                                     │\n+│                                                                         │\n+│  // No wire_client() call needed!                                       │\n+│  // Client is always available from ClientHub                           │\n+│  let calc = hub.get::<dyn CalculatorClientV1>()?;                       │\n+│  calc.add(ctx, a, b).await?;  // Lazy connect on first call             │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Detailed Implementation\n+\n+### Phase 1: REST as Default Transport\n+\n+**Rationale**: REST is simpler to debug, requires no code generation, and is sufficient for most OoP calls. gRPC remains available for streaming or high-throughput use cases.\n+\n+| Factor          | REST                            | gRPC                         |\n+|-----------------|---------------------------------|------------------------------|\n+| Debuggability   | ✅ curl, browser, any HTTP tool | ❌ Requires specialized tools |\n+| Simplicity      | ✅ JSON, standard HTTP          | ❌ Protobuf, code generation  |\n+| Browser support | ✅ Native                       | ❌ Requires gRPC-Web proxy    |\n+| API reuse       | ✅ Same as public REST API      | ❌ Separate interface         |\n+| Streaming       | ❌ Requires SSE/WebSocket       | ✅ Native support             |\n+| Performance     | ⚠️ JSON overhead                | ✅ Binary, efficient          |\n+\n+#### 1.1 Transport Enum\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/transport.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Transport protocol for OoP communication.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum Transport {\n+    /// REST with JSON serialization (default).\n+    #[default]\n+    Rest,\n+    /// gRPC with protobuf serialization (opt-in, requires feature = \"grpc\").\n+    #[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+    Grpc,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### 1.2 REST Service Discovery Infrastructure\n+\n+REST service discovery requires extending the existing `ModuleInstance`, `ModuleManager`, and `DirectoryClient` to track and resolve REST endpoints.\n+\n+##### 1.2.1 Extend `ModuleInstance` to track REST endpoints\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/runtime/module_manager.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Represents a single instance of a module\n+#[derive(Debug)]\n+pub struct ModuleInstance {\n+    pub module: String,\n+    pub instance_id: Uuid,\n+    pub control: Option<Endpoint>,\n+    pub grpc_services: HashMap<String, Endpoint>,\n+    pub rest_endpoint: Option<Endpoint>,  // NEW: REST base URL for this instance\n+    pub version: Option<String>,\n+    inner: Arc<parking_lot::RwLock<InstanceRuntimeState>>,\n+}\n+\n+impl ModuleInstance {\n+    // ... existing methods ...\n+\n+    /// Set the REST endpoint for this instance\n+    pub fn with_rest_endpoint(mut self, ep: Endpoint) -> Self {\n+        self.rest_endpoint = Some(ep);\n+        self\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.2 Extend `ModuleManager` with REST discovery\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/runtime/module_manager.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+impl ModuleManager {\n+    /// Pick a REST endpoint for a module using round-robin selection.\n+    /// Returns (module_name, instance, endpoint) if found.\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn pick_rest_endpoint_round_robin(\n+        &self,\n+        module_name: &str,\n+    ) -> Option<(String, Arc<ModuleInstance>, Endpoint)> {\n+        let instances_entry = self.inner.get(module_name)?;\n+        let instances = instances_entry.value();\n+\n+        // Filter to instances with REST endpoints and healthy/ready state\n+        let candidates: Vec<_> = instances\n+            .iter()\n+            .filter(|inst| {\n+                inst.rest_endpoint.is_some()\n+                    && matches!(inst.state(), InstanceState::Healthy | InstanceState::Ready)\n+            })\n+            .cloned()\n+            .collect();\n+\n+        if candidates.is_empty() {\n+            return None;\n+        }\n+\n+        let len = candidates.len();\n+        let rr_key = format!(\"rest:{}\", module_name);\n+        let mut counter = self.rr_counters.entry(rr_key).or_insert(0);\n+        let idx = *counter % len;\n+        *counter = (*counter + 1) % len;\n+\n+        candidates.get(idx).map(|inst| {\n+            (\n+                module_name.to_owned(),\n+                inst.clone(),\n+                inst.rest_endpoint.clone().expect(\"filtered above\"),\n+            )\n+        })\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.3 Extend `DirectoryClient` trait\n+\n+**Location**: `cf_system_sdks/src/directory.rs` (upstream crate — requires update)\n+\n+```rust\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait DirectoryClient: Send + Sync {\n+    /// Resolve REST endpoint for a module (default for OoP).\n+    async fn resolve_rest_service(&self, module_name: &str) -> Result<RestEndpoint>;\n+\n+    /// Resolve gRPC endpoint for a module (opt-in).\n+    async fn resolve_grpc_service(&self, service_name: &str) -> Result<ServiceEndpoint>;\n+\n+    // ... existing methods (list_instances, register_instance, etc.) ...\n+}\n+\n+/// REST endpoint for a module\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct RestEndpoint {\n+    /// Base URL for the module's REST API (e.g., \"http://calculator:8080\")\n+    pub base_url: String,\n+}\n+\n+impl RestEndpoint {\n+    pub fn new(base_url: impl Into<String>) -> Self {\n+        Self { base_url: base_url.into() }\n+    }\n+\n+    pub fn http(host: &str, port: u16) -> Self {\n+        Self { base_url: format!(\"http://{}:{}\", host, port) }\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.4 Implement `resolve_rest_service` in `LocalDirectoryClient`\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/directory.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl DirectoryClient for LocalDirectoryClient {\n+    async fn resolve_rest_service(&self, module_name: &str) -> Result<RestEndpoint> {\n+        if let Some((_, _, ep)) = self.mgr.pick_rest_endpoint_round_robin(module_name) {\n+            return Ok(RestEndpoint::new(ep.uri));\n+        }\n+\n+        anyhow::bail!(\"REST service not found or no healthy instances: {module_name}\")\n+    }\n+\n+    // ... existing methods unchanged ...\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.5 Extend `RegisterInstanceInfo` for REST registration\n+\n+**Location**: `cf_system_sdks/src/directory.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Information needed to register a module instance\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct RegisterInstanceInfo {\n+    pub module: String,\n+    pub instance_id: String,\n+    pub grpc_services: Vec<(String, ServiceEndpoint)>,\n+    pub rest_endpoint: Option<RestEndpoint>,  // NEW\n+    pub version: Option<String>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.6 OoP Module REST Registration\n+\n+When an OoP module starts, it registers its REST endpoint with the DirectoryService:\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/oop.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+async fn register_with_directory(\n+    directory: &dyn DirectoryClient,\n+    module_name: &str,\n+    instance_id: Uuid,\n+    rest_port: u16,\n+    grpc_services: Vec<(String, ServiceEndpoint)>,\n+) -> Result<()> {\n+    let info = RegisterInstanceInfo {\n+        module: module_name.to_owned(),\n+        instance_id: instance_id.to_string(),\n+        grpc_services,\n+        rest_endpoint: Some(RestEndpoint::http(\"0.0.0.0\", rest_port)),\n+        version: Some(env!(\"CARGO_PKG_VERSION\").to_owned()),\n+    };\n+\n+    directory.register_instance(info).await\n+}\n+```\n+\n+##### 1.2.7 Design Decisions\n+\n+| Decision | Rationale |\n+|----------|-----------|\n+| **One REST endpoint per instance** | Unlike gRPC (multiple services per instance), REST modules expose a single base URL with path-based routing |\n+| **Module-name based resolution** | REST discovery uses `module_name` (e.g., \"calculator\"), not service name |\n+| **Reuse existing health tracking** | REST endpoints use the same `InstanceState` and heartbeat mechanism as gRPC |\n+| **Symmetric API** | `resolve_rest_service()` mirrors `resolve_grpc_service()` for consistency |\n+\n+##### 1.2.8 Migration Notes\n+\n+1. **`cf_system_sdks` must be updated first** — Add `RestEndpoint`, extend `RegisterInstanceInfo`, and add `resolve_rest_service()` to `DirectoryClient`\n+2. **`ModuleInstance` is extended** — Existing code continues to work; `rest_endpoint` defaults to `None`\n+3. **OoP modules must register REST endpoints** — Update bootstrap to include REST port in registration\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Phase 2: ClientDescriptor Trait\n+\n+**Location**: `libs/modkit/src/clients/descriptor.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Client descriptor traits for typed OoP client metadata.\n+\n+use std::time::Duration;\n+\n+/// Availability policy for OoP clients.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum ClientAvailabilityPolicy {\n+    /// Client is optional; operations fail gracefully with SDK error (maps to HTTP 424).\n+    #[default]\n+    Optional,\n+    /// Client is required; module readiness may depend on availability.\n+    Required,\n+}\n+\n+/// Configuration for client behavior.\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct ClientConfig {\n+    /// Transport protocol (REST default, gRPC opt-in).\n+    pub transport: Transport,\n+    /// Connection timeout for initial connect.\n+    pub connect_timeout: Duration,\n+    /// Request timeout for individual calls.\n+    pub request_timeout: Duration,\n+    /// Maximum backoff duration between reconnect attempts.\n+    pub max_backoff: Duration,\n+    /// Availability policy.\n+    pub availability_policy: ClientAvailabilityPolicy,\n+}\n+\n+impl Default for ClientConfig {\n+    fn default() -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            transport: Transport::Rest,\n+            connect_timeout: Duration::from_secs(5),\n+            request_timeout: Duration::from_secs(30),\n+            max_backoff: Duration::from_secs(60),\n+            availability_policy: ClientAvailabilityPolicy::Optional,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl ClientConfig {\n+    /// Create a REST client config (default).\n+    pub fn rest() -> Self {\n+        Self::default()\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Create a gRPC client config (opt-in).\n+    #[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]\n+    pub fn grpc() -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            transport: Transport::Grpc,\n+            ..Self::default()\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Descriptor for an OoP client, defined in SDK crates.\n+///\n+/// This trait binds compile-time type information to runtime metadata\n+/// needed for lazy client resolution and registration.\n+pub trait ClientDescriptor: Send + Sync + 'static {\n+    /// The SDK API trait type (e.g., `dyn CalculatorClientV1`).\n+    type Api: ?Sized + Send + Sync + 'static;\n+\n+    /// Module name for dependency graph and Directory resolution.\n+    const MODULE_NAME: &'static str;","path":"docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md","commit_id":"edd86e3e6cf91af1a08e3970d60dc26bc6acb6e6","original_commit_id":"030bc79ea9322b429e351c332cbffd4f44791b3c","user":{"login":"striped-zebra-dev","id":225538363,"node_id":"U_kgDODXFxOw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225538363?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/striped-zebra-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Actually, I see some cases such as refactoring, and this custom name gives both opportunity to migrate smoothly and opportunity to mess up. I'm OK with that, in the end people can find 1000 ways to mess up. ","created_at":"2026-02-20T14:20:32Z","updated_at":"2026-02-20T14:20:32Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2833430835","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2833430835"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#discussion_r2833430835"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2833430835/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":411,"original_line":407,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2828719155,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":407,"position":411,"subject_type":"line"}],"source_reviews":[{"id":3798360415,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7iZmFf","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 3**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n````\nIn `@docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md`:\n- Around line 924-943: The fenced code block that shows the project tree (the\nblock beginning with \"libs/modkit/src/\") is missing a language specifier; update\nthat block to use a plain/text specifier (e.g., change ``` to ```text) so the\nfile tree renders correctly in the ADR (the block containing the clients/,\nmodkit-macros entries and example paths).\n- Around line 823-843: The ServiceError -> Problem conversion currently detects\ndependency failures by string matching inside the RemoteError message; instead\nuse the typed error classifier (e.g., call the\nLazyClientError::is_dependency_unavailable() helper or map\nCalculatorError::Unavailable earlier) so the From<ServiceError> for Problem\nmatch inspects the underlying error type/variant rather than\nmsg.contains(\"unavailable\"); update the ServiceError::RemoteError arm to check\nthe wrapped error's is_dependency_unavailable() (or add a new\nServiceError::DependencyUnavailable variant upstream and match that) and then\nreturn Problem::failed_dependency().with_detail(...) for that case, keeping\nother RemoteError/Internal branches unchanged.\n- Around line 34-86: The fenced ASCII diagram block lacks a language specifier;\nupdate the opening fence to include a language (e.g., change ``` to ```text) for\nthe diagram that begins with the \"SDK Crate (calculator-sdk)\" header so the\ndiagram renders correctly; ensure the closing fence remains ``` and apply this\nto the fenced block containing the GrpcClientProvider, LazyGrpcClient,\n#[modkit::module] section and the Consumer Module example.\n````\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (4)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md (4)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`164-166`: **Document the constructor requirement more clearly.**\n\nThe comment mentions that `GrpcClient` must implement `From<tonic::transport::Channel>` or have a `new(Channel)` constructor, but this isn't enforced by the trait bounds. Consider either:\n1. Adding a trait bound to enforce this at compile time\n2. Documenting this as a runtime requirement with examples\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>💡 Suggested trait bound approach</summary>\n\n```diff\n     /// The concrete gRPC client type that implements `Api`.\n-    /// Must implement `From<tonic::transport::Channel>` or have a `new(Channel)` constructor.\n-    type GrpcClient: Send + Sync + 'static;\n+    /// Must be constructible from a Channel.\n+    type GrpcClient: From<tonic::transport::Channel> + Send + Sync + 'static;\n```\n\nAlternatively, if supporting both patterns, document the requirement clearly in the trait-level documentation and show examples for both approaches.\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`291-291`: **Document why `unwrap()` is safe or use `expect()` with context.**\n\nWhile this `unwrap()` is likely safe (the semaphore is never closed), using `expect()` with a descriptive message would make the safety assumption explicit and improve debuggability.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>💡 Proposed improvement</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        let _permit = self.connect_semaphore.acquire().await.unwrap();\n+        let _permit = self.connect_semaphore.acquire().await\n+            .expect(\"semaphore is never closed\");\n```\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`347-348`: **Remove unnecessary `.into()` conversion.**\n\nThe error `e` is already of type `tonic::transport::Error`, which matches the expected type in `ConnectionFailed`. The `.into()` call is redundant.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n         let channel = Channel::from_shared(endpoint.uri.clone())\n-            .map_err(|e| GrpcProviderError::ConnectionFailed(e.into()))?\n+            .map_err(GrpcProviderError::ConnectionFailed)?\n             .connect_timeout(self.config.connect_timeout)\n```\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`576-576`: **Consider using the descriptor's `GrpcClient` type for consistency.**\n\nThe implementation creates `proto::calculator_service_client::CalculatorServiceClient` directly, but the `CalculatorClientDescriptor` specifies `type GrpcClient = CalculatorGrpcClient`. For consistency with the descriptor pattern, consider using the type specified in the descriptor or documenting why the proto client is used directly.\n\nThis may be intentional if `CalculatorGrpcClient` is a higher-level wrapper, but the relationship should be clarified in the ADR.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#pullrequestreview-3798360415","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#pullrequestreview-3798360415"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-13T16:55:18Z","commit_id":"f948350f607d352064e3588bf0d83968c9100d42"},{"id":3798412652,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7iZy1s","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 3**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md`:\n- Around line 53-56: The diagram label currently shows\nGrpcClientProvider<TClient> but the implementation is defined as the non-generic\nGrpcClientProvider; update the diagram and any nearby mentions to use\nGrpcClientProvider (remove the generic parameter) so the API shape matches the\nlater definition, and scan the file for any other occurrences of\nGrpcClientProvider<TClient> to replace for consistency.\n- Around line 787-792: The example for modkit::module (name =\n\"calculator_gateway\") is inconsistent: it lists deps = [\"calculator\"] even\nthough the macro auto-augments deps from clients; either remove the explicit\ndeps entry from the attribute to avoid redundancy, or add a one-line note above\nthe snippet clarifying that deps is optional when clients (e.g., clients =\n[calculator_sdk::CalculatorClientDescriptor]) are present and will be\nauto-augmented by the macro; update the example to show the preferred approach\n(recommended: remove deps) and keep the modkit::module attribute and its\nname/client symbols unchanged.\n- Around line 1-7: Update the architecture diagram label to use\nGrpcClientProvider (remove the generic parameter TClient) to match the actual\nimplementation, and clarify the example's deps behavior: specify whether the\nmacro auto-injects OoP dependencies when using the clients = [...] parameter or\nrequires explicit deps = [\"module_name\"] entries; then either remove the manual\ndeps from the \"After\" example (if auto-injected) or change the surrounding text\nto state that developers must declare deps manually. Finally, update the\nimplementation guide references so the migration section points to\n09_oop_grpc_sdk_pattern.md as the primary doc to change during migration.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#pullrequestreview-3798412652","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#pullrequestreview-3798412652"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-13T17:06:37Z","commit_id":"3c9e4819f47928ba3df27b37fd0199b2296eb259"},{"id":3798441951,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7iZ5_f","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 1**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md`:\n- Around line 714-757: The ResolvedDeps struct currently uses Vec<&'static str>\nbut resolve_dependencies_with_oop accepts &[&str] (non-'static), causing a\nlifetime mismatch; update the API by either making ResolvedDeps generic over a\nlifetime (e.g., struct ResolvedDeps<'a> { hard_deps: Vec<&'a str>, soft_deps:\nVec<&'a str> } and change resolve_dependencies_with_oop signature to return\nResult<ResolvedDeps<'_>, RegistryError>) or convert to owned strings (change\nfields to Vec<String>, push dep.to_string() when building hard_deps/soft_deps);\nadjust all callers of ResolvedDeps and the resolve_dependencies_with_oop\nsignature accordingly to match the chosen approach (modify function return type\nand any usages of ResolvedDeps::hard_deps / soft_deps).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`807-816`: **Align the “After” example with the typed error mapping guidance.**\n\nThe “After” example maps `CalculatorError::Unavailable` to `ServiceError::RemoteError`, but the next section recommends a typed `DependencyUnavailable` variant. Updating the example keeps the ADR consistent and avoids mixed guidance.  \n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested adjustment</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        calculator.add(ctx, a, b).await.map_err(|e| {\n-            // CalculatorError::Unavailable maps to HTTP 424\n-            ServiceError::RemoteError(e.to_string())\n-        })\n+        calculator.add(ctx, a, b).await.map_err(|e| match e {\n+            CalculatorError::Unavailable { message } => ServiceError::DependencyUnavailable {\n+                service: \"calculator\",\n+                source: message.into(),\n+            },\n+            other => ServiceError::RemoteError(other.to_string()),\n+        })\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#pullrequestreview-3798441951","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#pullrequestreview-3798441951"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-13T17:13:31Z","commit_id":"f27d777a7f704e5245de0afa449987e708c41cc7"},{"id":3815733575,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7jb3lH","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 1**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`946-975`: **Add \"See also\" section referencing ModKit unified system routing for REST wiring, ClientHub, and OoP SDK pattern.**\n\nThis ADR covers REST discovery, lazy ClientHub registration, and OoP module SDK patterns—all detailed in the ModKit unified system docs. Consider adding a \"See also\" section pointing to:\n- `docs/modkit_unified_system/03_clienthub_and_plugins.md` (ClientHub registration and typed clients)\n- `docs/modkit_unified_system/04_rest_operation_builder.md` (REST endpoint wiring)\n- `docs/modkit_unified_system/09_oop_sdk_pattern.md` (OoP SDK pattern and lazy client expectations)\n\nThis clarifies alignment with the broader module architecture and helps readers understand how the lazy client layer integrates into ModKit's routing and dependency model.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md` around lines 946 - 975,\nAdd a \"See also\" section to this ADR linking the related ModKit unified system\ndocs to show alignment: reference\ndocs/modkit_unified_system/03_clienthub_and_plugins.md (ClientHub registration\nand typed clients), docs/modkit_unified_system/04_rest_operation_builder.md\n(REST endpoint wiring), and docs/modkit_unified_system/09_oop_sdk_pattern.md\n(OoP SDK pattern and lazy client expectations); place this section near the end\nof the ADR (around the Implementation Timeline or right before References), give\na one-line descriptor for each link, and ensure the links use the exact\nfilenames shown so readers can jump to ClientHub, REST wiring, and OoP SDK\npattern docs.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nInline comments:\nIn `@docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md`:\n- Around line 698-767: The map_http_error signature currently expects\nreqwest::StatusCode but the LazyCalculatorClient implementation\n(response.status() from the HTTP client) yields http::StatusCode; change the\nmap_http_error function signature to accept http::StatusCode (fn\nmap_http_error(status: http::StatusCode, body: &str) -> CalculatorError) and\nupdate any imports/docs accordingly so map_http_error is called with the correct\ntype from response.status(); alternatively, document that the example assumes a\nreqwest-based client wrapper if you prefer to keep reqwest types.\n\n---\n\nDuplicate comments:\nIn `@docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md`:\n- Around line 830-863: The example has a lifetime mismatch:\nresolve_dependencies_with_oop accepts &[&str] but returns ResolvedDeps with\nVec<&'static str>; update ResolvedDeps and the function to use a compatible type\n— either give ResolvedDeps a lifetime parameter (e.g. struct ResolvedDeps<'a> {\nhard_deps: Vec<&'a str>, soft_deps: Vec<&'a str> } and propagate the lifetime on\nresolve_dependencies_with_oop) or change it to own Strings (Vec<String>) and\nclone/into_owned the dependency names before pushing; adjust return types and\nany callers in ModuleRegistry accordingly.\n\n---\n\nNitpick comments:\nIn `@docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md`:\n- Around line 946-975: Add a \"See also\" section to this ADR linking the related\nModKit unified system docs to show alignment: reference\ndocs/modkit_unified_system/03_clienthub_and_plugins.md (ClientHub registration\nand typed clients), docs/modkit_unified_system/04_rest_operation_builder.md\n(REST endpoint wiring), and docs/modkit_unified_system/09_oop_sdk_pattern.md\n(OoP SDK pattern and lazy client expectations); place this section near the end\nof the ADR (around the Implementation Timeline or right before References), give\na one-line descriptor for each link, and ensure the links use the exact\nfilenames shown so readers can jump to ClientHub, REST wiring, and OoP SDK\npattern docs.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#pullrequestreview-3815733575","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#pullrequestreview-3815733575"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-17T18:53:49Z","commit_id":"45c842d72a1b66b9fd91d166c47739812b96116d"},{"id":3815792182,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7jcF42","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 1**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nInline comments:\nIn `@docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md`:\n- Around line 761-769: The doc example's map_http_error signature is\ninconsistent with the actual usage of self.provider.http_client()\n(modkit_http::HttpClient) which returns http::StatusCode, not\nreqwest::StatusCode; update map_http_error to accept http::StatusCode (from the\nhttp crate) instead of reqwest::StatusCode and keep the same body: &str handling\nand match on status.as_u16() so it matches the surrounding implementation, or\nalternatively change the surrounding usage to provide a reqwest::StatusCode if\nyou prefer that client—adjust all references to map_http_error and calls from\nself.provider.http_client() accordingly.\n\n---\n\nDuplicate comments:\nIn `@docs/adrs/modkit/0003-modkit-universal-lazy-layer.md`:\n- Around line 832-865: The ResolvedDeps return type currently uses Vec<&'static\nstr> but resolve_dependencies_with_oop accepts deps: &[&str], causing a lifetime\nmismatch; fix by either (A) constraining the input to &'static str by changing\nthe signature to deps: &[&'static str] so you can safely push into\nResolvedDeps::hard_deps/soft_deps, or (B) make ResolvedDeps generic over a\nlifetime (e.g., pub struct ResolvedDeps<'a> { pub hard_deps: Vec<&'a str>, pub\nsoft_deps: Vec<&'a str> }) and change resolve_dependencies_with_oop to return\nResult<ResolvedDeps<'_>, RegistryError> so non-'static deps compile. Ensure you\nupdate the function signature and the ResolvedDeps type in the\nModuleRegistry::resolve_dependencies_with_oop implementation accordingly.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#pullrequestreview-3815792182","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/615#pullrequestreview-3815792182"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/615"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-17T19:07:22Z","commit_id":"0894889d189d3891110c1c1b1cb0855ecc970855"}]},{"source_pr_number":612,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/612","source_state":"closed","source_author":"aviator5","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #612] feat: implement authentication and authorization resolvers","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"authn-authz-impl-p1","pr_head_sha":"efa3ffa346090af62be89ff2519231ca07689fae","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"aviator5","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/612","id":3281340034,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPaLyBs7DlUaC","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/612","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/612.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/612.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/612","number":612,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat: implement authentication and authorization resolvers","user":{"login":"aviator5","id":245955115,"node_id":"U_kgDODqj6Kw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/245955115?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5","html_url":"https://github.com/aviator5","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"- Add cf-authn-resolver and cf-authn-resolver-sdk for bearer token validation\r\n- Add cf-authz-resolver and cf-authz-resolver-sdk for policy evaluation and scope compilation\r\n- Integrate AuthN/AuthZ into api-gateway middleware and request-scoped security context\r\n- Update users-info example and simple-user-settings with secure domain service patterns and PEP flow\r\n- Add PEP scope compilation and AccessScope constraint handling\r\n- Update architecture docs and authZ usage scenarios\r\n- Add comprehensive tests for scopable entity PEP evaluation\r\n\r\nThis establishes the foundation for multi-tenant authorization with fine-grained access control through policy engines and secure ORM integration.\r\n\r\ncloses #456, closes #457\r\n\r\n### Follow-up work\r\n\r\nThe following items are tracked as separate issues:\r\n- #630\r\n- #631\r\n- #632\r\n- #634\r\n- #637\r\n- #638\r\n- #639\r\n- #658\r\n\r\n\r\n### Key areas for review\r\n\r\n@MikeFalcon77, @Artifizer, @nonameffh, @capybutler FYI\r\n\r\n* **Design changes:**`docs/arch/authorization/` - updated design spec (`SecurityContext.subject_tenant_id` is required for now) and usage scenarios.\r\n* **AuthN Resolver:** `modules/system/authn-resolver/` - module + SDK + static plugin\r\n* **AuthZ Resolver:** `modules/system/authz-resolver/` - module + SDK + static plugin + PEP enforcer/compiler (`authz-resolver-sdk/src/pep/`)\r\n* **Secure ORM / Policy Enforcer:** `libs/modkit-db/src/secure/`, `libs/modkit-security`, `libs/modkit-db-macros`\r\n* **Usage examples**:\r\n  - `examples/modkit/users-info/` demonstrates the full PEP flow - PolicyEnforcer integration, Scopable entities, and secure domain service patterns with tests.\r\n  - `modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/domain/service.rs`","created_at":"2026-02-13T15:18:50Z","updated_at":"2026-02-18T13:39:42Z","closed_at":"2026-02-17T22:37:58Z","merged_at":"2026-02-17T22:37:58Z","merge_commit_sha":"39fe23528c33acc24c131ac778438c780f5eed28","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"nonameffh","id":5434885,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MzQ4ODU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5434885?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh","html_url":"https://github.com/nonameffh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nonameffh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},{"login":"capybutler","id":261428887,"node_id":"U_kgDOD5UWlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/261428887?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler","html_url":"https://github.com/capybutler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/capybutler/starred{/owner}