eRabbit -->\n\n✅ Confirmed as addressed by @pr0tey\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-13T10:46:26Z","updated_at":"2026-02-18T11:18:04Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2803577279","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2803577279"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2803577279"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2803577279/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":1172,"original_start_line":1129,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":1181,"original_line":1138,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":1252,"position":1305,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2818966440","pull_request_review_id":3816165818,"id":2818966440,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6oBgOo","diff_hunk":"@@ -1,33 +1,100 @@\n-# PRD\n+# PRD: Model Registry\n \n ## 1. Overview\n \n-**Purpose**: Model Registry provides a centralized catalog of AI models with tenant-level availability and approval workflow.\n+**Purpose**: Model Registry provides a centralized catalog of AI models with tenant-level availability and approval workflows.\n \n-Model Registry is the authoritative source for model metadata, capabilities, and tenant access control. It tracks which models are available from which providers, manages approval workflows for new models, and monitors provider health for routing decisions. LLM Gateway queries the registry to resolve model identifiers to provider endpoints and verify tenant access.\n+Model Registry is the authoritative source for model metadata, capabilities, pricing, and tenant access control. It tracks which models are available from which providers and manages approval workflows. LLM Gateway queries the registry to resolve model identifiers to provider endpoints and verify tenant access.","path":"modules/model-registry/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"15cb20127bb04236e91a1bb5d1860808534f7815","original_commit_id":"15cb20127bb04236e91a1bb5d1860808534f7815","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Here I'not sure it's possible to have accurate pricing here. From my PoV pricing must not live in the OSS modules, because there could plenty of ways to impact prices - promo, volume discounts, tiered pricing, regional pricing, etc. So we can't use it reliably here\n\nAlso, pricing metadata can be very confusing for the API clients. Pricing normally requires dedicated access permissions. Otherwise, a user (or API client) can see the \"wrong\" raw prices from this API and then see the other prices in the invoice\n\nI think the pricing should (must) be moved out this service responsibility","created_at":"2026-02-17T20:36:09Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T21:38:09Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2818966440","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2818966440"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2818966440"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2818966440/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":7,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":10,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2818991846","pull_request_review_id":3816165818,"id":2818991846,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6oBmbm","diff_hunk":"@@ -1,33 +1,100 @@\n-# PRD\n+# PRD: Model Registry\n \n ## 1. Overview\n \n-**Purpose**: Model Registry provides a centralized catalog of AI models with tenant-level availability and approval workflow.\n+**Purpose**: Model Registry provides a centralized catalog of AI models with tenant-level availability and approval workflows.\n \n-Model Registry is the authoritative source for model metadata, capabilities, and tenant access control. It tracks which models are available from which providers, manages approval workflows for new models, and monitors provider health for routing decisions. LLM Gateway queries the registry to resolve model identifiers to provider endpoints and verify tenant access.\n+Model Registry is the authoritative source for model metadata, capabilities, pricing, and tenant access control. It tracks which models are available from which providers and manages approval workflows. LLM Gateway queries the registry to resolve model identifiers to provider endpoints and verify tenant access.\n \n-The registry supports automatic model discovery from providers, requiring tenant admin approval before models become available. It also tracks provider health metrics (latency, error rates) to inform Gateway routing decisions.\n+**Key Concepts**:\n+\n+- **Canonical Model ID**: Deterministic identifier in format `{provider}::{provider_model_id}` (e.g., `openai::gpt-4o`). Parsing rule: split on **first** `::` occurrence.","path":"modules/model-registry/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"15cb20127bb04236e91a1bb5d1860808534f7815","original_commit_id":"15cb20127bb04236e91a1bb5d1860808534f7815","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I believe we'll need to support local LLMs or some alternative ways to access the same frontier models, so some \"instance id\" would probably make sense to distinguish:\n- azure corporate-global-subscription gpt5.2\n- azure rnd-subscription gpt5.2\n- ollama US-west-DC mistral\n- ollama US-east-DC mistral\n...\n\nwhat is your vision here?\n ","created_at":"2026-02-17T20:42:47Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T21:27:16Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2818991846","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2818991846"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2818991846"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2818991846/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":11,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":15,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819016086","pull_request_review_id":3816165818,"id":2819016086,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6oBsWW","diff_hunk":"@@ -37,217 +104,1036 @@ The registry supports automatic model discovery from providers, requiring tenant\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-tenant-admin`\n \n-**Role**: Approves or rejects models for tenant access. Configures auto-approval policies per provider.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Approves or rejects models for tenant access. Manages tenant-specific providers. Can only restrict access compared to parent tenant, not expand.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Platform Administrator\n+\n+**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-platform-admin`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Manages root tenant configuration. Configures global providers. Sets baseline that all tenants inherit.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n ### 2.2 System Actors\n \n #### LLM Gateway\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-llm-gateway`\n \n-**Role**: Queries registry to resolve model to provider, check tenant availability, and get model capabilities.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Queries registry to resolve model identifiers (canonical ID) to provider details. Checks tenant availability. Retrieves model capabilities and pricing.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Outbound API Gateway\n \n-**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-outbound-api-gateway`\n+**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-oagw`\n \n-**Role**: Executes provider API calls for model discovery and health probes.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Executes provider API calls for model discovery. Handles credential injection. Model Registry has no knowledge of credentials.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Provider API\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-provider-api`\n \n-**Role**: External provider endpoint that returns available models list and responds to health probes.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: External provider endpoint (OpenAI, Anthropic, Azure, etc.) that returns available models list.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+## 3. Domain Model\n+\n+### 3.1 Core Entities\n+\n+#### Provider\n+\n+Represents a configured AI provider for a tenant.\n+\n+**Fields**: id, tenant_id, name, type (plugin type), base_url, status (active/disabled), discovery config (enabled, interval), timestamps.\n+\n+**Inheritance**: Providers inherit down tenant hierarchy (additive only). Child tenant sees parent's providers + own. Child cannot hide inherited providers.\n+\n+**Health**: ProviderHealth stored at provider's owner tenant only. Child tenants inherit health status from parent.\n+\n+#### Model\n+\n+Represents an AI model in the catalog.\n+\n+**Fields**:\n+- **Identification**: canonical_id (`{provider}::{provider_model_id}`), provider_id, tenant_id, provider_model_id\n+- **Display**: name, description\n+- **Capabilities (Tier 1)**: Boolean flags for text/image/audio/video/document input/output, tools, structured_output, streaming, embeddings, realtime_audio, batch_api\n+- **Limits (Tier 2)**: context_window, max_output_tokens, max_images_per_request, max_image_size_mb, max_audio_duration_sec\n+- **Pricing**: AICredits per tier (sync/batch/cached) for input/output tokens and media (base pricing only)\n+- **Status**: active, deprecated (soft-delete with deprecated_at timestamp)\n+- **Version**: Provider's model version, stored as-is\n+\n+#### ModelApproval\n+\n+Tracks tenant approval status for a model.\n+\n+**Fields**: id, model_canonical_id, tenant_id, status (pending/approved/rejected/revoked), approved_at, approved_by, auto_approval_rule_id (reference to rule that triggered auto-approval, null for manual), rejected_at, rejected_by, revoked_at, revoked_by, timestamps.\n+\n+**Concurrency**: First write wins - once status changes from `pending`, subsequent approve/reject requests are rejected.\n+\n+**State Machine**:\n+\n+```mermaid\n+stateDiagram-v2\n+    [*] --> pending: Model discovered\n+    pending --> approved: Admin approves\n+    pending --> approved: Auto-approval rule matches\n+    pending --> rejected: Admin rejects\n+    approved --> revoked: Admin revokes\n+    rejected --> approved: Admin reconsiders\n+    revoked --> approved: Admin reinstates\n+```\n+\n+#### AutoApprovalRule (P2)\n+\n+Defines rules for automatic model approval.\n+\n+**Fields**: id, tenant_id (root = platform-wide), criteria, action (allow/block), priority, created_at, created_by.\n+\n+**Criteria schema**:\n+- `provider_type`: string | \"*\" (required, \"*\" = any)\n+- `provider_id`: string | \"*\" (required, \"*\" = any)\n+- `capabilities`: string[] (optional, empty = any)\n+\n+**Matching**: ALL criteria must match (AND). Model must have ALL listed capabilities (subset matching).\n+\n+**Rule evaluation**:\n+- Platform (root tenant) rules set the ceiling\n+- Tenant rules can only restrict further, not expand\n+- `block` from platform = blocked for all descendants\n+- Tenant cannot `allow` what platform blocked\n \n-## 3. Functional Requirements\n+**Authorization**: Read/list visible to tenant admins only.\n+\n+#### ProviderHealth (P2)\n+\n+Tracks provider health status from synthetic probes.","path":"modules/model-registry/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"15cb20127bb04236e91a1bb5d1860808534f7815","original_commit_id":"15cb20127bb04236e91a1bb5d1860808534f7815","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I would emphasize it's provider health status storage, not provider health status tracker/detector/workflow/scrapper, correct?","created_at":"2026-02-17T20:48:37Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T21:27:16Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2819016086","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819016086"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2819016086"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819016086/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":216,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":237,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819033790","pull_request_review_id":3816165818,"id":2819033790,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6oBwq-","diff_hunk":"@@ -1,33 +1,100 @@\n-# PRD\n+# PRD: Model Registry\n \n ## 1. Overview\n \n-**Purpose**: Model Registry provides a centralized catalog of AI models with tenant-level availability and approval workflow.\n+**Purpose**: Model Registry provides a centralized catalog of AI models with tenant-level availability and approval workflows.\n \n-Model Registry is the authoritative source for model metadata, capabilities, and tenant access control. It tracks which models are available from which providers, manages approval workflows for new models, and monitors provider health for routing decisions. LLM Gateway queries the registry to resolve model identifiers to provider endpoints and verify tenant access.\n+Model Registry is the authoritative source for model metadata, capabilities, pricing, and tenant access control. It tracks which models are available from which providers and manages approval workflows. LLM Gateway queries the registry to resolve model identifiers to provider endpoints and verify tenant access.\n \n-The registry supports automatic model discovery from providers, requiring tenant admin approval before models become available. It also tracks provider health metrics (latency, error rates) to inform Gateway routing decisions.\n+**Key Concepts**:\n+\n+- **Canonical Model ID**: Deterministic identifier in format `{provider}::{provider_model_id}` (e.g., `openai::gpt-4o`). Parsing rule: split on **first** `::` occurrence.\n+- **Tenant Hierarchy**: Tree structure with root tenant at top; providers and approvals inherit down the tree (additive only)\n+- **Provider Plugins**: Each provider type has its own plugin; all requests route through Outbound API Gateway\n \n **Target Users**:\n-- **LLM Gateway** - Primary consumer for model resolution and availability checks\n-- **Tenant Administrators** - Approve/reject models for their tenant\n+\n+- **LLM Gateway** — Primary consumer for model resolution and availability checks\n+- **Tenant Administrators** — Approve/reject models, manage tenant-specific providers\n+- **Platform Administrators** — Configure root tenant providers\n \n **Key Problems Solved**:\n+\n - **Model discovery**: Automatic polling of provider APIs to discover available models\n-- **Access control**: Tenant-level approval workflow for model access\n-- **Health tracking**: Provider health metrics for intelligent routing\n+- **Unified identification**: Canonical IDs abstract provider-specific naming\n+- **Access control**: Tenant-level approval workflow with hierarchical inheritance\n+- **Pricing normalization**: AICredits-based pricing with tier support (sync/batch/cached)","path":"modules/model-registry/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"15cb20127bb04236e91a1bb5d1860808534f7815","original_commit_id":"15cb20127bb04236e91a1bb5d1860808534f7815","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The same comment about pricing","created_at":"2026-02-17T20:52:10Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T21:27:16Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2819033790","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819033790"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2819033790"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819033790/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":26,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":34,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819039073","pull_request_review_id":3816165818,"id":2819039073,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6oBx9h","diff_hunk":"@@ -1,33 +1,100 @@\n-# PRD\n+# PRD: Model Registry\n \n ## 1. Overview\n \n-**Purpose**: Model Registry provides a centralized catalog of AI models with tenant-level availability and approval workflow.\n+**Purpose**: Model Registry provides a centralized catalog of AI models with tenant-level availability and approval workflows.\n \n-Model Registry is the authoritative source for model metadata, capabilities, and tenant access control. It tracks which models are available from which providers, manages approval workflows for new models, and monitors provider health for routing decisions. LLM Gateway queries the registry to resolve model identifiers to provider endpoints and verify tenant access.\n+Model Registry is the authoritative source for model metadata, capabilities, pricing, and tenant access control. It tracks which models are available from which providers and manages approval workflows. LLM Gateway queries the registry to resolve model identifiers to provider endpoints and verify tenant access.\n \n-The registry supports automatic model discovery from providers, requiring tenant admin approval before models become available. It also tracks provider health metrics (latency, error rates) to inform Gateway routing decisions.\n+**Key Concepts**:\n+\n+- **Canonical Model ID**: Deterministic identifier in format `{provider}::{provider_model_id}` (e.g., `openai::gpt-4o`). Parsing rule: split on **first** `::` occurrence.\n+- **Tenant Hierarchy**: Tree structure with root tenant at top; providers and approvals inherit down the tree (additive only)\n+- **Provider Plugins**: Each provider type has its own plugin; all requests route through Outbound API Gateway\n \n **Target Users**:\n-- **LLM Gateway** - Primary consumer for model resolution and availability checks\n-- **Tenant Administrators** - Approve/reject models for their tenant\n+\n+- **LLM Gateway** — Primary consumer for model resolution and availability checks\n+- **Tenant Administrators** — Approve/reject models, manage tenant-specific providers\n+- **Platform Administrators** — Configure root tenant providers\n \n **Key Problems Solved**:\n+\n - **Model discovery**: Automatic polling of provider APIs to discover available models\n-- **Access control**: Tenant-level approval workflow for model access\n-- **Health tracking**: Provider health metrics for intelligent routing\n+- **Unified identification**: Canonical IDs abstract provider-specific naming\n+- **Access control**: Tenant-level approval workflow with hierarchical inheritance\n+- **Pricing normalization**: AICredits-based pricing with tier support (sync/batch/cached)\n \n **Success Criteria**:\n-- All scenarios (S1-S6) implemented and operational\n-- Model resolution latency < 10ms P99\n-- Provider health status updated within health check interval\n \n-**Capabilities**:\n-- Model catalog management\n-- Tenant-level model availability\n-- Model approval workflow\n-- Provider health monitoring\n-- Model capability and pricing metadata\n+- Model resolution latency < 10ms P99\n+- 99.9% availability\n+\n+### 1.1 Background\n+\n+LLM Gateway requires a centralized source of truth for model availability, capabilities, and pricing. Without Model Registry, each consumer would need to maintain its own model catalog, leading to inconsistency and duplicated approval workflows.\n+\n+### 1.2 Goals\n+\n+1. Single source of truth for AI model metadata across the platform\n+2. Tenant-controlled model availability with inheritance from parent tenants\n+3. Streamlined approval process\n+\n+### 1.3 Scope\n+\n+#### In Scope\n+\n+- Model catalog CRUD (models, providers)\n+- Tenant-level model availability configuration\n+- Approval workflows (request → approve/reject)\n+- Base pricing metadata (AICredits per tier)","path":"modules/model-registry/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"15cb20127bb04236e91a1bb5d1860808534f7815","original_commit_id":"15cb20127bb04236e91a1bb5d1860808534f7815","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Base pricing is OK (if it's obtained from providers), but not the final pricing","created_at":"2026-02-17T20:53:17Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T21:27:16Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2819039073","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819039073"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2819039073"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819039073/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":50,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":67,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819048774","pull_request_review_id":3816165818,"id":2819048774,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6oB0VG","diff_hunk":"@@ -1,33 +1,100 @@\n-# PRD\n+# PRD: Model Registry\n \n ## 1. Overview\n \n-**Purpose**: Model Registry provides a centralized catalog of AI models with tenant-level availability and approval workflow.\n+**Purpose**: Model Registry provides a centralized catalog of AI models with tenant-level availability and approval workflows.\n \n-Model Registry is the authoritative source for model metadata, capabilities, and tenant access control. It tracks which models are available from which providers, manages approval workflows for new models, and monitors provider health for routing decisions. LLM Gateway queries the registry to resolve model identifiers to provider endpoints and verify tenant access.\n+Model Registry is the authoritative source for model metadata, capabilities, pricing, and tenant access control. It tracks which models are available from which providers and manages approval workflows. LLM Gateway queries the registry to resolve model identifiers to provider endpoints and verify tenant access.\n \n-The registry supports automatic model discovery from providers, requiring tenant admin approval before models become available. It also tracks provider health metrics (latency, error rates) to inform Gateway routing decisions.\n+**Key Concepts**:\n+\n+- **Canonical Model ID**: Deterministic identifier in format `{provider}::{provider_model_id}` (e.g., `openai::gpt-4o`). Parsing rule: split on **first** `::` occurrence.\n+- **Tenant Hierarchy**: Tree structure with root tenant at top; providers and approvals inherit down the tree (additive only)\n+- **Provider Plugins**: Each provider type has its own plugin; all requests route through Outbound API Gateway\n \n **Target Users**:\n-- **LLM Gateway** - Primary consumer for model resolution and availability checks\n-- **Tenant Administrators** - Approve/reject models for their tenant\n+\n+- **LLM Gateway** — Primary consumer for model resolution and availability checks\n+- **Tenant Administrators** — Approve/reject models, manage tenant-specific providers\n+- **Platform Administrators** — Configure root tenant providers\n \n **Key Problems Solved**:\n+\n - **Model discovery**: Automatic polling of provider APIs to discover available models\n-- **Access control**: Tenant-level approval workflow for model access\n-- **Health tracking**: Provider health metrics for intelligent routing\n+- **Unified identification**: Canonical IDs abstract provider-specific naming\n+- **Access control**: Tenant-level approval workflow with hierarchical inheritance\n+- **Pricing normalization**: AICredits-based pricing with tier support (sync/batch/cached)\n \n **Success Criteria**:\n-- All scenarios (S1-S6) implemented and operational\n-- Model resolution latency < 10ms P99\n-- Provider health status updated within health check interval\n \n-**Capabilities**:\n-- Model catalog management\n-- Tenant-level model availability\n-- Model approval workflow\n-- Provider health monitoring\n-- Model capability and pricing metadata\n+- Model resolution latency < 10ms P99\n+- 99.9% availability\n+\n+### 1.1 Background\n+\n+LLM Gateway requires a centralized source of truth for model availability, capabilities, and pricing. Without Model Registry, each consumer would need to maintain its own model catalog, leading to inconsistency and duplicated approval workflows.\n+\n+### 1.2 Goals\n+\n+1. Single source of truth for AI model metadata across the platform\n+2. Tenant-controlled model availability with inheritance from parent tenants\n+3. Streamlined approval process\n+\n+### 1.3 Scope\n+\n+#### In Scope\n+\n+- Model catalog CRUD (models, providers)\n+- Tenant-level model availability configuration\n+- Approval workflows (request → approve/reject)\n+- Base pricing metadata (AICredits per tier)\n+- Model capabilities metadata\n+- Cache management with TTL-based invalidation\n+\n+#### Out of Scope\n+\n+| Item | Reason / Owner |\n+|------|----------------|\n+| LLM inference execution | LLM Gateway |\n+| Provider credential management | OAGW |\n+| Usage metering & billing | License Manager |\n+| Tenant hierarchy management | Tenant Resolver |\n+| Actual rate limiting enforcement | Infrastructure / OAGW |\n+| Audit log storage & retention | Core platform |\n+| Model fine-tuning / training | Not in scope for v1 |\n+| Provider API contracts | Each provider plugin |\n+| Provider plugin architecture | DESIGN.md |\n+| Notifications | Separate notification system |\n+\n+### 1.4 Assumptions\n+\n+1. Tenant Resolver provides tenant hierarchy data reliably and is highly available\n+2. OAGW handles all provider authentication\n+3. OAGW enforces outbound URL policy (blocks internal networks, requires HTTPS)\n+4. Each provider plugin exposes an endpoint returning available models (implementation is plugin responsibility)\n+5. Redis is available for distributed caching; if unavailable, fallback to direct DB queries","path":"modules/model-registry/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"15cb20127bb04236e91a1bb5d1860808534f7815","original_commit_id":"15cb20127bb04236e91a1bb5d1860808534f7815","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I'd use a cache plugin... Or maybe even a dedicated module, so that vendors can decide what cache to use and with what security transport and such.","created_at":"2026-02-17T20:55:36Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T21:27:16Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2819048774","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819048774"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2819048774"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819048774/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":75,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":92,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819062840","pull_request_review_id":3816165818,"id":2819062840,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6oB3w4","diff_hunk":"@@ -37,217 +104,1036 @@ The registry supports automatic model discovery from providers, requiring tenant\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-tenant-admin`\n \n-**Role**: Approves or rejects models for tenant access. Configures auto-approval policies per provider.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Approves or rejects models for tenant access. Manages tenant-specific providers. Can only restrict access compared to parent tenant, not expand.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Platform Administrator\n+\n+**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-platform-admin`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Manages root tenant configuration. Configures global providers. Sets baseline that all tenants inherit.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n ### 2.2 System Actors\n \n #### LLM Gateway\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-llm-gateway`\n \n-**Role**: Queries registry to resolve model to provider, check tenant availability, and get model capabilities.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Queries registry to resolve model identifiers (canonical ID) to provider details. Checks tenant availability. Retrieves model capabilities and pricing.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Outbound API Gateway\n \n-**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-outbound-api-gateway`\n+**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-oagw`\n \n-**Role**: Executes provider API calls for model discovery and health probes.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Executes provider API calls for model discovery. Handles credential injection. Model Registry has no knowledge of credentials.","path":"modules/model-registry/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"15cb20127bb04236e91a1bb5d1860808534f7815","original_commit_id":"15cb20127bb04236e91a1bb5d1860808534f7815","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Technically OAGW is not an Actor. It never comes to Model Registry. In a PRD (and everywhere), an Actor is any entity that interacts with the system from the outside to achieve a goal.","created_at":"2026-02-17T20:58:52Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T21:27:16Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2819062840","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819062840"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2819062840"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819062840/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":134,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":153,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819066416","pull_request_review_id":3816165818,"id":2819066416,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6oB4ow","diff_hunk":"@@ -37,217 +104,1036 @@ The registry supports automatic model discovery from providers, requiring tenant\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-tenant-admin`\n \n-**Role**: Approves or rejects models for tenant access. Configures auto-approval policies per provider.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Approves or rejects models for tenant access. Manages tenant-specific providers. Can only restrict access compared to parent tenant, not expand.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Platform Administrator\n+\n+**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-platform-admin`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Manages root tenant configuration. Configures global providers. Sets baseline that all tenants inherit.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n ### 2.2 System Actors\n \n #### LLM Gateway\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-llm-gateway`\n \n-**Role**: Queries registry to resolve model to provider, check tenant availability, and get model capabilities.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Queries registry to resolve model identifiers (canonical ID) to provider details. Checks tenant availability. Retrieves model capabilities and pricing.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Outbound API Gateway\n \n-**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-outbound-api-gateway`\n+**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-oagw`\n \n-**Role**: Executes provider API calls for model discovery and health probes.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Executes provider API calls for model discovery. Handles credential injection. Model Registry has no knowledge of credentials.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Provider API\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-provider-api`\n \n-**Role**: External provider endpoint that returns available models list and responds to health probes.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: External provider endpoint (OpenAI, Anthropic, Azure, etc.) that returns available models list.","path":"modules/model-registry/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"15cb20127bb04236e91a1bb5d1860808534f7815","original_commit_id":"15cb20127bb04236e91a1bb5d1860808534f7815","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The same, it's not an actor.","created_at":"2026-02-17T20:59:41Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T21:27:16Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2819066416","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819066416"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2819066416"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819066416/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":142,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":162,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819073976","pull_request_review_id":3816165818,"id":2819073976,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6oB6e4","diff_hunk":"@@ -37,217 +104,1036 @@ The registry supports automatic model discovery from providers, requiring tenant\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-tenant-admin`\n \n-**Role**: Approves or rejects models for tenant access. Configures auto-approval policies per provider.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Approves or rejects models for tenant access. Manages tenant-specific providers. Can only restrict access compared to parent tenant, not expand.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Platform Administrator\n+\n+**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-platform-admin`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Manages root tenant configuration. Configures global providers. Sets baseline that all tenants inherit.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n ### 2.2 System Actors\n \n #### LLM Gateway\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-llm-gateway`\n \n-**Role**: Queries registry to resolve model to provider, check tenant availability, and get model capabilities.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Queries registry to resolve model identifiers (canonical ID) to provider details. Checks tenant availability. Retrieves model capabilities and pricing.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Outbound API Gateway\n \n-**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-outbound-api-gateway`\n+**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-oagw`\n \n-**Role**: Executes provider API calls for model discovery and health probes.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Executes provider API calls for model discovery. Handles credential injection. Model Registry has no knowledge of credentials.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Provider API\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-provider-api`\n \n-**Role**: External provider endpoint that returns available models list and responds to health probes.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: External provider endpoint (OpenAI, Anthropic, Azure, etc.) that returns available models list.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+## 3. Domain Model\n+\n+### 3.1 Core Entities\n+\n+#### Provider\n+\n+Represents a configured AI provider for a tenant.\n+\n+**Fields**: id, tenant_id, name, type (plugin type), base_url, status (active/disabled), discovery config (enabled, interval), timestamps.\n+\n+**Inheritance**: Providers inherit down tenant hierarchy (additive only). Child tenant sees parent's providers + own. Child cannot hide inherited providers.\n+\n+**Health**: ProviderHealth stored at provider's owner tenant only. Child tenants inherit health status from parent.\n+","path":"modules/model-registry/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"49408257b07b88ae694cb12f7e728b684041d575","original_commit_id":"15cb20127bb04236e91a1bb5d1860808534f7815","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I would assume we need a \"### Location\", so that providers could have multiple locations, maybe with different base pricing and SLAs and models list available.\n\nLocation could be \"subscription\", \"dc\", \"subscription+region\", \"prod/staging\", whatever... We can make it flexible and allow tenants to manage it for model routing","created_at":"2026-02-17T21:01:43Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T21:27:16Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2819073976","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819073976"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2819073976"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819073976/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":191,"original_line":158,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":178,"position":208,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819107825","pull_request_review_id":3816165818,"id":2819107825,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6oCCvx","diff_hunk":"@@ -37,217 +104,1036 @@ The registry supports automatic model discovery from providers, requiring tenant\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-tenant-admin`\n \n-**Role**: Approves or rejects models for tenant access. Configures auto-approval policies per provider.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Approves or rejects models for tenant access. Manages tenant-specific providers. Can only restrict access compared to parent tenant, not expand.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Platform Administrator\n+\n+**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-platform-admin`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Manages root tenant configuration. Configures global providers. Sets baseline that all tenants inherit.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n ### 2.2 System Actors\n \n #### LLM Gateway\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-llm-gateway`\n \n-**Role**: Queries registry to resolve model to provider, check tenant availability, and get model capabilities.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Queries registry to resolve model identifiers (canonical ID) to provider details. Checks tenant availability. Retrieves model capabilities and pricing.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Outbound API Gateway\n \n-**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-outbound-api-gateway`\n+**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-oagw`\n \n-**Role**: Executes provider API calls for model discovery and health probes.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Executes provider API calls for model discovery. Handles credential injection. Model Registry has no knowledge of credentials.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Provider API\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-provider-api`\n \n-**Role**: External provider endpoint that returns available models list and responds to health probes.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: External provider endpoint (OpenAI, Anthropic, Azure, etc.) that returns available models list.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+## 3. Domain Model\n+\n+### 3.1 Core Entities\n+\n+#### Provider\n+\n+Represents a configured AI provider for a tenant.\n+\n+**Fields**: id, tenant_id, name, type (plugin type), base_url, status (active/disabled), discovery config (enabled, interval), timestamps.","path":"modules/model-registry/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"15cb20127bb04236e91a1bb5d1860808534f7815","original_commit_id":"15cb20127bb04236e91a1bb5d1860808534f7815","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I would consider to use GTS type for provider, like `gts.x.genai.model.provider.v1~msft.azure._.ai_studio.v1~`\n\nwhy?\n\n1. we can have custom per-provider versioned metadata schema (settings, notes or even configurations displayable in UI)\n2. we can have vendor and service encoded, so it could be easier to understand what a 'deepseek' provider actually is - like a deepseek as vendor/provider, or deepseek as a service hosted by nvidia, ...\n3. we can use it for access check, e.g. grant/revoke access to azure model traffic natively\n4. we can use <vendor>.<package> to see what other artifacts an integration with <vendor> (<provider>) required, so that you can see all the different types in a common place. It would be easier to add/cleanup/upgrade all the per-vendor artifacts\n\nI'd expect the number of providers to grow so GTS would help to build proper lifecycle","created_at":"2026-02-17T21:11:43Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T21:27:16Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2819107825","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819107825"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2819107825"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819107825/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":153,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":173,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819130586","pull_request_review_id":3816165818,"id":2819130586,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6oCITa","diff_hunk":"@@ -37,217 +104,1036 @@ The registry supports automatic model discovery from providers, requiring tenant\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-tenant-admin`\n \n-**Role**: Approves or rejects models for tenant access. Configures auto-approval policies per provider.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Approves or rejects models for tenant access. Manages tenant-specific providers. Can only restrict access compared to parent tenant, not expand.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Platform Administrator\n+\n+**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-platform-admin`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Manages root tenant configuration. Configures global providers. Sets baseline that all tenants inherit.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n ### 2.2 System Actors\n \n #### LLM Gateway\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-llm-gateway`\n \n-**Role**: Queries registry to resolve model to provider, check tenant availability, and get model capabilities.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Queries registry to resolve model identifiers (canonical ID) to provider details. Checks tenant availability. Retrieves model capabilities and pricing.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Outbound API Gateway\n \n-**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-outbound-api-gateway`\n+**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-oagw`\n \n-**Role**: Executes provider API calls for model discovery and health probes.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Executes provider API calls for model discovery. Handles credential injection. Model Registry has no knowledge of credentials.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Provider API\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-provider-api`\n \n-**Role**: External provider endpoint that returns available models list and responds to health probes.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: External provider endpoint (OpenAI, Anthropic, Azure, etc.) that returns available models list.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+## 3. Domain Model\n+\n+### 3.1 Core Entities\n+\n+#### Provider\n+\n+Represents a configured AI provider for a tenant.\n+\n+**Fields**: id, tenant_id, name, type (plugin type), base_url, status (active/disabled), discovery config (enabled, interval), timestamps.\n+\n+**Inheritance**: Providers inherit down tenant hierarchy (additive only). Child tenant sees parent's providers + own. Child cannot hide inherited providers.\n+\n+**Health**: ProviderHealth stored at provider's owner tenant only. Child tenants inherit health status from parent.\n+\n+#### Model\n+\n+Represents an AI model in the catalog.\n+\n+**Fields**:\n+- **Identification**: canonical_id (`{provider}::{provider_model_id}`), provider_id, tenant_id, provider_model_id\n+- **Display**: name, description\n+- **Capabilities (Tier 1)**: Boolean flags for text/image/audio/video/document input/output, tools, structured_output, streaming, embeddings, realtime_audio, batch_api\n+- **Limits (Tier 2)**: context_window, max_output_tokens, max_images_per_request, max_image_size_mb, max_audio_duration_sec\n+- **Pricing**: AICredits per tier (sync/batch/cached) for input/output tokens and media (base pricing only)\n+- **Status**: active, deprecated (soft-delete with deprecated_at timestamp)\n+- **Version**: Provider's model version, stored as-is","path":"modules/model-registry/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"49408257b07b88ae694cb12f7e728b684041d575","original_commit_id":"15cb20127bb04236e91a1bb5d1860808534f7815","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I'd add all the potentially discoverable common fields, like:\n- lifecycle_status - production, experimental, preview, deprecated, sunset (i'd make it as GTS types to simplify access to experimental models - it would be enough just to check GTS claim in the the token to check if given category of models can be accessed)\n- managed true/false (to see if CyberFabric can load/unload this model)\n- architecture (e.g. qwen)\n- size (bytes)\n- max context window\n- format (gguf, mlx, etc)\n\netc.\n\nThe rationale is that for local LLMs it could be critical to discover the models that CAN/CAN NOT be used on given infrastructure, or manage overall capacity","created_at":"2026-02-17T21:17:29Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T21:27:16Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2819130586","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819130586"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2819130586"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819130586/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":209,"original_line":170,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":190,"position":226,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819140069","pull_request_review_id":3816165818,"id":2819140069,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6oCKnl","diff_hunk":"@@ -1,33 +1,100 @@\n-# PRD\n+# PRD: Model Registry\n \n ## 1. Overview\n \n-**Purpose**: Model Registry provides a centralized catalog of AI models with tenant-level availability and approval workflow.\n+**Purpose**: Model Registry provides a centralized catalog of AI models with tenant-level availability and approval workflows.\n \n-Model Registry is the authoritative source for model metadata, capabilities, and tenant access control. It tracks which models are available from which providers, manages approval workflows for new models, and monitors provider health for routing decisions. LLM Gateway queries the registry to resolve model identifiers to provider endpoints and verify tenant access.\n+Model Registry is the authoritative source for model metadata, capabilities, pricing, and tenant access control. It tracks which models are available from which providers and manages approval workflows. LLM Gateway queries the registry to resolve model identifiers to provider endpoints and verify tenant access.\n \n-The registry supports automatic model discovery from providers, requiring tenant admin approval before models become available. It also tracks provider health metrics (latency, error rates) to inform Gateway routing decisions.\n+**Key Concepts**:\n+\n+- **Canonical Model ID**: Deterministic identifier in format `{provider}::{provider_model_id}` (e.g., `openai::gpt-4o`). Parsing rule: split on **first** `::` occurrence.\n+- **Tenant Hierarchy**: Tree structure with root tenant at top; providers and approvals inherit down the tree (additive only)\n+- **Provider Plugins**: Each provider type has its own plugin; all requests route through Outbound API Gateway\n \n **Target Users**:\n-- **LLM Gateway** - Primary consumer for model resolution and availability checks\n-- **Tenant Administrators** - Approve/reject models for their tenant\n+\n+- **LLM Gateway** — Primary consumer for model resolution and availability checks\n+- **Tenant Administrators** — Approve/reject models, manage tenant-specific providers\n+- **Platform Administrators** — Configure root tenant providers\n \n **Key Problems Solved**:\n+\n - **Model discovery**: Automatic polling of provider APIs to discover available models\n-- **Access control**: Tenant-level approval workflow for model access\n-- **Health tracking**: Provider health metrics for intelligent routing\n+- **Unified identification**: Canonical IDs abstract provider-specific naming\n+- **Access control**: Tenant-level approval workflow with hierarchical inheritance\n+- **Pricing normalization**: AICredits-based pricing with tier support (sync/batch/cached)\n \n **Success Criteria**:\n-- All scenarios (S1-S6) implemented and operational\n-- Model resolution latency < 10ms P99\n-- Provider health status updated within health check interval\n \n-**Capabilities**:\n-- Model catalog management\n-- Tenant-level model availability\n-- Model approval workflow\n-- Provider health monitoring\n-- Model capability and pricing metadata\n+- Model resolution latency < 10ms P99\n+- 99.9% availability\n+\n+### 1.1 Background\n+\n+LLM Gateway requires a centralized source of truth for model availability, capabilities, and pricing. Without Model Registry, each consumer would need to maintain its own model catalog, leading to inconsistency and duplicated approval workflows.\n+\n+### 1.2 Goals\n+\n+1. Single source of truth for AI model metadata across the platform","path":"modules/model-registry/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"15cb20127bb04236e91a1bb5d1860808534f7815","original_commit_id":"15cb20127bb04236e91a1bb5d1860808534f7815","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":".. including unmanaged models (e.g. cloud, frontier models) and managed models (local, self-hosted)","created_at":"2026-02-17T21:20:10Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T21:27:16Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2819140069","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819140069"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2819140069"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819140069/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":39,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":56,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819152377","pull_request_review_id":3816165818,"id":2819152377,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6oCNn5","diff_hunk":"@@ -37,217 +104,1036 @@ The registry supports automatic model discovery from providers, requiring tenant\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-tenant-admin`\n \n-**Role**: Approves or rejects models for tenant access. Configures auto-approval policies per provider.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Approves or rejects models for tenant access. Manages tenant-specific providers. Can only restrict access compared to parent tenant, not expand.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Platform Administrator\n+\n+**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-platform-admin`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Manages root tenant configuration. Configures global providers. Sets baseline that all tenants inherit.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n ### 2.2 System Actors\n \n #### LLM Gateway\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-llm-gateway`\n \n-**Role**: Queries registry to resolve model to provider, check tenant availability, and get model capabilities.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Queries registry to resolve model identifiers (canonical ID) to provider details. Checks tenant availability. Retrieves model capabilities and pricing.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Outbound API Gateway\n \n-**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-outbound-api-gateway`\n+**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-oagw`\n \n-**Role**: Executes provider API calls for model discovery and health probes.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Executes provider API calls for model discovery. Handles credential injection. Model Registry has no knowledge of credentials.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Provider API\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-provider-api`\n \n-**Role**: External provider endpoint that returns available models list and responds to health probes.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: External provider endpoint (OpenAI, Anthropic, Azure, etc.) that returns available models list.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+## 3. Domain Model\n+\n+### 3.1 Core Entities\n+\n+#### Provider\n+\n+Represents a configured AI provider for a tenant.\n+\n+**Fields**: id, tenant_id, name, type (plugin type), base_url, status (active/disabled), discovery config (enabled, interval), timestamps.\n+\n+**Inheritance**: Providers inherit down tenant hierarchy (additive only). Child tenant sees parent's providers + own. Child cannot hide inherited providers.\n+\n+**Health**: ProviderHealth stored at provider's owner tenant only. Child tenants inherit health status from parent.\n+\n+#### Model\n+\n+Represents an AI model in the catalog.\n+\n+**Fields**:\n+- **Identification**: canonical_id (`{provider}::{provider_model_id}`), provider_id, tenant_id, provider_model_id\n+- **Display**: name, description\n+- **Capabilities (Tier 1)**: Boolean flags for text/image/audio/video/document input/output, tools, structured_output, streaming, embeddings, realtime_audio, batch_api\n+- **Limits (Tier 2)**: context_window, max_output_tokens, max_images_per_request, max_image_size_mb, max_audio_duration_sec\n+- **Pricing**: AICredits per tier (sync/batch/cached) for input/output tokens and media (base pricing only)\n+- **Status**: active, deprecated (soft-delete with deprecated_at timestamp)\n+- **Version**: Provider's model version, stored as-is\n+\n+#### ModelApproval\n+\n+Tracks tenant approval status for a model.\n+\n+**Fields**: id, model_canonical_id, tenant_id, status (pending/approved/rejected/revoked), approved_at, approved_by, auto_approval_rule_id (reference to rule that triggered auto-approval, null for manual), rejected_at, rejected_by, revoked_at, revoked_by, timestamps.\n+\n+**Concurrency**: First write wins - once status changes from `pending`, subsequent approve/reject requests are rejected.\n+\n+**State Machine**:\n+\n+```mermaid\n+stateDiagram-v2\n+    [*] --> pending: Model discovered\n+    pending --> approved: Admin approves\n+    pending --> approved: Auto-approval rule matches\n+    pending --> rejected: Admin rejects\n+    approved --> revoked: Admin revokes\n+    rejected --> approved: Admin reconsiders\n+    revoked --> approved: Admin reinstates\n+```\n+\n+#### AutoApprovalRule (P2)\n+\n+Defines rules for automatic model approval.\n+\n+**Fields**: id, tenant_id (root = platform-wide), criteria, action (allow/block), priority, created_at, created_by.\n+\n+**Criteria schema**:\n+- `provider_type`: string | \"*\" (required, \"*\" = any)\n+- `provider_id`: string | \"*\" (required, \"*\" = any)\n+- `capabilities`: string[] (optional, empty = any)\n+\n+**Matching**: ALL criteria must match (AND). Model must have ALL listed capabilities (subset matching).\n+\n+**Rule evaluation**:\n+- Platform (root tenant) rules set the ceiling\n+- Tenant rules can only restrict further, not expand\n+- `block` from platform = blocked for all descendants\n+- Tenant cannot `allow` what platform blocked\n \n-## 3. Functional Requirements\n+**Authorization**: Read/list visible to tenant admins only.\n+\n+#### ProviderHealth (P2)\n+\n+Tracks provider health status from synthetic probes.\n+","path":"modules/model-registry/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"49408257b07b88ae694cb12f7e728b684041d575","original_commit_id":"15cb20127bb04236e91a1bb5d1860808534f7815","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"also, status can vary based on link/route, that is not under Model Registry responsibility. For me it's more like OAGW responsibility to maintain links status. I'd make Model Registry to be responsible only for the registry, while connectivity and availability is out of scope.\n\nWhy?\n\nBecause single provider/location/model pair can have different availability and SLA metrics depending on route or per-tenant API key.","created_at":"2026-02-17T21:23:26Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T21:27:16Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2819152377","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819152377"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2819152377"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819152377/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":288,"original_line":217,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":238,"position":305,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819174435","pull_request_review_id":3816402132,"id":2819174435,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6oCTAj","diff_hunk":"@@ -1,33 +1,100 @@\n-# PRD\n+# PRD: Model Registry\n \n ## 1. Overview\n \n-**Purpose**: Model Registry provides a centralized catalog of AI models with tenant-level availability and approval workflow.\n+**Purpose**: Model Registry provides a centralized catalog of AI models with tenant-level availability and approval workflows.\n \n-Model Registry is the authoritative source for model metadata, capabilities, and tenant access control. It tracks which models are available from which providers, manages approval workflows for new models, and monitors provider health for routing decisions. LLM Gateway queries the registry to resolve model identifiers to provider endpoints and verify tenant access.\n+Model Registry is the authoritative source for model metadata, capabilities, pricing, and tenant access control. It tracks which models are available from which providers and manages approval workflows. LLM Gateway queries the registry to resolve model identifiers to provider endpoints and verify tenant access.\n \n-The registry supports automatic model discovery from providers, requiring tenant admin approval before models become available. It also tracks provider health metrics (latency, error rates) to inform Gateway routing decisions.\n+**Key Concepts**:\n+\n+- **Canonical Model ID**: Deterministic identifier in format `{provider}::{provider_model_id}` (e.g., `openai::gpt-4o`). Parsing rule: split on **first** `::` occurrence.\n+- **Tenant Hierarchy**: Tree structure with root tenant at top; providers and approvals inherit down the tree (additive only)\n+- **Provider Plugins**: Each provider type has its own plugin; all requests route through Outbound API Gateway\n \n **Target Users**:\n-- **LLM Gateway** - Primary consumer for model resolution and availability checks\n-- **Tenant Administrators** - Approve/reject models for their tenant\n+\n+- **LLM Gateway** — Primary consumer for model resolution and availability checks\n+- **Tenant Administrators** — Approve/reject models, manage tenant-specific providers\n+- **Platform Administrators** — Configure root tenant providers\n \n **Key Problems Solved**:\n+\n - **Model discovery**: Automatic polling of provider APIs to discover available models\n-- **Access control**: Tenant-level approval workflow for model access\n-- **Health tracking**: Provider health metrics for intelligent routing\n+- **Unified identification**: Canonical IDs abstract provider-specific naming\n+- **Access control**: Tenant-level approval workflow with hierarchical inheritance\n+- **Pricing normalization**: AICredits-based pricing with tier support (sync/batch/cached)\n \n **Success Criteria**:\n-- All scenarios (S1-S6) implemented and operational\n-- Model resolution latency < 10ms P99\n-- Provider health status updated within health check interval\n \n-**Capabilities**:\n-- Model catalog management\n-- Tenant-level model availability\n-- Model approval workflow\n-- Provider health monitoring\n-- Model capability and pricing metadata\n+- Model resolution latency < 10ms P99\n+- 99.9% availability\n+\n+### 1.1 Background\n+\n+LLM Gateway requires a centralized source of truth for model availability, capabilities, and pricing. Without Model Registry, each consumer would need to maintain its own model catalog, leading to inconsistency and duplicated approval workflows.\n+\n+### 1.2 Goals\n+\n+1. Single source of truth for AI model metadata across the platform\n+2. Tenant-controlled model availability with inheritance from parent tenants\n+3. Streamlined approval process\n+\n+### 1.3 Scope\n+\n+#### In Scope\n+\n+- Model catalog CRUD (models, providers)\n+- Tenant-level model availability configuration\n+- Approval workflows (request → approve/reject)","path":"modules/model-registry/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"49408257b07b88ae694cb12f7e728b684041d575","original_commit_id":"15cb20127bb04236e91a1bb5d1860808534f7815","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I'd make Approval workflow service generic. So you could just implement approvals for any resource. It could be pretty sophisticated service actually in the future, while Model Registry can remain stable as it could be just CRUD with minimal logic.","created_at":"2026-02-17T21:29:38Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T21:39:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2819174435","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819174435"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2819174435"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819174435/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":69,"original_line":49,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":66,"position":86,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819195152","pull_request_review_id":3816402132,"id":2819195152,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6oCYEQ","diff_hunk":"@@ -37,217 +104,1036 @@ The registry supports automatic model discovery from providers, requiring tenant\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-tenant-admin`\n \n-**Role**: Approves or rejects models for tenant access. Configures auto-approval policies per provider.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Approves or rejects models for tenant access. Manages tenant-specific providers. Can only restrict access compared to parent tenant, not expand.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Platform Administrator\n+\n+**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-platform-admin`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Manages root tenant configuration. Configures global providers. Sets baseline that all tenants inherit.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n ### 2.2 System Actors\n \n #### LLM Gateway\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-llm-gateway`\n \n-**Role**: Queries registry to resolve model to provider, check tenant availability, and get model capabilities.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Queries registry to resolve model identifiers (canonical ID) to provider details. Checks tenant availability. Retrieves model capabilities and pricing.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Outbound API Gateway\n \n-**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-outbound-api-gateway`\n+**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-oagw`\n \n-**Role**: Executes provider API calls for model discovery and health probes.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Executes provider API calls for model discovery. Handles credential injection. Model Registry has no knowledge of credentials.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Provider API\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-provider-api`\n \n-**Role**: External provider endpoint that returns available models list and responds to health probes.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: External provider endpoint (OpenAI, Anthropic, Azure, etc.) that returns available models list.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+## 3. Domain Model\n+\n+### 3.1 Core Entities\n+\n+#### Provider\n+\n+Represents a configured AI provider for a tenant.\n+\n+**Fields**: id, tenant_id, name, type (plugin type), base_url, status (active/disabled), discovery config (enabled, interval), timestamps.\n+\n+**Inheritance**: Providers inherit down tenant hierarchy (additive only). Child tenant sees parent's providers + own. Child cannot hide inherited providers.","path":"modules/model-registry/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"15cb20127bb04236e91a1bb5d1860808534f7815","original_commit_id":"15cb20127bb04236e91a1bb5d1860808534f7815","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I think we need an ability to exclude providers on child tenant level (by it's admins) because big partners may have their own policies regarding vendor partnership, liability cap, region restrictions, compliance isolation","created_at":"2026-02-17T21:35:43Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T21:39:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2819195152","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819195152"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2819195152"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819195152/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":155,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":175,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819215814","pull_request_review_id":3816447676,"id":2819215814,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6oCdHG","diff_hunk":"@@ -37,217 +104,1036 @@ The registry supports automatic model discovery from providers, requiring tenant\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-tenant-admin`\n \n-**Role**: Approves or rejects models for tenant access. Configures auto-approval policies per provider.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Approves or rejects models for tenant access. Manages tenant-specific providers. Can only restrict access compared to parent tenant, not expand.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Platform Administrator\n+\n+**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-platform-admin`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Manages root tenant configuration. Configures global providers. Sets baseline that all tenants inherit.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n ### 2.2 System Actors\n \n #### LLM Gateway\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-llm-gateway`\n \n-**Role**: Queries registry to resolve model to provider, check tenant availability, and get model capabilities.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Queries registry to resolve model identifiers (canonical ID) to provider details. Checks tenant availability. Retrieves model capabilities and pricing.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Outbound API Gateway\n \n-**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-outbound-api-gateway`\n+**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-oagw`\n \n-**Role**: Executes provider API calls for model discovery and health probes.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Executes provider API calls for model discovery. Handles credential injection. Model Registry has no knowledge of credentials.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Provider API\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-provider-api`\n \n-**Role**: External provider endpoint that returns available models list and responds to health probes.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: External provider endpoint (OpenAI, Anthropic, Azure, etc.) that returns available models list.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+## 3. Domain Model\n+\n+### 3.1 Core Entities\n+\n+#### Provider\n+\n+Represents a configured AI provider for a tenant.\n+\n+**Fields**: id, tenant_id, name, type (plugin type), base_url, status (active/disabled), discovery config (enabled, interval), timestamps.\n+\n+**Inheritance**: Providers inherit down tenant hierarchy (additive only). Child tenant sees parent's providers + own. Child cannot hide inherited providers.\n+\n+**Health**: ProviderHealth stored at provider's owner tenant only. Child tenants inherit health status from parent.\n+\n+#### Model\n+\n+Represents an AI model in the catalog.\n+\n+**Fields**:\n+- **Identification**: canonical_id (`{provider}::{provider_model_id}`), provider_id, tenant_id, provider_model_id\n+- **Display**: name, description\n+- **Capabilities (Tier 1)**: Boolean flags for text/image/audio/video/document input/output, tools, structured_output, streaming, embeddings, realtime_audio, batch_api\n+- **Limits (Tier 2)**: context_window, max_output_tokens, max_images_per_request, max_image_size_mb, max_audio_duration_sec\n+- **Pricing**: AICredits per tier (sync/batch/cached) for input/output tokens and media (base pricing only)\n+- **Status**: active, deprecated (soft-delete with deprecated_at timestamp)\n+- **Version**: Provider's model version, stored as-is\n+\n+#### ModelApproval\n+\n+Tracks tenant approval status for a model.\n+\n+**Fields**: id, model_canonical_id, tenant_id, status (pending/approved/rejected/revoked), approved_at, approved_by, auto_approval_rule_id (reference to rule that triggered auto-approval, null for manual), rejected_at, rejected_by, revoked_at, revoked_by, timestamps.\n+\n+**Concurrency**: First write wins - once status changes from `pending`, subsequent approve/reject requests are rejected.\n+\n+**State Machine**:\n+\n+```mermaid\n+stateDiagram-v2\n+    [*] --> pending: Model discovered\n+    pending --> approved: Admin approves\n+    pending --> approved: Auto-approval rule matches\n+    pending --> rejected: Admin rejects\n+    approved --> revoked: Admin revokes\n+    rejected --> approved: Admin reconsiders\n+    revoked --> approved: Admin reinstates\n+```\n+\n+#### AutoApprovalRule (P2)\n+\n+Defines rules for automatic model approval.\n+\n+**Fields**: id, tenant_id (root = platform-wide), criteria, action (allow/block), priority, created_at, created_by.\n+\n+**Criteria schema**:\n+- `provider_type`: string | \"*\" (required, \"*\" = any)\n+- `provider_id`: string | \"*\" (required, \"*\" = any)\n+- `capabilities`: string[] (optional, empty = any)\n+\n+**Matching**: ALL criteria must match (AND). Model must have ALL listed capabilities (subset matching).\n+\n+**Rule evaluation**:\n+- Platform (root tenant) rules set the ceiling\n+- Tenant rules can only restrict further, not expand\n+- `block` from platform = blocked for all descendants\n+- Tenant cannot `allow` what platform blocked\n \n-## 3. Functional Requirements\n+**Authorization**: Read/list visible to tenant admins only.\n+\n+#### ProviderHealth (P2)\n+\n+Tracks provider health status from synthetic probes.\n+\n+**Fields**: provider_id, tenant_id, status (healthy/degraded/unhealthy), metrics (latency p50/p99, consecutive failures/successes), last_check, last_success, last_error, last_error_message.\n+\n+**Status thresholds**:\n+- `unhealthy`: 3+ consecutive failures\n+- `degraded`: response latency > 2000ms\n+- `healthy`: 2+ consecutive successes, latency OK\n+\n+**Authorization**: `status` field visible to all authenticated users. Error details (`last_error_message`, `last_error`) visible to tenant admins only.\n+\n+#### Alias (P2)\n+\n+Maps human-friendly names to canonical model IDs.\n+\n+**Fields**: name (1-64 chars, alphanumeric + hyphen/underscore), tenant_id, canonical_id (must be canonical ID, not another alias), created_at, created_by.\n+\n+**Resolution order**: Tenant alias → Parent tenant alias → ... → Root tenant alias → Canonical ID\n+\n+**Shadowing**: Child tenant aliases can shadow parent aliases. Child tenant controls their namespace.\n+\n+## 4. Functional Requirements\n+\n+### P1 — Core (MVP)\n+\n+#### Tenant Isolation\n+\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-tenant-isolation`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must enforce tenant isolation for all operations.\n+\n+- All API operations MUST include tenant context\n+- Model/Approval queries MUST filter by tenant hierarchy (current tenant + ancestors)\n+- Write operations MUST validate tenant ownership\n+- Admin operations (approve/reject) MUST verify actor has admin role for target tenant\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Authorization\n+\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-authorization`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must enforce role-based authorization.\n+\n+| Operation | Required Role |\n+|-----------|---------------|\n+| List/Get models | Any authenticated user |\n+| Request model approval | Tenant member |\n+| Approve/Reject request | Tenant admin |\n+| Manage providers | Platform admin (root tenant) |\n+\n+**Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-tenant-admin`, `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-platform-admin`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Input Validation\n+\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-input-validation`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must validate all input data.\n+\n+| Field | Validation |\n+|-------|------------|\n+| Canonical ID | Must match pattern `{provider}::{model_id}`, provider must exist. Parse on first `::`. |\n+| Provider name | 1-32 chars, lowercase alphanumeric + hyphen |\n+| Capabilities | Must conform to GTS capability schema |\n+| Pricing values | Non-negative decimal (AICredits) |\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Cache Isolation\n+\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-cache-isolation`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must isolate cached data by tenant.\n+\n+Cache keys MUST include tenant_id as prefix.\n+\n+Format: `mr:{tenant_id}:{entity}:{id}`\n+\n+**TTL strategy**:\n+- Own data (tenant created): TTL 30 min\n+- Inherited data (from parent): TTL 5 min\n+\n+**Cache invalidation on tenant re-parenting**: On `tenant.reparented` event, invalidate ALL cache entries for that tenant.\n+\n+**Redis unavailable**: Fallback to direct DB queries (latency SLOs may be violated).\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Get Tenant Model\n \n-- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-get-tenant-model-v1`\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-get-tenant-model`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must resolve a canonical model ID for a tenant, returning model info and provider details if approved.\n+\n+Resolution:\n+1. Look up model in catalog by canonical ID\n+2. Check tenant approval status (direct or inherited)\n+3. Return model info + provider details\n \n-The system must resolve model availability for a tenant, returning model info and provider details if approved.\n+Response structure defined in GTS contract.\n \n **Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-llm-gateway`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### List Tenant Models\n \n-- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-list-tenant-models-v1`\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-list-tenant-models`\n \n-The system must return all models available for a tenant, supporting filtering by capability and provider.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must return all models available for a tenant.\n+\n+Includes:\n+- Models from tenant's own providers (if approved)\n+- Models inherited from parent tenant hierarchy (if approved at any level)\n+\n+Follows OData pagination standard. Supports OData `$filter` for filtering by capability, provider, approval_status.\n+\n+Capability filtering uses subset matching: model must have AT LEAST requested capabilities.\n \n **Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-llm-gateway`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Model Discovery\n \n-- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-model-discovery-v1`\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-model-discovery`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must periodically poll providers for available models via Outbound API Gateway.\n+\n+**Scheduling**: Fixed concurrency limit + staggered intervals across (tenant, provider) pairs.\n \n-The system must poll providers for available models via Outbound API Gateway, upserting new models and creating pending approvals.\n+Per (tenant, provider) pair where discovery is enabled:\n+- Fetch models from provider's models endpoint (plugin responsibility)\n+- New models → create with `pending` status\n+- Existing models → update metadata (capabilities, limits, pricing)\n+- Missing models → soft-delete (mark as `deprecated`)\n \n-**Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-outbound-api-gateway`, `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-provider-api`\n+**Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-oagw`, `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-provider-api`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Model Approval\n \n-- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-model-approval-v1`\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-model-approval`\n \n-The system must support model approval workflow with statuses: pending, approved, rejected, revoked. Must support auto-approval configuration per tenant/provider.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must support tenant-level model approval workflow.\n+\n+Approval granularity (P1): Tenant-level — approval grants access to all users in tenant.\n+\n+States: `pending` → `approved` | `rejected`, `approved` → `revoked`, `rejected` → `approved`, `revoked` → `approved`\n+\n+Concurrency: First write wins - once status changes from `pending`, subsequent approve/reject requests are rejected with `invalid_transition` error.\n \n **Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-tenant-admin`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Provider Management\n+\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-provider-management`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must support tenant-scoped provider configuration.\n+\n+Provider inheritance:\n+- Providers inherit down tenant hierarchy (additive only)\n+- Child tenant sees parent's providers + own providers\n+- Child cannot hide or disable inherited providers\n+\n+Provider config:\n+- ID, name, type (plugin), base URL, status (active/disabled)\n+- Discovery enabled/interval\n+\n+Credentials handled by OAGW — not stored in Model Registry.\n+\n+**Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-platform-admin`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Model Pricing\n+\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-model-pricing`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must store and provide model base pricing in AICredits.\n+\n+Pricing structure:\n+- Unit: AICredits (internal platform currency)\n+- Tiers: sync, batch, cached (different rates per tier)\n+- Media: per image input, per audio minute, per image output\n+\n+Model Registry returns **base pricing only**. Caller (LLM Gateway) fetches tenant multiplier from License Manager and computes final price.\n+\n+**Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-llm-gateway`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+### P2 — Enhanced Features\n+\n+#### Auto-Approval Rules\n+\n+- [ ] `p2` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-auto-approval`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must support automatic model approval based on configurable rules.\n+\n+Rule hierarchy:\n+- Platform (root tenant) rules set the ceiling (max allowed)\n+- Tenant rules can only restrict further\n+- Tenant cannot auto-approve what platform blocked\n+\n+Rule matching:\n+- Criteria: provider type, provider ID, required capabilities (all must match)\n+- Action: `allow` or `block`\n+- Priority ordering for conflict resolution\n+\n+Auto-approved models store reference to the triggering rule (`auto_approval_rule_id`).\n+\n+**Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-tenant-admin`, `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-platform-admin`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Provider Health Monitoring\n \n-- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-health-monitoring-v1`\n+- [ ] `p2` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-health-monitoring`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must track provider health via synthetic probes for LLM Gateway routing decisions.\n+\n+Probe method:\n+- Call provider's models endpoint (lightweight, read-only)\n+- Granularity: per provider (not per model)\n+- No actual inference calls (cost concern)\n+\n+Health status:\n+- `healthy`: responding normally, latency acceptable\n+- `degraded`: responding but latency > threshold\n+- `unhealthy`: consecutive failures exceed threshold\n+\n+Health stored at provider owner tenant only. Child tenants inherit parent's health status.\n+\n+**Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-oagw`, `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-provider-api`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Alias Management\n+\n+- [ ] `p2` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-alias-management`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must support model aliases with hierarchical scoping.\n+\n+Alias scope:\n+- Root tenant: global aliases visible to all tenants\n+- Child tenant: can override global aliases, add tenant-specific aliases\n+\n+Resolution order: tenant → parent → ... → root → canonical ID\n+\n+Constraint: Alias target MUST be a canonical ID, not another alias (prevents circular references).\n+\n+**Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-tenant-admin`, `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-platform-admin`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Degraded Mode\n+\n+- [ ] `p2` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-degraded-mode`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must define tiered behavior when database is unavailable.\n \n-The system must track provider health metrics (latency, error rate, availability status) via periodic health probes for LLM Gateway routing decisions.\n+- Model capabilities and metadata: serve from stale cache (up to 30 min TTL)\n+- Approval verification: fail request with `service_unavailable` error\n \n-**Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-outbound-api-gateway`, `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-provider-api`\n+P1 behavior: DB unavailable = all requests fail (fail-closed).\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n-## 4. Use Cases\n+#### Tenant Re-parenting\n \n-#### UC-001: Get Tenant Model\n+- [ ] `p2` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-tenant-reparenting`\n \n-- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-usecase-get-tenant-model-v1`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must handle tenant hierarchy changes.\n+\n+When tenant moves to different parent:\n+- Tenant Resolver owns re-parenting logic\n+- Model Registry invalidates all cache entries for affected tenant on `tenant.reparented` event\n+- Re-evaluation of approvals happens on next access\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->","path":"modules/model-registry/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"15cb20127bb04236e91a1bb5d1860808534f7815","original_commit_id":"15cb20127bb04236e91a1bb5d1860808534f7815","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I believe these `<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->` lines are not needed anywhere anymore","created_at":"2026-02-17T21:41:22Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T21:47:42Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2819215814","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819215814"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2819215814"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819215814/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":501,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":537,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819226770","pull_request_review_id":3816447676,"id":2819226770,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6oCfyS","diff_hunk":"@@ -37,217 +104,1036 @@ The registry supports automatic model discovery from providers, requiring tenant\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-tenant-admin`\n \n-**Role**: Approves or rejects models for tenant access. Configures auto-approval policies per provider.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Approves or rejects models for tenant access. Manages tenant-specific providers. Can only restrict access compared to parent tenant, not expand.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Platform Administrator\n+\n+**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-platform-admin`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Manages root tenant configuration. Configures global providers. Sets baseline that all tenants inherit.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n ### 2.2 System Actors\n \n #### LLM Gateway\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-llm-gateway`\n \n-**Role**: Queries registry to resolve model to provider, check tenant availability, and get model capabilities.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Queries registry to resolve model identifiers (canonical ID) to provider details. Checks tenant availability. Retrieves model capabilities and pricing.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Outbound API Gateway\n \n-**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-outbound-api-gateway`\n+**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-oagw`\n \n-**Role**: Executes provider API calls for model discovery and health probes.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Executes provider API calls for model discovery. Handles credential injection. Model Registry has no knowledge of credentials.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Provider API\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-provider-api`\n \n-**Role**: External provider endpoint that returns available models list and responds to health probes.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: External provider endpoint (OpenAI, Anthropic, Azure, etc.) that returns available models list.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+## 3. Domain Model\n+\n+### 3.1 Core Entities\n+\n+#### Provider\n+\n+Represents a configured AI provider for a tenant.\n+\n+**Fields**: id, tenant_id, name, type (plugin type), base_url, status (active/disabled), discovery config (enabled, interval), timestamps.\n+\n+**Inheritance**: Providers inherit down tenant hierarchy (additive only). Child tenant sees parent's providers + own. Child cannot hide inherited providers.\n+\n+**Health**: ProviderHealth stored at provider's owner tenant only. Child tenants inherit health status from parent.\n+\n+#### Model\n+\n+Represents an AI model in the catalog.\n+\n+**Fields**:\n+- **Identification**: canonical_id (`{provider}::{provider_model_id}`), provider_id, tenant_id, provider_model_id\n+- **Display**: name, description\n+- **Capabilities (Tier 1)**: Boolean flags for text/image/audio/video/document input/output, tools, structured_output, streaming, embeddings, realtime_audio, batch_api\n+- **Limits (Tier 2)**: context_window, max_output_tokens, max_images_per_request, max_image_size_mb, max_audio_duration_sec\n+- **Pricing**: AICredits per tier (sync/batch/cached) for input/output tokens and media (base pricing only)\n+- **Status**: active, deprecated (soft-delete with deprecated_at timestamp)\n+- **Version**: Provider's model version, stored as-is\n+\n+#### ModelApproval\n+\n+Tracks tenant approval status for a model.\n+\n+**Fields**: id, model_canonical_id, tenant_id, status (pending/approved/rejected/revoked), approved_at, approved_by, auto_approval_rule_id (reference to rule that triggered auto-approval, null for manual), rejected_at, rejected_by, revoked_at, revoked_by, timestamps.\n+\n+**Concurrency**: First write wins - once status changes from `pending`, subsequent approve/reject requests are rejected.\n+\n+**State Machine**:\n+\n+```mermaid\n+stateDiagram-v2\n+    [*] --> pending: Model discovered\n+    pending --> approved: Admin approves\n+    pending --> approved: Auto-approval rule matches\n+    pending --> rejected: Admin rejects\n+    approved --> revoked: Admin revokes\n+    rejected --> approved: Admin reconsiders\n+    revoked --> approved: Admin reinstates\n+```\n+\n+#### AutoApprovalRule (P2)\n+\n+Defines rules for automatic model approval.\n+\n+**Fields**: id, tenant_id (root = platform-wide), criteria, action (allow/block), priority, created_at, created_by.\n+\n+**Criteria schema**:\n+- `provider_type`: string | \"*\" (required, \"*\" = any)\n+- `provider_id`: string | \"*\" (required, \"*\" = any)\n+- `capabilities`: string[] (optional, empty = any)\n+\n+**Matching**: ALL criteria must match (AND). Model must have ALL listed capabilities (subset matching).\n+\n+**Rule evaluation**:\n+- Platform (root tenant) rules set the ceiling\n+- Tenant rules can only restrict further, not expand\n+- `block` from platform = blocked for all descendants\n+- Tenant cannot `allow` what platform blocked\n \n-## 3. Functional Requirements\n+**Authorization**: Read/list visible to tenant admins only.\n+\n+#### ProviderHealth (P2)\n+\n+Tracks provider health status from synthetic probes.\n+\n+**Fields**: provider_id, tenant_id, status (healthy/degraded/unhealthy), metrics (latency p50/p99, consecutive failures/successes), last_check, last_success, last_error, last_error_message.\n+\n+**Status thresholds**:\n+- `unhealthy`: 3+ consecutive failures\n+- `degraded`: response latency > 2000ms\n+- `healthy`: 2+ consecutive successes, latency OK\n+\n+**Authorization**: `status` field visible to all authenticated users. Error details (`last_error_message`, `last_error`) visible to tenant admins only.\n+\n+#### Alias (P2)\n+\n+Maps human-friendly names to canonical model IDs.\n+\n+**Fields**: name (1-64 chars, alphanumeric + hyphen/underscore), tenant_id, canonical_id (must be canonical ID, not another alias), created_at, created_by.\n+\n+**Resolution order**: Tenant alias → Parent tenant alias → ... → Root tenant alias → Canonical ID\n+\n+**Shadowing**: Child tenant aliases can shadow parent aliases. Child tenant controls their namespace.\n+\n+## 4. Functional Requirements\n+\n+### P1 — Core (MVP)\n+\n+#### Tenant Isolation\n+\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-tenant-isolation`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must enforce tenant isolation for all operations.\n+\n+- All API operations MUST include tenant context\n+- Model/Approval queries MUST filter by tenant hierarchy (current tenant + ancestors)\n+- Write operations MUST validate tenant ownership\n+- Admin operations (approve/reject) MUST verify actor has admin role for target tenant\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Authorization\n+\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-authorization`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must enforce role-based authorization.\n+\n+| Operation | Required Role |\n+|-----------|---------------|\n+| List/Get models | Any authenticated user |\n+| Request model approval | Tenant member |\n+| Approve/Reject request | Tenant admin |\n+| Manage providers | Platform admin (root tenant) |\n+\n+**Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-tenant-admin`, `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-platform-admin`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Input Validation\n+\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-input-validation`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must validate all input data.\n+\n+| Field | Validation |\n+|-------|------------|\n+| Canonical ID | Must match pattern `{provider}::{model_id}`, provider must exist. Parse on first `::`. |\n+| Provider name | 1-32 chars, lowercase alphanumeric + hyphen |\n+| Capabilities | Must conform to GTS capability schema |\n+| Pricing values | Non-negative decimal (AICredits) |\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Cache Isolation\n+\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-cache-isolation`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must isolate cached data by tenant.\n+\n+Cache keys MUST include tenant_id as prefix.\n+\n+Format: `mr:{tenant_id}:{entity}:{id}`\n+\n+**TTL strategy**:\n+- Own data (tenant created): TTL 30 min\n+- Inherited data (from parent): TTL 5 min\n+\n+**Cache invalidation on tenant re-parenting**: On `tenant.reparented` event, invalidate ALL cache entries for that tenant.\n+\n+**Redis unavailable**: Fallback to direct DB queries (latency SLOs may be violated).\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Get Tenant Model\n \n-- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-get-tenant-model-v1`\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-get-tenant-model`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must resolve a canonical model ID for a tenant, returning model info and provider details if approved.\n+\n+Resolution:\n+1. Look up model in catalog by canonical ID\n+2. Check tenant approval status (direct or inherited)\n+3. Return model info + provider details\n \n-The system must resolve model availability for a tenant, returning model info and provider details if approved.\n+Response structure defined in GTS contract.\n \n **Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-llm-gateway`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### List Tenant Models\n \n-- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-list-tenant-models-v1`\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-list-tenant-models`\n \n-The system must return all models available for a tenant, supporting filtering by capability and provider.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must return all models available for a tenant.\n+\n+Includes:\n+- Models from tenant's own providers (if approved)\n+- Models inherited from parent tenant hierarchy (if approved at any level)\n+\n+Follows OData pagination standard. Supports OData `$filter` for filtering by capability, provider, approval_status.\n+\n+Capability filtering uses subset matching: model must have AT LEAST requested capabilities.\n \n **Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-llm-gateway`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Model Discovery\n \n-- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-model-discovery-v1`\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-model-discovery`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must periodically poll providers for available models via Outbound API Gateway.\n+\n+**Scheduling**: Fixed concurrency limit + staggered intervals across (tenant, provider) pairs.\n \n-The system must poll providers for available models via Outbound API Gateway, upserting new models and creating pending approvals.\n+Per (tenant, provider) pair where discovery is enabled:\n+- Fetch models from provider's models endpoint (plugin responsibility)\n+- New models → create with `pending` status\n+- Existing models → update metadata (capabilities, limits, pricing)\n+- Missing models → soft-delete (mark as `deprecated`)\n \n-**Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-outbound-api-gateway`, `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-provider-api`\n+**Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-oagw`, `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-provider-api`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Model Approval\n \n-- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-model-approval-v1`\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-model-approval`\n \n-The system must support model approval workflow with statuses: pending, approved, rejected, revoked. Must support auto-approval configuration per tenant/provider.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must support tenant-level model approval workflow.\n+\n+Approval granularity (P1): Tenant-level — approval grants access to all users in tenant.\n+\n+States: `pending` → `approved` | `rejected`, `approved` → `revoked`, `rejected` → `approved`, `revoked` → `approved`\n+\n+Concurrency: First write wins - once status changes from `pending`, subsequent approve/reject requests are rejected with `invalid_transition` error.\n \n **Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-tenant-admin`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Provider Management\n+\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-provider-management`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must support tenant-scoped provider configuration.\n+\n+Provider inheritance:\n+- Providers inherit down tenant hierarchy (additive only)\n+- Child tenant sees parent's providers + own providers\n+- Child cannot hide or disable inherited providers\n+\n+Provider config:\n+- ID, name, type (plugin), base URL, status (active/disabled)\n+- Discovery enabled/interval\n+\n+Credentials handled by OAGW — not stored in Model Registry.\n+\n+**Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-platform-admin`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Model Pricing\n+\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-model-pricing`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must store and provide model base pricing in AICredits.\n+\n+Pricing structure:\n+- Unit: AICredits (internal platform currency)\n+- Tiers: sync, batch, cached (different rates per tier)\n+- Media: per image input, per audio minute, per image output\n+\n+Model Registry returns **base pricing only**. Caller (LLM Gateway) fetches tenant multiplier from License Manager and computes final price.\n+\n+**Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-llm-gateway`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+### P2 — Enhanced Features\n+\n+#### Auto-Approval Rules\n+\n+- [ ] `p2` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-auto-approval`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must support automatic model approval based on configurable rules.\n+\n+Rule hierarchy:\n+- Platform (root tenant) rules set the ceiling (max allowed)\n+- Tenant rules can only restrict further\n+- Tenant cannot auto-approve what platform blocked\n+\n+Rule matching:\n+- Criteria: provider type, provider ID, required capabilities (all must match)\n+- Action: `allow` or `block`\n+- Priority ordering for conflict resolution\n+\n+Auto-approved models store reference to the triggering rule (`auto_approval_rule_id`).\n+\n+**Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-tenant-admin`, `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-platform-admin`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Provider Health Monitoring\n \n-- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-health-monitoring-v1`\n+- [ ] `p2` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-health-monitoring`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must track provider health via synthetic probes for LLM Gateway routing decisions.\n+\n+Probe method:\n+- Call provider's models endpoint (lightweight, read-only)\n+- Granularity: per provider (not per model)\n+- No actual inference calls (cost concern)\n+\n+Health status:\n+- `healthy`: responding normally, latency acceptable\n+- `degraded`: responding but latency > threshold\n+- `unhealthy`: consecutive failures exceed threshold\n+\n+Health stored at provider owner tenant only. Child tenants inherit parent's health status.\n+\n+**Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-oagw`, `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-provider-api`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Alias Management\n+\n+- [ ] `p2` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-alias-management`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must support model aliases with hierarchical scoping.\n+\n+Alias scope:\n+- Root tenant: global aliases visible to all tenants\n+- Child tenant: can override global aliases, add tenant-specific aliases\n+\n+Resolution order: tenant → parent → ... → root → canonical ID\n+\n+Constraint: Alias target MUST be a canonical ID, not another alias (prevents circular references).\n+\n+**Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-tenant-admin`, `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-platform-admin`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Degraded Mode\n+\n+- [ ] `p2` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-degraded-mode`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must define tiered behavior when database is unavailable.\n \n-The system must track provider health metrics (latency, error rate, availability status) via periodic health probes for LLM Gateway routing decisions.\n+- Model capabilities and metadata: serve from stale cache (up to 30 min TTL)\n+- Approval verification: fail request with `service_unavailable` error\n \n-**Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-outbound-api-gateway`, `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-provider-api`\n+P1 behavior: DB unavailable = all requests fail (fail-closed).\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n-## 4. Use Cases\n+#### Tenant Re-parenting\n \n-#### UC-001: Get Tenant Model\n+- [ ] `p2` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-tenant-reparenting`\n \n-- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-usecase-get-tenant-model-v1`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must handle tenant hierarchy changes.\n+\n+When tenant moves to different parent:\n+- Tenant Resolver owns re-parenting logic\n+- Model Registry invalidates all cache entries for affected tenant on `tenant.reparented` event\n+- Re-evaluation of approvals happens on next access\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Bulk Operations\n+\n+- [ ] `p2` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-bulk-operations`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must support batch approval operations: `approve_models(model_ids[])`, `reject_models(model_ids[])`.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Manual Discovery/Probe Trigger\n+\n+- [ ] `p2` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-manual-trigger`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must allow platform admins to manually trigger discovery and health probes.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+### P3 — Fine-Grained Access Control\n+\n+#### User Group Approval\n+\n+- [ ] `p3` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-user-group-approval`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must support model approval scoped to user groups within a tenant.\n+\n+**Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-tenant-admin`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### User-Level Override\n+\n+- [ ] `p3` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-user-level-override`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must support individual user restrictions/allowances for model access.","path":"modules/model-registry/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"49408257b07b88ae694cb12f7e728b684041d575","original_commit_id":"15cb20127bb04236e91a1bb5d1860808534f7815","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I'd also use cheap generic rules:\n- access by provider (GTS)\n- model lifecycle/category type (GTS)\n\nit can increase flexibility at no development cost ","created_at":"2026-02-17T21:44:42Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T21:47:42Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2819226770","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819226770"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2819226770"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819226770/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":611,"original_line":536,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":572,"position":647,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819233139","pull_request_review_id":3816447676,"id":2819233139,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6oChVz","diff_hunk":"@@ -37,217 +104,1036 @@ The registry supports automatic model discovery from providers, requiring tenant\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-tenant-admin`\n \n-**Role**: Approves or rejects models for tenant access. Configures auto-approval policies per provider.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Approves or rejects models for tenant access. Manages tenant-specific providers. Can only restrict access compared to parent tenant, not expand.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Platform Administrator\n+\n+**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-platform-admin`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Manages root tenant configuration. Configures global providers. Sets baseline that all tenants inherit.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n ### 2.2 System Actors\n \n #### LLM Gateway\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-llm-gateway`\n \n-**Role**: Queries registry to resolve model to provider, check tenant availability, and get model capabilities.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Queries registry to resolve model identifiers (canonical ID) to provider details. Checks tenant availability. Retrieves model capabilities and pricing.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Outbound API Gateway\n \n-**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-outbound-api-gateway`\n+**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-oagw`\n \n-**Role**: Executes provider API calls for model discovery and health probes.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Executes provider API calls for model discovery. Handles credential injection. Model Registry has no knowledge of credentials.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Provider API\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-provider-api`\n \n-**Role**: External provider endpoint that returns available models list and responds to health probes.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: External provider endpoint (OpenAI, Anthropic, Azure, etc.) that returns available models list.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+## 3. Domain Model\n+\n+### 3.1 Core Entities\n+\n+#### Provider\n+\n+Represents a configured AI provider for a tenant.\n+\n+**Fields**: id, tenant_id, name, type (plugin type), base_url, status (active/disabled), discovery config (enabled, interval), timestamps.\n+\n+**Inheritance**: Providers inherit down tenant hierarchy (additive only). Child tenant sees parent's providers + own. Child cannot hide inherited providers.\n+\n+**Health**: ProviderHealth stored at provider's owner tenant only. Child tenants inherit health status from parent.\n+\n+#### Model\n+\n+Represents an AI model in the catalog.\n+\n+**Fields**:\n+- **Identification**: canonical_id (`{provider}::{provider_model_id}`), provider_id, tenant_id, provider_model_id\n+- **Display**: name, description\n+- **Capabilities (Tier 1)**: Boolean flags for text/image/audio/video/document input/output, tools, structured_output, streaming, embeddings, realtime_audio, batch_api\n+- **Limits (Tier 2)**: context_window, max_output_tokens, max_images_per_request, max_image_size_mb, max_audio_duration_sec\n+- **Pricing**: AICredits per tier (sync/batch/cached) for input/output tokens and media (base pricing only)\n+- **Status**: active, deprecated (soft-delete with deprecated_at timestamp)\n+- **Version**: Provider's model version, stored as-is\n+\n+#### ModelApproval\n+\n+Tracks tenant approval status for a model.\n+\n+**Fields**: id, model_canonical_id, tenant_id, status (pending/approved/rejected/revoked), approved_at, approved_by, auto_approval_rule_id (reference to rule that triggered auto-approval, null for manual), rejected_at, rejected_by, revoked_at, revoked_by, timestamps.\n+\n+**Concurrency**: First write wins - once status changes from `pending`, subsequent approve/reject requests are rejected.\n+\n+**State Machine**:\n+\n+```mermaid\n+stateDiagram-v2\n+    [*] --> pending: Model discovered\n+    pending --> approved: Admin approves\n+    pending --> approved: Auto-approval rule matches\n+    pending --> rejected: Admin rejects\n+    approved --> revoked: Admin revokes\n+    rejected --> approved: Admin reconsiders\n+    revoked --> approved: Admin reinstates\n+```\n+\n+#### AutoApprovalRule (P2)\n+\n+Defines rules for automatic model approval.\n+\n+**Fields**: id, tenant_id (root = platform-wide), criteria, action (allow/block), priority, created_at, created_by.\n+\n+**Criteria schema**:\n+- `provider_type`: string | \"*\" (required, \"*\" = any)\n+- `provider_id`: string | \"*\" (required, \"*\" = any)\n+- `capabilities`: string[] (optional, empty = any)\n+\n+**Matching**: ALL criteria must match (AND). Model must have ALL listed capabilities (subset matching).\n+\n+**Rule evaluation**:\n+- Platform (root tenant) rules set the ceiling\n+- Tenant rules can only restrict further, not expand\n+- `block` from platform = blocked for all descendants\n+- Tenant cannot `allow` what platform blocked\n \n-## 3. Functional Requirements\n+**Authorization**: Read/list visible to tenant admins only.\n+\n+#### ProviderHealth (P2)\n+\n+Tracks provider health status from synthetic probes.\n+\n+**Fields**: provider_id, tenant_id, status (healthy/degraded/unhealthy), metrics (latency p50/p99, consecutive failures/successes), last_check, last_success, last_error, last_error_message.\n+\n+**Status thresholds**:\n+- `unhealthy`: 3+ consecutive failures\n+- `degraded`: response latency > 2000ms\n+- `healthy`: 2+ consecutive successes, latency OK\n+\n+**Authorization**: `status` field visible to all authenticated users. Error details (`last_error_message`, `last_error`) visible to tenant admins only.\n+\n+#### Alias (P2)\n+\n+Maps human-friendly names to canonical model IDs.\n+\n+**Fields**: name (1-64 chars, alphanumeric + hyphen/underscore), tenant_id, canonical_id (must be canonical ID, not another alias), created_at, created_by.\n+\n+**Resolution order**: Tenant alias → Parent tenant alias → ... → Root tenant alias → Canonical ID\n+\n+**Shadowing**: Child tenant aliases can shadow parent aliases. Child tenant controls their namespace.\n+\n+## 4. Functional Requirements\n+\n+### P1 — Core (MVP)\n+\n+#### Tenant Isolation\n+\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-tenant-isolation`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must enforce tenant isolation for all operations.\n+\n+- All API operations MUST include tenant context\n+- Model/Approval queries MUST filter by tenant hierarchy (current tenant + ancestors)\n+- Write operations MUST validate tenant ownership\n+- Admin operations (approve/reject) MUST verify actor has admin role for target tenant\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Authorization\n+\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-authorization`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must enforce role-based authorization.\n+\n+| Operation | Required Role |\n+|-----------|---------------|\n+| List/Get models | Any authenticated user |\n+| Request model approval | Tenant member |\n+| Approve/Reject request | Tenant admin |\n+| Manage providers | Platform admin (root tenant) |\n+\n+**Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-tenant-admin`, `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-platform-admin`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Input Validation\n+\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-input-validation`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must validate all input data.\n+\n+| Field | Validation |\n+|-------|------------|\n+| Canonical ID | Must match pattern `{provider}::{model_id}`, provider must exist. Parse on first `::`. |\n+| Provider name | 1-32 chars, lowercase alphanumeric + hyphen |\n+| Capabilities | Must conform to GTS capability schema |\n+| Pricing values | Non-negative decimal (AICredits) |\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Cache Isolation\n+\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-cache-isolation`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must isolate cached data by tenant.\n+\n+Cache keys MUST include tenant_id as prefix.\n+\n+Format: `mr:{tenant_id}:{entity}:{id}`\n+\n+**TTL strategy**:\n+- Own data (tenant created): TTL 30 min\n+- Inherited data (from parent): TTL 5 min\n+\n+**Cache invalidation on tenant re-parenting**: On `tenant.reparented` event, invalidate ALL cache entries for that tenant.\n+\n+**Redis unavailable**: Fallback to direct DB queries (latency SLOs may be violated).\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Get Tenant Model\n \n-- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-get-tenant-model-v1`\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-get-tenant-model`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must resolve a canonical model ID for a tenant, returning model info and provider details if approved.\n+\n+Resolution:\n+1. Look up model in catalog by canonical ID\n+2. Check tenant approval status (direct or inherited)\n+3. Return model info + provider details\n \n-The system must resolve model availability for a tenant, returning model info and provider details if approved.\n+Response structure defined in GTS contract.\n \n **Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-llm-gateway`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### List Tenant Models\n \n-- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-list-tenant-models-v1`\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-list-tenant-models`\n \n-The system must return all models available for a tenant, supporting filtering by capability and provider.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must return all models available for a tenant.\n+\n+Includes:\n+- Models from tenant's own providers (if approved)\n+- Models inherited from parent tenant hierarchy (if approved at any level)\n+\n+Follows OData pagination standard. Supports OData `$filter` for filtering by capability, provider, approval_status.\n+\n+Capability filtering uses subset matching: model must have AT LEAST requested capabilities.\n \n **Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-llm-gateway`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Model Discovery\n \n-- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-model-discovery-v1`\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-model-discovery`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must periodically poll providers for available models via Outbound API Gateway.\n+\n+**Scheduling**: Fixed concurrency limit + staggered intervals across (tenant, provider) pairs.\n \n-The system must poll providers for available models via Outbound API Gateway, upserting new models and creating pending approvals.\n+Per (tenant, provider) pair where discovery is enabled:\n+- Fetch models from provider's models endpoint (plugin responsibility)\n+- New models → create with `pending` status\n+- Existing models → update metadata (capabilities, limits, pricing)\n+- Missing models → soft-delete (mark as `deprecated`)\n \n-**Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-outbound-api-gateway`, `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-provider-api`\n+**Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-oagw`, `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-provider-api`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Model Approval\n \n-- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-model-approval-v1`\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-model-approval`\n \n-The system must support model approval workflow with statuses: pending, approved, rejected, revoked. Must support auto-approval configuration per tenant/provider.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must support tenant-level model approval workflow.\n+\n+Approval granularity (P1): Tenant-level — approval grants access to all users in tenant.\n+\n+States: `pending` → `approved` | `rejected`, `approved` → `revoked`, `rejected` → `approved`, `revoked` → `approved`\n+\n+Concurrency: First write wins - once status changes from `pending`, subsequent approve/reject requests are rejected with `invalid_transition` error.\n \n **Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-tenant-admin`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Provider Management\n+\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-provider-management`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must support tenant-scoped provider configuration.\n+\n+Provider inheritance:\n+- Providers inherit down tenant hierarchy (additive only)\n+- Child tenant sees parent's providers + own providers\n+- Child cannot hide or disable inherited providers\n+\n+Provider config:\n+- ID, name, type (plugin), base URL, status (active/disabled)\n+- Discovery enabled/interval\n+\n+Credentials handled by OAGW — not stored in Model Registry.\n+\n+**Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-platform-admin`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Model Pricing\n+\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-model-pricing`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must store and provide model base pricing in AICredits.\n+\n+Pricing structure:\n+- Unit: AICredits (internal platform currency)\n+- Tiers: sync, batch, cached (different rates per tier)\n+- Media: per image input, per audio minute, per image output\n+\n+Model Registry returns **base pricing only**. Caller (LLM Gateway) fetches tenant multiplier from License Manager and computes final price.\n+\n+**Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-llm-gateway`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+### P2 — Enhanced Features\n+\n+#### Auto-Approval Rules\n+\n+- [ ] `p2` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-auto-approval`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must support automatic model approval based on configurable rules.\n+\n+Rule hierarchy:\n+- Platform (root tenant) rules set the ceiling (max allowed)\n+- Tenant rules can only restrict further\n+- Tenant cannot auto-approve what platform blocked\n+\n+Rule matching:\n+- Criteria: provider type, provider ID, required capabilities (all must match)\n+- Action: `allow` or `block`\n+- Priority ordering for conflict resolution\n+\n+Auto-approved models store reference to the triggering rule (`auto_approval_rule_id`).\n+\n+**Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-tenant-admin`, `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-platform-admin`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Provider Health Monitoring\n \n-- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-health-monitoring-v1`\n+- [ ] `p2` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-health-monitoring`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must track provider health via synthetic probes for LLM Gateway routing decisions.\n+\n+Probe method:\n+- Call provider's models endpoint (lightweight, read-only)\n+- Granularity: per provider (not per model)\n+- No actual inference calls (cost concern)\n+\n+Health status:\n+- `healthy`: responding normally, latency acceptable\n+- `degraded`: responding but latency > threshold\n+- `unhealthy`: consecutive failures exceed threshold\n+\n+Health stored at provider owner tenant only. Child tenants inherit parent's health status.\n+\n+**Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-oagw`, `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-provider-api`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Alias Management\n+\n+- [ ] `p2` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-alias-management`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must support model aliases with hierarchical scoping.\n+\n+Alias scope:\n+- Root tenant: global aliases visible to all tenants\n+- Child tenant: can override global aliases, add tenant-specific aliases\n+\n+Resolution order: tenant → parent → ... → root → canonical ID\n+\n+Constraint: Alias target MUST be a canonical ID, not another alias (prevents circular references).\n+\n+**Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-tenant-admin`, `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-platform-admin`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Degraded Mode\n+\n+- [ ] `p2` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-degraded-mode`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must define tiered behavior when database is unavailable.\n \n-The system must track provider health metrics (latency, error rate, availability status) via periodic health probes for LLM Gateway routing decisions.\n+- Model capabilities and metadata: serve from stale cache (up to 30 min TTL)\n+- Approval verification: fail request with `service_unavailable` error\n \n-**Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-outbound-api-gateway`, `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-provider-api`\n+P1 behavior: DB unavailable = all requests fail (fail-closed).\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n-## 4. Use Cases\n+#### Tenant Re-parenting\n \n-#### UC-001: Get Tenant Model\n+- [ ] `p2` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-tenant-reparenting`\n \n-- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-usecase-get-tenant-model-v1`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must handle tenant hierarchy changes.\n+\n+When tenant moves to different parent:\n+- Tenant Resolver owns re-parenting logic\n+- Model Registry invalidates all cache entries for affected tenant on `tenant.reparented` event\n+- Re-evaluation of approvals happens on next access\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Bulk Operations\n+\n+- [ ] `p2` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-bulk-operations`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must support batch approval operations: `approve_models(model_ids[])`, `reject_models(model_ids[])`.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Manual Discovery/Probe Trigger\n+\n+- [ ] `p2` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-manual-trigger`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must allow platform admins to manually trigger discovery and health probes.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+### P3 — Fine-Grained Access Control\n+\n+#### User Group Approval\n+\n+- [ ] `p3` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-user-group-approval`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must support model approval scoped to user groups within a tenant.\n+\n+**Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-tenant-admin`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### User-Level Override\n+\n+- [ ] `p3` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-fr-user-level-override`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+The system must support individual user restrictions/allowances for model access.\n+\n+**Actors**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-tenant-admin`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+## 5. Use Cases\n+\n+### UC-001: Get Tenant Model\n+\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-uc-get-tenant-model`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n **Actor**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-llm-gateway`\n \n-**Preconditions**: Model exists in catalog.\n+**Preconditions**: Tenant context available.\n \n **Flow**:\n-1. LLM Gateway sends get_tenant_model(ctx, model_id)\n+1. LLM Gateway sends `get_tenant_model(ctx, canonical_id)`\n 2. Registry looks up model in catalog\n-3. Registry checks tenant approval status\n-4. Registry returns model info + provider\n+3. Registry checks tenant approval (direct or inherited from parent)\n+4. Registry returns model info + provider details\n \n **Postconditions**: Model info returned or error.\n \n **Acceptance criteria**:\n-- Returns model_not_found if model not in catalog\n-- Returns model_not_approved if not approved for tenant\n-- Returns model_deprecated if model sunset\n+- Returns `model_not_found` (404) if model not in catalog\n+- Returns `model_not_approved` (403) if not approved for tenant (or any ancestor)\n+- Returns `model_deprecated` (410) if model was soft-deleted\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n-#### UC-002: List Tenant Models\n+### UC-002: List Tenant Models\n \n-- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-usecase-list-tenant-models-v1`\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-uc-list-tenant-models`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n **Actor**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-llm-gateway`\n \n **Preconditions**: Tenant context available.\n \n **Flow**:\n-1. LLM Gateway sends list_tenant_models(ctx, filter)\n-2. Registry queries approved models for tenant\n-3. Registry applies filters\n-4. Registry returns models list\n+1. LLM Gateway sends `list_tenant_models(ctx)` with OData query params\n+2. Registry collects approved models for tenant (direct + inherited)\n+3. Registry applies OData filters\n+4. Registry returns paginated models list\n \n **Postconditions**: Filtered models list returned.\n \n **Acceptance criteria**:\n-- Supports filtering by capability, provider, modality\n-- Returns only approved models\n-- Includes capabilities, context limits, pricing\n+- Follows OData pagination standard\n+- Supports `$filter` by capability flags, provider ID, provider type, approval_status\n+- Returns only approved models by default\n+- Excludes deprecated models\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+### UC-003: Model Discovery\n \n-#### UC-003: Model Discovery\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-uc-model-discovery`\n \n-- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-usecase-model-discovery-v1`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n **Actor**: Internal (scheduled job)\n \n-**Preconditions**: Provider configured in registry.\n+**Preconditions**: Provider configured with `discovery.enabled = true`.\n \n **Flow**:\n-1. Registry triggers discovery (scheduled or manual)\n-2. Registry sends GET /models via Outbound API Gateway\n+1. Scheduler triggers discovery for (tenant, provider) pair\n+2. Registry sends GET to provider's models endpoint via OAGW\n 3. Provider returns models list\n-4. Registry upserts models\n-5. Registry creates pending approvals for new models\n+4. Registry compares with current catalog:\n+   - New model → create as `pending`\n+   - Existing model → update metadata\n+   - Missing model → mark as `deprecated` (soft-delete)\n \n-**Postconditions**: Catalog updated, pending approvals created.\n+**Postconditions**: Catalog updated.\n \n **Acceptance criteria**:\n-- New models create pending approvals\n-- Existing models updated with latest metadata\n-- Removed models marked as deprecated\n+- Discovery runs per (tenant, provider) pair\n+- Fixed concurrency limit with staggered intervals\n+- Deprecated models are soft-deleted (hidden, not purged)\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n-#### UC-004: Model Approval\n+### UC-004: Model Approval\n \n-- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-usecase-model-approval-v1`\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-uc-model-approval`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n **Actor**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-tenant-admin`\n \n-**Preconditions**: Model in pending status for tenant.\n+**Preconditions**: Model in `pending` status for tenant.\n \n **Flow**:\n-1. Tenant admin reviews pending model\n+1. Tenant admin reviews pending model (use `$filter=approval_status eq 'pending'`)\n 2. Admin approves or rejects\n 3. Registry updates approval status\n-4. Model becomes available (if approved)\n \n **Postconditions**: Model approval status updated.\n \n **Acceptance criteria**:\n-- Statuses: pending → approved | rejected | revoked\n-- Auto-approval configurable per tenant/provider\n-- Revoked models immediately unavailable\n-\n-**State Machine**:\n-\n-```mermaid\n-stateDiagram-v2\n-    [*] --> pending: Model discovered\n-    pending --> approved: Admin approves\n-    pending --> approved: Auto-approval rule matches\n-    pending --> rejected: Admin rejects\n-    approved --> revoked: Admin revokes\n-    rejected --> approved: Admin reconsiders\n-    revoked --> approved: Admin reinstates\n-```\n+- State transitions: `pending` → `approved` | `rejected`\n+- Approval is tenant-scoped (P1)\n+- Approval recorded with actor and timestamp\n+- Concurrent requests: first write wins\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n-**State descriptions**:\n-- **pending**: New model discovered, awaiting tenant admin decision\n-- **approved**: Model available for tenant use\n-- **rejected**: Model explicitly denied for tenant\n-- **revoked**: Previously approved model access withdrawn\n+### UC-005: Model Revocation\n \n-#### UC-005: Model Revocation\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-uc-model-revocation`\n \n-- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-usecase-model-revocation-v1`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n **Actor**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-tenant-admin`\n \n-**Preconditions**: Model in approved status for tenant.\n+**Preconditions**: Model in `approved` status for tenant.\n \n **Flow**:\n 1. Tenant admin selects approved model\n 2. Admin initiates revocation\n-3. Registry updates status to revoked\n-4. Model immediately becomes unavailable for tenant\n+3. Registry updates status to `revoked`\n \n **Postconditions**: Model access revoked.\n \n **Acceptance criteria**:\n-- Revoked models return model_not_approved on access attempts\n-- Active streaming requests may continue, new requests rejected\n-- Revocation is auditable (timestamp, admin who revoked)\n-- Model can be reinstated (revoked → approved)\n+- Revoked models return `model_not_approved` on access attempts\n+- In-flight requests complete, new requests rejected\n+- Revocation recorded with actor and timestamp\n+- Model can be reinstated: `revoked` → `approved`\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n-#### UC-006: Provider Health Monitoring\n+### UC-006: Register Provider\n \n-- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-usecase-health-monitoring-v1`\n-**Actor**: Internal (scheduled job)\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-uc-register-provider`\n \n-**Preconditions**: Provider configured with health endpoint.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Actor**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-platform-admin`\n+\n+**Preconditions**: Provider plugin exists for the specified type.\n \n **Flow**:\n-1. Registry triggers health probe (on interval)\n-2. Registry sends probe via Outbound API Gateway\n-3. Provider responds (or times out/errors)\n-4. Registry updates provider health state\n+1. Admin provides provider config (name, type, base_url, discovery config)\n+2. Registry validates config against plugin requirements\n+3. Registry creates provider record with status `active`\n \n-**Postconditions**: Provider health metrics updated.\n+**Postconditions**: Provider available for model sync.\n \n **Acceptance criteria**:\n-- Metrics: latency, error rate, availability status\n-- Health state available for Gateway routing\n-- Configurable health check interval\n+- Provider ID must be unique within tenant\n+- Plugin type must be supported\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+### UC-007: Disable Provider\n+\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-uc-disable-provider`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Actor**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-platform-admin`\n+\n+**Preconditions**: Provider is active.\n+\n+**Flow**:\n+1. Admin requests provider disable\n+2. Registry marks provider status as `disabled`\n+3. Registry suspends discovery for this provider\n+\n+**Postconditions**: Provider disabled, models not resolvable.\n+\n+**Acceptance criteria**:\n+- Disabled provider's models return `provider_not_found`\n+- Discovery suspended\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+### UC-008: Re-enable Provider\n+\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-uc-reenable-provider`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Actor**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-platform-admin`\n+\n+**Preconditions**: Provider is disabled.\n+\n+**Flow**:\n+1. Admin requests provider re-enable\n+2. Registry marks provider status as `active`\n+3. Discovery resumes on next scheduled run\n+\n+**Postconditions**: Provider active, models resolvable.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+### UC-009: Get Model Pricing\n+\n+- [ ] `p1` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-uc-get-pricing`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Actor**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-llm-gateway`\n+\n+**Preconditions**: Model exists.\n+\n+**Flow**:\n+1. Gateway sends `get_pricing(model_id)`\n+2. Registry retrieves base pricing for model\n+3. Registry returns base pricing by tier\n+\n+**Postconditions**: Base pricing returned.\n+\n+**Acceptance criteria**:\n+- Returns base pricing in AICredits (caller computes final price)\n+- Tiers: sync, batch, cached\n+- Media pricing included if applicable\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+### UC-010: Configure Auto-Approval Rule\n+\n+- [ ] `p2` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-uc-auto-approval-rule`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Actor**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-tenant-admin`, `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-platform-admin`\n+\n+**Preconditions**: Actor has admin role for target tenant.\n+\n+**Flow**:\n+1. Admin defines rule criteria (provider type, provider ID, capabilities)\n+2. Admin sets action (`allow` or `block`) and priority\n+3. Registry validates rule does not expand beyond platform ceiling\n+4. Registry creates rule\n+\n+**Postconditions**: Rule active for future model discoveries.\n+\n+**Acceptance criteria**:\n+- Tenant rules cannot allow what platform blocked\n+- Rules evaluated in priority order\n+- Auto-approved models reference the triggering rule\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+### UC-011: Check Provider Health\n+\n+- [ ] `p2` - **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-uc-provider-health`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Actor**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-llm-gateway`\n+\n+**Preconditions**: Provider exists and health monitoring enabled.","path":"modules/model-registry/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"15cb20127bb04236e91a1bb5d1860808534f7815","original_commit_id":"15cb20127bb04236e91a1bb5d1860808534f7815","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"It's not that clear who will play a role of active scanner... Model Registry itself or some external \"workflow\" or just LLM gateway?","created_at":"2026-02-17T21:46:39Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T21:47:42Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2819233139","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819233139"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2819233139"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2819233139/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":773,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":883,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2820787363","pull_request_review_id":3818223817,"id":2820787363,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6oIcyj","diff_hunk":"@@ -1,33 +1,100 @@\n-# PRD\n+# PRD: Model Registry\n \n ## 1. Overview\n \n-**Purpose**: Model Registry provides a centralized catalog of AI models with tenant-level availability and approval workflow.\n+**Purpose**: Model Registry provides a centralized catalog of AI models with tenant-level availability and approval workflows.\n \n-Model Registry is the authoritative source for model metadata, capabilities, and tenant access control. It tracks which models are available from which providers, manages approval workflows for new models, and monitors provider health for routing decisions. LLM Gateway queries the registry to resolve model identifiers to provider endpoints and verify tenant access.\n+Model Registry is the authoritative source for model metadata, capabilities, pricing, and tenant access control. It tracks which models are available from which providers and manages approval workflows. LLM Gateway queries the registry to resolve model identifiers to provider endpoints and verify tenant access.\n \n-The registry supports automatic model discovery from providers, requiring tenant admin approval before models become available. It also tracks provider health metrics (latency, error rates) to inform Gateway routing decisions.\n+**Key Concepts**:\n+\n+- **Canonical Model ID**: Deterministic identifier in format `{provider}::{provider_model_id}` (e.g., `openai::gpt-4o`). Parsing rule: split on **first** `::` occurrence.\n+- **Tenant Hierarchy**: Tree structure with root tenant at top; providers and approvals inherit down the tree (additive only)\n+- **Provider Plugins**: Each provider type has its own plugin; all requests route through Outbound API Gateway\n \n **Target Users**:\n-- **LLM Gateway** - Primary consumer for model resolution and availability checks\n-- **Tenant Administrators** - Approve/reject models for their tenant\n+\n+- **LLM Gateway** — Primary consumer for model resolution and availability checks\n+- **Tenant Administrators** — Approve/reject models, manage tenant-specific providers\n+- **Platform Administrators** — Configure root tenant providers\n \n **Key Problems Solved**:\n+\n - **Model discovery**: Automatic polling of provider APIs to discover available models\n-- **Access control**: Tenant-level approval workflow for model access\n-- **Health tracking**: Provider health metrics for intelligent routing\n+- **Unified identification**: Canonical IDs abstract provider-specific naming\n+- **Access control**: Tenant-level approval workflow with hierarchical inheritance\n+- **Pricing normalization**: AICredits-based pricing with tier support (sync/batch/cached)\n \n **Success Criteria**:\n-- All scenarios (S1-S6) implemented and operational\n-- Model resolution latency < 10ms P99\n-- Provider health status updated within health check interval\n \n-**Capabilities**:\n-- Model catalog management\n-- Tenant-level model availability\n-- Model approval workflow\n-- Provider health monitoring\n-- Model capability and pricing metadata\n+- Model resolution latency < 10ms P99\n+- 99.9% availability\n+\n+### 1.1 Background\n+\n+LLM Gateway requires a centralized source of truth for model availability, capabilities, and pricing. Without Model Registry, each consumer would need to maintain its own model catalog, leading to inconsistency and duplicated approval workflows.\n+\n+### 1.2 Goals\n+\n+1. Single source of truth for AI model metadata across the platform\n+2. Tenant-controlled model availability with inheritance from parent tenants\n+3. Streamlined approval process\n+\n+### 1.3 Scope\n+\n+#### In Scope\n+\n+- Model catalog CRUD (models, providers)\n+- Tenant-level model availability configuration\n+- Approval workflows (request → approve/reject)\n+- Base pricing metadata (AICredits per tier)\n+- Model capabilities metadata\n+- Cache management with TTL-based invalidation\n+\n+#### Out of Scope","path":"modules/model-registry/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"49408257b07b88ae694cb12f7e728b684041d575","original_commit_id":"15cb20127bb04236e91a1bb5d1860808534f7815","user":{"login":"bsacrobatix","id":160073905,"node_id":"U_kgDOCYqIsQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/160073905?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsacrobatix","html_url":"https://github.com/bsacrobatix","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsacrobatix/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsacrobatix/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsacrobatix/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsacrobatix/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsacrobatix/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsacrobatix/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsacrobatix/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsacrobatix/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsacrobatix/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I would add that customer-provided \"bring your own\" API keys are out of scope (assuming that's the case).","created_at":"2026-02-18T07:34:36Z","updated_at":"2026-02-19T05:28:27Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2820787363","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2820787363"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2820787363"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/606"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2820787363/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":74,"original_line":54,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":71,"position":91,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2821322335","pull_request_review_id":3818789267,"id":2821322335,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6oKfZf","diff_hunk":"@@ -37,217 +104,1036 @@ The registry supports automatic model discovery from providers, requiring tenant\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-tenant-admin`\n \n-**Role**: Approves or rejects models for tenant access. Configures auto-approval policies per provider.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Approves or rejects models for tenant access. Manages tenant-specific providers. Can only restrict access compared to parent tenant, not expand.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+#### Platform Administrator\n+\n+**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-platform-admin`\n+\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Manages root tenant configuration. Configures global providers. Sets baseline that all tenants inherit.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n ### 2.2 System Actors\n \n #### LLM Gateway\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-llm-gateway`\n \n-**Role**: Queries registry to resolve model to provider, check tenant availability, and get model capabilities.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Queries registry to resolve model identifiers (canonical ID) to provider details. Checks tenant availability. Retrieves model capabilities and pricing.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Outbound API Gateway\n \n-**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-outbound-api-gateway`\n+**ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-oagw`\n \n-**Role**: Executes provider API calls for model discovery and health probes.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: Executes provider API calls for model discovery. Handles credential injection. Model Registry has no knowledge of credentials.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n \n #### Provider API\n \n **ID**: `cpt-cf-model-registry-actor-provider-api`\n \n-**Role**: External provider endpoint that returns available models list and responds to health probes.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+**Role**: External provider endpoint (OpenAI, Anthropic, Azure, etc.) that returns available models list.\n+<!-- cpt-cf-id-content -->\n+\n+## 3. Domain Model\n+\n+### 3.1 Core Entities\n+\n+#### Provider\n+\n+Represents a configured AI provider for a tenant.\n+\n+**Fields**: id, tenant_id, name, type (plugin type), base_url, status (active/disabled), discovery config (enabled, interval), timestamps.\n+\n+**Inheritance**: Providers inherit down tenant hierarchy (additive only). Child tenant sees parent's providers + own. Child cannot hide inherited providers.\n+\n+**Health**: ProviderHealth stored at provider's owner tenant only. Child tenants inherit health status from parent.\n+\n+#### Model\n+\n+Represents an AI model in the catalog.\n+\n+**Fields**:\n+- **Identification**: canonical_id (`{provider}::{provider_model_id}`), provider_id, tenant_id, provider_model_id\n+- **Display**: name, description\n+- **Capabilities (Tier 1)**: Boolean flags for text/image/audio/video/document input/output, tools, structured_output, streaming, embeddings, realtime_audio, batch_api\n+- **Limits (Tier 2)**: context_window, max_output_tokens, max_images_per_request, max_image_size_mb, max_audio_duration_sec\n+- **Pricing**: AICredits per tier (sync/batch/cached) for input/output tokens and media (base pricing only)\n+- **Status**: active, deprecated (soft-delete with deprecated_at timestamp)\n+- **Version**: Provider's model version, stored as-is\n+\n+#### ModelApproval\n+\n+Tracks tenant approval status for a model.\n+\n+**Fields**: id, model_canonical_id, tenant_id, status (pending/approved/rejected/revoked), approved_at, approved_by, auto_approval_rule_id (reference to rule that triggered auto-approval, null for manual), rejected_at, rejected_by, revoked_at, revoked_by, timestamps.\n+\n+**Concurrency**: First write wins - once status changes from `pending`, subsequent approve/reject requests are rejected.\n+\n+**State Machine**:\n+\n+```mermaid\n+stateDiagram-v2\n+    [*] --> pending: Model discovered\n+    pending --> approved: Admin approves\n+    pending --> approved: Auto-approval rule matches\n+    pending --> rejected: Admin rejects\n+    approved --> revoked: Admin revokes\n+    rejected --> approved: Admin reconsiders\n+    revoked --> approved: Admin reinstates\n+```\n+\n+#### AutoApprovalRule (P2)\n+\n+Defines rules for automatic model approval.\n+\n+**Fields**: id, tenant_id (root = platform-wide), criteria, action (allow/block), priority, created_at, created_by.\n+\n+**Criteria schema**:\n+- `provider_type`: string | \"*\" (required, \"*\" = any)\n+- `provider_id`: string | \"*\" (required, \"*\" = any)\n+- `capabilities`: string[] (optional, empty = any)\n+\n+**Matching**: ALL criteria must match (AND). Model must have ALL listed capabilities (subset matching).\n+\n+**Rule evaluation**:\n+- Platform (root tenant) rules set the ceiling\n+- Tenant rules can only restrict further, not expand\n+- `block` from platform = blocked for all descendants\n+- Tenant cannot `allow` what platform blocked\n \n-## 3. Functional Requirements\n+**Authorization**: Read/list visible to tenant admins only.\n+\n+#### ProviderHealth (P2)\n+\n+Tracks provider health status from synthetic probes.","path":"modules/model-registry/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"15cb20127bb04236e91a1bb5d1860808534f7815","original_commit_id":"15cb20127bb04236e91a1bb5d1860808534f7815","user":{"login":"pr0tey","id":1847966,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5NjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847966?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey","html_url":"https://github.com/pr0tey","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Model Registry does simple probing — calls provider's models endpoint periodically (lightweight, already part of discovery)","created_at":"2026-02-18T09:40:19Z","updated_at":"2026-02-18T11:14:54Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/606#discussion_r2821322335","pull_request_ur