RRC_kwDOPaLyBs6nDmxT","diff_hunk":"@@ -66,7 +66,14 @@ impl RateLimiterMap {\n                 ),\n                 |r| (r.rps, r.burst, r.in_flight),\n             );\n-            let key = (spec.method.clone(), spec.path.clone());\n+\n+            let path = if cfg.prefix_path.is_empty() {\n+                spec.path.clone()\n+            } else {\n+                format!(\"{}{}\", cfg.prefix_path, spec.path)\n+            };\n+\n+            let key = (spec.method.clone(), path.clone());","path":"modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/rate_limit.rs","commit_id":"4f8cf476f5ed4ddd1fde83948060eec0a8f97b9d","original_commit_id":"4f8cf476f5ed4ddd1fde83948060eec0a8f97b9d","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Normalize `prefix_path` before concatenation to avoid key mismatches.**\n\nIf `prefix_path` ends with `/`, keys become `//...` and won’t match `MatchedPath`, effectively disabling rate limits for those routes. Consider trimming trailing slashes (and validating a leading `/`) before joining.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛠️ Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-            let path = if cfg.prefix_path.is_empty() {\n-                spec.path.clone()\n-            } else {\n-                format!(\"{}{}\", cfg.prefix_path, spec.path)\n-            };\n+            let prefix = cfg.prefix_path.trim_end_matches('/');\n+            let path = if prefix.is_empty() {\n+                spec.path.clone()\n+            } else {\n+                format!(\"{prefix}{}\", spec.path)\n+            };\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/rate_limit.rs` around lines 70 -\n76, Normalize cfg.prefix_path before concatenation to avoid double slashes: trim\ntrailing '/' from cfg.prefix_path, ensure it either is empty or starts with a\nsingle leading '/', and then join it to spec.path with a single separator (or\nsimply concatenate when prefix_path is empty) so the computed path used for key\n= (spec.method.clone(), path.clone()) matches MatchedPath; update the logic that\nbuilds path (the block referencing cfg.prefix_path and spec.path) to perform\nthis normalization/validation before creating key.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 116abbb","created_at":"2026-02-13T07:35:23Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T07:56:09Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#discussion_r2802740307","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2802740307"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#discussion_r2802740307"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull