i-gateway/src/module.rs\necho \"---\"\nsed -n '175,186p' modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 1344\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Find MIME map creation\nrg -n \"mime_map|MimeValidationMap::from_specs\" modules/system/api-gateway/src -B 2 -A 2\necho \"---\"\n# Check LicenseRequirementMap implementation\nrg -n \"LicenseRequirementMap|from_specs\" modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/license_validation.rs -B 2 -A 15\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 2356\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Check how MIME map is built and how rest_finalize applies prefix_path\nrg -n \"build_mime_validation_map|from_specs\" modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/mime_validation.rs -B 2 -A 20\necho \"---\"\n# Find rest_finalize to understand route nesting\nrg -n \"rest_finalize|prefix_path\" modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs | head -30\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 2837\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Check if there are any clues about AuthPolicyLayer behavior or if auth should also use prefix_path\nrg -n \"build_auth_state_from_specs|req_map\" modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs -A 5 -B 5\necho \"---\"\n# Check the full rest_finalize context to see the router nesting\nsed -n '588,610p' modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 3273\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Verify the concern by checking if auth policy is applied before or after nesting\n# and whether it should also use prefix_path\nrg -n \"AuthPolicyLayer|apply_middleware_stack\" modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs -B 2 -A 2\necho \"---\"\n# Double-check: search for any comments or TODOs about prefix_path and auth\nrg -n \"prefix|auth|policy\" modules/system/api-gateway/src/auth.rs | grep -i \"prefix\\|todo\\|todo\\|fixme\"\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 1220\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Apply `prefix_path` when building auth policy, matching license/MIME validation.**\n\nAuth policy is built from unprefixed `spec.path` (line 128), but license and MIME validation maps apply `prefix_path` during construction (lines 22–35, 17–37). Since both middleware use `MatchedPath` for lookups and `apply_middleware_stack()` runs before route nesting (line 602–604), incoming requests to prefixed paths (e.g., `/api/v1/users`) will have `MatchedPath` set to the full path. Auth policy lookups against unprefixed keys will fail, potentially bypassing authentication for all routed operations when `prefix_path` is not empty.\n\nModify `build_auth_state_from_specs()` to pass `config.prefix_path` to `build_auth_state()` and apply it to `spec.path` the same way license/MIME maps do.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs` around lines 187 - 191,\nbuild_auth_state_from_specs currently builds auth policy using raw spec.path\nwhich doesn't apply config.prefix_path, causing lookups to mismatch prefixed\nMatchedPath values; update build_auth_state_from_specs to forward\nconfig.prefix_path into build_auth_state and ensure build_auth_state applies the\nprefix to each spec.path (same approach used by\nmiddleware::license_validation::LicenseRequirementMap::from_specs and the MIME\nvalidation map) so keys stored in the auth policy are the prefixed paths that\nwill match MatchedPath during middleware lookups.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 902fa44","created_at":"2026-02-13T07:35:24Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T07:56:19Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#discussion_r2802740312","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfa