```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 175\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check the context around those usages in module.rs\nsed -n '60,75p' modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs\nsed -n '668,680p' modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 1035\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if prefix_path is accessed or set after ApiGatewayConfig::default() calls\nrg -n 'prefix_path' modules/system/api-gateway/src/\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 1546\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Fix: Implement `Default` manually for `ApiGatewayConfig` to ensure `prefix_path` defaults to `\"/chat\"`.**\n\nThe `#[serde(default = \"default_prefix_path\")]` attribute only affects deserialization. Since `ApiGatewayConfig` derives `Default`, when `ApiGatewayConfig::default()` is called directly (as in module.rs:65 for production initialization), `prefix_path` will be set to an empty string, not `\"/chat\"`. This causes the routing prefix to be missing in runtime usage. Implement a custom `Default` impl that calls `default_prefix_path()` to fix this.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/config.rs` around lines 61 - 62,\nApiGatewayConfig's derived Default doesn't use the serde default function so\nprefix_path ends up empty; implement a manual impl Default for ApiGatewayConfig\nthat constructs the struct and sets prefix_path to default_prefix_path() while\ninitializing the other fields to their existing defaults (e.g., by calling their\ncurrent defaults or using the derived defaults), ensuring any code that calls\nApiGatewayConfig::default() gets prefix_path = \"/chat\".\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Confirmed as addressed by @dominic1988-lgtm\n\n<!-- This is an auto-genera