one());","path":"modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/mime_validation.rs","commit_id":"902fa44ef6ec29be13d51654b43d21bedaa21fdb","original_commit_id":"902fa44ef6ec29be13d51654b43d21bedaa21fdb","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Normalize prefix_path to avoid MIME validation bypass.**\n\nAs written, `format!(\"{}{}\", prefix_path, spec.path)` will produce `//` or missing leading `/` when prefix_path is user-supplied (e.g., `\"/chat/\"` or `\"chat\"`), which can cause lookup misses and skip MIME validation. Please normalize the join to guarantee a single leading slash and no double slashes.  \n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛠️ Suggested normalization</summary>\n\n```diff\n pub fn build_mime_validation_map(\n     specs: &[OperationSpec],\n     prefix_path: &str,\n ) -> MimeValidationMap {\n     let map = DashMap::new();\n\n     for spec in specs {\n         if let Some(ref allowed) = spec.allowed_request_content_types {\n-            let path = if prefix_path.is_empty() {\n-                spec.path.clone()\n-            } else {\n-                format!(\"{}{}\", prefix_path, spec.path)\n-            };\n+            let trimmed_prefix = prefix_path.trim_end_matches('/');\n+            let normalized_prefix = if trimmed_prefix.is_empty() {\n+                String::new()\n+            } else if trimmed_prefix.starts_with('/') {\n+                trimmed_prefix.to_owned()\n+            } else {\n+                format!(\"/{}\", trimmed_prefix)\n+            };\n+            let trimmed_path = spec.path.trim_start_matches('/');\n+            let path = if normalized_prefix.is_empty() {\n+                format!(\"/{}\", trimmed_path)\n+            } else {\n+                format!(\"{}/{}\", normalized_prefix, trimmed_path)\n+            };\n\n             let key = (spec.method.clone(), path.clone());\n             map.insert(key, allowed.clone());\n         }\n     }\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\npub fn build_mime_validation_map(\n    specs: &[OperationSpec],\n    prefix_path: &str,\n) -> MimeValidationMap {\n    let map = DashMap::new();\n\n    for spec in specs {\n        if let Some(ref allowed) = spec.allowed_request_content_types {\n            let trimmed_prefix = prefix_path.trim_end_matches('/');\n            let normalized_prefix = if trimmed_prefix.is_empty() {\n                String::new()\n            } else if trimmed_prefix.starts_with('/') {\n                trimmed_prefix.to_owned()\n            } else {\n                format!(\"/{}\", trimmed_prefix)\n            };\n            let trimmed_path = spec.path.trim_start_matches('/');\n            let path = if normalized_prefix.is_empty() {\n                format!(\"/{}\", trimmed_path)\n            } else {\n                format!(\"{}/{}\", normalized_prefix, trimmed_path)\n            };\n\n            let key = (spec.method.clone(), path.clone());\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/mime_validation.rs` around lines 17\n- 31, The code building the key in build_mime_validation_map can produce\nmalformed paths (double slashes or missing leading slash) by naively\nconcatenating prefix_path and spec.path; normalize prefix_path and spec.path\nbefore joining so the resulting path always has a single leading '/' and no\nduplicate slashes. Specifically, trim trailing slashes from prefix_path, ensure\nspec.path begins with a single leading slash, and then join them (or use\nspec.path alone when prefix_path is empty) before creating the key (the tuple of\nspec.method.clone() and the normalized path).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Confirmed as addressed by @dominic1988-lgtm\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-13T07:45:44Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T07:57:31Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#discussion_r2802774285","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2802774285"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#discussion_r2802774285"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2802774285/reactions","tot