?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@dominic1988-lgtm`, thank you for updating the code to address the path normalization issue! This ensures that MIME validation will work correctly regardless of how the prefix path is formatted.\n\n<!-- <review_comment_addressed> -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-13T07:57:32Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T07:57:33Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#discussion_r2802812930","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2802812930"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#discussion_r2802812930"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2802812930/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":17,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":31,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2802774285,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":20,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2802820520","pull_request_review_id":3795613261,"id":2802820520,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6nD6Wo","diff_hunk":"@@ -19,15 +19,19 @@ pub struct LicenseRequirementMap {\n \n impl LicenseRequirementMap {\n     #[must_use]\n-    pub fn from_specs(specs: &[OperationSpec]) -> Self {\n+    pub fn from_specs(specs: &[OperationSpec], prefix_path: &str) -> Self {\n         let requirements = DashMap::new();\n \n         for spec in specs {\n             if let Some(req) = spec.license_requirement.as_ref() {\n-                requirements.insert(\n-                    (spec.method.clone(), spec.path.clone()),\n-                    req.license_names.clone(),\n-                );\n+                let prefix_path = prefix_path.trim_end_matches('/');\n+                let path = if prefix_path.is_empty() {\n+                    spec.path.clone()\n+                } else {\n+                    format!(\"{}{}\", prefix_path, spec.path)\n+                };\n+\n+                requirements.insert((spec.method.clone(), path), req.license_names.clone());\n             }","path":"modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/license_validation.rs","commit_id":"1d0249fbdc2184d5c448596a80fc6a7cd3e8eace","original_commit_id":"116abbb75ee13dc5afec732ef5cc4c617fae9a7d","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🔴 Critical_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nrg -n \"prefix_path\" modules/system/api-gateway/src -g'*.rs' -A 3 -B 3\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 7641\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check for any config validation or schema files\nfind modules/system/api-gateway/src -name \"*.rs\" | xargs grep -l \"prefix_path\" | head -10\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 334\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Look at config.rs more thoroughly to see if there's any validation\ncat -n modules/system/api-gateway/src/config.rs | head -80\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 3143\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Verify the exact behavior by checking how keys are built and compared in the license middleware\ncat -n modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/license_validation.rs\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 3060\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Normalize `prefix_path` leading slash before using as key.**\n\nLicense validation silently fails if `prefix_path` is misconfigured without a leading slash (e.g., `chat` instead of `/chat`). The key becomes `chat/...` while `MatchedPath` from axum routing will be `/chat/...`, causing no match. This issue exists at config load time with no validation, and affects license validation (line 27-31), MIME validation, and rate limiting identically.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested normalization</summary>\n\n```diff\n     pub fn from_specs(specs: &[OperationSpec], prefix_path: &str) -> Self {\n         let requirements = DashMap::new();\n\n         for spec in specs {\n             if let Some(req) = spec.license_requirement.as_ref() {\n-                let prefix_path = prefix_path.trim_end_matches('/');\n-                let path = if prefix_path.is_empty() {\n+                let raw_prefix = prefix_path.trim_end_matches('/');\n+                let prefix = if raw_prefix.is_empty() {\n+                    \"\"\n+                } else if raw_prefix.starts_with('/') {\n+                    raw_prefix\n+                } else {\n+                    // Prepend leading slash if missing\n+                    &format!(\"/{}\", raw_prefix)\n+                };\n+                let path = if prefix.is_empty() {\n                     spec.path.clone()\n                 } else {\n-                    format!(\"{}{}\", prefix_path, spec.path)\n+                    format!(\"{}{}\", prefix, spec.path)\n                 };\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\npub fn from_specs(specs: &[OperationSpec], prefix_path: &str) -> Self {\n    let requirements = DashMap::new();\n\n    for spec in specs {\n        if let Some(req) = spec.license_requirement.as_ref() {\n            let raw_prefix = prefix_path.trim_end_matches('/');\n            let prefix = if raw_prefix.is_empty() {\n                String::new()\n            } else if raw_prefix.starts_with('/') {\n                raw_prefix.to_string()\n            } else {\n                // Prepend leading slash if missing\n                format!(\"/{}\", raw_prefix)\n            };\n            let path = if prefix.is_empty() {\n                spec.path.clone()\n            } else {\n                format!(\"{}{}\", prefix, spec.path)\n            };\n\n            requirements.insert((spec.method.clone(), path), req.license_names.clone());\n        }\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/license_validation.rs` around lines\n22 - 35, The code in from_specs builds keys using prefix_path but only trims\ntrailing slashes, so missing leading slash (e.g., \"chat\") produces keys like\n\"chat/...\" that won't match axum's MatchedPath \"/chat/...\"; normalize\nprefix_path by trimming whitespace and both leading/trailing slashes then ensure\nit starts with a single \"/\" (unless empty) before composing path; update the\npath construction in from_specs (the prefix_path variable used when creating the\nkey for requirements.insert((spec.method.clone(), path), ...)) so the stored\nkeys always use a leading slash, and apply the same normalization wherever\nprefix_path is used for MIME validation and rate limiting.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit c6bff84","created_at":"2026-02-13T07:59:55Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T08:09:52Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#discussion_r2802820520","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2802820520"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rus