sers/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@dominic1988-lgtm`, thank you for addressing the prefix path normalization! The fix ensures that regardless of whether `prefix_path` is configured as `\"chat\"` or `\"/chat\"`, the middleware will correctly match routes against axum's `MatchedPath` format (which always includes a leading slash).\n\n<!-- <review_comment_addressed> -->\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-10T18:54:33.294Z\nLearning: Applies to modules/system/types-registry/openspec/openspec/changes/**/specs/**/*.md : For MODIFIED requirements, paste the complete updated requirement block (header + all scenarios) with behavior changes; the archiver replaces the entire requirement\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-10T18:54:47.115Z\nLearning: Applies to modules/system/types-registry/openspec/openspec/changes/*/specs/**/spec.md : Use `## ADDED` for new capabilities that stand alone; use `## MODIFIED` for behavior changes to existing requirements (include full requirement content); use `## REMOVED` for deprecated features; use `## RENAMED` for name-only changes\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-10T18:54:47.115Z\nLearning: Applies to modules/system/types-registry/openspec/openspec/changes/*/specs/**/spec.md : In spec delta files under `changes/[change-id]/specs/`, use `## ADDED Requirements`, `## MODIFIED Requirements`, `## REMOVED Requirements`, and `## RENAMED Requirements` sections\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-10T18:54:33.294Z\nLearning: Applies to modules/system/types-registry/openspec/openspec/changes/**/specs/**/*.md : In spec delta files, use ADDED for new orthogonal capabilities, MODIFIED for behavior changes of existing requirements, and RENAMED for name-only changes\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-10T18:54:47.115Z\nLearning: Applies to modules/system/types-registry/openspec/openspec/changes/*/specs/**/spec.md : Spec file headers in `## ADDED|MODIFIED|REMOVED|RENAMED Requirements` are matched with `trim(header)` (whitespace ignored); ensure section names match exactly these keywords\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-10T18:54:47.115Z\nLearning: Applies to modules/system/types-registry/openspec/openspec/changes/*/specs/**/spec.md : Write spec deltas using `## ADDED|MODIFIED|REMOVED|RENAMED Requirements` headers; include at least one `#### Scenario:` per requirement\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-10T18:54:33.294Z\nLearning: Applies to modules/system/types-registry/openspec/openspec/changes/**/specs/**/*.md : Use `## ADDED|MODIFIED|REMOVED|RENAMED Requirements` headers in delta spec files with at least one `#### Scenario:` per requirement\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-10T18:54:47.115Z\nLearning: Applies to modules/system/types-registry/openspec/openspec/changes/*/proposal.md : In `proposal.md`, include sections: Why (1-2 sentences on problem/opportunity), What Changes (bullet list with breaking changes marked **BREAKING**), and Impact (affected specs and code)\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-13T08:10:29Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T08:10:29Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#discussion_r2802855096","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2802855096"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#discussion_r2802855096"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2802855096/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":22,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":35,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2802820520,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":22,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2802969494","pull_request_review_id":3795775963,"id":2802969494,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6nEeuW","diff_hunk":"@@ -123,9 +123,19 @@ impl ApiGateway {\n         public_routes.insert((Method::GET, \"/docs\".to_owned()));\n         public_routes.insert((Method::GET, \"/openapi.json\".to_owned()));\n \n+        let prefix_path = &self.get_cached_config().prefix_path;\n+        let trimmed_path = prefix_path.trim_end_matches('/');\n+\n         for spec in &self.openapi_registry.operation_specs {\n             let spec = spec.value();\n-            let route_key = (spec.method.cl