:3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`prefix_path` has no `#[serde(default)]`.\n\nAny existing YAML config that doesn't have `prefix_path` will **fail to deserialize** — gateway won't start. This breaks every deployment that hasn't updated their config yet.\n\nNeeds:\n```rust\n#[serde(default = \"default_prefix_path\")]\npub prefix_path: String,\n```\nplus `fn default_prefix_path() -> String { \"/cf\".to_owned() }` (or empty string if we want opt-in).\n\nAlso: `ApiGatewayConfig` derives `Default`, so `ApiGatewayConfig::default()` (called in module.rs:65) will set `prefix_path` to `\"\"`, not the serde default. Either implement `Default` manually or normalize on init.","created_at":"2026-02-26T12:31:17Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T12:31:18Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#discussion_r2858763592","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2858763592"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#discussion_r2858763592"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2858763592/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":45,"original_line":45,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":5,"position":5,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2858763600","pull_request_review_id":3860622032,"id":2858763600,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6qZUVQ","diff_hunk":"@@ -125,11 +125,13 @@ impl ApiGateway {\n         // Always mark built-in health check routes as public\n         public_routes.insert((Method::GET, \"/health\".to_owned()));\n         public_routes.insert((Method::GET, \"/healthz\".to_owned()));\n+\n         public_routes.insert((Method::GET, \"/docs\".to_owned()));\n         public_routes.insert((Method::GET, \"/openapi.json\".to_owned()));","path":"modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs","commit_id":"7700c01329592d1abc48d951aced4bc0752443ce","original_commit_id":"4c0928583f960a33eba625c5a7423a01da44a066","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"These public routes (`/docs`, `/openapi.json`) are registered without the prefix.\n\nAuth middleware resolves against `MatchedPath` which includes the full prefix — so it sees `/cf/docs`, looks it up in `public_routes`, finds no match → **docs and openapi.json will require authentication** even though they shouldn't.\n\nSame issue for `/health` and `/healthz` above.\n\nFix: either add prefixed versions to `public_routes`, or (better) strip `NestedPath` in auth middleware the same way it's already done in license/mime/rate_limit middleware.","created_at":"2026-02-26T12:31:18Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T12:31:18Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#discussion_r2858763600","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2858763600"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#discussion_r2858763600"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2858763600/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":130,"original_line":130,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":6,"position":6,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2858763606","pull_request_review_id":3860622032,"id":2858763606,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6qZUVW","diff_hunk":"@@ -595,6 +606,11 @@ impl modkit::contracts::ApiGatewayCapability for ApiGateway {\n         let authn_client = self.authn_client.lock().clone();\n         router = self.apply_middleware_stack(router, authn_client)?;\n \n+        if !config.prefix_path.is_empty() {\n+            let new_router = Router::new();\n+            router = new_router.nest(config.prefix_path.as_str(), router);","path":"modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs","commit_id":"7700c01329592d1abc48d951aced4bc0752443ce","original_commit_id":"4c0928583f960a33eba625c5a7423a01da44a066","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Three ways this blows up depending on what's in `prefix_path`:\n\n1. **`\"/\"` → panic**: Axum's `Router::nest(\"/\", ...)` panics — it expects `.merge()` for root.\n2. **Trailing slash** (`\"/cf/\"`): Axum treats `/cf` and `/cf/` as different paths. All routes silently break.\n3. **No leading slash** (`\"cf\"`): invalid path for `nest()`, also panics.\n\nNormalize once at config load time:\n```rust\nlet prefix = config.prefix_path.trim().trim_end_matches('/');\nif prefix.is_empty() || prefix == \"/\" {\n    // no nesting, just merge\n} else {\n    let prefix = if prefix.starts_with('/') { prefix.to_owned() } else { format!(\"/{prefix}\") };\n    router = Router::new().nest(&prefix, router);\n}\n```","created_at":"2026-02-26T12:31:18Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T12:31:18Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#discussion_r2858763606","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2858763606"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#discussion_r2858763606"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2858763606/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":611,"original_line":611,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":59,"position":59,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2858763617","pull_request_review_id":3860622032,"id":2858763617,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6qZUVh","diff_hunk":"@@ -54,6 +54,13 @@ pub async fn license_validation_middleware(\n         .get::<axum::extract::MatchedPath>()\n         .map_or_else(|| req.uri().path().to_owned(), |p| p.as_str().to_owned());\n \n+    let nestedpath = req.extensions().get::<axum::extract::NestedPath>();\n+\n+    let path = nestedpath\n+        .and_then(|np| path.strip_prefix(np.as_str()))\n+        .unwrap_or(&path)\n+        .to_owned();","path":"modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/license_validation.rs","commit_id":"7700c01329592d1abc48d951aced4bc0752443ce","original_commit_id":"4c0928583f960a33eba625c5a7423a01da44a066","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This NestedPath strip block is copy-pasted verbatim in three places:\r\n- here (license_validation.rs)\r\n- mime_validation.rs\r\n- rate_limit.rs\r\n\r\nAnd auth middleware doesn't have it at all — that's the root cause of the public_routes mismatch I flagged in module.rs.\r\n\r\nExtract into a shared helper:\r\n```rust\r\npub(crate) fn resolve_path(req: &Request, matched_path: &str) -> String {\r\n    req.extensions()\r\n        .get::<axum::extract::NestedPath>()\r\n        .and_then(|np| matched_path.strip_prefix(np.as_str()))\r\n        .unwrap_or(matched_path)\r\n        .to_owned()\r\n}\r\n```\r\nThen use it from all four middleware (including auth). Right now if you change the stripping logic in one place you'll forget the other two — and auth is already out of sync.","created_at":"2026-02-26T12:31:18Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T12:35:21Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#discussion_r2858763617","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2858763617"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#discussion_r2858763617"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2858763617/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":62,"original_line":62,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":9,"position":9,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2858763624","pull_request_review_id":3860622032,"id":2858763624,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6qZUVo","diff_hunk":"@@ -28,9 +28,14 @@ pub async fn health_check() -> Json<Value> {\n }\n \n #[cfg(not(feature = \"embed_elements\"))]\n-pub async fn serve_docs() -> Html<&'static str> {\n+pub fn serve_docs(prefix_path: &str) -> Html<String> {\n+    let openapi_url = if prefix_path.is_empty() {\n+        String::from(\"/openapi.json\")\n+    } else {\n+        format!(\"{prefix_path}/openapi.json\")","path":"modules/system/api-gateway/src/web.rs","commit_id":"7700c01329592d1abc48d951aced4bc0752443ce","original_commit_id":"4c0928583f960a33eba625c5a7423a01da44a066","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`prefix_path` is interpolated into HTML via `format!()` with no escaping. Currently it comes from server config so it's not a real XSS vector, but it's a footgun if prefix ever becomes dynamic.\n\nMore practically: both `serve_docs` variants allocate a new `String` on every request via `format!()`. The HTML is static after startup — build it once during init and store in an `Arc<String>`.","created_at":"2026-02-26T12:31:18Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T12:31:18Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#discussion_r2858763624","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2858763624"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#discussion_r2858763624"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2858763624/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":35,"original_line":35,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":9,"position":9,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2858763628","pull_request_review_id":3860622032,"id":2858763628,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6qZUVs","diff_hunk":"@@ -11,7 +11,7 @@\n @pytest.fixture\r\n def base_url():\r\n     \"\"\"Provide base URL for the API from E2E_BASE_URL env var.\"\"\"\r\n-    return os.getenv(\"E2E_BASE_URL\", \"http://localhost:8086\")\r\n+    return os.getenv(\"E2E_BASE_URL\", \"http://localhost:8086/cf\")\r","path":"testing/e2e/conftest.py","commit_id":"7700c01329592d1abc48d951aced4bc0752443ce","original_commit_id":"4c0928583f960a33eba625c5a7423a01da44a066","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Hardcoded `/cf` in the default URL. If someone changes `prefix_path` in the config (or removes it), e2e tests silently break with no obvious connection to the cause.\n\nEither pull the prefix from a separate env var (`E2E_API_PREFIX`) or keep `base_url` prefix-free and prepend it in individual tests.","created_at":"2026-02-26T12:31:18Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T12:31:18Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#discussion_r2858763628","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2858763628"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#discussion_r2858763628"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2858763628/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":14,"original_line":14,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":5,"position":5,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2858763633","pull_request_review_id":3860622032,"id":2858763633,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6qZUVx","diff_hunk":"@@ -165,6 +165,7 @@ async fn test_auth_disabled_mode() {\n                 \"enable_docs\": true,\n                 \"cors_enabled\": false,\n                 \"auth_disabled\": true,\n+                \"prefix_path\": \"/cf\",","path":"modules/system/api-gateway/tests/auth_middleware.rs","commit_id":"7700c01329592d1abc48d951aced4bc0752443ce","original_commit_id":"4c0928583f960a33eba625c5a7423a01da44a066","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Every single test uses `\"prefix_path\": \"/cf\"`. There's no coverage for:\n- empty prefix (backward compat — the most important case)\n- `\"/\"` (should either work like no prefix or be rejected at validation)\n- `\"cf\"` without leading slash\n- `\"/cf/\"` with trailing slash\n\nWithout at least a test for empty prefix there's no proof the old behavior still works.","created_at":"2026-02-26T12:31:18Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T12:31:18Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#discussion_r2858763633","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2858763633"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#discussion_r2858763633"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2858763633/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":168,"original_line":168,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":4,"position":4,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2859125716","pull_request_review_id":3861083225,"id":2859125716,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6qasvU","diff_hunk":"@@ -41,6 +41,8 @@ pub struct ApiGatewayConfig {\n     /// If true, routes without explicit security requirement still require authentication (AuthN-only).\n     #[serde(default = \"default_require_au