_id":2858763633,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":4,"position":4,"subject_type":"line"}],"source_reviews":[{"id":3795472570,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7iOlC6","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Some comments are outside the diff and can’t be posted inline due to platform limitations.\n> \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>⚠️ Outside diff range comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `121-124`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🔴 Critical_\n> \n> **Hardcoded public routes will fail auth checks when prefix_path is applied.**\n> \n> The public routes for `/docs` and `/openapi.json` are registered without the prefix (lines 121-124), but the auth middleware applies to the module_router before it's nested under `config.prefix_path` (lines 591-599). When a request arrives for the prefixed path (e.g., `/api/v1/docs`), the auth layer calls `resolve()` with the full URI path from `request.uri().path()` (axum_ext.rs:147). The `public_matchers` only know about `/docs` and `/openapi.json`, so the pattern match fails (auth.rs:137), and the routes incorrectly require authentication.\n> \n> These routes must either be registered with the full prefixed paths, or the public routes must be adjusted to match the actual request paths when a prefix is configured.\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit/src/contracts.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`80-90`: **Consider documenting the `module_router` parameter.**\n\nThe new `module_router` parameter represents a significant addition to the API contract. Adding a brief description in the docstring would help implementors understand its purpose and how it differs from the existing `router` parameter.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested documentation update</summary>\n\n```diff\n     /// Finalize before start: attach /openapi.json, /docs, persist the Router internally if needed.\n     /// Do NOT start the server here.\n     ///\n+    /// # Arguments\n+    /// * `router` - The base router with global middleware and system routes.\n+    /// * `module_router` - The router containing module-specific REST routes to be nested under the configured prefix.\n+    ///\n     /// # Errors\n     /// Returns an error if router finalization fails.\n     fn rest_finalize(\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/rate_limit.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`69-76`: **Consider defensive path normalization for edge cases.**\n\nThe path construction at line 73 concatenates `prefix_path` and `spec.path` directly without normalization. While all current path patterns start with `/`, the lack of validation creates potential issues:\n\n- If `prefix_path` is set to `\"/\"`, the result becomes `\"//users\"` instead of `\"/users\"`\n- If a `spec.path` omits the leading `/`, concatenation produces `\"/chatusers\"` instead of `\"/chat/users\"`\n\nAlthough these scenarios appear unlikely given current conventions, defensive path joining would prevent mismatches between bucket keys and Axum's `MatchedPath`. This same pattern appears in `mime_validation.rs` and `license_validation.rs` and could be normalized consistently across all three middleware.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛡️ Suggested defensive path construction</summary>\n\n```diff\n             let path = if cfg.prefix_path.is_empty() {\n                 spec.path.clone()\n             } else {\n-                format!(\"{}{}\", cfg.prefix_path, spec.path)\n+                // Ensure proper path joining without double slashes\n+                let prefix = cfg.prefix_path.trim_end_matches('/');\n+                let suffix = spec.path.strip_prefix('/').unwrap_or(&spec.path);\n+                format!(\"{}/{}\", prefix, suffix)\n             };\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/license_validation.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`32-37`: **Replace `eprintln!` with `tracing::debug!` for consistency.**\n\nUsing `eprintln!` for logging is inconsistent with the rest of the codebase, which uses the `tracing` crate. This debug output will bypass log levels and structured logging.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-                eprintln!(\n-                    \"Mapping license requirement for {} {}: {:?}\",\n-                    spec.method,\n-                    path,\n-                    req.license_names\n-                );\n+                tracing::debug!(\n+                    method = %spec.method,\n+                    path = %path,\n+                    license_names = ?req.license_names,\n+                    \"Mapping license requirement\"\n+                );\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#pullrequestreview-3795472570","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#pullrequestreview-3795472570"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-13T07:20:15Z","commit_id":"17c98912c7b75ce488a8d2e14401cecb651fd02f"},{"id":3795535232,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7iO0WA","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 2**\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Some comments are outside the diff and can’t be posted inline due to platform limitations.\n> \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>⚠️ Outside diff range comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `588-606`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n> \n> **Guard against empty `prefix_path` before calling `nest`.**\n> \n> If `prefix_path` is empty (explicitly supported elsewhere), `Router::nest` will reject it and can panic, dropping routes.\n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🛠️ Suggested fix</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n> -        let prefix_router = Router::new().nest(&config.prefix_path, module_router);\n> -\n> -        router = router.merge(prefix_router);\n> +        if config.prefix_path.is_empty() {\n> +            router = router.merge(module_router);\n> +        } else {\n> +            let prefix_router = Router::new().nest(&config.prefix_path, module_router);\n> +            router = router.merge(prefix_router);\n> +        }\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/rate_limit.rs`:\n- Around line 70-76: Normalize cfg.prefix_path before concatenation to avoid\ndouble slashes: trim trailing '/' from cfg.prefix_path, ensure it either is\nempty or starts with a single leading '/', and then join it to spec.path with a\nsingle separator (or simply concatenate when prefix_path is empty) so the\ncomputed path used for key = (spec.method.clone(), path.clone()) matches\nMatchedPath; update the logic that builds path (the block referencing\ncfg.prefix_path and spec.path) to perform this normalization/validation before\ncreating key.\n\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs`:\n- Around line 187-191: build_auth_state_from_specs currently builds auth policy\nusing raw spec.path which doesn't apply config.prefix_path, causing lookups to\nmismatch prefixed MatchedPath values; update build_auth_state_from_specs to\nforward config.prefix_path into build_auth_state and ensure build_auth_state\napplies the prefix to each spec.path (same approach used by\nmiddleware::license_validation::LicenseRequirementMap::from_specs and the MIME\nvalidation map) so keys stored in the auth policy are the prefixed paths that\nwill match MatchedPath during middleware lookups.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#pullrequestreview-3795535232","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#pullrequestreview-3795535232"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-13T07:35:24Z","commit_id":"4f8cf476f5ed4ddd1fde83948060eec0a8f97b9d"},{"id":3795568183,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7iO8Y3","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 2**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/config.rs`:\n- Around line 61-62: ApiGatewayConfig's derived Default doesn't use the serde\ndefault function so prefix_path ends up empty; implement a manual impl Default\nfor ApiGatewayConfig that constructs the struct and sets prefix_path to\ndefault_prefix_path() while initializing the other fields to their existing\ndefaults (e.g., by calling their current defaults or using the derived\ndefaults), ensuring any code that calls ApiGatewayConfig::default() gets\nprefix_path = \"/chat\".\n\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/mime_validation.rs`:\n- Around line 17-31: The code building the key in build_mime_validation_map can\nproduce malformed paths (double slashes or missing leading slash) by naively\nconcatenating prefix_path and spec.path; normalize prefix_path and spec.path\nbefore joining so the resulting path always has a single leading '/' and no\nduplicate slashes. Specifically, trim trailing slashes from prefix_path, ensure\nspec.path begins with a single leading slash, and then join them (or use\nspec.path alone when prefix_path is empty) before creating the key (the tuple of\nspec.method.clone() and the normalized path).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/api-gateway/tests/auth_middleware.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`408-412`: **Test inconsistent with new `module_router` pattern.**\n\nThis test uses the old pattern where `register_rest` is called with `router` directly, while all other tests in this file have been updated to use a separate `module_router`. This test also doesn't call `rest_finalize`, which is where the middleware stack and prefix nesting are applied.\n\nIf this test is intentionally testing pre-finalization behavior (OpenAPI spec registration), the code is fine but consider adding a comment explaining why it differs from other tests.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#pullrequestreview-3795568183","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#pullrequestreview-3795568183"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-13T07:45:46Z","commit_id":"902fa44ef6ec29be13d51654b43d21bedaa21fdb"},{"id":3795613261,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7iPHZN","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 1**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/license_validation.rs`:\n- Around line 22-35: The code in from_specs builds keys using prefix_path but\nonly trims trailing slashes, so missing leading slash (e.g., \"chat\") produces\nkeys like \"chat/...\" that won't match axum's MatchedPath \"/chat/...\"; normalize\nprefix_path by trimming whitespace and both leading/trailing slashes then ensure\nit starts with a single \"/\" (unless empty) before composing path; update the\npath construction in from_specs (the prefix_path variable used when creating the\nkey for requirements.insert((spec.method.clone(), path), ...)) so the stored\nkeys always use a leading slash, and apply the same normalization wherever\nprefix_path is used for MIME validation and rate limiting.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`126-138`: **Addresses previous review feedback on auth policy prefixing.**\n\nThe auth state now correctly applies `prefix_path` to route keys, ensuring auth policy lookups match the prefixed `MatchedPath` values set by Axum. The empty-prefix handling is sound.\n\nMinor formatting nit on line 126:\n```diff\n-        let prefix_path =&self.get_cached_config().prefix_path;\n+        let prefix_path = &self.get_cached_config().prefix_path;\n```\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#pullrequestreview-3795613261","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#pullrequestreview-3795613261"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602"}},"su