der cyberfabric-core includes a dependency on the 'openapi' target so OpenAPI generation runs as part of the local build. Verify that an openapi target exists and that including it does not introduce unnecessary rebuilds or circular dependencies.\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs`:\n- Around line 126-138: The public routes for docs (\"/docs\" and \"/openapi.json\")\nare being registered without the configured prefix so when\nrequire_auth_by_default is true the prefixed endpoints (e.g. \"/chat/docs\")\nbecome protected; use the same normalized prefix computed from\nself.get_cached_config().prefix_path (the trimmed_path variable) to register\nprefixed entries into public_routes as well. Locate where trimmed_path is\ncomputed and where public_routes is populated (around\nopenapi_registry.operation_specs handling) and add prefixed variants like\nformat!(\"{}{}\", trimmed_path, \"/docs\") and format!(\"{}{}\", trimmed_path,\n\"/openapi.json\") (or skip adding the prefix when trimmed_path is empty) so both\nunprefixed and prefixed docs/openapi.json are marked public consistently.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#pullrequestreview-3795673727","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#pullrequestreview-3795673727"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-13T08:18:06Z","commit_id":"c6bff84e6b5d28536f450df859f2dc5143b1d143"},{"id":3795961647,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7iQccv","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 1**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs`:\n- Around line 124-149: The code builds route keys using a trimmed prefix\n(trimmed_path) but calls Router::nest with the raw\nget_cached_config().prefix_path, causing mismatches and panics; fix by\nnormalizing prefix_path once (trim whitespace, remove trailing slash, and if\nnon-empty ensure it starts with a single leading '/'; represent empty prefix as\nan empty string) and then use that normalized_prefix everywhere: replace\ntrimmed_path usages with normalized_prefix when building docs_path,\nopenapi_path, and spec route_key, and when mounting the module use\nrouter.merge(module_router) if normalized_prefix is empty or\nRouter::nest(&normalized_prefix, module_router) otherwise; update any references\nto get_cached_config().prefix_path, trimmed_path, Router::nest, module_router,\npublic_routes, and openapi_registry.operation_specs accordingly.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#pullrequestreview-3795961647","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#pullrequestreview-3795961647"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-13T09:10:39Z","commit_id":"901795c563a2407020ea9172f131668146cecbd9"},{"id":3796068834,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7iQ2ni","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Some comments are outside the diff and can’t be posted inline due to platform limitations.\n> \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>⚠️ Outside diff range comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `277-288`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n> \n> **Prefix normalization mismatch: MIME validation and rate limiting skip when prefix lacks leading slash.**\n> \n> The router and auth code normalize `prefix_path` to ensure a leading `/`, nesting routes as `/chat/...`. However, `build_mime_validation_map` and `RateLimiterMap::from_specs` only trim trailing slashes—they don't add a leading `/`. This creates a lookup mismatch:\n> \n> - If `prefix_path` is configured as `chat` (no leading `/`), the map stores keys as `chat/...`\n> - The router nests routes at `/chat/...`\n> - Middleware look up using `MatchedPath` (set by Axum router, normalized), which is `/chat/...`\n> - Lookups fail silently; MIME validation and rate limiting are skipped\n> \n> License validation already has the normalization logic (adds leading `/` if missing), so it works correctly.\n> \n> The default `\"/chat\"` is safe, but user configurations without a leading `/` will break MIME validation and rate limiting. Normalize `prefix_path` once in `apply_middleware_stack` before passing to all three map builders, matching the pattern already used in `build_auth_state_from_specs`.\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🛠️ Suggested fix</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n>          let config = self.get_cached_config();\n> +        // Normalize prefix_path once so middleware maps align with router nesting.\n> +        let raw_prefix = config.prefix_path.trim();\n> +        let trimmed = raw_prefix.trim_end_matches('/');\n> +        let normalized_prefix = if trimmed.is_empty() {\n> +            String::new()\n> +        } else if trimmed.starts_with('/') {\n> +            trimmed.to_owned()\n> +        } else {\n> +            format!(\"/{}\", trimmed)\n> +        };\n> \n>          // Collect specs once; used by MIME validation + rate limiting maps.\n>          let specs: Vec<_> = self\n>              .openapi_registry\n>              .operation_specs\n>              .iter()\n>              .map(|e| e.value().clone())\n>              .collect();\n> \n>          // 12) License validation\n>          let license_map = middleware::license_validation::LicenseRequirementMap::from_specs(\n>              &specs,\n> -            &config.prefix_path,\n> +            &normalized_prefix,\n>          );\n> @@\n> -        let rate_map = middleware::rate_limit::RateLimiterMap::from_specs(&specs, &config)?;\n> +        let mut cfg = config.clone();\n> +        cfg.prefix_path = normalized_prefix.clone();\n> +        let rate_map = middleware::rate_limit::RateLimiterMap::from_specs(&specs, &cfg)?;\n> @@\n> -        let mime_map =\n> -            middleware::mime_validation::build_mime_validation_map(&specs, &config.prefix_path);\n> +        let mime_map =\n> +            middleware::mime_validation::build_mime_validation_map(&specs, &normalized_prefix);\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/mime_validation.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`175-175`: **Consider adding a test case with a non-empty prefix.**\n\nThe current test only covers the empty prefix scenario. While integration tests likely cover the prefixed path behavior, a unit test here would provide better coverage of the path construction logic with an actual prefix value.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#pullrequestreview-3796068834","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#pullrequestreview-3796068834"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-13T09:27:24Z","commit_id":"92a694ce09fb4c3345c333f496793ae5d2d94d12"},{"id":3796097882,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7iQ9ta","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 1**\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Some comments are outside the diff and can’t be posted inline due to platform limitations.\n> \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>⚠️ Outside diff range comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>modules/system/api-gateway/tests/cors_tests.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `111-111`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n> \n> **Simplify the duplicate `v1` segment in route paths.**\n> \n> The routes `/tests/v1/cors/v1/cors-test` and `/tests/v1/cors/v1/cors-post` contain a duplicated `v1` segment that doesn't appear elsewhere in the codebase. These should be simplified to `/tests/v1/cors-test` and `/tests/v1/cors-post` respectively.\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/mime_validation.rs`:\n- Around line 22-28: The prefix normalization in mime_validation.rs is\nincomplete: update the logic that builds `path` (using `prefix_path` and\n`spec.path`) to mirror license_validation.rs by trimming trailing slashes from\n`prefix_path`, ensuring a single leading slash is present (so keys become\n\"/chat/path\" not \"chat/path\"), and leaving empty prefix as before; modify the\ncode around the `prefix_path` variable and the block that computes `path` so it\nnormalizes leading slash consistently with `MatchedPath` lookups and\n`license_validation.rs`.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`124-135`: **Consider extracting prefix normalization to a shared helper.**\n\nThe same normalization logic (trim trailing slash, ensure leading slash) is duplicated in `build_auth_state_from_specs`, `rest_finalize`, and each middleware's map builder. A shared helper would reduce duplication and ensure consistent behavior.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Example helper</summary>\n\n```rust\n// In config.rs or a shared utility module\npub fn normalize_prefix_path(raw: &str) -> Option<String> {\n    let trimmed = raw.trim().trim_end_matches('/');\n    if trimmed.is_empty() {\n        None\n    } else if trimmed.starts_with('/') {\n        Some(trimmed.to_owned())\n    } else {\n        Some(format!(\"/{}\", trimmed))\n    }\n}\n```\n</details>\n\n\nAlso applies to: 634-642\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/api-gateway/tests/body_limit_tests.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`213-216`: **Consider updating to use `module_router` for consistency.**\n\nThis test doesn't use the `module_router` pattern that the other tests in this file follow. While functionally correct (the test only validates OpenAPI schema generation, not route serving), updating it for consistency would make the test suite more uniform and easier to maintain.\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Optional: Apply module_router pattern</summary>\n\n```diff\n     let module = BodyLimitTestModule;\n     let router = Router::new();\n-    let _router = module\n-        .register_rest(&ctx, router, &api_gateway)\n+    let module_router = Router::new();\n+    let _module_router = module\n+        .register_rest(&ctx, module_router, &api_gateway)\n         .expect(\"Failed to register routes\");\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/api-gateway/tests/auth_middleware.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`408-412`: **Consider updating to use `module_router` for consistency.**\n\nSimilar to `test_openapi_includes_413_response` in body_limit_tests.rs, this test doesn't use the `module_router` pattern. While functionally correct for OpenAPI schema validation, updating it would improve test suite consistency.\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Optional: Apply module_router pattern</summary>\n\n```diff\n     let router = Router::new();\n+    let module_router = Router::new();\n     let test_module = TestAuthModule;\n-    let _router = test_module\n-        .register_rest(&test_ctx, router, &api_gateway)\n+    let _module_router = test_module\n+        .register_rest(&test_ctx, module_router, &api_gateway)\n         .expect(\"Failed to register routes\");\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#pullrequestreview-3796097882","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfa