(lines 159–450) consistently use `/chat/tests/v1/api/protected`. Since both use the same module routes and `rest_finalize` applies the `/chat` prefix, the auth-enabled test URIs will fail with 404s unless updated to include the prefix.\n> \n> Update all auth-enabled test request URIs from `/tests/v1/api/...` to `/chat/tests/v1/api/...` (lines 632, 657, 680, 703, 727, 750, 776, 812) to match the auth-disabled tests and expected router behavior.\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n> \n> ```\n> Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n> \n> In `@modules/system/api-gateway/tests/auth_middleware.rs` around lines 548 - 586,\n> The auth-enabled tests are calling unprefixed endpoints and thus get 404s\n> because rest_finalize applies the \"/chat\" prefix; update all requests made in\n> the auth-enabled test block to use the \"/chat/tests/v1/api/...\" path instead of\n> \"/tests/v1/api/...\" (look for tests that use create_auth_enabled_router,\n> TestAuthEnabledModule, and the router finalized by api_gateway.rest_finalize) so\n> the URIs match the auth-disabled tests and the finalized router.\n> ```\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Makefile (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`445-446`: **Consider adding `openapi` as a dependency of `all` to ensure generated specs stay in sync with local builds.**\n\nThe `all` target (line 445) currently skips OpenAPI generation even though the `openapi` target exists (line 237) and is part of the development workflow. Adding it as a dependency would ensure API specifications are refreshed during local builds.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed change</summary>\n\n```diff\n-all: build check test-sqlite e2e-local\n+all: openapi build check test-sqlite e2e-local\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@Makefile` around lines 445 - 446, The Makefile's all target currently omits\nthe openapi dependency so generated API specs may be stale; update the all\ntarget's dependency list to include openapi (i.e., make \"all: build check\ntest-sqlite e2e-local openapi\") so the openapi target runs as part of local\nbuilds and keeps specs in sync with other build steps.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nOutside diff comments:\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/tests/auth_middleware.rs`:\n- Around line 548-586: The auth-enabled tests are calling unprefixed endpoints\nand thus get 404s because rest_finalize applies the \"/chat\" prefix; update all\nrequests made in the auth-enabled test block to use the \"/chat/tests/v1/api/...\"\npath instead of \"/tests/v1/api/...\" (look for tests that use\ncreate_auth_enabled_router, TestAuthEnabledModule, and the router finalized by\napi_gateway.rest_finalize) so the URIs match the auth-disabled tests and the\nfinalized router.\n\n---\n\nDuplicate comments:\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/config.rs`:\n- Around line 7-69: The serde default for prefix_path must match the\nApiGatewayConfig::default implementation; ensure the function\ndefault_prefix_path() is used in the struct attribute #[serde(default =\n\"default_prefix_path\")] and that ApiGatewayConfig::default sets prefix_path:\ndefault_prefix_path(); confirm default_prefix_path() returns the intended\n\"/chat\" string and remove any conflicting hard-coded or mismatched defaults in\nthe Default impl or struct attributes so both deserialization and Default\nproduce the same value.\n\n---\n\nNitpick comments:\nIn `@Makefile`:\n- Around line 445-446: The Makefile's all target currently omits the openapi\ndependency so generated API specs may be stale; update the all target's\ndependency list to include openapi (i.e., make \"all: build check test-sqlite\ne2e-local openapi\") so the openapi target runs as part of local builds and keeps\nspecs in sync with other build steps.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#pullrequestreview-3823368305","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#pullrequestreview-3823368305"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-19T03:47:47Z","commit_id":"26345bba7f02b722607f3cc447fe187606d85dc3"},{"id":3824082865,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7j7t-x","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Some comments are outside the diff and can’t be posted inline due to platform limitations.\n> \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>⚠️ Outside diff range comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>modules/system/api-gateway/tests/auth_middleware.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `444-466`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n> \n> **Comments reference outdated paths.**\n> \n> The comments at lines 444 and 462 still reference `/tests/v1/api/users/...` but the actual URIs now use `/chat/tests/v1/api/users/...`.\n> \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>📝 Proposed fix to update comments</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n> -    // Test that /tests/v1/api/users/123 is accessible (matches /tests/v1/api/users/{id})\n> +    // Test that /chat/tests/v1/api/users/123 is accessible (matches /chat/tests/v1/api/users/{id})\n>      let response = router\n>          .clone()\n>          .oneshot(\n>              Request::builder()\n>                  .uri(\"/chat/tests/v1/api/users/123\")\n> ...\n> -    // Test that /tests/v1/api/users/abc-def-456 is also accessible\n> +    // Test that /chat/tests/v1/api/users/abc-def-456 is also accessible\n>      let response = router\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n> \n> ```\n> Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n> \n> In `@modules/system/api-gateway/tests/auth_middleware.rs` around lines 444 - 466,\n> Update the outdated inline comments that mention \"/tests/v1/api/users/...\" to\n> include the current \"/chat\" prefix to match the actual test URIs used in this\n> test (the Request::builder() URIs); specifically change comments around the\n> router oneshot checks that reference the path parameter (the assertions\n> comparing response.status() to StatusCode::OK) so they read\n> \"/chat/tests/v1/api/users/123\" and \"/chat/tests/v1/api/users/abc-def-456\" to\n> reflect the actual Request::builder().uri(...) values.\n> ```\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`129-140`: **Duplicated prefix normalization logic.**\n\nThe prefix normalization pattern (trim, ensure leading slash, remove trailing slash) is duplicated here (lines 129-140) and in `rest_finalize` (lines 631-639). Consider extracting this to a helper method to ensure consistent normalization across the module and reduce code duplication.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Suggested helper method</summary>\n\n```rust\nimpl ApiGateway {\n    /// Normalize prefix_path: trim whitespace, ensure leading '/', remove trailing '/'.\n    /// Returns None if the result is empty.\n    fn normalize_prefix(&self) -> Option<String> {\n        let raw = self.get_cached_config().prefix_path.trim().to_owned();\n        let trimmed = raw.trim_end_matches('/');\n        if trimmed.is_empty() {\n            None\n        } else if trimmed.starts_with('/') {\n            Some(trimmed.to_owned())\n        } else {\n            Some(format!(\"/{trimmed}\"))\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThen use `self.normalize_prefix()` in both `build_route_policy_from_specs` and `rest_finalize`.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs` around lines 129 - 140, Duplicate\nprefix normalization (trim, ensure leading '/', remove trailing '/') appears in\nbuild_route_policy_from_specs and rest_finalize; extract it into a helper on\nApiGateway (e.g., fn normalize_prefix(&self) -> Option<String>) that calls\nself.get_cached_config().prefix_path, performs trim/trim_end_matches('/') and\nreturns None for empty or Some(\"/...\") normalized string, then replace the\ninline logic in build_route_policy_from_specs and rest_finalize with calls to\nself.normalize_prefix() (and use as_deref().unwrap_or(\"\") where needed).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/rate_limit.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`70-75`: **Inconsistent prefix normalization compared to other middleware.**\n\nThe prefix normalization here only trims trailing slashes, but `license_validation.rs` (lines 26-33) and `mime_validation.rs` (lines 21-28) also ensure the prefix has a leading slash if non-empty. If `prefix_path` is configured as `\"chat\"` (without leading slash), rate limit keys will be `chat/path` while other middleware keys will be `/chat/path`, causing lookup mismatches.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Proposed fix to match other middleware normalization</summary>\n\n```diff\n             let prefix = cfg.prefix_path.trim_end_matches('/');\n-            let path = if prefix.is_empty() {\n+            let prefix = if prefix.is_empty() {\n+                String::new()\n+            } else if prefix.starts_with('/') {\n+                prefix.to_owned()\n+            } else {\n+                format!(\"/{prefix}\")\n+            };\n+            let path = if prefix.is_empty() {\n                 spec.path.clone()\n             } else {\n-                format!(\"{}{}\", prefix, spec.path)\n+                format!(\"{prefix}{}\", spec.path)\n             };\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/rate_limit.rs` around lines 70 -\n75, The prefix normalization in rate_limit.rs only trims trailing slashes\ncausing inconsistent keys; update the logic that computes the local variable\nprefix (from cfg.prefix_path) to match license_validation.rs and\nmime_validation.rs by trimming trailing slashes and then, if the resulting\nprefix is non-empty, ensuring it begins with a leading '/' before concatenating\nwith spec.path so the final path construction (the code that uses prefix and\nspec.path) produces the same \"/prefix/...\" form as the other middleware.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/api-gateway/tests/auth_middleware.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`371-375`: **Inconsistent test setup: missing `module_router` pattern for consistency.**\n\nThis test registers routes directly on `router` instead of using the `module_router` pattern applied in all other tests (5 instances across the file). While this works for OpenAPI metadata inspection since the test doesn't call `rest_finalize` or make HTTP requests, adopting the same pattern would improve consistency.\n\nConsider updating to match the pattern used elsewhere:\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested diff</summary>\n\n```diff\n     let router = Router::new();\n+    let module_router = Router::new();\n     let test_module = TestAuthModule;\n-    let _router = test_module\n-        .register_rest(&test_ctx, router, &api_gateway)\n+    let _module_router = test_module\n+        .register_rest(&test_ctx, module_router, &api_gateway)\n         .expect(\"Failed to register routes\");\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/tests/auth_middleware.rs` around lines 371 - 375,\nThe test should use the same module_router pattern for consistency: replace the\ndirect Router::new() usage with a dedicated module_router (e.g. let\nmodule_router = Router::new()), pass that module_router into\nTestAuthModule.register_rest rather than the top-level router, and assign the\nreturned router back into the top-level router variable (as done in other tests)\nso the test mirrors the other five instances that use module_router even though\nrest_finalize or HTTP requests aren’t invoked; update the calls to\nTestAuthModule.register_rest and the variable names accordingly.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nOutside diff comments:\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/tests/auth_middleware.rs`:\n- Around line 444-466: Update the outdated inline comments that mention\n\"/tests/v1/api/users/...\" to include the current \"/chat\" prefix to match the\nactual test URIs used in this test (the Request::builder() URIs); specifically\nchange comments around the router oneshot checks that reference the path\nparameter (the assertions comparing response.status() to StatusCode::OK) so they\nread \"/chat/tests/v1/api/users/123\" and \"/chat/tests/v1/api/users/abc-def-456\"\nto reflect the actual Request::builder().uri(...) values.\n\n---\n\nNitpick comments:\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/rate_limit.rs`:\n- Around line 70-75: The prefix normalization in rate_limit.rs only trims\ntrailing slashes causing inconsistent keys; update the logic that computes the\nlocal variable prefix (from cfg.prefix_path) to match license_validation.rs and\nmime_validation.rs by trimming trailing slashes and then, if the resulting\nprefix is non-empty, ensuring it begins with a leading '/' before concatenating\nwith spec.path so the final path construction (the code that uses prefix and\nspec.path) produces the same \"/prefix/...\" form as the other middleware.\n\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs`:\n- Around line 129-140: Duplicate prefix normalization (trim, ensure leading '/',\nremove trailing '/') appears in build_route_policy_from_specs and rest_finalize;\nextract it into a helper on ApiGateway (e.g., fn normalize_prefix(&self) ->\nOption<String>) that calls self.get_cached_config().prefix_path, performs\ntrim/trim_end_matches('/') and returns None for empty or Some(\"/...\") normalized\nstring, then replace the inline logic in build_route_policy_from_specs and\nrest_finalize with calls to self.normalize_prefix() (and use\nas_deref().unwrap_or(\"\") where needed).\n\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/tests/auth_middleware.rs`:\n- Around line 371-375: The test should use the same module_router pattern for\nconsistency: replace the direct Router::new() usage with a dedicated\nmodule_router (e.g. let module_router = Router::new()), pass that module_router\ninto TestAuthModule.register_rest rather than the top-level router, and assign\nthe returned router back into the top-level router variable (as done in other\ntests) so the test mirrors the other five instances that use module_router even\nthough rest_finalize or HTTP requests aren’t invoked; update the calls to\nTestAuthModule.register_rest and the variable names accordingly.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#pullrequestreview-3824082865","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#pullrequestreview-3824082865"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-19T08:08:19Z","commit_id":"1d0249fbdc2184d5c448596a80fc6a7cd3e8eace"},{"id":3825376331,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7kApxL","user":{"login":"Bechma","id":19294519,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mjk0NTE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19294519?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma","html_url":"https://github.com/Bechma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Please, fix comments, and also, If the end goal is to add a specific prefix for each Rest API let's introduce this complex changes in the logic, let's add a basic `const PREFIX: Option<&'static> = None;` in the trait that can be overridden by the author in case someone want a prefix on the API, otherwise, it will not be applied.\n\nWe can discuss it further in chat if any questions.","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#pullrequestreview-3825376331","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#pullrequestreview-3825376331"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-19T11:56:35Z","commit_id":"1d0249fbdc2184d5c448596a80fc6a7cd3e8eace"},{"id":3829995912,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7kSRmI","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Some comments are outside the diff and can’t be posted inline due to platform limitations.\n> \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>⚠️ Outside diff range comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `138-152`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n> \n> **Operation spec routes lack prefix but docs/openapi routes apply it—inconsistent auth policy construction.**\n> \n> The `build_route_policy_from_specs()` method handles built-in routes and operation specs inconsistently. Lines 132–136 explicitly prefix docs and openapi paths with `middleware::common::prefixed_path(prefix, ...)` before adding them to `public_routes`. However, operation spec routes (lines 138–150) use `spec.path` directly without applying the prefix, despite all routes being looked up by the same auth policy at request time.\n> \n> This inconsistency suggests either:\n> - Doc/openapi paths should NOT be prefixed (if axum's `Router::nest()` strips the prefix in nested middleware), making specs correct\n> - Or operation spec paths SHOULD be prefixed (if prefix is NOT stripped), making docs/openapi correct\n> \n> The license and MIME validation middleware receive the spec paths and `prefix_path` separately and apply the prefix themselves, suggesting the pattern should be consistent. Either apply prefix to all route keys upfront, or apply it uniformly within each middleware layer.\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n> \n> ```\n> Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n> \n> In `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs` around lines 138 - 152, The auth\n> route keys built from operation_specs are missing the common prefix, causing\n> inconsistency with docs/openapi routes; in build_route_policy_from_specs() apply\n> middleware::common::prefixed_path(prefix, &spec.path) when constructing the\n> route_key for both public_routes and authenticated_routes (use\n> spec.method.clone() with the prefixed path) so that all routes use the same\n> prefixed key format as the docs/openapi entries, or alternatively remove\n> prefixing from the docs/openapi branch—ensure the change is applied where\n> operation_specs (operation_specs.iter()/spec.path) are handled and that\n> middleware layers (license/MIME) still receive prefix_path as before.\n> ```\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/common.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`23-47`: **Good test coverage for prefix variations.**\n\nThe tests cover the key scenarios: empty prefix, with/without leading slash, and trailing slash handling. Consider adding a test for a prefix that's just `/` (e.g., `prefixed_path(\"/\", \"/v1/users\")`) to ensure it behaves as expected (should return `/v1/users`).\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Optional: Add test for root prefix</summary>\n\n```diff\n+    #[test]\n+    fn prefix_root_slash_only() {\n+        assert_eq!(prefixed_path(\"/\", \"/v1/users\"), \"/v1/users\");\n+    }\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/common.rs` around lines 23 - 47,\nAdd a unit test in the tests module that calls prefixed_path(\"/\", \"/v1/users\")\nand asserts it returns \"/v1/users\"; place it alongside the existing tests (e.g.,\nname it root_prefix_returns_spec_path) to verify prefixed_path correctly treats\na single \"/\" prefix as no prefix.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`613-621`: **Consider reusing `common::prefixed_path` for prefix normalization.**\n\nThe prefix normalization logic here (lines 613-621) duplicates the logic in `middleware::common::prefixed_path`. While the current implementation is correct, extracting it to use the shared utility would improve maintainability and reduce duplication.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Proposed refactor to use shared utility</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        let raw_prefix = config.prefix_path.trim();\n-        let trimmed = raw_prefix.trim_end_matches('/');\n-        let prefix = if trimmed.is_empty() {\n-            None\n-        } else if trimmed.starts_with('/') {\n-            Some(trimmed.to_owned())\n-        } else {\n-            Some(format!(\"/{trimmed}\"))\n-        };\n+        // Use empty path to get just the normalized prefix\n+        let normalized = middleware::common::prefixed_path(&config.prefix_path, \"\");\n+        let prefix = if normalized.is_empty() {\n+            None\n+        } else {\n+            Some(normalized)\n+        };\n```\n\nNote: This requires `prefixed_path(\"prefix\", \"\")` to return just the normalized prefix, which the current implementation does.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs` around lines 613 - 621, Replace the\nmanual prefix normalization in module.rs with the shared utility\nmiddleware::common::prefixed_path: call\nprefixed_path(config.prefix_path.as_str(), \"\") (or the correct module path for\nthat function) to get the normalized prefix string, then convert an empty result\nto None and a non-empty result to Some(normalized) for the variable currently\nnamed prefix; also add the necessary use/import for\nmiddleware::common::prefixed_path and remove the duplicated trimming logic.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nOutside diff comments:\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs`:\n- Around line 138-152: The auth route keys built from operation_specs are\nmissing the common prefix, causing inconsistency with docs/openapi routes; in\nbuild_route_policy_from_specs() apply middleware::common::prefixed_path(prefix,\n&spec.path) when constructing the route_key for both public_routes and\nauthenticated_routes (use spec.method.clone() with the prefixed path) so that\nall routes use the same prefixed key format as the docs/openapi entries, or\nalternatively remove prefixing from the docs/openapi branch—ensure the change is\napplied where operation_specs (operation_specs.iter()/spec.path) are handled and\nthat middleware layers (license/MIME) still receive prefix_path as before.\n\n---\n\nNitpick comments:\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/common.rs`:\n- Around line 23-47: Add a unit test in the tests module that calls\nprefixed_path(\"/\", \"/v1/users\") and asserts it returns \"/v1/users\"; place it\nalongside the existing tests (e.g., name it root_prefix_returns_spec_path) to\nverify prefixed_path correctly treats a single \"/\" prefix as no prefix.\n\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs`:\n- Around line 613-621: Replace the manual prefix normalization in module.rs with\nthe shared utility middleware::common::prefixed_path: call\nprefixed_path(config.prefix_path.as_str(), \"\") (or the correct module path for\nthat function) to get the normalized prefix string, then convert an empty result\nto None and a non-empty result to Some(normalized) for the variable currently\nnamed prefix; also add the necessary use/import for\nmiddleware::common::prefixed_path and remove the duplicated trimming logic.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#pullrequestreview-3829995912","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#pullrequestreview-3829995912"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-20T05:02:56Z","commit_id":"ccd78de2a2fcb71f5123af27efa552fe3ffb30f1"},{"id":3830038438,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7kSb-m","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 1**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/api-gateway/tests/mime_validation_integration.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`38-81`: **Consider adding a test case for prefixed paths.**\n\nAll tests use an empty prefix. Consider adding a test that verifies MIME validation works correctly when a prefix is configured (e.g., `\"/cf\"`), ensuring the middleware correctly matches prefixed routes.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/tests/mime_validation_integration.rs` around lines\n38 - 81, Add a new async test (e.g.,\ntest_middleware_allows_configured_content_type_with_prefix) that mirrors\ntest_middleware_allows_configured_content_type but passes a non-empty prefix\n(e.g., \"/cf\") into build_mime_validation_map and registers the route with the\nsame prefix (e.g., Router::new().route(\"/cf/api/data\", post(test_handler))) then\nsend the request to \"/cf/api/data\" with the allowed \"application/json\"\ncontent-type and assert StatusCode::OK; this verifies mime_validation_middleware\ncorrectly matches prefixed routes when using build_mime_validation_map and\nmime_validation_middleware.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/common.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`28-46`: **Consider adding a test for spec_path edge cases.**\n\nThe current tests cover prefix variations well, but consider adding a test to document the expected behavior when `spec_path` doesn't start with `/`, or when it's empty.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>💡 Suggested additional test cases</summary>\n\n```diff\n     #[test]\n     fn prefix_with_trailing_slash() {\n         assert_eq!(prefixed_path(\"/cf/\", \"/v1/users\"), \"/cf/v1/users\");\n     }\n+\n+    #[test]\n+    fn spec_path_without_leading_slash() {\n+        // Documents expected behavior - no double slash inserted\n+        assert_eq!(prefixed_path(\"/cf\", \"v1/users\"), \"/cfv1/users\");\n+    }\n+\n+    #[test]\n+    fn empty_spec_path() {\n+        assert_eq!(prefixed_path(\"/cf\", \"\"), \"/cf\");\n+    }\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/common.rs` around lines 28 - 46,\nAdd unit tests for prefixed_path covering spec_path edge cases: one test where\nspec_path does not start with a leading slash (e.g., \"v1/users\") and assert the\nreturned path is normalized to include a leading slash with the prefix (e.g.,\n\"/cf/v1/users\"), and one test where spec_path is empty (\"\"), asserting the\nresult is just the normalized prefix (e.g., \"/cf\"). Add these tests alongside\nthe existing prefixed_path tests so behavior is documented and ensured for both\nnon-leading-slash and empty spec_path inputs.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nInline comments:\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/rate_limit.rs`:\n- Around line 70-75: The rate-limit middleware currently trims only trailing\nslashes for cfg.prefix_path which can omit a leading slash and create mismatched\nkeys; replace that manual normalization with the shared helper by calling\nsuper::common::prefixed_path(cfg.prefix_path.as_str(), &spec.path) (or the\nequivalent function signature) when computing path so it matches\nlicense_validation.rs and mime_validation.rs behavior and produces a\nconsistently prefixed path for rate-limiting keys.\n\n---\n\nNitpick comments:\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/common.rs`:\n- Around line 28-46: Add unit tests for prefixed_path covering spec_path edge\ncases: one test where spec_path does not start with a leading slash (e.g.,\n\"v1/users\") and assert the returned path is normalized to include a leading\nslash with the prefix (e.g., \"/cf/v1/users\"), and one test where spec_path is\nempty (\"\"), asserting the result is just the normalized prefix (e.g., \"/cf\").\nAdd these tests alongside the existing prefixed_path tests so behavior is\ndocumented and ensured for both non-leading-slash and empty spec_path inputs.\n\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/tests/mime_validation_integration.rs`:\n- Around line 38-81: Add a new async test (e.g.,\ntest_middleware_allows_configured_content_type_with_prefix) that mirrors\ntest_middleware_allows_configured_content_type but passes a non-empty prefix\n(e.g., \"/cf\") into build_mime_validation_map and registers the route with the\nsame prefix (e.g., Router::new().route(\"/cf/api/data\", post(test_handler))) then\nsend the request to \"/cf/api/data\" with the allowed \"application/json\"\ncontent-type and assert StatusCode::OK; this verifies mime_validation_middleware\ncorrectly matches prefixed routes when using build_mime_validation_map and\nmime_validation_middleware.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#pullrequestreview-3830038438","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#pullrequestreview-3830038438"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-20T05:15:13Z","commit_id":"1fb3beb12310653dfa95e0b1651c81deb1db0ec0"},{"id":3830064683,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7kSiYr","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 1**\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Some comments are outside the diff and can’t be posted inline due to platform limitations.\n> \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>⚠️ Outside diff range comments (2)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>Makefile (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `445-446`: _🛠️ Refactor suggestion_ | _🟠 Major_\n> \n> **Add `openapi` to the `all` target dependencies.**  \n> This keeps local builds generating OpenAPI by default, consistent with repo expectations.\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>Suggested update</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n> -all: build check test-sqlite e2e-local\n> +all: openapi build check test-sqlite e2e-local\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n>   \n> Based on learnings, \"Ensure that the default 'all' target in every Makefile under cyberfabric-core includes a dependency on the 'openapi' target so OpenAPI generation runs as part of the local build. Verify that an openapi target exists and that including it does not introduce unnecessary rebuilds or circular dependencies.\"\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n> \n> ```\n> Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n> \n> In `@Makefile` around lines 445 - 446, Update the Makefile's all target so it\n> depends on openapi (change \"all: build check test-sqlite e2e-local\" to include\n> openapi) so OpenAPI generation runs during local builds; ensure an openapi\n> target is defined in this Makefile and that adding openapi does not create\n> circular dependencies with build, check, test-sqlite, or e2e-local (adjust or\n> factor targets if necessary to avoid redundant rebuilds).\n> ```\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> <details>\n> <summary>modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `138-152`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n> \n> **Auth route policy uses unprefixed paths while license/MIME maps use prefixed paths, causing lookups to fail.**\n> \n> `authenticated_routes` and `public_routes` are populated with raw `spec.path` (line 141), but `LicenseRequirementMap::from_specs` and `build_mime_validation_map` apply `config.prefix_path` (lines 203, 262). Since the auth middleware uses `req.uri().path()` for lookups (which contains the full prefixed path after routing), the route policy matchers will fail to find matching entries while license/MIME validation will succeed.\n> \n> Apply the prefix to route keys in `build_route_policy_from_specs` for consistency:\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🐛 Proposed fix</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n>          for spec in &self.openapi_registry.operation_specs {\n>              let spec = spec.value();\n>  \n> -            let path = spec.path.clone();\n> -\n> -            let route_key = (spec.method.clone(), path);\n> +            let path = middleware::common::prefixed_path(prefix, &spec.path);\n> +            let route_key = (spec.method.clone(), path);\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n> \n> ```\n> Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n> \n> In `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs` around lines 138 - 152, The auth\n> route keys are built from raw spec.path causing mismatches with other maps that\n> use config.prefix_path; in build_route_policy_from_specs (the loop that\n> populates authenticated_routes and public_routes), prepend config.prefix_path to\n> spec.path before creating route_key so the tuple (spec.method.clone(),\n> prefixed_path) matches the keys used by LicenseRequirementMap::from_specs and\n> build_mime_validation_map and the middleware lookup via req.uri().path(); update\n> both authenticated_routes.insert(...) and public_routes.insert(...) to use the\n> prefixed path.\n> ```\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nInline comments:\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/config.rs`:\n- Around line 53-61: The Default impl for ApiGatewayConfig is causing infinite\nrecursion because it uses the struct update syntax with ..Default::default(),\nwhich calls ApiGatewayConfig::default() again; replace that by explicitly\ninitializing every field of ApiGatewayConfig inside impl Default::default\n(remove the ..Default::default() spread) and assign each field either its\nexplicit default value or by calling the appropriate helper default functions\n(e.g., use default_require_auth_by_default() and default_prefix_path() for those\nfields), so that ApiGatewayConfig::default returns a fully constructed struct\nwithout delegating to Default::default() recursively.\n\n---\n\nOutside diff comments:\nIn `@Makefile`:\n- Around line 445-446: Update the Makefile's all target so it depends on openapi\n(change \"all: build check test-sqlite e2e-local\" to include openapi) so OpenAPI\ngeneration runs during local builds; ensure an openapi target is defined in this\nMakefile and that adding openapi does not create circular dependencies with\nbuild, check, test-sqlite, or e2e-local (adjust or factor targets if necessary\nto avoid redundant rebuilds).\n\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs`:\n- Around line 138-152: The auth route keys are built from raw spec.path causing\nmismatches with other maps that use config.prefix_path; in\nbuild_route_policy_from_specs (the loop that populates authenticated_routes and\npublic_routes), prepend config.prefix_path to spec.path before creating\nroute_key so the tuple (spec.method.clone(), prefixed_path) matches the keys\nused by LicenseRequirementMap::from_specs and build_mime_validation_map and the\nmiddleware lookup via req.uri().path(); update both\nauthenticated_routes.insert(...) and public_routes.insert(...) to use the\nprefixed path.\n\n---\n\nDuplicate comments:\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/rate_limit.rs`:\n- Around line 70-77: The prefix normalization here is inconsistent; replace the\nmanual trim_end_matches logic with the shared helper from\nsuper::common::prefixed_path so the resulting path always has the same\nleading-slash behavior as other middlewares. Concretely, compute path by calling\nsuper::common::prefixed_path(&cfg.prefix_path, &spec.path) (instead of building\nprefix + spec.path) and then use that path when constructing key =\n(spec.method.clone(), path.clone()) to ensure consistent rate-limit keys.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#pullrequestreview-3830064683","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#pullrequestreview-3830064683"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-20T05:27:06Z","commit_id":"9269651c574e1ecad3d0c2eaadb8b96e81116b57"},{"id":3830095823,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7kSp_P","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nDuplicate comments:\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs`:\n- Around line 125-151: The auth route keys are built from raw spec.path which\nomits the gateway prefix, risking auth bypass when MatchedPath includes the\nprefix; update the code that builds route_key (used for authenticated_routes and\npublic_routes) to apply the same prefixing helper as elsewhere (use\nbinding.prefix_path and middleware::common::prefixed_path) so route_key is\n(spec.method.clone(), prefixed_path(prefix, &spec.path)) instead of\n(spec.method.clone(), spec.path.clone()); ensure this change is made where\nopenapi_registry.operation_specs are iterated (the block that references\nget_cached_config(), binding.prefix_path, authenticated_routes, and\npublic_routes).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#pullrequestreview-3830095823","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/602#pullrequestreview-3830095823"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/602"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-20T05:37:58Z","commit_id":"73ac29bb679a637d59c8f4a3cd1343451ea201ec"},{"id":3853595473,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7lsTNR","user":{"login":"Bechma","id":19294519,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mjk0NTE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19294519?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma","html_url":"https://github.com/Bechma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Remember to change the documentation generation.\nThere are hardcoded paths to /openapi.json /docs and assets\nThose need to take into consideration the prefix, if any.\n\nAlso, make sure to 