 avoid user confusion.  \n\n<details>\n<summary>✏️ Suggested wording tweak</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    /// (default: off, uses stricter discovery regex that catches malformed IDs)\n+    /// (default: off, uses a permissive discovery regex to catch malformed IDs)\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n    /// Strict mode: require all GTS identifiers to be perfectly formatted\n    /// (default: off, uses a permissive discovery regex to catch malformed IDs)\n    ///\n    /// When enabled, uses permissive regex to catch and report ALL malformed GTS IDs.\n    /// When disabled (default), only validates well-formed patterns (fewer false positives).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs` around lines 88 - 92, Update the Strict\nmode help comment in main.rs to correctly describe its behavior: change the\nphrase \"stricter discovery regex\" to indicate it uses a permissive discovery\nregex that catches malformed IDs, and reword the surrounding sentences so they\nstate that enabling strict mode uses a permissive (more inclusive) regex to\ndetect malformed GTS identifiers while the default disables that permissive\ndiscovery to reduce false positives; edit the doc comment block labeled \"Strict\nmode\" (the comment above the strict-mode option/flag) to reflect this accurate\nwording.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commits e6d8dfd to 2969660","created_at":"2026-02-12T17:44:23Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T16:54:47Z","h