    strict: bool,\n+) -> Vec<DocValidationError> {\n+    if verbose {\n+        eprintln!(\"  Scanning: {}\", path.display());\n+    }\n+\n+    match path.extension().and_then(|e| e.to_str()) {\n+        Some(\"md\") => scan_markdown_file(path, vendor, verbose, max_file_size, strict),\n+        Some(\"json\") => scan_json_file(path, vendor, verbose, max_file_size, scan_keys),\n+        Some(\"yaml\" | \"yml\") => scan_yaml_file(path, vendor, verbose, max_file_size, scan_keys),\n+        _ => {","path":"apps/gts-docs-validator/src/scanner.rs","commit_id":"49e69d4dd72edc297f621afaccd64b100ba27e00","original_commit_id":"4910ea81d8189b0056e4724b45625823d03e84a6","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Handle uppercase extensions consistently.**  \n`find_files` lowercases extensions, but `scan_file` matches the raw extension, so files like `FOO.YAML` are discovered then skipped. Normalize the extension before matching.  \n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    match path.extension().and_then(|e| e.to_str()) {\n-        Some(\"md\") => scan_markdown_file(path, vendor, verbose, max_file_size, strict),\n-        Some(\"json\") => scan_json_file(path, vendor, verbose, max_file_size, scan_keys),\n-        Some(\"yaml\" | \"yml\") => scan_yaml_file(path, vendor, verbose, max_file_size, scan_keys),\n+    let ext = path\n+        .extension()\n+        .and_then(|e| e.to_str())\n+        .map(|s| s.to_ascii_lowercase());\n+    match ext.as_deref() {\n+        Some(\"md\") => scan_markdown_file(path, vendor, verbose, max_file_size, strict),\n+        Some(\"json\") => scan_json_file(path, vendor, verbose, max_file_size, scan_keys),\n+        Some(\"yaml\" | \"yml\") => scan_yaml_file(path, vendor, verbose, max_file_size, scan_keys),\n         _ => {\n             if verbose {\n                 eprintln!(\"  Skipping {} (unsupported extension)\", path.display());\n             }\n             vec![]\n         }\n     }\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n    let ext = path\n        .extension()\n        .and_then(|e| e.to_str())\n        .map(|s| s.to_ascii_lowercase());\n    match ext.as_deref() {\n        Some(\"md\") => scan_markdown_file(path, vendor, verbose, max_file_size, strict),\n        Some(\"json\") => scan_json_file(path, vendor, verbose, max_file_size, scan_keys),\n        Some(\"yaml\" | \"yml\") => scan_yaml_file(path, vendor, verbose, max_file_size, scan_keys),\n        _ => {\n            if verbose {\n                eprintln!(\"  Skipping {} (unsupported extension)\", path.display());\n            }\n            vec![]\n        }\n    }\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@apps/gts-docs-validator/src/scanner.rs` around lines 147 - 151, The extension\nmatching in scan_file currently uses the raw extension from\npath.extension().and_then(|e| e.to_str()) causing uppercase extensions (e.g.,\nFOO.YAML) to be skipped; normalize the extension string to lowercase before\nmatching (e.g., call to_lowercase or map the &str to a lowercased String) and\nthen match against \"md\", \"json\", \"yaml\" | \"yml\" so scan_file behaves\nconsistently with find_files; update the match that calls\nscan_markdown_file/scan_json_file/scan_yaml_file to use the normalized extension\nvariable.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 2584661","created_at":"2026-02-12T17:44:23Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T17:23:10Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/592#discussion_r2800228745","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/592","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2800228745"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/592#discussion_r2800228745"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/592"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2800228745/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":147,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":151,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":92,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2841991912","pull_request_