te_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Empty vendor string is not validated.**\n\n`--vendor \"\"` produces `VendorPolicy::MustMatch(\"\")` with no guard, which could result in every GTS ID failing vendor validation silently. A trim + emptiness check guards against accidental shell quoting issues.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛡️ Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    validation_config.vendor_policy = match cli.vendor {\n-        Some(v) => VendorPolicy::MustMatch(v),\n-        None => VendorPolicy::Any,\n-    };\n+    validation_config.vendor_policy = match cli.vendor {\n+        Some(v) => {\n+            let v = v.trim().to_string();\n+            if v.is_empty() {\n+                eprintln!(\"Error: --vendor value must not be empty\");\n+                return ExitCode::FAILURE;\n+            }\n+            VendorPolicy::MustMatch(v)\n+        }\n+        None => VendorPolicy::Any,\n+    };\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n    validation_config.vendor_policy = match cli.vendor {\n        Some(v) => {\n            let v = v.trim().to_string();\n            if v.is_empty() {\n                eprintln!(\"Error: --vendor value must not be empty\");\n                return ExitCode::FAILURE;\n            }\n            VendorPolicy::MustMatch(v)\n        }\n        None => VendorPolicy::Any,\n    };\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs` around lines 118 - 120, The vendor\nhandling sets validation_config.vendor_policy to\nVendorPolicy::MustMatch(cli.vendor) even when cli.vendor is an empty or\nwhitespace-only string; change the logic to trim the provided cli.vendor and\nonly create VendorPolicy::MustMatch when the trimmed string is non-empty,\notherwise fall back to VendorPolicy::Any. Update the match/assignment that\nreferences cli.vendor and validation_config.vendor_policy (and the\nVendorPolicy::MustMatch enum variant) to perform the trim() + is_empty() check\nbefore deciding which variant to set.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:churro -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-23T17:30:18Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T17:30:20Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/592#discussion_r2842146502","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/592","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2842146502"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/592#discussion_r2842146502"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/592"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2842146502/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":118,"original_start_line":118,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":120,"original_line":120,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":94,"position":94,"subject_type":"line"}],"source_reviews":[{"id":3792610172,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7iDqN8","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/follow