ome(v) => VendorPolicy::MustMatch(v),\n+            None => VendorPolicy::Any,\n+        },\n+        scan_keys: cli.scan_keys,\n+        discovery_mode: if cli.strict {\n+            DiscoveryMode::Heuristic\n+        } else {\n+            DiscoveryMode::StrictSpecOnly\n+        },\n+        skip_tokens: cli.skip_tokens,\n+        ..ValidationConfig::default()\n+    };\n```\n</details>\n\n> Note: this assumes `FsSourceConfig` and `ValidationConfig` have public fields, which they must if the current sequential-assignment code compiles. If the fields are `pub(crate)`, the current approach is the only option.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs` around lines 112 - 128, Replace the\ncurrent mutable-then-assign pattern for FsSourceConfig and ValidationConfig by\nconstructing them with struct literals plus ..Default::default() to avoid\nunnecessary mutability: build an FsSourceConfig { paths: paths, exclude:\ncli.exclude, max_file_size: cli.max_file_size, ..Default::default() } and a\nValidationConfig { vendor_policy: match cli.vendor { Some(v) =>\nVendorPolicy::MustMatch(v), None => VendorPolicy::Any }, scan_keys:\ncli.scan_keys, discovery_mode: if cli.strict { DiscoveryMode::Heuristic } else {\nDiscoveryMode::StrictSpecOnly }, skip_tokens: cli.skip_tokens,\n..Default::default() } so you can remove the mut bindings for fs_config and\nvalidation_config while keeping the same field values.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`137-139`: **Prefer match-ergonomics over the `ref` keyword (Rust 2021+/2024 edition).**\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Proposed nit</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        if let VendorPolicy::MustMatch(ref vendor) = validation_config.vendor_policy {\n+        if let VendorPolicy::MustMatch(vendor) = &validation_config.vendor_policy {\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each fi