97-105`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n> \n> **Explicit paths bypass the existence check applied to defaults.**\n> \n> Default scan dirs are filtered by `p.exists()` (line 101), but user-supplied paths (line 104) skip this check entirely. A nonexistent explicit path propagates into `validate_fs` and surfaces as a less actionable `\"Error: ...\"` message instead of a clear CLI-level diagnostic.\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🛡️ Proposed fix</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n>  } else {\n> -    cli.paths\n> +    let invalid: Vec<_> = cli.paths.iter().filter(|p| !p.exists()).collect();\n> +    if !invalid.is_empty() {\n> +        for p in &invalid {\n> +            eprintln!(\"Error: path does not exist: {}\", p.display());\n> +        }\n> +        return ExitCode::FAILURE;\n> +    }\n> +    cli.paths\n>  };\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n> \n> ```\n> Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n> \n> In `@apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs` around lines 97 - 105, The code builds\n> `paths` from `DEFAULT_SCAN_DIRS` with an existence filter but directly uses\n> `cli.paths` when provided, allowing nonexistent user paths to reach\n> `validate_fs`; update the `paths` construction so that when `cli.paths` is\n> non-empty you validate each `PathBuf` (from `cli.paths`) with `.exists()` and\n> produce a clear CLI-level error (or exit) for any missing path instead of\n> passing them to `validate_fs`; reference `DEFAULT_SCAN_DIRS`, the `paths`\n> variable, `cli.paths`, and `validate_fs` when making this change.\n> ```\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`131-135`: **Redundant type annotation in closure.**\n\nThe `: &PathBuf` annotation on line 134 is inferred by the compiler; removing it keeps the closure concise.\n\n<details>\n<summary>✏️ Proposed cleanup</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        let path_list: Vec<String> = fs_config\n-            .paths\n-            .iter()\n-            .map(|p: &PathBuf| p.display().to_string())\n-            .collect();\n+        let path_list: Vec<String> = fs_config\n+            .paths\n+            .iter()\n+            .map(|p| p.display().to_string())\n+            .collect();\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs` around lines 131 - 135, The closure\nmapping fs_config.paths into path_list has an unnecessary explicit type\nannotation (`: &PathBuf`) — remove the `: &PathBuf` from the closure in the call\nthat builds path_list so it becomes map(|p| p.display().to_string()), relying on\ntype inference for fs_config.paths and the variable p.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nInline comments:\nIn `@apps/gts-docs-validator/Cargo.toml`:\n- Around line 19-20: The Cargo.toml adds the workspace dependency gts-validator\n(symbol: gts-validator = { workspace = true }) but this dependency is not\nrecorded in DEPENDENCIES.md; update DEPENDENCIES.md to add an entry for\ngts-validator (include name, pinned version 0.8.2, purpose/notes, and any\nlicensing or source details per the project's dependency documentation template)\nso the workspace-level addition in Cargo.toml is documented before merge.\n\nIn `@apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs`:\n- Around line 118-120: The vendor handling sets validation_config.vendor_policy\nto VendorPolicy::MustMatch(cli.vendor) even when cli.vendor is an empty or\nwhitespace-only string; change the logic to trim the provided cli.vendor and\nonly create VendorPolicy::MustMatch when the trimmed string is non-empty,\notherwise fall back to VendorPolicy::Any. Update the match/assignment that\nreferences cli.vendor and validation_config.vendor_policy (and the\nVendorPolicy::MustMatch enum variant) to perform the trim() + is_empty() check\nbefore deciding which variant to set.\n\n---\n\nOutside diff comments:\nIn `@apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs`:\n- Around line 97-105: The code builds `paths` from `DEFAULT_SCAN_DIRS` with an\nexistence filter but directly uses `cli.paths` when provided, allowing\nnonexistent user paths to reach `validate_fs`; update the `paths` construction\nso that when `cli.paths` is non-empty you validate each `PathBuf` (from\n`cli.paths`) with `.exists()` and produce a clear CLI-level error (or exit) for\nany missing path instead of passing them to `validate_fs`; reference\n`DEFAULT_SCAN_DIRS`, the `paths` variable, `cli.paths`, and `validate_fs` when\nmaking this change.\n\n---\n\nNitpick comments:\nIn `@apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs`:\n- Around line 131-135: The closure mapping fs_config.paths into path_list has an\nunnecessary explicit type annotation (`: &PathBuf`) — remove the `: &PathBuf`\nfrom the closure in the call that builds path_list so it becomes map(|p|\np.display().to_string()), relying on type inference for fs_config.paths and the\nvariable p.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Review info</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Pro\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 2969660fd3b10ebf18300217f97250c4a1db5339 and 258466144a384c4095789268e263bd2d41bedb30.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⛔ Files ignored due to path filters (1)</summary>\n\n* `Cargo.lock` is excluded by `!**/*.lock`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (6)</summary>\n\n* `Cargo.toml`\n* `apps/gts-docs-validator/Cargo.toml`\n* `apps/gts-docs-v