url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2802401829","pull_request_review_id":3795180242,"id":2802401829,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6nCUIl","diff_hunk":"@@ -353,6 +353,8 @@ regex = \"1.10\"\n # CLI and terminal output\n glob = \"0.3\"\n colored = \"3.1\"\n+supports-color = \"3\"\n+enable-ansi-support = \"0.2\"","path":"Cargo.toml","commit_id":"f29e2d446c2721b42038a2461ff04cac2efd4da8","original_commit_id":"f29e2d446c2721b42038a2461ff04cac2efd4da8","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# First, find and read the DEPENDENCIES.md guideline file\nfind . -name \"DEPENDENCIES.md\" -o -name \"dependencies.md\" 2>/dev/null | head -20\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 100\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check the Cargo.toml file context around lines 356-357\nif [ -f Cargo.toml ]; then\n  echo \"=== Lines 350-365 of Cargo.toml ===\"\n  sed -n '350,365p' Cargo.toml\nelse\n  echo \"Cargo.toml not found at root\"\n  find . -name \"Cargo.toml\" -type f | head -5\nfi\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 447\n\n---\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`supports-color crate rust version 3 latest`\n\n💡 Result:\n\nThe latest **v3.x** release of the Rust crate **`supports-color`** (imported as `supports_color`) is **3.0.2**. [1][2]\n\n---\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`enable-ansi-support crate rust latest version`\n\n💡 Result:\n\nThe latest published version of the Rust crate **`enable-ansi-support`** is **`0.3.1`**. [1]\n\nAdd it to your `Cargo.toml` like:\n\n```toml\n[dependencies]\nenable-ansi-support = \"0.3.1\"\n```  \n\n**Docs:** `enable_ansi_support` (module name uses underscores). [1]\n\n**Sources:**  \n[1] ([docs.rs](https://docs.rs/crate/enable-ansi-support/0.3.1?utm_source=openai))\n\nCitations:\n\n- 1: https://docs.rs/crate/enable-ansi-support/0.3.1?utm_source=openai\n\n---\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`supports-color rust crate security vulnerabilities`\n\n💡 Result:\n\n## Rust crate `supports-color` (crates.io)\n\n- I did **not find any published RustSec advisory** for the Rust crate `supports-color` (the one currently at **v3.0.2**). RustSec is the main advisory database for Rust crates, and crates.io’s new **Security** tab is sourced from RustSec advisories. [1][2]\n\n## Important name collision: npm `supports-color` (JavaScript)\n\n- There *has* been a reported **security incident involving the npm package** `supports-color` (malicious code reported in a compromised release). This is **not the Rust crate**, but it’s easy to confuse them because the Rust crate is a port “by the same name.” [3][4]\n\n### Sources\n[1] Rust blog (crates.io Security tab / RustSec-backed advisories) ([blog.rust-lang.org](https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/01/21/crates-io-development-update/?utm_source=openai))  \n[2] RustSec overview (Rust ecosystem advisory DB) ([rustsec.org](https://rustsec.org/?utm_source=openai))  \n[3] Vulert report about npm `supports-color` malicious code ([vulert.com](https://vulert.com/vuln-db/npm-supports-color-238662?utm_source=openai))  \n[4] Snyk note about npm `supports-color` incident ([security.snyk.io](https://security.snyk.io/package/npm/supports-color?utm_source=openai))\n\nCitations:\n\n- 1: https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/01/21/crates-io-development-update/?utm_source=openai\n- 2: https://rustsec.org/?utm_source=openai\n- 3: https://vulert.com/vuln-db/npm-supports-color-238662?utm_source=openai\n- 4: https://security.snyk.io/package/npm/supports-color?utm_source=openai\n\n---\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`enable-ansi-support rust crate security vulnerabilities`\n\n💡 Result:\n\nNo RustSec / OSV / CVE entries specifically targeting the **`enable-ansi-support`** crate turned up in the public advisory databases during this search; it appears to be a small utility crate that **only enables Windows console “virtual terminal” (ANSI) processing via Windows API calls**, and is a no-op on non-Windows platforms. [1][2]\n\nWhat you *should* worry about is the **security impact of enabling ANSI rendering** in your application: if you print/log **untrusted input** to a terminal with ANSI enabled, attackers can inject escape sequences that manipulate what operators see (e.g., clear screen, move cursor, spoof prompts). This class of issue is documented in Rust ecosystem advisories—for example, **`tracing-subscriber`** had an ANSI escape sequence injection issue in versions **before 0.3.20** (CVE-2025-58160 / RUSTSEC-2025-0055), fixed by escaping ANSI control characters. [3]\n\nPractical mitigations:\n- **Do not render untrusted input as terminal output** without escaping/sanitizing control characters.\n- If you use `tracing-subscriber`, **upgrade to `>= 0.3.20`** to get the escaping fix. [3]\n\n**Sources:** docs.rs crate docs for `enable-ansi-support` [1][2]; RustSec advisory RUSTSEC-2025-0055 for ANSI injection in `tracing-subscriber` [3].  \n\nReferences:  \n[1] https://docs.rs/enable-ansi-support/latest/enable_ansi_support/  \n[2] https://docs.rs/crate/enable-ansi-support/latest  \n[3] https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2025-0055\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat -n ./guidelines/DEPENDENCIES.md\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 1194\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if tracing-subscriber is in Cargo.toml and its version\ngrep -n \"tracing-subscriber\" Cargo.toml\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 128\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Get the exact version of tracing-subscriber\ngrep -A 2 \"tracing-subscriber = \" Cargo.toml\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 154\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Update `enable-ansi-support` to `\"0.3\"` or latest compatible version.**\n\nThe `supports-color = \"3\"` dependency is current (latest is 3.0.2) and has no known security advisories. However, `enable-ansi-support = \"0.2\"` is outdated—the latest published version is 0.3.1. Update this dependency to maintain currency.\n\nAdditionally, when rendering terminal output with ANSI support enabled, ensure untrusted input is properly escaped to prevent ANSI escape sequence injection attacks. If using `tracing-subscriber`, verify the version is at least `0.3.20` to get the ANSI character escaping fix (CVE-2025-58160/RUSTSEC-2025-0055).\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@Cargo.toml` around lines 356 - 357, The Cargo.toml entry for the crate\nenable-ansi-support is pinned to \"0.2\" and must be updated to \"0.3\" (preferably\n\"0.3.1\") to stay current; change the dependency version for enable-ansi-support\nto 0.3.x and ensure supports-color remains at \"3\". Also audit any\nterminal/console output code paths that render untrusted input (e.g., places\nthat pass user strings into formatters or tracing logs) to escape or sanitize\nANSI control sequences before emitting them, and if you use tracing-subscriber,\nbump its dependency to at least \"0.3.20\" to include the ANSI escaping fix\n(CVE/RUSTSEC fix).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-13T05:44:06Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T05:44:07Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/590#discussion_r2802401829","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/590","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2802401829"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/590#discussion_r2802401829"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/590"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2802401829/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":356,"original_start_line":356,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":357,"original_line":357,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":5,"position":5,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2802401833","pull_request_review_id":3795180242,"id":2802401833,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6nCUIp","diff_hunk":"@@ -383,6 +383,15 @@ fn create_crate_file_writer(\n     }\n }\n \n+// ================= ANSI color support =================\n+\n+/// Returns `true` if stderr supports ANSI color escape codes.\n+/// On Windows, also attempts to enable virtual-terminal color processing.\n+fn stderr_supports_ansi() -> bool {\n+    let _ = enable_ansi_support::enable_ansi_support();\n+    supports_color::on(supports_color::Stream::Stderr).is_some_and(|level| level.has_basic)\n+}","path":"libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/host/logging.rs","commit_id":"f29e2d446c2721b42038a2461ff04cac2efd4da8","original_commit_id":"f29e2d446c2721b42038a2461ff04cac2efd4da8","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`supports-color rust crate ColorLevel has_basic API v3`\n\n💡 Result:\n\nIn **supports-color v3** (current docs show **v3.0.2**), `ColorLevel` includes a **public** `has_basic: bool` field (alongside `has_256` and `has_16m`). You access it like:\n\n```rust\nif let Some(level) = supports_color::on(supports_color::Stream::Stdout) {\n    if level.has_basic { /* basic ANSI colors supported */ }\n}\n```  \n\n[1]\n\n**Source(s):**  \n[1] docs.rs `supports-color` v3 `ColorLevel` struct fields (`has_basic`, `has_256`, `has_16m`) and example usage.\n\n---\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`enable-ansi-support rust crate API documentation`\n\n💡 Result:\n\nThe **`enable-ansi-support`** Rust crate’s API docs are on **docs.rs**: ([docs.rs](https://docs.rs/enable-ansi-support/latest/enable_ansi_support/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- Crate/module docs: ([docs.rs](https://docs.rs/enable-ansi-support/latest/enable_ansi_support/?utm_source=openai))  \n- Crate page (includes version/MSRV notes): ([docs.rs](https://docs.rs/crate/enable-ansi-support/latest?utm_source=openai))  \n\n### What the API provides\nIt provides a single function:\n\n- `enable_ansi_support::enable_ansi_support() -> Result<(), std::io::Error>` (enables ANSI escape codes on **Windows 10+**; **no-op** on non-Windows). ([docs.rs](https://docs.rs/enable-ansi-support/latest/enable_ansi_support/?utm_source=openai))  \n\n### Minimal usage\n```rust\nfn main() -> std::io::Result<()> {\n    enable_ansi_support::enable_ansi_support()?;\n    println!(\"\\x1b[31mHello, red text\\x1b[0m\");\n    Ok(())\n}\n```\n(Example pattern shown in the docs.) ([docs.rs](https://docs.rs/enable-ansi-support/latest/enable_ansi_support/?utm_source=openai))\n\nCitations:\n\n- 1: https://docs.rs/enable-ansi-support/latest/enable_ansi_support/?utm_source=openai\n- 2: https://docs.rs/enable-ansi-support/latest/enable_ansi_support/?utm_source=openai\n- 3: https://docs.rs/crate/enable-ansi-support/latest?utm_source=openai\n- 4: https://docs.rs/enable-ansi-support/latest/enable_ansi_support/?utm_source=openai\n- 5: https://docs.rs/enable-ansi-support/latest/enable_ansi_support/?utm_source=openai\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncd libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/host && sed -n '386,393p' logging.rs\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 454\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**API usage is correct, but reconsider the Result handling pattern.**\n\nThe `supports_color` v3 API with `has_basic` field usage is verified and correct. However, silently discarding the `Result` from `enable_ansi_support::enable_ansi_support()` with `let _` is non-idiomatic Rust and typically flagged by clippy.\n\nWhile your reasoning is sound—the actual capability is determined by the subsequent `supports_color` check—consider making the intent explicit:\n- Use `.ok()` to explicitly ignore the Result value: `let _ = enable_ansi_support::enable_ansi_support().ok();`\n- Or use `.expect()` if a panic is acceptable: `enable_ansi_support::enable_ansi_support().expect(\"failed to enable ANSI\");`\n\nThe current pattern works functionally but doesn't align with Rust idioms for Result handling.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/host/logging.rs` around lines 386 - 393, In\nstderr_supports_ansi(), replace the non-idiomatic silent discard of the Result\nfrom enable_ansi_support::enable_ansi_support() with an explicit intent: either\ncall .ok() on the returned Result to intentionally ignore errors (making the\nignore explicit) or call .expect(\"failed to enable ANSI\") if you want a panic on\nfailure; update the line using enable_ansi_support::enable_ansi_support()\naccordingly to reflect one of these two patterns so clippy/Rust idioms are\nsatisfied.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-13T05:44:06Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T05:44:07Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/590#discussion_r2802401833","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/590","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2802401833"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/590#discussion_r2802401833"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/590"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2802401833/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":386,"original_start_line":386,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":393,"original_line":393,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":20,"position":20,"subject_type":"line"}],"source_reviews":[{"id":3795180242,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7iNdrS","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 2**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@Cargo.toml`:\n- Around line 356-357: The Cargo.toml entry for the crate enable-ansi-support is\npinned to \"0.2\" and must be updated to \"0.3\" (preferably \"0.3.1\") to stay\ncurrent; change the dependency version for enable-ansi-support to 0.3.x and\nensure supports-color remains at \"3\". Also audit any terminal/console output\ncode paths that render untrusted input (e.g., places that pass user strings into\nformatters or tracing logs) to escape or sanitize ANSI control sequences before\nemitting them, and if you use tracing-subscriber, bump its dependency to at\nleast \"0.3.20\" to include the ANSI escaping fix (CVE/RUSTSEC fix).\n\nIn `@libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/host/logging.rs`:\n- Around line 386-393: In stderr_supports_ansi(), replace the non-idiomatic\nsilent discard of the Result from enable_ansi_support::enable_ansi_support()\nwith an explicit intent: either call .ok() on the returned Result to\nintentionally ignore errors (making the ignore explicit) or call .expect(\"failed\nto enable ANSI\") if you want a panic on failure; update the line using\nenable_ansi_support::enable_ansi_support() accordingly to reflect one of these\ntwo patterns so clippy/Rust idioms are satisfied.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/590#pullrequestreview-3795180242","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/590","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/590#pullrequestreview-3795180242"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/590"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-13T05:44:07Z","commit_id":"f29e2d446c2721b42038a2461ff04cac2efd4da8"}]},{"source_pr_number":588,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/588","source_state":"closed","source_author":"MikeFalcon77","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #588] fix(release-plz, ci): fix publish ordering and changelog duplication,fix PR rust-cache cleanup logic, CodeQL redundant runs removal","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"chore/improve_release-plz","pr_head_sha":"132ad567ebbec880ad1b28475afe0fd773d57c80","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"MikeFalcon77","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/588","id":3276737241,"node_id":"P