NT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n    // Match if request path ends with a registered path (suffix match)\n    let matching_entry = validation_map\n        .iter()\n        .filter(|entry| {\n            let (ref map_method, ref map_path) = *entry.key();\n            map_method == &method && path.ends_with(map_path)\n        })\n        .max_by_key(|entry| entry.key().1.len());\n\n    let Some(allowed_types) = matching_entry else {\n        // No validation configured - proceed\n        return next.run(req).await;\n    };\n    let allowed_types = allowed_types.value().clone();\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/mime_validation.rs` around lines 99\n- 110, The current suffix match uses validation_map.iter().find(...) which can\nreturn an arbitrary match when multiple map_path suffixes match; change this to\niterate/filter entries where map_method == &method and path.ends_with(map_path)\nand then choose the entry with the longest map_path (most specific) — e.g. use\nvalidation_map.iter().filter(...).max_by_key(|entry| entry.key().1.len()) to\nassign matching_entry, then handle the Option as before and clone allowed_types\nfrom matching_entry.value().\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 522f284","created_at":"2026-02-12T07:47:42Z","updated_at":"2026-02-12T08:27:23Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/578#discussion_r2797239185","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/578","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyb