bot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat -n modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/rate_limit.rs | head -150\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 6037\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check Tokio version and OwnedSemaphorePermit behavior\nrg \"tokio\" modules/system/api-gateway/Cargo.toml -A 3\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 228\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check workspace tokio version\nfd Cargo.toml | xargs rg -l \"workspace = true\" | head -1 | xargs cat | grep -A 2 \"\\[workspace.dependencies\\]\" | grep tokio\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 54\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check root Cargo.toml for workspace definition\ncat Cargo.toml | grep -A 50 \"\\[workspace.dependencies\\]\"\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 2600\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Verify the behavior of OwnedSemaphorePermit in async context\n# Check if there are any other usages of try_acquire_owned in the codebase\nrg \"try_acquire_owned\" modules/\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 179\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Hold the inflight permit across the await to prevent early release.**\n\nThe `OwnedSemaphorePermit` from `try_acquire_owned()` is dropped before `next.run(req).await` completes. In async lowering, the unused `_permit` binding can be dropped at earlier suspension points, releasing the semaphore slot before the request finishes. This defeats the in-flight request limit.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛠️ Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-            match sem.clone().try_acquire_owned() {\n-                Ok(_permit) => {\n-                    return next.run(req).await;\n-                }\n+            match sem.clone().try_acquire_owned() {\n+                Ok(permit) => {\n+                    let response = next.run(req).await;\n+                    drop(permit);\n+                    return response;\n+                }\n                 Err(_) => {\n                     return StatusCode::SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE.into_response();\n                 }\n             }\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n        // Check inflight limit using the matched key\n        if let Some(sem) = map.inflight.get(key) {\n            match sem.clone().try_acquire_owned() {\n                Ok(permit) => {\n                    let response = next.run(req).await;\n                    drop(permit);\n                    return response;\n                }\n                Err(_) => {\n                    return StatusCode::SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE.into_response();\n                }\n            }\n        }\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/rate_limit.rs` around lines 124 -\n129, The acquired OwnedSemaphorePermit from sem.clone().try_acquire_owned() is\nbeing dropped before next.run(req).await completes because it was bound to an\nunused _permit; keep the permit alive across the await by binding it to a named\nvariable (e.g., permit) in the match arm that succeeded and ensuring that\nvariable remains in scope until after next.run(req).await finishes (drop it or\nlet it go out of scope after the await). Update the match on map.inflight /\ntry_acquire_owned to hold the permit variable across the await rather than using\nan unused _permit.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Confirmed as addressed by @dominic1988-lgtm\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-12T07:55:26Z","updated_at":"2026-02-12T08:38:10Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/578#discussion_r2797266227","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/578","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2797266227"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/578#discussion_r2797266227"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/578"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2797266227/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":124,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":129,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":36,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2797421304","pull_request_review_id":3789381346,"id":2797421304,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6mvUL4","diff_hunk":"@@ -91,9 +91,13 @@ pub async fn rate_limit_middleware(map: RateLimiterMap, mut req: Request, next:\n         .extensions()\n         .get::<axum::extract::MatchedPath>()\n         .map_or_else(|| req.uri().path().to_owned(), |p| p.as_str().to_owned());\n-    let key = (method, path);\n \n-    if let Some(bucker_map_entry) = map.buckets.get(&key) {\n+    // Match if request path ends with a registered path (suffix