it(\":\")[-1]\n+    port = base_url.split(\":\")[-1].split(\"/\")[0]\n     kill_existing_server(port)","path":"scripts/ci.py","commit_id":"85446d43727215387b536df493a4c2abe26e947c","original_commit_id":"85446d43727215387b536df493a4c2abe26e947c","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat -n scripts/ci.py | sed -n '280,300p'\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 869\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nhead -50 scripts/ci.py | cat -n\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 1667\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nrg \"def cmd_e2e\" -A 15 scripts/ci.py\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 536\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Use `urlparse` for robust port detection instead of string splitting.**\n\nThe current approach `base_url.split(\":\")[-1].split(\"/\")[0]` works for the default URL but fails when `E2E_BASE_URL` omits an explicit port (e.g., `https://host/chat` yields an empty string). Use `urllib.parse.urlparse` to safely extract the port and skip `kill_existing_server` if no port is present.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n+from urllib.parse import urlparse\n-    port = base_url.split(\":\")[-1].split(\"/\")[0]\n-    kill_existing_server(port)\n+    parsed = urlparse(base_url)\n+    port = parsed.port\n+    if port is not None:\n+        kill_existing_server(str(port))\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@scripts/ci.py` around lines 289 - 295, The port extraction in cmd_e2e is\nfragile (base_url.split(...)) — use urllib.parse.urlparse to parse base_url,\nread parsed.port (which will be an int or None), and only call\nkill_existing_server when parsed.port is not None; convert the int to a string\nif kill_existing_server expects a string. Update references to base_url/port in\ncmd_e2e accordingly so URLs without an explicit port (e.g., https://host/chat)\nskip kill_existing_server.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 4745646","created_at":"2026-02-12T08:32:46Z","updated_at":"2026-02-12T08:35:43Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/578#discussion_r2797455310","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/578","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2797455310"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/578#discussion_r2797455310"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/578"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2797455310/reactions","total_count