ation changes</code> <code> +7/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Windsurf workflow for PR status\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/565/files#diff-d8a87dfc1881c158176253ac8f89c70c8d5cd142b1b82b60920c5bd5ccad6784'> .windsurf/workflows/cypilot-pr-status.md\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>13. cypilot-agents.json\n <code>⚙️ Configuration changes</code> <code> +30/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Add PR review and status agent templates\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/565/files#diff-8b11c577bb6761eff24cb89ffd05d4ea8a42eba462e0b0aeaa965583dd18f3a8'> cypilot-agents.json\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>14. docs/checklists/ADR.md\n <code>📝 Documentation</code> <code> +12/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Add PR review focus section for ADRs\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/565/files#diff-a6329658c5cda51859ed7a871cf8e529c7a232f16850b2a1b15f3c9dfca3e6b2'> docs/checklists/ADR.md\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>15. docs/checklists/DESIGN.md\n <code>📝 Documentation</code> <code> +17/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Add PR review focus section for designs\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/565/files#diff-eb4234b19a76ffa9fffa560d5c5ef325aa9886e5313a7b5db99fd9cfdb2eea64'> docs/checklists/DESIGN.md\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>16. docs/checklists/PRD.md\n <code>📝 Documentation</code> <code> +15/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Add PR review focus section for requirements\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/565/files#diff-5e5a7aa55bae7074ecdcf851a4a1fd837968deb4bc9c336a604905ee8791a81c'> docs/checklists/PRD.md\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>17. docs/checklists/README.md\n <code>📝 Documentation</code> <code> +30/-1 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Document PR review integration and references\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/565/files#diff-479815d3a0034124617a852321396bc76d4d2f1c1bc17be18d54cacce3bc79e9'> docs/checklists/README.md\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n\n<a href=\"https://www.qodo.ai\"><img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/qodo-logo.svg\" width=\"80\" alt=\"Qodo Logo\"></a>","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3886150924/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":484649,"client_id":"Iv1.8b06d3cf5deea057","slug":"qodo-code-review","node_id":"A_kwHOCuzIt84AB2Up","owner":{"login":"qodo-ai","id":183290039,"node_id":"O_kgDOCuzItw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/183290039?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai","html_url":"https://github.com/qodo-ai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Qodo Code Review","description":"### The AI Code Review Platform\r\n\r\n## Get Started\r\nSimply sign into Github and click the \"Configure\" button. Check out our documentation for more info: https://docs.qodo.ai/get-started.\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\nQodo automatically reviews every GitHub pull request, identifies logic bugs, edge cases, security issues, and code quality problems, and provides actionable suggestions your team can apply immediately.\r\n\r\nInstall in minutes. Integrates seamlessly into your existing workflows.\r\n\r\n## Qodo is designed for developers who:\r\n- Handle frequent pull requests and need reliable review coverage\r\n- Balance code quality with fast delivery\r\n- Work in complex, multi-repo systems\r\n- Use AI-generated code and need stronger guardrails\r\n- Build production software where reliability matters\r\n\r\n## Qodo Capabilities\r\n- ## Automated PR Analysis\r\n  - Reviews every pull request automatically\r\n  - No manual trigger required\r\n\r\n- ## Context-Aware Code Review\r\n  - Understands cross-file changes\r\n  - Detects architectural inconsistencies\r\n\r\n- ## Actionable Suggestions\r\n  - Concrete code fixes\r\n  - Clear explanations\r\n  - Prioritized feedback\r\n\r\n- ## Security & Reliability Checks\r\n  - Identifies risky patterns\r\n  - Reduces attack surface area","external_url":"https://www.qodo.ai/","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","created_at":"2023-11-16T16:18:38Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T15:53:40Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"read","contents":"write","discussions":"write","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","discussion_comment","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review_comment","push"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3886178636","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/565#issuecomment-3886178636","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/565","id":3886178636,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7nomFM","user":{"login":"qodo-code-review[bot]","id":151058649,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCQD42Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/484649?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-11T18:27:37Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T18:27:37Z","body":"<pre>ⓘ You are approaching your monthly quota for Qodo. <a href=\"https://www.qodo.ai/pricing\">Upgrade your plan</a></pre>\n\n<h3>Code Review by Qodo</h3>\n\n<code>🐞 Bugs (3)</code>  <code>📘 Rule violations (0)</code>  <code>📎 Requirement gaps (0)</code>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n<br/>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/action-required.png\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Action required\">\n\n<details>\n<summary>  1.  Invalid Cursor rule frontmatter <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>⛯ Reliability</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n><b><i>.cursor/rules/cypilot-pr-status.mdc</i></b> declares <b><i>globs:</i></b> with no value (YAML null), which can break\n>rule parsing/loading and prevent the rule from applying.\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[.cursor/rules/cypilot-pr-status.mdc[R1-5]](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/565/files#diff-41bd75c479193aa97a40ac480244714a15bb7ba37b80a6b8212599de9d095340R1-R5)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>+---\n>+description: Generate status reports for GitHub PRs with severity assessment\n>+globs:\n>+alwaysApply: false\n>+---\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details >\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>The new rule file contains an empty <b><i>globs:</i></b> key, unlike the existing working Cursor rule which\n>omits <b><i>globs</i></b> entirely. This makes the front matter structurally inconsistent and likely invalid for\n>consumers expecting <b><i>globs</i></b> to be omitted or a list.\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>[.cursor/rules/cypilot-pr-status.mdc[1-5]](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/blob/671cb6b6d5d8f83883a50093ae908028d7dd82ec/.cursor/rules/cypilot-pr-status.mdc/#L1-L5)</code>\n> <code>[.cursor/rules/cypilot.mdc[1-4]](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/blob/671cb6b6d5d8f83883a50093ae908028d7dd82ec/.cursor/rules/cypilot.mdc/#L1-L4)</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>```\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>### Issue description\n>`.cursor/rules/cypilot-pr-status.mdc` has an empty `globs:` field in YAML front matter. This can break Cursor’s rule parsing or cause the rule to be ignored.\n>\n>### Issue Context\n>Existing Cursor rule files in this repo don’t use `globs` at all.\n>\n>### Fix Focus Areas\n>- .cursor/rules/cypilot-pr-status.mdc[1-5]\n>```\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n<br/>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/review-recommended.png\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Remediation recommended\">\n\n<details>\n<summary>  2.  Broken docs cross-references <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>⛯ Reliability</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n><b><i>docs/checklists/README.md</i></b> links to <b><i>.cypilot-adapter/pr-review.json</i></b> and <b><i>docs/pr-review/</i></b>, but\n>neither exists in this repository tree, leading to broken navigation and confusing setup\n>instructions.\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[docs/checklists/README.md[R157-163]](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/565/files#diff-479815d3a0034124617a852321396bc76d4d2f1c1bc17be18d54cacce3bc79e9R157-R163)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>+- Cypilot PR review config: `.cypilot-adapter/pr-review.json`\n>+- PR review workflow: `.cypilot/workflows/pr-review.md`\n>+- PR status workflow: `.cypilot/workflows/pr-status.md`\n>+- PR review prompts: `.cypilot/prompts/pr/`\n>+- PR review script: `.cypilot/skills/scripts/pr.py`\n>+- PR review templates: `.cypilot/templates/pr/`\n>+- PR review documentation: `docs/pr-review/`\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details >\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>The checklist README explicitly advertises these paths as cross-references, but the repository’s\n><b><i>docs/</i></b> and <b><i>.cypilot-adapter/</i></b> top-level contents do not include them (no <b><i>docs/pr-review</i></b>\n>directory and no <b><i>.cypilot-adapter/pr-review.json</i></b> file).\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>[docs/checklists/README.md[153-163]](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/blob/671cb6b6d5d8f83883a50093ae908028d7dd82ec/docs/checklists/README.md/#L153-L163)</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>```\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>### Issue description\n>`docs/checklists/README.md` contains cross-reference links to paths that are not present in this repository, which will create broken links and mislead contributors.\n>\n>### Issue Context\n>The referenced paths are:\n>- `.cypilot-adapter/pr-review.json`\n>- `docs/pr-review/`\n>\n>### Fix Focus Areas\n>- docs/checklists/README.md[153-163]\n>```\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>  3.  PR workflows depend on submodule <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>⛯ Reliability</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>All new PR review/status commands/prompts point to <b><i>.cypilot/workflows/pr-review.md</i></b> and\n><b><i>pr-status.md</i></b>, but this repo stores <b><i>.cypilot</i></b> as a git submodule; if the submodule SHA doesn’t\n>include these workflow files or submodules aren’t checked out, the new commands will fail.\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[.claude/commands/cypilot-pr-review.md[6]](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/565/files#diff-67e7ef6fceedf98ae7082c37a7fd17ddadb7039595025400b66f16ba336fb821R6-R6)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>+ALWAYS open and follow `../../.cypilot/workflows/pr-review.md`\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details >\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>New command/prompt wrappers instruct users/agents to open workflow markdown files under\n><b><i>.cypilot/workflows/...</i></b>. The repo defines <b><i>.cypilot</i></b> as a submodule, and the main CI workflow does\n>not fetch submodules by default—so any automation expecting these paths without explicit submodule\n>checkout (or without updating the submodule revision to contain the new workflows) is fragile.\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>[.claude/commands/cypilot-pr-review.md[1-6]](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/blob/671cb6b6d5d8f83883a50093ae908028d7dd82ec/.claude/commands/cypilot-pr-review.md/#L1-L6)</code>\n> <code>[.claude/commands/cypilot-pr-status.md[1-6]](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/blob/671cb6b6d5d8f83883a50093ae908028d7dd82ec/.claude/commands/cypilot-pr-status.md/#L1-L6)</code>\n> <code>[.gitmodules[4-6]](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/blob/671cb6b6d5d8f83883a50093ae908028d7dd82ec/.gitmodules/#L4-L6)</code>\n> <code>[.github/workflows/ci.yml[45-47]](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/blob/671cb6b6d5d8f83883a50093ae908028d7dd82ec/.github/workflows/ci.yml/#L45-L47)</code>\n> <code>[.github/workflows/docs.yml[24-29]](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/blob/671cb6b6d5d8f83883a50093ae908028d7dd82ec/.github/workflows/docs.yml/#L24-L29)</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>```\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>### Issue description\n>New PR review/status command wrappers depend on workflow files inside the `.cypilot` submodule. If the submodule isn’t checked out (or doesn’t contain these workflow files at the pinned SHA), the commands/prompts will break.\n>\n>### Issue Context\n>This repo uses `.cypilot` as a git submodule. Some CI workflows check out submodules, but `ci.yml` does not.\n>\n>### Fix Focus Areas\n>- .gitmodules[4-6]\n>- .claude/commands/cypilot-pr-review.md[1-6]\n>- .claude/commands/cypilot-pr-status.md[1-6]\n>- .github/workflows/ci.yml[45-47]\n>```\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n<pre>ⓘ The new review experience is currently in Beta. <a href=\"https://docs.qodo.ai/qodo-documentation/code-review\">Learn more</a></pre>\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n\n<!-- https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/commit/671cb6b6d5d8f83883a50093ae908028d7dd82ec -->\n\n<a href=\"https://www.qodo.ai\"><img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/qodo-logo.svg\" width=\"80\" alt=\"Qodo Logo\"></a>","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3886178636/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":484649,"client_id":"Iv1.8b06d3cf5deea057","slug":"qodo-code-review","node_id":"A_kwHOCuzIt84AB2Up","owner":{"login":"qodo-ai","id":183290039,"node_id":"O_kgDOCuzItw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/183290039?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai","html_url":"https://github.com/qodo-ai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Qodo Code Review","description":"### The AI Code Review Platform\r\n\r\n## Get Started\r\nSimply sign into Github and click the \"Configure\" button. Check out our documentation for more info: https://docs.qodo.ai/get-started.\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\nQodo automatically reviews every GitHub pull request, identifies logic bugs, edge cases, security issues, and code quality problems, and provides actionable suggestions your team can apply immediately.\r\n\r\nInstall in minutes. Integrates seamlessly into your existing workflows.\r\n\r\n## Qodo is designed for developers who:\r\n- Handle frequent pull requests and need reliable review coverage\r\n- Balance code quality with fast delivery\r\n- Work in complex, multi-repo systems\r\n- Use AI-generated code and need stronger guardrails\r\n- Build production software where reliability matters\r\n\r\n## Qodo Capabilities\r\n- ## Automated PR Analysis\r\n  - Reviews every pull request automatically\r\n  - No manual trigger required\r\n\r\n- ## Context-Aware Code Review\r\n  - Understands cross-file changes\r\n  - Detects architectural inconsistencies\r\n\r\n- ## Actionable Suggestions\r\n  - Concrete code fixes\r\n  - Clear explanations\r\n  - Prioritized feedback\r\n\r\n- ## Security & Reliability Checks\r\n  - Identifies risky patterns\r\n  - Reduces attack surface area","external_url":"https://www.qodo.ai/","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","created_at":"2023-11-16T16:18:38Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T15:53:40Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"read","contents":"write","discussions":"write","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","discussion_comment","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review_comment","push"]}}],"source_review_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2794806215","pull_request_review_id":3786525807,"id":2794806215,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6mlVvH","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@\n+---\n+description: Generate status reports for GitHub PRs with severity assessment\n+globs:\n+alwaysApply: false\n+---","path":".cursor/rules/cypilot-pr-status.mdc","commit_id":"1015089615b358bed96ea9838cb338de769d4bd2","original_commit_id":"671cb6b6d5d8f83883a50093ae908028d7dd82ec","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`Cursor .mdc rule front matter schema documentation globs field alwaysApply`\n\n💡 Result:\n\nCursor **project rules** are `.mdc` files stored in **`.cursor/rules/`** with **YAML front matter** that controls when the rule is included. The Cursor “Rule Type” UI mainly toggles these front-matter fields: **`description`**, **`globs`**, **`alwaysApply`**. [1]\n\n### Front-matter fields (what they mean)\n```yaml\n---\ndescription: <string>        # used for relevance; required for “Agent Requested”\nglobs: <glob(s)>             # used for “Auto Attached” (attach when matching files are referenced)\nalwaysApply: <true|false>    # “Always” type => true (always included)\n---\n```\n[1]\n\n### How they map to Rule Types\n- **Always** → `alwaysApply: true` (included in every context). [1]  \n- **Auto Attached** → `alwaysApply: false` + `globs: ...` (included when matching files are referenced). [1]  \n- **Agent Requested** → must provide `description:`; the agent decides whether to include it. [1]  \n- **Manual** → only included when explicitly mentioned (e.g., `@ruleName`). [1]\n\n### Notes on `globs` + `alwaysApply`\nSome users have reported cases where `alwaysApply: true` didn’t actually include the rule unless `globs` was also set (e.g., `[\"*\"]`), which appears to be a product bug/behavior discrepancy in certain versions. [2]\n\n**Sources:** Cursor Rules docs (rule anatomy/types + fields). [1] GitHub issue discussing `alwaysApply` behavior. [2]\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if there are other .mdc files in the .cursor/rules directory\nfind .cursor/rules -name \"*.mdc\" -type f 2>/dev/null | head -20\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 133\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Get the content of a few .mdc files to see how they structure front matter\nfind .cursor/rules -name \"*.mdc\" -type f 2>/dev/null | head -5 | xargs -I {} sh -c 'echo \"=== {} ===\" && head -10 \"{}\"'\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 1174\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if there's a schema or configuration file that validates .mdc files\nfind .cursor -type f \\( -name \"*.json\" -o -name \"*.yaml\" -o -name \"*.yml\" -o -name \"*.schema\" \\) 2>/dev/null | head -20\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 54\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if there are any other .mdc files with empty globs for comparison\ngrep -r \"^globs:$\" .cursor/rules/ 2>/dev/null\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 114\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Remove or explicitly set the empty `globs` field.**\n\nThe empty `globs:` parses as null in YAML and creates semantic ambiguity. Since `alwaysApply: false` with no matching patterns makes this a Manual rule (included only when explicitly requested), either remove `globs` entirely or set it to `globs: []` explicitly. The pattern in the repository (e.g., `cypilot.mdc`) is to omit unused front-matter fields.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n ---\n description: Generate status reports for GitHub PRs with severity assessment\n-globs:\n alwaysApply: false\n ---\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn @.cursor/rules/cypilot-pr-status.mdc around lines 1 - 5, The front-matter\nincludes an empty nullable globs field which creates ambiguity; edit the\ncypilot-pr-status.mdc front-matter to either remove the globs key entirely or\nset it explicitly to an empty list (globs: []) so the YAML parses\ndeterministically, and keep alwaysApply: false unchanged to preserve the manual\nrule behavior.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-11T18:25:42Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T18:25:45Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/565#discussion_r2794806215","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/565","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2794806215"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/565#discussion_r2794806215"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/565"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2794806215/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":1,"original_start_line":1,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":5,"original_line":5,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":5,"position":5,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2794806232","pull_request_review_id":3786525807,"id":2794806232,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6mlVvY","diff_hunk":"@@ -128,7 +129,35 @@ Generate draft content for missing CRITICAL items.\n \n ---\n \n+## PR Review Integration\n+\n+These checklists are integrated with the Cypilot PR review workflow. When reviewing PRs:\n+\n+- **PRD PRs**: Use `PRD.md` — covers requirements completeness, testability, traceability, and industry alignment\n+- **Design PRs**: Use `DESIGN.md` — covers architecture, trade-offs, API contracts, security, and antipatterns\n+- **ADR PRs**: Use `ADR.md` — covers decision significance, alternatives analysis, and overlap detection\n+- **Code PRs**: Use `CODING.md` — covers Rust correctness, architecture (ModKit/SDK pattern), security (secure ORM), clippy/dylint compliance, testing, performance, etc.","path":"docs/checklists/README.md","commit_id":"1015089615b358bed96ea9838cb338de769d4bd2","original_commit_id":"671cb6b6d5d8f83883a50093ae908028d7dd82ec","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Overly specific technology references for a generic checklist README.**\n\nLine 139 hardcodes Rust-specific technologies (ModKit/SDK, secure ORM, clippy/dylint) in what is presented as a \"Comprehensive expert-driven quality checklists\" framework. This creates inconsistency with the generic tone of the document.\n\nConsider either:\n1. Making the description more generic: \"covers language-specific correctness, architectural patterns, security, linting compliance, testing, performance\"\n2. Adding a note that CODING.md is tailored to this project's tech stack\n3. Moving tech-specific details to CODING.md itself\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Suggested refactor for generic wording</summary>\n\n```diff\n-- **Code PRs**: Use `CODING.md` — covers Rust correctness, architecture (ModKit/SDK pattern), security (secure ORM), clippy/dylint compliance, testing, performance, etc.\n+- **Code PRs**: Use `CODING.md` — covers language correctness, architectural patterns, security practices, linter compliance, testing, and performance\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n- **Code PRs**: Use `CODING.md` — covers language correctness, architectural patterns, security practices, linter compliance, testing, and performance\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@docs/checklists/README.md` at line 139, The README entry for \"**Code PRs**:\nUse `CODING.md` — covers Rust correctness, architecture (ModKit/SDK pattern),\nsecurity (secure ORM), clippy/dylint compliance, testing, performance, etc.\" is\ntoo Rust-specific for a generic checklist; update this line to either use\ngeneric wording (e.g., \"covers language-specific correctness, architectural\npatterns, security, linting compliance, testing, performance\"), or keep the\ncurrent short pointer to `CODING.md` and add a parenthetical note that\n`CODING.md` is tailored to this project's tech stack, or move the explicit\nRust/tooling details into `CODING.md` itself so README only references\n`CODING.md`.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-11T18:25:42Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T18:25:45Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/565#discussion_r2794806232","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/565","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2794806232"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/565#discussion_r2794806232"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/565"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2794806232/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":139,"original_line":139,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":27,"position":27,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2794806253","pull_request_review_id":3786525807,"id":2794806253,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6mlVvt","diff_hunk":"@@ -128,7 +129,35 @@ Generate draft content for missing CRITICAL items.\n \n ---\n \n+## PR Review Integration\n+\n+These checklists are integrated with the Cypilot PR review workflow. When reviewing PRs:\n+\n+- **PRD PRs**: Use `PRD.md` — covers requirements completeness, testability, traceability, and industry alignment\