cb6b6d5d8f83883a50093ae908028d7dd82ec","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n```\n#!/bin/bash\n# Check if .gitmodules exists and contains .cypilot submodule\necho \"=== Checking for .gitmodules file ===\"\nif [ -f \".gitmodules\" ]; then\n  echo \"Contents of .gitmodules:\"\n  cat .gitmodules\nelse\n  echo \".gitmodules not found\"\nfi\n\necho -e \"\\n=== Checking git submodule status ===\"\ngit submodule status 2>/dev/null || echo \"No submodules or git command unavailable\"\n\necho -e \"\\n=== Check if .cypilot directory now has content ===\"\nif [ -d \".cypilot\" ]; then\n  echo \"Contents of .cypilot directory:\"\n  ls -la .cypilot/ 2>/dev/null | head -20\n  echo -e \"\\nChecking for the configuration files mentioned:\"\n  [ -f \".cypilot/.cypilot-config.json\" ] && echo \"✓ .cypilot/.cypilot-config.json exists\" || echo \"✗ .cypilot/.cypilot-config.json not found\"\n  [ -f \".cypilot/workflows/pr-review.md\" ] && echo \"✓ .cypilot/workflows/pr-review.md exists\" || echo \"✗ .cypilot/workflows/pr-review.md not found\"\nelse\n  echo \".cypilot directory not found\"\nfi\n```\n\nLength of output: 739\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n`@Artifizer`, I can see the `.cypilot` submodule is registered in `.gitmodules`, but it appears the submodule is not yet initialized in the current PR state. The `git submodule status` shows a `-` prefix, indicating the submodule directory is empty and the configuration files are still missing:\n\n```\n✗ .cypilot/.cypilot-config.json not found\n✗ .cypilot/workflows/pr-review.md not found\n```\n\nTo fully resolve this, you'll need to:\n\n```bash\ngit submodule update --init .cypilot\ngit add .cypilot\ngit commit -m \"Initialize .cypilot submodule\"\ngit push\n```\n\nThis will populate the submodule with the actual files from the `cyber-pilot` repository so the documentation references are valid.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-10T18:54:47.115Z\nLearning: Applies to modules/system/types-registry/openspec/openspec/changes/*/tasks.md : In `tasks.md`, create an implementation checklist with sequential steps using Markdown checkbox syntax (`- [ ] item`) under numbered sections\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-10T18:54:47.115Z\nLearning: Complete implementation steps sequentially from `tasks.md` and update the checklist to `- [x]` after all work is done to reflect reality\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-10T18:54:47.115Z\nLearning: Applies to modules/system/types-registry/openspec/openspec/changes/*/specs/**/spec.md : Use `## ADDED` for new capabilities that stand alone; use `## MODIFIED` for behavior changes to existing requirements (include full requirement content); use `## REMOVED` for deprecated features; use `## RENAMED` for name-only changes\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-10T18:54:47.115Z\nLearning: Applies to modules/system/types-registry/openspec/openspec/changes/*/proposal.md : In `proposal.md`, include sections: Why (1-2 sentences on problem/opportunity), What Changes (bullet list with breaking changes marked **BREAKING**), and Impact (affected specs and code)\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-10T18:54:33.294Z\nLearning: Create `design.md` only when the change involves: cross-cutting changes, new external dependencies, significant data model changes, security/performance complexity, or design ambiguity\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-10T18:54:47.115Z\nLearning: Applies to modules/system/types-registry/openspec/openspec/changes/*/specs/**/spec.md : In spec delta files under `changes/[change-id]/specs/`, use `## ADDED Requirements`, `## MODIFIED Requirements`, `## REMOVED Requirements`, and `## RENAMED Requirements` sections\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-10T18:54:47.115Z\nLearning: Create `design.md` only if the change involves: cross-cutting changes, new architectural patterns, new external dependencies, significant data model changes, security/performance complexity, or ambiguity benefiting from technical decisions\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This 