s/\"","path":".cypilot-adapter/pr-review.json","commit_id":"1015089615b358bed96ea9838cb338de769d4bd2","original_commit_id":"1015089615b358bed96ea9838cb338de769d4bd2","user":{"login":"qodo-code-review[bot]","id":151058649,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCQD42Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/484649?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"### Question: \nIt's because it's in submodule\n\n### Answer:\nIf you’re on **GitLab**, Qodo Merge can be configured to expand submodule diffs (otherwise GitLab often shows only `Subproject commit ...`, and the agent won’t “see” the actual file-level changes inside the submodule).\n\nAdd this to your repo’s `.pr_agent.toml` (or wiki config):\n\n```toml\n[gitlab]\nexpand_submodule_diffs = true\n```\n\nWhen enabled, Qodo Merge will fetch and attach diffs from the submodule repositories (default is `false` to avoid extra GitLab API calls).\n\nIf you’re **not on GitLab** (e.g., GitHub/Bitbucket/Azure), the docs here don’t specify a submodule-diff expansion setting—tell me which git provider you’re using and how the agent is running (GitHub App vs Action vs webhook/CI), and I can point to the most relevant configuration/approach from the docs.\n\n#### Relevant Sources:\n\n> - https://docs.qodo.ai/qodo-documentation/qodo-merge/usage-guide/additional_configurations#expand-gitlab-submodule-diffs\n> - https://docs.qodo.ai/qodo-documentation/qodo-merge/usage-guide/automations_and_usage#gitlab-webhook\n","created_at":"2026-02-11T19:23:18Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T19:23:19Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/565#discussion_r2795058610","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/565","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2795058610"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/565#discussion_r2795058610"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/565"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2795058610/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":1,"original_start_line":1,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":37,"original_line":37,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2795014104,"author_association":"NONE","original_position":37,"position":37,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2795059055","pull_request_review_id":3786838869,"id":2795059055,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6mmTdv","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@\n+{\n+  \"scriptPath\": \".cypilot/skills/scripts/pr.py\",\n+  \"dataDir\": \".prs\",\n+  \"templatesDir\": \".cypilot/templates/pr\",\n+  \"prompts\": [\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"Code Review\",\n+      \"description\": \"Review for PRs that change source code. Covers correctness, style, performance, security, and test coverage.\",\n+      \"promptFile\": \".cypilot/prompts/pr/code-review.md\",\n+      \"checklist\": \"docs/checklists/CODING.md\",\n+      \"coding_guidelines\": \"guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md\",\n+      \"security_guidelines\": \"guidelines/SECURITY.md\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"Design Review\",\n+      \"description\": \"Review for PRs that add or change design documents (DESIGN.md). Evaluates architecture, trade-offs, API contracts, industry alignment, and antipatterns.\",\n+      \"promptFile\": \".cypilot/prompts/pr/design-review.md\",\n+      \"checklist\": \"docs/checklists/DESIGN.md\",\n+      \"template\": \"docs/spec-templates/DESIGN.md\",\n+      \"architecture\": \"docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"ADR Review\",\n+      \"description\": \"Review for PRs that add or change Architecture Decision Records. Checks problem scoping, template compliance, and overlap with existing ADRs.\",\n+      \"promptFile\": \".cypilot/prompts/pr/adr-review.md\",\n+      \"checklist\": \"docs/checklists/ADR.md\",\n+      \"template\": \"docs/spec-templates/ADR.md\",\n+      \"existing_artifacts\": \"docs/adrs/\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"PRD Review\",\n+      \"description\": \"Review for PRs that add or change PRD/requirements documents. Evaluates completeness, testability, traceability, and industry alignment.\",\n+      \"promptFile\": \".cypilot/prompts/pr/prd-review.md\",\n+      \"checklist\": \"docs/checklists/PRD.md\",\n+      \"template\": \"docs/spec-templates/PRD.md\",\n+      \"project_domain\": \"docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md\",\n+      \"existing_artifacts\": \"docs/prds/\"","path":".cypilot-adapter/pr-review.json","commit_id":"1015089615b358bed96ea9838cb338de769d4bd2","original_commit_id":"1015089615b358bed96ea9838cb338de769d4bd2","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"> Skipped: comment is from another GitHub bot.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-11T19:23:24Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T19:23:25Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/565#discussion_r2795059055","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/565","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2795059055"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/565#discussion_r2795059055"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/565"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2795059055/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":1,"original_start_line":1,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":37,"original_line":37,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2795014104,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":37,"position":37,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2795059327","pull_request_review_id":3786839162,"id":2795059327,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6mmTh_","diff_hunk":"@@ -128,7 +129,35 @@ Generate draft content for missing CRITICAL items.\n \n ---\n \n+## PR Review Integration\n+\n+These checklists are integrated with the Cypilot PR review workflow. When reviewing PRs:\n+\n+- **PRD PRs**: Use `PRD.md` — covers requirements completeness, testability, traceability, and industry alignment\n+- **Design PRs**: Use `DESIGN.md` — covers architecture, trade-offs, API contracts, security, and antipatterns\n+- **ADR PRs**: Use `ADR.md` — covers decision significance, alternatives analysis, and overlap detection\n+- **Code PRs**: Use `CODING.md` — covers Rust correctness, architecture (ModKit/SDK pattern), security (secure ORM), clippy/dylint compliance, testing, performance, etc.\n+\n+The checklist is auto-selected by the `/cypilot-pr-review` workflow based on the PR content. Configuration is in `.cypilot/.cypilot-config.json` under the `pr.prompts` key.\n+\n+Example prompts:\n+\n+```\n+cypilot review PR 123\n+cypilot review PR #59 with CODE checklist\n+review PR 42\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n ## Cross-References\n \n - Existing project docs (architecture docs, API specs, runbooks)\n - Source code and tests\n+- Cypilot PR review config: `.cypilot-adapter/pr-review.json`","path":"docs/checklists/README.md","commit_id":"1015089615b358bed96ea9838cb338de769d4bd2","original_commit_id":"03d3f713a0aff58901520cc648c97d5f5bb7fbcd","user":{"login":"qodo-code-review[bot]","id":151058649,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCQD42Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/484649?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"### Question: \nIt's because it's in submodule\n\n### Answer:\nIn Qodo Merge / PR-Agent, persistent configuration is not read from arbitrary JSON files (or from a submodule by default). The supported persistent configuration locations are:\n\n- **Wiki configuration page** named `.pr_agent.toml` (overrides everything else) 💎\n- **Local repo file** `.pr_agent.toml` in the **root of the repo’s default branch**\n- **Global org repo** `pr-agent-settings/.pr_agent.toml` 💎\n\nSo if “the config is in a submodule”, Qodo Merge will typically **not** pick it up. The practical fix is to keep the effective Qodo Merge configuration in one of the supported locations above (usually a root `.pr_agent.toml` or the wiki page), and—if needed—add instructions that tell the model how to treat the submodule content.\n\nExample (root `.pr_agent.toml`) to make reviews/suggestions explicitly account for submodule-only changes:\n\n```toml\n[pr_reviewer]\nextra_instructions = \"\"\"\\\nThis repository includes code in submodules. If the PR touches submodule updates, treat them as meaningful changes and call out any risks/required follow-ups (version pinning, sync steps, CI impact).\n\"\"\"\n\n[pr_code_suggestions]\nextra_instructions = \"\"\"\\\nThis repo uses submodules. When suggesting fixes, mention whether the change belongs in the main repo or inside the submodule, and avoid suggesting edits that assume submodule files are directly editable here unless they are part of this PR.\n\"\"\"\n```\n\nIf your actual problem is that Qodo Merge can’t “see” the file-level diff inside submodules (common on GitLab where MRs show “Subproject commit …”), then you also need the platform-specific setting (GitLab only):\n\n```toml\n[gitlab]\nexpand_submodule_diffs = true\n```\n\nIf you tell me which git platform you’re on (GitHub / GitLab / Bitbucket) and how Qodo Merge is installed (App vs Action vs webhook), I can suggest the most precise configuration location and settings.\n\n#### Relevant Sources:\n\n> - https://docs.qodo.ai/qodo-documentation/qodo-merge/usage-guide/configuration_options#wiki-configuration-file\n> - https://docs.qodo.ai/qodo-documentation/qodo-merge/usage-guide/configuration_options#local-configuration-file\n> - https://docs.qodo.ai/qodo-documentation/qodo-merge/usage-guide/configuration_options#global-configuration-file\n> - https://docs.qodo.ai/qodo-documentation/qodo-merge/tools/review#extra-instructions\n> - https://docs.qodo.ai/qodo-documentation/qodo-merge/tools/improve#extra-instructions-and-best-practices\n> - https://docs.qodo.ai/qodo-documentation/qodo-merge/usage-guide/additional_configurations#expand-gitlab-submodule-diffs\n","created_at":"2026-02-11T19:23:28Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T19:23:28Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/565#discussion_r2795059327","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/565","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2795059327"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/565#discussion_r2795059327"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/565"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2795059327/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":141,"original_start_line":141,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":157,"original_line":157,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2794993253,"author_association":"NONE","original_position":45,"position":45,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2795062234","pull_request_review_id":3786843178,"id":2795062234,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6mmUPa","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@\n+{\n+  \"scriptPath\": \".cypilot/skills/scripts/pr.py\",\n+  \"dataDir\": \".prs\",\n+  \"templatesDir\": \".cypilot/templates/pr\",\n+  \"prompts\": [\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"Code Review\",\n+      \"description\": \"Review for PRs that change source code. Covers correctness, style, performance, security, and test coverage.\",\n+      \"promptFile\": \".cypilot/prompts/pr/code-review.md\",\n+      \"checklist\": \"docs/checklists/CODING.md\",\n+      \"coding_guidelines\": \"guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md\",\n+      \"security_guidelines\": \"guidelines/SECURITY.md\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"Design Review\",\n+      \"description\": \"Review for PRs that add or change design documents (DESIGN.md). Evaluates architecture, trade-offs, API contracts, industry alignment, and antipatterns.\",\n+      \"promptFile\": \".cypilot/prompts/pr/design-review.md\",\n+      \"checklist\": \"docs/checklists/DESIGN.md\",\n+      \"template\": \"docs/spec-templates/DESIGN.md\",\n+      \"architecture\": \"docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"ADR Review\",\n+      \"description\": \"Review for PRs that add or change Architecture Decision Records. Checks problem scoping, template compliance, and overlap with existing ADRs.\",\n+      \"promptFile\": \".cypilot/prompts/pr/adr-review.md\",\n+      \"checklist\": \"docs/checklists/ADR.md\",\n+      \"template\": \"docs/spec-templates/ADR.md\",\n+      \"existing_artifacts\": \"docs/adrs/\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"PRD Review\",\n+      \"description\": \"Review for PRs that add or change PRD/requirements documents. Evaluates completeness, testability, traceability, and industry alignment.\",\n+      \"promptFile\": \".cypilot/prompts/pr/prd-review.md\",\n+      \"checklist\": \"docs/checklists/PRD.md\",\n+      \"template\": \"docs/spec-templates/PRD.md\",\n+      \"project_domain\": \"docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md\",\n+      \"existing_artifacts\": \"docs/prds/\"","path":".cypilot-adapter/pr-review.json","commit_id":"1015089615b358bed96ea9838cb338de769d4bd2","original_commit_id":"1015089615b358bed96ea9838cb338de769d4bd2","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n```\n#!/bin/bash\n# Check if .cypilot is a submodule and inspect its structure\necho \"=== Checking .cypilot submodule ===\"\nif [ -f .gitmodules ]; then\n  echo \"Found .gitmodules:\"\n  cat .gitmodules | grep -A 3 \"cypilot\"\nfi\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Checking .cypilot directory ===\"\nif [ -d .cypilot ]; then\n  echo \".cypilot directory exists\"\n  echo \"\"\n  echo \"Checking for referenced paths in submodule:\"\n  \n  # Check scriptPath\n  [ -f .cypilot/skills/scripts/pr.py ] && echo \"✓ .cypilot/skills/scripts/pr.py\" || echo \"✗ .cypilot/skills/scripts/pr.py\"\n  \n  # Check prompt files\n  [ -f .cypilot/prompts/pr/code-review.md ] && echo \"✓ .cypilot/prompts/pr/code-review.md\" || echo \"✗ .cypilot/prompts/pr/code-review.md\"\n  [ -f .cypilot/prompts/pr/design-review.md ] && echo \"✓ .cypilot/prompts/pr/design-review.md\" || echo \"✗ .cypilot/prompts/pr/design-review.md\"\n  [ -f .cypilot/prompts/pr/adr-review.md ] && echo \"✓ .cypilot/prompts/pr/adr-review.md\" || echo \"✗ .cypilot/prompts/pr/adr-review.md\"\n  [ -f .cypilot/prompts/pr/prd-review.md ] && echo \"✓ .cypilot/prompts/pr/prd-review.md\" || echo \"✗ .cypilot/prompts/pr/prd-review.md\"\n  \n  # Check templates directory\n  [ -d .cypilot/templates/pr ] && echo \"✓ .cypilot/templates/pr (directory)\" || echo \"✗ .cypilot/templates/pr (directory)\"\n  \n  echo \"\"\n  echo \"Top-level structure of .cypilot:\"\n  ls -la .cypilot/ | head -20\nelse\n  echo \".cypilot directory not found (submodule may not be initialized)\"\nfi\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Checking other referenced paths ===\"\n[ -d docs/prds/ ] && echo \"✓ docs/prds/\" || echo \"✗ docs/prds/\"\n[ -f guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md ] && echo \"✓ guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md\" || echo \"✗ guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md\"\n```\n\nLength of output: 717\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n`@Artifizer`, you're absolutely right—I apologize for the false alarm! The `.cypilot` submodule (pointing to `https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-pilot`) contains those resources, and my verification script didn't initialize submodules, so it couldn't see them.\n\nThe configuration looks correct. The paths referenced in `.cypilot-adapter/pr-review.json` should resolve properly when the submodule is initialized in actual usage.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>✏️ Learnings added</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: Artifizer\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 565\nFile: .cypilot-adapter/pr-review.json:1-37\nTimestamp: 2026-02-11T19:23:56.158Z\nLearning: The `.cypilot` directory in cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core is a Git submodule pointing to https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-pilot. It contains PR review scripts, prompts, templates, and workflows referenced by `.cypilot-adapter/pr-review.json`. Paths like `.cypilot/skills/scripts/pr.py`, `.cypilot/prompts/pr/*.md`, and `.cypilot/templates/pr/` exist in the submodule, not the main repository.\n```\n\n> Note: Learnings are effective only in the context of similar code segments. To apply general coding guidelines, please configure [review instructions](https://docs.coderabbit.ai/guides/review-instructions). You can manage existing learnings in the [app](https://app.coderabbit.ai/learnings).\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-10T18:54:47.115Z\nLearning: Scaffold change proposals with `proposal.md`, `tasks.md`, `design.md` (only if needed), and delta specs per affected capability\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-10T18:54:33.294Z\nLearning: Scaffold new changes with directory structure: `changes/[change-id]/` containing `proposal.md`, `tasks.md`, optional `design.md`, and `specs/[capability]/spec.md` delta files\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-11T19:24:06Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T19:24:06Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/565#discussion_r2795062234","pull_request_url":"https