“upgrade toolchain / action to latest” suggestions when your repo intentionally pins Rust **1.92**, add explicit guidance via the `/improve` tool’s `pr_code_suggestions.extra_instructions` (this is the recommended way to steer suggestions toward your project’s needs).\n\n```toml\n[pr_code_suggestions]\nextra_instructions = \"\"\"\\\n- This repository intentionally pins the Rust toolchain to 1.92.x.\n- Do NOT suggest Rust/toolchain version bumps (or “update to latest stable”) unless the PR explicitly requests it or there is a clear security/compatibility requirement.\n- Do NOT suggest bumping GitHub Actions / workflow dependencies just to “stay current”; only flag them if they are broken, insecure, or incompatible with our pinned toolchain.\n\"\"\"\n```\n\nIf you want it even stricter, specify your policy for action upgrades too (e.g., “only update release-plz when we schedule dependency updates”).\n\nTo tailor this further, it would help to know where you run Qodo Merge (GitHub App vs GitHub Action) and whether you have a documented “supported toolchain versions” policy (e.g., “1.92 only until next quarter”).\n\n#### Relevant Sources:\n\n> - https://docs.qodo.ai/qodo-documentation/qodo-merge/tools/improve#extra-instructions-and-best-practices\n> - https://docs.qodo.ai/qodo-documentation/qodo-merge/faq/index#-note-\"q:-i-received-an-incorrect-or-irrelevant-suggestion-why\"\n> - https://docs.qodo.ai/qodo-documentation/qodo-merge/usage-guide/additional_configurations#extra-instructions\n","created_at":"2026-02-11T11:52:49Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T11:52:49Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/557#discussion_r2792861840","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/557","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2792861840"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/557#discussion_r2792861840"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://a