1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>.github/workflows/ci.yml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `288-289`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n> \n> **Inconsistency: Missing `RUSTFLAGS` on this test step.**\n> \n> Other integration test steps (e.g., `modkit_db_integration` at line 247, `dylint` at line 327) have `RUSTFLAGS: \"-C debuginfo=0\"` set, but this step does not. Consider adding it for consistency and the same compile-time benefits.\n> \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🔧 Suggested fix</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n>        - name: Test users_info with Postgres (integration)\n> +        env:\n> +          RUSTFLAGS: \"-C debuginfo=0\"\n>          run: make test-users-info-pg\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn @.github/workflows/release-plz.yml:\n- Around line 86-87: The step name \"cargo test (workspace)\" is outdated given\nthe command now runs `make test-no-macros`; update the GitHub Actions step name\nto accurately describe the command (for example use \"make test-no-macros\" or\n\"make test (no macros)\") so the step label matches the run command and improves\nclarity for readers; modify the step's name field that corresponds to the shown\nstep containing the `run: make test-no-macros` entry.\n- Around line 44-48: Update the GitHub Actions workflow to use the newer Rust\ntoolchain and release-plz action: change the dtolnay/rust-toolchain reference\ncurrently pinned to 1.92.0 to the 1.93.0 release (update the commit hash to the\none for Rust 1.93.0) and update the release-plz/action reference from v0.3.155\nto v0.5 (replace the commit hash to the v0.5 tag commit); keep the pattern of\npinning commit hashes while updating the comment/version labels so\ndtolnay/rust-toolchain and release-plz/action reflect the new versions.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>.github/workflows/ci.yml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`137-141`: **Minor formatting nit: missing blank line between jobs.**\n\nA blank line between the `test_macros` job's last step and the `security` job definition would improve readability and match typical YAML workflow conventions.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>✨ Suggested formatting</summary>\n\n```diff\n       - name: UI tests for modkit macros libraries\n         env:\n           RUSTFLAGS: \"-C debuginfo=0\"\n         run: make test-macros\n+\n   security:\n     name: Security (cargo-deny & cargo-audit on Ubuntu)\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/557#pullrequestreview-3784325037","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/557","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/557#pullrequestreview-3784325037"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/557"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-11T11:48:50Z","commit_id":"703419d7bb15145ba8904aa1546f252d912a9dad"}]},{"source_pr_number":556,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/556","source_state":"closed","source_author":"github-actions[bot]","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #556] chore: release","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"release-plz-2026-02-11T10-35-22Z","pr_head_sha":"b8284d07188f066daa795742ab6e5fb8da7ab5b1","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"cyberfabric","pr_from_fork":0,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/556","id":3271002310,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPaLyBs7C94jG","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/556","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/556.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/556.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/556","number":556,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"chore: release","user":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"\n\n\n## 🤖 New release\n\n* `cf-modkit-security`: 0.2.2 -> 0.2.5\n* `cf-modkit-transport-grpc`: 0.2.4 -> 0.2.5\n* `cf-system-sdk-directory`: 0.1.7 -> 0.1.8\n* `cf-system-sdks`: 0.1.7 -> 0.1.8\n* `cf-modkit-db-macros`: 0.2.4 -> 0.2.5\n* `cf-modkit-errors`: 0.2.4 -> 0.2.5\n* `cf-modkit-errors-macro`: 0.2.4 -> 0.2.5\n* `cf-modkit-odata`: 0.2.4 -> 0.2.5\n* `cf-modkit-utils`: 0.2.2 -> 0.2.5\n* `cf-modkit-db`: 0.2.1 -> 0.2.5\n* `cf-modkit-macros`: 0.2.1 -> 0.2.5\n* `cf-modkit-odata-macros`: 0.2.4 -> 0.2.5\n* `cf-modkit-sdk`: 0.2.4 -> 0.2.5\n* `cf-modkit`: 0.2.1 -> 0.2.5\n* `cf-modkit-http`: 0.2.4 -> 0.2.5\n* `cf-modkit-auth`: 0.2.1 -> 0.2.5\n* `cf-api-gateway`: 0.1.1 -> 0.1.2\n* `cf-grpc-hub`: 0.1.1 -> 0.1.2\n* `cf-types-registry-sdk`: 0.1.1 -> 0.1.2\n* `types-sdk`: 0.2.4 -> 0.2.5\n* `cf-file-parser`: 0.1.1 -> 0.1.2\n* `cf-module-orchestrator`: 0.1.1 -> 0.1.2\n* `cf-modkit-node-info`: 0.2.0 -> 0.2.5\n* `cf-nodes-registry-sdk`: 0.1.1 -> 0.1.2\n* `cf-nodes-registry`: 0.1.1 -> 0.1.2\n* `cf-tenant-resolver-sdk`: 0.1.2 -> 0.1.3\n* `cf-single-tenant-tr-plugin`: 0.1.1 -> 0.1.2\n* `cf-static-tr-plugin`: 0.1.1 -> 0.1.2\n* `cf-tenant-resolver-gw`: 0.1.1 -> 0.1.2\n* `cf-types-registry`: 0.1.1 -> 0.1.2\n\n<details><summary><i><b>Changelog</b></i></summary><p>\n\n\n\n## `cf-system-sdk-directory`\n\n<blockquote>\n\n\n## [0.1.8](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/compare/cf-system-sdk-directory-v0.1.7...cf-system-sdk-directory-v0.1.8) - 2026-02-11\n\n### Other\n\n- release (by @github-actions[bot]) - #546\n\n### Contributors\n\n* @github-actions[bot]\n</blockquote>\n\n## `cf-system-sdks`\n\n<blockquote>\n\n\n## [0.1.8](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/compare/cf-system-sdks-v0.1.7...cf-system-sdks-v0.1.8) - 2026-02-11\n\n### Other\n\n- release (by @github-actions[bot]) - #546\n\n### Contributors\n\n* @github-actions[bot]\n</blockquote>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n## `cf-modkit`\n\n<blockquote>\n\n\n## [0.2.5](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/compare/cf-modkit-v0.2.1...cf-modkit-v0.2.5) - 2026-02-11\n\n### Added\n\n- *(modkit-http)* introduce HttpClient (hyper+tower), replace reqwest and harden JWKS handling (by @MikeFalcon77)\n\n### Fixed\n\n- update module names to use kebab-case convention (by @yoskini) - #459\n- *(dylint/de1301)* allow proc-macro impl methods via visit_assoc_item (by @Artifizer)\n\n### Other\n\n- Merge branch 'main' into shutdown-nl (by @Artifizer) - #475\n- Merge branch 'main' into rescue-docs-standards (by @Artifizer) - #478\n\n### Contributors\n\n* @yoskini\n* @MikeFalcon77\n* @Artifizer\n</blockquote>\n\n## `cf-modkit-http`\n\n<blockquote>\n\n\n## [0.2.5](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/compare/cf-modkit-http-v0.2.4...cf-modkit-http-v0.2.5) - 2026-02-11\n\n### Added\n\n- *(modkit-auth)* add outbound OAuth2 client-credentials token + bearer auth layer (by @MikeFalcon77)\n- *(modkit-http)* introduce HttpClient (hyper+tower), replace reqwest and harden JWKS handling (by @MikeFalcon77)\n\n### Contributors\n\n* @MikeFalcon77\n</blockquote>\n\n\n## `cf-api-gateway`\n\n<blockquote>\n\n\n## [0.1.2](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/compare/cf-api-gateway-v0.1.1...cf-api-gateway-v0.1.2) - 2026-02-11\n\n### Fixed\n\n- update module names to use kebab-case convention (by @yoskini) - #459\n\n### Contributors\n\n* @yoskini\n</blockquote>\n\n## `cf-grpc-hub`\n\n<blockquote>\n\n\n## [0.1.2](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/compare/cf-grpc-hub-v0.1.1...cf-grpc-hub-v0.1.2) - 2026-02-11\n\n### Fixed\n\n- update module names to use kebab-case convention (by @yoskini) - #459\n\n### Contributors\n\n* @yoskini\n</blockquote>\n\n## `cf-types-registry-sdk`\n\n<blockquote>\n\n\n## [0.1.2](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/compare/cf-types-registry-sdk-v0.1.1...cf-types-registry-sdk-v0.1.2) - 2026-02-11\n\n### Fixed\n\n- update module names to use kebab-case convention (by @yoskini) - #459\n\n### Contributors\n\n* @yoskini\n</blockquote>\n\n## `types-sdk`\n\n<blockquote>\n\n\n## [0.2.5](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/compare/types-sdk-v0.2.4...types-sdk-v0.2.5) - 2026-02-11\n\n### Other\n\n- update Cargo.toml dependencies\n</blockquote>\n\n## `cf-file-parser`\n\n<blockquote>\n\n\n## [0.1.2](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/compare/cf-file-parser-v0.1.1...cf-file-parser-v0.1.2) - 2026-02-11\n\n### Fixed\n\n- update module names to use kebab-case convention (by @yoskini) - #459\n\n### Other\n\n- update operation IDs and module names to kebab-case convention (by @yoskini) - #459\n\n### Contributors\n\n* @yoskini\n</blockquote>\n\n## `cf-module