Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat -n ./modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/mime_validation.rs | tail -50\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 2255\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat -n ./modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/mime_validation.rs | sed -n '75,120p'\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 1930\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat -n ./modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/rate_limit.rs | head -120\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 5391\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nrg \"MatchedPath\" -B 3 -A 3\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 2365\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**License gating is bypassed on parameterized endpoints.**\n\n`LicenseRequirementMap` stores template paths from specs (e.g., `/nodes/{id}`), but `req.uri().path()` returns concrete paths (e.g., `/nodes/abc-123`). The exact-match lookup will fail for all parameterized routes, skipping license checks entirely. Use `MatchedPath` to retrieve the matched route template instead.\n\nThe comment claiming this middleware runs \"before nesting\" and that paths are \"already prefix-stripped\" does not apply at the API gateway level where routes are registered with their full paths. This same issue affects `mime_validation.rs` and `rate_limit.rs` identically.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-use axum::extract::Request;\n+use axum::extract::{MatchedPath, Request};\n@@\n-    let path = req.uri().path().to_owned();\n+    let path = req\n+        .extensions()\n+        .get::<MatchedPath>()\n+        .map(|m| m.as_str().to_owned())\n+        .unwrap_or_else(|| req.uri().path().to_owned());\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n    // Use MatchedPath to get the route template, which matches keys in\n    // LicenseRequirementMap. Falls back to the concrete path if unavailable.\n    let path = req\n        .extensions()\n        .get::<MatchedPath>()\n        .map(|m| m.as_str().to_owned())\n        .unwrap_or_else(|| req.uri().path().to_owned());\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/license_validation.rs` around lines\n52 - 56, The middleware uses req.uri().path() for lookups which yields concrete\npaths and so bypasses LicenseRequirementMap for parameterized routes; replace\nthe exact-match logic to first obtain the route template via Axum's MatchedPath\n(e.g., read MatchedPath from request extensions or use MatchedPath extractor)\nand use that template string for LicenseRequirementMap lookups (falling back to\nreq.uri().path() only if MatchedPath is not present); apply the same change to\nmime_validation.rs and rate_limit.rs so all three middlewares match\nparameterized routes by template rather than concrete paths.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-11T07:10:35Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T07:19:58Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/553#discussion_r2791746498","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/553","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2791746498"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/553#discussion_r2791746498"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/553"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://