thub.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/553#pullrequestreview-3782852260","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/553","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/553#pullrequestreview-3782852260"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/553"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-11T05:14:48Z","commit_id":"a2487b2f0851fc9bca27d52ec3cfb223c4fbac87"},{"id":3782909306,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7hep16","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 1**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/module.rs`:\n- Around line 593-601: The middleware is being applied after nesting so\nmiddleware (in apply_middleware_stack) sees prefixed paths and cannot match\noperation keys; to fix, call self.apply_middleware_stack(router)? before doing\nlet prefix = self.prefix() and router = axum::Router::new().nest(&prefix,\nrouter) (i.e., apply_middleware_stack to the un-nested router first), ensuring\nyou keep the same router variable and then perform nesting with prefix()\nafterward so middleware builds its auth/rate-limit/MIME/license maps from\nunprefixed paths.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/553#pullrequestreview-3782909306","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/553","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/553#pullrequestreview-3782909306"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/553"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-11T05:42:36Z","commit_id":"0d7d5a0e99efceccb0d53022abf43c90d4a7e6af"},{"id":3783191567,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7hfuwP","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 3**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/license_validation.rs`:\n- Around line 52-56: The middleware uses req.uri().path() for lookups which\nyields concrete paths and so bypasses LicenseRequirementMap for parameterized\nroutes; replace the exact-match logic to first obtain the route template via\nAxum's MatchedPath (e.g., read MatchedPath from request extensions or use\nMatchedPath extractor) and use that template string for LicenseRequirementMap\nlookups (falling back to req.uri().path() only if MatchedPath is not present);\napply the same change to mime_validation.rs and rate_limit.rs so all three\nmiddlewares match parameterized routes by template rather than concrete paths.\n\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/mime_validation.rs`:\n- Around line 91-94: The middleware currently looks up validation_map using the\nconcrete request path (req.uri().path()), which fails for parameterized routes;\nchange the lookup to use the Axum MatchedPath extension (extract MatchedPath\nfrom req.extensions() or use axum::extract::MatchedPath::from_request parts) to\nobtain the route template (matching OperationSpec.path like \"/users/{id}\") and\nfall back to req.uri().path() only if MatchedPath is absent; apply the same\nchange in the rate_limit_middleware so both mime validation (where\nvalidation_map is consulted) and rate limit lookups use the route template\ninstead of the concrete path.\n\nIn `@modules/system/api-gateway/src/middleware/rate_limit.rs`:\n- Around line 88-92: The middleware currently builds the lookup key from\nreq.uri().path(), causing mismatches with RateLimiterMap keys\n(OperationSpec.path templates like /users/{id}); change the key construction in\nthe rate_limit middleware to first try to read the Axum MatchedPath extension\n(MatchedPath::from_request or req.extensions().get::<MatchedPath>()) and use its\ntemplate string as the path component for the key, falling back to\nreq.uri().path() only if MatchedPath is absent; keep the method as\nreq.method().clone() and ensure the resulting key (method, template_path) is\nused for lookups in RateLimiterMap so parameterized routes correctly hit their\nrate limits.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/553#pullrequestreview-3783191567","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/553","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/553#pullrequestreview-3783191567"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/553"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-11T07:10:36Z","commit_id":"b602411b9be5245571122ee074d4f134c8cd3225"}]},{"source_pr_number":551,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/551","source_state":"closed","source_author":"Artifizer","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #551] chore(cypilot): rename the make target from 'validate-atifacts' to 'cypilot-validate'","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"rescue-docs-standards","pr_head_sha":"c8d5249666dd53c7389ae0d1a399bb95b4fb7c0c","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"Artifizer","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/551","id":3269234247,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPaLyBs7C3I5H","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/551","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/551.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/551.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/551","