/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 1**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n````\nIn `@docs/modkit_unified_system/02_module_layout_and_sdk_pattern.md`:\n- Around line 295-300: The fenced code block showing the error message is\nmissing a language tag which triggers MD040; update the block by adding a\nlanguage identifier such as \"text\" (or \"rust\" if you prefer highlighting) after\nthe opening triple backticks that wrap the error message so the block becomes\n```text (or ```rust) and close as before, ensuring the block starts with the\nlanguage tag and ends with ``` to satisfy the linter.\n````\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/543#pullrequestreview-3780537665","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/543","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/543#pullrequestreview-3780537665"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/543"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-10T17:38:45Z","commit_id":"e7c87acf29a6d049ddfe025dcc7dd76cb0a70e66"}]},{"source_pr_number":540,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/540","source_state":"closed","source_author":"KvizadSaderah","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #540] feat: add REST API to list registered modules (#500)","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"feature/500-list-modules-api","pr_head_sha":"197de1d1dee54331bc777edde2441b3160a8a4be","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"KvizadSaderah","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/540","id":3266613586,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPaLyBs7CtJFS","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/540","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/540.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/540.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/540","number":540,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat: add REST API to list registered modules (#500)","user":{"login":"KvizadSaderah","id":14391797,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzkxNzk3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14391797?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah","html_url":"https://github.com/KvizadSaderah","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\r\n\r\n- Add `GET /module-orchestrator/v1/modules` endpoint that returns all registered modules\r\n- Each module shows: name, capabilities, dependencies, deployment mode (compiled_in / out_of_process), running instances with version/state/gRPC services\r\n- Plugins field reserved in API contract (not yet populated, deferred to follow-up)\r\n\r\n### Changes\r\n\r\n**modkit (libs/modkit)**\r\n- `registry.rs`: Add `ModuleRegistrySnapshot`, `ModuleSnapshot`, `CapabilitySet::labels()`, public getters on `ModuleEntry`\r\n- `system_context.rs`: Extend `SystemContext` with `registry_snapshot` and `oop_module_names`\r\n- `host_runtime.rs`: Build snapshot at startup, pass through `SystemContext`\r\n\r\n**module_orchestrator**\r\n- Add `rest` capability alongside existing `grpc` and `system`\r\n- New `api/rest/` layer (dto, handlers, routes) following `OperationBuilder` pattern\r\n- New `domain/` layer (model, service) with proper domain ↔ DTO separation\r\n- 7 unit tests covering: compiled-in, OoP, dynamic instances, dual-mode modules, state mapping, deterministic ordering\r\n\r\n## Test plan\r\n\r\n- [x] `cargo check` — compiles cleanly\r\n- [x] `cargo test -p cf-modkit` — 199 tests pass\r\n- [x] `cargo test -p cf-module-orchestrator` — 7 tests pass\r\n- [x] `cargo clippy --workspace` — no warnings\r\n- [x] Manual: `curl http://localhost:8087/module-orchestrator/v1/modules` returns 200 with all modules\r\n\r\nCloses #500\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * REST endpoint to list registered modules (capabilities, dependencies, deployment mode, instances, service endpoints) with OpenAPI.\n  * ModulesService for deterministic, sorted module listings aggregated from registry snapshot, runtime manager, and out-of-process sources.\n  * Runtime introspection: registry snapshots and out-of-process module tracking available via runtime/system context.\n\n* **Tests**\n  * Added tests for capability labels, registry snapshots, module listing behavior, and instance state mappings.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-02-10T10:43:42Z","updated_at":"2026-02-19T10:29:36Z","closed_at":"2026-02-19T10:29:36Z","merged_at":"2026-02-19T10:29:35Z","merge_commit_sha":"9d4d5e614cbf81de006466d9838d0b45d80c2082","assignees":[{"login":"KvizadSaderah","id":14391797,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzkxNzk3","avatar_ur