-\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# List directory tree of first level\nls -la | head -30\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 1881\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Try a direct path based on the review comment\ncat \"modules/system/module_orchestrator/src/module.rs\" 2>&1 | head -200\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 5799\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\npwd && ls -la\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 2528\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for ModulesService to find the file\nrg \"ModulesService\" -l | head -10\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 295\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for the exact init function pattern\nrg \"oop_module_names\" -l\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 259\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Look for registry_snapshot pattern\nrg \"registry_snapshot\" -B5 -A15 | head -100\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 7100\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for other uses of arc_swap::ArcSwapOption in the codebase\nrg \"ArcSwapOption\" -B2 -A2 | head -60\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 4394\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if modules_service is ever reassigned elsewhere\nrg \"modules_service\" -B1 -A1\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 1199\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Look for init being called more than once or defensive patterns\nrg \"\\.init\\(\" -B2 -A2 | head -80\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 5200\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Guard `ModulesService` initialization against double init for consistency**\n\nLine 119 stores the service without a guard. While `directory_api` and other fields on lines 104, 67, 71, 75 explicitly error on double initialization via `OnceLock::set()`, the `modules_service` uses `ArcSwapOption::store()` which silently replaces the value. For consistency with the error-on-double-init pattern established for other fields, add an explicit guard.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n         let modules_service = ModulesService::new(registry_snapshot, manager, oop_module_names);\n-        self.modules_service.store(Some(Arc::new(modules_service)));\n+        if self.modules_service.load().is_some() {\n+            return Err(anyhow::anyhow!(\"ModulesService already set (init called twice?)\"));\n+        }\n+        self.modules_service.store(Some(Arc::new(modules_service)));\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n        // Create the ModulesService for the REST endpoint\n        let registry_snapshot = self\n            .registry_snapshot\n            .get()\n            .cloned()\n            .ok_or_else(|| anyhow::anyhow!(\"RegistrySnapshot not wired\"))?;\n        let oop_module_names = self\n            .oop_module_names\n            .get()\n            .cloned()\n            .ok_or_else(|| anyhow::anyhow!(\"OoP module names not wired\"))?;\n\n        let modules_service = ModulesService::new(registry_snapshot, manager, oop_module_names);\n        if self.modules_service.load().is_some() {\n            return Err(anyhow::anyhow!(\"ModulesService already set (init called twice?)\"));\n        }\n        self.modules_service.store(Some(Arc::new(modules_service)));\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/module_orchestrator/src/module.rs` around lines 106 - 119,\nProtect ModulesService from double initialization like the other fields: before\ncalling self.modules_service.store(...), check whether self.modules_service\nalready contains a value (e.g., self.modules_service.load().is_some()) and\nreturn an error (anyhow::anyhow!(\"ModulesService already initialized\")) instead\nof silently overwriting; locate the ModulesService::new(...) and\nself.modules_service.store(...) sequence in module.rs and add that guard so\ninitialization fails on double init consistent with OnceLock::set() behavior\nused for directory_api and others.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Confirmed as addressed by @KvizadSaderah\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-10T12:58:22Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T13:14:58Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/540#discussion_r2787819953","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/540","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787819953"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/540#discussion_r2787819953"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/540"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787819953/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":106,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":119,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":100,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787895039","pull_request_review_id":3778888642,"id":2787895039,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6m