m/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/535#issuecomment-3874556556","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/535","id":3874556556,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7m8QqM","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-10T00:07:44Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T19:41:49Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> ## Review skipped\n> \n> This PR was authored by the user configured for CodeRabbit reviews. By default, CodeRabbit skips reviewing PRs authored by this user. It's recommended to use a dedicated user account to post CodeRabbit review feedback.\n> \n> To trigger a single review, invoke the `@coderabbitai review` command.\n> \n> You can disable this status message by setting the `reviews.review_status` to `false` in the CodeRabbit configuration file.\n> \n> Use the checkbox below for a quick retry:\n> - [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\": \"e9bb8d72-00e8-4f67-9cb2-caf3b22574fe\"} --> 🔍 Trigger review\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nAdds outbound OAuth2 client‑credentials support and secret-safe token handling in libs/modkit-auth, introduces a modkit-http auth hook to inject auth into the tower stack, centralizes HTTP error formatting, and adds a zeroizing SecretString utility in libs/modkit-utils.\n\n## Changes\n\n|Cohort / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**Workspace & Manifests** <br> `Cargo.toml`, `libs/modkit-utils/Cargo.toml`, `libs/modkit-auth/Cargo.toml`|Added dependencies: `zeroize`, `aliri_tokens`, `aliri_clock`, `url`, `base64`, `modkit-utils`, and test/dev deps to support token lifecycle, secrets, and HTTP interactions.|\n|**Architecture & ADRs** <br> `docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md`, `docs/adrs/modkit/0001-modkit-hyper-tower-http-client.md`, `docs/adrs/modkit/0002-modkit-auth-client-with-aliri.md`, `docs/modkit_unified_system/README.md`|Introduced `modkit-http` entry and expanded `modkit-auth` docs; added ADR documenting generic auth-layer hook and OAuth2 client‑credentials design.|\n|**Design & Implementation Plan** <br> `libs/modkit-auth/docs/*`|Added phased implementation/design docs for OAuth2 token sourcing, watcher semantics, bearer layer, OIDC discovery, error mapping, and tests.|\n|**Public Surface & Module Layout** <br> `libs/modkit-auth/src/lib.rs`, `libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/mod.rs`|Added `oauth2` and `http_error` modules; re-exported OAuth2 public API items (Token, BearerAuthLayer, OAuthClientConfig, TokenError, HttpClientBuilderExt, SecretString).|\n|**OAuth2 Config, Types & Errors** <br> `libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/config.rs`, `.../types.rs`, `.../error.rs`|New `OAuthClientConfig` with validation and redacted Debug; `ClientAuthMethod`, `TokenResponse`, and `TokenError` enum with tests.|\n|**OIDC Discovery & Token Source** <br> `libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/discovery.rs`, `libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/source.rs`|Added OIDC discovery helper and `OAuthTokenSource` implementing client‑credentials exchange (Form/Basic), parsing, TTL handling, and HTTP error mapping with tests.|\n|**Token Management & Watcher** <br> `libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/token.rs`|New `Token` handle using ArcSwap and background TokenWatcher; APIs: `new`, `get`, `invalidate`; includes OIDC discovery integration and extensive tests.|\n|**Bearer Layer & Builder Ext** <br> `libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/layer.rs`, `libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/builder_ext.rs`|Tower `BearerAuthLayer`/`BearerAuthService` for injecting Authorization header and `HttpClientBuilderExt` to wire it into `modkit_http::HttpClientBuilder`.|\n|**Shared HTTP Error Formatting & JWKS tweak** <br> `libs/modkit-auth/src/http_error.rs`, `libs/modkit-auth/src/providers/jwks.rs`|Added `format_http_error(&HttpError, prefix)` and adjusted JWKS error mapping to call it by reference to avoid ownership moves; unit tests added for formatting.|\n|**HttpClient Auth Hook** <br> `libs/modkit-http/src/builder.rs`|Added `InnerService` alias and `auth_layer: Option<Box<dyn FnOnce(InnerService)->InnerService + Send>>`; added `with_auth_layer()` and applied wrapper in build() between boxing and retry/timeout.|\n|**Secret utilities** <br> `libs/modkit-utils/src/lib.rs`, `libs/modkit-utils/src/secret_string.rs`|Added `SecretString` wrapper with `Zeroize`/`ZeroizeOnDrop`, redacted Debug/Display, clone and expose() accessor, and re-exported type.|\n\n## Sequence Diagram(s)\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant App as Application\n    participant Token as Token Handle\n    participant Watcher as Background Watcher\n    participant Source as OAuthTokenSource\n    participant HttpClient as modkit_http::HttpClient\n    participant TokenEndpoint as OAuth2 Token Endpoint\n\n    App->>Token: Token::new(config) async\n    Token->>Token: validate config\n    alt issuer_url provided\n        Token->>HttpClient: discover_token_endpoint(issuer_url)\n        HttpClient->>TokenEndpoint: GET /.well-known/openid-configuration\n        TokenEndpoint-->>HttpClient: {token_endpoint}\n        HttpClient-->>Token: token_endpoint_url\n    end\n    Token->>Watcher: spawn_watcher(source, config)\n    Watcher->>Source: request_token()\n    Source->>HttpClient: POST /token (client creds)\n    HttpClient->>TokenEndpoint: HTTP POST\n    TokenEndpoint-->>HttpClient: {access_token, expires_in, token_type}\n    HttpClient-->>Source: TokenResponse\n    Source->>Watcher: TokenWithLifetime\n    Watcher->>Token: Atomic swap via ArcSwap\n    App->>Token: token.get()\n    Token->>Watcher: watcher.watch()\n    Watcher-->>Token: AccessToken\n    Token-->>App: SecretString\n```\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant Builder as HttpClientBuilder\n    participant Client as modkit_http::HttpClient\n    participant AuthLayer as BearerAuthLayer\n    participant AuthService as BearerAuthService\n    participant Token as Token Handle\n    participant Inner as InnerService\n\n    Builder->>Client: build() (auth_layer applied)\n    Client->>AuthService: Service::call(request)\n    AuthService->>Token: token.get()\n    Token->>Token: read via ArcSwap\n    Token-->>AuthService: SecretString\n    AuthService->>Inner: call(request with Authorization)\n    Inner-->>AuthService: Response\n    AuthService-->>Client: Response\n```\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~60 minutes\n\n## Possibly related issues\n\n- cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core#538: Adds outbound OAuth2 client‑credentials and bearer layer in libs/modkit-auth — aligns with this PR's OAuth2 implementation.\n\n## Possibly related PRs\n\n- cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core#433: Modifies `modkit-http` HttpClientBuilder auth-layer and integrates with `modkit-auth` — strong overlap with builder/auth-layer changes.\n\n## Suggested reviewers\n\n- Artifizer  \n- striped-zebra-dev  \n- Bechma\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐇 I hid the secrets in a string so neat,  \n> and zeroed them out when day was complete.  \n> Watchers hum, tokens hop in time,  \n> Bearer headers leap — no tangled line.  \n> A rabbit's nibble: tidy, safe, and sweet.\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚥 Pre-merge checks | ✅ 3</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Passed checks (3 passed)</summary>\n\n|     Check name     | Status   | Explanation                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| :----------------: | :------- | :------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n|  Description Check | ✅ Passed | Check skipped - CodeRabbit’s high-level summary is enabled.                                                                                                                                                                                             |\n|     Title check    | ✅ Passed | The title 'feat(modkit-auth): add outbound OAuth2 client-credentials token + bearer auth layer' accurately describes the main changes: adding OAuth2 client credentials support with token management and a Bearer authentication layer to modkit-auth. |\n| Docstring Coverage | ✅ Passed | Docstring coverage is 100.00% which is sufficient. The required threshold is 80.00%.                                                                                                                                                                    |\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can configure your own custom pre-merge checks in the settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_end -->\n\n<!-- announcements_start -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> [Issue Planner](https://www.coderabbit.ai/issue-planner) is now in beta. Read the [docs](https://docs.coderabbit.ai/issues/planning) and try it out! Share your feedback on [Discord](https://discord.com/invite/coderabbit).\n\n<!-- announcements_end -->\n\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3874556556/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3874557535","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/535#issuecomment-3874557535","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/535","id":3874557535,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7m8Q5f","user":{"login":"qodo-code-review[bot]","id":151058649,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCQD42Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/484649?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-10T00:08:04Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T00:08:04Z","body":"<h3>Review Summary by Qodo</h3>\n\nAdd outbound OAuth2 client credentials with automatic token refresh and bearer auth layer\n\n<code>✨ Enhancement</code> <code>📝 Documentation</code>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n<h3>Walkthroughs</h3>\n\n<details open>\n<summary>Description</summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n<pre>\n• Implement outbound OAuth2 client credentials flow with automatic token refresh using\n  <b><i>aliri_tokens</i></b> library\n• Add <b><i>Token</i></b> handle with lock-free <b><i>ArcSwap</i></b>-based invalidation for token rotation after 401 errors\n• Implement <b><i>BearerAuthLayer</i></b> tower middleware to inject <b><i>Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;</i></b> headers\n  into outbound requests\n• Support OIDC discovery via <b><i>/.well-known/openid-configuration</i></b> for dynamic token endpoint\n  resolution\n• Extract shared <b><i>format_http_error()</i></b> helper for consistent HTTP error formatting across modules\n• Implement <b><i>SecretString</i></b> wrapper type with automatic buffer zeroization to prevent accidental\n  secret exposure\n• Add <b><i>with_auth_layer()</i></b> hook to <b><i>HttpClientBuilder</i></b> for composing custom auth middleware without\n  circular dependencies\n• Provide fluent API via <b><i>HttpClientBuilderExt</i></b> trait for integrating bearer auth into HTTP client\n  configuration\n• Include comprehensive configuration validation, error handling, and security-focused design\n  (secret redaction, no response body logging)\n• Document OAuth2 architecture decisions and implementation plan in ADRs and design specifications\n</pre>\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Diagram</summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n>\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  A[\"HttpClientBuilder\"] -->|with_bearer_auth| B[\"BearerAuthLayer\"]\n  B -->|requests token| C[\"OAuthTokenSource\"]\n  C -->|exchanges credentials| D[\"Token Endpoint\"]\n  D -->|returns token| E[\"Token Handle\"]\n  E -->|ArcSwap invalidation| F[\"Bearer Header Injection\"]\n  G[\"OIDC Discovery\"] -->|resolves endpoint| C\n  H[\"SecretString\"] -->|redacts secrets| I[\"Error Formatting\"]\n```\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n<h3>File Changes</h3>\n\n<details>\n<summary>1. libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/source.rs\n <code>✨ Enhancement</code> <code> +441/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>OAuth2 token source with client credentials exchange\n><pre>\n>• Implements <b><i>OAuthTokenSource</i></b> struct that performs OAuth2 client credentials token exchange using\n>  <b><i>modkit-http::HttpClient</i></b>\n>• Implements <b><i>aliri_tokens::AsyncTokenSource</i></b> trait with <b><i>request_token()</i></b> method handling\n>  form/Basic auth, scope joining, and token validation\n>• Supports both Basic auth (Authorization header) and Form auth (credentials in request body)\n>  methods\n>• Includes comprehensive unit tests covering auth methods, scope handling, error cases, and token\n>  type validation\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/535/files#diff-97ecc9ecfda2877507e4613735f74b7a273d000657cc9a9c0349dfac26d3e393'> libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/source.rs\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>2. libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/token.rs\n <code>✨ Enhancement</code> <code> +400/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Token handle with ArcSwap-based invalidation and OIDC discovery\n><pre>\n>• Implements public <b><i>Token</i></b> handle wrapping <b><i>aliri_tokens::TokenWatcher</i></b> with <b><i>ArcSwap</i></b> for\n>  lock-free invalidation\n>• Provides <b><i>get()</i></b> method for lock-free token reads and <b><i>invalidate()</i></b> for forcing token refresh\n>  after 401 errors\n>• Supports OIDC discovery via <b><i>issuer_url</i></b> as alternative to direct <b><i>token_endpoint</i></b>\n>• Includes tests for concurrent access, invalidation, OIDC discovery, and debug safety\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/535/files#diff-7c72c399351f6ef2f2b293e40d1e7c2fbad231545e1cf4c4c545a0e862c94e10'> libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/token.rs\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>3. libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/layer.rs\n <code>✨ Enhancement</code> <code> +273/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Tower layer for bearer token injection in outbound requests\n><pre>\n>• Implements <b><i>BearerAuthLayer</i></b> and <b><i>BearerAuthService</i></b> tower middleware for injecting\n>  <b><i>Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;</i></b> headers\n>• Supports custom header names via <b><i>with_header_name()</i></b> for vendor-specific requirements\n>• Handles async token acquisition within the service call with proper error mapping to <b><i>HttpError</i></b>\n>• Includes tests for header injection, custom headers, and debug safety\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/535/files#diff-a1efdd0441f4e2c1efc086f845a0e57bfaa25def37db44e8d6cb687a9e66d0cc'> libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/layer.rs\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary><ins><strong>View more (20)</strong></ins></summary><br/>\n<details>\n<summary>4. libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/config.rs\n <code>✨ Enhancement</code> <code> +223/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>OAuth2 client configuration with validation and secret redaction\n><pre>\n>• Defines <b><i>OAuthClientConfig</i></b> with support for both direct <b><i>token_endpoint</i></b> and OIDC <b><i>issuer_url</i></b>\n>  (mutually exclusive)\n>• Includes refresh policy parameters (offset, jitter, min period, default TTL) and HTTP client\n>  configuration override\n>• Implements manual <b><i>Debug</i></b> to redact <b><i>client_secret</i></b> and <b><i>validate()</i></b> method for config consistency\n>  checks\n>• Provides sensible defaults (30 min refresh offset, 5 min jitter, 10 sec min period, 5 min default\n>  TTL)\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/535/files#diff-9f032e0d45e85fdb71a642d34ee3c5c746faecdbe9487bb413b19f44b4d3a9e9'> libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/config.rs\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>5. libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/discovery.rs\n <code>✨ Enhancement</code> <code> +200/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>OIDC discovery for resolving token endpoints from issuer URLs\n><pre>\n>• Implements OIDC discovery via <b><i>discover_token_endpoint()</i></b> function that fetches\n>  <b><i>/.well-known/openid-configuration</i></b>\n>• Parses minimal <b><i>OidcDiscoveryDoc</i></b> with only required <b><i>token_endpoint</i></b> field, ignoring unknown\n>  fields\n>• Handles trailing slash normalization and URL validation with proper error mapping\n>• Includes tests for valid responses, missing fields, invalid URLs, and HTTP errors\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/535/files#diff-87102288c69ae97bc226508595d294486e0d2e9da1f84d753b7bd605b84681cd'> libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/discovery.rs\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>6. libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/builder_ext.rs\n <code>✨ Enhancement</code> <code> +156/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Extension trait for HttpClientBuilder bearer auth integration\n><pre>\n>• Implements <b><i>HttpClientBuilderExt</i></b> trait adding <b><i>with_bearer_auth()</i></b> and\n>  <b><i>with_bearer_auth_header()</i></b> methods to <b><i>HttpClientBuilder</i></b>\n>• Integrates <b><i>BearerAuthLayer</i></b> into the HTTP client tower stack via the auth layer hook\n>• Provides fluent API for composing bearer auth with other client configuration\n>• Includes integration tests verifying header injection and absence without auth\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/535/files#diff-052b0ab415a5fbfff382900b399d3b9a263d5cf98514e62df850f496122f7438'> libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/builder_ext.rs\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>7. libs/modkit-auth/src/http_error.rs\n <code>✨ Enhancement</code> <code> +119/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Shared HTTP error formatting helper with context prefix\n><pre>\n>• Extracts shared <b><i>format_http_error()</i></b> helper function for consistent HTTP error formatting across\n>  modules\n>• Handles all <b><i>HttpError</i></b> variants exhaustively with context prefix parameter (e.g., &quot;JWKS&quot;, &quot;OAuth2\n>  token&quot;)\n>• Deliberately excludes response body from output for security (prevents server diagnostics leaking\n>  into logs)\n>• Includes comprehensive unit tests for all error variants\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/535/files#diff-8e04c40c4dd3267759835cc36c09e654b4a3463f5b1ddbbb2865ecdf659b8f99'> libs/modkit-auth/src/http_error.rs\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>8. libs/modkit-auth/src/providers/jwks.rs\n <code> Refactoring </code> <code> +4/-58 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Refactor JWKS error mapping to use shared helper\n><pre>\n>• Refactors <b><i>map_http_error()</i></b> function to use shared <b><i>format_http_error()</i></b> helper from <b><i>http_error</i></b>\n>  module\n>• Removes exhaustive match on <b><i>HttpError</i></b> variants, replacing with single-line delegation\n>• Maintains identical error message formatting and security properties\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/535/files#diff-b05539620684dec3c45023537eed4367c4c0c79f79f23ece6bc0a71c1eef7cae'> libs/modkit-auth/src/providers/jwks.rs\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>9. libs/modkit-http/src/builder.rs\n <code>✨ Enhancement</code> <code> +43/-2 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Add auth layer hook to HttpClientBuilder tower stack\n><pre>\n>• Adds <b><i>with_auth_layer()</i></b> method to <b><i>HttpClientBuilder</i></b> for inserting custom auth middleware\n>• Defines <b><i>InnerService</i></b> type alias for type-erased service between layer composition steps\n>• Positions auth layer between retry and timeout in tower stack (inside retry loop, outside timeout)\n>• Includes unit test verifying auth layer integration\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/535/files#diff-609ca597a824cbcfb1c8bb86a29690bd2b2932b73fe3e4178088939dd25b8cef'> libs/modkit-http/src/builder.rs\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>10. libs/modkit-utils/src/secret_string.rs\n <code>✨ Enhancement</code> <code> +96/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>\n><pre>\n>  Opaque secret string wrapper with automatic buffer zeroization\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/535/files#diff-00c1157820461cafcdb11d3bfd33b1bc9f756bb02eb9f5eecc9c8ef74ab22c7a'> libs/modkit-utils/src/secret_string.rs\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>11. libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/types.rs\n <code>✨ Enhancement</code> <code> +71/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>OAuth2 types for auth methods and token responses\n><pre>\n>• Defines <b><i>ClientAuthMethod</i></b> enum with <b><i>Basic</i></b> (default) and <b><i>Form</i></b> variants for OAuth2 credential\n>  transmission\n>• Implements <b><i>TokenResponse</i></b> struct (Deserialize-only) with <b><i>access_token</i></b>, <b><i>expires_in</i></b>, and\n>  <b><i>token_type</i></b> fields\n>• Re-exports <b><i>SecretString</i></b> from <b><i>modkit-utils</i></b> for consistent secret handling\n>• Includes tests for deserialization of full and minimal responses with unknown field handling\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/535/files#diff-fa7f760d1219509d3715bd8bccc571edc6353f8cc83408c3ecdfb46eedf7762a'> libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/types.rs\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>12. libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/error.rs\n <code>✨ Enhancement</code> <code> +73/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>OAuth2 token error types with secret-safe formatting\n><pre>\n>• Defines <b><i>TokenError</i></b> enum with variants for HTTP, invalid response, unsupported token type,\n>  config, and unavailable states\n>• Uses <b><i>thiserror</i></b> for Display implementation with careful message construction to prevent secret\n>  leakage\n>• Marked <b><i>#[non_exhaustive]</i></b> for forward compatibility\n>• Includes unit tests verifying error message rendering\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/535/files#diff-9cde83be03f5c5e36bdc276c9af50c455a789c0a2ff3b26ae54a46c52cf68995'> libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/error.rs\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>13. libs/modkit-auth/src/lib.rs\n <code>✨ Enhancement</code> <code> +10/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Wire OAuth2 module and shared error formatting into crate\n><pre>\n>• Adds <b><i>pub mod http_error</i></b> for shared HTTP error formatting\n>• Adds <b><i>pub mod oauth2</i></b> for outbound OAuth2 client credentials functionality\n>• Re-exports public OAuth2 types and traits at crate root: <b><i>Token</i></b>, <b><i>TokenError</i></b>,\n>  <b><i>OAuthClientConfig</i></b>, <b><i>ClientAuthMethod</i></b>, <b><i>BearerAuthLayer</i></b>, <b><i>HttpClientBuilderExt</i></b>, <b><i>SecretString</i></b>\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/535/files#diff-5a2032742f259de9df5bde8c26eccaa856849b1c1fc7e2aac3cc0cb5c352ce54'> libs/modkit-auth/src/lib.rs\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>14. libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/mod.rs\n <code>✨ Enhancement</code> <code> +20/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>OAuth2 module structure and public API re-exports\n><pre>\n>• Declares OAuth2 submodules: <b><i>builder_ext</i></b>, <b><i>config</i></b>, <b><i>discovery</i></b>, <b><i>error</i></b>, <b><i>layer</i></b>, <b><i>source</i></b>,\n>  <b><i>token</i></b>, <b><i>types</i></b>\n>• Re-exports public API: <b><i>HttpClientBuilderExt</i></b>, <b><i>OAuthClientConfig</i></b>, <b><i>TokenError</i></b>,\n>  <b><i>BearerAuthLayer</i></b>, <b><i>Token</i></b>, <b><i>ClientAuthMethod</i></b>, <b><i>SecretString</i></b>\n>• Marks internal modules (<b><i>discovery</i></b>, <b><i>source</i></b>) as <b><i>pub(crate)</i></b>\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/535/files#diff-d5c282feec1df9c324e83350589f06cd586d3fe8d7d08b86639899a80bce8734'> libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/mod.rs\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>15. libs/modkit-utils/src/lib.rs\n <code>✨ Enhancement</code> <code> +3/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Export SecretString from modkit-utils\n><pre>\n>• Adds <b><i>pub mod secret_string</i></b> module declaration\n>• Re-exports <b><i>SecretString</i></b> at crate root for convenient access\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/535/files#diff-0f469fe729291cd84105a232d9bef16554b9b4501155c53c7f17c03ff02ed379'> libs/modkit-utils/src/lib.rs\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>16. libs/modkit-auth/docs/modkit-auth-client-impl.md\n <code>📝 Documentation</code> <code> +792/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Implementation plan for OAuth2 client credentials phases 0-6\n><pre>\n>• Comprehensive implementation plan for outbound OAuth2 client credentials across 6 phases\n>• Documents existing code patterns to reuse from JWKS provider (ArcSwap, HttpClient, error mapping)\n>• Provides detailed prompts and guards for each phase with specific file locations, function\n>  signatures, and test requirements\n>• Includes reference to ADR 0002 and establishes patterns for secret safety, lock-free reads, and\n>  tower middleware integration\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/535/files#diff-1e4623c77cc84adb0f04914dd4f9cae3170f9ef2fa3102c52afa0c028fe114f5'> libs/modkit-auth/docs/modkit-auth-client-impl.md\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>17. docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md\n <code>📝 Documentation</code> <code> +2/-1 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Update architecture manifest for OAuth2 client credentials\n><pre>\n>• Updates <b><i>modkit-auth</i></b> description to include outbound OAuth2 client credentials with automatic\n>  token refresh\n>• Adds reference to ADR 0002 for OAuth2 design decisions\n>• Clarifies distinction between inbound JWT/OIDC validation and outbound OAuth2 flows\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/535/files#diff-5f16192750d1dcd73eb6e577bac6e1b2e35814ad58723cf0fc077d599998bea5'> docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>18. docs/adrs/modkit/0001-modkit-hyper-tower-http-client.md\n <code>📝 Documentation</code> <code> +1/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Document auth layer hook in HTTP client ADR\n><pre>\n>• Adds note about generic auth layer hook via <b><i>HttpClientBuilder::with_auth_layer()</i></b>\n>• Explains how the hook enables <b><i>modkit-auth</i></b> to inject <b><i>BearerAuthLayer</i></b> without circular\n>  dependency\n>• Documents that auth layer is inserted between retry and timeout in tower stack\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/535/files#diff-c680063ef30dc241cb9673777c8e177516c04e11b3e86a918709f13485626307'> docs/adrs/modkit/0001-modkit-hyper-tower-http-client.md\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>19. libs/modkit-auth/Cargo.toml\n <code> Dependencies </code> <code> +12/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Add OAuth2 and secret handling dependencies\n><pre>\n>• Adds dependencies for OAuth2: <b><i>aliri_tokens</i></b>, <b><i>aliri_clock</i></b>, <b><i>base64</i></b>, <b><i>url</i></b>\n>• Adds <b><i>modkit-utils</i></b> dependency for <b><i>SecretString</i></b>\n>• Adds <b><i>zeroize</i></b> for secure buffer clearing\n>• Adds dev-dependencies: <b><i>bytes</i></b>, <b><i>http-body-util</i></b> for test support\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/535/files#diff-91b97aaa8a02d0309470cad35380c7898b2dbd9fccfc0d115880cff4905d5d6e'> libs/modkit-auth/Cargo.toml\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>20. Cargo.toml\n <code> Dependencies </code> <code> +5/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Add workspace dependencies for OAuth2 and zeroization\n><pre>\n>• Adds workspace-level dependencies: <b><i>zeroize</i></b> with derive feature, <b><i>aliri_tokens</i></b>, <b><i>aliri_clock</i></b>\n>• Enables secure secret handling and OAuth2 token lifecycle management across workspace\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/535/files#diff-2e9d962a08321605940b5a657135052fbcef87b5e360662bb527c96d9a615542'> Cargo.toml\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>21. libs/modkit-utils/Cargo.toml\n <code> Dependencies </code> <code> +1/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Add zeroize dependency for secret string handling\n><pre>\n>• Adds <b><i>zeroize</i></b> dependency for secure buffer clearing in <b><i>SecretString</i></b>\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/535/files#diff-f5f9084de644dc0b8384753a02c908718f8bdf03997a07fca455104b29fc7428'> libs/modkit-utils/Cargo.toml\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>22. docs/adrs/modkit/0002-modkit-auth-client-with-aliri.md <code>📝 Documentation</code> <code> +72/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>ADR for OAuth2 client credentials with aliri_tokens\n><pre>\n>• Introduces ADR documenting OAuth2 Client Credentials implementation using <b><i>aliri_tokens</i></b> and\n>  <b><i>modkit-http</i></b>\n>• Details decision rationale: delegating token lifecycle to <b><i>aliri_tokens</i></b>, reusing\n>  <b><i>modkit-http::HttpClient</i></b> for token endpoint calls, implementing auth as a tower layer\n>• Documents all public API modules (<b><i>config</i></b>, <b><i>types</i></b>, <b><i>error</i></b>, <b><i>token</i></b>, <b><i>layer</i></b>, <b><i>builder_ext</i></b>,\n>  <b><i>discovery</i></b>, <b><i>source</i></b>) with their responsibilities and types\n>• Explains architecture decisions: no circular dependency via extension trait pattern, one-time OIDC\n>  discovery, secret safety via <b><i>Zeroizing&lt;String&gt;</i></b>, and tower stack ordering\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/535/files#diff-9b9acd8afca5860fe0c51a47bc7d234a9b2be303511b8765ea42c1dda06d3b95'> docs/adrs/modkit/0002-modkit-auth-client-with-aliri.md </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>23. libs/modkit-auth/docs/design.md <code>📝 Documentation</code> <code> +138/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Detailed design specification for modkit-auth OAuth2\n><pre>\n>• Provides detailed design specification for <b><i>modkit-auth</i></b> OAuth2 implementation covering dependency\n>  policy, public API, and token configuration\n>• Specifies <b><i>Token</i></b> struct API with <b><i>get()</i></b> and <b><i>invalidate()</i></b> methods, ensuring modules never see\n>  raw credentials\n>• Documents token source responsibilities: endpoint resolution (direct or via OIDC discovery),\n>  client credentials grant exchange, response parsing, and error handling\n>• Details invalidation semantics using <b><i>ArcSwap</i></b> for lock-free token rotation and outbound auth\n>  layer integration via tower middleware\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/535/files#diff-fe0a3902dd4ff15deb48d47e24f57c6432c3e61941c604c74ae7bbb79e198eb2'> libs/modkit-auth/docs/design.md </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n\n<a href=\"https://www.qodo.ai\"><img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/qodo-logo.svg\" width=\"80\" alt=\"Qodo Logo\"></a>","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3874557535/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":484649,"client_id":"Iv1.8b06d3cf5deea057","slug":"qodo-code-review","node_id":"A_kwHOCuzIt84AB2Up","owner":{"login":"qodo-ai","id":183290039,"node_id":"O_kgDOCuzItw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/183290039?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai","html_url":"https://github.com/qodo-ai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Qodo Code Review","description":"### The AI Code Review Platform\r\n\r\n## Get Started\r\nSimply sign into Github and click the \"Configure\" button. Check out our documentation for more info: https://docs.qodo.ai/get-started.\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\nQodo automatically reviews every GitHub pull request, identifies logic bugs, edge cases, security issues, and code quality problems, and provides actionable suggestions your team can apply immediately.\r\n\r\nInstall in minutes. Integrates seamlessly into your existing workflows.\r\n\r\n## Qodo is designed for developers who:\r\n- Handle frequent pull requests and need reliable review coverage\r\n- Balance code quality with fast delivery\r\n- Work in complex, multi-repo systems\r\n- Use AI-generated code and need stronger guardrails\r\n- Build production software where reliability matters\r\n\r\n## Qodo Capabilities\r\n- ## Automated PR Analysis\r\n  - Reviews every pull request automatically\r\n  - No manual trigger required\r\n\r\n- ## Context-Aware Code Review\r\n  - Understands cross-file changes\r\n  - Detects architectural inconsistencies\r\n\r\n- ## Actionable Suggestions\r\n  - Concrete code fixes\r\n  - Clear explanations\r\n  - Prioritized feedback\r\n\r\n- ## Security & Reliability Checks\r\n  - Identifies risky patterns\r\n  - Reduces attack surface area","external_url":"https://www.qodo.ai/","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","created_at":"2023-11-16T16:18:38Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T15:53:40Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"read","contents":"write","discussions":"write","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","discussion_comment","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review_comment","push"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3874594996","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/535#issuecomment-3874594996","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/535","id":3874594996,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7m8aC0","user":{"login":"qodo-code-review[bot]","id":151058649,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCQD42Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/484649?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-10T00:17:08Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T00:17:08Z","body":"<h3>Code Review by Qodo</h3>\n\n<code>🐞 Bugs (2)</code>  <code>📘 Rule violations (2)</code>  <code>📎 Requirement gaps (0)</code>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n<br/>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/action-required.png\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Action required\">\n\n<details>\n<summary>  1.  <b><i>OAuthClientConfig::validate()</i></b> misses credentials <code>📘 Rule violation</code> <code>⛨ Security</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>• <b><i>OAuthClientConfig::validate()</i></b> only checks mutual exclusivity of <b><i>token_endpoint</i></b> vs\n>   <b><i>issuer_url</i></b>, but does not validate other external inputs like empty <b><i>client_id</i></b>, empty\n>   <b><i>client_secret</i></b>, or nonsensical durations (e.g., <b><i>default_ttl == 0</i></b>).\n>• This can lead to malformed/unauthenticated token requests and confusing downstream failures rather\n>   than failing fast with actionable configuration errors.\n>• It violates the requirement to validate and securely handle external inputs used for\n>   authentication flows.\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/config.rs[R69-79]](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/535/files#diff-9f032e0d45e85fdb71a642d34ee3c5c746faecdbe9487bb413b19f44b4d3a9e9R69-R79)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>+    pub fn validate(&self) -> Result<(), TokenError> {\n>+        match (&self.token_endpoint, &self.issuer_url) {\n>+            (Some(_), Some(_)) => Err(TokenError::ConfigError(\n>+                \"token_endpoint and issuer_url are mutually exclusive\".into(),\n>+            )),\n>+            (None, None) => Err(TokenError::ConfigError(\n>+                \"one of token_endpoint or issuer_url must be set\".into(),\n>+            )),\n>+            _ => Ok(()),\n>+        }\n>+    }\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details >\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>The compliance rule requires validation of external inputs used in authentication and secure data\n>handling. The code shows <b><i>validate()</i></b> only enforces endpoint exclusivity and the defaults allow\n>empty credentials, indicating missing validation for critical auth inputs.\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>Rule 6: Generic: Security-First Input Validation and Data Handling</code>\n> <code>[libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/config.rs[69-79]](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/blob/230e97719711844b492ea9e46842dcd2d2ba4119/libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/config.rs/#L69-L79)</code>\n> <code>[libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/config.rs[121-137]](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/blob/230e97719711844b492ea9e46842dcd2d2ba4119/libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/config.rs/#L121-L137)</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>```\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>## Issue description\n>`OAuthClientConfig::validate()` currently only checks endpoint exclusivity and does not fail fast for invalid authentication inputs (e.g., empty `client_id` / `client_secret`, zero durations). This is missing security-first input validation for an outbound OAuth2 client-credentials flow.\n>\n>## Issue Context\n>The config is fed by external configuration and directly drives authentication behavior. Invalid inputs should be rejected early with `TokenError::ConfigError` to avoid ambiguous runtime failures.\n>\n>## Fix Focus Areas\n>- libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/config.rs[61-79]\n>- libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/config.rs[121-137]\n>```\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>  2.  <b><i>expires_in=0</i></b> yields zero lifetime <code>📘 Rule violation</code> <code>⛯ Reliability</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>• <b><i>OAuthTokenSource::request_token()</i></b> uses <b><i>expires_in</i></b> as-is, so a token response with `expires_in:\n>   0` results in a zero-second lifetime.\n>• A zero lifetime can cause immediate refresh loops / hot spinning under load, degrading reliability\n>   and increasing token endpoint traffic.\n>• This is an unhandled boundary case in a critical auth flow.\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/source.rs[R156-165]](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/535/files#diff-97ecc9ecfda2877507e4613735f74b7a273d000657cc9a9c0349dfac26d3e393R156-R165)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>+        // -- compute lifetime ----------------------------------------------------\n>+        let lifetime_secs = token_resp.expires_in.unwrap_or(self.default_ttl.as_secs());\n>+\n>+        let access_token = AccessToken::new(token_resp.access_token);\n>+        let token = self.lifetime_config.create_token(\n>+            &access_token,\n>+            None::<&IdToken>,\n>+            DurationSecs(lifetime_secs),\n>+        );\n>+\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details >\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>The compliance rule requires explicit edge-case handling. The code directly converts <b><i>expires_in</i></b>\n>into <b><i>lifetime_secs</i></b> without guarding against <b><i>0</i></b>, enabling a zero-duration token lifetime and\n>potential refresh storms.\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>Rule 3: Generic: Robust Error Handling and Edge Case Management</code>\n> <code>[libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/source.rs[156-165]](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/blob/230e97719711844b492ea9e46842dcd2d2ba4119/libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/source.rs/#L156-L165)</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>```\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>## Issue description\n>A token response with `expires_in: 0` currently produces a zero lifetime (`DurationSecs(0)`), which can trigger hot refresh loops and excess load.\n>\n>## Issue Context\n>OAuth2 token endpoints can return unexpected/invalid values; this code should explicitly handle boundary cases for stability.\n>\n>## Fix Focus Areas\n>- libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/source.rs[156-165]\n>- libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/config.rs[61-79]\n>```\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>  3.  Boxed future not &#x27;static <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>✓ Correctness</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>• <b><i>BearerAuthService::call</i></b> returns a boxed *trait-object* future but boxes <b><i>inner.call(req)</i></b>\n>   directly, which generally requires <b><i>S::Future: &#x27;static</i></b> even though the impl only bounds `S::Future:\n>   Send`.\n>• This can fail to compile for valid <b><i>tower::Service</i></b> implementations whose <b><i>Future</i></b> borrows <b><i>self</i></b>,\n>   or silently over-constrain the layer to only work with <b><i>&#x27;static</i></b> futures.\n>• Repo precedent (<b><i>OtelService</i></b>, <b><i>AuthPolicyService</i></b>) avoids this by boxing an <b><i>async move</i></b> wrapper\n>   and awaiting the inner future inside it.\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/layer.rs[R79-107]](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/535/files#diff-a1efdd0441f4e2c1efc086f845a0e57bfaa25def37db44e8d6cb687a9e66d0ccR79-R107)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>+    type Future = Pin<Box<dyn Future<Output = Result<Response<ResBody>, HttpError>> + Send>>;\n>+\n>+    fn poll_ready(&mut self, cx: &mut Context<'_>) -> Poll<Result<(), Self::Error>> {\n>+        self.inner.poll_ready(cx)\n>+    }\n>+\n>+    fn call(&mut self, mut req: Request<B>) -> Self::Future {\n>+        let bearer_value = match self.token.get() {\n>+            Ok(secret) => {\n>+                let raw = format!(\"Bearer {}\", secret.expose());\n>+                match HeaderValue::from_str(&raw) {\n>+                    Ok(v) => v,\n>+                    Err(e) => return Box::pin(async { Err(HttpError::InvalidHeaderValue(e)) }),\n>+                }\n>+            }\n>+            Err(e) => {\n>+                return Box::pin(async { Err(HttpError::Transport(Box::new(e))) });\n>+            }\n>+        };\n>+\n>+        req.headers_mut()\n>+            .insert(self.header_name.clone(), bearer_value);\n>+\n>+        // Clone-swap pattern (Tower Service contract).\n>+        let clone = self.inner.clone();\n>+        let mut inner = std::mem::replace(&mut self.inner, clone);\n>+\n>+        Box::pin(inner.call(req))\n>+    }\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details >\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n><b><i>BearerAuthService</i></b> defines a boxed trait-object future type but returns <b><i>Box::pin(inner.call(req))</i></b>\n>directly. In contrast, other services in this repo that return <b><i>Pin&lt;Box&lt;dyn Future...&gt;&gt;</i></b> wrap the\n>inner call in <b><i>async move { ... await ... }</i></b>, which avoids needing the inner future to be <b><i>&#x27;static</i></b>.\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>[libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/layer.rs[67-107]](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/blob/230e97719711844b492ea9e46842dcd2d2ba4119/libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/layer.rs/#L67-L107)</code>\n> <code>[libs/modkit-http/src/layers/otel.rs[43-107]](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/blob/230e97719711844b492ea9e46842dcd2d2ba4119/libs/modkit-http/src/layers/otel.rs/#L43-L107)</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>````\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>### Issue description\n>`BearerAuthService` returns `Pin&lt;Box&lt;dyn Future + Send&gt;&gt;` but currently does `Box::pin(inner.call(req))`, which generally requires the inner future to be `&#x27;static`. The impl bounds only require `S::Future: Send`, so this can break compilation or unnecessarily restrict what services can be wrapped.\n>\n>### Issue Context\n>Other tower layers in this repo that box futures use `Box::pin(async move { ... inner.call(req).await ... })` to avoid `&#x27;static` requirements on `S::Future`.\n>\n>### Fix Focus Areas\n>- libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/layer.rs[67-107]\n>\n>### Suggested change (sketch)\n>In `call()`:\n>- keep the header construction logic as-is\n>- after clone-swap, return:\n>```rust\n>Box::pin(async move { inner.call(req).await })\n>```\n>This should remove any implicit `&#x27;static` requirement on `S::Future` while preserving the tower contract pattern.\n>````\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n<br/>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/review-recommended.png\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Remediation recommended\">\n\n<details>\n<summary>  4.  Backoff overflow panic <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>⛯ Reliability</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>• <b><i>spawn_watcher</i></b> computes <b><i>config.min_refresh_period * 30</i></b>; <b><i>Duration</i></b> multiplication can overflow\n>   and panic for extreme values.\n>• <b><i>OAuthClientConfig::validate</i></b> currently validates only endpoint selection, so a bad/untrusted\n>   config can crash the process during <b><i>Token::new()</i></b>.\n>• Defensive validation (or <b><i>checked_mul</i></b>) would turn this into a recoverable\n>   <b><i>TokenError::ConfigError</i></b>.\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/token.rs[R145-154]](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/535/files#diff-7c72c399351f6ef2f2b293e40d1e7c2fbad231545e1cf4c4c545a0e862c94e10R145-R154)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>+async fn spawn_watcher(\n>+    source: OAuthTokenSource,\n>+    config: &WatcherConfig,\n>+) -> Result<TokenWatcher, TokenError> {\n>+    let jitter = RandomEarlyJitter::new(DurationSecs(config.jitter_max.as_secs()));\n>+    let backoff =\n>+        ErrorBackoffConfig::new(config.min_refresh_period, config.min_refresh_period * 30, 2);\n>+\n>+    TokenWatcher::spawn_from_token_source(source, jitter, backoff).await\n>+}\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details >\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>The backoff max duration is derived via unchecked <b><i>Duration</i></b> multiplication, and the public config\n>validation does not constrain that value, so invalid configuration can reach this code path.\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>[libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/token.rs[144-154]](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/blob/230e97719711844b492ea9e46842dcd2d2ba4119/libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/token.rs/#L144-L154)</code>\n> <code>[libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/config.rs[61-79]](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/blob/230e97719711844b492ea9e46842dcd2d2ba4119/libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/config.rs/#L61-L79)</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>```\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>### Issue description\n>`spawn_watcher()` uses `config.min_refresh_period * 30` when constructing the backoff configuration. `Duration` multiplication can overflow and panic for extremely large durations.\n>\n>### Issue Context\n>`OAuthClientConfig::validate()` currently only checks the mutual exclusivity of `token_endpoint` vs `issuer_url`. It does not validate duration ranges, so a malformed config can reach `spawn_watcher()`.\n>\n>### Fix Focus Areas\n>- libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/token.rs[144-154]\n>- libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/config.rs[61-79]\n>\n>### Suggested fix\n>Option A (best): validate in `OAuthClientConfig::validate()`:\n>- compute `self.min_refresh_period.checked_mul(30)` and return `TokenError::ConfigError(...)` on `None`\n>\n>Option B: make `spawn_watcher()` use checked math:\n>- replace `config.min_refresh_period * 30` with `config.min_refresh_period.checked_mul(30).ok_or_else(|| TokenError::ConfigError(&quot;min_refresh_period too large&quot;.into()))?`\n>\n>Consider adding similar defensive checks anywhere else you do duration arithmetic.\n>```\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n<pre>ⓘ The new review experience is currently in Beta. <a href=\"https://docs.qodo.ai/qodo-documentation/code-review\">Learn more</a></pre>\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n\n<!-- https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/commit/230e97719711844b492ea9e46842dcd2d2ba4119 -->\n\n<a href=\"https://www.qodo.ai\"><img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/qodo-logo.svg\" width=\"80\" alt=\"Qodo Logo\"></a>","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3874594996/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":484649,"client_id":"Iv1.8b06d3cf5deea057","slug":"qodo-code-review","node_id":"A_kwHOCuzIt84AB2Up","owner":{"login":"qodo-ai","id":183290039,"node_id":"O_kgDOCuzItw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/183290039?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai","html_url":"https://github.com/qodo-ai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Qodo Code Review","description":"### The AI Code Review Platform\r\n\r\n## Get Started\r\nSimply sign into Github and click the \"Configure\" button. Check out our documentation for more info: https://docs.qodo.ai/get-started.\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\nQodo automatically reviews every GitHub pull request, identifies logic bugs, edge cases, security issues, and code quality problems, and provides actionable suggestions your team can apply immediately.\r\n\r\nInstall in minutes. Integrates seamlessly into your existing workflows.\r\n\r\n## Qodo is designed for developers who:\r\n- Handle frequent pull requests and need reliable review coverage\r\n- Balance code quality with fast delivery\r\n- Work in complex, multi-repo systems\r\n- Use AI-generated code and need stronger guardrails\r\n- Build production software where reliability matters\r\n\r\n## Qodo Capabilities\r\n- ## Automated PR Analysis\r\n  - Reviews every pull request automatically\r\n  - No manual trigger required\r\n\r\n- ## Context-Aware Code Review\r\n  - Understands cross-file changes\r\n  - Detects architectural inconsistencies\r\n\r\n- ## Actionable Suggestions\r\n  - Concrete code fixes\r\n  - Clear explanations\r\n  - Prioritized feedback\r\n\r\n- ## Security & Reliability Checks\r\n  - Identifies risky patterns\r\n  - Reduces attack surface area","external_url":"https://www.qodo.ai/","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","created_at":"2023-11-16T16:18:38Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T15:53:40Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"read","contents":"write","discussions":"write","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","discussion_comment","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review_comment","push"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3876279260","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/535#issuecomment-3876279260","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/535","id":3876279260,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7nC1Pc","user":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-10T09:01:02Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T09:01:02Z","body":"There are unresolved review comments awaiting response.\n\nUnanswered human review threads: 4\nUnresolved comments: 4","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3876279260/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":15368,"client_id":"Iv1.05c79e9ad1f6bdfa","slug":"github-actions","node_id":"MDM6QXBwMTUzNjg=","owner":{"login":"github","id":9919,"node_id":"MD