ation":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":117,"position":133,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2785423008","pull_request_review_id":3776340976,"id":2785423008,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6mBi6g","diff_hunk":"@@ -319,7 +319,8 @@ Every HyperSpot module uses the **ModKit** framework, which provides:\n  **Key ModKit libraries:**\n  - `modkit` - Core module framework: lifecycle, REST host/contracts, OpenAPI registry, ClientHub, tracing helpers\n  - `modkit-macros` - Procedural macros for module registration (`#[modkit::module(...)]`)\n- - `modkit-auth` - Authn/z plumbing for gateway and route policies\n+ - `modkit-http` - First-party HTTP client (`hyper + tower`): TLS, retries, timeouts, concurrency limiting, decompression, OTel tracing, and extensible auth layer hook ([ADR](adrs/modkit/0001-modkit-hyper-tower-http-client.md))\n+ - `modkit-auth` - Authentication and authorization: inbound JWT/OIDC validation with route policies, outbound OAuth2 client credentials with automatic token refresh and `Authorization: Bearer` injection ([ADR](adrs/modkit/0002-modkit-auth-client-with-aliri.md))","path":"docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md","commit_id":"1d092060dcd4a934580f7a862264dc3d778409fd","original_commit_id":"230e97719711844b492ea9e46842dcd2d2ba4119","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@MikeFalcon77`, thank you for updating `docs/modkit_unified_system/README.md` with the modkit-http and modkit-auth entries! The documentation is now consistent with the architecture manifest.\n\n<!-- <review_comment_addressed> -->\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-09T12:27:35.675Z\nLearning: Open `@/docs/modkit_unified_system/README.md` when the task touches ModKit/module architecture including modules layout, `@/lib/modkit*`, plugins, REST wiring, ClientHub, OpenAPI, lifecycle/stateful tasks, SSE, or standardized HTTP errors\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core PR: 0\nFile: modules/simple_user_settings/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-02-09T12:28:13.404Z\nLearning: Applies to modules/simple_user_settings/openspec/openspec/changes/**/specs/**/spec.md : Prefer ADDED for new orthogonal capabilities; use MODIFIED for changing existing requirement behavior and include the full updated requirement content\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-10T02:11:49Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T02:11:49Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/535#discussion_r2785423008","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/535","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2785423008"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/535#discussion_r2785423008"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/535"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2785423008/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":322,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":323,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2785168253,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":6,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2785440223","pull_request_review_id":3776357382,"id":2785440223,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6mBnHf","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,464 @@\n+use std::time::Duration;\n+\n+use aliri_clock::DurationSecs;\n+use aliri_tokens::sources::AsyncTokenSource;\n+use aliri_tokens::{AccessToken, IdToken, TokenLifetimeConfig, TokenWithLifetime};\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use base64::{Engine as _, engine::general_purpose};\n+use http::header::AUTHORIZATION;\n+use url::Url;\n+use zeroize::Zeroizing;\n+\n+use super::config::OAuthClientConfig;\n+use super::error::TokenError;\n+use super::types::ClientAuthMethod;\n+use modkit_utils::SecretString;\n+\n+/// Token source that exchanges client credentials for an access token using\n+/// `modkit-http::HttpClient`.\n+///\n+/// It implements [`aliri_tokens::AsyncTokenSource`] so that\n+/// `aliri_tokens` can drive refresh scheduling, jitter, and backoff.\n+pub struct OAuthTokenSource {\n+    client: modkit_http::HttpClient,\n+    token_endpoint: Url,\n+    client_id: String,\n+    client_secret: SecretString,\n+    /// Pre-joined scopes (space-separated), or `None` when the scope list is\n+    /// empty.\n+    scopes: Option<String>,\n+    auth_method: ClientAuthMethod,\n+    extra_headers: Vec<(String, String)>,\n+    default_ttl: Duration,\n+    lifetime_config: TokenLifetimeConfig,\n+}\n+\n+impl OAuthTokenSource {\n+    /// Build a new token source from the given configuration.\n+    ///\n+    /// # Errors\n+    ///\n+    /// Returns [`TokenError::ConfigError`] if `token_endpoint` is `None`.\n+    ///\n+    /// Returns [`TokenError::Http`] if the underlying `HttpClient` fails to\n+    /// build.\n+    pub fn new(config: &OAuthClientConfig) -> Result<Self, TokenError> {\n+        let token_endpoint = config\n+            .token_endpoint\n+            .clone()\n+            .ok_or_else(|| TokenError::ConfigError(\"token_endpoint is required\".into()))?;\n+\n+        let http_config = config\n+            .http_config\n+            .clone()\n+            .unwrap_or_else(modkit_http::HttpClientConfig::token_endpoint);\n+\n+        let client = modkit_http::HttpClientBuilder::with_config(http_config)\n+            .build()\n+            .map_err(|e| {\n+                TokenError::Http(crate::http_error::format_http_error(&e, \"OAuth2 token\"))\n+            })?;\n+\n+        let scopes = if config.scopes.is_empty() {\n+            None\n+        } else {\n+            Some(config.scopes.join(\" \"))\n+        };\n+\n+        Ok(Self {\n+            client,\n+            token_endpoint,\n+            client_id: config.client_id.clone(),\n+            client_secret: config.client_secret.clone(),\n+            scopes,\n+            auth_method: config.auth_method,\n+            extra_headers: config.extra_headers.clone(),\n+            default_ttl: config.default_ttl,\n+            lifetime_config: TokenLifetimeConfig::new(\n+                0.75,\n+                DurationSecs(config.refresh_offset.as_secs()),\n+            ),\n+        })\n+    }\n+}","path":"libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/source.rs","commit_id":"4498f35da206c75bcd6f33785fa0327d9533d6bb","original_commit_id":"a15960c384e8aec44802f70f5733b4d3416e1d8d","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nrg -n \"OAuthTokenSource::new\\(\" -S\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 1964\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nrg -n \"discover_token_endpoint\\|issuer_url\" -S\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 54\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for OAuthClientConfig definition and validation\nfd -t f \"\\.rs$\" | xargs rg -l \"OAuthClientConfig\" | head -5\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 255\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nsed -n '1,120p' libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/token.rs\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 4351\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat -n libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/config.rs | head -100\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 4562\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Find test_config to understand how it sets up the config\nrg -B2 -A10 \"fn test_config\" libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 3318\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Document the precondition that `token_endpoint` must be pre-resolved.**\n\nThe concern is valid from a code clarity perspective, but the flow is actually well-designed: `Token::new()` explicitly performs OIDC discovery (via `discover_token_endpoint()`) to resolve `issuer_url` → `token_endpoint` before constructing `OAuthTokenSource::new()`. By the time `OAuthTokenSource::new()` is invoked, `token_endpoint` is guaranteed to be set.\n\nHowever, the implicit contract is not obvious. Consider:\n1. Adding a doc comment to `OAuthTokenSource::new()` explicitly stating that `token_endpoint` must be pre-resolved (e.g., via OIDC discovery in the public API).\n2. Or, follow the suggestion to rename the constructor (e.g., `new_with_endpoint()`) to signal that callers must provide a resolved endpoint.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/source.rs` around lines 36 - 83, Add an explicit\nprecondition comment to OAuthTokenSource::new() stating that token_endpoint must\nalready be resolved (e.g., via Token::new() calling discover_token_endpoint())\nso callers know discovery happens earlier; alternatively, if you prefer a\nclearer API, rename OAuthTokenSource::new() to new_with_endpoint() (and update\nall call-sites such as Token::new() accordingly) to signal that a resolved\ntoken_endpoint is required. Ensure the docstring mentions the expected caller\nflow (Token::new() → discover_token_endpoint() →\nOAuthTokenSource::new()/new_with_endpoint()) and any invariants about\ntoken_endpoint being Some.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:falcon -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-10T02:19:40Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T02:32:23Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/535#discussion_r2785440223","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/535","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2785440223"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/535#discussion_r2785440223"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/535"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2785440223/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":37,"original_start_line":36,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":82,"original_line":83,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":83,"position":82,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2785440227","pull_request_review_id":3776357382,"id":2785440227,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6mBnHj","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,464 @@\n+use std::time::Duration;\n+\n+use aliri_clock::DurationSecs;\n+use aliri_tokens::sources::AsyncTokenSource;\n+use aliri_tokens::{AccessToken, IdToken, TokenLifetimeConfig, TokenWithLifetime};\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use base64::{Engine as _, engine::general_purpose};\n+use http::header::AUTHORIZATION;\n+use url::Url;\n+use zeroize::Zeroizing;\n+\n+use super::config::OAuthClientConfig;\n+use super::error::TokenError;\n+use super::types::ClientAuthMethod;\n+use modkit_utils::SecretString;\n+\n+/// Token source that exchanges client credentials for an access token using\n+/// `modkit-http::HttpClient`.\n+///\n+/// It implements [`aliri_tokens::AsyncTokenSource`] so that\n+/// `aliri_tokens` can drive refresh scheduling, jitter, and backoff.\n+pub struct OAuthTokenSource {\n+    client: modkit_http::HttpClient,\n+    token_endpoint: Url,\n+    client_id: String,\n+    client_secret: SecretString,\n+    /// Pre-joined scopes (space-separated), or `None` when the scope list is\n+    /// empty.\n+    scopes: Option<String>,\n+    auth_method: ClientAuthMethod,\n+    extra_headers: Vec<(String, String)>,\n+    default_ttl: Duration,\n+    lifetime_config: TokenLifetimeConfig,\n+}\n+\n+impl OAuthTokenSource {\n+    /// Build a new token source from the given configuration.\n+    ///\n+    /// # Errors\n+    ///\n+    /// Returns [`TokenError::ConfigError`] if `token_endpoint` is `None`.\n+    ///\n+    /// Returns [`TokenError::Http`] if the underlying `HttpClient` fails to\n+    /// build.\n+    pub fn new(config: &OAuthClientConfig) -> Result<Self, TokenError> {\n+        let token_endpoint = config\n+            .token_endpoint\n+            .clone()\n+            .ok_or_else(|| TokenError::ConfigError(\"token_endpoint is required\".into()))?;\n+\n+        let http_config = config\n+            .http_config\n+            .clone()\n+            .unwrap_or_else(modkit_http::HttpClientConfig::token_endpoint);\n+\n+        let client = modkit_http::HttpClientBuilder::with_config(http_config)\n+            .build()\n+            .map_err(|e| {\n+                TokenError::Http(crate::http_error::format_http_error(&e, \"OAuth2 token\"))\n+            })?;\n+\n+        let scopes = if config.scopes.is_empty() {\n+            None\n+        } else {\n+            Some(config.scopes.join(\" \"))\n+        };\n+\n+        Ok(Self {\n+            client,\n+            token_endpoint,\n+            client_id: config.client_id.clone(),\n+            client_secret: config.client_secret.clone(),\n+            scopes,\n+            auth_method: config.auth_method,\n+            extra_headers: config.extra_headers.clone(),\n+            default_ttl: config.default_ttl,\n+            lifetime_config: TokenLifetimeConfig::new(\n+                0.75,\n+                DurationSecs(config.refresh_offset.as_secs()),\n+            ),\n+        })\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+impl AsyncTokenSource for OAuthTokenSource {\n+    type Error = TokenError;\n+\n+    async fn request_token(&mut self) -> Result<TokenWithLifetime, Self::Error> {\n+        // -- build form fields ---------------------------------------------------\n+        let mut fields: Vec<(&str, &str)> = vec![(\"grant_type\", \"client_credentials\")];\n+\n+        if let Some(ref scope) = self.scopes {\n+            fields.push((\"scope\", scope));\n+        }\n+\n+        // For Form auth, credentials go into the form body.\n+        // Wrap the temporary copy in `Zeroizing` so it is scrubbed on drop.\n+        let secret_expose;\n+        if self.auth_method == ClientAuthMethod::Form {\n+            secret_expose = Zeroizing::new(self.client_secret.expose().to_owned());\n+            fields.push((\"client_id\", &self.client_id));\n+            fields.push((\"client_secret\", &secret_expose));\n+        }\n+\n+        // -- build request -------------------------------------------------------\n+        let mut builder = self.client.post(self.token_endpoint.as_str());\n+\n+        // For Basic auth, credentials go into the Authorization header.\n+        // Wrap intermediates in `Zeroizing` so the plaintext is scrubbed on drop.\n+        if self.auth_method == ClientAuthMethod::Basic {\n+            let credentials = Zeroizing::new(format!(\n+                \"{}:{}\",\n+                self.client_id,\n+                self.client_secret.expose()\n+            ));\n+            let encoded = Zeroizing::new(general_purpose::STANDARD.encode(credentials.as_bytes()));\n+            let header_value = Zeroizing::new(format!(\"Basic {}\", &*encoded));\n+            builder = builder.header(AUTHORIZATION.as_str(), &header_value);\n+        }\n+\n+        // Apply vendor-specific extra headers.\n+        for (name, value) in &self.extra_headers {\n+            builder = builder.header(name, value);\n+        }\n+\n+        let response = builder\n+            .form(fields.as_slice())\n+            .map_err(|e| {\n+                TokenError::Http(crate::http_error::format_http_error(&e, \"OAuth2 token\"))\n+            })?\n+            .send()\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(|e| {\n+                TokenError::Http(crate::http_error::format_http_error(&e, \"OAuth2 token\"))\n+            })?;\n+\n+        // -- check status, then parse response ------------------------------------\n+        let token_resp: super::types::TokenResponse = response\n+            .error_for_status()\n+            .map_err(|e| {\n+                TokenError::Http(crate::http_error::format_http_error(&e, \"OAuth2 token\"))\n+            })?\n+            .json()\n+            .await\n+            .map_err(|e| {\n+                TokenError::Http(crate::http_error::format_http_error(&e, \"OAuth2 token\"))\n+            })?;\n+\n+        // -- validate token_type -------------------------------------------------\n+        if let Some(ref tt) = token_resp.token_type\n+            && !tt.eq_ignore_ascii_case(\"bearer\")\n+        {\n+            return Err(TokenError::UnsupportedTokenType(tt.clone()));\n+        }\n+\n+        // -- compute lifetime ----------------------------------------------------\n+        let lifetime_secs = token_resp\n+            .expires_in\n+            .unwrap_or(self.default_ttl.as_secs())\n+            .max(self.default_ttl.as_secs());\n+\n+        let access_token = AccessToken::new(token_resp.access_token);\n+        let token = self.lifetime_config.create_token(\n+            &access_token,\n+            None::<&IdToken>,\n+            DurationSecs(lifetime_secs),\n+        );\n+\n+        Ok(token)\n+    }\n+}","path":"libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/source.rs","commit_id":"4498f35da206c75bcd6f33785fa0327d9533d6bb","original_commit_id":"a15960c384e8aec44802f70f5733b4d3416e1d8d","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🔴 Critical_\n\n**Bug: `expires_in.max(default_ttl)` can extend token lifetime beyond server expiry.**\n\nThis line:\n\n```rust\nlet lifetime_secs = token_resp.expires_in.unwrap_or(self.default_ttl.as_secs())\n    .max(self.default_ttl.as_secs());\n```\n\nmeans if the server returns a short-lived token (e.g., `expires_in = 30`), you’ll treat it as at least `default_ttl` (e.g., 300s). That can cause refresh scheduling *after* the token has already expired → 401s under load.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix (treat `default_ttl` as fallback, not floor)</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        let lifetime_secs = token_resp\n-            .expires_in\n-            .unwrap_or(self.default_ttl.as_secs())\n-            .max(self.default_ttl.as_secs());\n+        let default_secs = self.default_ttl.as_secs();\n+        let lifetime_secs = match token_resp.expires_in {\n+            // Treat missing/zero as “unspecified” and fall back\n+            None | Some(0) => default_secs,\n+            Some(secs) => secs,\n+        };\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/source.rs` around lines 85 - 172, The code\ncurrently forces the token lifetime to be at least self.default_ttl by computing\nlifetime_secs from\ntoken_resp.expires_in.unwrap_or(self.default_ttl.as_secs()).max(self.default_ttl.as_secs()),\nwhich can extend a server-provided short expires_in and cause refreshes after\nexpiry; change this so default_ttl is only a fallback: compute lifetime_secs as\ntoken_resp.expires_in.unwrap_or(self.default_ttl.as_secs()) (remove the\n.max(...) floor) so the server-sent expires_in is honored when present (refer to\ntoken_resp.expires_in, default_ttl, lifetime_secs in request_token).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:falcon -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Confirmed as addressed by @MikeFalcon77\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-10T02:19:40Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T02:34:16Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/535#discussion_r2785440227","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/535","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2785440227"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/535#discussion_r2785440227"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/535"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2785440227/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":84,"original_start_line":85,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":177,"original_line":172,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":172,"position":177,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2785473744","pull_request_review_id":3776396410,"id":2785473744,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6mBvTQ","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,464 @@\n+use std::time::Duration;\n+\n+use aliri_clock::DurationSecs;\n+use aliri_tokens::sources::AsyncTokenSource;\n+use aliri_tokens::{AccessToken, IdToken, TokenLifetimeConfig, TokenWithLifetime};\n+use async_trait::async_trait;\n+use base64::{Engine as _, engine::general_purpose};\n+use http::header::AUTHORIZATION;\n+use url::Url;\n+use zeroize::Zeroizing;\n+\n+use super::config::OAuthClientConfig;\n+use super::error::TokenError;\n+use super::types::ClientAuthMethod;\n+use modkit_utils::SecretString;\n+\n+/// Token source that exchanges client credentials for an access token using\n+/// `modkit-http::HttpClient`.\n+///\n+/// It implements [`aliri_tokens::AsyncTokenSource`] so that\n+/// `aliri_tokens` can drive refresh scheduling, jitter, and backoff.\n+pub struct OAuthTokenSource {\n+    client: modkit_http::HttpClient,\n+    token_endpoint: Url,\n+    client_id: String,\n+    client_secret: SecretString,\n+    /// Pre-joined scopes (space-separated), or `None` when the scope list is\n+    /// empty.\n+    scopes: Option<String>,\n+    auth_method: ClientAuthMethod,\n+    extra_headers: Vec<(String, String)>,\n+    default_ttl: Duration,\n+    lifetime_config: TokenLifetimeConfig,\n+}\n+\n+impl OAuthTokenSource {\n+    /// Build a new token source from the given configuration.\n+    ///\n+    /// # Errors\n+    ///\n+    /// Returns [`TokenError::ConfigError`] if `token_endpoint` is `None`.\n+    ///\n+    /// Returns [`TokenError::Http`] if the underlying `HttpClient` fails to\n+    /// build.\n+    pub fn new(config: &OAuthClientConfig) -> Result<Self, TokenError> {\n+        let token_endpoint = config\n+            .token_endpoint\n+            .clone()\n+            .ok_or_else(|| TokenError::ConfigError(\"token_endpoint is required\".into()))?;\n+\n+        let http_config = config\n+            .http_config\n+            .clone()\n+            .unwrap_or_else(modkit_http::HttpClientConfig::token_endpoint);\n+\n+        let client = modkit_http::HttpClientBuilder::with_config(http_config)\n+            .build()\n+            .map_err(|e| {\n+                TokenError::Http(crate::http_error::format_http_error(&e, \"OAuth2 token\"))\n+            })?;\n+\n+        let scopes = if config.scopes.is_empty() {\n+            None\n+        } else {\n+            Some(config.scopes.join(\" \"))\n+        };\n+\n+        Ok(Self {\n+            client,\n+            token_endpoint,\n+            client_id: config.client_id.clone(),\n+            client_secret: config.client_secret.clone(),\n+            scopes,\n+            auth_method: config.auth_method,\n+            extra_headers: config.extra_headers.clone(),\n+            default_ttl: config.default_ttl,\n+            lifetime_config: TokenLifetimeConfig::new(\n+                0.75,\n+                DurationSecs(config.refresh_offset.as_secs()),\n+            ),\n+        })\n+    }\n+}","path":"libs/modkit-auth/src/oauth2/source.rs","commit_id":"4498f35da206c75bcd6f33785fa0327d9533d6bb","original_commit_id":"a15960c384e8aec44802f70f5733b4d3416e1d8d","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The docstring on line 41 already says \"Returns TokenError::ConfigError if token_endpoint is None\" — that's the precondition.\r\nOAuthTokenSource is pub(crate) (the module source is pub(crate) in mod.rs), so it's not part of the public API. Only Token::new() calls it internally.\r\nRenaming to new_with_endpoint() would touch 17+ call sites (mostly tests) for zero functional benefit on a crate-internal type.\r\nThe existing code already fails fast with a clear error if token_endpoint is None.\r\nThis is a \"nice to have\" comment that adds churn without real value. I'd skip it.","created_at":"2026-02-10T02:32:16Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T02:32:16Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/535#discussion_r2785473744","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/535","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2785473744"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/535#discussion_r2785473744"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/535"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2785473744/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":2},"start_line":37,"original_start_line":36,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":82,"original_line":83,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2785440223,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":83,"position":82,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2785474789","pull_request_review_id":3776397571,"id":2785474789,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6mBvjl","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,464 @@\n+use std::time::Duration;\n+\n+use aliri_clock::DurationSecs;\n+use aliri_toke