om/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-09T13:08:54Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T13:08:54Z","body":"<h3>Review Summary by Qodo</h3>\n\nRename HyperSpot to Cyber Fabric and add MFA open question\n\n<code>📝 Documentation</code>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n<h3>Walkthroughs</h3>\n\n<details open>\n<summary>Description</summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n<pre>\n• Rename all &quot;HyperSpot&quot; references to &quot;Cyber Fabric&quot; across authorization architecture\n  documentation\n• Add open question #10 on Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) support with detailed sub-questions\n• Cover MFA handling across AuthN and AuthZ layers, including OIDC claims, step-up authentication,\n  and policy-level MFA requirements\n</pre>\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Diagram</summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n>\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  A[\"Documentation Files\"] -->|Rename HyperSpot| B[\"Cyber Fabric References\"]\n  C[\"Open Questions Section\"] -->|Add Question 10| D[\"MFA Support Design\"]\n  D -->|AuthN Layer| E[\"OIDC acr/amr claims\"]\n  D -->|AuthZ Layer| F[\"MFA-aware policies\"]\n  D -->|Dynamic| G[\"Step-up authentication\"]\n```\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n<h3>File Changes</h3>\n\n<details>\n<summary>1. docs/arch/authorization/ADR/0001-pdp-pep-authorization-model.md\n <code>📝 Documentation</code> <code> +13/-13 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Rename HyperSpot to Cyber Fabric in PDP/PEP ADR\n><pre>\n>• Replaced all instances of &quot;HyperSpot&quot; with &quot;Cyber Fabric&quot; throughout the document\n>• Updated references in context, requirements, architecture descriptions, and decision drivers\n>• Maintained consistency across PDP/PEP model explanations and option evaluations\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/531/files#diff-7b69e94885f7873c77a70f1eb1c6e0a29e160a138a9f27ebc856698f2943fefe'> docs/arch/authorization/ADR/0001-pdp-pep-authorization-model.md\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>2. docs/arch/authorization/ADR/0002-split-authn-authz-resolvers.md\n <code>📝 Documentation</code> <code> +2/-2 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Rename HyperSpot to Cyber Fabric in resolver split ADR\n><pre>\n>• Replaced &quot;HyperSpot&quot; with &quot;Cyber Fabric&quot; in context statement and architectural question\n>• Updated references to resolver module design and integration concerns\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/531/files#diff-fbfd46fe2bc3d2ca0b1fd1a6db254948ebfea6a684366b97051660b3232eba0e'> docs/arch/authorization/ADR/0002-split-authn-authz-resolvers.md\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>3. docs/arch/authorization/ADR/0003-authn-resolver-minimalist-interface.md\n <code>📝 Documentation</code> <code> +1/-1 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Rename HyperSpot to Cyber Fabric in AuthN resolver ADR\n><pre>\n>• Updated &quot;HyperSpot&quot; to &quot;Cyber Fabric&quot; in vendor neutrality decision driver\n>• Maintained context around IdP integration and plugin flexibility\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/531/files#diff-c90563548c9bd2725a9444232e5d9a69c2f7483c3c29df6d3c94fefcd7ae4d5c'> docs/arch/authorization/ADR/0003-authn-resolver-minimalist-interface.md\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary><ins><strong>View more (4)</strong></ins></summary><br/>\n<details>\n<summary>4. docs/arch/authorization/AUTHN_JWT_OIDC_PLUGIN.md\n <code>📝 Documentation</code> <code> +4/-4 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Rename HyperSpot to Cyber Fabric in JWT/OIDC plugin documentation\n><pre>\n>• Replaced &quot;HyperSpot&quot; with &quot;Cyber Fabric&quot; in use case description and OpenID Connect integration\n>  sections\n>• Updated references to standard distribution, trust anchors, and discovery processes\n>• Maintained technical accuracy of JWT validation and OIDC workflows\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/531/files#diff-ce769ce178fe7b39aaa8d2552649238a3fdf2ed673d37ecb3a1f3f6d9b745944'> docs/arch/authorization/AUTHN_JWT_OIDC_PLUGIN.md\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>5. docs/arch/authorization/DESIGN.md\n <code>📝 Documentation</code> <code> +36/-21 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Rename HyperSpot to Cyber Fabric and add MFA open question\n><pre>\n>• Replaced all &quot;HyperSpot&quot; references with &quot;Cyber Fabric&quot; throughout the comprehensive design\n>  document\n>• Updated references in overview, architecture descriptions, gateway/plugin patterns, and constraint\n>  generation sections\n>• Added new open question #10 on Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) support with extensive\n>  sub-questions covering AuthN layer (OIDC acr/amr claims, NIST SP 800-63B AAL, step-up\n>  authentication, SecurityContext changes), AuthZ layer (MFA-aware policies, constraint-level MFA,\n>  dynamic step-up), and cross-cutting concerns (IdP transparency, industry practices, token scopes\n>  interaction)\n>• Maintained all technical content and architectural patterns while updating branding\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/531/files#diff-11905321862805e42f0ebec5a049a581dbd73e6e796761a8cacf71fbf664ef0f'> docs/arch/authorization/DESIGN.md\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>6. docs/arch/authorization/RESOURCE_GROUP_MODEL.md\n <code>📝 Documentation</code> <code> +6/-6 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Rename HyperSpot to Cyber Fabric in resource group model\n><pre>\n>• Replaced &quot;HyperSpot&quot; with &quot;Cyber Fabric&quot; in overview, group model descriptions, and vendor\n>  integration sections\n>• Updated references to resource group infrastructure, local projections, and RG Resolver plugin\n>• Maintained consistency with authorization and hierarchy concepts\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/531/files#diff-3d4d8801fbd75f9444310c5e7a4d59a9ef1f388308083d2cf429cdca943ace5b'> docs/arch/authorization/RESOURCE_GROUP_MODEL.md\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>7. docs/arch/authorization/TENANT_MODEL.md\n <code>📝 Documentation</code> <code> +3/-3 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Rename HyperSpot to Cyber Fabric in tenant model documentation\n><pre>\n>• Replaced &quot;HyperSpot&quot; with &quot;Cyber Fabric&quot; in title, overview, and multi-tenancy model descriptions\n>• Updated references to hierarchical tenancy, closure tables, and tenant scope parameters\n>• Maintained technical accuracy of tenant topology and isolation mechanisms\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/531/files#diff-e9befcff1774fa6acfc9519c9735f464bf2036cc743fd825de647e1b2d10aaca'> docs/arch/authorization/TENANT_MODEL.md\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n\n<a href=\"https://www.qodo.ai\"><img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/qodo-logo.svg\" width=\"80\" alt=\"Qodo Logo\"></a>","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3871609582/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":484649,"client_id":"Iv1.8b06d3cf5deea057","slug":"qodo-code-review","node_id":"A_kwHOCuzIt84AB2Up","owner":{"login":"qodo-ai","id":183290039,"node_id":"O_kgDOCuzItw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/183290039?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai","html_url":"https://github.com/qodo-ai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Qodo Code Review","description":"### The AI Code Review Platform\r\n\r\n## Get Started\r\nSimply sign into Github and click the \"Configure\" button. Check out our documentation for more info: https://docs.qodo.ai/get-started.\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\nQodo automatically reviews every GitHub pull request, identifies logic bugs, edge cases, security issues, and code quality problems, and provides actionable suggestions your team can apply immediately.\r\n\r\nInstall in minutes. Integrates seamlessly into your existing workflows.\r\n\r\n## Qodo is designed for developers who:\r\n- Handle frequent pull requests and need reliable review coverage\r\n- Balance code quality with fast delivery\r\n- Work in complex, multi-repo systems\r\n- Use AI-generated code and need stronger guardrails\r\n- Build production software where reliability matters\r\n\r\n## Qodo Capabilities\r\n- ## Automated PR Analysis\r\n  - Reviews every pull request automatically\r\n  - No manual trigger required\r\n\r\n- ## Context-Aware Code Review\r\n  - Understands cross-file changes\r\n  - Detects architectural inconsistencies\r\n\r\n- ## Actionable Suggestions\r\n  - Concrete code fixes\r\n  - Clear explanations\r\n  - Prioritized feedback\r\n\r\n- ## Security & Reliability Checks\r\n  - Identifies risky patterns\r\n  - Reduces attack surface area","external_url":"https://www.qodo.ai/","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","created_at":"2023-11-16T16:18:38Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T15:53:40Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"read","contents":"write","discussions":"write","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","discussion_comment","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review_comment","push"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3871624010","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/531#issuecomment-3871624010","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/531","id":3871624010,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7mxEtK","user":{"login":"qodo-code-review[bot]","id":151058649,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCQD42Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/484649?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-09T13:11:57Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T13:11:57Z","body":"<h3>Code Review by Qodo</h3>\n\n<code>🐞 Bugs (1)</code>  <code>📘 Rule violations (0)</code>  <code>📎 Requirement gaps (0)</code>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n<br/>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/review-recommended.png\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Remediation recommended\">\n\n<details>\n<summary>  1.  Mixed product naming <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>✓ Correctness</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>• This PR updates the authorization architecture docs to refer to the product as “Cyber Fabric”, but\n>   other top-level docs still refer to “HyperSpot”.\n>• This creates inconsistent terminology across the docs set, making it unclear whether “Cyber\n>   Fabric” is a rename, a component name, or a different product—hurting onboarding and architectural\n>   clarity.\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[docs/arch/authorization/DESIGN.md[25]](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/pull/531/files#diff-11905321862805e42f0ebec5a049a581dbd73e6e796761a8cacf71fbf664ef0fR25-R25)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>+This document describes Cyber Fabric's approach to authentication (AuthN) and authorization (AuthZ).\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details >\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>The updated authorization design docs now consistently use “Cyber Fabric”, while other prominent\n>docs in the same repo still say “HyperSpot”, demonstrating repo-wide naming inconsistency\n>introduced/continued by this PR.\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>[docs/arch/authorization/DESIGN.md[23-31]](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/blob/aadd4e24ad78bd6cb84a0bb1a112c323a82c2fb6/docs/arch/authorization/DESIGN.md/#L23-L31)</code>\n> <code>[README.md[1-6]](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/blob/aadd4e24ad78bd6cb84a0bb1a112c323a82c2fb6/README.md/#L1-L6)</code>\n> <code>[docs/QUICKSTART_GUIDE.md[1-4]](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/blob/aadd4e24ad78bd6cb84a0bb1a112c323a82c2fb6/docs/QUICKSTART_GUIDE.md/#L1-L4)</code>\n> <code>[docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md[1-8]](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/blob/aadd4e24ad78bd6cb84a0bb1a112c323a82c2fb6/docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md/#L1-L8)</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>```\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>## Issue description\n>Authorization docs were updated to refer to the product as **Cyber Fabric**, but other prominent repo docs still refer to **HyperSpot**. This mixed branding/terminology is confusing and makes the documentation set inconsistent.\n>\n>## Issue Context\n>The repository README already presents the project as “Cyber Fabric”, while multiple docs under `docs/` still start with “HyperSpot”. This PR continues the partial rename by updating only the authorization docs.\n>\n>## Fix Focus Areas\n>- docs/QUICKSTART_GUIDE.md[1-6]\n>- docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md[1-15]\n>- docs/arch/authorization/DESIGN.md[23-31]\n>- README.md[1-6]\n>\n>(Optionally) run a repo-wide search for `HyperSpot` and either replace with `Cyber Fabric` where appropriate, or add a short note in docs that intentionally keep the old name explaining the relationship/transition plan.\n>```\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n<pre>ⓘ The new review experience is currently in Beta. <a href=\"https://docs.qodo.ai/qodo-documentation/code-review\">Learn more</a></pre>\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n\n<!-- https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/commit/aadd4e24ad78bd6cb84a0bb1a112c323a82c2fb6 -->\n\n<a href=\"https://www.qodo.ai\"><img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/qodo-logo.svg\" width=\"80\" alt=\"Qodo Logo\"></a>","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3871624010/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":484649,"client_id":"Iv1.8b06d3cf5deea057","slug":"qodo-code-review","node_id":"A_kwHOCuzIt84AB2Up","owner":{"login":"qodo-ai","id":183290039,"node_id":"O_kgDOCuzItw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/183290039?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai","html_url":"https://github.com/qodo-ai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Qodo Code Review","description":"### The AI Code Review Platform\r\n\r\n## Get Started\r\nSimply sign into Github and click the \"Configure\" button. Check out our documentation for more info: https://docs.qodo.ai/get-started.\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\nQodo automatically reviews every GitHub pull request, identifies logic bugs, edge cases, security issues, and code quality problems, and provides actionable suggestions your team can apply immediately.\r\n\r\nInstall in minutes. Integrates seamlessly into your existing workflows.\r\n\r\n## Qodo is designed for developers who:\r\n- Handle frequent pull requests and need reliable review coverage\r\n- Balance code quality with fast delivery\r\n- Work in complex, multi-repo systems\r\n- Use AI-generated code and need stronger guardrails\r\n- Build production software where reliability matters\r\n\r\n## Qodo Capabilities\r\n- ## Automated PR Analysis\r\n  - Reviews every pull request automatically\r\n  - No manual trigger required\r\n\r\n- ## Context-Aware Code Review\r\n  - Understands cross-file changes\r\n  - Detects architectural inconsistencies\r\n\r\n- ## Actionable Suggestions\r\n  - Concrete code fixes\r\n  - Clear explanations\r\n  - Prioritized feedback\r\n\r\n- ## Security & Reliability Checks\r\n  - Identifies risky patterns\r\n  - Reduces attack surface area","external_url":"https://www.qodo.ai/","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","created_at":"2023-11-16T16:18:38Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T15:53:40Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"read","contents":"write","discussions":"write","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","discussion_comment","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review_comment","push"]}}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":527,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527","source_state":"closed","source_author":"striped-zebra-dev","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #527] OAGW design changes","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"OAGW-design-changes","pr_head_sha":"141f08c649b048bdf4b4c9e7add110efb09054c6","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"striped-zebra-dev","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527","id":3262232201,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPaLyBs7CcbaJ","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/527","number":527,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"OAGW design changes","user":{"login":"striped-zebra-dev","id":225538363,"node_id":"U_kgDODXFxOw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225538363?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/striped-zebra-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added custom header routing via X-OAGW-Target-Host for explicit endpoint selection in multi-endpoint upstreams\n  * Enabled disable/re-enable functionality for upstreams and routes\n  * Introduced plugin system supporting authentication, guarding, and request/response transformation\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Expanded architecture and deployment guidance documentation\n  * Added comprehensive request flow and management operation scenarios\n  * Enhanced error handling documentation with RFC 9457 Problem Details format\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-02-09T10:27:28Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T10:36:12Z","closed_at":"2026-02-11T10:36:12Z","merged_at":"2026-02-11T10:36:12Z","merge_commit_sha":"bbba7932ebb6ef6ea83c6f7af11160c3d6676799","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"binarycode","id":415262,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxNTI2Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/415262?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/binarycode","html_url":"https://github.com/binarycode","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/binarycode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/binarycode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/binarycode/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/binarycode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/binarycode/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/binarycode/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/binarycode/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/binarycode/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/binarycode/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},{"login":"mattgarmon","id":22921875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTIxODc1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22921875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattgarmon","html_url":"https://github.com/mattgarmon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattgarmon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattgarmon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattgarmon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattgarmon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattgarmon/subscriptions","org