om/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782689730","pull_request_review_id":3773354051,"id":2782689730,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6l3HnC","diff_hunk":"@@ -100,6 +101,23 @@ CRUD for upstream configurations. Each upstream defines: server endpoints, proto\n \n CRUD for routes. Routes define matching rules (method, path, query allowlist) mapping requests to upstreams.\n \n+### Enable/Disable Semantics\n+\n+Upstreams and routes support an `enabled` boolean field (default: `true`).\n+\n+**Behavior**:\n+- **Disabled upstream**: All proxy requests to this upstream rejected with gateway error\n+- **Disabled route**: Route excluded from matching; request falls through to next match or returns 404\n+\n+**Hierarchical Inheritance**:\n+- If ancestor tenant disables an upstream, it is disabled for all descendants\n+- Descendant cannot re-enable an ancestor-disabled resource\n+","path":"modules/system/oagw/PRD.md","commit_id":"141f08c649b048bdf4b4c9e7add110efb09054c6","original_commit_id":"01e0ad53b85847fcec0a7b350f97a06da9e5aa11","user":{"login":"striped-zebra-dev","id":225538363,"node_id":"U_kgDODXFxOw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225538363?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/striped-zebra-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Thx, fixed.","created_at":"2026-02-09T13:39:31Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T13:39:32Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2782689730","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782689730"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2782689730"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782689730/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":148,"original_start_line":104,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":159,"original_line":115,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2781860692,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":23,"position":199,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782715640","pull_request_review_id":3773384752,"id":2782715640,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6l3N74","diff_hunk":"@@ -152,6 +343,67 @@ Cache entry TTL: 1 hour. OAGW does not retry failed requests.\n \n HTTP/3 (QUIC) support is future work.\n \n+**HTTP/2 `:authority` Pseudo-Header and X-OAGW-Target-Host**:\n+\n+In HTTP/2, the `:authority` pseudo-header replaces the HTTP/1.1 `Host` header. OAGW's `X-OAGW-Target-Host` header behavior applies consistently across both protocols:\n+\n+- **HTTP/1.1**: `X-OAGW-Target-Host` is used for routing; standard `Host` header is replaced with upstream host\n+- **HTTP/2**: `X-OAGW-Target-Host` is used for routing; `:authority` pseudo-header is replaced with upstream authority\n+- **Header name**: `X-OAGW-Target-Host` is lowercased to `x-oagw-target-host` in HTTP/2 (per HTTP/2 specification)\n+- **Routing behavior**: Identical across HTTP/1.1 and HTTP/2 - custom header controls endpoint selection, standard authority mechanisms are replaced\n+\n+The `:authority` pseudo-header does NOT replace `X-OAGW-Target-Host` for routing purposes. Both headers serve different functions:\n+\n+- `:authority`: Standard HTTP/2 authority component (replaced by OAGW with upstream authority)\n+- `X-OAGW-Target-Host`: OAGW-specific routing control (consumed by OAGW, not forwarded)\n+\n+### Plugin System Overview\n+\n+OAGW provides a plugin system for extending request/response processing. Plugins are executed by Control Plane during proxy operations.\n+\n+**Plugin Types** (defined in `oagw-core`):\n+\n+1. **AuthPlugin** (`gts.x.core.oagw.plugin.auth.v1~*`)\n+    - Purpose: Inject authentication credentials into requests\n+    - Examples: API key, OAuth2, Bearer token, Basic auth\n+    - Execution: Once per request, before guards\n+\n+2. **GuardPlugin** (`gts.x.core.oagw.plugin.guard.v1~*`)\n+    - Purpose: Validate requests and enforce policies (can reject)\n+    - Examples: Timeout enforcement, CORS validation, rate limiting\n+    - Execution: After auth, before transform\n+\n+3. **TransformPlugin** (`gts.x.core.oagw.plugin.transform.v1~*`)\n+    - Purpose: Modify request/response/error data\n+    - Examples: Logging, metrics collection, request ID propagation\n+    - Execution: Before and after proxy call\n+\n+**Plugin Execution Order**:\n+\n+```\n+Incoming Request\n+  -> Auth Plugin (credential injection)\n+  -> Guard Plugins (validation, can reject)\n+  -> Transform Plugins (modify request)\n+  -> HTTP call to external service\n+  -> Transform Plugins (modify response)\n+  -> Return to client\n+```","path":"modules/system/oagw/DESIGN.md","commit_id":"141f08c649b048bdf4b4c9e7add110efb09054c6","original_commit_id":"484dbf65efad76bd5da70776fa1647ae1f526174","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Add language labels to fenced code blocks.**\n\nMarkdownlint flags fenced blocks without languages. Adding a language like `text` (or a specific language where applicable) will silence MD040 and improve readability.  \n\n<details>\n<summary>✍️ Example tweak</summary>\n\n```diff\n-```\n+```text\n Incoming Request\n   -> Auth Plugin (credential injection)\n   -> Guard Plugins (validation, can reject)\n   -> Transform Plugins (modify request)\n   -> HTTP call to external service\n   -> Transform Plugins (modify response)\n   -> Return to client\n ```\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n````\nIn `@modules/system/oagw/DESIGN.md` around lines 383 - 391, The fenced code block\nshowing the request flow in DESIGN.md lacks a language label and triggers MD040;\nedit the block containing the \"Incoming Request -> Auth Plugin ...\" flow and add\na language identifier (e.g., use ```text) to the opening fence so the block\nbecomes a labelled fenced code block, preserving the exact content and\nindentation of the \"Incoming Request\" sequence.\n````\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit d4f1c80","created_at":"2026-02-09T13:43:59Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T14:05:52Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2782715640","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782715640"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2782715640"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782715640/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":407,"original_start_line":383,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":415,"original_line":391,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":422,"position":557,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782715648","pull_request_review_id":3773384752,"id":2782715648,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6l3N8A","diff_hunk":"@@ -388,14 +643,53 @@ def resolve_upstream_by_alias(tenant_id, alias, req):\n     # Closest tenant wins for routing target\n     selected = matches[0]\n \n-    # Multiple endpoints with common suffix alias require Host header\n+    # Reject if upstream is disabled (distinct gateway error, not 404)\n+    if not selected.enabled:\n+        return ErrorResponse(\n+            status=503,\n+            type=\"gts.x.core.errors.err.v1~x.oagw.routing.upstream_disabled.v1\",\n+            detail=f\"Upstream '{selected.alias}' is disabled\",\n+            upstream_id=selected.id\n+        )\n+\n+    # Multiple endpoints with common suffix alias require X-OAGW-Target-Host header\n     if len(selected.endpoints) > 1:\n         has_common_suffix = any(\n             ep.host != alias and ep.host.endswith(\".\" + alias)\n             for ep in selected.endpoints\n         )\n-        if has_common_suffix and \"Host\" not in req.headers:\n-            return Response(status=400)  # Missing Host header\n+        if has_common_suffix and \"X-OAGW-Target-Host\" not in req.headers:\n+            return ErrorResponse(\n+                status=400,\n+                type=\"gts.x.core.errors.err.v1~x.oagw.routing.missing_target_host.v1\",\n+                detail=f\"X-OAGW-Target-Host header required. Valid hosts: {[ep.host for ep in selected.endpoints]}\"\n+            )","path":"modules/system/oagw/DESIGN.md","commit_id":"141f08c649b048bdf4b4c9e7add110efb09054c6","original_commit_id":"484dbf65efad76bd5da70776fa1647ae1f526174","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Tighten common‑suffix detection to avoid false positives.**\n\n`has_common_suffix` uses `any(...)`, which would require `X-OAGW-Target-Host` even if only one endpoint happens to end with the alias. Consider requiring *all* endpoints to share the suffix (or an explicit “alias derived from common suffix” flag) so explicit aliases don’t accidentally trigger the requirement.  \n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Suggested adjustment</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        has_common_suffix = any(\n+        has_common_suffix = all(\n             ep.host != alias and ep.host.endswith(\".\" + alias)\n             for ep in selected.endpoints\n         )\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n    # Multiple endpoints with common suffix alias require X-OAGW-Target-Host header\n    if len(selected.endpoints) > 1:\n        has_common_suffix = all(\n            ep.host != alias and ep.host.endswith(\".\" + alias)\n            for ep in selected.endpoints\n        )\n        if has_common_suffix and \"X-OAGW-Target-Host\" not in req.headers:\n            return ErrorResponse(\n                status=400,\n                type=\"gts.x.core.errors.err.v1~x.oagw.routing.missing_target_host.v1\",\n                detail=f\"X-OAGW-Target-Host header required. Valid hosts: {[ep.host for ep in selected.endpoints]}\"\n            )\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/oagw/DESIGN.md` around lines 655 - 666, The current detection\nuses has_common_suffix = any(...) which triggers when only a single endpoint\nends with the alias; change the logic to require that every endpoint in\nselected.endpoints shares the common-suffix (use all(...) semantics) so the\nX-OAGW-Target-Host header is only required when all endpoints are alias-derived;\nupdate the condition that computes has_common_suffix (referencing\nhas_common_suffix, selected.endpoints, alias) and leave the subsequent header\ncheck and ErrorResponse usage intact.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-09T13:44:00Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T13:54:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2782715648","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782715648"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2782715648"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782715648/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":679,"original_start_line":655,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":690,"original_line":666,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":515,"position":730,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782715670","pull_request_review_id":3773384752,"id":2782715670,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6l3N8W","diff_hunk":"@@ -83,43 +90,46 @@ Implement CORS as a guard plugin. Configurable per upstream/route.\n CORS as first-class feature in upstream/route configuration. Handled before plugin chain.\n \n **Configuration**:\n+\n ```json\n {\n   \"server\": {\n-    \"endpoints\": [{\"scheme\": \"https\", \"host\": \"api.service.com\", \"port\": 443}]\n+    \"endpoints\": [ { \"scheme\": \"https\", \"host\": \"api.service.com\", \"port\": 443 } ]\n   },\n   \"cors\": {\n     \"enabled\": true,\n-    \"allowed_origins\": [\"https://app.example.com\"],\n-    \"allowed_methods\": [\"GET\", \"POST\"],\n-    \"allowed_headers\": [\"Content-Type\", \"Authorization\"],\n-    \"expose_headers\": [\"X-Request-ID\"],\n+    \"allowed_origins\": [ \"https://app.example.com\" ],\n+    \"allowed_methods\": [ \"GET\", \"POST\" ],\n+    \"allowed_headers\": [ \"Content-Type\", \"Authorization\" ],\n+    \"expose_headers\": [ \"X-Request-ID\" ],\n     \"max_age\": 86400,\n     \"allow_credentials\": true\n   }\n }\n ```\n ","path":"modules/system/oagw/docs/adr-cors.md","commit_id":"141f08c649b048bdf4b4c9e7add110efb09054c6","original_commit_id":"484dbf65efad76bd5da70776fa1647ae1f526174","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Add language identifiers to fenced code blocks.**  \nmarkdownlint flags MD040 here; please add a language (e.g., `json`) to keep docs lint-clean.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n````\nIn `@modules/system/oagw/docs/adr-cors.md` around lines 94 - 110, The fenced code\nblock showing the JSON example that begins with { \"server\": { \"endpoints\": ... }\n} should include a language identifier; update the opening triple-backtick for\nthat block to ```json so the block is marked as JSON (this will satisfy\nmarkdownlint MD040). Locate the fenced block in adr-cors.md containing the CORS\nexample and add the `json` label immediately after the backticks.\n````\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit d4f1c80","created_at":"2026-02-09T13:44:00Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T14:05:51Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2782715670","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782715670"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2782715670"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782715670/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":94,"original_start_line":94,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":110,"original_line":110,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":91,"position":91,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782715674","pull_request_review_id":3773384752,"id":2782715674,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6l3N8a","diff_hunk":"@@ -83,43 +90,46 @@ Implement CORS as a guard plugin. Configurable per upstream/route.\n CORS as first-class feature in upstream/route configuration. Handled before plugin chain.\n \n **Configuration**:\n+\n ```json\n {\n   \"server\": {\n-    \"endpoints\": [{\"scheme\": \"https\", \"host\": \"api.service.com\", \"port\": 443}]\n+    \"endpoints\": [ { \"scheme\": \"https\", \"host\": \"api.service.com\", \"port\": 443 } ]\n   },\n   \"cors\": {\n     \"enabled\": true,\n-    \"allowed_origins\": [\"https://app.example.com\"],\n-    \"allowed_methods\": [\"GET\", \"POST\"],\n-    \"allowed_headers\": [\"Content-Type\", \"Authorization\"],\n-    \"expose_headers\": [\"X-Request-ID\"],\n+    \"allowed_origins\": [ \"https://app.example.com\" ],\n+    \"allowed_methods\": [ \"GET\", \"POST\" ],\n+    \"allowed_headers\": [ \"Content-Type\", \"Authorization\" ],\n+    \"expose_headers\": [ \"X-Request-ID\" ],\n     \"max_age\": 86400,\n     \"allow_credentials\": true\n   }\n }\n ```\n \n **Pros**:\n+\n - First-class feature (no plugin ordering issues)\n - Preflight handled before routing/auth/plugins (fast path)\n - Clear configuration model\n - Standards-compliant default behavior\n \n **Cons**:\n+\n - Adds built-in logic to OAGW core\n - Not extensible via plugins (but can be overridden)\n \n ## Comparison Matrix\n \n-| Criteria                  | Option 1 (Proxy) | Option 2 (Plugin) | Option 3 (Built-in) |\n-|---------------------------|:----------------:|:-----------------:|:-------------------:|\n-| Preflight latency         |       High       |        Low        |         Low         |\n-| Configuration complexity  |       None       |      Medium       |        Low          |\n-| Upstream independence     |        No        |        Yes        |         Yes         |\n-| Plugin ordering issues    |       N/A        |        Yes        |         No          |\n-| Standards compliance      |     Depends      |        Yes        |         Yes         |\n-| Works when upstream down  |        No        |        Yes        |         Yes         |\n+| Criteria                 | Option 1 (Proxy) | Option 2 (Plugin) | Option 3 (Built-in) |\n+|--------------------------|:----------------:|:-----------------:|:-------------------:|\n+| Preflight latency        |       High       |        Low        |         Low         |\n+| Configuration complexity |       None       |      Medium       |         Low         |\n+| Upstream independence    |        No        |        Yes        |         Yes         |\n+| Plugin ordering issues   |       N/A        |        Yes        |         No          |\n+| Standards compliance     |     Depends      |        Yes        |         Yes         |\n+| Works when upstream down |        No        |        Yes        |         Yes         |\n ","path":"modules/system/oagw/docs/adr-cors.md","commit_id":"141f08c649b048bdf4b4c9e7add110efb09054c6","original_commit_id":"484dbf65efad76bd5da70776fa1647ae1f526174","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Add language identifiers to fenced code blocks.**  \nmarkdownlint flags MD040 here; please add a language (e.g., `markdown` or omit table fence if not needed).\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Tools</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 markdownlint-cli2 (0.20.0)</summary>\n\n[warning] 112-112: Fenced code blocks should have a language specified\n\n(MD040, fenced-code-language)\n\n---\n\n[warning] 124-124: Fenced code blocks should have a language specified\n\n(MD040, fenced-code-language)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n````\nIn `@modules/system/oagw/docs/adr-cors.md` around lines 111 - 133, The MD040 lint\nerror means there are fenced code blocks without a language tag around the\ncontent near the \"## Comparison Matrix\" section (the table is likely wrapped in\ntriple backticks or other fenced blocks); fix by either removing the code fence\nso the table is plain Markdown, or add an explicit language identifier (e.g.,\n```markdown) to the opening fence for any fenced block in adr-cors.md (look for\nthe table under \"## Comparison Matrix\" and any other fenced snippets) so\nmarkdownlint MD040 is satisfied.\n````\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit d4f1c80","created_at":"2026-02-09T13:44:00Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T14:05:57Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2782715674","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782715674"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2782715674"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527"}},"reactions":{"url":