"484dbf65efad76bd5da70776fa1647ae1f526174","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@striped-zebra-dev` Thank you for the feedback. You're right that the placement needs reconsideration.\n\nCould you clarify where this validation should live? A few options I see based on the architecture:\n\n1. **Upstream creation/validation time** (Data Plane): Compute `has_common_suffix` as a property when the upstream is created/updated, store it in the config, and just check that flag at routing time?\n\n2. **Different component boundary**: Should the header validation happen in API Handler before calling CP, or stay in CP's alias resolution?\n\n3. **Earlier in the request flow**: Should this check happen as part of route matching rather than alias resolution?\n\nLooking at the component architecture, it seems like the \"common suffix\" characteristic should be determined once during upstream configuration (in the Data Plane) rather than computed on every request in the Control Plane's alias resolution path.\n\nWhat's your preferred approach?\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-09T13:54:39Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T13:54:39Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2782778780","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782778780"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2782778780"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782778780/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":679,"original_start_line":655,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":690,"original_line":666,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2782715648,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":515,"position":730,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782779323","pull_request_review_id":3773456368,"id":2782779323,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6l3de7","diff_hunk":"@@ -388,14 +643,53 @@ def resolve_upstream_by_alias(tenant_id, alias, req):\n     # Closest tenant wins for routing target\n     selected = matches[0]\n \n-    # Multiple endpoints with common suffix alias require Host header\n+    # Reject if upstream is disabled (distinct gateway error, not 404)\n+    if not selected.enabled:\n+        return ErrorResponse(\n+            status=503,\n+            type=\"gts.x.core.errors.err.v1~x.oagw.routing.upstream_disabled.v1\",\n+            detail=f\"Upstream '{selected.alias}' is disabled\",\n+            upstream_id=selected.id\n+        )\n+\n+    # Multiple endpoints with common suffix alias require X-OAGW-Target-Host header\n     if len(selected.endpoints) > 1:\n         has_common_suffix = any(\n             ep.host != alias and ep.host.endswith(\".\" + alias)\n             for ep in selected.endpoints\n         )\n-        if has_common_suffix and \"Host\" not in req.headers:\n-            return Response(status=400)  # Missing Host header\n+        if has_common_suffix and \"X-OAGW-Target-Host\" not in req.headers:\n+            return ErrorResponse(\n+                status=400,\n+                type=\"gts.x.core.errors.err.v1~x.oagw.routing.missing_target_host.v1\",\n+                detail=f\"X-OAGW-Target-Host header required. Valid hosts: {[ep.host for ep in selected.endpoints]}\"\n+            )","path":"modules/system/oagw/DESIGN.md","commit_id":"141f08c649b048bdf4b4c9e7add110efb09054c6","original_commit_id":"484dbf65efad76bd5da70776fa1647ae1f526174","user":{"login":"qodo-code-review[bot]","id":151058649,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCQD42Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/484649?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"### Question: \nwrong place for validation logic\n\n### Answer:\nIf you’re frequently getting suggestions that add/modify “validation logic” in places your architecture considers off-limits (e.g., design/spec files, routing layers, handlers), steer the `/improve` suggestions with repo-level instructions.\n\nAdd this to your `.pr_agent.toml` (or the repo wiki `.pr_agent.toml`) to reduce “wrong layer” recommendations and require the bot to justify placement:\n\n```toml\n[pr_code_suggestions]\nextra_instructions=\"\"\"\\\n- Treat architecture/layering as a hard constraint: do not suggest adding validation/authorization/business-rule enforcement in documentation/spec files, routing tables, or transport/adapters unless the PR explicitly changes that layer for this purpose.\n- If suggesting validation changes, always state *where* the logic should live (e.g., domain/service layer vs handler) and why.\n- Prefer minimal, localized fixes in the most appropriate existing module/layer; avoid moving responsibilities across layers without explicit PR intent.\n- If the “best fix” is architectural (moving validation elsewhere), suggest it as a non-committable high-level note rather than an inline patch.\n\"\"\"\n```\n\nIf the issue is specifically about suggestions touching `*.md` / design docs, you can also ignore those files entirely for suggestions:\n\n```toml\n[ignore]\nglob = [\"**/*.md\"]\n```\n\nIf you share which git provider you’re using (GitHub/GitLab/Bitbucket) and whether this is coming from `/improve` auto-feedback or a manual command, I can tailor the exact placement (wiki vs local vs global config) and patterns to ignore.\n\n#### Relevant Sources:\n\n> - https://docs.qodo.ai/qodo-documentation/qodo-merge/tools/improve#extra-instructions-and-best-practices\n> - https://docs.qodo.ai/qodo-documentation/qodo-merge/usage-guide/additional_configurations#extra-instructions\n> - https://docs.qodo.ai/qodo-documentation/qodo-merge/usage-guide/additional_configurations#ignoring-files-from-analysis\n> - https://docs.qodo.ai/qodo-documentation/qodo-merge/usage-guide/configuration_options#wiki-configuration-file\n","created_at":"2026-02-09T13:54:43Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T13:54:44Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2782779323","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782779323"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2782779323"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782779323/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":679,"original_start_line":655,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":690,"original_line":666,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2782715648,"author_association":"NONE","original_position":515,"position":730,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782780085","pull_request_review_id":3773457132,"id":2782780085,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6l3dq1","diff_hunk":"@@ -388,14 +643,53 @@ def resolve_upstream_by_alias(tenant_id, alias, req):\n     # Closest tenant wins for routing target\n     selected = matches[0]\n \n-    # Multiple endpoints with common suffix alias require Host header\n+    # Reject if upstream is disabled (distinct gateway error, not 404)\n+    if not selected.enabled:\n+        return ErrorResponse(\n+            status=503,\n+            type=\"gts.x.core.errors.err.v1~x.oagw.routing.upstream_disabled.v1\",\n+            detail=f\"Upstream '{selected.alias}' is disabled\",\n+            upstream_id=selected.id\n+        )\n+\n+    # Multiple endpoints with common suffix alias require X-OAGW-Target-Host header