p.host != alias and ep.host.endswith(\".\" + alias)\n             for ep in selected.endpoints\n         )\n-        if has_common_suffix and \"Host\" not in req.headers:\n-            return Response(status=400)  # Missing Host header\n+        if has_common_suffix and \"X-OAGW-Target-Host\" not in req.headers:\n+            return ErrorResponse(\n+                status=400,\n+                type=\"gts.x.core.errors.err.v1~x.oagw.routing.missing_target_host.v1\",\n+                detail=f\"X-OAGW-Target-Host header required. Valid hosts: {[ep.host for ep in selected.endpoints]}\"\n+            )\n+\n+    # Validate X-OAGW-Target-Host header if present (applies to both single and multi-endpoint)\n+    matched_endpoint = None\n+    if \"X-OAGW-Target-Host\" in req.headers:\n+        target_host = req.headers[\"X-OAGW-Target-Host\"]","path":"modules/system/oagw/DESIGN.md","commit_id":"141f08c649b048bdf4b4c9e7add110efb09054c6","original_commit_id":"59ec3ad08935366fc94a9dbd6274bddd9d00dd06","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Header lookup should be case‑insensitive.**\n\nThe pseudocode checks `\"X-OAGW-Target-Host\"` with exact casing. HTTP headers are case‑insensitive, so the lookup should normalize or use a case‑insensitive map to avoid false “missing header” errors.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/oagw/DESIGN.md` around lines 675 - 678, The header lookup for\n\"X-OAGW-Target-Host\" is case-sensitive; update the check around matched_endpoint\nand req.headers so header names are normalized (e.g., lowercased) or use a\ncase-insensitive map/get to fetch the header value; specifically, when reading\ntarget_host from req.headers in the validation logic, perform a case-insensitive\nlookup for \"x-oagw-target-host\" (or normalize req.headers keys) so the code that\nsets target_host and later uses matched_endpoint works correctly regardless of\nheader casing.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commits cff4866 to 9f1410f","created_at":"2026-02-09T14:13:54Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T12:42:41Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2782878609","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782878609"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2782878609"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782878609/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":692,"original_start_line":675,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":695,"original_line":678,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":399,"position":735,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782878611","pull_request_review_id":3773555657,"id":2782878611,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6l31uT","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,146 @@\n+# ADR: Data Plane Caching Strategy\n+\n+- **Status**: Accepted\n+- **Date**: 2026-02-09\n+- **Deciders**: OAGW Team\n+\n+## Context\n+\n+Data Plane handles config resolution for Control Plane during proxy requests. Configuration data (upstreams, routes, plugins) is read-heavy and changes infrequently. We need a\n+caching strategy that:\n+\n+- Minimizes database load\n+- Provides fast lookups (<1ms for hot configs)\n+- Supports both single-exec and microservice modes\n+- Handles cache invalidation on config writes\n+\n+## Decision\n+\n+**Multi-layer caching**: L1 (in-memory) + optional L2 (Redis) + Database\n+\n+### Cache Layers\n+\n+**L1 Cache (In-Memory)**:\n+\n+- Per-instance LRU cache\n+- Max 10,000 entries\n+- No TTL (evicted by LRU)\n+- Access time: <1μs\n+\n+**L2 Cache (Redis, Optional)**:\n+\n+- Shared across DP instances (microservice mode)\n+- TTL: 5 minutes\n+- Serialization: MessagePack\n+- Access time: ~1-2ms\n+\n+**Database (Source of Truth)**:\n+\n+- PostgreSQL with JSONB support\n+- Queried only on L1+L2 miss\n+- Access time: ~5-10ms\n+\n+### Lookup Flow\n+\n+```rust\n+async fn get_config(key: &CacheKey) -> Result<ConfigValue> {\n+    // Check L1\n+    if let Some(value) = l1_cache.get(key) {\n+        return Ok(value);  // <1μs\n+    }\n+\n+    // Check L2 (if enabled)\n+    if let Some(redis) = l2_cache {\n+        if let Some(value) = redis.get(key).await? {\n+            l1_cache.insert(key, value.clone());\n+            return Ok(value);  // ~1-2ms\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    // Query DB\n+    let value = db.query(key).await?;  // ~5-10ms\n+\n+    // Populate caches\n+    l1_cache.insert(key, value.clone());\n+    if let Some(redis) = l2_cache {\n+        redis.set(key, &value, TTL_5MIN).await?;\n+    }\n+\n+    Ok(value)\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Cache Keys\n+\n+- `upstream:{tenant_id}:{alias}` → UpstreamConfig\n+- `route:{upstream_id}:{method}:{path}` → RouteConfig\n+- `plugin:{plugin_id}` → Plugin definition","path":"modules/system/oagw/docs/adr-data-plane-caching.md","commit_id":"141f08c649b048bdf4b4c9e7add110efb09054c6","original_commit_id":"59ec3ad08935366fc94a9dbd6274bddd9d00dd06","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Include tenant scoping in cache keys to avoid cross-tenant collisions.**\n\n`route:{upstream_id}:{method}:{path}` (and possibly `plugin:{plugin_id}`) looks tenant-agnostic. If IDs aren’t globally unique or if route matching is tenant‑scoped, this can cross‑pollute caches. Consider adding `{tenant_id}` or explicitly documenting global uniqueness.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Suggested doc tweak</summary>\n\n```diff\n-- `route:{upstream_id}:{method}:{path}` → RouteConfig\n-- `plugin:{plugin_id}` → Plugin definition\n+- `route:{tenant_id}:{upstream_id}:{method}:{path}` → RouteConfig\n+- `plugin:{tenant_id}:{plugin_id}` → Plugin definition (if tenant-scoped)\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/oagw/docs/adr-data-plane-caching.md` around lines 73 - 77, The\ncache key patterns for routes and plugins are tenant-agnostic and risk\ncross-tenant collisions; update the keys so they include tenant scoping (e.g.,\nchange \"route:{upstream_id}:{method}:{path}\" to include \"{tenant_id}\" and\nsimilarly add \"{tenant_id}\" to \"plugin:{plugin_id}\"), or explicitly state that\nupstream_id and plugin_id are globally unique and immutable across tenants;\nensure the ADR text references the exact key patterns\n(\"upstream:{tenant_id}:{alias}\", \"route:{upstream_id}:{method}:{path}\",\n\"plugin:{plugin_id}\") and describes the chosen approach (add \"{tenant_id}\" to\nroute/plugin keys or document global uniqueness) so implementers know which\nvariant to use.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-09T14:13:54Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T14:13:56Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2782878611","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782878611"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2782878611"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782878611/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":73,"original_start_line":73,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":77,"original_line":77,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":77,"position":77,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782878616","pull_request_review_id":3773555657,"id":2782878616,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6l31uY","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,146 @@\n+# ADR: Data Plane Caching Strategy\n+\n+- **Status**: Accepted\n+- **Date**: 2026-02-09\n+- **Deciders**: OAGW Team\n+\n+## Context\n+\n+Data Plane handles config resolution for Control Plane during proxy requests. Configuration data (upstreams, routes, plugins) is read-heavy and changes infrequently. We need a\n+caching strategy that:\n+\n+- Minimizes database load\n+- Provides fast lookups (<1ms for hot configs)\n+- Supports both single-exec and microservice modes\n+- Handles cache invalidation on config writes\n+\n+## Decision\n+\n+**Multi-layer caching**: L1 (in-memory) + optional L2 (Redis) + Database\n+\n+### Cache Layers\n+\n+**L1 Cache (In-Memory)**:\n+\n+- Per-instance LRU cache\n+- Max 10,000 entries\n+- No TTL (evicted by LRU)\n+- Access time: <1μs\n+\n+**L2 Cache (Redis, Optional)**:\n+\n+- Shared across DP instances (microservice mode)\n+- TTL: 5 minutes\n+- Serialization: MessagePack\n+- Access time: ~1-2ms\n+\n+**Database (Source of Truth)**:\n+\n+- PostgreSQL with JSONB support\n+- Queried only on L1+L2 miss\n+- Access time: ~5-10ms\n+\n+### Lookup Flow\n+\n+```rust\n+async fn get_config(key: &CacheKey) -> Result<ConfigValue> {\n+    // Check L1\n+    if let Some(value) = l1_cache.get(key) {\n+        return Ok(value);  // <1μs\n+    }\n+\n+    // Check L2 (if enabled)\n+    if let Some(redis) = l2_cache {\n+        if let Some(value) = redis.get(key).await? {\n+            l1_cache.insert(key, value.clone());\n+            return Ok(value);  // ~1-2ms\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    // Query DB\n+    let value = db.query(key).await?;  // ~5-10ms\n+\n+    // Populate caches\n+    l1_cache.insert(key, value.clone());\n+    if let Some(redis) = l2_cache {\n+        redis.set(key, &value, TTL_5MIN).await?;\n+    }\n+\n+    Ok(value)\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Cache Keys\n+\n+- `upstream:{tenant_id}:{alias}` → UpstreamConfig\n+- `route:{upstream_id}:{method}:{path}` → RouteConfig\n+- `plugin:{plugin_id}` → Plugin definition\n+\n+### Cache Invalidation\n+\n+On config write (e.g., `PUT /upstreams/{id}`):\n+\n+1. DP writes to database\n+2. DP flushes L1 cache for affected keys\n+3. DP flushes L2 cache (if enabled) for affected keys\n+4. DP returns success\n+5. CP flushes its own L1 cache (notified by DP or periodic sync)\n+","path":"modules/system/oagw/docs/adr-data-plane-caching.md","commit_id":"141f08c649b048bdf4b4c9e7add110efb09054c6","original_commit_id":"59ec3ad08935366fc94a9dbd6274bddd9d00dd06","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Clarify that cache invalidation happens only after a successful DB commit.**\n\nThe flow currently implies cache flush immediately after the write. Please make it explicit that L1/L2 invalidation and CP notification occur only after the DB transaction is committed, to prevent cache misses/staleness on failed writes.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📌 Suggested clarification</summary>\n\n```diff\n-1. DP writes to database\n-2. DP flushes L1 cache for affected keys\n-3. DP flushes L2 cache (if enabled) for affected keys\n-4. DP returns success\n+1. DP writes to database (commit succeeds)\n+2. DP flushes L1 cache for affected keys\n+3. DP flushes L2 cache (if enabled) for affected keys\n+4. DP returns success\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/oagw/docs/adr-data-plane-caching.md` around lines 81 - 88,\nClarify the write flow to state that cache invalidation and CP notification\noccur only after a successful DB commit: update the sequence for \"On config\nwrite (e.g., PUT /upstreams/{id})\" to explicitly perform the DB write and commit\nfirst (DP writes to database and commits transaction), and only then flush DP L1\ncache, flush L2 cache (if enabled), return success, and notify CP (or let CP\npick up via periodic sync); mention that invalidation should not happen if the\nDB commit fails to avoid stale/incorrect cache state.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commits cff4866 to 16f2c0b","created_at":"2026-02-09T14:13:54Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T12:35:00Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2782878616","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782878616"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2782878616"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782878616/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":81,"original_start_line":81,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":88,"original_line":88,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":88,"position":88,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782878621","pull_request_review_id":3773555657,"id":2782878621,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6l31ud","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,198 @@\n+# ADR: Plugin System\n+\n+- **Status**: Accepted\n+- **Date**: 2026-02-09\n+- **Deciders**: OAGW Team\n+\n+## Context\n+\n+OAGW needs extensibility for request/response processing. Different use cases require different behaviors:\n+\n+- Authentication: API key, OAuth2, JWT, custom schemes\n+- Validation: Timeouts, CORS, rate limiting, custom rules\n+- Transformation: Logging, metrics, request ID, custom headers\n+\n+## Decision\n+\n+**Plugin system with three plugin types**, executed by Control Plane:\n+\n+### Plugin Types\n+\n+**1. AuthPlugin** (`gts.x.core.oagw.plugin.auth.v1~*`)\n+\n+- Purpose: Inject authentication credentials\n+- Execution: Once per request, before guards\n+- Examples: API key, OAuth2, Bearer token, Basic auth\n+\n+**2. GuardPlugin** (`gts.x.core.oagw.plugin.guard.v1~*`)\n+\n+- Purpose: Validate requests and enforce policies (can reject)\n+- Execution: After auth, before transform\n+- Examples: Timeout enforcement, CORS validation, rate limiting\n+\n+**3. TransformPlugin** (`gts.x.core.oagw.plugin.transform.v1~*`)\n+\n+- Purpose: Modify request/response/error data\n+- Execution: Before and after proxy call\n+- Examples: Logging, metrics collection, request ID propagation\n+\n+### Plugin Traits\n+\n+```rust\n+// oagw-sdk/src/plugins.rs\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait AuthPlugin: Send + Sync {\n+    fn id(&self) -> &str;\n+    fn plugin_type(&self) -> &str;\n+    async fn authenticate(&self, ctx: &mut RequestContext) -> Result<()>;\n+}\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait GuardPlugin: Send + Sync {\n+    fn id(&self) -> &str;\n+    fn plugin_type(&self) -> &str;\n+    async fn guard_request(&self, ctx: &RequestContext) -> Result<GuardDecision>;\n+    async fn guard_response(&self, ctx: &ResponseContext) -> Result<GuardDecision>;\n+}\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait TransformPlugin: Send + Sync {\n+    fn id(&self) -> &str;\n+    fn plugin_type(&self) -> &str;\n+    async fn transform_request(&self, ctx: &mut RequestContext) -> Result<()>;\n+    async fn transform_response(&self, ctx: &mut ResponseContext) -> Result<()>;\n+    async fn transform_error(&self, ctx: &mut ErrorContext) -> Result<()>;\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Plugin Execution Order\n+\n+```\n+Incoming Request\n+  → Auth Plugin (credential injection)\n+  → Guard Plugins (validation, can reject)\n+  → Transform Plugins (modify request)\n+  → HTTP call to external service\n+  → Transform Plugins (modify response)\n+  → Return to client\n+```","path":"modules/system/oagw/docs/adr-plugin-system.md","commit_id":"141f08c649b048bdf4b4c9e7add110efb09054c6","original_commit_id":"59ec3ad08935366fc94a9dbd6274bddd9d00dd06","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Add language labels to fenced code blocks (MD040).**\n\nmarkdownlint flags fenced blocks without a language.  \n\n<details>\n<summary>✍️ Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-```\n+```rust\n // oagw-sdk/src/plugins.rs\n ...\n-```\n+```\n\n-```\n+```text\n Incoming Request\n   → Auth Plugin (credential injection)\n   → Guard Plugins (validation, can reject)\n   → Transform Plugins (modify request)\n   → HTTP call to external service\n   → Transform Plugins (modify response)\n   → Return to client\n-```\n+```\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Tools</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 markdownlint-cli2 (0.20.0)</summary>\n\n[warning] 70-70: Fenced code blocks should have a language specified\n\n(MD040, fenced-code-language)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n````\nIn `@modules/system/oagw/docs/adr-plugin-system.md` around lines 41 - 79, The\nmarkdown has unlabeled fenced code blocks; add language labels so linting\npasses: mark the first fenced block that contains the Rust traits (AuthPlugin,\nGuardPlugin, TransformPlugin in oagw-sdk/src/plugins.rs) as ```rust (ensure the\nclosing fence matches), and label the \"Plugin Execution Order\" fenced block as a\nplain text block using ```text (or ```markdown if preferred) so the diagram is\nfenced with a language identifier and the opening/closing fences are consistent.\n````\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-09T14:13:54Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T14:13:56Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2782878621","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782878621"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2782878621"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782878621/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":41,"original_start_line":41,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":79,"original_line":79,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":79,"position":79,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782878626","pull_request_review_id":3773555657,"id":2782878626,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6l31ui","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,438 @@\n+# Cache Invalidation Flow\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+Cache invalidation ensures consistency across Data Plane and Control Plane caches when configuration changes. Writes trigger immediate invalidation in DP L1/L2, followed by CP L1\n+notification.\n+\n+## Cache Architecture\n+\n+### Data Plane Caches\n+\n+- **L1 (In-Memory)**: LRU cache, 10k entries, <1μs access\n+- **L2 (Redis, Optional)**: Shared across DP instances, ~1-2ms access\n+- **Database**: Source of truth, ~5-10ms access\n+\n+### Control Plane Cache\n+\n+- **L1 (In-Memory)**: LRU cache, 1000 entries, <1μs access\n+- **No L2**: CP depends on DP for config resolution\n+\n+## Invalidation Trigger: Config Write\n+\n+When a management operation modifies configuration (upstream, route, plugin), invalidation flows through multiple layers.\n+\n+## Scenario 1: Update Upstream Config\n+\n+### Initial State\n+\n+**CP L1 cache**:\n+\n+```\n+upstream:{tenant_id}:openai → {...config...} (cached 5 minutes ago)\n+```\n+\n+**DP L1 cache**:\n+\n+```\n+upstream:{tenant_id}:openai → {...config...} (cached 10 minutes ago)\n+```\n+\n+**DP L2 cache (Redis)**:\n+\n+```\n+upstream:{tenant_id}:openai → {...config...} (TTL: 3 minutes remaining)\n+```\n+\n+### Management Request\n+\n+```http\n+PUT /api/oagw/v1/upstreams/gts.x.core.oagw.upstream.v1~7c9e6679... HTTP/1.1\n+Host: oagw.example.com\n+Authorization: Bearer <tenant-token>\n+Content-Type: application/json\n+\n+{\n+  \"server\": {\n+    \"endpoints\": [\n+      { \"scheme\": \"https\", \"host\": \"api.openai.com\", \"port\": 443 }\n+    ]\n+  },\n+  \"protocol\": \"gts.x.core.oagw.protocol.v1~x.core.http.v1\",\n+  \"alias\": \"openai\",\n+  \"rate_limit\": {\n+    \"sustained\": { \"rate\": 50, \"window\": \"minute\" }\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Invalidation Flow\n+\n+```\n+Client → API Handler\n+  ↓\n+API Handler → Data Plane\n+  ↓\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│ Data Plane Processing               │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│ 1. Validate request                 │\n+│ 2. Write to database                │\n+│    UPDATE oagw_upstream             │\n+│    SET config = ...                 │\n+│    WHERE id = ...                   │\n+│                                     │\n+│ 3. Invalidate DP L1 cache           │\n+│    DELETE upstream:{tenant}:openai  │\n+│                                     │\n+│ 4. Invalidate DP L2 cache (Redis)  │\n+│    DEL upstream:{tenant}:openai     │\n+│                                     │\n+│ 5. Return success                   │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────┘\n+  ↓\n+API Handler receives success\n+  ↓\n+API Handler → Control Plane (notification)\n+  ↓\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│ Control Plane Processing            │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│ 1. Receive invalidation message     │\n+│    {                                │\n+│      \"cache_key\": \"upstream:...\",   │\n+│      \"tenant_id\": \"...\",            │\n+│      \"upstream_id\": \"...\"           │\n+│    }                                │\n+│                                     │\n+│ 2. Invalidate CP L1 cache           │\n+│    DELETE upstream:{tenant}:openai  │\n+│                                     │\n+│ 3. Acknowledge                      │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────┘\n+  ↓\n+API Handler → Client (200 OK)\n+```\n+\n+### Post-Invalidation State\n+\n+**CP L1 cache**:\n+\n+```\n+(empty - invalidated)\n+```\n+\n+**DP L1 cache**:\n+\n+```\n+(empty - invalidated)\n+```\n+\n+**DP L2 cache (Redis)**:\n+\n+```\n+(empty - invalidated)\n+```\n+\n+**Database**:\n+\n+```\n+upstream config = updated value (source of truth)\n+```\n+\n+### Next Proxy Request\n+\n+```\n+Client → API Handler → Control Plane\n+  ↓\n+CP checks L1 cache: MISS\n+  ↓\n+CP calls DP.resolve_upstream(\"openai\")\n+  ↓\n+DP checks L1 cache: MISS\n+  ↓\n+DP checks L2 cache: MISS\n+  ↓\n+DP queries database: HIT (fresh config)\n+  ↓\n+DP populates L1 and L2 with fresh config\n+  ↓\n+DP returns to CP\n+  ↓\n+CP populates L1 with fresh config\n+  ↓\n+CP uses fresh config for request\n+```\n+\n+**Result**: Next request uses updated rate limit (50/min instead of 100/min).\n+\n+## Scenario 2: Create New Route\n+\n+### Management Request\n+\n+```http\n+POST /api/oagw/v1/routes HTTP/1.1\n+Host: oagw.example.com\n+Authorization: Bearer <tenant-token>\n+Content-Type: application/json\n+\n+{\n+  \"upstream_id\": \"gts.x.core.oagw.upstream.v1~7c9e6679...\",\n+  \"match\": {\n+    \"http\": {\n+      \"methods\": [\"POST\"],\n+      \"path\": \"/v1/completions\"\n+    }\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Invalidation Flow\n+\n+```\n+Data Plane:\n+  1. Insert into oagw_route table\n+  2. No cache to invalidate (new resource)\n+  3. Return 201 Created\n+\n+No CP notification needed (route not cached yet)\n+```\n+\n+**Result**: Next request matching this route will query DP, get fresh route, cache it.\n+\n+## Scenario 3: Delete Upstream (with cascade)\n+\n+### Management Request\n+\n+```http\n+DELETE /api/oagw/v1/upstreams/gts.x.core.oagw.upstream.v1~7c9e6679...?cascade=true HTTP/1.1\n+Host: oagw.example.com\n+Authorization: Bearer <tenant-token>\n+```\n+\n+### Invalidation Flow\n+\n+```\n+Data Plane:\n+  1. Find all routes for upstream\n+     SELECT id FROM oagw_route WHERE upstream_id = ...\n+     Result: [route1, route2, route3]\n+\n+  2. Delete routes (cascade)\n+     DELETE FROM oagw_route WHERE upstream_id = ...\n+\n+  3. Delete upstream\n+     DELETE FROM oagw_upstream WHERE id = ...\n+\n+  4. Invalidate all affected cache keys:\n+     DP L1/L2:\n+       - upstream:{tenant}:openai\n+       - route:{upstream_id}:POST:/v1/chat/completions\n+       - route:{upstream_id}:POST:/v1/completions\n+       - route:{upstream_id}:GET:/v1/models\n+\n+  5. Return 204 No Content\n+\n+API Handler:\n+  Notify CP to invalidate all affected keys\n+```\n+\n+**Result**: All cached config for this upstream and its routes invalidated.\n+\n+## Scenario 4: Multi-Instance Environment\n+\n+### Setup\n+\n+3 Data Plane instances behind load balancer, shared Redis L2 cache.\n+2 Control Plane instances.\n+\n+### Update Flow\n+\n+```\n+Client → API Handler → DP Instance 1\n+  ↓\n+DP1:\n+  1. Write to database (shared)\n+  2. Flush DP1 L1 cache (local)\n+  3. Flush Redis L2 cache (shared)\n+  4. Return success\n+  ↓\n+API Handler → Broadcast to all CP instances\n+  ↓\n+CP1: Flush L1 cache (local)\n+CP2: Flush L1 cache (local)\n+```\n+\n+### Next Request to Different Instance\n+\n+```\n+Client → API Handler → CP2\n+  ↓\n+CP2 L1: MISS (just flushed)\n+  ↓\n+CP2 → DP Instance 2 (load balanced)\n+  ↓\n+DP2 L1: MISS (different instance)\n+  ↓\n+DP2 L2 (Redis): MISS (shared, was flushed)\n+  ↓\n+DP2 Database: HIT (shared, has fresh data)\n+  ↓\n+DP2 populates L1 and L2\n+  ↓\n+DP2 → CP2\n+  ↓\n+CP2 populates L1\n+  ↓\n+Fresh config used\n+```\n+\n+**Result**: Invalidation works across multiple instances via shared L2 and DB.\n+\n+## Invalidation Timing\n+\n+| Event               | Latency         |\n+|---------------------|-----------------|\n+| DP L1 flush         | <1ms (local)    |\n+| DP L2 flush (Redis) | 1-2ms (network) |\n+| CP notification     | 10-50ms (async) |\n+| CP L1 flush         | <1ms (local)    |\n+\n+**Total window**: ~50-100ms from write to all caches invalidated.\n+\n+**Staleness window**: Worst case 100ms for CP to receive notification and flush.\n+\n+## Consistency Guarantees\n+\n+### Strong Consistency in DP\n+\n+- L1 flush before returning success\n+- L2 flush before returning success\n+- Next DP read sees fresh data\n+\n+### Eventual Consistency in CP\n+\n+- Notification is asynchronous\n+- CP may serve stale data for ~50-100ms\n+- Acceptable for MVP (config changes are rare)\n+\n+### Future: Immediate Consistency\n+\n+For strict consistency requirements:\n+\n+1. CP waits for DP write + invalidation to complete\n+2. CP synchronously flushes its L1 before proxy call\n+3. Adds latency, only enable if needed\n+\n+## Cache Key Patterns\n+\n+### Upstream\n+\n+```\n+upstream:{tenant_id}:{alias}\n+```\n+\n+Invalidated on:\n+\n+- `PUT /upstreams/{id}`\n+- `DELETE /upstreams/{id}`\n+\n+### Route\n+\n+```\n+route:{upstream_id}:{method}:{path}\n+```\n+\n+Invalidated on:\n+\n+- `PUT /routes/{id}`\n+- `DELETE /routes/{id}`\n+- `DELETE /upstreams/{id}` (cascade)\n+\n+### Plugin\n+\n+```\n+plugin:{plugin_id}\n+```\n+\n+Invalidated on:\n+\n+- `PUT /plugins/{id}` (immutable, rare)\n+- `DELETE /plugins/{id}`\n+\n+## Failure Scenarios\n+\n+### Redis Unavailable During Invalidation\n+\n+```\n+DP writes to database\n+  ↓\n+DP flushes L1: SUCCESS\n+  ↓\n+DP tries to flush L2 (Redis): FAILURE\n+  ↓\n+DP logs error, continues\n+  ↓\n+Returns success (L1 flushed, DB updated)\n+```\n+\n+**Impact**:\n+\n+- DP instance L1 is fresh\n+- Other DP instances L2 cache may be stale (until TTL expires)\n+- Max staleness: 5 minutes (L2 TTL)\n+\n+**Mitigation**: L2 TTL prevents unbounded staleness.\n+\n+### CP Notification Failure\n+\n+```\n+DP completes write and flush\n+  ↓\n+API Handler sends CP notification: FAILURE\n+  ↓\n+API Handler logs error, continues\n+  ↓\n+Returns success to client\n+```\n+\n+**Impact**:\n+\n+- CP L1 cache may be stale until TTL or eviction\n+- CP cache is small (1000 entries), likely to be evicted soon\n+\n+**Mitigation**:\n+\n+- CP cache has implicit TTL via LRU eviction\n+- Config changes are rare, brief staleness acceptable for MVP","path":"modules/system/oagw/scenarios/cache-invalidation.md","commit_id":"141f08c649b048bdf4b4c9e7add110efb09054c6","original_commit_id":"59ec3ad08935366fc94a9dbd6274bddd9d00dd06","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Align CP cache staleness language with “no TTL” policy.**\n\nThe CP notification failure impact says “until TTL or eviction,” but earlier CP cache guidance implies no TTL. Please update this to eviction-only or introduce a defined TTL policy.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/oagw/scenarios/cache-invalidation.md` around lines 399 - 407,\nUpdate the Impact wording in the \"Impact\" section so it aligns with the no-TTL\npolicy for the CP cache: replace \"CP L1 cache may be stale until TTL or\neviction\" with language specifying eviction-only staleness (e.g., \"CP L1 cache\nmay be stale until eviction (no TTL)\") or alternatively add a short TTL policy\nsentence in the \"Mitigation\" section; target the \"Impact\" and \"Mitigation\" lines\nreferencing the CP cache/L1 cache entries to ensure consistency with earlier\nguidance.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-09T14:13:54Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T14:13:56Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2782878626","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782878626"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2782878626"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782878626/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":399,"original_start_line":399,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":407,"original_line":407,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":407,"position":407,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782878629","pull_request_review_id":3773555657,"id":2782878629,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6l31ul","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,459 @@\n+# Plugin Execution Flow\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+Plugins execute in Control Plane during proxy request processing. Three plugin types execute in strict order: Auth → Guards → Transform → Proxy Call → Transform.\n+\n+## Plugin Types\n+\n+### AuthPlugin\n+- **Purpose**: Inject authentication credentials\n+- **Execution**: Once per request, before guards\n+- **Can terminate**: No (always succeeds or errors)\n+- **Examples**: API key, OAuth2, Bearer token\n+\n+### GuardPlugin\n+- **Purpose**: Validate and enforce policies\n+- **Execution**: After auth, before transform\n+- **Can terminate**: Yes (reject request with error)\n+- **Examples**: Timeout, CORS, rate limiting\n+\n+### TransformPlugin\n+- **Purpose**: Modify request/response/error data\n+- **Execution**: Before and after proxy call\n+- **Can terminate**: No (mutations only)\n+- **Examples**: Logging, metrics, request ID\n+\n+## Execution Order\n+\n+```\n+Incoming Request\n+  ↓\n+1. Auth Plugin (credential injection)\n+  ↓\n+2. Guard Plugins (validation, can reject)\n+  ↓\n+3. Transform Plugins (modify request)\n+  ↓\n+4. HTTP call to external service\n+  ↓\n+5. Transform Plugins (modify response)\n+  ↓\n+Response to Client\n+```","path":"modules/system/oagw/scenarios/plugin-execution.md","commit_id":"141f08c649b048bdf4b4c9e7add110efb09054c6","original_commit_id":"59ec3ad08935366fc94a9dbd6274bddd9d00dd06","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Add language identifiers to fenced code blocks (markdownlint MD040).**\n\nSeveral fences lack language tags (e.g., around Line 29, Line 114, Line 171, Line 341, Line 363, Line 412). Please add `text` (or a more specific language) to satisfy linting.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-```\n+```text\n Incoming Request\n   ↓\n 1. Auth Plugin (credential injection)\n   ↓\n 2. Guard Plugins (validation, can reject)\n   ↓\n 3. Transform Plugins (modify request)\n   ↓\n 4. HTTP call to external service\n   ↓\n 5. Transform Plugins (modify response)\n   ↓\n Response to Client\n-```\n+```\n\n-```\n+```text\n Headers:\n   + Authorization: Bearer sk-proj-abc123...\n-```\n+```\n\n-```\n+```text\n Headers:\n   + X-Request-ID: req_abc123...\n-```\n+```\n\n-```\n+```text\n Upstream returns 500 error\n   ↓\n Transform plugins (post-error) execute\n   ↓\n   - LoggingTransformPlugin: logs error\n   - RequestIdTransformPlugin: preserves request ID\n   ↓\n Error response returned to client\n-```\n+```\n\n-```\n+```text\n LoggingTransformPlugin:\n   → Log error response\n\n RequestIdTransformPlugin:\n   → Ensure X-Request-ID present in response\n-```\n+```\n\n-```\n+```text\n Guards: [timeout, cors]\n Transforms (pre): [request_id, logging, metrics]\n Transforms (post): [request_id, logging, metrics]\n-```\n+```\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Tools</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 markdownlint-cli2 (0.20.0)</summary>\n\n[warning] 29-29: Fenced code blocks should have a language specified\n\n(MD040, fenced-code-language)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n````\nIn `@modules/system/oagw/scenarios/plugin-execution.md` around lines 27 - 43,\nSeveral fenced code blocks in plugin-execution.md lack language identifiers;\nupdate each block (the \"Execution Order\" block starting with \"Incoming Request\",\nthe \"Headers:\" examples, the \"Upstream returns 500 error\" / post-error flow, the\n\"LoggingTransformPlugin:\" / \"RequestIdTransformPlugin:\" block, and the \"Guards:\n[...] / Transforms (pre/post): [...]\" block) to use a language tag (e.g., change\n``` to ```text) so markdownlint MD040 is satisfied; keep the existing content\nand closing fences unchanged.\n````\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-09T14:13:54Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T14:13:56Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2782878629","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782878629"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2782878629"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2782878629/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":27,"original_start_line":27,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":43,"original_line":43,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":43,"position":43,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2784106009","pull_request_review_id":3774841550,"id":2784106009,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6l8hYZ","diff_hunk":"@@ -104,62 +172,916 @@ pub type HttpClient = RpcClient;\n ```\n \n **Pros**:\n-- ✅ Zero-cost abstraction (static dispatch)\n-- ✅ Simpler implementation\n+\n+- Zero-cost abstraction (static dispatch)\n+- Simpler implementation\n+\n+**Cons**:\n+\n+- - Cannot use both modes in same binary\n+- - Harder to test (need feature-gated test code)\n+- - Less flexible for future extensions\n+\n+### Option 3: Hybrid Approach with Deployment Abstraction (Recommended)\n+\n+Single `OagwClient` type that internally dispatches to the appropriate implementation:\n+\n+```rust\n+// Public API - deployment-agnostic\n+pub struct OagwClient {\n+    inner: OagwClientImpl,\n+}\n+\n+// Internal implementation enum (not exposed)\n+enum OagwClientImpl {\n+    SharedProcess(SharedProcessClient),\n+    RemoteProxy(RemoteProxyClient),\n+}\n+\n+impl OagwClient {\n+    /// Create from configuration (automatically selects implementation)\n+    pub fn from_config(config: OagwClientConfig) -> Result<Self, ClientError> {\n+        let inner = match config.mode {\n+            ClientMode::SharedProcess { control_plane } => {\n+                OagwClientImpl::SharedProcess(SharedProcessClient::new(control_plane)?)\n+            }\n+            ClientMode::RemoteProxy { base_url, auth_token } => {\n+                OagwClientImpl::RemoteProxy(RemoteProxyClient::new(base_url, auth_token)?)\n+            }\n+        };\n+        Ok(Self { inner })\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Execute plain HTTP request\n+    pub async fn execute(&self, alias: &str, req: Request) -> Result<Response, ClientError> {\n+        match &self.inner {\n+            OagwClientImpl::SharedProcess(c) => c.execute(alias, req).await,\n+            OagwClientImpl::RemoteProxy(c) => c.execute(alias, req).await,\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    // Same for execute_streaming, websocket, etc.\n+}\n+\n+// Configuration that determines deployment mode\n+pub struct OagwClientConfig {\n+    mode: ClientMode,\n+    timeout: Duration,\n+    // ... other common config\n+}\n+\n+pub enum ClientMode {\n+    /// OAGW in same process - use direct function calls\n+    SharedProcess {\n+        control_plane: Arc<dyn ControlPlaneService>,\n+    },\n+    /// OAGW in separate process - use HTTP proxy endpoint\n+    RemoteProxy {\n+        base_url: String,\n+        auth_token: String,\n+    },\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Usage (same code in both modes)**:\n+\n+```rust\n+// Configuration comes from environment/settings\n+let config = OagwClientConfig::from_env()?;  // Auto-detects mode\n+let client = OagwClient::from_config(config)?;\n+\n+// Application code - identical regardless of deployment\n+let request = Request::builder()\n+    .method(Method::POST)\n+    .path(\"/v1/chat/completions\")\n+    .json(&payload)?\n+    .build()?;\n+\n+let response = client.execute(\"openai\", request).await?;\n+```\n+\n+**Pros**:\n+\n+- + **Deployment-agnostic**: Application code never changes\n+- + **Zero-cost abstraction**: Enum dispatch is optimized away by compiler\n+- + **Easy to test**: Mock can be added as third variant\n+- + **Type-safe**: Single concrete type, no trait objects\n+- + **Configuration-driven**: Mode selected from config, not code\n+\n+**Cons**:\n+\n+- Slightly more boilerplate in enum dispatch methods\n+\n+**Decision**: Use hybrid approach with deployment abstraction (Option 3).\n+\n+## SDK Integration Patterns\n+\n+Third-party Rust SDKs (OpenAI, Anthropic, AWS, etc.) need to route requests through OAGW. This section analyzes all integration approaches.\n+\n+### Pattern 1: Drop-In Replacement for reqwest\n+\n+**Approach**: Provide a `reqwest`-compatible API so SDKs can use our client as a custom HTTP backend.","path":"modules/system/oagw/docs/adr-rust-abi-client-library.md","commit_id":"141f08c649b048bdf4b4c9e7add110efb09054c6","original_commit_id":"9982ec747de7bee87d4ec0c22a81b523feec996b","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Let's use modkit-http compatible API.","created_at":"2026-02-09T18:56:48Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T01:03:30Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2784106009","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2784106009"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2784106009"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2784106009/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":283,"original_line":283,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":317,"position":317,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2785277134","pull_request_review_id":3774841550,"id":2785277134,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6mA_TO","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,198 @@\n+# ADR: Plugin System\n+\n+- **Status**: Accepted\n+- **Date**: 2026-02-09\n+- **Deciders**: OAGW Team\n+\n+## Context\n+\n+OAGW needs extensibility for request/response processing. Different use cases require different behaviors:\n+\n+- Authentication: API key, OAuth2, JWT, custom schemes\n+- Validation: Timeouts, CORS, rate limiting, custom rules\n+- Transformation: Logging, metrics, request ID, custom headers\n+\n+## Decision\n+\n+**Plugin system with three plugin types**, executed by Control Plane:\n+\n+### Plugin Types\n+\n+**1. AuthPlugin** (`gts.x.core.oagw.plugin.auth.v1~*`)\n+\n+- Purpose: Inject authentication credentials\n+- Execution: Once per request, before guards\n+- Examples: API key, OAuth2, Bearer token, Basic auth\n+\n+**2. GuardPlugin** (`gts.x.core.oagw.plugin.guard.v1~*`)\n+\n+- Purpose: Validate requests and enforce policies (can reject)\n+- Execution: After auth, before transform\n+- Examples: Timeout enforcement, CORS validation, rate limiting\n+\n+**3. TransformPlugin** (`gts.x.core.oagw.plugin.transform.v1~*`)\n+\n+- Purpose: Modify request/response/error data\n+- Execution: Before and after proxy call\n+- Examples: Logging, metrics collection, request ID propagation\n+\n+### Plugin Traits\n+\n+```rust\n+// oagw-sdk/src/plugins.rs\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait AuthPlugin: Send + Sync {\n+    fn id(&self) -> &str;\n+    fn plugin_type(&self) -> &str;\n+    async fn authenticate(&self, ctx: &mut RequestContext) -> Result<()>;\n+}\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait GuardPlugin: Send + Sync {\n+    fn id(&self) -> &str;\n+    fn plugin_type(&self) -> &str;\n+    async fn guard_request(&self, ctx: &RequestContext) -> Result<GuardDecision>;\n+    async fn guard_response(&self, ctx: &ResponseContext) -> Result<GuardDecision>;\n+}\n+\n+#[async_trait]\n+pub trait TransformPlugin: Send + Sync {\n+    fn id(&self) -> &str;\n+    fn plugin_type(&self) -> &str;\n+    async fn transform_request(&self, ctx: &mut RequestContext) -> Result<()>;\n+    async fn transform_response(&self, ctx: &mut ResponseContext) -> Result<()>;\n+    async fn transform_error(&self, ctx: &mut ErrorContext) -> Result<()>;\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Plugin Execution Order\n+\n+```\n+Incoming Request\n+  → Auth Plugin (credential injection)\n+  → Guard Plugins (validation, can reject)\n+  → Transform Plugins (modify request)\n+  → HTTP call to external service\n+  → Transform Plugins (modify response)\n+  → Return to client\n+```\n+\n+### Built-in Plugins\n+\n+Included in `oagw-cp` crate:\n+\n+**Auth Plugins**:\n+\n+- `ApiKeyAuthPlugin`: API key injection (header/query)\n+- `BasicAuthPlugin`: HTTP Basic authentication\n+- `BearerTokenAuthPlugin`: Bearer token injection\n+- `OAuth2ClientCredPlugin`: OAuth2 client credentials flow\n+\n+**Guard Plugins**:\n+\n+- `TimeoutGuardPlugin`: Request timeout enforcement\n+- `CorsGuardPlugin`: CORS preflight validation\n+- `RateLimitGuardPlugin`: Rate limiting (token bucket)\n+\n+**Transform Plugins**:","path":"modules/system/oagw/docs/adr-plugin-system.md","commit_id":"141f08c649b048bdf4b4c9e7add110efb09054c6","original_commit_id":"9982ec747de7bee87d4ec0c22a81b523feec996b","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Looks like Transform plugins will have access to secrets (API tokens, bearer tokens)","created_at":"2026-02-10T01:03:00Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T01:03:30Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2785277134","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2785277134"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2785277134"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2785277134/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":98,"original_line":98,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":98,"position":98,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2786654543","pull_request_review_id":3777599335,"id":2786654543,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6mGPlP","diff_hunk":"@@ -51,13 +51,15 @@ X-OAGW-Error-Source: gateway\n ```\n \n **Advantages**:\n-- ✅ No memory overhead\n-- ✅ Predictable latency (no queueing delay)\n-- ✅ Simple to implement\n+\n+- No memory overhead\n+- Predictable latency (no queueing delay)\n+- Simple to implement\n \n **Disadvantages**:\n-- ❌ Poor UX during spikes\n-- ❌ Clients must implement retry logic\n+\n+- No Poor UX during spikes\n+- No Clie