/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 174\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat -n modules/system/oagw/openspec/changes/archive/2026-02-09-scaffold-oagw-crates/proposal.md 2>/dev/null | head -40\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 2239\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Add language identifiers to all unlabeled code fences to resolve markdownlint MD040.**\n\nLines 9, 18, 59, 65, 72, 76, 86, 104, 108, 112, 129, 133, 150, 154, 163, 167, 172, 176, 181, 206, 211, 214, 217, 220, 223, 227, 255, 272, 288, 304, 319 contain unlabeled code blocks. Add appropriate language identifiers: use `` `text`` for ASCII flow diagrams, `` `json`` for JSON examples, `` `http`` for HTTP messages, and `` `bash`` or similar for shell commands.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/oagw/scenarios/proxy-operations.md` around lines 1 - 6, The\nmarkdown contains many unlabeled code fences in the \"Proxy Operations Flow\"\ndocument; update each unlabeled triple-backtick block to include the appropriate\nlanguage tag (use text for ASCII flow diagrams, json for JSON payloads, http for\nHTTP request/response examples, and bash for shell/command snippets) so\nmarkdownlint rule MD040 is satisfied; search for unlabeled fences under headings\nlike \"Proxy Operations Flow\", \"Overview\", and the subsequent example sections\nand add the matching language identifier to each code fence.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-10T08:53:46Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T08:53:49Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2786654620","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2786654620"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2786654620"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2786654620/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":1,"original_start_line":1,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":6,"original_line":6,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":6,"position":6,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2786654628","pull_request_review_id":3777599335,"id":2786654628,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6mGPmk","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,339 @@\n+# Proxy Operations Flow\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+Proxy operations execute API calls to external services. Requests are routed from API Handler → Control Plane → Data Plane (config resolution) → Control Plane (execution).\n+\n+## Request Flow\n+\n+```\n+Client Request\n+  → API Handler (auth, rate limit)\n+    → Control Plane (orchestrate)\n+      → Data Plane (resolve upstream config)\n+      → Data Plane (resolve route config)\n+      → CP: Execute plugins (auth, guard, transform)\n+      → CP: HTTP call to external service\n+    → Response\n+```\n+\n+## Component Responsibilities\n+\n+### API Handler\n+- Validates Bearer token\n+- Applies inbound rate limiting\n+- Routes `/api/oagw/v1/proxy/*` requests to Control Plane","path":"modules/system/oagw/scenarios/proxy-operations.md","commit_id":"c4001447ea4b5a7a1747d7b00479084589d01bd9","original_commit_id":"c4001447ea4b5a7a1747d7b00479084589d01bd9","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Hyphenate the compound adjective.**\n\n“Inbound rate-limiting” reads correctly as an adjective.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Tools</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 LanguageTool</summary>\n\n[uncategorized] ~24-~24: If this is a compound adjective that modifies the following noun, use a hyphen.\nContext: ...alidates Bearer token - Applies inbound rate limiting - Routes `/api/oagw/v1/proxy/*` request...\n\n(EN_COMPOUND_ADJECTIVE_INTERNAL)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/oagw/scenarios/proxy-operations.md` around lines 22 - 25,\nUpdate the \"API Handler\" bullet that currently reads \"Applies inbound rate\nlimiting\" to use the hyphenated compound adjective \"Applies inbound\nrate-limiting\" in the modules/system/oagw/scenarios/proxy-operations.md\ndocumentation; locate the \"API Handler\" section and edit the second bullet so\nthe compound modifier is hyphenated.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-10T08:53:46Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T08:53:49Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2786654628","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2786654628"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2786654628"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2786654628/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":22,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":25,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":25,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787338000","pull_request_review_id":3778318677,"id":2787338000,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6mI2cQ","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,173 @@\n+# ADR: Component Architecture\n+\n+- **Status**: Accepted\n+- **Date**: 2026-02-09\n+- **Deciders**: OAGW Team\n+\n+## Context and Problem Statement\n+\n+OAGW is being designed as a greenfield project without existing code. We need to establish the architectural foundation for how components are organized, how they communicate, and\n+how deployment flexibility is achieved.\n+\n+**Key Requirements**:\n+\n+- Support both single-executable and microservice deployment modes\n+- Clear separation of concerns between configuration management and request execution\n+- Enable independent scaling of different concerns\n+- Minimize latency through efficient communication patterns\n+\n+## Decision Drivers\n+\n+- Testability: Each component should be testable in isolation\n+- Deployment flexibility: Support multiple deployment topologies without code changes\n+- Separation of concerns: Configuration management vs request execution\n+- Performance: Minimize overhead in communication between components\n+- Maintainability: Clear boundaries and responsibilities\n+\n+## Decision\n+\n+OAGW is composed of three distinct components, packaged as separate library crates:\n+\n+### Components\n+\n+**1. API Handler (`oagw-api`)**\n+\n+- **Responsibility**: Entry point for all HTTP requests\n+- **Functions**:\n+    - Incoming authentication (validate Bearer tokens)\n+    - Incoming rate limiting (protect gateway from overload)\n+    - Path-based routing to CP or DP\n+- **Routes**:\n+    - `/api/oagw/v1/proxy/*` → Control Plane\n+    - `/api/oagw/v1/upstreams/*`, `/routes/*`, `/plugins/*` → Data Plane\n+\n+**2. Control Plane (`oagw-cp`)**","path":"modules/system/oagw/docs/adr-component-architecture.md","commit_id":"c4001447ea4b5a7a1747d7b00479084589d01bd9","original_commit_id":"c4001447ea4b5a7a1747d7b00479084589d01bd9","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"It seems like the Data/Control plane terms are swapped.","created_at":"2026-02-10T11:11:49Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T11:11:57Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2787338000","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787338000"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2787338000"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787338000/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":44,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":44,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787684514","pull_request_review_id":3778663122,"id":2787684514,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6mKLCi","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,451 @@\n+#!/usr/bin/env python3\n+\"\"\"\n+Python-based OAGW Gateway Mock Server for Integration Testing\n+\n+This server simulates both:\n+1. An OAGW gateway that routes requests to external services\n+2. Mock external APIs (e.g., OpenAI, GitHub, custom services)\n+\n+The server provides realistic testing scenarios for the Rust OAGW client library.\n+\"\"\"\n+\n+import json\n+import time\n+from flask import Flask, request, Response, jsonify, stream_with_context\n+import sys\n+\n+app = Flask(__name__)\n+\n+# Configuration\n+VALID_TOKEN = \"test-integration-token\"\n+\n+# Mock data stores\n+chat_history = []\n+github_repos = {\n+    \"octocat\": {\n+        \"login\": \"octocat\",\n+        \"id\": 1,\n+        \"type\": \"User\",\n+        \"name\": \"The Octocat\",\n+        \"company\": \"GitHub\",\n+        \"blog\": \"https://github.blog\"\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+\n+def check_auth():\n+    \"\"\"Validate authorization token\"\"\"\n+    auth_header = request.headers.get(\"Authorization\", \"\")\n+    if not auth_header.startswith(\"Bearer \"):\n+        return False, jsonify({\"error\": \"Missing or invalid authorization\"}), 401\n+\n+    token = auth_header.replace(\"Bearer \", \"\")\n+    if token != VALID_TOKEN:\n+        return False, jsonify({\"error\": \"Invalid token\"}), 403\n+\n+    return True, None, None\n+\n+\n+def add_error_source_header(response, source=\"upstream\"):\n+    \"\"\"Add X-OAGW-Error-Source header to response\"\"\"\n+    response.headers[\"X-OAGW-Error-Source\"] = source\n+    return response\n+\n+\n+# ============================================================================\n+# OAGW Proxy Endpoints\n+# ============================================================================\n+\n+@app.route(\"/api/oagw/v1/proxy/<alias>/<path:service_path>\", methods=[\"GET\", \"POST\", \"PUT\", \"DELETE\"])\n+def proxy_request(alias, service_path):\n+    \"\"\"\n+    Main OAGW proxy endpoint that routes requests to mock external services\n+    \"\"\"\n+    # Check authorization\n+    is_valid, error_response, status_code = check_auth()\n+    if not is_valid:\n+        response = add_error_source_header(Response(\n+            json.dumps({\"error\": \"Unauthorized\"}),\n+            status=status_code,\n+            mimetype=\"application/json\"\n+        ), \"gateway\")\n+        return response\n+\n+    # Route to appropriate service handler\n+    if alias == \"openai\":\n+        return handle_openai(service_path)\n+    elif alias == \"github\":\n+        return handle_github(service_path)\n+    elif alias == \"weather\":\n+        return handle_weather(service_path)\n+    elif alias == \"calculator\":\n+        return handle_calculator(service_path)\n+    elif alias == \"stream-test\":\n+        return handle_stream_test(service_path)\n+    else:\n+        response = add_error_source_header(Response(\n+            json.dumps({\"error\": f\"Unknown alias: {alias}\"}),\n+            status=404,\n+            mimetype=\"application/json\"\n+        ), \"gateway\")\n+        return response\n+\n+\n+# ============================================================================\n+# Mock OpenAI API\n+# ============================================================================\n+\n+def handle_openai(path):\n+    \"\"\"Handle OpenAI API requests\"\"\"\n+    if path == \"v1/chat/completions\":\n+        return handle_chat_completions()\n+    elif path == \"v1/models\":\n+        return handle_list_models()\n+    else:\n+        response = add_error_source_header(Response(\n+            json.dumps({\"error\": \"Not found\"}),\n+            status=404,\n+            mimetype=\"application/json\"\n+        ), \"upstream\")\n+        return response\n+\n+\n+def handle_chat_completions():\n+    \"\"\"Handle chat completions (both streaming and non-streaming)\"\"\"\n+    try:\n+        data = request.get_json()\n+        model = data.get(\"model\", \"gpt-4\")\n+        messages = data.get(\"messages\", [])\n+        stream = data.get(\"stream\", False)\n+\n+        # Store in history\n+        chat_history.append({\n+            \"timestamp\": time.time(),\n+            \"model\": model,\n+            \"messages\": messages\n+        })\n+\n+        if stream:\n+            return handle_streaming_chat(model, messages)\n+        else:\n+            return handle_buffered_chat(model, messages)\n+    except Exception as e:\n+        response = add_error_source_header(Response(\n+            json.dumps({\"error\": str(e)}),","path":"modules/system/oagw/oagw-client-prototype/tests/python_integration/server.py","commit_id":"c9c711923d4db2ea8af2f40aeccc2fc2bb664b5a","original_commit_id":"c9c711923d4db2ea8af2f40aeccc2fc2bb664b5a","user":{"login":"github-advanced-security[bot]","id":62310815,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NjIzMTA4MTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/57789?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-advanced-security%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-advanced-security","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-advanced-security%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-advanced-security%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-advanced-security%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-advanced-security%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-advanced-security%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-advanced-security%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-advanced-security%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-advanced-security%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-advanced-security%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Information exposure through an exception\n\n[Stack trace information](1) flows to this location and may be exposed to an external user.\n\n[Show more details](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/security/code-scanning/98)","created_at":"2026-02-10T12:31:02Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T12:31:02Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2787684514","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787684514"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2787684514"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787684514/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":134,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":134,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787684528","pull_request_review_id":3778663122,"id":2787684528,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6mKLCw","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,451 @@\n+#!/usr/bin/env python3\n+\"\"\"\n+Python-based OAGW Gateway Mock Server for Integration Testing\n+\n+This server simulates both:\n+1. An OAGW gateway that routes requests to external services\n+2. Mock external APIs (e.g., OpenAI, GitHub, custom services)\n+\n+The server provides realistic testing scenarios for the Rust OAGW client library.\n+\"\"\"\n+\n+import json\n+import time\n+from flask import Flask, request, Response, jsonify, stream_with_context\n+import sys\n+\n+app = Flask(__name__)\n+\n+# Configuration\n+VALID_TOKEN = \"test-integration-token\"\n+\n+# Mock data stores\n+chat_history = []\n+github_repos = {\n+    \"octocat\": {\n+        \"login\": \"octocat\",\n+        \"id\": 1,\n+        \"type\": \"User\",\n+        \"name\": \"The Octocat\",\n+        \"company\": \"GitHub\",\n+        \"blog\": \"https://github.blog\"\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+\n+def check_auth():\n+    \"\"\"Validate authorization token\"\"\"\n+    auth_header = request.headers.get(\"Authorization\", \"\")\n+    if not auth_header.startswith(\"Bearer \"):\n+        return False, jsonify({\"error\": \"Missing or invalid authorization\"}), 401\n+\n+    token = auth_header.replace(\"Bearer \", \"\")\n+    if token != VALID_TOKEN:\n+        return False, jsonify({\"error\": \"Invalid token\"}), 403\n+\n+    return True, None, None\n+\n+\n+def add_error_source_header(response, source=\"upstream\"):\n+    \"\"\"Add X-OAGW-Error-Source header to response\"\"\"\n+    response.headers[\"X-OAGW-Error-Source\"] = source\n+    return response\n+\n+\n+# ============================================================================\n+# OAGW Proxy Endpoints\n+# ============================================================================\n+\n+@app.route(\"/api/oagw/v1/proxy/<alias>/<path:service_path>\", methods=[\"GET\", \"POST\", \"PUT\", \"DELETE\"])\n+def proxy_request(alias, service_path):\n+    \"\"\"\n+    Main OAGW proxy endpoint that routes requests to mock external services\n+    \"\"\"\n+    # Check authorization\n+    is_valid, error_response, status_code = check_auth()\n+    if not is_valid:\n+        response = add_error_source_header(Response(\n+            json.dumps({\"error\": \"Unauthorized\"}),\n+            status=status_code,\n+            mimetype=\"application/json\"\n+        ), \"gateway\")\n+        return response\n+\n+    # Route to appropriate service handler\n+    if alias == \"openai\":\n+        return handle_openai(service_path)\n+    elif alias == \"github\":\n+        return handle_github(service_path)\n+    elif alias == \"weather\":\n+        return handle_weather(service_path)\n+    elif alias == \"calculator\":\n+        return handle_calculator(service_path)\n+    elif alias == \"stream-test\":\n+        return handle_stream_test(service_path)\n+    else:\n+        response = add_error_source_header(Response(\n+            json.dumps({\"error\": f\"Unknown alias: {alias}\"}),\n+            status=404,\n+            mimetype=\"application/json\"\n+        ), \"gateway\")\n+        return response\n+\n+\n+# ============================================================================\n+# Mock OpenAI API\n+# ============================================================================\n+\n+def handle_openai(path):\n+    \"\"\"Handle OpenAI API requests\"\"\"\n+    if path == \"v1/chat/completions\":\n+        return handle_chat_completions()\n+    elif path == \"v1/models\":\n+        return handle_list_models()\n+    else:\n+        response = add_error_source_header(Response(\n+            json.dumps({\"error\": \"Not found\"}),\n+            status=404,\n+            mimetype=\"application/json\"\n+        ), \"upstream\")\n+        return response\n+\n+\n+def handle_chat_completions():\n+    \"\"\"Handle chat completions (both streaming and non-streaming)\"\"\"\n+    try:\n+        data = request.get_json()\n+        model = data.get(\"model\", \"gpt-4\")\n+        messages = data.get(\"messages\", [])\n+        stream = data.get(\"stream\", False)\n+\n+        # Store in history\n+        chat_history.append({\n+            \"timestamp\": time.time(),\n+            \"model\": model,\n+            \"messages\": messages\n+        })\n+\n+        if stream:\n+            return handle_streaming_chat(model, messages)\n+        else:\n+            return handle_buffered_chat(model, messages)\n+    except Exception as e:\n+        response = add_error_source_header(Response(\n+            json.dumps({\"error\": str(e)}),\n+            status=400,\n+            mimetype=\"application/json\"\n+        ), \"upstream\")\n+        return response\n+\n+\n+def handle_buffered_chat(model, messages):\n+    \"\"\"Handle non-streaming chat completion\"\"\"\n+    last_message = messages[-1] if messages else {\"content\": \"\"}\n+    user_content = last_message.get(\"content\", \"\")\n+\n+    # Generate a simple response based on the prompt\n+    if \"hello\" in user_content.lower():\n+        response_text = \"Hello! How can I assist you today?\"\n+    elif \"error\" in user_content.lower():\n+        # Simulate an upstream error\n+        response = add_error_source_header(Response(\n+            json.dumps({\"error\": {\"message\": \"Rate limit exceeded\", \"type\": \"rate_limit_error\"}}),\n+            status=429,\n+            mimetype=\"application/json\"\n+        ), \"upstream\")\n+        return response\n+    else:\n+        response_text = f\"I received your message: '{user_content}'. This is a mock response from the Python test server.\"\n+\n+    result = {\n+        \"id\": f\"chatcmpl-{int(time.time())}\",\n+        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\n+        \"created\": int(time.time()),\n+        \"model\": model,\n+        \"choices\": [{\n+            \"index\": 0,\n+            \"message\": {\n+                \"role\": \"assistant\",\n+                \"content\": response_text\n+            },\n+            \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n+        }],\n+        \"usage\": {\n+            \"prompt_tokens\": 10,\n+            \"completion_tokens\": 20,\n+            \"total_tokens\": 30\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    response = add_error_source_header(\n+        jsonify(result),\n+        \"upstream\"\n+    )\n+    return response\n+\n+\n+def handle_streaming_chat(model, messages):\n+    \"\"\"Handle streaming chat completion using SSE\"\"\"\n+    def generate():\n+        last_message = messages[-1] if messages else {\"content\": \"\"}\n+        user_content = last_message.get(\"content\", \"\")\n+\n+        # Generate response tokens\n+        response_text = f\"Streaming response to: {user_content}\"\n+        words = response_text.split()\n+\n+        # Stream each word as a separate event\n+        for i, word in enumerate(words):\n+            chunk = {\n+                \"id\": f\"chatcmpl-{int(time.time())}\",\n+                \"object\": \"chat.completion.chunk\",\n+                \"created\": int(time.time()),\n+                \"model\": model,\n+                \"choices\": [{\n+                    \"index\": 0,\n+                    \"delta\": {\"content\": word + \" \"},\n+                    \"finish_reason\": None\n+                }]\n+            }\n+            yield f\"data: {json.dumps(chunk)}\\n\\n\"\n+            time.sleep(0.05)  # Small delay to simulate streaming\n+\n+        # Send final chunk\n+        final_chunk = {\n+            \"id\": f\"chatcmpl-{int(time.time())}\",\n+            \"object\": \"chat.completion.chunk\",\n+            \"created\": int(time.time()),\n+            \"model\": model,\n+            \"choices\": [{\n+                \"index\": 0,\n+                \"delta\": {},\n+                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n+            }]\n+        }\n+        yield f\"data: {json.dumps(final_chunk)}\\n\\n\"\n+        yield \"data: [DONE]\\n\\n\"\n+\n+    response = Response(\n+        stream_with_context(generate()),\n+        mimetype=\"text/event-stream\"\n+    )\n+    response.headers[\"Cache-Control\"] = \"no-cache\"\n+    response.headers[\"X-Accel-Buffering\"] = \"no\"\n+    response = add_error_source_header(response, \"upstream\")\n+    return response\n+\n+\n+def handle_list_models():\n+    \"\"\"Handle list models request\"\"\"\n+    models = {\n+        \"object\": \"list\",\n+        \"data\": [\n+            {\"id\": \"gpt-4\", \"object\": \"model\", \"owned_by\": \"openai\"},\n+            {\"id\": \"gpt-3.5-turbo\", \"object\": \"model\", \"owned_by\": \"openai\"}\n+        ]\n+    }\n+    response = add_error_source_header(jsonify(models), \"upstream\")\n+    return response\n+\n+\n+# ============================================================================\n+# Mock GitHub API\n+# ============================================================================\n+\n+def handle_github(path):\n+    \"\"\"Handle GitHub API requests\"\"\"\n+    if path.startswith(\"users/\"):\n+        username = path.replace(\"users/\", \"\")\n+        return handle_get_user(username)\n+    elif path.startswith(\"repos/\"):\n+        return handle_get_repo(path.replace(\"repos/\", \"\"))\n+    else:\n+        response = add_error_source_header(Response(\n+            json.dumps({\"message\": \"Not Found\"}),\n+            status=404,\n+            mimetype=\"application/json\"\n+        ), \"upstream\")\n+        return response\n+\n+\n+def handle_get_user(username):\n+    \"\"\"Handle get user request\"\"\"\n+    if username in github_repos:\n+        response = add_error_source_header(\n+            jsonify(github_repos[username]),\n+            \"upstream\"\n+        )\n+        return response\n+    else:\n+        response = add_error_source_header(Response(\n+            json.dumps({\"message\": \"Not Found\"}),\n+            status=404,\n+            mimetype=\"application/json\"\n+        ), \"upstream\")\n+        return response\n+\n+\n+def handle_get_repo(repo_path):\n+    \"\"\"Handle get repository request\"\"\"\n+    response = add_error_source_header(jsonify({\n+        \"name\": repo_path,\n+        \"full_name\": repo_path,\n+        \"description\": \"A mock repository for testing\",\n+        \"private\": False,\n+        \"html_url\": f\"https://github.com/{repo_path}\"\n+    }), \"upstream\")\n+    return response\n+\n+\n+# ============================================================================\n+# Mock Weather API\n+# ============================================================================\n+\n+def handle_weather(path):\n+    \"\"\"Handle weather API requests\"\"\"\n+    if \"current\" in path:\n+        city = request.args.get(\"city\", \"Unknown\")\n+        weather_data = {\n+            \"location\": city,\n+            \"temperature\": 72,\n+            \"unit\": \"fahrenheit\",\n+            \"condition\": \"sunny\",\n+            \"humidity\": 45,\n+            \"wind_speed\": 8\n+        }\n+        response = add_error_source_header(jsonify(weather_data), \"upstream\")\n+        return response\n+    else:\n+        response = add_error_source_header(Response(\n+            json.dumps({\"error\": \"Invalid endpoint\"}),\n+            status=404,\n+            mimetype=\"application/json\"\n+        ), \"upstream\")\n+        return response\n+\n+\n+# ============================================================================\n+# Mock Calculator API\n+# ============================================================================\n+\n+def handle_calculator(path):\n+    \"\"\"Handle calculator API requests\"\"\"\n+    try:\n+        data = request.get_json()\n+        operation = data.get(\"operation\")\n+        a = data.get(\"a\", 0)\n+        b = data.get(\"b\", 0)\n+\n+        if operation == \"add\":\n+            result = a + b\n+        elif operation == \"subtract\":\n+            result = a - b\n+        elif operation == \"multiply\":\n+            result = a * b\n+        elif operation == \"divide\":\n+            if b == 0:\n+                response = add_error_source_header(Response(\n+                    json.dumps({\"error\": \"Division by zero\"}),\n+                    status=400,\n+                    mimetype=\"application/json\"\n+                ), \"upstream\")\n+                return response\n+            result = a / b\n+        else:\n+            response = add_error_source_header(Response(\n+                json.dumps({\"error\": f\"Unknown operation: {operation}\"}),\n+                status=400,\n+                mimetype=\"application/json\"\n+            ), \"upstream\")\n+            return response\n+\n+        response = add_error_source_header(jsonify({\n+            \"operation\": operation,\n+            \"a\": a,\n+            \"b\": b,\n+            \"result\": result\n+        }), \"upstream\")\n+        return response\n+    except Exception as e:\n+        response = add_error_source_header(Response(\n+            json.dumps({\"error\": str(e)}),","path":"modules/system/oagw/oagw-client-prototype/tests/python_integration/server.py","commit_id":"c9c711923d4db2ea8af2f40aeccc2fc2bb664b5a","original_commit_id":"c9c711923d4db2ea8af2f40aeccc2fc2bb664b5a","user":{"login":"github-advanced-security[bot]","id":62310815,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NjIzMTA4MTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/57789?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-advanced-security%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-advanced-security","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-advanced-security%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-advanced-security%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-advanced-security%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-advanced-security%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-advanced-security%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-advanced-security%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-advanced-security%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-advanced-security%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-advanced-security%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Information exposure through an exception\n\n[Stack trace information](1) flows to this location and may be exposed to an external user.\n\n[Show more details](https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core/security/code-scanning/99)","created_at":"2026-02-10T12:31:02Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T12:31:02Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2787684528","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787684528"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2787684528"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787684528/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":371,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":371,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787703386","pull_request_review_id":3778682279,"id":2787703386,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6mKPpa","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,173 @@\n+# ADR: Component Architecture\n+\n+- **Status**: Accepted\n+- **Date**: 2026-02-09\n+- **Deciders**: OAGW Team\n+\n+## Context and Problem Statement\n+\n+OAGW is being designed as a greenfield project without existing code. We need to establish the architectural foundation for how components are organized, how they communicate, and\n+how deployment flexibility is achieved.\n+\n+**Key Requirements**:\n+\n+- Support both single-executable and microservice deployment modes\n+- Clear separation of concerns between configuration management and request execution\n+- Enable independent scaling of different concerns\n+- Minimize latency through efficient communication patterns\n+\n+## Decision Drivers\n+\n+- Testability: Each component should be testable in isolation\n+- Deployment flexibility: Support multiple deployment topologies without code changes\n+- Separation of concerns: Configuration management vs request execution\n+- Performance: Minimize overhead in communication between components\n+- Maintainability: Clear boundaries and responsibilities\n+\n+## Decision\n+\n+OAGW is composed of three distinct components, packaged as separate library crates:\n+\n+### Components\n+\n+**1. API Handler (`oagw-api`)**\n+\n+- **Responsibility**: Entry point for all HTTP requests\n+- **Functions**:\n+    - Incoming authentication (validate Bearer tokens)\n+    - Incoming rate limiting (protect gateway from overload)\n+    - Path-based routing to CP or DP\n+- **Routes**:\n+    - `/api/oagw/v1/proxy/*` → Control Plane\n+    - `/api/oagw/v1/upstreams/*`, `/routes/*`, `/plugins/*` → Data Plane\n+\n+**2. Control Plane (`oagw-cp`)**","path":"modules/system/oagw/docs/adr-component-architecture.md","commit_id":"c4001447ea4b5a7a1747d7b00479084589d01bd9","original_commit_id":"c4001447ea4b5a7a1747d7b00479084589d01bd9","user":{"login":"striped-zebra-dev","id":225538363,"node_id":"U_kgDODXFxOw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225538363?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/striped-zebra-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Thx, fixed.","created_at":"2026-02-10T12:35:15Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T12:35:15Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2787703386","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787703386"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2787703386"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787703386/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":44,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2787338000,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":44,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787767161","pull_request_review_id":3778753151,"id":2787767161,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6mKfN5","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@\n+[workspace]\n+resolver = \"2\"\n+members = [\n+    \"oagw-sdk\",\n+    \"oagw-core\",\n+    \"oagw-api\",\n+    \"oagw-cp\",\n+    \"oagw-dp\",\n+]\n+\n+[workspace.package]\n+edition = \"2021\"\n+version = \"0.1.0\"","path":"modules/system/oagw/Cargo.toml","commit_id":"141f08c649b048bdf4b4c9e7add110efb09054c6","original_commit_id":"9f1410ff06eed7a636699d488d73f43928f784cf","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Check if root Cargo.toml exists and whether it references this sub-workspace\nif [ -f \"Cargo.toml\" ]; then\n  echo \"=== Root Cargo.toml workspace members ===\"\n  rg -A 20 '^\\[workspace\\]' Cargo.toml | head -30\n  echo \"\"\n  echo \"=== Checking for oagw references ===\"\n  rg 'oagw' Cargo.toml || echo \"No oagw references found in root Cargo.toml\"\nelse\n  echo \"No root Cargo.toml found\"\nfi\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/cyberfabric-core\n\nLength of output: 733\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Add `modules/system/oagw` to root workspace members in `Cargo.toml`.**\n\nThe sub-workspace configuration is correct, but it is not integrated with the repository's root workspace. The root `Cargo.toml` currently lists only `apps/*` and `libs/*` members; `modules/system/oagw` must be added to the workspace members list to ensure proper workspace coherence and dependency resolution.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/oagw/Cargo.toml` around lines 1 - 13, The root Cargo.toml's\nworkspace members list is missing the sub-workspace \"modules/system/oagw\";\nupdate the root workspace members array to include \"modules/system/oagw\" so the\nsub-workspace declared by the [workspace] and [workspace.package] blocks in\nCargo.toml is part of the repository workspace; ensure the entry matches the\nrelative path exactly and that the root [workspace] resolver and members syntax\nremains valid.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-10T12:48:36Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T12:48:41Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2787767161","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787767161"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2787767161"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787767161/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":1,"original_start_line":1,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":13,"original_line":13,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":13,"position":13,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787767176","pull_request_review_id":3778753151,"id":2787767176,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6mKfOI","diff_hunk":"@@ -352,18 +360,18 @@ Circuit breaker configuration follows same inheritance rules as rate limits:\n \n ### Positive\n \n-- ✅ Fast failure detection and automatic recovery\n-- ✅ Prevents cascading failures\n-- ✅ Reduces wasted resources on unhealthy upstreams\n-- ✅ Better user experience (fast 503 vs long timeout)\n-- ✅ Core functionality with consistent behavior\n+- Fast failure detection and automatic recovery\n+- Prevents cascading failures\n+- Reduces wasted resources on unhealthy upstreams\n+- Better user experience (fast 503 vs long timeout)\n+- Core functionality with consistent behavior\n \n ### Negative\n \n-- ❌ Adds complexity to request handling path\n-- ❌ Dependency on Redis for distributed state\n-- ❌ False positives possible during upstream maintenance\n-- ❌ Additional monitoring/alerting needed\n+- No Adds complexity to request handling path\n+- No Dependency on Redis for distributed state\n+- No False positives possible during upstream maintenance\n+- No Additional monitoring/alerting needed\n ","path":"modules/system/oagw/docs/adr-circuit-breaker.md","commit_id":"141f08c649b048bdf4b4c9e7add110efb09054c6","original_commit_id":"9f1410ff06eed7a636699d488d73f43928f784cf","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Remove stray “No” prefixes in negative bullets.**\n\nThese read like accidental edits and invert the intended meaning.  \n\n\n<details>\n<summary>✍️ Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n- - No Adds complexity to request handling path\n- - No Dependency on Redis for distributed state\n- - No False positives possible during upstream maintenance\n- - No Additional monitoring/alerting needed\n+ - Adds complexity to request handling path\n+ - Dependency on Redis for distributed state\n+ - False positives possible during upstream maintenance\n+ - Additional monitoring/alerting needed\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/oagw/docs/adr-circuit-breaker.md` around lines 371 - 375,\nRemove the stray \"No \" prefixes from the four negative bullets so they read as\nintended; change \"- No Adds complexity to request handling path\", \"- No\nDependency on Redis for distributed state\", \"- No False positives possible\nduring upstream maintenance\", and \"- No Additional monitoring/alerting needed\"\nto \"Adds complexity to request handling path\", \"Dependency on Redis for\ndistributed state\", \"False positives possible during upstream maintenance\", and\n\"Additional monitoring/alerting needed\" respectively so the list items no longer\nincorrectly include \"No\".\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-10T12:48:36Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T12:48:41Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2787767176","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787767176"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2787767176"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787767176/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":371,"original_start_line":371,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":375,"original_line":375,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":159,"position":159,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787767184","pull_request_review_id":3778753151,"id":2787767184,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6mKfOQ","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,173 @@\n+# ADR: Component Architecture\n+\n+- **Status**: Accepted\n+- **Date**: 2026-02-09\n+- **Deciders**: OAGW Team\n+\n+## Context and Problem Statement\n+\n+OAGW is being designed as a greenfield project without existing code. We need to establish the architectural foundation for how components are organized, how they communicate, and\n+how deployment flexibility is achieved.\n+\n+**Key Requirements**:\n+\n+- Support both single-executable and microservice deployment modes\n+- Clear separation of concerns between configuration management and request execution\n+- Enable independent scaling of different concerns\n+- Minimize latency through efficient communication patterns\n+\n+## Decision Drivers\n+\n+- Testability: Each component should be testable in isolation\n+- Deployment flexibility: Support multiple deployment topologies without code changes\n+- Separation of concerns: Configuration management vs request execution\n+- Performance: Minimize overhead in communication between components\n+- Maintainability: Clear boundaries and responsibilities\n+\n+## Decision\n+\n+OAGW is composed of three distinct components, packaged as separate library crates:\n+\n+### Components\n+\n+**1. API Handler (`oagw-api`)**\n+\n+- **Responsibility**: Entry point for all HTTP requests\n+- **Functions**:\n+    - Incoming authentication (validate Bearer tokens)\n+    - Incoming rate limiting (protect gateway from overload)\n+    - Path-based routing to CP or DP\n+- **Routes**:\n+    - `/api/oagw/v1/proxy/*` → Data Plane\n+    - `/api/oagw/v1/upstreams/*`, `/routes/*`, `/plugins/*` → Control Plane\n+\n+**2. Data Plane (`oagw-cp`)**\n+\n+- **Responsibility**: Orchestrate proxy requests to external services\n+- **Functions**:\n+    - Call Control Plane for config resolution (upstream, route)\n+    - Execute auth plugins (credential injection)\n+    - Execute guard plugins (validation, rate limiting)\n+    - Execute transform plugins (request/response mutation)\n+    - Make HTTP calls to external services\n+    - L1 cache for hot configs (1000 entries, LRU)\n+- **Dependencies**: Control Plane (config resolution), cred_store (secret retrieval)\n+\n+**3. Control Plane (`oagw-dp`)**\n+\n+- **Responsibility**: Manage configuration data with multi-layer caching\n+- **Functions**:\n+    - CRUD operations for upstreams/routes/plugins\n+    - Config resolution with hierarchical tenant inheritance\n+    - L1 cache (in-memory, 10k entries, LRU)\n+    - Optional L2 cache (Redis, shared across instances)\n+    - Database access (source of truth)\n+    - Cache invalidation on config writes\n+- **Dependencies**: modkit-db (database), types_registry (schema validation)\n+\n+### Module Structure\n+\n+```\n+modules/system/oagw/\n+├── oagw-sdk/          # Public API traits, models, errors\n+│                      # OAGWClientV1, AuthPlugin, GuardPlugin, TransformPlugin\n+├── oagw-core/         # Shared internals, service traits\n+│                      # ControlPlaneService, DataPlaneService\n+├── oagw-api/          # API Handler implementation\n+├── oagw-cp/           # Data Plane implementation\n+├── oagw-dp/           # Control Plane implementation","path":"modules/system/oagw/docs/adr-component-architecture.md","commit_id":"141f08c649b048bdf4b4c9e7add110efb09054c6","original_commit_id":"9f1410ff06eed7a636699d488d73f43928f784cf","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Counterintuitive crate naming may cause persistent confusion.**\n\nThe crate naming reverses industry conventions:\n- `oagw-cp` = **Data Plane** (CP typically means Control Plane)\n- `oagw-dp` = **Control Plane** (DP typically means Data Plane)\n\nThis unconventional naming is already causing documentation errors (e.g., in management-operations.md where \"DP\" is used when describing Control Plane operations).\n\n**Consider either:**\n1. Renaming crates to align with conventions: `oagw-data-plane` and `oagw-control-plane` (or `oagw-dp` for Data Plane, `oagw-cp` for Control Plane)\n2. Adding a prominent warning box at the top of this ADR and all related docs about the non-standard abbreviation usage\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🎯 Recommended approach</summary>\n\nOption 1 (preferred): Use full names to eliminate ambiguity:\n```diff\n-├── oagw-cp/           # Data Plane implementation\n-├── oagw-dp/           # Control Plane implementation\n+├── oagw-data-plane/   # Data Plane implementation\n+├── oagw-control-plane/ # Control Plane implementation\n```\n\nOption 2: Add warning box:\n```markdown\n> ⚠️ **Naming Convention**: In this codebase, `oagw-cp` refers to the Data Plane\n> and `oagw-dp` refers to the Control Plane. This differs from typical industry\n> usage where CP=Control Plane and DP=Data Plane. Always use full names in\n> documentation to avoid confusion.\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Tools</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 markdownlint-cli2 (0.20.0)</summary>\n\n[warning] 70-70: Fenced code blocks should have a language specified\n\n(MD040, fenced-code-language)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/oagw/docs/adr-component-architecture.md` around lines 44 - 78,\nThe repo uses reversed crate names: oagw-cp actually implements the Data Plane\nand oagw-dp implements the Control Plane; either rename crates to clear names\n(preferred) or add a prominent warning in ADR and all docs. To fix, pick one:\n(A) Rename crates from oagw-cp -> oagw-data-plane and oagw-dp ->\noagw-control-plane (update folder names, Cargo.toml package names, any\nreferences in code/tests/CI, and adjust module exports and imports such as\nOAGWClientV1, ControlPlaneService, DataPlaneService), and update docs\n(adr-component-architecture.md, management-operations.md, README) to use the new\nnames; or (B) add a bold warning at the top of adr-component-architecture.md and\npropagate the same note to management-operations.md and other docs clarifying\nthat oagw-cp = Data Plane and oagw-dp = Control Plane and recommend using full\nnames in prose; ensure all references to oagw-cp/oagw-dp in code comments and\ndocs are updated to match the chosen approach.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-10T12:48:36Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T12:48:41Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2787767184","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787767184"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2787767184"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787767184/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":44,"original_start_line":44,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":78,"original_line":78,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":78,"position":78,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787767188","pull_request_review_id":3778753151,"id":2787767188,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLy