ement Operations Flow\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+Management operations (CRUD for upstreams, routes, plugins) are routed directly from API Handler to Control Plane. This document describes the request flow and cache invalidation behavior.\n+\n+## Request Flow\n+\n+```\n+Client Request\n+  → API Handler (auth, rate limit)\n+    → Control Plane (validate, write DB, invalidate cache)\n+      → Response\n+```\n+\n+## Component Responsibilities\n+\n+### API Handler\n+- Validates Bearer token\n+- Applies inbound rate limiting\n+- Routes request to Control Plane based on path pattern:\n+  - `/api/oagw/v1/upstreams/*` → DP\n+  - `/api/oagw/v1/routes/*` → DP\n+  - `/api/oagw/v1/plugins/*` → DP","path":"modules/system/oagw/scenarios/management-operations.md","commit_id":"141f08c649b048bdf4b4c9e7add110efb09054c6","original_commit_id":"9f1410ff06eed7a636699d488d73f43928f784cf","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Correct component routing: Management APIs route to Control Plane, not Data Plane.**\n\nLines 22-24 state that management paths route to \"DP\" (Data Plane), but per the component architecture (adr-component-architecture.md), the Control Plane (`oagw-dp`) owns CRUD operations for upstreams/routes/plugins. Data Plane (`oagw-cp`) handles proxy requests.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Proposed correction</summary>\n\n```diff\n - Routes request to Control Plane based on path pattern:\n-  - `/api/oagw/v1/upstreams/*` → DP\n-  - `/api/oagw/v1/routes/*` → DP\n-  - `/api/oagw/v1/plugins/*` → DP\n+  - `/api/oagw/v1/upstreams/*` → Control Plane\n+  - `/api/oagw/v1/routes/*` → Control Plane\n+  - `/api/oagw/v1/plugins/*` → Control Plane\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n- Routes request to Control Plane based on path pattern:\n  - `/api/oagw/v1/upstreams/*` → Control Plane\n  - `/api/oagw/v1/routes/*` → Control Plane\n  - `/api/oagw/v1/plugins/*` → Control Plane\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/oagw/scenarios/management-operations.md` around lines 21 - 24,\nThe routing table incorrectly labels management paths as going to the Data\nPlane; update the three entries for `/api/oagw/v1/upstreams/*`,\n`/api/oagw/v1/routes/*`, and `/api/oagw/v1/plugins/*` so they route to the\nControl Plane (i.e., replace \"DP\" with \"Control Plane\" or \"oagw-dp\") to reflect\nthat CRUD management APIs are owned by the Control Plane.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-10T12:48:37Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T12:48:42Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2787767251","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787767251"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2787767251"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787767251/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":21,"original_start_line":21,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":24,"original_line":24,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":24,"position":24,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787767264","pull_request_review_id":3778753151,"id":2787767264,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6mKfPg","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,236 @@\n+# Management Operations Flow\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+Management operations (CRUD for upstreams, routes, plugins) are routed directly from API Handler to Control Plane. This document describes the request flow and cache invalidation behavior.\n+\n+## Request Flow\n+\n+```\n+Client Request\n+  → API Handler (auth, rate limit)\n+    → Control Plane (validate, write DB, invalidate cache)\n+      → Response\n+```\n+\n+## Component Responsibilities\n+\n+### API Handler\n+- Validates Bearer token\n+- Applies inbound rate limiting\n+- Routes request to Control Plane based on path pattern:\n+  - `/api/oagw/v1/upstreams/*` → DP\n+  - `/api/oagw/v1/routes/*` → DP\n+  - `/api/oagw/v1/plugins/*` → DP\n+\n+### Control Plane\n+- Validates request payload against schema\n+- Checks tenant authorization (via SecureConn scoping)\n+- Writes to database\n+- Invalidates affected cache entries (L1 and L2)\n+- Returns success/error response\n+\n+## Example: Create Upstream\n+\n+### Request\n+\n+```http\n+POST /api/oagw/v1/upstreams HTTP/1.1\n+Host: oagw.example.com\n+Authorization: Bearer <tenant-token>\n+Content-Type: application/json\n+\n+{\n+  \"server\": {\n+    \"endpoints\": [\n+      { \"scheme\": \"https\", \"host\": \"api.openai.com\", \"port\": 443 }\n+    ]\n+  },\n+  \"protocol\": \"gts.x.core.oagw.protocol.v1~x.core.http.v1\",\n+  \"alias\": \"openai\"\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Flow Steps\n+\n+1. **API Handler** receives request\n+   - Validates Bearer token → 401 if invalid\n+   - Checks `oagw:upstream:create` permission → 403 if denied\n+   - Routes to Control Plane\n+\n+2. **Control Plane** processes request\n+   - Validates JSON schema\n+   - Checks alias uniqueness within tenant\n+   - Writes to `oagw_upstream` table (scoped to tenant)\n+   - Returns `201 Created` with upstream ID\n+\n+3. **No cache invalidation** (new resource, nothing cached yet)\n+\n+### Response\n+\n+```http\n+HTTP/1.1 201 Created\n+Content-Type: application/json\n+Location: /api/oagw/v1/upstreams/gts.x.core.oagw.upstream.v1~7c9e6679...\n+\n+{\n+  \"id\": \"gts.x.core.oagw.upstream.v1~7c9e6679-7425-40de-944b-e07fc1f90ae7\",\n+  \"tenant_id\": \"...\",\n+  \"alias\": \"openai\",\n+  \"server\": { ... },\n+  \"enabled\": true,\n+  \"created_at\": \"2026-02-09T12:00:00Z\"\n+}\n+```\n+\n+## Example: Update Upstream\n+\n+### Request\n+\n+```http\n+PUT /api/oagw/v1/upstreams/gts.x.core.oagw.upstream.v1~7c9e6679... HTTP/1.1\n+Host: oagw.example.com\n+Authorization: Bearer <tenant-token>\n+Content-Type: application/json\n+\n+{\n+  \"server\": {\n+    \"endpoints\": [\n+      { \"scheme\": \"https\", \"host\": \"api.openai.com\", \"port\": 443 }\n+    ]\n+  },\n+  \"protocol\": \"gts.x.core.oagw.protocol.v1~x.core.http.v1\",\n+  \"alias\": \"openai\",\n+  \"rate_limit\": {\n+    \"sustained\": { \"rate\": 100, \"window\": \"minute\" }\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Flow Steps\n+\n+1. **API Handler** validates and routes to DP\n+\n+2. **Control Plane** processes update\n+   - Loads existing upstream (tenant-scoped)\n+   - Validates changes\n+   - Writes to database\n+   - **Invalidates caches**:\n+     - DP L1: `upstream:{tenant_id}:openai`\n+     - DP L2 (Redis): `upstream:{tenant_id}:openai`\n+   - Notifies API Handler to notify CP instances\n+\n+3. **API Handler** notifies Data Plane\n+   - Sends cache invalidation message to CP instances\n+   - CP flushes its L1 cache for this upstream\n+\n+4. **Response** returned\n+\n+### Cache Invalidation Flow\n+\n+```\n+DP writes to DB\n+  → DP flushes L1 cache\n+  → DP flushes L2 cache (Redis)\n+  → DP returns success to API Handler\n+  → API Handler notifies CP to flush L1 cache\n+```","path":"modules/system/oagw/scenarios/management-operations.md","commit_id":"141f08c649b048bdf4b4c9e7add110efb09054c6","original_commit_id":"9f1410ff06eed7a636699d488d73f43928f784cf","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Clarify component names throughout update flow description.**\n\nThe flow description mixes \"DP\" and \"Control Plane\" terminology inconsistently:\n- Line 112: \"routes to DP\"\n- Line 114: \"Control Plane processes update\"\n- Line 132: \"DP writes to DB\"\n- Line 136: \"API Handler notifies CP\"\n\nPer the architecture, Control Plane owns config writes. Use consistent naming: either \"Control Plane\" or \"CP\" throughout (not \"DP\").\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested terminology fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-1. **API Handler** validates and routes to DP\n+1. **API Handler** validates and routes to Control Plane\n\n-2. **Control Plane** processes update\n+2. **Control Plane (CP)** processes update\n    ...\n-   - Notifies API Handler to notify CP instances\n+   - Notifies API Handler to notify other CP instances\n\n ### Cache Invalidation Flow\n\n ```\n-DP writes to DB\n-  → DP flushes L1 cache\n-  → DP flushes L2 cache (Redis)\n-  → DP returns success to API Handler\n+CP writes to DB\n+  → CP flushes L1 cache\n+  → CP flushes L2 cache (Redis)\n+  → CP returns success to API Handler\n   → API Handler notifies CP to flush L1 cache\n ```\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Tools</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 markdownlint-cli2 (0.20.0)</summary>\n\n[warning] 131-131: Fenced code blocks should have a language specified\n\n(MD040, fenced-code-language)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/oagw/scenarios/management-operations.md` around lines 110 -\n137, The document inconsistently uses \"DP\" and \"Control Plane/CP\" in the update\nand cache-invalidation flows; standardize to \"Control Plane\" (or its\nabbreviation \"CP\") everywhere by replacing instances like \"routes to DP\", \"DP\nwrites to DB\", \"DP flushes L1/L2 cache\", and \"DP returns success to API Handler\"\nwith \"routes to Control Plane/CP\", \"CP writes to DB\", \"CP flushes L1/L2 cache\",\nand \"CP returns success to API Handler\", and ensure the Cache Invalidation Flow\nblock and the step list consistently use the chosen term and the same cache key\nnames (e.g., `upstream:{tenant_id}:openai`) and \"API Handler\" references remain\nunchanged.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-10T12:48:37Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T12:48:42Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2787767264","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787767264"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2787767264"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787767264/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":110,"original_start_line":110,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":137,"original_line":137,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":137,"position":137,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787767272","pull_request_review_id":3778753151,"id":2787767272,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6mKfPo","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,236 @@\n+# Management Operations Flow\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+Management operations (CRUD for upstreams, routes, plugins) are routed directly from API Handler to Control Plane. This document describes the request flow and cache invalidation behavior.\n+\n+## Request Flow\n+\n+```\n+Client Request\n+  → API Handler (auth, rate limit)\n+    → Control Plane (validate, write DB, invalidate cache)\n+      → Response\n+```\n+\n+## Component Responsibilities\n+\n+### API Handler\n+- Validates Bearer token\n+- Applies inbound rate limiting\n+- Routes request to Control Plane based on path pattern:\n+  - `/api/oagw/v1/upstreams/*` → DP\n+  - `/api/oagw/v1/routes/*` → DP\n+  - `/api/oagw/v1/plugins/*` → DP\n+\n+### Control Plane\n+- Validates request payload against schema\n+- Checks tenant authorization (via SecureConn scoping)\n+- Writes to database\n+- Invalidates affected cache entries (L1 and L2)\n+- Returns success/error response\n+\n+## Example: Create Upstream\n+\n+### Request\n+\n+```http\n+POST /api/oagw/v1/upstreams HTTP/1.1\n+Host: oagw.example.com\n+Authorization: Bearer <tenant-token>\n+Content-Type: application/json\n+\n+{\n+  \"server\": {\n+    \"endpoints\": [\n+      { \"scheme\": \"https\", \"host\": \"api.openai.com\", \"port\": 443 }\n+    ]\n+  },\n+  \"protocol\": \"gts.x.core.oagw.protocol.v1~x.core.http.v1\",\n+  \"alias\": \"openai\"\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Flow Steps\n+\n+1. **API Handler** receives request\n+   - Validates Bearer token → 401 if invalid\n+   - Checks `oagw:upstream:create` permission → 403 if denied\n+   - Routes to Control Plane\n+\n+2. **Control Plane** processes request\n+   - Validates JSON schema\n+   - Checks alias uniqueness within tenant\n+   - Writes to `oagw_upstream` table (scoped to tenant)\n+   - Returns `201 Created` with upstream ID\n+\n+3. **No cache invalidation** (new resource, nothing cached yet)\n+\n+### Response\n+\n+```http\n+HTTP/1.1 201 Created\n+Content-Type: application/json\n+Location: /api/oagw/v1/upstreams/gts.x.core.oagw.upstream.v1~7c9e6679...\n+\n+{\n+  \"id\": \"gts.x.core.oagw.upstream.v1~7c9e6679-7425-40de-944b-e07fc1f90ae7\",\n+  \"tenant_id\": \"...\",\n+  \"alias\": \"openai\",\n+  \"server\": { ... },\n+  \"enabled\": true,\n+  \"created_at\": \"2026-02-09T12:00:00Z\"\n+}\n+```\n+\n+## Example: Update Upstream\n+\n+### Request\n+\n+```http\n+PUT /api/oagw/v1/upstreams/gts.x.core.oagw.upstream.v1~7c9e6679... HTTP/1.1\n+Host: oagw.example.com\n+Authorization: Bearer <tenant-token>\n+Content-Type: application/json\n+\n+{\n+  \"server\": {\n+    \"endpoints\": [\n+      { \"scheme\": \"https\", \"host\": \"api.openai.com\", \"port\": 443 }\n+    ]\n+  },\n+  \"protocol\": \"gts.x.core.oagw.protocol.v1~x.core.http.v1\",\n+  \"alias\": \"openai\",\n+  \"rate_limit\": {\n+    \"sustained\": { \"rate\": 100, \"window\": \"minute\" }\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Flow Steps\n+\n+1. **API Handler** validates and routes to DP\n+\n+2. **Control Plane** processes update\n+   - Loads existing upstream (tenant-scoped)\n+   - Validates changes\n+   - Writes to database\n+   - **Invalidates caches**:\n+     - DP L1: `upstream:{tenant_id}:openai`\n+     - DP L2 (Redis): `upstream:{tenant_id}:openai`\n+   - Notifies API Handler to notify CP instances\n+\n+3. **API Handler** notifies Data Plane\n+   - Sends cache invalidation message to CP instances\n+   - CP flushes its L1 cache for this upstream\n+\n+4. **Response** returned\n+\n+### Cache Invalidation Flow\n+\n+```\n+DP writes to DB\n+  → DP flushes L1 cache\n+  → DP flushes L2 cache (Redis)\n+  → DP returns success to API Handler\n+  → API Handler notifies CP to flush L1 cache\n+```\n+\n+### Response\n+\n+```http\n+HTTP/1.1 200 OK\n+Content-Type: application/json\n+\n+{\n+  \"id\": \"gts.x.core.oagw.upstream.v1~7c9e6679...\",\n+  \"tenant_id\": \"...\",\n+  \"alias\": \"openai\",\n+  \"rate_limit\": {\n+    \"sustained\": { \"rate\": 100, \"window\": \"minute\" }\n+  },\n+  \"updated_at\": \"2026-02-09T12:05:00Z\"\n+}\n+```\n+\n+## Example: Delete Upstream\n+\n+### Request\n+\n+```http\n+DELETE /api/oagw/v1/upstreams/gts.x.core.oagw.upstream.v1~7c9e6679... HTTP/1.1\n+Host: oagw.example.com\n+Authorization: Bearer <tenant-token>\n+```\n+\n+### Flow Steps\n+\n+1. **API Handler** validates and routes to DP\n+\n+2. **Control Plane** processes deletion\n+   - Checks if upstream has dependent routes\n+   - If `cascade=true`: deletes routes first\n+   - If `cascade=false` and routes exist: returns `409 Conflict`\n+   - Deletes upstream from database\n+   - Invalidates all related cache entries:\n+     - Upstream config\n+     - All routes for this upstream\n+\n+3. **Cache invalidation** propagates to CP\n+\n+### Response (success)\n+\n+```http\n+HTTP/1.1 204 No Content\n+```\n+\n+### Response (conflict)\n+\n+```http\n+HTTP/1.1 409 Conflict\n+Content-Type: application/problem+json\n+\n+{\n+  \"type\": \"gts.x.core.errors.err.v1~x.oagw.config.upstream_has_routes.v1\",\n+  \"title\": \"Upstream Has Dependent Routes\",\n+  \"status\": 409,\n+  \"detail\": \"Cannot delete upstream with active routes. Use cascade=true or delete routes first.\",\n+  \"instance\": \"/api/oagw/v1/upstreams/gts.x.core.oagw.upstream.v1~7c9e6679...\",\n+  \"route_count\": 3\n+}\n+```\n+\n+## Cache Keys Affected\n+\n+Management operations invalidate these cache keys:\n+\n+### Upstream Operations\n+- DP L1/L2: `upstream:{tenant_id}:{alias}`\n+- CP L1: Same key (notified by API Handler)\n+\n+### Route Operations\n+- DP L1/L2: `route:{upstream_id}:{method}:{path}`\n+- CP L1: Same key (notified by API Handler)","path":"modules/system/oagw/scenarios/management-operations.md","commit_id":"141f08c649b048bdf4b4c9e7add110efb09054c6","original_commit_id":"9f1410ff06eed7a636699d488d73f43928f784cf","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Route cache key missing tenant scoping — potential cross-tenant cache collision.**\n\nThe route cache key `route:{upstream_id}:{method}:{path}` does not include `tenant_id`. If `upstream_id` is not globally unique or if route resolution is tenant-scoped, this can cause cross-tenant cache collisions, violating RISK-05 mitigation from the security review.\n\nConsider whether `upstream_id` is globally unique across all tenants. If not, include `tenant_id` in the key pattern.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Proposed fix if tenant scoping is needed</summary>\n\n```diff\n ### Route Operations\n-- DP L1/L2: `route:{upstream_id}:{method}:{path}`\n+- DP L1/L2: `route:{tenant_id}:{upstream_id}:{method}:{path}`\n - CP L1: Same key (notified by API Handler)\n```\n</details>\n\nBased on learnings: RISK-05 from the security review recommends including tenant_id in all cache keys to prevent cross-tenant leaks.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/oagw/scenarios/management-operations.md` around lines 211 -\n213, The route cache key \"route:{upstream_id}:{method}:{path}\" lacks tenant\nscoping and can cause cross-tenant collisions; update all usages and\ndocumentation to include tenant_id (e.g.,\n\"route:{tenant_id}:{upstream_id}:{method}:{path}\"), and ensure the same change\nis applied for DP L1/L2 and CP L1 (notified by the API Handler) so cache\nreads/writes use the tenant-scoped key consistently.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-10T12:48:37Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T12:48:42Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2787767272","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787767272"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2787767272"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787767272/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":211,"original_start_line":211,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":213,"original_line":213,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":213,"position":213,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787767285","pull_request_review_id":3778753151,"id":2787767285,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6mKfP1","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,459 @@\n+# Plugin Execution Flow\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+Plugins execute in Data Plane during proxy request processing. Three plugin types execute in strict order: Auth → Guards → Transform → Proxy Call → Transform.\n+\n+## Plugin Types\n+\n+### AuthPlugin\n+- **Purpose**: Inject authentication credentials\n+- **Execution**: Once per request, before guards\n+- **Can terminate**: No (always succeeds or errors)\n+- **Examples**: API key, OAuth2, Bearer token\n+\n+### GuardPlugin\n+- **Purpose**: Validate and enforce policies\n+- **Execution**: After auth, before transform\n+- **Can terminate**: Yes (reject request with error)\n+- **Examples**: Timeout, CORS, rate limiting\n+\n+### TransformPlugin\n+- **Purpose**: Modify request/response/error data\n+- **Execution**: Before and after proxy call\n+- **Can terminate**: No (mutations only)\n+- **Examples**: Logging, metrics, request ID\n+\n+## Execution Order\n+\n+```\n+Incoming Request\n+  ↓\n+1. Auth Plugin (credential injection)\n+  ↓\n+2. Guard Plugins (validation, can reject)\n+  ↓\n+3. Transform Plugins (modify request)\n+  ↓\n+4. HTTP call to external service\n+  ↓\n+5. Transform Plugins (modify response)\n+  ↓\n+Response to Client\n+```\n+\n+## Example: Full Plugin Chain\n+\n+### Configuration\n+\n+**Upstream config:**\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"alias\": \"openai\",\n+  \"auth\": {\n+    \"plugin\": \"gts.x.core.oagw.plugin.auth.v1~x.core.bearer_token.v1\",\n+    \"config\": { \"secret_ref\": \"gts.x.core.cred.v1~abc123...\" }\n+  },\n+  \"plugins\": {\n+    \"guards\": [\n+      \"gts.x.core.oagw.plugin.guard.v1~x.core.timeout.v1\"\n+    ],\n+    \"transforms\": [\n+      \"gts.x.core.oagw.plugin.transform.v1~x.core.request_id.v1\",\n+      \"gts.x.core.oagw.plugin.transform.v1~x.core.logging.v1\"\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Route config:**\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"match\": {\n+    \"http\": {\n+      \"methods\": [\"POST\"],\n+      \"path\": \"/v1/chat/completions\"\n+    }\n+  },\n+  \"plugins\": {\n+    \"guards\": [\n+      \"gts.x.core.oagw.plugin.guard.v1~x.core.cors.v1\"\n+    ]\n+  },\n+  \"rate_limit\": {\n+    \"sustained\": { \"rate\": 100, \"window\": \"minute\" }\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Request\n+\n+```http\n+POST /api/oagw/v1/proxy/openai/v1/chat/completions HTTP/1.1\n+Host: oagw.example.com\n+Authorization: Bearer <tenant-token>\n+Origin: https://example.com\n+Content-Type: application/json\n+\n+{\"model\": \"gpt-4\", \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Hello\"}]}\n+```\n+\n+### Execution Steps\n+\n+#### Phase 1: Auth Plugin\n+\n+**Plugin**: BearerTokenAuthPlugin\n+**Input**: Request context with no upstream auth\n+\n+**Actions**:\n+1. Retrieve secret from `cred_store` using `secret_ref`\n+2. Extract API key: `sk-proj-abc123...`\n+3. Inject into request headers\n+\n+**Output**: Request context updated\n+```\n+Headers:\n+  + Authorization: Bearer sk-proj-abc123...\n+```","path":"modules/system/oagw/scenarios/plugin-execution.md","commit_id":"141f08c649b048bdf4b4c9e7add110efb09054c6","original_commit_id":"9f1410ff06eed7a636699d488d73f43928f784cf","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Redact example API keys to avoid secret-scanner hits.**\n\nThe `sk-proj-abc123...` value is triggering secret scanners; replace with an obvious placeholder (e.g., `sk-REDACTED` or `sk-test-XXXX`).  \n\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Suggested redaction</summary>\n\n```diff\n-2. Extract API key: `sk-proj-abc123...`\n+2. Extract API key: `sk-REDACTED`\n...\n-  + Authorization: Bearer sk-proj-abc123...\n+  + Authorization: Bearer sk-REDACTED\n...\n-Authorization: Bearer sk-proj-abc123...\n+Authorization: Bearer sk-REDACTED\n```\n</details>\n\n\nAlso applies to: 203-212\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Tools</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 Gitleaks (8.30.0)</summary>\n\n[high] 110-110: Detected a Generic API Key, potentially exposing access to various services and sensitive operations.\n\n(generic-api-key)\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 markdownlint-cli2 (0.20.0)</summary>\n\n[warning] 114-114: Fenced code blocks should have a language specified\n\n(MD040, fenced-code-language)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/oagw/scenarios/plugin-execution.md` around lines 108 - 117,\nThe example API key \"sk-proj-abc123...\" in the plugin-execution scenario should\nbe redacted to avoid secret-scanner hits; update the example in the\nActions/Output blocks (the Authorization header example and any other\noccurrences around the noted range) to use a non-secret placeholder such as\n\"sk-REDACTED\" or \"sk-test-XXXX\" (e.g., replace `sk-proj-abc123...` with\n`sk-REDACTED`) so the request context/Headers examples remain illustrative but\ncontain no real-looking secrets.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-10T12:48:37Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T12:48:42Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2787767285","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787767285"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2787767285"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787767285/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":108,"original_start_line":108,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":117,"original_line":117,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":117,"position":117,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787767298","pull_request_review_id":3778753151,"id":2787767298,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6mKfQC","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@\n+# Unknown X-OAGW-Target-Host not in endpoint list\n+\n+## Setup\n+\n+- Upstream `vendor.com` with multiple endpoints:\n+  - `endpoints`: `[{\"scheme\": \"https\", \"host\": \"us.vendor.com\", \"port\": 443}, {\"scheme\": \"https\", \"host\": \"eu.vendor.com\", \"port\": 443}]`\n+  - `alias`: `vendor.com`\n+\n+## Request\n+\n+```http\n+POST /api/oagw/v1/proxy/vendor.com/v1/api/resource HTTP/1.1\n+Host: oagw.example.com\n+Authorization: Bearer <token>\n+X-OAGW-Target-Host: apac.vendor.com\n+Content-Type: application/json\n+\n+{\"key\": \"value\"}\n+```\n+\n+## Expected behavior\n+\n+- Request is rejected with `400 Bad Request`\n+- Error response:\n+\n+```http\n+HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request\n+X-OAGW-Error-Source: gateway\n+Content-Type: application/problem+json\n+\n+{\n+  \"type\": \"gts.x.core.errors.err.v1~x.oagw.routing.unknown_target_host.v1\",\n+  \"title\": \"Unknown Target Host\",\n+  \"status\": 400,\n+  \"detail\": \"X-OAGW-Target-Host 'apac.vendor.com' does not match any configured endpoint. Valid hosts: [us.vendor.com, eu.vendor.com]\",\n+  \"instance\": \"/api/oagw/v1/proxy/vendor.com/v1/api/resource\",\n+  \"upstream_id\": \"gts.x.core.oagw.upstream.v1~...\",\n+  \"invalid_value\": \"apac.vendor.com\",\n+  \"valid_hosts\": [\"us.vendor.com\", \"eu.vendor.com\"]\n+}\n+```\n+\n+## Validation\n+\n+- Header value must exactly match one of the configured endpoint hosts\n+- Allowlist validation prevents routing to arbitrary servers\n+- Error response includes list of valid hosts for debugging","path":"modules/system/oagw/scenarios/proxy-api/custom-header-routing/negative-2.1-unknown-host.md","commit_id":"141f08c649b048bdf4b4c9e7add110efb09054c6","original_commit_id":"9f1410ff06eed7a636699d488d73f43928f784cf","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Search for additional negative test scenarios covering RISK-04 attack vectors\n\n# Find all negative test scenarios in this directory\necho \"=== All test scenario files ===\"\nfd -e md . modules/system/oagw/scenarios/proxy-api/custom-header-routing/ 2>/dev/null | sort\n\necho -e \"\\n=== Negative test scenarios ===\"\nfd -e md . modules/system/oagw/scenarios/proxy-api/custom-header-routing/ 2>/dev/null | grep -i negative | sort\n\necho -e \"\\n=== Checking for IDN/punycode test coverage ===\"\nrg -i 'punycode|IDN|xn--|unicode' modules/system/oagw/scenarios/proxy-api/custom-header-routing/ 2>/dev/null || echo \"No ma