n/problem+json\n+\n+{\n+  \"type\": \"gts.x.core.errors.err.v1~x.oagw.routing.unknown_target_host.v1\",\n+  \"title\": \"Unknown Target Host\",\n+  \"status\": 400,\n+  \"detail\": \"X-OAGW-Target-Host 'apac.vendor.com' does not match any configured endpoint. Valid hosts: [us.vendor.com, eu.vendor.com]\",\n+  \"instance\": \"/api/oagw/v1/proxy/vendor.com/v1/api/resource\",\n+  \"upstream_id\": \"gts.x.core.oagw.upstream.v1~...\",\n+  \"invalid_value\": \"apac.vendor.com\",\n+  \"valid_hosts\": [\"us.vendor.com\", \"eu.vendor.com\"]\n+}\n+```\n+\n+## Validation\n+\n+- Header value must exactly match one of the configured endpoint hosts\n+- Allowlist validation prevents routing to arbitrary servers\n+- Error response includes list of valid hosts for debugging","path":"modules/system/oagw/scenarios/proxy-api/custom-header-routing/negative-2.1-unknown-host.md","commit_id":"141f08c649b048bdf4b4c9e7add110efb09054c6","original_commit_id":"9f1410ff06eed7a636699d488d73f43928f784cf","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Clarify validation normalization and edge-case handling.**\n\nThe \"exact match\" requirement must specify normalization rules to prevent bypass:\n\n- **Case-sensitivity**: Are `us.vendor.com` and `US.VENDOR.COM` treated as equivalent? (Hostnames are case-insensitive per RFC 1035.)\n- **Punycode normalization**: Is `xn--s7y.vendor.com` compared before or after IDN decoding?\n- **Trailing dots**: Does `us.vendor.com.` (FQDN) match `us.vendor.com`?\n- **Whitespace**: Are leading/trailing spaces rejected or trimmed?\n- **Port specifications**: If the header includes `:443`, is it stripped before comparison or rejected?\n\nBased on RISK-04 recommendations, document that validation must:\n1. Normalize to ASCII punycode before comparison\n2. Apply case-insensitive matching\n3. Forbid control characters, `@`, and reject malformed input\n4. Strip or validate ports separately if allowed\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Proposed additions to validation section</summary>\n\n```diff\n ## Validation\n \n - Header value must exactly match one of the configured endpoint hosts\n+  - Comparison is case-insensitive (per RFC 1035)\n+  - IDN hostnames are normalized to ASCII punycode before comparison\n+  - Trailing dots are normalized (FQDN trailing dot is stripped)\n+  - Leading/trailing whitespace is rejected\n+  - Control characters, `@`, and invalid URL syntax are rejected with 400\n+  - Port specifications (e.g., `:443`) are rejected or stripped (TBD policy)\n - Allowlist validation prevents routing to arbitrary servers\n - Error response includes list of valid hosts for debugging\n+  (note: exposing valid_hosts may be disabled in production per security policy)\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n- Header value must exactly match one of the configured endpoint hosts\n  - Comparison is case-insensitive (per RFC 1035)\n  - IDN hostnames are normalized to ASCII punycode before comparison\n  - Trailing dots are normalized (FQDN trailing dot is stripped)\n  - Leading/trailing whitespace is rejected\n  - Control characters, `@`, and invalid URL syntax are rejected with 400\n  - Port specifications (e.g., `:443`) are rejected or stripped (TBD policy)\n- Allowlist validation prevents routing to arbitrary servers\n- Error response includes list of valid hosts for debugging\n  (note: exposing valid_hosts may be disabled in production per security policy)\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn\n`@modules/system/oagw/scenarios/proxy-api/custom-header-routing/negative-2.1-unknown-host.md`\naround lines 45 - 47, Update the \"exact match\" validation wording in the\ncustom-header routing spec (negative-2.1-unknown-host.md) to prescribe\nnormalization and edge-case handling: state that header hostnames must be\nnormalized to ASCII/Punycode, compared case-insensitively, trimmed of\nleading/trailing whitespace, and with any trailing dot removed before\ncomparison; explicitly forbid control characters and `@` and treat malformed\ninput as rejected; and specify how port suffixes are handled (either strip\n`:port` and validate separately or reject headers containing a port). Reference\nRISK-04 recommendations 1–4 in the text and include the four concrete\nnormalization rules (punycode, case-insensitive, forbidden characters, port\nhandling) so implementers know exactly how to normalize and validate header\nvalues.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-10T12:48:37Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T12:48:42Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2787767311","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787767311"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2787767311"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787767311/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":45,"original_start_line":45,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":47,"original_line":47,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":47,"position":47,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787767322","pull_request_review_id":3778753151,"id":2787767322,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6mKfQa","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,339 @@\n+# Proxy Operations Flow\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+Proxy operations execute API calls to external services. Requests are routed from API Handler → Data Plane → Control Plane (config resolution) → Data Plane (execution).\n+\n+## Request Flow\n+\n+```\n+Client Request\n+  → API Handler (auth, rate limit)\n+    → Data Plane (orchestrate)\n+      → Control Plane (resolve upstream config)\n+      → Control Plane (resolve route config)\n+      → CP: Execute plugins (auth, guard, transform)\n+      → CP: HTTP call to external service\n+    → Response\n+```\n+\n+## Component Responsibilities\n+\n+### API Handler\n+- Validates Bearer token\n+- Applies inbound rate limiting\n+- Routes `/api/oagw/v1/proxy/*` requests to Data Plane\n+\n+### Data Plane\n+- Orchestrates proxy request execution\n+- Checks L1 cache for hot configs\n+- Calls DP for config resolution (on cache miss)\n+- Executes plugin chain:\n+  1. Auth plugin (inject credentials)\n+  2. Guard plugins (validate, enforce policies)\n+  3. Transform plugins (modify request)\n+  4. HTTP call to external service\n+  5. Transform plugins (modify response)\n+- Returns response to client\n+\n+### Control Plane\n+- Resolves upstream by alias (tenant hierarchy walk)\n+- Resolves route by (upstream_id, method, path)\n+- Returns config from L1 cache → L2 cache → DB\n+- Serves as authoritative config source","path":"modules/system/oagw/scenarios/proxy-operations.md","commit_id":"141f08c649b048bdf4b4c9e7add110efb09054c6","original_commit_id":"9f1410ff06eed7a636699d488d73f43928f784cf","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Clarify CP/DP terminology in component responsibilities.**\n\nThere's terminology confusion:\n- Line 30: \"Calls DP for config resolution (on cache miss)\" \n- Lines 39-43: Control Plane \"Resolves upstream by alias\" and \"Returns config from L1 cache → L2 cache → DB\"\n\nBut the Data Plane section (lines 27-37) describes the Data Plane checking L1 cache and calling \"DP\" for config resolution. Should line 30 say \"Calls CP\" instead of \"Calls DP\"?\n\nAdditionally, comparing with `adr-request-routing.md` (lines 55-60), it states \"DP owns configuration data and database access.\" This seems inconsistent with this document suggesting Control Plane handles config resolution.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/oagw/scenarios/proxy-operations.md` around lines 27 - 43,\nSummary: The document misuses CP/DP labels—\"Calls DP for config resolution\"\nshould refer to the Control Plane and the ownership statements conflict with\nadr-request-routing.md. Fix: update the Data Plane section to say \"Calls CP for\nconfig resolution (on cache miss)\" and reconcile the ownership sentence by\neither changing \"DP owns configuration data and database access\" in\nadr-request-routing.md to match this doc or add a clarifying note here that\nControl Plane resolves and serves authoritative configs while Data Plane may\ncache and read from L1/L2; ensure references to \"Resolves upstream by alias\",\n\"Returns config from L1 cache → L2 cache → DB\", \"Data Plane\", and \"Control\nPlane\" use consistent ownership language across both docs.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-10T12:48:38Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T12:48:42Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2787767322","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787767322"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2787767322"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2787767322/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":27,"original_start_line":27,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":43,"original_line":43,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":43,"position":43,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2790987314","pull_request_review_id":3782386256,"id":2790987314,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6mWxYy","diff_hunk":"@@ -93,12 +159,56 @@\n CyberFabric needs a reliable way to manage outbound API calls to external services.\n The Outbound API Gateway (OAGW) provides a centralized layer for routing, authentication, rate limiting, and monitoring of those requests.\n \n+### Component Architecture\n+\n+OAGW is designed with three distinct components to enable independent scaling and clear separation of concerns:\n+\n+1. **API Handler**: Entry point for all requests. Handles incoming authentication, rate limiting, and routes requests to either Data Plane (proxy operations) or Control Plane (\n+   configuration management).\n+\n+2. **Control Plane (DP)**: Manages configuration data and provides fast config resolution. Handles CRUD operations for upstreams/routes/plugins, owns database access, and\n+   implements multi-layer caching (L1 in-memory + optional L2 Redis).\n+\n+3. **Data Plane (CP)**: Orchestrates proxy requests to external services. Calls Control Plane for configuration resolution, validates policies, executes HTTP calls to upstream\n+   services, and manages plugin execution.\n+\n+**Request Flow**:\n+\n+- Management operations (`POST /upstreams`, `PUT /routes`, etc.) → API Handler → **Control Plane**\n+- Proxy operations (`GET /proxy/{alias}/*`) → API Handler → **Data Plane** → Control Plane (config resolution) → Data Plane (execute)\n+\n+**Deployment**: Modkit framework handles both single-executable and microservice deployment modes, wiring components via in-process function calls or RPC transparently.\n+\n+For detailed architectural decisions, see:\n+\n+- [ADR: Component Architecture](./docs/adr-component-architecture.md)\n+- [ADR: Request Routing](./docs/adr-request-routing.md)\n+\n+### Terminology Note\n+\n+**Crate Names vs. Component Terminology**: Due to historical naming decisions, crate names do not align with component terminology:","path":"modules/system/oagw/DESIGN.md","commit_id":"141f08c649b048bdf4b4c9e7add110efb09054c6","original_commit_id":"9f1410ff06eed7a636699d488d73f43928f784cf","user":{"login":"mattgarmon","id":22921875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTIxODc1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22921875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattgarmon","html_url":"https://github.com/mattgarmon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattgarmon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattgarmon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattgarmon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattgarmon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattgarmon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattgarmon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattgarmon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattgarmon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattgarmon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"For module stubs, we have `oagw-cp/src/control_plane.rs` and `oagw-dp/src/data_plane.rs`\nIn the cargo files, they align with the descriptions described here.\n\nFiles should be renamed to be consistent.\n\n","created_at":"2026-02-11T00:55:18Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T00:55:18Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2790987314","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2790987314"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/527#discussion_r2790987314"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/527"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2790987314/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":189,"original_line":189,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":258,"position":264,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2792087318","pull_request_review_id":3783541568,"id":2792087318,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6ma98W","diff_hunk":"@@ -93,12 +159,56 @@\n CyberFabric needs a reliable way to manage outbound API calls to external services.\n The Outbound API Gateway (OAGW) provides a centralized layer for routing, authentication, rate limiting, and monitoring of those requests.\n \n+### Component Architecture\n+\n+OAGW is designed with three distinct components to enable independent scaling and clear separation of concerns:\n+\n+1. **API Handler**: Entry point for all requests. Handles incoming authentication, rate limiting, and routes requests to either Data Plane (proxy operations) or Control Plane (\n+   configuration management).\n+\n+2. **Control Plane (DP)**: Manages configuration data and provides fast config resolution. Handles CRUD operations for upstreams/routes/plugins, owns database access, and\n+   implements multi-layer caching (L1 in-memory + optional L2 Redis).\n+\n+3. **Data Plane (CP)**: Orchestrates proxy requests to external services. Calls Control Plane for configuration resolution, validates policies, executes HTTP calls to upstream\n+   services, and manages plugin execution.\n+\n+**Request Flow**:\n+\n+- Management operations (`POST /upstreams`, `PUT /routes`, etc.) → API Handler → **Control Plane**\n+- Proxy operations (`GET /proxy/{alias}/*`) → API Handler → **Data Plane** → Control Plane (config resolution) → Data Plane (execute)\n+\n+**Deployment**: Modkit framework handles both single-executable and microservice deployment modes, wiring components via in-process function calls or RPC transparently.\n+\n+For detailed architectural decisions, see:\n+\n+- [ADR: Component Architecture](./docs/adr-component-architecture.md)\n+- [ADR: Request Routing](./docs/adr-request-routing.md)\n+\n+### Terminology Note\n+\n+**Crate Names vs. Component Terminology**: Due to historical naming decisions, crate names do not align with component terminology:","path":"modules/system/oagw/DESIGN.md","commit_id":"141f08c649b048bdf4b4c9e7add110efb09054c6","original_commit_id":"9f1410ff06eed7a636699d488d73f43928f784cf","user":{"login":"striped-zebra-dev","id":225538363,"node_id":"U_kgDODXFxOw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225538363?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/striped-zebra-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/striped-zebra-dev/events{/privacy}","receive