config write (e.g., PUT /upstreams/{id})\" to explicitly perform the DB write\nand commit first (DP writes to database and commits transaction), and only then\nflush DP L1 cache, flush L2 cache (if enabled), return success, and notify CP\n(or let CP pick up via periodic sync); mention that invalidation should not\nhappen if the DB commit fails to avoid stale/incorrect cache state.\n\nIn `@modules/system/oagw/docs/adr-plugin-system.md`:\n- Around line 41-79: The markdown has unlabeled fenced code blocks; add language\nlabels so linting passes: mark the first fenced block that contains the Rust\ntraits (AuthPlugin, GuardPlugin, TransformPlugin in oagw-sdk/src/plugins.rs) as\n```rust (ensure the closing fence matches), and label the \"Plugin Execution\nOrder\" fenced block as a plain text block using ```text (or ```markdown if\npreferred) so the diagram is fenced with a language identifier and the\nopening/closing fences are consistent.\n\nIn `@modules/system/oagw/scenarios/cache-invalidation.md`:\n- Around line 399-407: Update the Impact wording in the \"Impact\" section so it\naligns with the no-TTL policy for the CP cache: replace \"CP L1 cache may be\nstale until TTL or eviction\" with language specifying eviction-only staleness\n(e.g., \"CP L1 cache may be stale until eviction (no TTL)\") or alternatively add\na short TTL policy sentence in the \"Mitigation\" section; target the \"Impact\" and\n\"Mitigation\" lines referencing the CP cache/L1 cache entries to ensure\nconsistency with earlier guidance.\n\nIn `@modules/system/oagw/scenarios/plugin-execution.md`:\n- Around line 27-43: Several fenced code blocks in plugin-execution.md lack\nlanguage identifiers; update each block (the \"Execution Order\" block starting\nwith \"Incoming Request\", the \"Headers:\" examples, the \"Upstream returns 500\nerror\" / post-error flow, the \"LoggingTransformPlugin:\" /\n\"RequestIdTransformPlugin:\" block, and the \"Guards: [...] / Transforms\n(pre/post): [...]\" block) to use